// Generated from approved Golden Manual Markdown. Run tools/import-synonym-lessons.py.
export const lessons = [{"id":"lesson-003","sourceId":2,"headword":"a lot of","title":"A Lot Of","titleZh":"很多；相當大的（壓力）","subtitle":"很多；相當大的（壓力）","description":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 7.3〈Meditation in School〉問讀者小學時是否感到 under a lot of pressure。此處 a lot of 修飾不可數名詞 pressure，說壓力的程度或總量，不是數算幾件壓力。下列替換用在這個搭配；換到可數名詞如 exams 時，選詞要重新判斷。","sourceSense":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 7.3〈Meditation in School〉問讀者小學時是否感到 under a lot of pressure。此處 a lot of 修飾不可數名詞 pressure，說壓力的程度或總量，不是數算幾件壓力。下列替換用在這個搭配；換到可數名詞如 exams 時，選詞要重新判斷。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["many","此處不成立","Many 直接修飾複數可數名詞，如 many exams；不可說 many pressure。可改說 many sources of pressure，但意思變成數算來源。"],["numerous","此處不成立","Numerous 也要求複數可數名詞，如 numerous deadlines；numerous pressure 不合語法。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["著重點","較合適說法"],"rows":[["壓力總量大、較正式","a great deal of pressure"],["程度明顯而不必極端","considerable pressure"],["某一刻的強烈壓迫感","intense pressure"],["長期或外在要求造成沉重負擔","heavy pressure"],["語境明確支持極大、難以承受","enormous pressure"]],"note":"快選規則： 先看 pressure 是不可數名詞，排除直接接在它前面的 many/numerous。再看語境是否只說「量大」、說當下強度、說沉重外壓，還是明確說難以承受；不要把普通「很多」自動升格為「極大」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"A Great Deal Of","meaning":"大量的（不可數）","note":"直接表示大量不可數壓力，語體比 a lot of 稍正式；不說壓力一定達危機程度。","collocations":"under a great deal of pressure; a great deal of work / stress.","example":"The pupils were under a great deal of pressure before the interview.","exampleZh":"面試前，學生承受很大壓力。","contrast":"A great deal of 後可接 pressure，但不可接複數可數的 deadlines；不要與 a great deal 的副詞用法混淆。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At primary school, Mei felt under a lot of pressure because she had tests almost every week.","zh":"阿美在小學時幾乎每週都要測驗，因此感到承受很大壓力。","upgrade":"At primary school, Mei felt under a great deal of pressure because she had tests almost every week.","answer":"a great deal of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"many","explanation":"Many 不能直接修飾不可數的 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a great deal of","explanation":"可與 pressure 搭配，保留壓力總量很大的意思。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a number of","explanation":"A number of 要接複數可數名詞，不可接 pressure。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"Numerous 數算多項事物，不可說 numerous pressure。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a great deal","explanation":"缺少 of；在此名詞前必須說 a great deal of。"},{"letter":"F","text":"several","explanation":"Several 要接可數複數，如 several tests。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Her classmates put a lot of pressure on the class monitor to share an unverified rumour, although she wanted to check it first.","zh":"同學們向班長施加很大壓力，要她轉發一則未經核實的傳聞，雖然她想先查證。","upgrade":"Her classmates put a great deal of pressure on the class monitor to share an unverified rumour, although she wanted to check it first.","answer":"a great deal of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a few","explanation":"A few 須修飾複數可數項目，不能修飾 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a lot","explanation":"沒有 of，不能直接放在名詞 pressure 前。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a great deal of","explanation":"同學施加的是不可數的壓力總量；put a great deal of pressure on 是自然搭配。"},{"letter":"D","text":"many","explanation":"Many 可修飾多名同學或多次催促，不能直接說 many pressure。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a series of","explanation":"若有多次催促，可說 a series of requests；此處不可把壓力總量說成事件序列。"},{"letter":"F","text":"numerous","explanation":"Numerous 須接複數可數名詞。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Considerable","meaning":"相當大的","note":"表示壓力程度已足以受注意，適合較正式的報告；改寫時刪去 of。","collocations":"considerable pressure; under considerable pressure; place considerable pressure on someone.","example":"The expectation to rank first placed considerable pressure on the pupil.","exampleZh":"必須考第一的期望使那名學生承受相當大的壓力。","contrast":"Considerable 評估程度顯著，但不像 enormous 必然推到極端；不是 considerable of pressure。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The report describes a lot of pressure on children whose parents expect perfect grades; it calls the burden substantial but not overwhelming.","zh":"報告說，父母期望滿分令孩子承受很大壓力，並形容這種負擔相當大，但未至難以承受。","upgrade":"The report describes considerable pressure on children whose parents expect perfect grades; it calls the burden substantial but not overwhelming.","answer":"considerable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"considerable","explanation":"正式報告評估壓力顯著，形容詞可直接修飾 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"considerably","explanation":"副詞 considerably 不能直接放在 pressure 前。"},{"letter":"C","text":"enormous","explanation":"報告已明言負擔雖大但未至難以承受，enormous 會把程度說得過重。"},{"letter":"D","text":"intense","explanation":"家長期望造成持續而相當大的負擔；intense 偏重某時刻的強烈感受。"},{"letter":"E","text":"countless","explanation":"Countless 數算項目，且誇大成無數，不合此句。"},{"letter":"F","text":"considerable of","explanation":"形容詞 considerable 後不加 of。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The council faced a lot of pressure from residents to keep the library open; the petition was influential but did not force a decision.","zh":"居民要求圖書館繼續開放，令議會承受很大壓力；請願具影響力，但未迫使議會作決定。","upgrade":"The council faced considerable pressure from residents to keep the library open; the petition was influential but did not force a decision.","answer":"considerable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enormous","explanation":"請願有影響力，但尚未迫使議會讓步；enormous 對已知程度說得過重。"},{"letter":"B","text":"considerably","explanation":"Considerably 是副詞，後面不能這樣接名詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"considerable","explanation":"居民請願對議會有顯著影響，卻非壓倒性；faced considerable pressure 合適。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several","explanation":"Several 會數算幾件事，而非壓力程度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a quantity of","explanation":"A quantity of 常說可量度物質，用於心理壓力生硬。"},{"letter":"F","text":"intense","explanation":"句子談一場有影響力、尚未決定結果的公共請願，沒有突出某個瞬間的強烈緊迫感。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Intense","meaning":"強烈的","note":"強調某個時刻或短期情境中壓力感受非常強，尤其競賽、測試或緊迫關頭。","collocations":"intense pressure; face intense pressure; intense pressure during an exam.","example":"During the final minute of the contest, the speaker felt intense pressure.","exampleZh":"比賽最後一分鐘，發言者感到壓力極大。","contrast":"Intense 形容強度，不表示有很多不同來源；不能無條件把所有 a lot of pressure 都升格為強烈壓力。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"During the timed oral exam, Amir felt a lot of pressure in the final thirty seconds and his hands shook.","zh":"限時口試最後三十秒，阿米爾感到很大壓力，雙手發抖。","upgrade":"During the timed oral exam, Amir felt intense pressure in the final thirty seconds and his hands shook.","answer":"intense","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"considerable","explanation":"最後三十秒手發抖，重點是當下壓力強烈；considerable 只說程度相當大。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intensely","explanation":"Intensely 是副詞，這個位置需要形容詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intense","explanation":"限時最後三十秒及發抖顯示當下壓力強烈，這個形容詞貼切。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several","explanation":"Several 要數算複數事物。"},{"letter":"E","text":"pressureful","explanation":"Pressureful 不是此處自然的標準搭配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"heavy","explanation":"Heavy pressure 可說持續負擔，但這裏強調倒數三十秒的急迫感。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The spokesperson came under a lot of pressure from reporters demanding an answer during a live briefing.","zh":"發言人在直播簡報期間面對記者要求即時回答，承受很大壓力。","upgrade":"The spokesperson came under intense pressure from reporters demanding an answer during a live briefing.","answer":"intense","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a lot","explanation":"缺少 of，不能直接接 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intensity","explanation":"Intensity 是名詞，不能直接以此方式修飾 pressure。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intense","explanation":"直播現場被記者催促即時答覆，重點是當下高度緊迫的壓力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"considerable","explanation":"Considerable 可說程度顯著，但沒有 intense 對直播即時追問的強度那麼準確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"pressured","explanation":"Pressured 形容人感到被逼迫，不說 pressured pressure。"},{"letter":"F","text":"heavy","explanation":"Heavy 較像累積的沉重負擔；此句聚焦直播追問的即時緊張。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Heavy","meaning":"沉重的","note":"Heavy pressure 是常見搭配，常指持續或外來要求帶來的沉重負擔；不一定是瞬間的強烈感受。","collocations":"under heavy pressure; heavy pressure from parents; put heavy pressure on a team.","example":"The committee was under heavy pressure from parents to change the timetable.","exampleZh":"委員會受到家長沉重壓力，被要求更改時間表。","contrast":"Heavy 在這裏是比喻，不是物理重量；寫 under heavy pressure，不加 of。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The head teacher was under a lot of pressure from parents to cancel the extra Saturday class, and the demands continued for months.","zh":"家長要求取消額外的星期六課，校長長達數月承受很大壓力。","upgrade":"The head teacher was under heavy pressure from parents to cancel the extra Saturday class, and the demands continued for months.","answer":"heavy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"heavily","explanation":"副詞 heavily 不能直接修飾 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"heavy","explanation":"家長長期施加的要求構成沉重壓力，搭配 under heavy pressure 自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intense","explanation":"家長要求持續數月，heavy 較能表達長期沉重壓力；intense 偏向強烈瞬間。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enormous","explanation":"持續要求構成重壓，但句中沒有說已到極端、難以承受的程度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"weighty of","explanation":"Weighty of 不是自然英語搭配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"several","explanation":"Several 只能數算項目，如 several complaints。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A shortage of coaches put a lot of pressure on the remaining sports staff throughout the term.","zh":"教練人手短缺，在整個學期都令其餘體育職員承受很大壓力。","upgrade":"A shortage of coaches put heavy pressure on the remaining sports staff throughout the term.","answer":"heavy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"intense","explanation":"人手短缺貫穿整個學期，較像長期沉重負擔，而非某一刻的壓迫感。"},{"letter":"B","text":"heavy","explanation":"一整學期的人手短缺使職員持續承擔更多工作，put heavy pressure on 搭配自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"heaviness","explanation":"Heaviness 是名詞，不可直接修飾另一個 pressure。"},{"letter":"D","text":"under heavy","explanation":"句中已有 put，不能再接 under heavy pressure on；那是另一種句型。"},{"letter":"E","text":"countless","explanation":"Countless 會數算項目，且不合不可數名詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"enormous","explanation":"人手不足造成重壓，但句中未說工作量大到難以承受。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Enormous","meaning":"極大的","note":"強調壓力程度非常高，較 a lot of 更有力；必須由句子提供足以支持的極端情境。","collocations":"enormous pressure; under enormous pressure; place enormous pressure on someone.","example":"The sole organiser faced enormous pressure when three venues cancelled on the same morning.","exampleZh":"三個場地同日上午取消預訂，唯一的主辦人承受極大壓力。","contrast":"Enormous 強調極大，不是任何一般的 a lot of 都能替換；若只是「相當大」，選 considerable 較審慎。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"As the only school counsellor for a thousand pupils during an emergency, Leung faced a lot of pressure and said the burden was overwhelming.","zh":"緊急情況下，梁老師是千名學生唯一的學校輔導員；他承受極大壓力，並說負擔令人難以招架。","upgrade":"As the only school counsellor for a thousand pupils during an emergency, Leung faced enormous pressure and said the burden was overwhelming.","answer":"enormous","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enormously","explanation":"Enormously 是副詞，不能直接修飾名詞 pressure。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enormous","explanation":"一人負責千名學生且難以招架，足以支持「極大」的較強說法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"many","explanation":"一人照顧千名學生所受的是不可數的壓力總量；many 可修飾 pupils，不能修飾 pressure。"},{"letter":"D","text":"considerable","explanation":"一人處理千名學生且遇緊急事故，並自述負擔難以承受，considerable 程度較弱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"large of","explanation":"Large of 不是此處自然的量詞或形容詞結構。"},{"letter":"F","text":"heavy","explanation":"Heavy 也指沉重負擔，但此處給出極端工作量和『難以承受』，enormous 更準確。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The charity came under a lot of pressure when its only food supplier cancelled overnight; it had to feed 2,000 families the next morning, and the director said the scale was overwhelming.","zh":"慈善機構唯一的食物供應商一夜間取消供貨，翌晨仍須為二千個家庭提供食物；總監說事態規模令人難以招架，機構承受極大壓力。","upgrade":"The charity came under enormous pressure when its only food supplier cancelled overnight; it had to feed 2,000 families the next morning, and the director said the scale was overwhelming.","answer":"enormous","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"considerable","explanation":"一夜失去唯一供應商，翌晨仍要服務二千家庭且總監稱規模難以招架，已超過一般『相當大』。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enormity","explanation":"Enormity 通常是名詞，不能直接作 pressure 的形容詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"enormous","explanation":"機構面對二千家庭的緊急食物缺口且自述難以招架，足以用 enormous。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enormously","explanation":"Enormously 是副詞，不能直接放在 pressure 前。"},{"letter":"E","text":"heavy","explanation":"Heavy 可指沉重負擔；此處緊急規模極大且自述難以招架，enormous 更準確。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a few","explanation":"A few 須接複數可數項目。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"many / numerous：可數性","zh":"原句 pressure 是不可數名詞，many pressure 和 numerous pressure 均錯；若要數算壓力來源，可寫 many deadlines 或 numerous demands，但已改變所量度的事物。","point":"Many and numerous count plural items; a lot of pressure measures an uncountable amount."},{"word":"a lot / a lot of / lots of：結構","zh":"名詞 pressure 前須有 of：a lot of pressure。A lot 可作副詞，如 I worry a lot；口語 lots of pressure 也可行，但語體較隨意。","point":"The noun phrase needs of; a lot without of is adverbial in this contrast."},{"word":"pressure / stress：外在要求與感受","zh":"Pressure 可指家長、考試等施加的要求；stress 側重人在這些要求下感到的緊張。兩者可同時存在，但不能把原句的名詞無條件換成 stress。","point":"Pressure can name demands; stress often names the resulting strain."},{"word":"intense / considerable / enormous：程度","zh":"Considerable 表示值得注意的高程度；intense 強調當下的強烈感受；enormous 把程度提高至極大。原文 a lot of 本身不精確，強化詞須有練習語境支持。","point":"These adjectives add different strength or focus; none is a universal one-for-one replacement."},{"word":"under pressure / pressure on：搭配","zh":"人通常 be under pressure；某件要求 put pressure on 某人。若把 a lot of 改成形容詞，說 under heavy pressure，不是 under heavy of pressure。","point":"Keep the original preposition pattern and remove of when the replacement is an adjective."}],"moduleNumber":3},{"id":"lesson-004","sourceId":7,"headword":"able","title":"Able","titleZh":"能夠觀看；有機會觀看","subtitle":"能夠觀看；有機會觀看","description":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 4.3〈3D - I See the Future〉說迪士尼經典作品的影迷會因 being able to watch these films with wonderful 3D visual effects 而高興。這裏 able to watch 指放映／供應安排使觀賞變得可行，不是影迷受過訓練、具備「會看電影」的技能。0006 ability levels 是學習能力程度，不能把那課的技能與天資詞直接移到本課。","sourceSense":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 4.3〈3D - I See the Future〉說迪士尼經典作品的影迷會因 being able to watch these films with wonderful 3D visual effects 而高興。這裏 able to watch 指放映／供應安排使觀賞變得可行，不是影迷受過訓練、具備「會看電影」的技能。0006 ability levels 是學習能力程度，不能把那課的技能與天資詞直接移到本課。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["capable","不合源句重點","Capable of watching 語法可行，但慣常暗示個人有能力應付任務；本段講新3D放映帶來觀賞機會。"],["competent","不合源句","Competent 指勝任任務或達標；影迷不需證明「看電影很能幹」。"],["having the ability","有條件但不優先","形式上可改成 having the ability to watch，卻容易讓讀者想到個人技能；若明說設備／放映令觀看可行，仍以 can / have the opportunity to 自然。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["問題","用語"],"rows":[["現在／將來可看嗎？","can watch"],["過去某場次當時可看嗎？","could watch"],["想突出場次提供但未必採用的機會嗎？","have the opportunity to watch"],["想口語說終於有機會嗎？","get the chance to watch"],["想說有合法場地、服務或門票渠道嗎？","have access to the film"]],"note":"快選規則： 先找放映、門票或服務這個「使觀看可行」的條件，再決定時間與語體。影迷不是因為變得 competent 才能看3D；他們只是有機會。對照 0006，ability 在學徒課指個人能力程度。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Can","meaning":"可以；能夠","note":"最簡潔說當下或將來的放映條件讓人可以觀賞；後接動詞原形。","collocations":"can watch / see / attend; can now watch in 3D.","example":"Families can watch the restored film in 3D at the weekend screening.","exampleZh":"家庭可在週末放映場觀看修復後的3D電影。","contrast":"Can 在別處也可表示技能或許可；本課由放映安排限定為觀賞可行性，且不說已經看了。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Because the cinema has added a 3D screening this weekend, families are able to watch the restored film on Saturday.","zh":"戲院本週末增設3D場次，所以家庭星期六可以觀看修復後的電影。","upgrade":"Because the cinema has added a 3D screening this weekend, families can watch the restored film on Saturday.","answer":"can","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"can","explanation":"增設場次令觀看可行，can watch 直接而自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"can to","explanation":"Can 後不能加 to。"},{"letter":"C","text":"are permitted to","explanation":"新增放映令家庭有機會觀看，句中沒有提特別規則或許可。"},{"letter":"D","text":"competent","explanation":"Competent 指勝任工作，不能這樣接 watch。"},{"letter":"E","text":"can able to","explanation":"Can able to 混合兩個助動結構。"},{"letter":"F","text":"will watch","explanation":"戲院有場次不代表每個家庭已決定星期六一定去看。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the app launches next month, will fans be able to watch the restored 3D film on their phones?","zh":"下個月應用程式推出後，影迷能否在手機上觀看修復後的3D電影？","upgrade":"After the app launches next month, can fans watch the restored 3D film on their phones?","answer":"can","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"did","explanation":"Did fans watch...? 問過去是否真的看過，與下個月程式推出後可否觀看的問題時態及意思都不合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"can","explanation":"把 will fans be able to watch 自然改成 can fans watch，問的是新程式會否提供觀賞渠道。"},{"letter":"C","text":"can to","explanation":"Can 後接原形 watch，不能寫 can to watch。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have watched","explanation":"這會問影迷是否已經看過，而題句問下個月推出後可否觀看。"},{"letter":"E","text":"must","explanation":"Must fans watch...? 問是否必須觀看，與程式能否提供觀看途徑不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"will watch","explanation":"Will fans watch...? 問影迷將來是否真的會看，未回答程式屆時是否讓他們看。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Could","meaning":"當時可以；有機會","note":"在明確的過去時間敘事中表達當時可觀看的條件；也可有假設義，需靠語境分辨。","collocations":"could watch / see; could then watch; could watch at that time.","example":"At the 2012 festival, visitors could watch the classic in 3D for the first time.","exampleZh":"在2012年的電影節，訪客當時首次可以觀賞該經典電影的3D版本。","contrast":"Could 不保證實際入場；若句子沒有過去時間，也可能被讀成條件假設。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At last year’s film festival, ticket holders were able to watch the restored film in 3D for one evening.","zh":"去年電影節上，持票人士有一晚可以觀看修復後的3D電影。","upgrade":"At last year’s film festival, ticket holders could watch the restored film in 3D for one evening.","answer":"could","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"can","explanation":"Can 是現在形，與去年的明確過去場次不合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"could","explanation":"去年一晚的觀看機會，could watch 表達當時可行。"},{"letter":"C","text":"could to","explanation":"Could 後不加 to。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were required to","explanation":"持票者去年可以觀看，沒有說他們被要求必須進場。"},{"letter":"E","text":"watched","explanation":"有觀看機會不等於每人已看；直接替換還會形成不合語法的 watched watch。"},{"letter":"F","text":"will be able","explanation":"Will be able 指未來，與去年相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the school lent out 3D headsets in 2019, pupils were able to watch the short film at home while the cinema was closed.","zh":"2019年戲院關閉期間，學校借出3D頭戴式裝置，學生因此可以在家觀看短片。","upgrade":"When the school lent out 3D headsets in 2019, pupils could watch the short film at home while the cinema was closed.","answer":"could","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"could","explanation":"2019年借到頭戴式裝置，學生當時可在家觀看；could watch 表過去的可行性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"can to","explanation":"Can to 形式錯，且沒有過去時標。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were expected to","explanation":"學校借出裝置讓學生可在家看，並未要求或預期所有學生都一定觀看。"},{"letter":"D","text":"will watch","explanation":"Will watch 說一定將來會看，與過去可行性不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"saw","explanation":"借出裝置不證實每人真的看了；直接替換還會形成不合語法的 saw watch。"},{"letter":"F","text":"could able to","explanation":"Could able to 混合兩個結構。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Have The Opportunity To","meaning":"有機會去","note":"明確指出某個場次或安排給觀眾觀看機會；比 can 更突出機會的來源。","collocations":"have the opportunity to watch / see; give fans the opportunity to attend.","example":"At the festival, pupils had the opportunity to watch a classic on a large 3D screen.","exampleZh":"在電影節，學生有機會在大型3D銀幕觀看一部經典電影。","contrast":"有機會不等於已觀看；後面接 to + 動詞原形。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school reserved seats at a special screening, so pupils were able to watch the 3D film if they wished.","zh":"學校在特別場預留座位，學生如願意就有機會觀看該3D電影。","upgrade":"The school reserved seats at a special screening, so pupils had the opportunity to watch the 3D film if they wished.","answer":"had the opportunity to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were going to","explanation":"預留座位讓學生可選擇，但 if they wished 不表示他們已計劃一定去看。"},{"letter":"B","text":"had the opportunity to","explanation":"學校預留座位提供機會，且不聲稱每個學生都去看。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were expected to","explanation":"學校預留座位供自願觀看；if they wished 不表示校方期望每人都去看。"},{"letter":"D","text":"could not","explanation":"學校已預留座位供自願觀看，說學生 could not watch 與條件相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were forced to","explanation":"Were forced to 說被迫，與可自行決定相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"had the capacity to","explanation":"Capacity 偏個人承受或執行能力；學校預留的座位給的是這次場次的機會。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Festival visitors were able to see the animated classic on a large 3D screen, although some chose another film.","zh":"電影節觀眾有機會在大型3D銀幕觀看該動畫經典，但有些人選了另一部電影。","upgrade":"Festival visitors had the opportunity to see the animated classic on a large 3D screen, although some chose another film.","answer":"had the opportunity to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"had planned to","explanation":"觀眾有機會但部分改選另一片，原句未說所有人事前已打算看這一部。"},{"letter":"B","text":"had the opportunity to","explanation":"明言有觀賞機會，同時容許有些人沒有採用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were required to","explanation":"Were required to 指必須觀看，與可選另一部相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were competent to","explanation":"Were competent to 說技能，非電影節機會。"},{"letter":"E","text":"had the capacity to","explanation":"Capacity 指個人能力或承受力，電影節只是提供可選的觀影機會。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were scheduled to","explanation":"訪客可選另一部影片，不表示每個人都已被安排觀看這部動畫。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Get The Chance To","meaning":"得到機會去（口語）","note":"較口語地說人獲得一次可能較難得的觀賞機會；若是過去時用 got。","collocations":"get the chance to watch; got the chance to see; finally get a chance to.","example":"Fans got the chance to see the remastered film at the one-night event.","exampleZh":"影迷在只辦一晚的活動得到機會觀看重新製作的電影。","contrast":"Chance 在此是機會，不是運氣或機率；也不保證影迷真的到場。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After years without a local 3D screening, fans were able to watch the restored classic at a one-night event.","zh":"多年來本地沒有3D場次，影迷終於在只辦一晚的活動有機會看修復後的經典電影。","upgrade":"After years without a local 3D screening, fans got the chance to watch the restored classic at a one-night event.","answer":"got the chance to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"got lucky to","explanation":"Got lucky to 口語且語法彆扭，也未準確說明場次機會。"},{"letter":"B","text":"got the chance to","explanation":"久候後終有一晚可看，口語 got the chance to 貼切。"},{"letter":"C","text":"had access to","explanation":"多年來本地沒有 3D 場次，這次是難得的一晚機會，不表示有持續觀看渠道。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were made to","explanation":"Were made to 表示被迫，原句沒有。"},{"letter":"E","text":"planned to","explanation":"一晚特別場次給影迷機會，但不表示每位影迷已訂下觀影計劃。"},{"letter":"F","text":"got the chance of watch","explanation":"Got the chance of watch 介詞結構錯，應 chance to watch。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During a family trip abroad, Lara was able to watch the 3D version she had missed when it bypassed cinemas in her hometown.","zh":"拉娜與家人到外地旅行時，終於有機會看那部未曾在她家鄉戲院放映的3D版本。","upgrade":"During a family trip abroad, Lara got the chance to watch the 3D version she had missed when it bypassed cinemas in her hometown.","answer":"got the chance to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"got the chance to","explanation":"拉娜在旅行時終於能補看家鄉錯過的版本，口語說 got the chance to watch 自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"got a skill to","explanation":"去外地看電影是得到機會，並非習得一項看3D電影的技能。"},{"letter":"C","text":"had access to","explanation":"外地旅行提供這一次補看機會；access to 需要把後面改成影片名詞，而且偏向渠道而非她的難得經歷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"planned to","explanation":"旅行帶來補看機會，但原句未說拉娜在出發前已作了觀影計劃。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was obliged to","explanation":"拉娜沒有被迫觀看；她只是碰上可以補看的機會。"},{"letter":"F","text":"got chances of","explanation":"Got chances of 不能自然接 watch；機會片語是 got the chance to watch。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Have Access To","meaning":"有渠道觀看／取得","note":"需把句子改寫成觀眾可透過合法場地、服務或設備取得影片；重點由個人的可行行動轉到觀看渠道。","collocations":"have access to films / a streaming library / 3D screenings.","example":"Members have access to the film through the library’s licensed streaming service.","exampleZh":"會員可透過圖書館的授權串流服務觀看該電影。","contrast":"這是有條件的視角轉換；access to a film 不保證每人已看，也不表示內容容易理解。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Through the library’s licensed streaming service, members are able to watch archived 3D films at home.","zh":"會員可透過圖書館的授權串流服務，在家觀看館藏3D電影。","upgrade":"Through the library’s licensed streaming service, members have access to archived 3D films at home.","answer":"have access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have access to","explanation":"有授權串流渠道，改成 have access to 保留可觀看的實際條件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"have permission to","explanation":"句尾已是影片名詞，permission to 後應接動詞如 watch；即使獲准，單有許可仍未保證有圖書館串流片源。"},{"letter":"C","text":"are competent in","explanation":"Are competent in 說技能，且不能自然接電影。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have watched already","explanation":"Have watched already 說已看過，原句只是可以看。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have access for","explanation":"接影片名詞時說 have access to archived 3D films；for 不能在此替代 to。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have no access to","explanation":"會員可經授權服務觀看，所以 have no access to archived films 與事實相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"With a ticket to the museum’s 3D screening, visitors are able to watch the film on the large screen.","zh":"持有博物館3D放映場門票的訪客，可以在大銀幕觀看該電影。","upgrade":"With a ticket to the museum’s 3D screening, visitors have access to the film on the large screen.","answer":"have access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have access to","explanation":"門票提供明確觀看渠道，have access to 在這個條件下成立。"},{"letter":"B","text":"have access for","explanation":"門票提供觀看渠道，但片語須說 have access to the film，不能用 for 接影片。"},{"letter":"C","text":"have already viewed","explanation":"Have already viewed 說已看完，原句沒說。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have talent for","explanation":"Talent for 說天分，與門票無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have no access to","explanation":"Have no access to 會說無法觀看，與持票相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have a subscription to","explanation":"一張博物館場次門票提供當次觀看渠道，並不等於訂閱了影片服務。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"capable / competent：技能誤讀","zh":"Capable 可說某人有能力完成難事，competent 說達到工作標準；影迷看3D電影只是有放映機會，不是在受技能評核。","point":"The source concerns availability, not a test of personal competence."},{"word":"can：可能與准許","zh":"Can 可說「能夠」，也可說「獲准」。本課須靠放映、門票、設備等語境判斷可行性；有票可看不等於已實際看了。","point":"Can may express possibility or permission; context identifies the intended reading."},{"word":"could：過去與假設","zh":"Could watch 可指過去有機會，亦可指假設；不能不檢查時間就把源句當成現在或未來。","point":"Could can be past opportunity or hypothetical possibility, so the tense context matters."},{"word":"opportunity / actual viewing：機會不等於結果","zh":"Had the opportunity to watch 說有機會，並不保證影迷真的入場。若句子說 watched，那是已發生的觀看，意思較強。","point":"Having an opportunity does not assert that the person took it."},{"word":"access / accessible：可取得與易明白","zh":"Have access to films 要有合法播放服務、放映場或設備等具體渠道；accessible 也可能指內容容易理解。源句講可觀看3D版本，不是電影容易理解。","point":"Access needs a resource/channel; accessible may mean obtainable or comprehensible in other contexts."},{"word":"can + 原形 / able to + 原形","zh":"Can watch 後不加 to；be able to watch 必須有 to。Can able to watch 把兩種結構錯誤地疊在一起。","point":"Can takes the base verb; able takes to plus the base verb."}],"moduleNumber":4},{"id":"lesson-005","sourceId":58,"headword":"allow","title":"Allow","titleZh":"允許","subtitle":"允許","description":"原文： 2013 年 DSE 8.1〈Hong Kong Loves Blogs〉說，學生小組想開設班網誌，並希望說服班主任 allow you to do this。Allow 在此是「有權決定的老師准許學生做某事」，不是提供電腦技術使網誌變得可行，也不是容忍某行為已經發生。原句尚未說老師是否答應。","sourceSense":"原文： 2013 年 DSE 8.1〈Hong Kong Loves Blogs〉說，學生小組想開設班網誌，並希望說服班主任 allow you to do this。Allow 在此是「有權決定的老師准許學生做某事」，不是提供電腦技術使網誌變得可行，也不是容忍某行為已經發生。原句尚未說老師是否答應。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["permit","direct/close","Permit someone to do something 與准許相近，語氣稍正式；可用於老師或校規。"],["enable","false for this source","Enable 是使人有能力或條件做到，如提供帳戶或網絡；即使網誌技術已備妥，仍需老師准許。"],["let","direct/close","Let someone do something 是較口語的准許；後面接不帶 to 的動詞原形。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Permit someone to do 是較正式的一般准許；let someone do 是較口語的准許，不加 to。\n- Give someone permission to do 明說許可，可配合口頭或書面同意。\n- Authorise someone to do 用於具正式權限的校方決定或政策。\n- Approve a proposal/post 是審批方案或內容，須改寫受詞；不能寫 approve someone to do。\n- Enable 是提供能力／條件；有技術能力仍可能沒有老師許可。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"permit","meaning":"准許；較正式","note":"有權者允許另一人做某事，可用於班主任決定或明文校規；形式比 let 正式。句法是 permit someone to do something。","collocations":"permit students to start a blog; permit publication; be permitted to post","example":"The teacher permitted the pupils to open a class blog after reviewing their plan.","exampleZh":"老師審閱計劃後，准許學生開設班網誌。","contrast":"Permit 指准許；enable 指提供能力或條件。即使老師提供登入帳號，也不必然表示她准許公開發文。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After reading the class-blog plan, the teacher allowed the pupils to publish their first article.","zh":"老師看過班網誌計劃後，准許學生發佈第一篇文章。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After reading the class-blog plan, the teacher permitted the pupils to publish their first article.","answer":"permitted the pupils to publish their first article","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permitted the pupils to publish their first article","explanation":"老師審閱後作出准許決定，permitted pupils to publish 在語義和句法上都吻合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enabled the pupils to publish their first article","explanation":"enable 只表示提供能力或條件，未必是准許。"},{"letter":"C","text":"permitted the pupils publish their first article","explanation":"permit 後必須接 pupils to publish，此項漏掉 to。"},{"letter":"D","text":"approved the blog plan but withheld permission to publish","explanation":"只批准網誌計劃卻暫不准發佈，不能保留原句已准許第一篇文章的結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"encouraged the pupils to publish their first article","explanation":"encourage 只是鼓勵發佈，不等於老師給予發佈許可。"},{"letter":"F","text":"agreed to consider the pupils’ first article","explanation":"agree to consider 表示願意審閱文章，原句已作出可發佈的決定。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"School rules allow class editors to post articles only after a teacher checks the content.","zh":"校規只准班級編輯在老師審核內容後發佈文章。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"School rules permit class editors to post articles only after a teacher checks the content.","answer":"permit class editors to post articles","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enable class editors to post articles","explanation":"enable 指能力，未準確表達校規的許可條件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"permit class editors post articles","explanation":"permit 後要加 to，不能直接接 post。"},{"letter":"C","text":"permit class editors to post articles","explanation":"校規在審核後准許編輯發文，permit someone to do 正確且語氣適合規則。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ask class editors to draft articles","explanation":"要求編輯先起草文章，不等於校規准許審核後發佈。"},{"letter":"E","text":"recommend that class editors post articles","explanation":"recommend 只是建議發文，校規原句是有條件地准許。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permit class editors to post before a teacher checks the content","explanation":"此項把發文時間改成老師審核前，違反原句的 only after 條件。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"let","meaning":"讓；口語准許","note":"日常對話中說有權者讓某人做某事；let + 人 + 動詞原形，不加 to。若要嚴肅正式的文件，通常選 permit/authorise。","collocations":"let us start the blog; let pupils post; let the class try","example":"“I’ll let you publish the first post after I read it,” the teacher said.","exampleZh":"老師說：「我看過第一篇文章後，就讓你們發佈。」","contrast":"Let 句法與 allow/permit someone to do 不同；make someone do 表強迫，並非准許。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"“I’ll allow you to try a private class blog for a month,” the teacher told us.","zh":"老師告訴我們：「我會讓你們試用一個私人班網誌一個月。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"“I’ll let you try a private class blog for a month,” the teacher told us.","answer":"let you try a private class blog","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"let you to try a private class blog","explanation":"let 後不能加 to，應直接接 try。"},{"letter":"B","text":"make you try a private class blog","explanation":"make 變成強迫你們試用，原話是准許。"},{"letter":"C","text":"encourage you to try a private class blog","explanation":"鼓勵試用不等於已准許試用一個月。"},{"letter":"D","text":"let you try a private class blog","explanation":"口頭對話用 let you try 自然，也保留一個月的試用許可。"},{"letter":"E","text":"agree to review your class-blog idea","explanation":"答應審閱構思仍未決定是否准許試用。"},{"letter":"F","text":"enable you to try a private class blog","explanation":"enable 是提供能力，未必有老師同意。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The teacher allowed parents to comment on the class blog only after a moderator was assigned.","zh":"老師只在安排好版主後，才准許家長在班網誌留言。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The teacher let parents comment on the class blog only after a moderator was assigned.","answer":"let parents comment on the class blog","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"let parents comment on the class blog","explanation":"安排好版主後才准許家長留言；let parents comment 保留這項有條件的許可。"},{"letter":"B","text":"let parents to comment on the class blog","explanation":"let 後接動詞原形，不能寫 let parents to comment。"},{"letter":"C","text":"agree to moderate parents’ comments","explanation":"同意管理家長留言，不等於版主就位後已准許家長留言。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enable parents to comment on the class blog","explanation":"enable 可指提供留言功能，但不表示版主到位後老師給了許可。"},{"letter":"E","text":"make parents comment on the class blog","explanation":"make 意思是強迫家長留言，原句只是版主到位後准許。"},{"letter":"F","text":"approve a moderation plan but keep comments closed","explanation":"批准管理方案但維持關閉留言，與原句准許家長留言不同。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"give permission to","meaning":"給予許可；明說決定","note":"把准許本身說出來，可用於家長同意、老師批准或書面許可。注意 give someone permission to do something，而不是 give permission someone to do。","collocations":"give the class permission to publish; written permission; ask for permission","example":"The teacher gave the class permission to share its first article online.","exampleZh":"老師准許全班把第一篇文章分享到網上。","contrast":"此說法可強調許可是口頭還是書面；approve a plan 審核的是方案，未必逐項准許學生的後續行動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Each parent must allow the class to use their child’s photo in the blog by signing the consent form.","zh":"每位家長須簽署同意書，准許班級在網誌使用其子女的照片。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Each parent must give the class permission to use their child’s photo in the blog by signing the consent form.","answer":"give the class permission to use their child’s photo","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"give the class access to use their child’s photo","explanation":"access 可指技術存取照片，不足以表示家長簽署使用許可。"},{"letter":"B","text":"give the class permission to use their child’s photo","explanation":"同意書明示准許使用照片，give the class permission to use 最精確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approve the page layout but withhold photo consent","explanation":"批准頁面排版卻不准用子女照片，未給原句要求的影像使用許可。"},{"letter":"D","text":"give permission the class to use their child’s photo","explanation":"give permission 後不能直接接 the class，應說 give the class permission。"},{"letter":"E","text":"ask to inspect the photos before deciding on consent","explanation":"要求先看照片只是審核步驟，尚未簽署同意書准許使用。"},{"letter":"F","text":"enable the class to use their child’s photo","explanation":"enable 只表示使能做到，簽同意書在此給的是許可。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In a signed letter, the school allowed the blog team to use the media room after lessons.","zh":"學校在簽署的信件中准許網誌小組放學後使用媒體室。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"In a signed letter, the school gave the blog team permission to use the media room after lessons.","answer":"gave the blog team permission to use the media room","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"made the blog team use the media room","explanation":"made 表示要求或強迫使用，信件只是准許。"},{"letter":"B","text":"agreed to consider the team’s room request","explanation":"答應考慮房間申請，未等於簽署信件已批准使用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"gave permission the blog team to use the media room","explanation":"give permission 的受詞位置錯，應 give the blog team permission。"},{"letter":"D","text":"gave the blog team permission to use the media room","explanation":"簽署信明確授予小組放學後使用場地的許可。"},{"letter":"E","text":"gave the blog team a key to the media room","explanation":"給房間鑰匙只表示能進入，不等於簽署信中的正式准用決定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"recommended the media room to the blog team","explanation":"推薦某房間供小組考慮，不等於校方批准使用。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"authorise","meaning":"正式授權","note":"有正式權限的人或機構在規則、文件或系統權限中准許某人做某事。用於明示校方授權的情境；普通口頭「好，你們試試」用它會太正式。","collocations":"authorise students to manage a blog; authorised users; authorise publication","example":"The school formally authorised the class editors to manage the blog account.","exampleZh":"學校正式授權班級編輯管理網誌帳戶。","contrast":"Authorise 強調具權限者作正式決定；enable 是提供工具或登入能力，未必包含合法或校內許可。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The principal’s signed notice allowed two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account.","zh":"校長簽署的通知正式准許兩名指名學生管理班級的官方網誌帳戶。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The principal’s signed notice authorised two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account.","answer":"authorised two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enabled two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account","explanation":"enable 可指給登入工具，但校長簽署通知表達的是正式權限。"},{"letter":"B","text":"authorised two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account","explanation":"校長有權決定並指名管理者，authorised 明確表達正式授權。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approved their plan but withheld account-management rights","explanation":"批准計劃但不授帳戶管理權，與校長通知中的正式授權不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"invited two named pupils to request management rights","explanation":"邀請提出管理權申請，沒有作出已授權的決定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"required two named pupils to manage the official class-blog account","explanation":"require 表必須管理，通知說的是准許，非命令。"},{"letter":"F","text":"listed two named pupils as possible future managers","explanation":"列為日後可能人選，不等於通知已授權他們管理。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school policy allows only designated student editors to upload posts from the shared account.","zh":"校方政策只准指定學生編輯透過共用帳戶上載文章。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The school policy authorises only designated student editors to upload posts from the shared account.","answer":"authorises only designated student editors to upload posts","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"authorises only designated student editors to upload posts","explanation":"政策界定具正式上載權限的人，authorises 保留指定與許可。"},{"letter":"B","text":"lists only designated student editors as eligible to request upload rights","explanation":"列為可申請人員不等於政策已准許他們上載。"},{"letter":"C","text":"grants only designated student editors access to the upload screen","explanation":"可進入上載畫面是技術存取，未必表示政策准許公開文章。"},{"letter":"D","text":"permits all student editors to upload posts","explanation":"此項容許所有學生編輯，失去原句 only designated 的限制。"},{"letter":"E","text":"allows designated editors to draft posts but not upload them","explanation":"這只准指定編輯起草，卻明說不可上載；原政策准他們從共用帳戶上載。"},{"letter":"F","text":"recommends that designated student editors upload posts","explanation":"建議指定編輯上載文章，與政策規定誰獲准上載不同。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"approve","meaning":"批准方案或內容；須改寫受詞","note":"當老師審閱並同意網誌提案或某篇文章時，可改寫為 approve the proposal/post。不能直接以 approve you to start 代替 allow you to start；批准提案也須在題句明示才成立。","collocations":"approve the blog proposal; approve a post for publication; gain approval","example":"After checking the safety rules, the teacher approved the class-blog proposal.","exampleZh":"老師核對安全規則後，批准了班網誌提案。","contrast":"Approve 的受詞是提案、計劃或內容；allow 的受詞可直接是學生，後接 to 不定式。單是喜歡某篇文章，不等於批准上載。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The class submitted a detailed blog proposal, and the teacher allowed the project to go ahead after reviewing it.","zh":"全班提交詳細的網誌提案；老師審閱後准許計劃推行。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The class submitted a detailed blog proposal; after reviewing it, the teacher approved the plan.","answer":"approved the proposal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"approved the proposal","explanation":"題句明說提交與審閱提案，approve the proposal 是准予推行的合適改寫。"},{"letter":"B","text":"agreed to review the proposal later","explanation":"答應稍後審閱提案，未等於審閱後已批准。"},{"letter":"C","text":"provided resources for the proposal","explanation":"提供資源使提案可行，不代表老師准許推行。"},{"letter":"D","text":"praised the proposal","explanation":"稱讚提案可以只是好評，沒有作出准許推行的決定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"asked questions about the proposal","explanation":"提出問題表示仍在審議，未必已批准。"},{"letter":"F","text":"approved a budget but postponed the blog launch","explanation":"只批出預算卻延期啟動網誌，與原句准許計劃推行不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The teacher read the revised first post and allowed it to be published after the names were removed.","zh":"老師讀過修改後的第一篇文章；刪除姓名後，准許發佈。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The teacher read the revised first post and approved it for publication after the names were removed.","answer":"approved the revised post for publication","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cleared the images but left the text under review","explanation":"只通過圖片而文字仍待審，不能代表刪名後的整篇文章已獲准發佈。"},{"letter":"B","text":"agreed to examine the post again","explanation":"同意再看一次文章，未等於准許修改版公開。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approved the revised post for publication","explanation":"老師讀過並准許特定文章發佈，approve the revised post for publication 準確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"asked for another revision before publication","explanation":"要求再次修改表示暫未准許此版本發佈。"},{"letter":"E","text":"praised the post but withheld publication approval","explanation":"稱讚文章但暫不准公開，失去原句的發佈許可。"},{"letter":"F","text":"approved an earlier draft but not the revision","explanation":"批准早前版本而非刪名後的修改版，對象不一致。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Enable / make possible · 有能力不等於有許可","zh":"中文辨析： 學校開帳號、提供 Wi-Fi 或教學生編輯網頁，可以 enable 學生開網誌；班主任仍可能不准許公開發佈。原文問的是教師是否批准。","point":"Technical ability and permission are separate."},{"word":"Let us to / permit us start · 不定式句法","zh":"中文辨析： Let us start 不帶 to；permit us to start 要 to。兩者都是可能的准許用語，但形式不能互換。","point":"Let takes a bare infinitive; permit takes a to-infinitive."},{"word":"Approve / agree / support · 支持與正式准許","zh":"中文辨析： 老師支持網誌想法未必已准許開始；approve 通常接提案或文章；agree to 可表示同意某請求，但不能把 agree us to start 當標準句法。","point":"Favouring an idea is not automatically granting permission to act."},{"word":"Authorise / license · 正式權力的範圍","zh":"中文辨析： 有校方正式授權時可用 authorise；license 常涉及法定牌照或權利，班網誌一般無需推斷取得牌照。","point":"School approval does not imply a legal licence."},{"word":"Require / make / force · 命令不等於准許","zh":"中文辨析： Require/make/force 表學生必須做；原文是學生希望老師允許，完全沒有說老師命令他們開網誌。","point":"Permission leaves a choice; an obligation does not."}],"moduleNumber":5},{"id":"lesson-006","sourceId":50,"headword":"agree","title":"Agree","titleZh":"同意某種看法","subtitle":"同意某種看法","description":"The 2023 individual question asks, “Do you agree that meat is essential in Chinese cuisine?” Here agree means accepting or sharing a view about cuisine. A student may agree, disagree or qualify the claim. The question neither grants permission nor treats the claim as established fact.","sourceSense":"The 2023 individual question asks, “Do you agree that meat is essential in Chinese cuisine?” Here agree means accepting or sharing a view about cuisine. A student may agree, disagree or qualify the claim. The question neither grants permission nor treats the claim as established fact.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["concur","Formal verb for sharing a judgment or conclusion. It can take that or with someone, but sounds more formal than conversational agree."],["be of the same opinion","Good contextual paraphrase when two named people hold the same view; requires a grammatical recast, often be of the same opinion as X."],["consent","False for this source sense: consent means give permission or assent to an action or arrangement, not simply think a proposition about cuisine is true."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Share the view that is a natural direct recast of agree that in opinion questions. Concur is the formal verb; be of the same opinion makes the other opinion holder explicit. Think so too is a conversational reply but depends on a preceding statement and largely duplicates the shared-opinion route. Accept the claim may suggest reluctant acknowledgement and is not always mutual agreement. Approve evaluates a plan rather than endorsing a factual proposition; consent concerns permission."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["concur","正式報告或會議中，兩個判斷一致。","不等於准許、服從或勉強讓步。"],["share the view","認同或否定一項 that 引出的主張。","主張仍可有爭議，不是已證實或獲批准。"],["be of the same opinion","明說兩人對同一問題看法相同，常用 as/about。","意見相同不等於口味完全相同或互相授權。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 原題 agree that 是問你是否認同一項主張，可改為 share the view that；正式記錄多人的一致判斷，可用 concur that/with；若重點是「我與某人看法相同」，用 be of the same opinion as。Consent 是給許可，comply 是照做，都不能代替此處的「認同看法」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"concur","meaning":"意見一致（較正式）","note":"正式表示與某結論或判斷一致；可用 concur that 接完整句子，或 concur with 某人。","collocations":"concur that a proposal is sound; concur with a reviewer; concur in a decision.","example":"After reading both menus, the two reviewers concurred that the vegetarian option was suitable for the event.","exampleZh":"看過兩份菜單後，兩名評論員一致認為素食選項適合該活動。","contrast":"Concur 較正式，重點是判斷相同；comply 是照做，consent 是准許，不可混淆。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After separately reviewing the survey, both examiners agree that the figures do not support the claim, and their joint report records that shared judgment.","zh":"兩名考官分別審閱調查後，都認為數字不支持該主張，並在聯合報告記下這項共同判斷。","upgrade":"After separately reviewing the survey, both examiners concur that the figures do not support the claim, and their joint report records that shared judgment.","answer":"concur","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consent","explanation":"考官是在判斷數據是否支持主張，沒有准許他人做某事。"},{"letter":"B","text":"comply","explanation":"報告記下兩人看法一致，不是他們服從指示。"},{"letter":"C","text":"concede","explanation":"Concede 常指勉強承認對方一點；題目只說兩人獨立得出同一判斷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"concur","explanation":"Concur that 正式表示兩名考官對數據的結論一致，符合聯合報告語境。"},{"letter":"E","text":"approve","explanation":"他們沒有批准一項計劃，反而判定數據不支持某主張。"},{"letter":"F","text":"speculate","explanation":"兩人已檢視數字並作共同判斷，不是沒有根據地猜測。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the site inspection, the architect agreed with the engineer's assessment that the cracked railing was unsafe, having checked the measurements independently.","zh":"現場檢查時，建築師自行核對量度數據後，認同工程師對裂開欄杆並不安全的評估。","upgrade":"During the site inspection, the architect concurred with the engineer's assessment that the cracked railing was unsafe, having checked the measurements independently.","answer":"concurred","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"concurred","explanation":"Concurred with the assessment 正式表示建築師核對數據後與工程師的安全判斷一致。"},{"letter":"B","text":"consented","explanation":"建築師是在判斷欄杆安全，並非准許工程師採取行動；consented with 也不合此處搭配。"},{"letter":"C","text":"complied","explanation":"他並非遵從工程師指示，而是獨立核對數據後得出相同結論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"conceded","explanation":"沒有爭辯或勉強讓步的線索；conceded with the assessment 也不合搭配。"},{"letter":"E","text":"authorised","explanation":"句子未說建築師批准更換欄杆，只說他認同安全評估。"},{"letter":"F","text":"dissented","explanation":"Dissented 表不同意，與他核對數據後認同工程師的敘述相反。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"share the view","meaning":"持相同看法","note":"明確指出自己同意一項看法，常用 share the view that + 完整句子；適合由 agree that 改寫。","collocations":"share the view that; share someone's view on a proposal; do not share that view.","example":"I share the view that school menus should offer a choice of vegetarian dishes.","exampleZh":"我同意學校餐單應提供素食菜式選擇這個看法。","contrast":"這片語承認是某種觀點，不代表觀點已被證實，也不等於批准執行某項計劃。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Do you agree that the school can serve traditional dishes without meat, or do you think meat is indispensable to every dish?","zh":"你是否認同學校可以供應不含肉類的傳統菜式，還是認為每道菜都非有肉不可？","upgrade":"Do you share the view that the school can serve traditional dishes without meat, or do you think meat is indispensable to every dish?","answer":"share the view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consent","explanation":"問題要你表達對菜式主張的看法，不是問你會否准許別人做事。"},{"letter":"B","text":"share the view","explanation":"Share the view that 自然承接完整主張，仍讓答者認同或反對。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approve the menu","explanation":"題目沒有要求批准某一份實際餐單，只問傳統菜式能否無肉。"},{"letter":"D","text":"comply with the rule","explanation":"句子沒有須遵守的規則，只有待討論的飲食觀點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"accept as proven","explanation":"題目開放討論，沒有說「可無肉」已經被證實。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permit the claim","explanation":"認同主張不等於准許某人發表主張。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"I do not agree that every Chinese banquet must include pork; I think a vegetarian banquet can still honour tradition.","zh":"我不認同每席中式宴會都一定要有豬肉；我認為素宴也可以尊重傳統。","upgrade":"I do not share the view that every Chinese banquet must include pork; I think a vegetarian banquet can still honour tradition.","answer":"share the view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consent","explanation":"Do not consent that 不合此處用法，也把看法錯寫成准許。"},{"letter":"B","text":"obey the claim","explanation":"一項宴會主張不是可「服從」的指令。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approve","explanation":"Approve that 在此不自然；我否定的是「每席都要豬肉」的主張，不是審批餐單。"},{"letter":"D","text":"concede","explanation":"我沒有勉強承認對方正確，而是明確表示不認同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"share the view","explanation":"Do not share the view that 保留否定立場和後面完整主張。"},{"letter":"F","text":"authorise","explanation":"我並非決定誰可製作宴會，而是在說個人看法。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"be of the same opinion","meaning":"意見相同","note":"說兩名或以上人士對同一問題看法一致；通常須指出與誰一致或雙方各持甚麼觀點。","collocations":"be of the same opinion as a colleague; be of the same opinion about a question.","example":"Mei and her brother are of the same opinion about the new menu: both want a meat-free option.","exampleZh":"美和哥哥對新餐單意見相同：兩人都希望有不含肉類的選項。","contrast":"這是人與人意見一致，不表示其中一人給另一人許可；改寫要調整主語及 as/about 的搭配。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Mei and her brother agree about the canteen proposal: both want a vegetarian option each day, although they prefer different dishes.","zh":"美和哥哥對飯堂建議意見一致：兩人都希望每天有素食選項，儘管各自喜歡的菜式不同。","upgrade":"Mei and her brother are of the same opinion about the canteen proposal: both want a vegetarian option each day, although they prefer different dishes.","answer":"are of the same opinion","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"are of different opinions","explanation":"兩人都想每天有素食選項，對建議的看法相同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"consent to each other's meals","explanation":"他們沒有互相批准對方吃甚麼，而是持相同政策看法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"are of the same opinion","explanation":"Are of the same opinion about 把兩人的共同主張說清楚，仍容許他們愛吃不同菜。"},{"letter":"D","text":"make the same food choice","explanation":"題目反說兩人喜歡不同菜，意見一致不等於選同一道菜。"},{"letter":"E","text":"follow the same rule","explanation":"飯堂建議尚在討論，沒有一條兩人都須遵守的規則。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have the same taste in dishes","explanation":"他們對每日素食選項看法一致，但口味明說不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"I agree with the chef about the tasting menu: both of us think the plant-based dish should be offered, but neither of us has authority to approve it.","zh":"我和廚師對試食餐單看法一致：我們都認為應供應植物製菜式，但我們都沒有權批准餐單。","upgrade":"I am of the same opinion as the chef about the tasting menu: both of us think the plant-based dish should be offered, but neither of us has authority to approve it.","answer":"am of the same opinion as the chef","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consent to the chef's action","explanation":"兩人只發表餐單看法，並非我准許廚師採取行動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"comply with the chef's order","explanation":"廚師沒有下指令，我也沒有表示會照做。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approve the chef's menu","explanation":"題目明說我們都無權批准餐單。"},{"letter":"D","text":"am of the same opinion as the chef","explanation":"Of the same opinion as 保留我與廚師對植物製菜式的共同看法，不加上批准權。"},{"letter":"E","text":"concede to the chef","explanation":"沒有爭辯或勉強讓步；兩人本來都持同一看法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"share the chef's authority","explanation":"句子特意說兩人都沒有批准權，談的是意見不是權限。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"consent / agree with a view","zh":"中文辨析： Consent to 是同意某人做某事或准許某安排；來源問是否認同一句關於菜式的主張。","point":"Agreeing that a dish needs meat is not giving anyone permission to cook it."},{"word":"comply / concur","zh":"中文辨析： Comply with 表遵守指示，即使本人不同意其理由也可照做；concur 是判斷一致。","point":"Following a rule does not prove one shares its rationale."},{"word":"approve / share the view","zh":"中文辨析： 批准一個餐單方案是行動決定；認同「餐單應提供素食」是一項看法。","point":"Approving a plan and endorsing a proposition are different acts."},{"word":"factual agreement / permission","zh":"中文辨析： Agree that 後接陳述句，判斷真假或合理性；agree to 常接安排或要求，語法及意思均可能不同。","point":"Agree that the menu is varied; agree to print the menu."},{"word":"question / fact","zh":"中文辨析： 原題「你是否同意？」容許不同答案，不等於來源已斷言肉類在中菜中不可缺少。","point":"Asking for an opinion does not certify the claim."}],"moduleNumber":6},{"id":"lesson-007","sourceId":61,"headword":"although","title":"Although","titleZh":"雖然；讓步對照","subtitle":"雖然；讓步對照","description":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，3.3 的日本食品裝飾活動介紹說：「Most are simple enough to master in seconds, although a handful will challenge your skills.」前句說大部分裝飾容易掌握，後句指出少數仍具難度。Although 在此連接兩個事實，表示「雖然大多容易，仍有幾種較難」；它不表示時間先後，也不推翻前句。原卷前文提到廚師會示範六十多種裝飾；這裏的 most 指那些裝飾方法。以下例句及練習均為原創。來源：[2012 DSE English Paper 4, set 3.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，3.3 的日本食品裝飾活動介紹說：「Most are simple enough to master in seconds, although a handful will challenge your skills.」前句說大部分裝飾容易掌握，後句指出少數仍具難度。Although 在此連接兩個事實，表示「雖然大多容易，仍有幾種較難」；它不表示時間先後，也不推翻前句。原卷前文提到廚師會示範六十多種裝飾；這裏的 most 指那些裝飾方法。以下例句及練習均為原創。來源：[2012 DSE English Paper 4, set 3.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","此處的界線"],"rows":[["though","直接，較口語","可接完整子句；句末 though 是另一種位置，改寫時須重排。"],["even though","語境可用，語氣較強","強調反差出乎意料；原文未必需要這麼強的讓步。"],["while","語境可用","While 可表示對照，也可表示「當……時」；兩個分句要清楚呈現對比。"]],"note":"擴展候選與遺漏挑戰： Whereas 適合平衡比較兩組事物；despite the fact that 保留完整子句但需重排；however 需另起獨立分句及標點；but 可連接兩個主要分句，是原文非常常用的簡潔改寫。Nevertheless/nonetheless 亦可用句間改寫，但與 however 在本課同屬相近的獨立轉折副詞。Yet 可作並列連詞，帶較強「儘管如此仍」的語氣；這裏的重點只是多數和少數的差別，與 but 的基本機制重疊，故沒有再增一整組練習。Despite/in spite of 後接名詞或 `-ing`，不能直接接 `a handful will challenge...`；其合法名詞化改寫在易混淆詞中說明。Even if 是假設，非這裏已知事實；because 是原因。沒有把這些形式一概稱為錯詞。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Though 近於一般 although；even though 強調明顯的意外反差。\n- While/whereas 可把兩組事物對照；while 亦有時間義，whereas 專注比較。\n- Despite the fact that 保留完整事實子句但較正式；單獨 despite 後不能直接放限定子句。\n- However 須另起句或用分號；because 是原因，even if 是假設，均不可把原文的已知反差說成另一種關係。\n- But 可直接連接兩個主要分句，適合「多數容易，但少數困難」的簡潔改寫；yet 亦可表示轉折，但通常更強調出乎意料的結果。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"though","meaning":"雖然；較輕的讓步","note":"Though + 完整子句 可在句首或句中引出與主句相反的事實。語氣一般比 even though 輕，口語及書面語均常見。","collocations":"though most are easy; though it looks simple; difficult, though not impossible","example":"Though most paper flowers are quick to fold, the final design takes patience.","exampleZh":"雖然大部分紙花很快就能摺好，最後一款設計卻需要耐心。","contrast":"Though 可近換原文的 although；even though 會更刻意強調意外反差。句尾 The design is difficult, though 可用，但須改動原句結構。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although most of the paper flowers were easy to fold, the smallest one needed a delicate final twist.","zh":"雖然大部分紙花容易摺好，最小的一朵最後仍需要細緻地扭轉。","upgrade":"Though most of the paper flowers were easy to fold, the smallest one needed a delicate final twist.","answer":"Though most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Because most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"容易摺並不是最小那朵需要細緻扭轉的原因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Though most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"讓步承認大部分容易，同時保留最小一朵較難的對照。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Even if most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"題句已確定大部分容易，沒有把這件事當假設條件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"During most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"during 後不能接這個完整子句，也把對照誤作時間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Therefore most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"therefore 表結果，無法引出後面的困難例外。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Unless most of the paper flowers were easy to fold","explanation":"unless 表「除非」，題句不是附條件才需要扭轉。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The beginner finished the first garnish quickly, although her final design still looked uneven.","zh":"這名初學者很快完成第一款裝飾，雖然她最後的設計看起來仍不平均。","upgrade":"The beginner finished the first garnish quickly, though her final design still looked uneven.","answer":"though her final design still looked uneven","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"because her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"不平均不能合理解釋她為何很快完成，原句只把速度與成果對照。"},{"letter":"B","text":"if her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"她的成品已經看起來不平均，不是未確定的條件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"until her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"until 說等到某時，不表示速度與品質的反差。"},{"letter":"D","text":"though her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"保留「完成得快但成果欠平整」的輕度讓步。"},{"letter":"E","text":"so her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"so 說快完成導致不平均；原句沒有主張因果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as soon as her final design still looked uneven","explanation":"as soon as 表時間先後，與成品品質的對照無關。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"even though","meaning":"儘管；強調反差","note":"兩個已知事實之間的反差令人意外時，可用 even though 加強讓步。後面接陳述事實的完整子句。","collocations":"even though the lesson is short; even though most are simple; even though she practised","example":"Even though Leo had practised the knot all week, he still needed help with the final loop.","exampleZh":"儘管利奧整星期都在練習打結，最後一個繩圈仍要別人協助。","contrast":"Even though 講已發生或已知的事；even if 偏向假設條件。原文只需一般讓步，若練習明說預期本應容易，強調式便更貼切。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times, I still could not make the final corner hold.","zh":"儘管廚師已示範摺疊技巧三次，我仍無法令最後一角固定。","upgrade":"Even though the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times, I still could not make the final corner hold.","answer":"Even though the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Even though the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"示範三次本應有助成功，仍做不到的意外反差適合強調式讓步。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Even if the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"示範三次是已知事實，不需改作假設。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Once the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"once 只交代示範之後，沒有「理應會做卻不會」的語氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Since the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"since 在這裏易讀成原因，不能解釋示範後仍失敗。"},{"letter":"E","text":"In case the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"in case 用於預備可能發生的事，示範已發生。"},{"letter":"F","text":"As long as the chef had demonstrated the folding technique three times","explanation":"as long as 是充分條件，與仍做不到的結果矛盾。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners, nearly half the class needed an expert to finish the first one.","zh":"儘管套裝聲稱每款圖案都適合初學者，班上接近一半的人連第一款也要專家協助完成。","upgrade":"Even though the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners, nearly half the class needed an expert to finish the first one.","answer":"Even though the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Provided that the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"provided that 設條件，不能表達宣傳與實際難度的落差。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Because the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"包裝聲稱容易不是半班需要專家協助的原因。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Even though the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"明示包裝承諾與實際情況大相逕庭，強調反差恰當。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Whenever the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"whenever 說每逢某時，宣傳不是反覆發生的時間點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Only if the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"only if 會把宣傳變成求助的必要條件，與句意不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Until the kit claimed that every pattern was suitable for beginners","explanation":"until 表截止時間，不能說明為何一開始就困難。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"while","meaning":"雖然／而；對照兩面","note":"While 可把兩個同時成立的情況相對照：一部分容易，另一部分困難。若兩句主語或性質有明顯對比，就不易誤解為「正在……的時候」。","collocations":"while most are easy, a few are hard; while one design is simple, another is intricate","example":"While the first two decorations are simple, the sugar sculpture takes an hour.","exampleZh":"前兩款裝飾雖然簡單，糖雕卻要花一小時。","contrast":"While 同時有時間義；whereas 只用於對照。本課句中若說 while she was cutting vegetables，那是時間，不是讓步。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although the flat flower needs only three folds, the layered flower requires careful cutting and glue.","zh":"扁平紙花雖然只需摺三次，分層紙花卻需要仔細剪裁及黏貼。","upgrade":"While the flat flower needs only three folds, the layered flower requires careful cutting and glue.","answer":"While the flat flower needs only three folds","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"While the flat flower needs only three folds","explanation":"兩款紙花需求不同，while 清楚對比簡單摺疊與細緻剪貼。"},{"letter":"B","text":"While the flat flower is being folded","explanation":"變成摺花期間做另一款，原句比較的是難度而非同時進行。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Because the flat flower needs only three folds","explanation":"第一款簡單不是第二款需要剪貼的原因。"},{"letter":"D","text":"If the flat flower needs only three folds","explanation":"第一款的做法已確定，不是假設第二款做法的條件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"After the flat flower needs only three folds","explanation":"after 表時間，且不自然地接「需要三摺」這種狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"So that the flat flower needs only three folds","explanation":"so that 表目的；第二款的工序不是為了令第一款簡單。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes, the advanced group spent an hour on the decorative edge.","zh":"大多數初學者數分鐘便掌握基本壽司卷，但進階組在裝飾邊緣上花了一小時。","upgrade":"While most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes, the advanced group spent an hour on the decorative edge.","answer":"While most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"As soon as most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"as soon as 把兩組情況說成先後，而非難度差異。"},{"letter":"B","text":"In case most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"in case 指防備某可能情況，不符合已觀察到的學習結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Since most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"since 易形成原因關係；初學者學得快未令進階組花更長時間。"},{"letter":"D","text":"While most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"while 平衡對照兩組不同任務所花的時間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Until most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"until 表等待到某時，與兩組學習時間比較無關。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Provided that most beginners mastered the basic roll in minutes","explanation":"provided that 設先決條件；進階組用一小時不以初學者速度為條件。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"whereas","meaning":"而；兩組差異","note":"Whereas 對比兩個群組、方法或屬性，常用於較清晰、平衡的比較。它不是單純加強意外程度；重點是 A 與 B 不同。","collocations":"most ... whereas a few ...; the basic pattern ..., whereas the advanced pattern ...","example":"Most garnishes take seconds to learn, whereas the carved swan requires an afternoon.","exampleZh":"大部分食物裝飾幾秒便學會，而雕刻天鵝卻要花一個下午。","contrast":"Whereas 很適合明示兩群的差別；although 可只表示主句出乎預料，未必是平衡對照。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Most of the chef's garnishes are simple enough to learn in seconds, although a handful involve carving and take much longer.","zh":"廚師的大多數食物裝飾幾秒便學會，但其中少數需要雕刻，花的時間長得多。","upgrade":"Most of the chef's garnishes are simple enough to learn in seconds, whereas a handful involve carving and take much longer.","answer":"whereas a handful involve carving and take much longer","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"because a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"難做的少數不是大多數易學的成因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"if a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"少數需要雕刻是既定情況，無須改成假設。"},{"letter":"C","text":"after a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"after 表時間先後，沒有比較兩組裝飾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in case a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"in case 表預防可能情況，這裏是在分類已有裝飾。"},{"letter":"E","text":"whereas a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"把多數易學與少數費時兩組平衡對照。"},{"letter":"F","text":"so that a handful involve carving and take much longer","explanation":"so that 表目的，易學的多數不是為了令少數更難。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds, the live workshop teaches slow, precise knife work.","zh":"影片課程雖然以快捷的基本摺法為主，現場工作坊卻教授緩慢而精準的刀工。","upgrade":"Whereas the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds, the live workshop teaches slow, precise knife work.","answer":"Whereas the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Whereas the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"兩種課程各有不同重點，whereas 以比較而非時間關係連接。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Even if the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"影片內容已知，不是假設現場課程可能如何。"},{"letter":"C","text":"When the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"會令人以為現場課程恰在影片播放時教刀工。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Therefore the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"therefore 說現場刀工令影片聚焦基本摺法，既次序不合也無因果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"In order that the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"in order that 表目的；現場課程不是為了控制影片重點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Until the video lesson focuses on quick basic folds","explanation":"until 說時間截止，並非兩種教學內容的對比。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"despite the fact that","meaning":"儘管有這個事實","note":"這個較長、較正式的結構後接 that + 完整子句；可用在要突出一項已知事實卻仍有相反結果時。它常需移動分句以保持自然。","collocations":"despite the fact that most are easy; despite the fact that she practised; succeed despite the fact that...","example":"Despite the fact that the instructions were brief, the volunteers assembled the display correctly.","exampleZh":"儘管說明簡短，義工仍正確組裝了展品。","contrast":"Despite 單獨後接名詞或動名詞；despite the fact that 才可接完整子句。它比 although 冗長，口語通常選短形式。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although the recipe contained only four ingredients, preparing the garnish took the whole afternoon.","zh":"雖然食譜只列出四種材料，製作食物裝飾卻花了一整個下午。","upgrade":"Despite the fact that the recipe contained only four ingredients, preparing the garnish took the whole afternoon.","answer":"Despite the fact that the recipe contained only four ingredients","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Despite the recipe contained only four ingredients","explanation":"despite 不能直接接「食譜只含四項」這個完整子句。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Because of the fact that the recipe contained only four ingredients","explanation":"雖合句法，卻把材料少說成耗一下午的原因；原句說反差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Despite the fact that the recipe contained only four ingredients","explanation":"保留完整事實子句及「材料少但耗時長」的正式讓步。"},{"letter":"D","text":"In spite the fact that the recipe contained only four ingredients","explanation":"固定說法需 in spite of the fact that，缺 of。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Owing to the recipe containing only four ingredients","explanation":"owing to 引原因；材料少不是題句宣稱的耗時成因。"},{"letter":"F","text":"In case the recipe contained only four ingredients","explanation":"in case 表預備或假設，與已知的四項材料不符。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The visitors admired the finished display, although several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked.","zh":"參觀者欣賞完成的展品，雖然其中幾個紙製人偶仍有點歪斜。","upgrade":"The visitors admired the finished display, despite the fact that several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked.","answer":"despite the fact that several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"because of the fact that several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"不平整並非觀眾欣賞的原因，會倒轉原文的讓步關係。"},{"letter":"B","text":"despite several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"despite 後不能直接接 figures were 這種限定子句。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unless several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"unless 令歪斜變成欣賞的條件，與原句相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"despite the fact that several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"參觀者欣賞展品這件事與局部瑕疵並存，保留正式讓步。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in spite several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"固定結構需 in spite of，且完整子句須加 the fact that。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as a result of several of its paper figures were still slightly crooked","explanation":"as a result of 引因果，亦不能直接接這個限定子句。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"however","meaning":"然而；另起分句","note":"However 是連接副詞；可把原來的兩個分句寫成兩句，或用分號接續。它不能單獨像 although 一樣在同一句中引出從屬子句。","collocations":"Most are simple. However, a few are difficult.; Most are simple; however, a few require practice.","example":"The first pattern took five minutes. However, the final one required careful measuring.","exampleZh":"第一款圖案只花了五分鐘。然而，最後一款需要仔細量度。","contrast":"However 需要句界或分號及適當逗號；but 是並列連詞，通常在同一句連接兩個主要分句。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although the first pattern looked easy, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","zh":"雖然第一款圖案看起來容易，最後一個繩結仍花了我十五分鐘才打好。","upgrade":"The first pattern looked easy; however, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","answer":"The first pattern looked easy; however, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"The first pattern looked easy, however the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"單用逗號連兩個獨立分句屬逗號拼接錯誤；however 須另起句或用分號。"},{"letter":"B","text":"The first pattern looked easy; however, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"分號和 however 正確保留「看似容易但實際費時」的反差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"The first pattern looked easy because the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"打結費時不是第一款看起來容易的原因。"},{"letter":"D","text":"The first pattern looked easy; therefore, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"therefore 會說因為看起來容易，所以打結費時，因果無依據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"The first pattern looked easy, unless the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"unless 把費時設為例外條件，但兩件事在題句中都確實發生。"},{"letter":"F","text":"The first pattern looked easy. For example, the final knot took me fifteen minutes to tie.","explanation":"十五分鐘是反差，不是「看起來容易」的例證。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds, although our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","zh":"廚師說這款裝飾幾秒便能學會，然而我們小組試了好幾次才做得像樣。","upgrade":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. However, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","answer":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. However, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. Therefore, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"therefore 把廚師的容易說法當作多次嘗試的原因，原文只說說法與經驗不一致。"},{"letter":"B","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. Besides, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"besides 表附加資料，沒有正面指出宣稱與實際經驗的反差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. Likewise, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"likewise 表相似，與秒學會和多次嘗試的差距相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. For instance, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"多次嘗試不能作為「秒學會」的例子。"},{"letter":"E","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. However, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"however 清楚把廚師的預期與小組的實際困難對立。"},{"letter":"F","text":"The chef said the garnish could be mastered in seconds. As a result, our group needed several attempts before it looked right.","explanation":"as a result 表因果；說法本身沒有導致練習多次。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"but","meaning":"但；兩個主要分句的簡潔對照","note":"But 把兩個同等地位的分句連起來；在「大多容易，但少數較難」的句型中非常自然。它不把其中一個分句語法上降作讓步附屬成分；若各分句都有主語，通常在 but 前加逗號。","collocations":"most are easy, but a few are difficult; simple but time-consuming; tried, but failed","example":"The basic garnish took ten seconds, but the carved rose required several attempts.","exampleZh":"基本食物裝飾只花了十秒，但雕刻玫瑰要嘗試好幾次。","contrast":"But 直接連同一句的主要分句；however 作連接副詞，須另起句或用分號。And 只作附加，未必指出預期上的反差。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, although the carved bird took almost an hour.","zh":"工作坊的大部分設計只需一分鐘，但雕刻小鳥幾乎花了一小時。","upgrade":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, but the carved bird took almost an hour.","answer":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, but the carved bird took almost an hour.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, and therefore the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"因果連接說前者導致後者費時，原句只是比較兩組設計。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, because the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"雕刻小鳥費時不是大多數設計快捷的原因。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, or the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"or 提供二選一，但兩件事在原句中同時成立。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, but the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"兩個主要分句對照大多數快捷與少數費時，且不加入因果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, but only if the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"把小鳥費時變成其他設計快捷的必要條件，原句沒有此關係。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Most of the workshop designs took only a minute, so the carved bird took almost an hour.","explanation":"so 同樣錯誤地加入因果。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The instructions looked clear, although the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","zh":"說明看起來清晰，但全班首次嘗試仍犯了好幾個錯誤。","upgrade":"The instructions looked clear, but the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","answer":"The instructions looked clear, but the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"The instructions looked clear, but the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"but 連接「看似清晰」與「實際仍出錯」兩個已知事實，語意及句法均合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"The instructions looked clear, so the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"清晰說明通常不會自然導致犯錯；原句沒有因果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"The instructions looked clear, and the class therefore made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"therefore 更明確地誤稱清晰導致失誤。"},{"letter":"D","text":"The instructions looked clear, unless the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"班上已確實犯錯，不是判斷說明清晰與否的假設條件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"The instructions looked clear, as the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"as 易讀作原因；犯錯不能證明說明清晰。"},{"letter":"F","text":"The instructions looked clear, but only when the class still made several mistakes on its first attempt.","explanation":"only when 把說明清晰限制在班上犯錯之時，原句沒有時間限制。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"even if · 假設不等於已知反差","zh":"中文辨析： 原文已說大部分裝飾容易、少數較難。Even if a handful will challenge... 把事實拉向「即使將來真的有難度」的假設語氣；若情境是假定困難會否發生，才適合 even if。","point":"Even though accepts a fact; even if presents a possible condition."},{"word":"because / since · 原因不是讓步","zh":"中文辨析： 「大多容易因為少數很難」沒有原文的意思。Because、原因義 since 應在後句解釋前句成因時用；這裏的後句只是例外或反差。","point":"A contrast between many and a few is not a causal explanation."},{"word":"despite / in spite of + clause · 介詞後的結構","zh":"中文辨析： Despite a few difficult designs 合文法；despite a few designs are difficult 不合文法。若保留完整子句，要說 despite the fact that a few designs are difficult。這是結構差異，不代表 despite 沒有讓步義。","point":"Despite takes a noun phrase or `-ing` phrase, not an ordinary finite clause."},{"word":"but / however / although · 連接方式不同","zh":"中文辨析： 可寫 Most are easy, but a few are hard；亦可寫 Most are easy. However, a few are hard. 但 Most are easy, however a few are hard 是逗號拼接錯誤；although 可在從屬子句前使用。意思相近，標點與句法不能互換。","point":"A conjunction, conjunctive adverb and subordinating conjunction have different sentence patterns."},{"word":"while · 時間義與對照義","zh":"中文辨析： While she was learning the garnish, the chef spoke 指同一時段；While most are easy, a few are difficult 是兩組對照。若句子沒有清楚的對照，不能假設 while 自動等於 although。","point":"While can mean either “during the time” or “in contrast.”"}],"moduleNumber":7},{"id":"lesson-008","sourceId":59,"headword":"alone","title":"Alone","titleZh":"單計這一年","subtitle":"單計這一年","description":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 1.2〈Mooncake Giving - A Time-honoured or Outdated Tradition?〉說：「In 2009 alone, China produced 250,000 tons of mooncakes...」。這裏的 alone 是數量焦點：單計 2009 年已有這個產量，尚未加上其他年份。它不表示中國「孤獨地」生產，也不表示月餅只在 2009 年生產。原文的 250,000 tons 是該歷史資料的說法；下列練習採用原創示例數字，不把它們冒充真實統計。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 1.2〈Mooncake Giving - A Time-honoured or Outdated Tradition?〉說：「In 2009 alone, China produced 250,000 tons of mooncakes...」。這裏的 alone 是數量焦點：單計 2009 年已有這個產量，尚未加上其他年份。它不表示中國「孤獨地」生產，也不表示月餅只在 2009 年生產。原文的 250,000 tons 是該歷史資料的說法；下列練習採用原創示例數字，不把它們冒充真實統計。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["just","contextual","Just in 2009 可把焦點放在單一年；孤立的 just 可有「剛剛／恰好」等其他意思，位置須妥善安排。"],["by itself","contextual recast","可說 the 2009 total by itself，主語須是單一年份的數字；不能把 In 2009 alone 直接換成 In 2009 by itself。"],["in that year alone","valid anaphoric restatement, not a new synonym","已提及年份時可用 in that year alone，但仍保留 alone，只是把 2009 換成 that year；本課避免把它當作新教學同義詞湊數。"],["by themselves","false for this singular-year construction","複數形式可修飾 those yearly totals 等複數數字；不能修飾單一的 2009 年或單一年總額。"],["solely","misleading here","Solely in 2009 容易表示只在 2009 年發生、其他年沒發生；原句只說單計當年已有多少。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- 原句的 alone 把 2009 一年的總量單獨提出，不否認其他年份也有生產。\n- Just in 2009 可把 just 的數量焦點放在年份上；in that one year 要能回指已說出的年份。\n- By itself 可配合 the 2009 total/figure 等單數數字主語，或在明確統計句中配合 the year 2009；不可直接寫 in 2009 by itself。\n- Only/solely in 2009 易被讀成只在那年發生；throughout 2009 只描述時間跨度。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"just in 2009","meaning":"單在 2009 年","note":"Just 放在 in 2009 前，指「光是 2009 年這段時間」的數量；應配合明確數字或總量，不能誤讀成「生產僅發生於該年」。句末位置 ... just in 2009 也自然。","collocations":"just in 2009; spent ... just in one year; produced ... just in 2009","example":"The school collected six hundred wrappers just in 2009, before counting later years.","exampleZh":"學校單在 2009 年就收集了六百張包裝紙，還未計算之後幾年。","contrast":"Just in 2009 聚焦該年數量；only in 2009 可被理解為「只在該年，其他年沒有」，須避免這種排他性歧義。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In 2009 alone, the school collected 600 used gift boxes, before counting any later years.","zh":"單計 2009 年，學校便收集了六百個舊禮盒，尚未計入之後幾年。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Just in 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes, before counting any later years.","answer":"Just in 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Only in 2009, and in no other year, did the school collect used gift boxes","explanation":"此項明說別的年份沒有收集，原句只表示尚未把後年數字加入。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Throughout 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes","explanation":"throughout 說在整段期間收集，未突出光是一年就有六百個。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Just in 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes","explanation":"just in 2009 聚焦單一年份，保留六百個只是部分年份總量的意思。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Every year after 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes","explanation":"every year after 2009 改成之後每年，年份及數量範圍都錯。"},{"letter":"E","text":"By itself in 2009, the school collected 600 used gift boxes","explanation":"by itself 不能放在 In 2009 前當這種時間狀語。"},{"letter":"F","text":"The school had just collected 600 used gift boxes in 2009","explanation":"had just collected 可解「剛收集完」，且原句不強調剛剛完成。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The library spent 12,000 dollars on printing in 2009 alone; later years added further costs.","zh":"圖書館單在 2009 年就花了一萬二千元印刷費；後續年份另有費用。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The library spent 12,000 dollars on printing just in 2009; later years added further costs.","answer":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing just in 2009","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing only in 2009","explanation":"only in 2009 可能說印刷支出只發生在該年，與後年另有費用衝突。"},{"letter":"B","text":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing just in 2009","explanation":"just in 2009 放在費用後，保留單年已達一萬二千元。"},{"letter":"C","text":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing throughout every year","explanation":"throughout every year 說逐年都花同額，原句未說。"},{"letter":"D","text":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing by itself in 2009","explanation":"by itself 不能在此直接修飾時間片語。"},{"letter":"E","text":"had just spent 12,000 dollars on printing in 2009","explanation":"had just spent 可解剛花完，焦點不是單年對比。"},{"letter":"F","text":"spent 12,000 dollars on printing solely in 2009","explanation":"solely in 2009 易排除後續年份，與後年另有費用矛盾。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"in that one year","meaning":"單在那一年；承接上文","note":"上文先明確說出年份，後句可用 that one year 指回該年並突出單年總量。若沒有可指的年份，that 會失去明確先行詞。","collocations":"in that one year; during that single year; the total for that one year","example":"The campaign began in 2009. In that one year, volunteers gathered hundreds of used boxes.","exampleZh":"活動於 2009 年開始。單在那一年，義工已收集了數百個舊盒。","contrast":"That one year 聚焦一年；throughout that year 只表示事件持續經過全年，不必突出單年總數。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The recycling drive started in 2009. In 2009 alone, it filled three classrooms with recovered boxes.","zh":"回收活動於 2009 年開始。單在 2009 年，回收的盒子便裝滿了三間課室。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The recycling drive started in 2009. In that one year, it filled three classrooms with recovered boxes.","answer":"In that one year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"In every year","explanation":"every year 擴大成每年都有三間課室，原句只計 2009。"},{"letter":"B","text":"In that one year","explanation":"that one year 指回已提及的 2009，突出單年已有三間課室的數量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Throughout those years","explanation":"those years 是複數，與剛開始的 2009 單年不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"In only the years after 2009","explanation":"only the years after 2009 排除原句的起始年。"},{"letter":"E","text":"In 2009 by itself","explanation":"in 2009 by itself 搭配不自然；by itself 應修飾總數。"},{"letter":"F","text":"For 2009 exclusively","explanation":"exclusively 可能暗示只在 2009 年有回收活動。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The chart compares 2009 with five later years. How many boxes did the team use in 2009 alone?","zh":"圖表把 2009 年與之後五年作比較。單計 2009 年，小組用了多少個盒子？\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The chart compares 2009 with five later years. How many boxes did the team use in that one year?","answer":"in that one year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in all six years","explanation":"這會問六年合計，原題只問 2009 年。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in each of those years","explanation":"這會問六年每年各用了多少，原題只聚焦 2009 年一項。"},{"letter":"C","text":"only in the later five years","explanation":"排除 2009，與原題指定的年份相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in that one year and the next","explanation":"合併 2009 與 2010，失去單年焦點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in that one year","explanation":"that 回指圖表剛提及的 2009；one year 保留只問該年總數。"},{"letter":"F","text":"in the average year","explanation":"問的是六年平均，與 2009 年實際用量不同。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"by itself","meaning":"單計該數字；需改寫主語","note":"主語是某年的總數或代表該數字的年份時，可說 the 2009 total by itself 或在統計句中說 the year 2009 by itself，意思是不用加上其他年份，這個數值已達某比較標準。它是數量改寫，不是說數字會自行做事。","collocations":"the 2009 figure by itself; that year's total by itself; by itself exceeded the target","example":"The 2009 waste total by itself exceeded the storage limit.","exampleZh":"單計 2009 年的廢物總量，就已超出儲存上限。","contrast":"By itself 常有「獨自、無協助」的其他意思；本課只有明確數字主語時才讀成「不合併其他數字」。By themselves 與單數 total 不合。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The 2009 total alone exceeded the storage limit; totals from later years were not included.","zh":"單計 2009 年的總量就已超過儲存上限；尚未計入之後年份的數字。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The 2009 total by itself exceeded the storage limit; totals from later years were not included.","answer":"The 2009 total by itself","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"The 2009 total together with all later totals","explanation":"把後續年份加起來才超上限，與原句「2009 單年已超」不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"The 2009 total averaged across the decade","explanation":"十年平均數不是 2009 的單年總額。"},{"letter":"C","text":"The 2009 total before the year ended","explanation":"年底前的部分數字未必等於 2009 全年總量。"},{"letter":"D","text":"The 2009 total by itself","explanation":"by itself 修飾單數 total，表示不用加上後年數字也已超上限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"The 2009 total including the next year","explanation":"連 2010 年也算進來，與原句未計後年矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"The 2009 total after adding earlier years","explanation":"加入前幾年數字，已不是 2009 單年總量。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Of the ten years in the chart, 2009 alone accounted for nearly half the donated boxes.","zh":"在圖表所列十年中，單計 2009 年已佔捐贈盒子總數近半。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Of the ten years in the chart, the year 2009 by itself accounted for nearly half the donated boxes.","answer":"the year 2009 by itself","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"the average year from 2009 to 2018","explanation":"十年平均數不是 2009 單年的貢獻。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the year 2009 by itself","explanation":"以 2009 年本身作統計主語，表示其單年數字已佔近半。"},{"letter":"C","text":"2009 together with the other nine years","explanation":"十年合計應是全部捐贈盒子，不能只佔近半。"},{"letter":"D","text":"every year from 2009 to 2018","explanation":"變成每一年各佔近半，既非原意也與十年總數不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"2009 after adding the 2010 figure","explanation":"加入 2010 年便成兩年合計，失去 2009 單年的比例。"},{"letter":"F","text":"2009 and 2010 together","explanation":"把兩年當成統計主語，而原句單列 2009。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Only / solely in 2009 · 可能變成「僅該年發生」","zh":"中文辨析： 原句不否認其他年也生產月餅。Only/solely in 2009 若修飾整個生產事件，可能說成其他年沒有生產；若要用 only，必須重新安排焦點並加清楚語境。","point":"One-year tally is not an exclusive date of production."},{"word":"Just now / recently · 時間副詞另一義","zh":"中文辨析： Just 可解作「剛才」。原句有 2009 年和明確產量，講的是單年統計，不是最近才發生。","point":"Just here means a single focus, not recent time."},{"word":"Alone / by itself · 數量焦點與獨自行動","zh":"中文辨析： 一個人在家 alone 是無伴；機器 by itself 操作是無協助。2009 年的產量「單計已達某數」與孤獨或自主運作無關。","point":"The year is singled out for counting, not acting independently."},{"word":"By themselves · 單複數與指涉","zh":"中文辨析： The 2009 total by themselves 錯配：單數 total 要 by itself。若說 the totals for 2009 and 2010 by themselves，複數才可能成立，但那就合計兩年，偏離原句。","point":"A singular year's total cannot take a plural reflexive pronoun."},{"word":"Throughout / during / every year · 持續與頻率","zh":"中文辨析： Throughout 2009 強調整段期間的持續；during 2009 只是時間定位；every year 說年年如此。三者都未自行表達「單計一年已達這個總數」。","point":"Duration and repetition do not by themselves isolate one year's tally."}],"moduleNumber":8},{"id":"lesson-009","sourceId":21,"headword":"actually","title":"Actually","titleZh":"其實／說真的","subtitle":"其實／說真的","description":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 4.2〈Couponing — Job, Hobby, or Necessity?〉： “I actually feel couponing is a hobby more than a job because hobbies are something people do because they enjoy it.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 4.2〈Couponing — Job, Hobby, or Necessity?〉： “I actually feel couponing is a hobby more than a job because hobbies are something people do because they enjoy it.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["in fact","recast / 句首改寫","可在句首提出對照觀點：In fact, I feel...；要移動位置及加逗號。"],["really","near / 同位置","I really feel... 表示真心相信，但語氣可比 actually 更強。"],["in reality","false in this source sense","通常對比表象與客觀實況；In reality, I feel... 不自然地把個人感受說成外在事實。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["really","真心認為；較強語氣：Really 也可加強程度，如 really expensive；本課只教修飾個人判斷的用法。"],["in fact","其實；可在句首提出糾正，或置於強調式 I do, in fact, ... 中；直接放在 I 與 feel 之間雖合文法，但較書面。"],["to be honest","坦白說；依語境：比 actually 多了「坦白說」的自我揭示語氣；若只報告中性事實，並不適用。"],["genuinely","着重感受真實，適合回應「是否裝作喜歡」之類的疑問。"],["honestly","直接修飾 think/feel，適合坦率提出可能與別人不同的個人看法。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 在 I feel 原位置可用 really 強調看法，genuinely 突出感受真實，honestly 突出坦率；糾正既有看法可用句首 In fact, 或強調式 I do, in fact, ...；整句以「坦白說」開場可用 To be honest,。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"really","meaning":"真心認為；較強語氣","note":"在 I ... feel/think 的動詞前，強調說話者確實持此看法，不替它提供外在證據。","collocations":"really feel; really think; really believe","example":"I really feel that searching for coupons can be enjoyable.","exampleZh":"我真的認為搜尋優惠券可以是一件有趣的事。","contrast":"Really 也可加強程度，如 really expensive；本課只教修飾個人判斷的用法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although his friends call couponing a job, Ben actually feels it is a hobby.","zh":"雖然朋友稱使用優惠券為工作，阿斌其實認為它是一種興趣。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Although his friends call couponing a job, Ben really feels it is a hobby.","answer":"really feels","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"really feels","explanation":"「朋友另有看法」下，此處仍保留阿斌真心持有的個人判斷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"apparently feels","explanation":"「看來」像旁人推測他的感受，沒有保留本人表態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"supposedly feels","explanation":"暗示這種感受只是傳聞或可疑說法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"certainly proves","explanation":"把個人感受錯變成已證明的事實。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in reality feels","explanation":"in reality 放在主語與 feels 之間不自然，亦偏向客觀實況。"},{"letter":"F","text":"admittedly feels","explanation":"admittedly 帶有勉強承認的味道，原句並沒有。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After tracking her spending for a month, Mina actually thinks couponing helps her plan meals, although she cannot prove it would help everyone.","zh":"記錄一個月的開支後，美娜確實認為使用優惠券有助她安排膳食，卻不能證明這方法對每個人都有用。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After tracking her spending for a month, Mina really thinks couponing helps her plan meals, although she cannot prove it would help everyone.","answer":"really thinks","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reportedly thinks","explanation":"表示別人轉述她的想法，不能直接呈現她試行一個月後的本人判斷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"really thinks","explanation":"保留她確實持有這個想法，同時沒有把它說成對所有人適用的事實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"seemingly thinks","explanation":"只說她看似這樣想，削弱題句中她自己的看法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"objectively thinks","explanation":"她不能證明方法對人人有效，不能把個人判斷說成客觀結論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in reality thinks","explanation":"此位置和「個人判斷」的語用都不自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"necessarily thinks","explanation":"一個月的個人經驗不使結論成為必然推論。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"in fact","meaning":"其實；句首糾正","note":"在前一句已有錯誤猜測時，可於句首說明真正的個人意見，後面仍保留 I think/feel；也可在強調句 I do, in fact, ... 中作插入語。","collocations":"In fact, I feel...; In fact, she thinks...; I do, in fact, enjoy it.","example":"Some classmates assume I sell coupons. In fact, I use them for fun.","exampleZh":"有同學以為我賣優惠券；其實，我使用優惠券純粹為了樂趣。","contrast":"In fact 常置於句首並加逗號，也可在強調式 I do, in fact, ... 中插入。I in fact feel... 在語法上可行，但語氣較書面。各種位置都須保留說話者的個人看法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After someone calls it paid work, Mei replies, “I actually feel couponing is a hobby.”","zh":"有人稱使用優惠券是受薪工作後，阿美回答：「我其實認為它是一種興趣。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After someone calls it paid work, Mei replies, “In fact, I feel couponing is a hobby.”","answer":"In fact, I feel couponing is a hobby.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"In fact, I felt couponing was a hobby.","explanation":"句首標記雖可糾正看法，卻把阿美現在的個人判斷改成過去曾經這樣想。"},{"letter":"B","text":"In reality, couponing is a hobby.","explanation":"刪去 I feel，錯把她的個人看法變成客觀定論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"In fact, I feel couponing is a hobby.","explanation":"句首糾正「受薪工作」的猜測，同時保留 I feel 的主觀性。"},{"letter":"D","text":"As a result, I feel couponing is a hobby.","explanation":"表示因果結果，前文的錯誤看法不是造成她感受的原因。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Likewise, I feel couponing is a hobby.","explanation":"表示相同看法，但阿美正在反駁先前說法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"For example, I feel couponing is a hobby.","explanation":"把她的結論當例子，未呈現糾正關係。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"People assume Lee dislikes looking for bargains. Lee says, “I actually enjoy it.”","zh":"大家以為阿李討厭尋找優惠；阿李說：「其實我很享受。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"People assume Lee dislikes looking for bargains. Lee says, “I do, in fact, enjoy it.”","answer":"I do, in fact, enjoy it.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Nevertheless, I enjoy it.","explanation":"可表示讓步，但較像承認不利情況，沒有直接指出假設錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Therefore, I enjoy it.","explanation":"錯說享受是別人猜測所造成的結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Apparently, I enjoy it.","explanation":"看來是旁人推測，與本人直接澄清不符。"},{"letter":"D","text":"I do, in fact, enjoy it.","explanation":"用助動詞 do 和插入語 in fact 強調澄清「我其實喜歡」，仍是本人經驗。"},{"letter":"E","text":"In the meantime, I enjoy it.","explanation":"表示同時發生的時間關係，無關澄清。"},{"letter":"F","text":"For instance, I enjoy it.","explanation":"表示舉例，沒有處理先前錯誤印象。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"to be honest","meaning":"坦白說；依語境","note":"當說話者願意坦白講出與聽者預期不同的個人感受時，可改為句首插入語。","collocations":"To be honest, I feel...; To be honest, I think...","example":"To be honest, I find couponing more relaxing than paid work.","exampleZh":"坦白說，我覺得使用優惠券比受薪工作輕鬆。","contrast":"比 actually 多了「坦白說」的自我揭示語氣；若只報告中性事實，並不適用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Asked to give her frank opinion despite her friends’ objections, Yan says, “I actually feel couponing is relaxing.”","zh":"即使朋友反對，阿欣仍被要求坦白說出看法；她說：「我其實覺得使用優惠券令人放鬆。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Asked to give her frank opinion despite her friends’ objections, Yan says, “To be honest, I feel couponing is relaxing.”","answer":"To be honest, I feel couponing is relaxing.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"To be honest, I feel couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"題目要求坦白說出自己的感受；此句保留 I feel 並標明坦率。"},{"letter":"B","text":"In reality, couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"刪去 I feel，誤把個人感受說成所有人都適用的事實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Reportedly, I feel couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"本人親述，不需「據報」的轉述標記。"},{"letter":"D","text":"In theory, I feel couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"「理論上」與親身感受不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"For example, I feel couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"沒有上位概念可供舉例，亦未標示坦白。"},{"letter":"F","text":"As a consequence, I feel couponing is relaxing.","explanation":"沒有可導致這份感受的前因。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although he usually tells people that saving money is his only reason, Ho volunteers, “I actually think finding bargains is fun in itself.”","zh":"雖然阿豪通常告訴別人省錢是唯一原因，他這次主動說：「其實我覺得尋找優惠本身也有趣。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Although he usually tells people that saving money is his only reason, Ho volunteers, “To be honest, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.”","answer":"To be honest, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"On balance, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"表示衡量不同因素後作判斷，未標明他主動說出平常隱藏的感受。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Consequently, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"平常只談省錢並非造成這份樂趣的原因。"},{"letter":"C","text":"To be honest, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"主動坦白平常未說出的個人感受，也保留 I think。"},{"letter":"D","text":"In reality, finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"刪去 I think，過度把個人樂趣說成客觀實況。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Apparently, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"看似由旁人推測，不是他本人主動坦白。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Similarly, I think finding bargains is fun in itself.","explanation":"沒有另一個相似觀點供他附和。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"genuinely","meaning":"真心地；由衷地","note":"強調感受或興趣是真的，而非做給別人看；在已有人質疑說話者是否真喜歡使用優惠券時，可改寫 actually enjoy/feel。語氣比中性的 actually 更着重真誠。","collocations":"genuinely enjoy an activity; genuinely feel that...; genuinely believe...","example":"Ella genuinely enjoys looking for useful discounts, even when she saves very little.","exampleZh":"即使省下的錢不多，艾拉仍真心喜歡尋找實用折扣。","contrast":"Apparently enjoys 是旁人看來如此；genuinely enjoys 說她的興趣確實存在。若只是糾正一項客觀數據，不宜用 genuinely。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her friends think she only collects coupons to save money, but May actually enjoys the search itself.","zh":"朋友以為阿美收集優惠券純粹為了省錢，但她其實喜歡尋找優惠券的過程。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Her friends think she only collects coupons to save money, but May genuinely enjoys the search itself.","answer":"genuinely enjoys","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"apparently enjoys","explanation":"只是別人看來她喜歡；題句要糾正朋友的猜測，說她確有這份樂趣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"claims to enjoy","explanation":"只報告她聲稱喜歡，仍可能讓讀者懷疑其真心。"},{"letter":"C","text":"occasionally enjoys","explanation":"把真誠程度改成「偶爾」的頻率，未表達她確實喜歡尋找過程。"},{"letter":"D","text":"genuinely enjoys","explanation":"對照朋友只談省錢的看法，準確指出她由衷享受尋找過程。"},{"letter":"E","text":"is expected to enjoy","explanation":"變成別人的預期，而非阿美本人的感受。"},{"letter":"F","text":"seems to enjoy","explanation":"仍只是觀察所得的印象，未保留 actually 表達的真實興趣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After testing different methods for months, Tim actually believes that sorting coupons helps him budget, although he does not claim it works for everyone.","zh":"試行不同方法數月後，阿添真心相信整理優惠券有助他編排開支，但沒有聲稱這方法對人人有效。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After testing different methods for months, Tim genuinely believes that sorting coupons helps him budget, although he does not claim it works for everyone.","answer":"genuinely believes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reportedly believes","explanation":"把阿添的判斷變成外界轉述，未呈現本人經試行後確實持有的看法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"would like to believe","explanation":"表示希望方法有用，未確認他真心認為方法已幫助自己。"},{"letter":"C","text":"apparently believes","explanation":"只表示旁人看來他相信，未明確交代他的真正判斷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"occasionally believes","explanation":"改成有時才相信的頻率，與題句經數月試行後的看法不符。"},{"letter":"E","text":"genuinely believes","explanation":"說明他真心持有此個人判斷，仍不把效果推廣為人人適用的事實。"},{"letter":"F","text":"is told to believe","explanation":"變成受別人告知而相信，與他親自試行方法不同。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"honestly","meaning":"說真的；坦率地","note":"說話者坦率提出可能與別人看法不同的意見。放在 think/feel 前，可保留第一人稱判斷；比 actually 多一點「不隱瞞看法」的語氣。","collocations":"honestly think that...; honestly feel that...; honestly believe...","example":"I honestly think the fun of couponing matters more to her than the savings.","exampleZh":"說真的，我認為對她來說，使用優惠券的樂趣比省下的錢更重要。","contrast":"Honestly 與句首 to be honest 很接近，但前者可直接修飾 think/feel；reportedly 則表示據他人所說，不能代替本人坦率表態。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After her friends call couponing a dull chore, Lai says, “I actually think it is a relaxing hobby.”","zh":"朋友說使用優惠券是沉悶的差事後，阿麗說：「說真的，我認為這是一種令人放鬆的興趣。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After her friends call couponing a dull chore, Lai says, “I honestly think it is a relaxing hobby.”","answer":"honestly think","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reportedly think","explanation":"「據報」不適合她親口說自己的看法，也失去坦率表態。"},{"letter":"B","text":"apparently think","explanation":"彷彿旁人推斷她怎樣想，而非她本人直接說明。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reluctantly think","explanation":"加入不情願；原句沒有說她不願承認喜歡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"secretly think","explanation":"暗示一直保密，朋友持不同看法不等於她曾隱藏意見。"},{"letter":"E","text":"claim to think","explanation":"使她的看法像一項未必可信的聲稱，改變說話者語氣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"honestly think","explanation":"她在朋友反對後坦率說出自己的個人判斷，仍保留 I think。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At a public discussion, Bo says, “I actually feel that couponing helps some families, though I cannot speak for everyone.”","zh":"在公開討論中，阿寶說：「說真的，我覺得使用優惠券對部分家庭有幫助，但不能替所有人下結論。」\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"At a public discussion, Bo says, “I honestly feel that couponing helps some families, though I cannot speak for everyone.”","answer":"honestly feel","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"honestly feel","explanation":"在公開討論中坦率表達個人判斷，並明說不能推廣至所有家庭。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reportedly feel","explanation":"阿寶本人正在發言，並非旁人據報轉述其感受。"},{"letter":"C","text":"objectively prove","explanation":"原句只是個人看法，而且他明說無法替所有人下結論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"apparently feel","explanation":"變成旁人從表象推測，未保留阿寶親口陳述。"},{"letter":"E","text":"am supposed to feel","explanation":"說別人預期他應有甚麼感受，與他提出有限度的個人判斷不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reluctantly admit","explanation":"他沒有表示不情願，只是坦白交代看法的適用範圍。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"In reality · 客觀實況","zh":"中文辨析： 原句保留 I feel 的主觀立場。In reality 通常反駁表象，常用於可查證的外在情況；不能隨便取代這裏的個人看法。","point":"In reality contrasts appearance with an external state; I actually feel is a personal stance."},{"word":"Apparently / seemingly · 看似","zh":"中文辨析： 這些詞表示旁人從跡象推斷或事物看似如此，不表示說話者本人真心認為。","point":"Apparently reports appearance or inference, not the speaker’s sincere opinion."},{"word":"Admittedly · 勉強承認","zh":"中文辨析： Admittedly 常引入對自己論點不利、但不得不承認的讓步；原文只表達與「工作」相比更像興趣。","point":"Admittedly concedes a point; actually here marks a genuine view."},{"word":"Actual / real · 詞性陷阱","zh":"中文辨析： Actual 和 real 是形容詞，不能直接修飾 feel；真的認為可說 really feel。","point":"Use an adverb before feel; actual and real are adjectives."},{"word":"Genuinely / honestly · 真誠與坦率不是客觀證明","zh":"中文辨析： 兩者在適合的個人陳述中可改寫 actually，但 genuinely 着重感受真實，honestly 着重說話坦率；都不會令「我覺得」成為已證實的普遍事實。","point":"Genuinely marks sincerity; honestly marks frank expression. Neither turns a personal view into a verified fact."}],"moduleNumber":9},{"id":"lesson-010","sourceId":13,"headword":"according to","title":"According To","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 mooncake article attributes production and wrapping figures to the People’s Daily website. According to marks the source of a reported claim; it does not assert independent verification or an inference made by the present writer.","sourceSense":"The 2012 mooncake article attributes production and wrapping figures to the People’s Daily website. According to marks the source of a reported claim; it does not assert independent verification or an inference made by the present writer.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["as stated by","contextual: explicit source statement"],["based on","false as simple attribution; marks evidential basis"],["as reported by","contextual: news report"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： As cited by 可用於引述鏈，但會改變直接來源；based on 是推論依據而非同一歸屬；citing 需改寫主句主語，故不作直接替換題。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["as reported by","適合新聞機構傳達的數字或事件；保留來源歸屬，不保證報道已核實。","來源必須真的報道該說法；不可把自己的計算冒充其報道。"],["as stated by","來源明確說出某項主張或數字時使用；較強調來源自己的說法。","若資料只是作者從圖表自行計出，不可說來源 stated 該結論。"],["per","簡短而偏正式的來源標記，常見於報告、商務及美式英語；須有可信的明確來源。","在一般香港學生口語中 according to 較自然；per 可顯得過分簡略。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 新聞媒體刊載的數字或事件可說 as reported by；某人或機構明確宣告的內容可說 as stated by；在正式書面註記中引述時間表、名單等文件時可用簡潔的 per。三者標明資訊來源，不等於 as verified by 已查證其真確。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"as reported by","meaning":"據……報道","note":"適合新聞機構傳達的數字或事件；保留來源歸屬，不保證報道已核實。","collocations":"as reported by the newspaper; as reported by the website.","example":"The attendance exceeded a thousand, as reported by the local paper.","exampleZh":"據本地報章報道，出席人數超過一千。","contrast":"來源必須真的報道該說法；不可把自己的計算冒充其報道。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The charity raised $80,000, according to the newspaper that published the figure.","zh":"據刊登該數字的報章報道，慈善機構籌得八萬元。","upgrade":"The charity raised $80,000, as reported by the newspaper that published the figure.","answer":"as reported by","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"based on","explanation":"Based on 標示推論依據；這句直接把籌款數字歸於報章報道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"as verified by","explanation":"刊登數字不等於報章已獨立核實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"as inferred from","explanation":"句中沒有從報章資料自行推算籌款額。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"不是按照報章規則籌款。"},{"letter":"E","text":"as reported by","explanation":"As reported by 準確表明數字是報章報道的。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as predicted by","explanation":"報章刊登的是已發生的數字，不是預測。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A bridge reopened on Tuesday, according to the local news site whose reporter attended the reopening.","zh":"據有記者到場採訪的本地新聞網站報道，一座橋於星期二重新開放。","upgrade":"A bridge reopened on Tuesday, as reported by the local news site whose reporter attended the reopening.","answer":"as reported by","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"as reported by","explanation":"記者到場後網站刊出重開消息，as reported by 準確作新聞來源歸屬。"},{"letter":"B","text":"based on","explanation":"句子直接轉述現場報道，不是作者從網站資料自行推算重開日期。"},{"letter":"C","text":"as announced by","explanation":"新聞網站報道了重開；句中沒有說它是作出正式重開公告的主管機構。"},{"letter":"D","text":"as inferred from","explanation":"重開日期是報道內容，不是作者從線索推論出來。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"橋樑重開不是「遵照網站規則」進行。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as forecast by","explanation":"星期二重開是已發生的事件，不是網站對未來的預測。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"as stated by","meaning":"正如……所述","note":"來源明確說出某項主張或數字時使用；較強調來源自己的說法。","collocations":"as stated by the report; as stated by the organiser.","example":"The event starts at nine, as stated by the organiser.","exampleZh":"正如主辦方所述，活動九時開始。","contrast":"若資料只是作者從圖表自行計出，不可說來源 stated 該結論。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The gallery will close on Monday, according to the curator, who explicitly announced it.","zh":"據館長明確宣布，畫廊將於星期一關閉。","upgrade":"The gallery will close on Monday, as stated by the curator, who explicitly announced it.","answer":"as stated by","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"as inferred from","explanation":"館長直接宣布，不是讀者從線索推測。"},{"letter":"B","text":"as verified by","explanation":"館長陳述日期不等於獨立核實關館安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"句子歸屬消息來源，不是說依照館長命令行事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"as predicted by","explanation":"已宣布的關閉日不是推測。"},{"letter":"E","text":"as disputed by","explanation":"館長是在宣布，不是在反駁關閉日期。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as stated by","explanation":"As stated by 把關閉日期歸於館長的明確說法。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The deadline is 5 p.m., according to the school, which set out the timetable in an email.","zh":"據學校在電郵中所述，截止時間是下午五時。","upgrade":"The deadline is 5 p.m., as stated by the school in its email.","answer":"as stated by","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"as calculated from","explanation":"學校直接寫出截止時間，不是讀者計算所得。"},{"letter":"B","text":"as inferred from","explanation":"電郵明載截止時間，無須自行推斷。"},{"letter":"C","text":"as stated by","explanation":"As stated by 把截止時間歸於學校的明確陳述。"},{"letter":"D","text":"as verified by","explanation":"來源陳述與獨立核實是兩回事。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"不是說學生依照規則行動，而是說時間來自學校。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as disputed by","explanation":"學校並未否認這個截止時間。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"per","meaning":"依據／據","note":"簡短而偏正式的來源標記，常見於報告、商務及美式英語；須有可信的明確來源。","collocations":"per the report; per the website.","example":"Per the published timetable, the exhibition opens at ten.","exampleZh":"據已公布的時間表，展覽十時開放。","contrast":"在一般香港學生口語中 according to 較自然；per 可顯得過分簡略。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"According to the published schedule, the workshop begins at ten.","zh":"根據已公布的時間表，工作坊十時開始。","upgrade":"Per the published schedule, the workshop begins at ten.","answer":"per","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"based on","explanation":"時間表直接列出開始時間，不是作者據數據推論。"},{"letter":"B","text":"as proved by","explanation":"公布時間表不等於活動實際開場已獲證實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"不是說工作坊遵守某條規則，而是在交代時間來源。"},{"letter":"D","text":"per","explanation":"Per 可在正式簡短通知中引出來源。"},{"letter":"E","text":"as estimated from","explanation":"開始時間是列明的，不是估算。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as contradicted by","explanation":"沒有與時間表相反的資料。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club has registered 18 entrants (according to the final enrolment list).","zh":"據最後的報名名單，社團已登記十八名參賽者。","upgrade":"The club has registered 18 entrants (per the final enrolment list).","answer":"per","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"based on","explanation":"括號內直接標明名單上的已登記人數，沒有另行估算。"},{"letter":"B","text":"per","explanation":"括號中的 per the final enrolment list 是精簡的書面資料來源註記。"},{"letter":"C","text":"as proved by","explanation":"名單記錄十八人，卻不表示整項活動的實際到場人數已獲證明。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in accordance with","explanation":"不是社團依照名單規則行事，而是引述名單上的報名人數。"},{"letter":"E","text":"as estimated from","explanation":"十八人是名單所記的數目，並非估算值。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as disputed by","explanation":"名單提供人數，沒有對十八人這個數字提出異議。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"based on / according to","zh":"中文辨析： Based on 引入推論所依據的資料；according to 則把陳述歸於來源。","point":"Evidence for an inference is not always the reporter of the claim."},{"word":"proved by / reported by","zh":"中文辨析： 報道數字不等於證實數字；proved by 誇大了證據。","point":"Reporting a figure does not independently prove it."},{"word":"in accordance with / according to","zh":"中文辨析： In accordance with 指依照規則行事，並非引述消息來源。","point":"A regulation can be followed; a newspaper is cited."},{"word":"according to me / in my opinion","zh":"中文辨析： 表達自己意見時慣用 in my opinion；according to me 不自然。","point":"According to usually introduces an external source."}],"moduleNumber":10},{"id":"lesson-011","sourceId":79,"headword":"answer","title":"Answer","titleZh":"回覆電郵","subtitle":"回覆電郵","description":"原文： 2014 DSE Speaking 1.1〈Why Are Young People Abandoning Email?〉指出，電郵訊息可能要過數小時才會被收到或 answered（“might not be received or answered for hours”）。Answered 是動詞 answer 的被動分詞，意思是「有人回覆電郵」；不是名詞「答案」，也不是解決難題。原文說回覆可能延遲，不表示必然沒有人讀到訊息。以下練習句均為原創，並非試卷原句。","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 DSE Speaking 1.1〈Why Are Young People Abandoning Email?〉指出，電郵訊息可能要過數小時才會被收到或 answered（“might not be received or answered for hours”）。Answered 是動詞 answer 的被動分詞，意思是「有人回覆電郵」；不是名詞「答案」，也不是解決難題。原文說回覆可能延遲，不表示必然沒有人讀到訊息。以下練習句均為原創，並非試卷原句。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文語境中的理由"],"rows":[["response","詞性不合；可改寫","名詞，指一則回應；可說 receive a response to an email，不能直接放在 be answered 的動詞位置。"],["reply","可用，須作動詞並配 to","be replied to 可改寫被動句；reply 作名詞時仍須重組句子。"],["solution","不適合","解決辦法可回答問題，卻不能表示寄件人收到電郵回覆。"]],"note":"原圖譜錯把這個條目當名詞 answer 教。本課按原文改正為動詞義。Acknowledge receipt 只表示確認收到，尚未必答覆內容；react to 也未必發出回信。兩者列在易混淆詞中。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["想表達的重點","優先選用","勿誤認為"],"rows":[["對一封來信發回信","reply to an email","只讀到或收到電郵"],["對查詢作回應，渠道可以不同","respond to an enquiry","必然從原收件匣寄回"],["寫信回覆先前聯絡自己的人","write back to the sender","對外發一般通告"],["查核後稍遲再聯絡對方","get back to someone by email","已即時解決所有問題"]],"note":"原文 might not be ... answered for hours 只說回覆可能延遲。若學生要用名詞 response/reply，應完整改為「可能數小時內都收不到回覆」，不要把名詞當動詞。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"reply to","meaning":"回覆收到的訊息","note":"向某封已收到的電郵發回覆；reply to an email，被動式為 the email was replied to。不必逐項回答電郵內的每一條問題，但須有實際回信。","collocations":"reply to an email; reply to a sender; reply to a request by Friday","example":"The librarian replied to the student's email with the book's availability.","exampleZh":"圖書館員回覆學生的電郵，告知該書是否可借。","contrast":"比 respond to 更明確指向訊息的回覆；reply 可作名詞，但原文 answered 的語法位置需要動詞或被動動詞詞組。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The club secretary answered each membership email from the same inbox before closing it for the day.","zh":"社團秘書每天關閉同一個收件匣前，都從該收件匣回覆每封入會電郵。","upgrade":"The club secretary replied to each membership email from the same inbox before closing it for the day.","answer":"replied to each membership email","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"read each membership email","explanation":"只說秘書看了入會電郵，沒有交代她從收件匣寄出回覆。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replied to each membership email","explanation":"說明秘書對每封入會電郵發出回信，保留原句的動作和對象。"},{"letter":"C","text":"solved each membership problem","explanation":"原句沒有說入會者有難題，更沒有說秘書解決了問題。"},{"letter":"D","text":"acknowledged receipt of each membership email automatically","explanation":"自動收件確認不等於秘書逐封回覆內容。"},{"letter":"E","text":"forwarded each membership email to another club","explanation":"轉寄改變訊息去向，不表示秘書回信給寄件人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reacted to each membership email privately","explanation":"私下有反應，寄件人仍未必收到答覆。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The teacher answered Mia's email by using the Reply button and writing a short message about the timetable.","zh":"老師按「回覆」鍵，寫了一則有關時間表的短訊，回覆美雅的電郵。","upgrade":"The teacher replied to Mia's email by using the Reply button and writing a short message about the timetable.","answer":"replied to Mia's email","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"opened Mia's email again","explanation":"再次打開電郵，仍未說老師有寄出那則時間表短訊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"shared Mia's email with the class","explanation":"分享訊息給全班不是按回覆鍵寫給美雅。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replied to Mia's email","explanation":"明確表示老師按回覆鍵後向原寄件人發回書面訊息。"},{"letter":"D","text":"gave Mia a solution to every timetable conflict","explanation":"原句只說短訊涉及時間表，沒說每個衝突都已解決。"},{"letter":"E","text":"confirmed only that Mia's email had arrived","explanation":"單純確認收到，弱於老師寫了時間表短訊這個事實。"},{"letter":"F","text":"deleted Mia's email after reading it","explanation":"刪除是處理收件匣，不是寄出回覆。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"respond to","meaning":"對訊息作回應","note":"對電郵、查詢或請求作回應；可透過電郵或另一指定渠道回應。若原句只是要求收到確認，不能擅自寫成已處理請求。","collocations":"respond to an email; respond to an enquiry; respond to a request in writing","example":"The office responded to the parents' enquiry in writing the next morning.","exampleZh":"辦事處翌日上午以書面回應家長的查詢。","contrast":"Respond to 的渠道與內容較廣；若原句特別說「按回覆鍵寄回電郵」，reply to 更準確。React to 可能只指情緒反應。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The office answered the parent's emailed enquiry in writing, but sent the information through its secure portal.","zh":"辦事處以書面回應家長用電郵提出的查詢，但資料是經其安全網站送出的。","upgrade":"The office responded to the parent's emailed enquiry in writing, but sent the information through its secure portal.","answer":"responded to the parent's emailed enquiry in writing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"forwarded the parent's enquiry to a public forum","explanation":"公開轉寄既非回應家長，也與安全網站傳送相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replied to the parent's email from the same inbox","explanation":"假定回信仍由原收件匣寄出；原句特別說改用安全網站。"},{"letter":"C","text":"acknowledged that the parent's message had arrived","explanation":"只確認已收到，沒保留提供資料的書面回應。"},{"letter":"D","text":"responded to the parent's emailed enquiry in writing","explanation":"涵蓋查詢已獲書面回應，同時不擅自限定傳送渠道。"},{"letter":"E","text":"solved every concern the parent had about the school","explanation":"原句只說回應這次查詢，沒有保證解決所有關注。"},{"letter":"F","text":"read the parent's enquiry on its secure portal","explanation":"只描述閱讀，沒有表達辦事處送出了資料。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The council answered residents' emails at a public meeting by addressing their questions one by one.","zh":"議會在公開會議上逐一回答居民透過電郵提出的問題，以回應那些電郵。","upgrade":"The council responded to residents' emails at a public meeting by addressing their questions one by one.","answer":"responded to residents' emails at a public meeting","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"sent an automated receipt for residents' emails","explanation":"自動回執不會在會上逐一回應居民提出的問題。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replied by email to every resident before the meeting","explanation":"加入原句沒有的會前電郵回覆，還改變回應渠道。"},{"letter":"C","text":"counted the number of emails received","explanation":"統計數量沒有回答任何在電郵中提出的問題。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reacted angrily to residents' emails","explanation":"情緒反應不能代替會議上的逐項答覆。"},{"letter":"E","text":"responded to residents' emails at a public meeting","explanation":"保留對電郵內容作回應及回應地點，沒有假裝寄出了回信。"},{"letter":"F","text":"found a complete solution to every local issue","explanation":"回答問題不保證已解決每個社區議題。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"write back to","meaning":"寫信回覆某人","note":"寫訊息回覆之前聯絡自己的人；後接人，或用 write back about the email。口語自然，強調有書面回信，不是只接起電話。","collocations":"write back to the sender; write back by email; write back with the details","example":"The coach wrote back to the applicant with a time for the trial session.","exampleZh":"教練寫信回覆申請人，告知試練的時間。","contrast":"Write back to 接收件人最自然；answer an email 接訊息本身。改寫時通常要把受詞由「電郵」改成「寄件人」。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After receiving Jordan's email, the curator answered it with a written invitation to visit the gallery.","zh":"策展人收到佐敦的電郵後，寫信邀請他參觀畫廊，以回覆該電郵。","upgrade":"After receiving Jordan's email, the curator wrote back to Jordan with an invitation to visit the gallery.","answer":"wrote back to Jordan with an invitation to visit the gallery","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"wrote back to Jordan with an invitation to visit the gallery","explanation":"保留寫信回覆寄件人及邀請參觀兩項資訊，並正確以人作受詞。"},{"letter":"B","text":"invited Jordan over the phone without writing to him","explanation":"電話邀請與原句明示的書面回信不符。"},{"letter":"C","text":"acknowledged receipt of Jordan's email and said nothing else","explanation":"只確認收到，漏掉策展人在回信中的邀請。"},{"letter":"D","text":"showed Jordan's email to gallery visitors","explanation":"展示來信給別人，不等於回覆佐敦。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reacted to Jordan's email without contacting him","explanation":"沒有聯絡寄件人，與寫信回覆相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"wrote about Jordan in the gallery newsletter","explanation":"寫的是給讀者看的通訊，不是回信給佐敦。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The organiser did not answer the volunteer's email until the volunteer sent a reminder a week later; then she wrote an apology.","zh":"主辦人直到義工一星期後寄來催問，才回覆他的電郵，並寫了一封道歉信。","upgrade":"The organiser did not write back to the volunteer until he sent a reminder a week later; then she wrote an apology.","answer":"wrote back to the volunteer after the reminder, with an apology","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"wrote back to the volunteer after the reminder, with an apology","explanation":"保留「催問後才寫回信」的時間次序及道歉內容。"},{"letter":"B","text":"wrote to all volunteers before anyone sent a reminder","explanation":"原句是向一名催問過的義工遲來回信，並非事前群發。"},{"letter":"C","text":"called the volunteer after the reminder but sent no written message","explanation":"有稍後聯絡，卻把書面道歉改成電話。"},{"letter":"D","text":"forwarded the volunteer's email to another organiser without replying","explanation":"轉寄來信沒有把道歉信送回原寄件人。"},{"letter":"E","text":"acknowledged receipt automatically on the day of the first email","explanation":"即日回執不等於一星期催問後才發的道歉信。"},{"letter":"F","text":"wrote a note about the volunteer but did not send it to him","explanation":"寫關於義工的筆記並非寫給他，不能稱為回覆。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"get back to","meaning":"稍後回覆某人","note":"在有了資料或經過一段時間後再聯絡對方；尤其適合強調回覆時限或延遲。它可用於電話或面談；若題目要求電郵，須明說 by email。","collocations":"get back to someone by email; get back to someone within a day; get back to a sender with an answer","example":"The organiser got back to the parent by email after checking the bus schedule.","exampleZh":"主辦人查核巴士時間表後，以電郵回覆那名家長。","contrast":"強調稍後聯絡；若沒有 by email 等線索，不能保證以書面回覆。Get back an email 則可能指取回電郵，不是這個片語。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The travel adviser said she would answer my email tomorrow after checking the ferry timetable.","zh":"旅遊顧問說她查過渡輪時間表後，明天會回覆我的電郵。","upgrade":"The travel adviser said she would get back to me tomorrow by email after checking the ferry timetable.","answer":"get back to me tomorrow by email after checking the ferry timetable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"get back to me tomorrow by email after checking the ferry timetable","explanation":"保留查核後、明天、以電郵聯絡我這三個回覆條件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"send me the ferry timetable before checking it","explanation":"把先查核後回覆的時間次序顛倒。"},{"letter":"C","text":"confirm that she had received my email without checking anything","explanation":"只發收件確認，未作原句承諾的查核和翌日答覆。"},{"letter":"D","text":"solve every travel delay tomorrow morning","explanation":"渡輪時間表查詢不等於解決所有旅程延誤。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reply to a different traveller instead of me","explanation":"改成回覆其他旅客，錯了收件人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"discuss my email with colleagues but never contact me","explanation":"內部討論沒有向寄件人作回應。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The admissions officer answered the applicants' emails three days later by email, after finding a clerical error in their files.","zh":"招生主任發現申請人檔案中的文書錯誤後，三天後以電郵回覆了他們的來信。","upgrade":"The admissions officer got back to the applicants by email three days later, after finding a clerical error in their files.","answer":"got back to the applicants by email three days later after finding the error","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"got back to the applicants by email three days later after finding the error","explanation":"保留已完成的電郵聯絡、三天延遲及先發現錯誤的次序。"},{"letter":"B","text":"promised to reply within two days but never sent a message","explanation":"把已完成的三天後回覆改成未履行的承諾。"},{"letter":"C","text":"acknowledged their emails automatically before finding the error","explanation":"只有即時收件確認，沒有發現錯誤後的實際答覆。"},{"letter":"D","text":"discussed the error with colleagues but did not contact the applicants","explanation":"內部討論沒有向申請人寄出電郵。"},{"letter":"E","text":"phoned only one applicant three days later","explanation":"把對多名申請人的電郵改成只致電一人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"sent an acceptance decision to every applicant immediately","explanation":"原句既沒說全部錄取，也不是立即回覆。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Response / answer / reply as nouns · 詞性轉換","zh":"中文辨析： 原文的 answered 是動詞。名詞 response 或 reply 可用於「收到回應」，但須改為 receive a response/reply 等完整結構；an answer 在「問題的答案」語境才直接對應名詞。不能把名詞單獨塞進 be answered 的位置。","point":"A response is something received; answering an email is an action."},{"word":"Solution / explanation · 解難或解說不是回信","zh":"中文辨析： 電郵可能問一個難題，但收件人寄來一封回覆，不代表已找到 solution；explanation 是回覆可能載有的內容。若原句問「解決數學題」，solution 才有用。","point":"A solution solves a problem; it does not itself mean that an email was replied to."},{"word":"Acknowledge / confirm receipt · 收到不等於回答","zh":"中文辨析： 自動電郵可確認「已收到」，仍未處理寄件人的問題。若原句只要求回執，acknowledge receipt 正確；若要求實質回覆，不能當作 answer。","point":"A receipt notice confirms delivery without necessarily answering the message."},{"word":"React / read / open · 行為階段不同","zh":"中文辨析： Read、open 是查看電郵；react to 可以只是感到驚訝，並未發信。原文將 received 與 answered 分開，正好說明「收到」與「回覆」不是同一件事。","point":"Reading or reacting to a message need not produce a reply."},{"word":"Answer a question / answer an email · 受詞與語意","zh":"中文辨析： Answer a question 可指提供問題的答案；answer an email 指回覆訊息。電郵內若有多條問題，回信可以沒有逐題解決。改寫時要保持句子到底要求「寄出回覆」還是「答對問題」。","point":"Replying to an email is not necessarily solving every question in it."}],"moduleNumber":11},{"id":"lesson-012","sourceId":46,"headword":"age","title":"Age","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 article says men seeking plastic surgery “come from all age groups and professions.” Age is part of the compound age groups: categories based on how old the men are. The source reports a broad age spread; it does not list numerical boundaries, give any man's exact age, or establish that every individual year of age is represented.","sourceSense":"The 2012 article says men seeking plastic surgery “come from all age groups and professions.” Age is part of the compound age groups: categories based on how old the men are. The source reports a broad age spread; it does not list numerical boundaries, give any man's exact age, or establish that every individual year of age is represented.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["years","Not a direct replacement in age groups: all years groups is ungrammatical. A specified age can be expressed as 40 years of age, but the source supplies no exact years."],["generation","False as a general replacement: a birth cohort or family generation is not a present-day age bracket."],["stage of life","Contextual recast only if adult phases such as early, middle and later adulthood are explicitly intended; this is broader than numerical age groups."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Age brackets names defined categories, age ranges the spans of ages included, and different ages the diversity without formal categories; all are taught. Adult life stages is a qualified version of the incoming stage of life, but it changes from age classification to life circumstances and is therefore audited as a near-miss rather than taught as a synonym. Age bands largely duplicates age brackets; age cohorts often means groups born around the same time, so it can slide toward generation and is not treated as a general equivalent. Years old needs a number for an individual and cannot replace the source compound."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["age brackets","已設有明確歲數界線，並按類別分配人或票價。","不等於個人確切歲數、出生世代或職業。"],["age ranges","焦點在每段年齡的數字起止或跨度是否改動。","單一跨度未必表示人已被正式分組。"],["different ages","只需說人群有年齡差異，不強調統計組別。","不把多樣性說成每個單一年歲都有人。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 先看句子是否有二十至二十九歲等明確分組：選 age brackets；若焦點是各段起止歲數及其跨度，選 age ranges；若只說男女或講者年齡各異、沒有正式分組，改為 people of different ages。Generation 按出生世代，stage of life 按人生階段，兩者均不能無條件代替來源的 age groups。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"age brackets","meaning":"年齡組別","note":"按明確年齡上下限劃分的人群類別，如二十至二十九歲；最接近來源 age groups 的分類含義。","collocations":"different age brackets; the 20–29 age bracket; compare results across age brackets.","example":"The survey sorted adult participants into five age brackets before comparing their answers.","exampleZh":"調查在比較答案前，把成年參加者分成五個年齡組別。","contrast":"Bracket 是研究者設定的分類，不是一名參加者的精確年歲或其出生世代。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The clinic sorted respondents into age groups of 20–29, 30–39 and 40–49 before comparing their answers.","zh":"診所在比較答案前，先把受訪者分為二十至二十九、三十至三十九及四十至四十九歲的組別。","upgrade":"The clinic sorted respondents into age brackets of 20–29, 30–39 and 40–49 before comparing their answers.","answer":"age brackets","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"birth-year cohorts","explanation":"出生年份群組不是此處按目前歲數劃分的三個十歲組別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"age brackets","explanation":"三段清楚的年齡上下限是供統計比較的 age brackets。"},{"letter":"C","text":"years of age","explanation":"Years of age 要連着個別歲數，不指把受訪者分組的類別。"},{"letter":"D","text":"adult life stages","explanation":"診所用明確十歲界限，而非入職或退休等人生階段分類。"},{"letter":"E","text":"average ages","explanation":"三個區間不是各組算出的平均歲數。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age thresholds","explanation":"二十、三十、四十歲是分界點；整個 20–29 等組別不是單一門檻。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"On the ticket machine, three age groups determine the fare: under 18, 18–64 and 65 or over; a passenger selects one category.","zh":"售票機按三個年齡組別決定票價：十八歲以下、十八至六十四歲，以及六十五歲或以上；乘客須選其中一類。","upgrade":"On the ticket machine, three age brackets determine the fare: under 18, 18–64 and 65 or over; a passenger selects one category.","answer":"age brackets","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age thresholds","explanation":"十八及六十五歲是門檻；乘客要選的是由門檻形成的整個票價組別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adult life stages","explanation":"十八歲以下一組也在票價表內；人生階段沒有售票機列出的清楚歲數界線。"},{"letter":"C","text":"birth cohorts","explanation":"票價根據當下年齡而非出生年份所屬世代。"},{"letter":"D","text":"age brackets","explanation":"三類互不重疊的年齡界限直接決定票價，正是 age brackets。"},{"letter":"E","text":"estimated ages","explanation":"票價表寫的是規定界限，不是目測年齡的估計。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age averages","explanation":"票價表列界限，不是三組乘客的平均年齡。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"age ranges","meaning":"年齡範圍","note":"指所涵蓋的起止年齡，或多個有界限的年齡跨度；比 bracket 更着重每段跨度本身。","collocations":"a wide age range; age ranges from 20 to 29 and 30 to 39; list age ranges.","example":"The leaflet listed age ranges from 20–29 through 60–69 so readers could see whom the survey included.","exampleZh":"單張列出由二十至二十九歲到六十至六十九歲的年齡範圍，讓讀者知道調查涵蓋哪些人。","contrast":"單一 range 可是整體跨度，未必代表分組；來源說 groups，練習須保留多個有界限的範圍。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The appendix prints the age groups as intervals, from 25–34 through 65–74, so readers can see the lower and upper ages in each span.","zh":"附錄把年齡組別列成區間，由二十五至三十四歲直到六十五至七十四歲，讓讀者看到每段的年齡上下限。","upgrade":"The appendix prints the age ranges as intervals, from 25–34 through 65–74, so readers can see the lower and upper ages in each span.","answer":"age ranges","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"exact ages","explanation":"附錄列的是多段上下限，不是每名受訪者的一個準確歲數。"},{"letter":"B","text":"life stages","explanation":"二十五至三十四等是數字區間，未定義工作、家庭或退休等人生階段。"},{"letter":"C","text":"birth generations","explanation":"這些是研究中的年齡跨度，不是按出生年代命名的世代。"},{"letter":"D","text":"age averages","explanation":"附錄列 25–34 等區間，並非計算各組平均歲數。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age ranges","explanation":"Age ranges 突出每段的起止年齡，符合附錄特別列明上下限的目的。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age limits","explanation":"這裏列出多段資料跨度，並非規定誰不可參加的最高或最低歲數。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before changing the questionnaire, the researcher widened its age groups from 30–39 and 40–49 to 30–44 and 45–59; she changed the numerical spans, not anyone's age.","zh":"修改問卷前，研究員把原來三十至三十九歲及四十至四十九歲的年齡組別，改成三十至四十四歲及四十五至五十九歲；她改的是數字跨度，不是任何人的年齡。","upgrade":"Before changing the questionnaire, the researcher widened its age ranges from 30–39 and 40–49 to 30–44 and 45–59; she changed the numerical spans, not anyone's age.","answer":"age ranges","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age ranges","explanation":"研究員擴闊的是問卷各段年齡的上下限，age ranges 精確指出被改動的跨度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"birth cohorts","explanation":"她沒有改受訪者所屬出生世代，只改問卷的數字區間。"},{"letter":"C","text":"career phases","explanation":"問卷沒有按入職、中期或退休等職業階段重劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"exact ages","explanation":"不能把任何人的實際歲數擴闊；改的是問卷組別界線。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age thresholds","explanation":"研究員改動的是 30–44 等完整跨度，不只是其中一個分界點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"average ages","explanation":"新舊數字是區間上下限，不是算出的平均年齡。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"different ages","meaning":"不同年齡","note":"不強調正式組別，只說受訪者年齡並不相同；可用 people of different ages 改寫跨年齡人群。","collocations":"people of different ages; men of different ages; include adults of different ages.","example":"The discussion included men of different ages, from younger adults to retirees.","exampleZh":"討論包括不同年齡的男性，由較年輕的成年人到退休人士都有。","contrast":"Different ages 保留年齡多樣性，卻不交代每個人所屬的統計組別或確切年歲。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The interview brought together men from several age groups, from young adults to retirees; the interviewer noted approximate ages but did not set fixed survey brackets.","zh":"訪談找來不同年齡組別的男性，由年輕成年人到退休人士都有；訪問員只記大約歲數，沒有設定固定的調查年齡帶。","upgrade":"The interview brought together men of different ages, from young adults to retirees; the interviewer noted approximate ages but did not set fixed survey brackets.","answer":"men of different ages","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"men of one generation","explanation":"年輕成年人和退休人士年齡跨距很大，句子沒有說他們同屬一個出生世代。"},{"letter":"B","text":"men at one life stage","explanation":"句子重點是歲數差異，並沒有判定所有人處於同一人生階段。"},{"letter":"C","text":"men of different ages","explanation":"由年輕成年人到退休人士，重點是歲數不同；改寫沒有虛構固定調查年齡帶。"},{"letter":"D","text":"men with different jobs","explanation":"來源句子另外提職業；本題只給年齡線索，沒有列出各人的工作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"men with exact ages","explanation":"訪問員只記大約歲數，沒有記下每人確切年齡。"},{"letter":"F","text":"men of different seniority","explanation":"Seniority 常指職級或資歷，不等於年齡不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For each trio in the choir, the director mixed age groups by placing a teenager with middle-aged and older singers instead of seating each age together.","zh":"合唱團指揮在每個三人組內混合不同年齡組別，讓青少年與中年和較年長的歌手同組，而非把同齡人士坐在一起。","upgrade":"For each trio in the choir, the director mixed singers of different ages by placing a teenager with middle-aged and older singers instead of seating each age together.","answer":"singers of different ages","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"singers from one cohort","explanation":"每組刻意同時放青少年與中老年歌手，不是同一出生世代的人聚在一起。"},{"letter":"B","text":"singers in different jobs","explanation":"指揮按年齡混合，沒有提歌手各自的職業。"},{"letter":"C","text":"singers at the same life stage","explanation":"青少年與較年長成人並非同一人生階段。"},{"letter":"D","text":"singers with listed birth years","explanation":"原句只有青少年、中年及較年長的描述，沒列任何出生年。"},{"letter":"E","text":"singers in formal age brackets","explanation":"指揮的動作是把年齡不同的人放進同一組，並非建立數字界限的統計組別。"},{"letter":"F","text":"singers of different ages","explanation":"Singers of different ages 可直接配合 mixed，說清楚每組混齡而不增加正式分組。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"years / age groups","zh":"中文辨析： Forty years of age 可表某人的確切歲數，但 all years groups 不合語法；來源沒有每人年歲。","point":"A numerical age is not itself a category of people."},{"word":"generation / age bracket","zh":"中文辨析： Generation 常按出生年代或家族輩分劃分；目前同屬一個年齡組別，不一定同一代。","point":"Birth cohort and current age range answer different questions."},{"word":"adult life stage / defined age range","zh":"中文辨析： 青年、中年等階段沒有固定十歲界線；若調查明列二十至二十九歲，應說 age bracket/range。","point":"A broad phase of adulthood is not a numerical interval by itself."},{"word":"every age / all age groups","zh":"中文辨析： 來源說各年齡組別都有男性，不是從十八歲到八十歲每個單一年歲都有人。","point":"Representation across groups does not prove every exact age occurs."},{"word":"profession / age","zh":"中文辨析： 來源同時提職業和年齡；職業是工作類型，不可把兩種分類混為一談。","point":"How old a person is differs from what job he does."}],"moduleNumber":12},{"id":"lesson-013","sourceId":96,"headword":"area","title":"Area","titleZh":"人可到訪的地區","subtitle":"人可到訪的地區","description":"The 2013 DSE set 2.2 empty-shop project passage says “More than 4,000 people visited the area over one weekend.” The preceding account describes activities in seven unused shops in a UK city. Area is a physical urban place people visited. The local index’s note “part of an issue” contradicts the quoted sentence and is rejected. It is not merely one indoor shop space. All practice sentences below are original.","sourceSense":"The 2013 DSE set 2.2 empty-shop project passage says “More than 4,000 people visited the area over one weekend.” The preceding account describes activities in seven unused shops in a UK city. Area is a physical urban place people visited. The local index’s note “part of an issue” contradicts the quoted sentence and is rejected. It is not merely one indoor shop space. All practice sentences below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["aspect","此處錯誤","議題的一方面，不能讓數千人實地到訪。"],["domain","此處錯誤","知識或活動領域，非街區。"],["region","太大，無來源支持","地理區域往往跨城甚至更大；若題句真的覆蓋廣域才可用。"],["space","太小或太泛","可指一間店內的空間，不能無證據縮小整個街區。"],["locality","有條件近義","指某一帶地方，較正式。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： Neighbourhood 適合有街舖與居民的社區；district 適合有界線的市區片區；vicinity 只指某明確地點周邊。Site 偏單一活動地點，community 可指人群而非地點；均不能機械取代來源 area。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"來源的 area 是七間空置店舖所在的一帶實際地方。若強調住戶與街舖，用 neighbourhood；有名稱或正式界線的市內片區，用 district；較中性正式地說某一帶，用 locality；指車站、劇院等某點周圍，用 vicinity of。Aspect/domain 是抽象方面，region 可能過大，space/site 可能過小。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"neighbourhood","meaning":"社區；附近街區","note":"店舖、住戶及相連街道構成的可步行社區；英式拼寫 neighbourhood。","collocations":"visit the neighbourhood; shops in the neighbourhood; neighbourhood residents","example":"Families explored the neighbourhood after the empty shops reopened as galleries.","exampleZh":"空置店舖改作畫廊重開後，家庭到附近街區探索。","contrast":"與 district 可重疊，但 neighbourhood 較突出生活社區。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the vacant shops reopened, children from nearby homes led visitors around the area and introduced local shopkeepers.","zh":"空置店舖重開後，附近住戶的孩子帶訪客走訪該區，並介紹本地店主。","upgrade":"After the vacant shops reopened, children from nearby homes led visitors around the neighbourhood and introduced local shopkeepers.","answer":"neighbourhood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"neighbourhood","explanation":"附近住戶、店主和相連街道構成生活社區，neighbourhood 最貼切。"},{"letter":"B","text":"individual shop space","explanation":"帶訪客走訪的不只一間店內。"},{"letter":"C","text":"wider region","explanation":"wider region 把街舖周邊擴大過度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"officially designated district","explanation":"題句有附近住戶和街舖，未說政府正式劃區；neighbourhood 較合生活社區。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resident community alone","explanation":"居民群體是當地的人；題句帶訪客走訪的是有街道和商店的地方。"},{"letter":"F","text":"immediate vicinity of one shop","explanation":"孩子帶訪客走訪多間街舖與住戶周邊，不只某一間店門外。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The walking map showed the area’s small parks, corner shops and routes between homes across several connected streets.","zh":"步行地圖標示了相連數條街道上的小公園、街角店舖，以及住宅之間的路線。","upgrade":"The walking map showed the neighbourhood’s small parks, corner shops and routes between homes across several connected streets.","answer":"neighbourhood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one residential block","explanation":"地圖橫跨數條相連街道，不只一個住宅街段。"},{"letter":"B","text":"neighbourhood","explanation":"住宅間路線和街角商店呈現一個 neighbourhood。"},{"letter":"C","text":"whole region","explanation":"沒有跨城範圍，whole region 過大。"},{"letter":"D","text":"officially bounded district","explanation":"沒有正式邊界資訊；地圖呈現日常步行社區。"},{"letter":"E","text":"one shopping site","explanation":"小公園與住宅間路線不會全在單一購物地點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"the resident community alone","explanation":"居民是人群，而地圖標示的是他們生活的街道與設施。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"district","meaning":"城區；片區","note":"城市內可辨認的片區，常有名稱、界線或共同功能；不等於整個城市。","collocations":"the arts district; a shopping district; visit the district","example":"The festival brought visitors into the old market district.","exampleZh":"節日活動把訪客帶到舊街市區。","contrast":"District 可按行政或功能劃分；vicinity 只說某點周圍。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The former warehouse street and the market square are both inside the city’s officially designated arts area.","zh":"舊貨倉街和街市廣場都位於市政府正式劃定的藝術區內。","upgrade":"The former warehouse street and the market square are both inside the city’s officially designated arts district.","answer":"arts district","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one arts venue","explanation":"舊貨倉街與街市廣場是兩處地點，超過單一場館。"},{"letter":"B","text":"arts district","explanation":"市內正式劃定的藝術片區可稱 arts district。"},{"letter":"C","text":"whole city","explanation":"不能把市內一區說成全城。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one gallery site","explanation":"兩處公共地點不是同一畫廊範圍。"},{"letter":"E","text":"informal arts neighbourhood","explanation":"可描述生活社區，但 officially designated 指正式劃定片區，arts district 更準。"},{"letter":"F","text":"artist community","explanation":"藝術家群體是人，不是市政府劃定的地理範圍。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The area contains several connected streets of independent bookshops and is marked on city signs as the Book Quarter.","zh":"該區有幾條相連街道，聚集獨立書店，市內路牌標示為「書店區」。","upgrade":"The book district contains several connected streets of independent bookshops and is marked on city signs as the Book Quarter.","answer":"book district","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one bookshop site","explanation":"題句是數條相連街道與多間獨立書店，不能縮成一店。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bookshop neighbourhood","explanation":"可泛指附近書店社區，但路牌明定 Book Quarter，district 更表達命名片區。"},{"letter":"C","text":"entire city","explanation":"路牌標的是城市其中一區。"},{"letter":"D","text":"book district","explanation":"數條相連街道有共同書店功能和路牌名稱，book district 最精確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"one shop interior","explanation":"幾條街的範圍不是一間書店內。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bookshop community","explanation":"可指經營者和讀者社群，並非路牌標示的地理片區。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"locality","meaning":"一帶地方","note":"較正式的地點說法，適合報告某一帶的客流、人流或設施；未必有正式邊界。","collocations":"visit the locality; businesses in the locality; the surrounding locality","example":"The survey recorded how many people visited the locality during the exhibition.","exampleZh":"調查記錄展覽期間有多少人到訪該一帶。","contrast":"比 neighbourhood 中性、正式；不是抽象 domain。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The report counted visitors to the area across several streets around the weekend market, without defining an official district boundary.","zh":"報告統計週末市集周圍數條街道一帶的到訪人數，沒有劃定正式分區邊界。","upgrade":"The report counted visitors to the locality across several streets around the weekend market, without defining an official district boundary.","answer":"locality","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"single market site","explanation":"報告統計市集周圍數條街道，不只市集單一場地。"},{"letter":"B","text":"market community as people","explanation":"題目統計到訪的地點，不是把被到訪的人群稱作地方。"},{"letter":"C","text":"administrative district","explanation":"沒有行政邊界，district 的正式感不合此處線索。"},{"letter":"D","text":"entire metropolitan region","explanation":"週末市集的周邊不等於整個都會區。"},{"letter":"E","text":"locality","explanation":"沒有正式邊界的一帶地方可用 locality，符合報告的客流統計。"},{"letter":"F","text":"policy area of commerce","explanation":"商業政策範疇是抽象分類，不能被週末市場訪客實地到訪。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Researchers listed the area’s bus stops, vacant shops and clinics across several connected streets before estimating weekend foot traffic there.","zh":"研究人員列出相連數條街道一帶的巴士站、空置店舖及診所，再估計當地週末人流。","upgrade":"Researchers listed the locality’s bus stops, vacant shops and clinics across several connected streets before estimating weekend foot traffic there.","answer":"locality","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"locality","explanation":"巴士站、店舖、診所在某一帶分布，locality 概括中性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one vacant-shop block","explanation":"巴士站、店舖與診所橫跨數條街道，超過一個店舖街段。"},{"letter":"C","text":"metropolitan region","explanation":"沒有整個都會區的規模。"},{"letter":"D","text":"official administrative district","explanation":"沒有正式行政界線線索；locality 只說這一帶。"},{"letter":"E","text":"local community as residents","explanation":"研究列出設施及到訪人流，並非只研究常住居民。"},{"letter":"F","text":"immediate vicinity of one bus stop","explanation":"設施分布包括店舖與診所，未限定單一車站周邊。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"vicinity","meaning":"某地附近","note":"必須有可辨認的中心點，如車站、店舖或廣場；常說 the vicinity of。","collocations":"in the vicinity of the station; shops in the vicinity; explore the immediate vicinity","example":"The new exhibition drew people into the vicinity of the old station.","exampleZh":"新展覽吸引人們來到舊車站附近。","contrast":"Vicinity 是某點周圍，不能把整座城市或遙遠地區稱其 vicinity。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the station opened, visitors explored the area around it, including the two lanes behind the ticket office.","zh":"車站啟用後，訪客探索車站周圍一帶，包括售票處後面的兩條小巷。","upgrade":"After the station opened, visitors explored the vicinity of the station, including the two lanes behind the ticket office.","answer":"vicinity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"whole station district","explanation":"題句只描寫車站周邊兩條小巷，district 暗示更完整片區。"},{"letter":"B","text":"station building alone","explanation":"訪客探索售票處後方小巷，非只進車站大樓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"vicinity","explanation":"around it 與兩條小巷清楚指車站附近，即 vicinity。"},{"letter":"D","text":"official railway district","explanation":"沒有劃定鐵路行政片區的線索。"},{"letter":"E","text":"entire metropolitan region","explanation":"兩條小巷不等於整個都會區。"},{"letter":"F","text":"station precinct as a formal zone","explanation":"沒有正式 precinct 邊界；around it 只說車站附近。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The new exhibition brought customers to the area near the old theatre, and cafés on the adjacent streets stayed open late.","zh":"新展覽把顧客帶到舊劇院附近；鄰近街道的咖啡店因此延長營業。","upgrade":"The new exhibition brought customers to the vicinity of the old theatre, and cafés on the adjacent streets stayed open late.","answer":"vicinity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"theatre foyer only","explanation":"鄰街咖啡店亦受益，顧客不只到劇院門廳。"},{"letter":"B","text":"vicinity","explanation":"near the old theatre 和 adjacent streets 支持 vicinity。"},{"letter":"C","text":"whole theatre district","explanation":"只明言劇院旁的鄰街，未說整個劇院片區。"},{"letter":"D","text":"official theatre precinct","explanation":"沒有正式劇院專區界線，near the theatre 只指周邊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"theatre audience as people","explanation":"觀眾是人，句中到訪的是劇院及鄰街一帶。"},{"letter":"F","text":"theatre grounds only","explanation":"鄰近街道的咖啡店在劇院地界之外，only 過窄。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"aspect / facet · 議題的方面不能被到訪","zh":"中文辨析： 若說 an area of concern，area 可抽象；來源說數千人 visited the area，且前文是七間店所在處，故 aspect/facet 會把實地地點變成想法。","point":"Visit a place; discuss an aspect."},{"word":"domain / field · 知識領域與地理位置不同","zh":"中文辨析： Domain 可指科學、商業等領域；數千訪客到街舖參觀，不是在知識領域內旅遊。只有課題討論才可能用 domain。","point":"A field of study is not the urban locality visited."},{"word":"region / city · 空間規模被擴大","zh":"中文辨析： Region 可跨多個區甚至城市；city 是全城。原文只證明七間空舖周邊一帶吸引訪客，不能推論 4,000 人走遍整個地區或城市。","point":"The scale must come from the sentence."},{"word":"shop space / site · 空間規模被縮小","zh":"中文辨析： 一間店內 space 或單一 site 是可能活動地點，來源的 the area 指店舖周圍的地區。若句子確實只描述店內才可用 space。","point":"One room or site is narrower than the surrounding area."},{"word":"community / residents · 人群與地方不同","zh":"中文辨析： Community 有時可指社區地點，也可指當地人；the residents 是人群。題句說訪客到訪物理場所，不能改成訪問所有居民。","point":"A neighbourhood may have a community, but people and place are distinct."}],"moduleNumber":13},{"id":"lesson-014","sourceId":66,"headword":"amount","title":"Amount","titleZh":"少得可數的食材份量","subtitle":"少得可數的食材份量","description":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，6.1 的餐廳評論批評海鮮飯食材有限，稱蛤蜊、蝦及切碎香腸只有「a count-on-your-fingers amount」。整句還說食客對乾飯及少量配料失望。Amount 是數量名詞；count-on-your-fingers 給它「少得屈指可數」的負面語氣。蛤蜊與蝦可以數個，切碎香腸也可按碎塊計，但 sausage 作食材時常可視為不可數，因此改寫須小心名詞與量詞搭配。以下練習為原創，數字不冒充考卷實際份量。[2012 Paper 4 set 6.1 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，6.1 的餐廳評論批評海鮮飯食材有限，稱蛤蜊、蝦及切碎香腸只有「a count-on-your-fingers amount」。整句還說食客對乾飯及少量配料失望。Amount 是數量名詞；count-on-your-fingers 給它「少得屈指可數」的負面語氣。蛤蜊與蝦可以數個，切碎香腸也可按碎塊計，但 sausage 作食材時常可視為不可數，因此改寫須小心名詞與量詞搭配。以下練習為原創，數字不冒充考卷實際份量。[2012 Paper 4 set 6.1 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["quantity","直接","指數量；若要保留「少得可數」，須另加 small/tiny 等修飾語。"],["total","不宜直接換","指加總後的全部數；可說 the total number of prawns，但不能用 a total of clams 無數字地替換原片語。"],["sum","假近義","主要指款項或數字相加結果，a sum of clams 不自然。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： A small quantity of 保留少量；a small number of 限可數蝦/蛤蜊；only a handful of 口語具體、近原文屈指可數；a meagre portion of 說餐盤上分給食客的份量不足；a pitifully small quantity of 強化評論者認為少得可憐。Scant 可寫 scant seafood，但較正式且與 paltry 的缺乏評價相近；a few 與 small number/handful 重疊；a smattering/scattering 要配合零星分布的視覺情境，不是一般重量。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Quantity 是中性數量；a small quantity of 明說整體少量。\n- A small number of 數蛤蜊、蝦或香腸片；only a handful of 是更生動的寥寥幾個。\n- A meagre portion of 批評分到的餐點份量不足；a pitifully small quantity of 是更直接的少得可憐、不值的評價。\n- Sum 多指相加數字，total 要有完整加總結構；variety 是種類，不能替代食材數量。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"quantity","meaning":"數量；中性量度詞","note":"只談某種食材有多少、可量度多少時用；本身不說多或少，需保留 tiny/small 等負面量度線索。","collocations":"the quantity of seafood; a tiny quantity of prawns; measure a quantity in grams","example":"The chef weighed the quantity of seafood added to each pan.","exampleZh":"廚師稱量每個平底鍋加入的海鮮份量。","contrast":"Quantity 近於 amount，但單獨沒有原文「少得可數」的批評；sum 不是食材的常用量詞。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The amount of seafood in the paella was only forty grams, according to the kitchen scale.","zh":"根據廚房磅秤，海鮮飯中的海鮮份量只有四十克。","upgrade":"The quantity of seafood in the paella was only forty grams, according to the kitchen scale.","answer":"quantity of seafood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"quantity of seafood","explanation":"磅秤以克數量整體海鮮，quantity 直接替換 amount；only forty grams 保留少量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"number of seafood items","explanation":"number 要逐個數海鮮個體，四十克是質量而非個數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"portion of seafood","explanation":"portion 偏一人分到的一份，此句稱的是海鮮飯中磅得的總量。"},{"letter":"D","text":"total number of seafood items","explanation":"total number 須按件數，原句以磅秤稱整體海鮮重量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"variety of seafood","explanation":"variety 指海鮮種類，不是四十克的質量。"},{"letter":"F","text":"quality of seafood","explanation":"quality 指品質，不能由克數推知。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The reviewer checked the amount of stock left in the paella pan: the measuring cup showed only thirty millilitres.","zh":"評論者檢查海鮮飯鍋中剩餘的高湯份量：量杯顯示只有三十毫升。","upgrade":"The reviewer checked the quantity of stock left in the paella pan: the measuring cup showed only thirty millilitres.","answer":"quantity of stock","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"number of stock portions","explanation":"stock 是液體，題句用毫升量度，不是數有幾份高湯。"},{"letter":"B","text":"capacity for stock","explanation":"capacity 是容器可盛多少，原句是鍋內實際剩餘高湯。"},{"letter":"C","text":"supply of stock","explanation":"supply 指備用庫存，不是鍋中量杯量得的殘餘。"},{"letter":"D","text":"quantity of stock","explanation":"量杯顯示三十毫升，quantity 可自然說鍋裏剩餘高湯的量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"serving of stock","explanation":"serving 是供人飲用的一份，不是鍋底剩餘液體。"},{"letter":"F","text":"quality of stock","explanation":"quality 說味道或品質，毫升說量。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"a small quantity of","meaning":"少量的；可配總體食材","note":"整體食材或質量不多時用，適合 seafood、rice、sauce 等不可數或集合名詞；比 a small number of 更不強調個數。","collocations":"a small quantity of seafood; a small quantity of rice; only a small quantity of sauce","example":"The shared paella contained a small quantity of seafood beneath the rice.","exampleZh":"這份共食海鮮飯的米飯下只有少量海鮮。","contrast":"Small quantity 描述總量；small number 須接可數的 clams/prawns，不宜接 seafood 當物質總量。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The amount of mixed seafood in the paella barely covered one corner of the pan, though the dish was meant for two people.","zh":"海鮮飯中的混合海鮮幾乎只鋪滿鍋的一角，儘管這道菜是供兩人享用。","upgrade":"A small quantity of mixed seafood in the paella barely covered one corner of the pan, though the dish was meant for two people.","answer":"a small quantity of mixed seafood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a meagre assortment of mixed seafood","explanation":"assortment 說種類組合，原句說總量僅佔鍋的一角。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a small number of mixed seafood","explanation":"mixed seafood 作集合物質，不能直接用 number 數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a small quantity of mixed seafood","explanation":"混合海鮮佔鍋一角，small quantity 說整體少量且不必逐件數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a paltry selection of mixed seafood","explanation":"selection 重在可選的種類，不能替換鍋內配料總量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a limited variety of mixed seafood","explanation":"variety 說種類少，不是總量少。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a handful of mixed seafood","explanation":"handful 適合個別蝦或蛤蜊；mixed seafood 可含切碎不可數食材。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The amount of sauce left at the bottom of the bowl was too little to coat the rice.","zh":"碗底剩餘的醬汁太少，無法拌勻米飯。","upgrade":"The small quantity of sauce left at the bottom of the bowl was too little to coat the rice.","answer":"a small quantity of sauce","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small number of sauce portions","explanation":"number 須數可數的獨立份；碗底剩的醬汁是液體總量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a meagre portion of sauce","explanation":"portion 暗示供人吃的一份，此處是碗底殘餘。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a handful of sauce","explanation":"handful 不可自然量醬汁。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a small supply of sauce","explanation":"supply 指可用庫存；這裏是碗底實際剩餘的一點醬汁。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a limited variety of sauce","explanation":"variety 指醬汁種類，與碗底剩餘量無關。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a small quantity of sauce","explanation":"醬汁液體只剩一點，small quantity 合 mass noun 又保留客觀少量。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"a small number of","meaning":"少數幾個；限可數名詞","note":"數得出的蝦、蛤蜊或香腸片只有幾件時用；後面接複數可數名詞。","collocations":"a small number of clams; a small number of prawns; only a small number of sausage pieces","example":"There were a small number of prawns in the large pan of rice.","exampleZh":"一大鍋飯裏只有少數幾隻蝦。","contrast":"Number 數個體；amount/quantity 可量整體食材。不可說 a small number of sauce。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The amount of clams in the two-person paella was just three, so the diners each received at most two.","zh":"雙人海鮮飯裏的蛤蜊只有三隻，所以每名食客最多分到兩隻。","upgrade":"A small number of clams—just three—were in the two-person paella, so the diners each received at most two.","answer":"a small number of clams","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a limited supply of clams","explanation":"supply 指可用存貨，不是已放進這鍋飯的三隻蛤蜊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a small number of clams","explanation":"三隻蛤蜊為可數個體，small number 最精確；完整改寫須用 were。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a meagre portion of clams","explanation":"portion 說分給一人吃的一份，題句先說鍋裏三隻總數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"only a scattering of clams","explanation":"scattering 暗示零星散布，原句直接給出確切隻數；不能由三隻推知分布。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a total amount of clams","explanation":"total amount 對可數三隻不如 total number，且未完成自然改寫。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a limited variety of clams","explanation":"variety 是種類，不是三隻個數。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The amount of sausage pieces in the rice was four; the cook had cut them into separate slices.","zh":"飯裏的香腸片只有四片；廚師已把香腸切成獨立薄片。","upgrade":"A small number of sausage pieces—four—were in the rice; the cook had cut them into separate slices.","answer":"a small number of sausage pieces","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small quantity of sausage","explanation":"quantity of sausage 可量肉的總重量，句中明數四片。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a meagre portion of sausage","explanation":"portion 指分給食客的份，未表四片個數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a scattering of sausage pieces","explanation":"scattering 說碎片零散分布，句中只明說四片而未說分布。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a small number of sausage","explanation":"sausage 作食材物質時不能直接用 number，需加 pieces。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a small number of sausage pieces","explanation":"切成四片可數 pieces，small number 精確，重寫主語須用複數 were。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a sum of sausage pieces","explanation":"sum 不與香腸片作自然量詞。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"only a handful of","meaning":"只有寥寥幾個","note":"在評論中形象地說可數物寥寥無幾；不一定真的用手抓或剛好五個。","collocations":"only a handful of clams; a handful of prawns; a handful of sausage pieces","example":"Only a handful of clams appeared among the rice grains.","exampleZh":"米粒之間只見到寥寥幾隻蛤蜊。","contrast":"Handful of 可呼應 count-on-your-fingers 的口語少量，但食材若是液體，宜用 a small quantity of 而非 a handful of sauce。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The amount of prawns in the big pan was tiny: the diners could point to each one without moving the rice.","zh":"大鍋飯裏的蝦極少，食客不用撥開米飯就能逐隻指出來。","upgrade":"There were only a handful of prawns in the big pan: the diners could point to each one without moving the rice.","answer":"only a handful of prawns","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"only a handful of prawns","explanation":"蝦寥寥幾隻，食客不用撥飯就可逐一指出，handful 生動呼應屈指可數。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a small supply of prawns","explanation":"supply 指廚房可用的蝦存貨，句中說鍋裏露出的蝦。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a meagre portion of prawns","explanation":"portion 焦點在食客分到的份，句中是鍋內一共幾隻。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a measured volume of prawns","explanation":"volume 以體積量度；句中食客是逐隻看見蝦，沒有體積資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a sparse selection of prawns","explanation":"selection 暗示蝦種類，題句只談隻數。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a measured quantity of prawns","explanation":"measured quantity 需秤重或體積資料，這裏以眼數個體。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The amount of olives the cook put on the salad was small enough for a child to count them on one hand before the dish reached the table.","zh":"廚師放在沙律上的橄欖少得讓一名孩子在菜上桌前就能用一隻手數完。","upgrade":"The cook put only a handful of olives on the salad; a child could count them on one hand before the dish reached the table.","answer":"only a handful of olives","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a limited supply of olives","explanation":"supply 指備用橄欖庫存，句中孩子數的是沙律上已有的橄欖。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a meagre portion of olives","explanation":"meagre portion 表餐量不足，但此句聚焦一手可數的顆數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a sparse scattering of olives","explanation":"sparse scattering 指橄欖零散分布；題句只說數量少，未說位置。"},{"letter":"D","text":"only a handful of olives","explanation":"孩子一隻手便數完，only a handful of 準確保留口語「屈指可數」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a small quantity of olive oil","explanation":"olive oil 把整顆橄欖改成橄欖油。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a pitifully small quantity of olives","explanation":"paltry 表不值批評，句中只給可數的趣味畫面。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"a meagre portion of","meaning":"少得不足的一份","note":"分到餐盤上的配料份量不足、令食客覺得不值時用；焦點是分配給人吃的食物，而不只是倉庫裏有多少。","collocations":"a meagre portion of seafood; a meagre portion of prawns; a meagre serving","example":"For two diners, the plate held a meagre portion of seafood.","exampleZh":"對兩位食客來說，盤上的海鮮份量少得可憐。","contrast":"Portion 是供食客享用的一份；quantity 可指食材總量，並不一定說每份夠不夠。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The amount of seafood served to the two diners barely filled one spoon, leaving both dissatisfied with their share.","zh":"供兩名食客吃的海鮮份量連一匙也幾乎裝不滿，兩人都不滿自己分到的部分。","upgrade":"A meagre portion of seafood served to the two diners barely filled one spoon, leaving both dissatisfied with their share.","answer":"a meagre portion of seafood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small stock of seafood","explanation":"stock 指廚房存貨，這裏說已端給兩位食客的一份。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a paltry selection of seafood","explanation":"selection 著眼種類或可選項，句中投訴的是兩人分得太少。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a meagre portion of seafood","explanation":"兩人分到的海鮮連一匙也不滿、均失望，meagre portion 最貼合供餐不足。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a small number of seafood pieces","explanation":"題句未數海鮮碎塊個數，只說一匙的份量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a scant variety of seafood","explanation":"variety 指種類而非供餐多寡。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a measured serving of seafood","explanation":"沒有秤重或精確量度，且 measured 不說不足。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The amount of vegetables each child received at school lunch covered only one edge of the tray, and the staff had to offer extra servings.","zh":"學校午餐中，每名孩子分到的蔬菜只鋪滿餐盤的一邊，職員不得不再添菜。","upgrade":"The meagre portion of vegetables each child received at school lunch covered only one edge of the tray, and the staff had to offer extra servings.","answer":"a meagre portion of vegetables","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small number of vegetable pieces","explanation":"沒有逐塊數蔬菜，只說每名孩子分到的一份太小。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a limited supply of vegetables","explanation":"supply 說廚房存貨，句中說每名孩子餐盤上的份量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a scant selection of vegetables","explanation":"selection 說種類，非餐盤覆蓋面積。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an exact quantity of vegetables","explanation":"沒有精確數字可說 exact。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a paltry price for vegetables","explanation":"價格未提，paltry price 也會指廉價而不是少量。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a meagre portion of vegetables","explanation":"每名孩子分到的蔬菜只佔盤邊，需再添菜，meagre portion 聚焦供餐不足。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"a pitifully small quantity of","meaning":"少得可憐的量；較強批評","note":"評論者認為食材量遠低於合理期望、帶明顯不滿時用；語氣比中性的 small quantity 強。","collocations":"a pitifully small quantity of seafood; a pitifully small quantity of filling; a pitifully small quantity for the price","example":"The costly seafood rice contained a pitifully small quantity of prawns and clams.","exampleZh":"這份昂貴的海鮮飯只放了少得可憐的蝦和蛤蜊。","contrast":"Paltry 是評價不足和失望；small 可只是客觀量少，例如試吃份量。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At that price, the reviewer called the amount of seafood in the paella insulting: three tiny pieces were buried in a large pan of rice.","zh":"以這個價錢，評論者認為海鮮飯的海鮮份量少得不像話：一大鍋飯裏只藏着三小塊。","upgrade":"At that price, the reviewer called the pitifully small quantity of seafood in the paella insulting: three tiny pieces were buried in a large pan of rice.","answer":"a pitifully small quantity of seafood","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small supply of seafood","explanation":"supply 指庫存，原句批評這份已上桌海鮮飯裏的配料量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a pitifully small quantity of seafood","explanation":"昂貴餐點只放三小塊，評論者更覺受辱；pitifully small quantity 同時表明量少及強烈不滿。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a thin layer of seafood","explanation":"thin layer 說海鮮如何鋪在飯面；原句批評的是整鍋只得三小塊，不是覆蓋厚薄。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a scant number of seafood","explanation":"seafood 作集合物質不可直接用 number。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a limited variety of seafood","explanation":"variety 說種類，題句批評食材總量。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a measured quantity of seafood","explanation":"沒有量度數據，measured 亦不表不值。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The meal kit claimed it would fill six dumplings, but the amount of filling inside barely filled one; customers demanded refunds.","zh":"餐包聲稱餡料足夠包六隻餃子，實際上卻連一隻也幾乎填不滿，顧客要求退款。","upgrade":"The meal kit claimed it would fill six dumplings, but the pitifully small quantity of filling inside barely filled one; customers demanded refunds.","answer":"a pitifully small quantity of filling","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a small stock of filling","explanation":"stock 指廠方存貨，題句說這一包餐包內的餡料。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a meagre portion of filling","explanation":"portion 指供人吃的一份，不如 amount 指整包餡料總量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an insufficient supply of filling","explanation":"supply 指可用庫存，句中是單一餐包內實際裝入的餡料。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a disappointing serving of filling","explanation":"serving 偏餐桌上分給人的一份，這裏是餐包內餡料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a pitifully small quantity of filling","explanation":"號稱六隻卻幾乎填不滿一隻，還要求退款，paltry 直接表少得可憐。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a limited variety of filling","explanation":"variety 說餡料種類，句中是餡料總量。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"sum / total · 加總與食材量不可直接互換","zh":"中文辨析： Sum 常說錢或數字相加；total 可說 the total number of prawns was four。原文的 an amount of clams 是食材數量，沒有一個要相加的款項或明列的總數。","point":"A food quantity is not automatically a numerical sum or final total."},{"word":"amount / number · 可數與不可數搭配","zh":"中文辨析： A number of prawns/clams 可以；a number of sauce 不行。An amount of seafood/sauce 自然；把每隻蝦當個體時 number 更清楚。原文把多種配料混說，改寫須選合適上位名詞或重排。","point":"Count individual items with number; measure an aggregate with amount or quantity."},{"word":"portion / ingredient · 一份與一種食材不同","zh":"中文辨析： A small portion of seafood 說分到的份量；few ingredients 可能只說種類少，即使每種放很多。原評論兩者都批評，但原 headword 的局部意思是具體數量少。","point":"Few kinds of ingredients and too little food are different complaints."},{"word":"handful / hand · 慣用量詞不是抓握動作","zh":"中文辨析： A handful of clams 指寥寥幾隻，通常不是說廚師真的抓一把；a hand of clams 不自然。液體醬汁則不能用 handful。","point":"Handful is an idiomatic small count, not a literal action or liquid measure."},{"word":"small / paltry / meagre · 客觀少量與失望評價","zh":"中文辨析： Small quantity 可是刻意提供的試吃份量；paltry 表少得不合理，meagre portion 表供餐不足。原餐評的不滿支持負面詞，但在中性食譜不能隨意加批評。","point":"A low quantity is a fact; paltry or meagre adds judgement about adequacy."}],"moduleNumber":14},{"id":"lesson-015","sourceId":41,"headword":"affect","title":"Affect","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 individual question asks whether technology has negatively affected our lives. Affected is the past participle of the verb affect: technology may have caused a change in people's lives. Negatively supplies the adverse direction. The question asks for an opinion; it does not establish that technology has harmed everyone.","sourceSense":"The 2012 individual question asks whether technology has negatively affected our lives. Affected is the past participle of the verb affect: technology may have caused a change in people's lives. Negatively supplies the adverse direction. The question asks for an opinion; it does not establish that technology has harmed everyone.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["influence","Contextual: may suggest gradual shaping of behaviour or opinion; add negatively to preserve direction."],["impact","Contextual: transitive verb often suggests a noticeable consequence; do not assume a large effect without a scale clue."],["change","Recast: names what became different; changed our lives alone loses the adverse direction, so add for the worse or an explicit harmful result."],["have an effect on","Close noun-phrase recast: have a negative effect on preserves the source direction."],["have an impact on","Contextual noun-phrase recast: use have a negative impact on where a substantial consequence is supported."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Shape is useful when a long-term pattern develops, but it overlaps influence here and does not by itself preserve the negative judgment; it is noted as a close boundary, not inflated into a duplicate lesson item. Alter overlaps change and often suggests a tangible revision; harm/damage assert a stronger harmful outcome than the source question establishes. Effect is a noun in have an effect on, whereas affect is normally the verb here. No major incoming candidate is omitted."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["influence","人的決定或看法在一段時間內受作用，可保留未被強迫的程度。","不能把影響誇大成 determine/dictate；改寫原題須保留負面方向。"],["impact","有取消過半服務、重大預算變動等明顯作用時，用作及物動詞。","Impact 不自帶負面，也不宜為小事虛增程度。"],["change","句子交代前後有甚麼不同，例如作息或照片權限。","Change 不說明好壞；原題要補回 for the worse 等負面線索。"],["have an effect on","用名詞 effect 說明某事對聽覺、閱讀速度等有無作用。","須說 effect on；不要把開放疑問改成已證實的結果。"],["have an impact on","強調一條規則或服務停擺影響的人數、範圍或持續時間。","須接 on；在來源語境加 negative 才保留原題的方向。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 人的看法或選擇逐漸受左右，用 influence；作用規模明顯可用動詞 impact 或名詞片語 have an impact on；要指出具體前後差異，用 change；只問是否有作用，用 have an effect on。2012 原題另有 negatively 和 Do you believe：任何整句改寫都要保留負面方向與待討論語氣。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"influence","meaning":"影響選擇或看法","note":"使人的選擇、習慣或看法朝某方向變化，常指逐漸或間接的作用。","collocations":"influence decisions; influence attitudes; negatively influence habits.","example":"Repeated product videos influenced the pupils' buying decisions over several months.","exampleZh":"幾個月來，反覆播放的產品影片影響了學生的購物決定。","contrast":"Influence 未必是強烈或有害的作用；若改寫原題，須保留 negatively，亦不能把影響寫成強迫或決定一切。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Repeated recommendations on the app affected which books pupils borrowed over the term, though no one had to follow them.","zh":"一整個學期，應用程式反覆推薦書籍，影響了學生借閱哪些書，儘管沒有人必須照做。","upgrade":"Repeated recommendations on the app influenced which books pupils borrowed over the term, though no one had to follow them.","answer":"influence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"determine","explanation":"Determined 表示推薦決定了借書結果；句子說學生無須照做，沒有這麼強的控制。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reflect","explanation":"Reflected 會說推薦反映既有借書選擇，倒轉了句中推薦作用於選擇的方向。"},{"letter":"C","text":"influence","explanation":"Influenced 保留推薦逐漸左右借書選擇、但沒有強迫學生的意思。"},{"letter":"D","text":"prohibit","explanation":"Prohibited 是禁止借某些書；程式只是推薦，沒有設下禁令。"},{"letter":"E","text":"predict","explanation":"Predicted 是預測借書結果，不表示推薦改變了學生的選擇。"},{"letter":"F","text":"record","explanation":"Recorded 只表示記下借閱紀錄，沒有表達推薦對選擇的作用。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Her opinion of the reading app was affected by other parents' comments over several weeks, although she made up her own mind in the end.","zh":"幾星期來，其他家長的評論影響了她對閱讀應用程式的看法，雖然最後仍由她自己作決定。","upgrade":"Her opinion of the reading app was influenced by other parents' comments over several weeks, although she made up her own mind in the end.","answer":"influence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"confirm","explanation":"評論可能改變而非證實她原有看法；原句沒有說最後意見與起初相同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replace","explanation":"Replaced 暗示評論完全取代她自己的看法；句末說她仍自行決定。"},{"letter":"C","text":"dictate","explanation":"Dictated 表示他人控制結論，與最後自己作決定不符。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reflect","explanation":"被動句說看法受評論作用；was reflected by 會變成評論呈現她的看法，因果方向相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"predict","explanation":"家長評論不是對她日後看法的預測，句子說的是幾星期中的影響。"},{"letter":"F","text":"influence","explanation":"Was influenced by 自然表示她的看法受其他家長評論左右，同時保留自主決定。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"impact","meaning":"對……造成顯著影響","note":"作及物動詞，表示對某事造成可察覺、通常較大的影響；正式語境亦可改用 have an impact on。","collocations":"impact services; impact a budget; negatively impact learning.","example":"The week-long network failure impacted almost every online lesson at the centre.","exampleZh":"長達一星期的網絡故障影響了中心幾乎每一節網課。","contrast":"小小不便也可 affect 人，未必足以說 impact；句中應有作用範圍或後果線索。Impact 本身不等於負面。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The three-day outage affected the clinic's remote appointments: more than half had to be cancelled.","zh":"長達三天的網絡故障影響了診所的遠程診症預約：超過一半須取消。","upgrade":"The three-day outage impacted the clinic's remote appointments: more than half had to be cancelled.","answer":"impact","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"predict","explanation":"故障沒有預報預約會取消；句子交代它實際造成大規模取消。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reflect","explanation":"Reflected 只表示反映取消情況，不表達網絡故障造成診症中斷。"},{"letter":"C","text":"improve","explanation":"超過一半預約取消，不是診所服務得到改善。"},{"letter":"D","text":"coincide with","explanation":"同時發生不能保留故障導致預約取消的因果關係。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impact","explanation":"Impacted 可指故障對診所服務造成顯著影響；取消過半提供了規模線索。"},{"letter":"F","text":"follow","explanation":"故障在取消之後才出現的時間順序，與句中原因不符。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The proposed fee could affect the food bank's annual budget by nearly a third if it is approved.","zh":"如果建議收費獲批准，它可能影響食物銀行近三分之一的年度預算。","upgrade":"The proposed fee could impact the food bank's annual budget by nearly a third if it is approved.","answer":"impact","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"impact","explanation":"Could impact 保留收費仍屬建議、但一旦通過可能對近三分之一預算造成重大作用的意思。"},{"letter":"B","text":"document","explanation":"記錄預算是會計工作，不是新收費對預算造成的影響。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reflect","explanation":"預算可能反映收費後的變化，但收費不是只「反映」既有預算。"},{"letter":"D","text":"guarantee","explanation":"建議收費尚未獲批，亦不能說它保證食物銀行的預算結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"result from","explanation":"Result from 會把收費寫成預算產生的結果，倒轉句中的因果方向。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ignore","explanation":"收費若影響近三分之一預算，便不能說它忽略預算。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"change","meaning":"改變","note":"使做法、狀態或結果變得不同，重點在前後差異；須指出改變了甚麼。","collocations":"change a routine; change the way people study; change lives for the worse.","example":"The new timetable changed when pupils could use the library after school.","exampleZh":"新時間表改變了學生放學後可使用圖書館的時間。","contrast":"Change 不自帶好壞判斷；原題的 negatively affected 應改作 changed ... for the worse 或寫出不利結果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Online homework affected how the family planned its evenings: they began checking assignments after dinner rather than before it.","zh":"網上功課影響了這家人安排晚間時間的方式：他們開始在晚飯後而非飯前查看作業。","upgrade":"Online homework changed how the family planned its evenings: they began checking assignments after dinner rather than before it.","answer":"change","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"improve","explanation":"句子只說查看作業由飯前改為飯後，沒有證據說晚間安排變得更好。"},{"letter":"B","text":"change","explanation":"Changed how 對應飯前與飯後的明確差別，沒有憑空加入好壞判斷。"},{"letter":"C","text":"limit","explanation":"Limited 表示限制可安排的選擇；原句只交代時間改了。"},{"letter":"D","text":"repeat","explanation":"新習慣與舊習慣不同，不能說只是重複原有安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"measure","explanation":"Measured 是量度安排，不能表示安排本身由飯前轉成飯後。"},{"letter":"F","text":"copy","explanation":"家庭沒有模仿另一個家庭的安排，句子描述自身時間變化。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The new privacy setting affected who could see the club's photos: only members could open them now.","zh":"新的私隱設定影響了誰能看到社團照片：現在只有會員能開啟照片。","upgrade":"The new privacy setting changed who could see the club's photos: only members could open them now.","answer":"change","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"improve","explanation":"會員專用可能更私密，但原句未評價這是否較好，只說觀看權限不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"describe","explanation":"設定改動了觀看資格，不只是描述誰原本可看照片。"},{"letter":"C","text":"measure","explanation":"私隱設定不會量度觀眾人數；句子說它限制現在的開啟權限。"},{"letter":"D","text":"confirm","explanation":"Confirmed 是核實既有權限，未表達權限被設定改動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"change","explanation":"Changed who could see 保留「現在只有會員能開啟」所顯示的權限改變。"},{"letter":"F","text":"predict","explanation":"設定不是預測誰可能開啟照片，而是決定誰目前有權開啟。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"have an effect on","meaning":"對……有影響","note":"以名詞 effect 表達因果影響；可加 negative 等形容詞說明方向。","collocations":"have an effect on concentration; have a negative effect on sleep; have little effect on results.","example":"The broken air conditioner had a negative effect on the class's concentration.","exampleZh":"故障的冷氣機對全班的專注力造成負面影響。","contrast":"動詞是 affect，此片語中的名詞是 effect；have an effect on 不自帶負面方向。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The faulty microphone affected how well the audience heard the speaker: several words were inaudible.","zh":"故障的咪高峰影響了觀眾聽清講者說話的程度：有幾個字聽不到。","upgrade":"The faulty microphone had an effect on how well the audience heard the speaker: several words were inaudible.","answer":"have an effect on","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have an affect on","explanation":"片語須用名詞 effect；affect 在原句是動詞，不能作此處的名詞。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be an effect of","explanation":"這會說咪高峰是觀眾聽不清的結果，倒轉故障與聽覺問題的因果方向。"},{"letter":"C","text":"have an effect on","explanation":"Had an effect on 正確以名詞片語表達咪高峰故障對聽清程度的作用，並保留過去時。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have an effect to","explanation":"此搭配要說 effect on 聽清程度，不能接 to。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be affected by","explanation":"被動式需改以「觀眾聽清程度」作主語；不能說咪高峰被聽清程度影響。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have no effect on","explanation":"有些字聽不到，已顯示咪高峰故障確有影響。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Does the font size on a screen affect how quickly pupils can read its instructions, or is speed unchanged?","zh":"螢幕字體大小會影響學生閱讀指示的速度，還是速度不變？","upgrade":"Does the font size on a screen have an effect on how quickly pupils can read its instructions, or is speed unchanged?","answer":"have an effect on","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"determine","explanation":"Determine 暗示字體大小足以決定閱讀速度；問題只問它是否有影響，未排除其他因素。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be the result of","explanation":"字體大小不是學生閱讀速度造成的結果；原句把字體大小放在可能的原因位置。"},{"letter":"C","text":"have an influence from","explanation":"要說 have an influence on 才能接受詞；from 在此把作用方向寫錯。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reflect","explanation":"字體大小可以反映設計選擇，卻不是只「反映」學生的閱讀速度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have an effect on","explanation":"Does ... have an effect on 保留是否影響閱讀速度的開放問題，沒有預設結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have an effect to","explanation":"名詞片語接 on 加受影響的速度，to 不是此搭配。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"have an impact on","meaning":"對……產生顯著影響","note":"以名詞 impact 強調作用的範圍或分量；改寫來源時可說 have a negative impact on。","collocations":"have an impact on daily life; have a major impact on services; have a negative impact on wellbeing.","example":"Closing the only bus route for a month would have a major impact on local commuters.","exampleZh":"唯一一條巴士路線若停駛一個月，會對當地通勤人士造成重大影響。","contrast":"Impact 可正可負，亦常暗示較大作用；若只是短暫小變化，effect 較穩妥。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The new safety rule affected every delivery driver in the district, forcing route changes for six months.","zh":"新安全規則影響了區內每名送貨司機，令他們在六個月內都要改道。","upgrade":"The new safety rule had an impact on every delivery driver in the district, forcing route changes for six months.","answer":"have an impact on","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have only a passing effect on","explanation":"每名司機都須改道六個月，並非轉瞬即逝的輕微作用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be impacted by","explanation":"被動式會把規則寫成受司機影響者，倒轉原句的原因與對象。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reflect","explanation":"規則使司機改道，不只是反映既有路線。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have an impact to","explanation":"此名詞片語要接 on 加受影響的人，不能接 to。"},{"letter":"E","text":"result from","explanation":"句中司機改道源自規則，並非規則源自司機改道。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have an impact on","explanation":"Had an impact on 表規則對所有司機造成持續六個月的明顯作用；過去時符合原句。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Could closing the only bus route for a month affect thousands of commuters?","zh":"若唯一一條巴士路線停駛一個月，會否影響數以千計的通勤人士？","upgrade":"Could closing the only bus route for a month have an impact on thousands of commuters?","answer":"have an impact on","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have an impact on","explanation":"Could ... have an impact on 保留假設疑問，唯一巴士線停駛一個月提供可能影響甚廣的線索。"},{"letter":"B","text":"have an affect on","explanation":"這裏需要名詞 effect 或 impact；affect 是原句的動詞，不可放在 an 後。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be an impact of","explanation":"巴士線停駛是可能的原因，不是數千名通勤人士造成的結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have an impact to","explanation":"影響通勤人士應說 impact on commuters，不能用 to。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have no effect on","explanation":"把開放問題改成「完全沒有影響」的斷言，且忽略唯一巴士線停駛的情況。"},{"letter":"F","text":"result from","explanation":"會說停駛由通勤人士造成，倒轉句中的可能因果方向。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"effect / affect","zh":"中文辨析： 原句 affected 是動詞；effect 通常是名詞，須改成 have an effect on 才能放進句子。不要寫 technology has negatively effected our lives 來表示「影響」。","point":"Affect is the ordinary verb for influence; effect is the noun in have an effect on."},{"word":"change / negatively affect","zh":"中文辨析： Change 只說不同，可能變好、變壞或好壞參半；原題有 negatively，不能改掉評價方向。","point":"Changed our lives does not itself mean changed our lives for the worse."},{"word":"impact / have an impact on","zh":"中文辨析： Impact 可作動詞直接接受詞；have an impact 要接 on。兩者都可正可負，須由語境交代方向和程度。","point":"Compare the outage impacted lessons with the outage had an impact on lessons."},{"word":"harm / negatively affect","zh":"中文辨析： Harm 表明已造成損害；來源只提出「是否有負面影響」的討論問題，沒有證明實際傷害。","point":"An opinion question about possible negative effects is not proof of injury."},{"word":"be affected by / affect","zh":"中文辨析： 被動式 be affected by 可用，但要倒轉主語與原因：pupils were affected by alerts，不能讓警報變成受影響者。","point":"The cause and the affected person change grammatical places in a passive recast."}],"moduleNumber":15},{"id":"lesson-016","sourceId":85,"headword":"appear","title":"Appear","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 passage says government regulations “appear to have exerted a major influence on the mooncake market.” Here appear is an evidential verb followed by a perfect infinitive: the writer cautiously infers a past effect. It does not mean that regulations came into view. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.2](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2012 passage says government regulations “appear to have exerted a major influence on the mooncake market.” Here appear is an evidential verb followed by a perfect infinitive: the writer cautiously infers a past effect. It does not mean that regulations came into view. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.2](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["seem","Close with the same to have + past participle construction and cautious inference."],["look","Contextual recast as it looks as if/though + clause where observations support an inference; bare look to have is unnatural here."],["become visible","False for this source. That is the literal arrival-in-sight sense of appear."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Suggest that is taught as a conditional evidence-led recast when sales figures or reports are named. Apparently can mean “as far as one knows” and may signal hearsay, so it does not preserve the exact evidence basis automatically. Likely predicts probability rather than the source’s observed inference; prove/confirm removes the qualification. Emerge means come into view or become known, another sense. It seems that is a routine clause variant of the taught seem to rather than a separate pedagogic item."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子重點","用法"],"rows":[["主語是規例／情況，保留謹慎推論","seem to have + 過去分詞"],["有眼前可見跡象，改寫整句","it looks as though + 從句"],["主語是數據、訪談等證據","evidence/figures suggest that + 從句"]],"note":"來源的完成式 appear to have exerted 指「看來已造成影響」，不可改成單純將來可能，也不可寫成已完全證實。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"seem to","meaning":"看來似乎","note":"最接近來源的審慎判斷；與完成式 to have + 過去分詞 連用，可保留「看來已經影響」的時間。","collocations":"seem to have affected; seem to be changing; seem to have had an effect.","example":"The new rule seems to have reduced the number of gift boxes sold.","exampleZh":"新規定看來已令禮盒銷量下降。","contrast":"Seem 與 appear 同樣保留不確定；prove 則把推測變成已證實。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The regulations appear to have reduced the sale of luxury mooncake boxes, although the records are incomplete.","zh":"雖然紀錄不完整，這些規例看來已令豪華月餅禮盒銷量下降。","upgrade":"The regulations seem to have reduced the sale of luxury mooncake boxes, although the records are incomplete.","answer":"seem to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"seem to","explanation":"紀錄不完整，seem to have reduced 保留對已發生效果的審慎判斷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"are known to","explanation":"Are known to 暗示已有充分確證，比原句肯定。"},{"letter":"C","text":"are intended to","explanation":"設立規例的意圖不等於從不完整紀錄推斷出的實際銷售效果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"are reported to","explanation":"Are reported to 指其他人的報告，原句是作者從現有紀錄推斷。"},{"letter":"E","text":"are alleged to","explanation":"Alleged 暗示有待證實的指控，此處不是在指控規例。"},{"letter":"F","text":"are expected to","explanation":"Expected 指預期結果，沒有保留從已有銷售紀錄作出的推斷。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"From the shop owners’ interviews, the new limits appear to have changed what customers choose as festival gifts.","zh":"根據店主訪談，新限制看來已改變顧客選擇節日禮物的方式。","upgrade":"From the shop owners’ interviews, the new limits seem to have changed what customers choose as festival gifts.","answer":"seem to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"tend to","explanation":"Tend to 指經常或一般趨向，題句是根據訪談推斷這次限制已帶來的效果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"are designed to","explanation":"規例的設計目的不等於店主觀察到的選購變化。"},{"letter":"C","text":"are proven to","explanation":"訪談提供跡象，未達到 proven 所表示的證明程度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seem to","explanation":"訪談是推斷依據，seem to have changed 保留「看來已改變」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"are claimed to","explanation":"Are claimed to 需要可辨識的聲稱者，原句直接表達作者的謹慎推斷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"are scheduled to","explanation":"Scheduled 指預定將來發生，題句談已產生的影響。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"it looks as though","meaning":"從跡象看來似乎","note":"把主語換為無人稱 it，再接完整從句；多用於可見跡象支持、但尚未定論的判斷。","collocations":"it looks as though sales have changed; it looks as if the rule has affected shops.","example":"It looks as though the new packaging rule has changed how shops display their products.","exampleZh":"從跡象看來，新包裝規則似乎已改變商店展示產品的方式。","contrast":"不能直接說 the regulations look to have；必須改寫為 It looks as though + 從句。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Judging from the empty shelves, the change in gift sizes appears to have affected what the shop stocked.","zh":"從空置的貨架看來，禮品尺寸的改變似乎已影響商店的存貨。","upgrade":"Judging from the empty shelves, it looks as though the change in gift sizes has affected what the shop stocked.","answer":"it looks as though","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"it proves that","explanation":"空架是線索，未足以 prove 商店改變存貨的全部原因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"it looks as though","explanation":"可見的貨架跡象支持但未確證判斷，it looks as though 合適，後接完整從句。"},{"letter":"C","text":"it has been reported that","explanation":"句中是從貨架直接觀察，沒有指別人報道。"},{"letter":"D","text":"it is certain that","explanation":"原句有 appears 的保留，不能改為完全確定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"it is possible that","explanation":"泛稱「有可能」太弱，漏掉貨架提供的實際跡象。"},{"letter":"F","text":"it was intended that","explanation":"規劃意圖不同於空架顯示出的已發生變化。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After reading several customers’ comments, the older design appears to have lost favour with buyers.","zh":"讀過幾名顧客的留言後，舊設計看來似乎已不受買家歡迎。","upgrade":"After reading several customers’ comments, it looks as though the older design has lost favour with buyers.","answer":"it looks as though","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"it is guaranteed that","explanation":"幾則留言未能保證所有買家的喜好。"},{"letter":"B","text":"it was formally announced that","explanation":"顧客留言不是正式公布市場結論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"it is merely possible that","explanation":"「僅僅可能」忽略了已有數則留言作支持。"},{"letter":"D","text":"it has been proven that","explanation":"留言不足以證明整體市場的因果結論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"it looks as though","explanation":"留言提供尚未確證的跡象，it looks as though 可改寫整句審慎判斷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"it was planned that","explanation":"買家喜好不是按事前計劃安排的結果。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示／暗示（但未證實）","note":"當句中指明銷售數據、訪談等證據時，讓證據作主語，說其支持某推論；比 prove 較保留。","collocations":"sales figures suggest that; interviews suggest that; the evidence suggests that.","example":"The month-by-month figures suggest that buyers are choosing smaller boxes.","exampleZh":"逐月數字顯示，買家可能正選擇較小的禮盒。","contrast":"Suggest that 需由證據作主語；若主語是規例本身，不應說規例 suggest that it exerted 某影響。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The sales figures appear to show that smaller mooncake boxes gained market share after the new rule.","zh":"銷售數據看來顯示，新規定實施後較小的月餅盒取得更多市場份額。","upgrade":"The sales figures suggest that smaller mooncake boxes gained market share after the new rule.","answer":"suggest that","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"prove conclusively that","explanation":"數字提供跡象，但未必排除其他原因，不能說已作出無可爭議的證明。"},{"letter":"B","text":"predict that","explanation":"數字記錄已發生的份額變化，不是預測將來。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suggest that","explanation":"以銷售數據作主語，suggest that 保留由證據推論而非確證。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were designed to show that","explanation":"表格的設計目的與其數值所支持的趨勢不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"are reported to claim that","explanation":"數字不是有意見的說話者，claim 也把推論轉成聲稱。"},{"letter":"F","text":"make it certain that","explanation":"現有資料沒有令市場份額變化成為毫無疑問的定論。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Several shopkeepers’ interviews appear to indicate that gift buyers are asking more often about packaging waste.","zh":"多位店主的訪談看來顯示，購買禮物的人更常詢問包裝廢物問題。","upgrade":"Several shopkeepers’ interviews suggest that gift buyers are asking more often about packaging waste.","answer":"suggest that","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"confirm beyond doubt that","explanation":"幾名店主的訪談不足以無疑義地確認所有買家的行為。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were intended to show that","explanation":"訪談者原先的研究目的與答案實際透露的趨勢不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"forecast that","explanation":"訪談談的是已聽到的提問，不是預測將來。"},{"letter":"D","text":"are consistent with the claim that","explanation":"Consistent with 只說資料與某說法不矛盾，較弱於訪談實際指向的趨勢，且需另有一項「說法」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"establish for all buyers that","explanation":"For all buyers 把幾名店主的觀察誇大到每一位買家。"},{"letter":"F","text":"suggest that","explanation":"訪談提供可能的趨勢線索，suggest that 保留暫定推論。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"appear to / appear in sight","zh":"中文辨析： 來源是「看來似乎」，不是某物突然在視線中出現；become visible 只適合人或物顯現的場景。","point":"Evidence-based inference and visual emergence are different senses of appear."},{"word":"seem / prove / confirm","zh":"中文辨析： Seem 保留證據未充分的語氣；prove/confirm 要更強確證。來源沒有把規例影響斷言為完全證實。","point":"A qualified inference cannot be rewritten as a proven causal conclusion."},{"word":"look / look as though","zh":"中文辨析： Look 在此需補成 it looks as though + 完整從句；不能把 look 直接塞進 regulations appear to have...，也不能把它理解為「觀看規例」。","point":"The look recast changes sentence structure and uses evidential appearance."},{"word":"apparently / reportedly","zh":"中文辨析： Apparently 可表示據了解，reportedly 明指據別人報道；來源是作者審慎推斷，若沒有傳聞或報道線索，兩者會改變依據。","point":"Source of evidence matters as well as degree of certainty."},{"word":"suggest / cause","zh":"中文辨析： Suggest 是資料支持某推論；cause 是規例實際造成變化。不要把「數據看來顯示」當成已確定的因果關係。","point":"What figures suggest is not identical to what a regulation caused."}],"moduleNumber":16},{"id":"lesson-017","sourceId":88,"headword":"apply","title":"Apply","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 Paper 4 prompt asks, “Would you like to apply for a summer internship?” The construction is apply for + placement. It asks about willingness to seek consideration; no actual submission has yet been established. This is separate from apply sunscreen or apply a rule. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.1](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2012 Paper 4 prompt asks, “Would you like to apply for a summer internship?” The construction is apply for + placement. It asks about willingness to seek consideration; no actual submission has yet been established. This is separate from apply sunscreen or apply a rule. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.1](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["submit an application","Contextual: completed submission step, only when the sentence states that a form or materials have actually been sent."],["seek a position","Contextual broader pursuit of a role; does not by itself prove a formal application."],["put oneself forward","Contextual idiom for volunteering to be considered; often used in selection or nomination settings."],["use","False here; belongs to applying a method or product."],["put into practice","False here; belongs to applying a lesson or rule."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Make an application for is a grammatical formal nominal recast but duplicates the mapped submit an application without adding a major distinction. Apply to takes an organisation, whereas apply for takes the internship itself; taught as a grammar contrast. Register for reserves a place in an event and need not involve selection; enrol in starts a course. Volunteer for can fit unpaid service but not necessarily a competitive internship. Be shortlisted/accepted are later outcomes, not the attempt."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["時點與語境","表達"],"rows":[["已把履歷或表格送出","submit an application for"],["仍在尋找／打算爭取機會","seek a position"],["在選拔場合自薦","put oneself forward for"]],"note":"來源只是問「你想不想申請暑期實習」，所以不能當成考生已提交文件或已被錄取。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"submit an application for","meaning":"提交……申請","note":"明說申請材料已送出；比單純 apply for 更聚焦完成提交這一步。","collocations":"submit an application for an internship; submit an application online; submit an application by Friday.","example":"Yuki submitted an application for the summer internship before the deadline.","exampleZh":"由紀在截止日期前提交了暑期實習申請。","contrast":"來源只問會否想申請，不代表已提交；在原創題目中必須有寄出或按下提交的線索。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Mei applied for the summer internship yesterday by uploading her CV and clicking the final Submit button.","zh":"阿美昨天上載履歷並按下最後的「提交」按鈕，申請了暑期實習。","upgrade":"Mei submitted an application for the summer internship yesterday by uploading her CV and clicking the final Submit button.","answer":"submitted an application for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"expressed interest in","explanation":"表達興趣可以停在詢問階段，題句明說履歷已上載並按下提交。"},{"letter":"B","text":"submitted an application for","explanation":"已完成網上送件，submitted an application for 準確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was shortlisted for","explanation":"入選短名單是機構之後的決定，原句只說送件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"registered for","explanation":"登記通常指報名佔位，不一定經過實習甄選。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was accepted into","explanation":"錄取是申請後的結果，題句沒有。"},{"letter":"F","text":"considered applying for","explanation":"只是考慮申請與已按下提交鍵相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The student applied for the internship by mailing the completed form and two references to the employer before noon.","zh":"學生在中午前把填好的表格和兩封推薦信郵寄給僱主，以申請實習。","upgrade":"The student submitted an application for the internship by mailing the completed form and two references to the employer before noon.","answer":"submitted an application for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"asked about","explanation":"詢問詳情不等於把表格和推薦信寄給僱主。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accepted an offer for","explanation":"接受聘用須先有錄取；原句只說申請材料已寄出。"},{"letter":"C","text":"signed a contract for","explanation":"簽約是更後期的聘用步驟，沒有證據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"volunteered to help at","explanation":"一般義工服務未必是有表格和推薦信的實習申請。"},{"letter":"E","text":"submitted an application for","explanation":"材料已郵寄給僱主，submitted an application for 保留正式送件。"},{"letter":"F","text":"planned to seek","explanation":"計劃尋求與已完成郵寄不同。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"seek a position","meaning":"尋求職位／實習機會","note":"較廣地表示想獲得某個工作或實習機會；可包含查詢、準備及申請，未必已提交材料。","collocations":"seek an internship position; seek a placement; seek a role in a firm.","example":"Before sending any forms, Anson sought a position in a local design studio.","exampleZh":"在寄出任何表格前，安信已開始尋找本地設計工作室的實習機會。","contrast":"Seek 保留尋求機會，卻不保證進入正式申請程序；要靠題句界定這種較廣的讀法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Would you like to apply for a summer internship at a museum, even though the application period has not opened yet?","zh":"雖然申請期尚未開始，你會想尋求博物館暑期實習機會嗎？","upgrade":"Would you like to seek a summer internship position at a museum, even though the application period has not opened yet?","answer":"seek a position","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"seek a position","explanation":"申請期未開始，這裏只能談尋求機會的意願，seek a position 合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"submit a form","explanation":"表格尚不能提交，不能把「想申請」寫成已交件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accept a placement","explanation":"沒有錄取通知，不可能已接受實習名額。"},{"letter":"D","text":"complete the programme","explanation":"課程未開始，更不能說已完成。"},{"letter":"E","text":"register as a visitor","explanation":"訪客登記不等於爭取博物館實習。"},{"letter":"F","text":"become an employee","explanation":"尋求暫時實習機會不等於已成為正式員工。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After reading about three local firms, Daniel decided to apply for an internship in exhibition design next summer.","zh":"看過三間本地公司的資料後，丹尼爾決定明年夏天尋求展覽設計實習機會。","upgrade":"After reading about three local firms, Daniel decided to seek an internship position in exhibition design next summer.","answer":"seek a position","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"claim a position","explanation":"Claim 暗示職位已有權取得，原句沒有。"},{"letter":"B","text":"take up a position","explanation":"Take up 是開始已獲得的職位，時序過早。"},{"letter":"C","text":"renew a position","explanation":"Renew 通常是延續已有安排，這裏是首次尋找。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seek a position","explanation":"丹尼爾只是作出尋求實習的決定，seek a position 保留事前階段。"},{"letter":"E","text":"decline a position","explanation":"Decline 是拒絕機會，與決定申請相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"advertise a position","explanation":"Advertise 是僱主刊登空缺，不是丹尼爾尋求實習。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"put oneself forward for","meaning":"主動提出競逐／接受考慮","note":"主動表示願意被考慮，常用於選拔或推薦；反身代詞隨主語改變。","collocations":"put herself forward for an internship; put yourself forward for selection; put a candidate forward.","example":"After the career talk, Nora put herself forward for the library internship.","exampleZh":"職業講座後，諾拉主動提出接受圖書館實習的遴選。","contrast":"Put oneself forward 強調自薦；nominate someone else 是推薦別人，不能混淆。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"When the teacher invited volunteers to be considered for the one summer internship, Ali applied for it by raising his hand and naming himself.","zh":"老師邀請有意競逐唯一暑期實習名額的學生表態時，阿里舉手自薦。","upgrade":"When the teacher invited volunteers to be considered for the one summer internship, Ali put himself forward for it by raising his hand and naming himself.","answer":"put himself forward for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was selected for","explanation":"舉手只是自薦，老師尚未選定人選。"},{"letter":"B","text":"nominated a classmate for","explanation":"原句說他報自己名字，不是提名同學。"},{"letter":"C","text":"put himself forward for","explanation":"阿里親自表態願接受考慮，put himself forward for 準確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was assigned to","explanation":"沒有老師分派實習名額的資訊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"enrolled in","explanation":"登記加入課程不同於競逐唯一實習機會。"},{"letter":"F","text":"submitted a written application for","explanation":"他以舉手表態，沒有提交書面申請。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the careers fair, Suki applied for the trainee role by telling the selection panel that she wanted to be considered.","zh":"在職業展上，淑琪告訴遴選小組自己希望獲考慮擔任見習職位，主動提出申請。","upgrade":"At the careers fair, Suki put herself forward for the trainee role by telling the selection panel that she wanted to be considered.","answer":"put herself forward for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was recruited for","explanation":"被招募意味機構已作決定，原句只見她表態。"},{"letter":"B","text":"put a friend forward for","explanation":"她推薦的是自己，不是朋友。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accepted an offer for","explanation":"尚未收到聘用條件，不能說接受聘用。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was placed in","explanation":"獲分配到職位也是甄選結果，不是自薦。"},{"letter":"E","text":"registered for information about","explanation":"她直接向遴選小組表明想競逐，強於索取資料。"},{"letter":"F","text":"put herself forward for","explanation":"淑琪向遴選小組表達自己願接受考慮，put herself forward for 表自薦。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"apply for / apply to","zh":"中文辨析： Apply for an internship：for 後面是職位或實習；apply to a company：to 後面是機構。介詞換錯會令語法或指向不清。","point":"One applies for a role and to an organisation."},{"word":"apply / submit / be accepted","zh":"中文辨析： 來源「會否想申請」未說已送件；submit 要有材料送出，be accepted 要機構錄取。這是三個不同階段。","point":"Interest, completed submission and selection outcome should not be collapsed."},{"word":"seek / register / enrol","zh":"中文辨析： Seek 是尋求職位；register 可只是登記活動，enrol 通常是加入課程。正式實習甄選不一定等於報名佔位。","point":"A competitive placement is not simply event registration."},{"word":"put oneself forward / nominate another","zh":"中文辨析： Put oneself forward 指自薦；put someone else forward 是推薦他人，反身代詞及受詞必須跟實際人選一致。","point":"The reflexive object identifies the person volunteering for selection."},{"word":"apply a rule / apply cream","zh":"中文辨析： Apply a rule 是運用規則，apply cream 是塗抹；這些對應原映射 use/put into practice，但不適用於 apply for an internship。","point":"The direct-object senses of apply differ from seeking a placement."}],"moduleNumber":17},{"id":"lesson-018","sourceId":9,"headword":"access","title":"Access","titleZh":"取得及使用媒體與互聯網的機會","subtitle":"取得及使用媒體與互聯網的機會","description":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 1.3〈Cosplay in Hong Kong〉把香港年輕人更投入角色扮演，部分歸因於 easy access to multimedia and the internet。這裏 access 是名詞，指有渠道、設備或許可去取得並使用網上媒體，不是建築物入口。Easy 說取得容易；若新詞只表示網上有資源，卻未說年輕人有設備可用，就會改變角度。","sourceSense":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 1.3〈Cosplay in Hong Kong〉把香港年輕人更投入角色扮演，部分歸因於 easy access to multimedia and the internet。這裏 access 是名詞，指有渠道、設備或許可去取得並使用網上媒體，不是建築物入口。Easy 說取得容易；若新詞只表示網上有資源，卻未說年輕人有設備可用，就會改變角度。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["entry","此處錯義","Entry 可指進入建築物、活動或資料庫的入口；entry to multimedia 不自然，無法保留上網使用的機會。"],["availability","有條件","資源本身可被取得；須說明網絡與設備能讓目標用戶使用，才可貼近他們的 access。"],["ability to use","有條件","強調使用者實際可以操作媒體或網絡；可能兼含技能，因此須由設備、連線或教學語境支持。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子重點","說法"],"rows":[["用戶有即時可用的渠道","ready access to"],["地點、時間或介面安排便利","convenient access to"],["資源本身公開供應","availability of（核查用戶條件）"],["設備與訓練使人懂得使用","ability to use"],["只談互聯網連線","internet connectivity"]],"note":"快選規則： 問「誰可以用甚麼、靠甚麼用？」有網站不一定有設備；有網絡不一定有影片權限；有設備也不一定懂操作。源文的 access to multimedia and the internet 涵蓋使用機會，不是實體 entry。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Ready Access To","meaning":"容易隨時取得及使用","note":"強調資源就在手邊、可以順利使用；ready 近於源句的 easy，但仍須有實際渠道。","collocations":"ready access to the internet / multimedia / online tutorials.","example":"With free Wi-Fi and shared tablets, pupils had ready access to online tutorials.","exampleZh":"有免費 Wi-Fi 和共用平板電腦，學生便容易取得並使用網上教學資源。","contrast":"Ready access 不表示學生擁有設備；也不保證網上資料正確。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"With school tablets and free Wi-Fi, pupils had easy access to online costume tutorials after class.","zh":"學校提供平板電腦和免費 Wi-Fi，學生放學後可以輕易使用網上服裝製作教學。","upgrade":"With school tablets and free Wi-Fi, pupils had ready access to online costume tutorials after class.","answer":"ready access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"ready access to","explanation":"設備及連線讓教程可隨時使用，ready access to 保留這個意思。"},{"letter":"B","text":"permission to use","explanation":"學校有平板和免費 Wi-Fi，句中突出資源容易取得；單有許可不保證設備和連線。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"Ownership of 誤說學生擁有網上教程。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission to","explanation":"Admission to 偏入場或入會，並無這種門檻。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a receipt for","explanation":"A receipt for 是收據，與使用權無關。"},{"letter":"F","text":"availability of","explanation":"教學影片可能已上網，但此句主語是學生及其可使用程度，ready access to 保留使用者角度。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Because the multimedia guides remain online day and night, volunteers have easy access to them whenever a late costume problem arises.","zh":"多媒體指南日夜都放在網上；義工遇上臨時服裝問題時，隨時可以取用。","upgrade":"Because the multimedia guides remain online day and night, volunteers have ready access to them whenever a late costume problem arises.","answer":"ready access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permission to view","explanation":"指南日夜在線，重點是義工遇事可立即取用，不是有人特別授權查看。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ready access to","explanation":"Whenever 與日夜在線的條件支持義工隨時可用，正合 ready access to。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"義工隨時取用公開指南，不等於擁有指南。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission of","explanation":"Admission of 不是取用多媒體指南的自然搭配。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a path into","explanation":"A path into 偏比喻進入某領域，不能表示遇到服裝問題時即刻取用指南。"},{"letter":"F","text":"availability of","explanation":"指南本身在線是供應條件；題句主語是義工及他們何時可用，ready access 保留使用者角度。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Convenient Access To","meaning":"方便取得及使用","note":"強調位置、時間或介面安排便利，例如多個服務點或不需長途走到電腦室。","collocations":"convenient access to online materials / computers / the internet.","example":"Library kiosks on every floor give visitors convenient access to digital archives.","exampleZh":"圖書館每層都設有資訊站，讓訪客方便使用數碼檔案。","contrast":"Convenient 加入使用過程省時省力的意思；若只是資源存在，不一定方便。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Computer kiosks beside every classroom give students easy access to online media without a trip to the library.","zh":"每間課室旁都有電腦資訊站，學生毋須走到圖書館就可輕易使用網上媒體。","upgrade":"Computer kiosks beside every classroom give students convenient access to online media without a trip to the library.","answer":"convenient access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permission to view","explanation":"設在每間教室旁的電腦亭令使用方便；允許查看不足以說明毋須走到圖書館。"},{"letter":"B","text":"convenient access to","explanation":"課室旁設資訊站免走遠路，convenient 的方便意味有根據。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"Ownership 誤說學生擁有媒體內容。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission to","explanation":"Admission 偏獲准進入場所或團體。"},{"letter":"E","text":"physical entrance to","explanation":"Physical entrance 是實體入口，非數碼資源渠道。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unrestricted access to","explanation":"電腦亭位置方便，不表示學生能無限制使用所有網上媒體；權限範圍沒有交代。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The museum’s late-opening media room gives working students easy access to its digital collection after evening classes.","zh":"博物館媒體室延長開放時間，讓在職學生晚課後方便使用數碼館藏。","upgrade":"The museum’s late-opening media room gives working students convenient access to its digital collection after evening classes.","answer":"convenient access to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"convenient access to","explanation":"延長開放時間配合晚課，重點是使用時段方便。"},{"letter":"B","text":"around-the-clock access to","explanation":"延長到晚間不等於媒體室二十四小時開放，不能擴大成全天候使用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"Ownership 會誤說學生擁有館藏。"},{"letter":"D","text":"entry point to","explanation":"Entry point 可說登入頁，卻不概括延時服務的方便。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a receipt for","explanation":"Receipt 是收據。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permission to use","explanation":"是否獲准使用並非問題；晚間開放令在職學生能按時間安排方便取得收藏。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Availability","meaning":"可取得性；供應情況","note":"從資料或服務這一方說「存在且可提供」，而非直接說特定用戶必然能用。","collocations":"availability of online guides / computers / Wi-Fi; wide availability of resources.","example":"The wide availability of costume tutorials made it easier for beginners to learn.","exampleZh":"服裝製作教學資源廣泛可得，令初學者更容易學習。","contrast":"若學生沒有裝置，資源仍可 available 卻不等於 access；改寫原句時要有實際可用的線索。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Because the guides were free online and everyone in the class had a device, easy access to costume tutorials helped the pupils learn.","zh":"教學指南免費放在網上，班上每人都有裝置，因此學生容易取得教程，有助學習。","upgrade":"Because the guides were free online and everyone in the class had a device, the availability of costume tutorials helped the pupils learn.","answer":"availability of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"availability of","explanation":"指南公開且學生皆有裝置，從資源供應角度改寫仍能解釋學習機會。"},{"letter":"B","text":"internet connectivity","explanation":"全班有裝置且指南免費上網；單說有網絡連線，不能說明教學資源本身已公開供應。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"Ownership 沒有根據；學生不用擁有網上指南。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission to","explanation":"Admission 指獲准加入或入場，非資源供應。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a physical doorway to","explanation":"Physical doorway 不適用網上教學指南。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permission to use","explanation":"可否獲准看並不是本句重點；免費上網且全班有裝置使教程可取得。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club gained easy access to hundreds of free costume patterns after their creators posted them in a public archive; every member already had a connected device.","zh":"設計者把數百款免費服裝紙樣放入公共資料庫後，社團便可輕易取得；每名會員本來已有可連網裝置。","upgrade":"The club benefited from the availability of hundreds of free costume patterns after their creators posted them in a public archive; every member already had a connected device.","answer":"availability of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"internet connectivity","explanation":"會員原已有可連網裝置；新增的是紙樣公開供應，不是新網絡連線。"},{"letter":"B","text":"availability of","explanation":"創作者把大量免費紙樣公開後，社團受惠於資源本身的可取得性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ownership of","explanation":"公開紙樣可使用但並非社團所有。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission to","explanation":"Admission 說進入場所或組織，不能代替紙樣公開供應。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a doorway into","explanation":"這是比喻入口，不會清楚說明公共資料庫新增了紙樣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permission to view","explanation":"紙樣公開且會員已有裝置；重點是資源供應量擴大，並非另發查看許可。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Ability To Use","meaning":"能夠使用","note":"把重點放在人實際可以操作或使用資源；在有設備並學過操作的情境可教，不能自動從「資源存在」推斷技能。","collocations":"ability to use the internet / editing software / a device.","example":"After the centre installed computers and taught basic browsing, members had the ability to use online costume guides.","exampleZh":"中心安裝電腦並教授基本瀏覽方法後，會員能使用網上的服裝製作指南。","contrast":"這是視角轉換：access 可來自權限、設備或連線；ability to use 可能兼指操作技能。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the club provided tablets and taught members how to open the apps, they gained easy access to costume-design apps.","zh":"社團提供平板電腦並教會員開啟應用程式後，會員便容易使用服裝設計應用程式。","upgrade":"After the club provided tablets and taught members how to open the apps, they gained the ability to use costume-design apps.","answer":"ability to use","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permission to use","explanation":"學會開啟應用程式並有平板，說明具實際操作能力；只得許可未必會操作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ownership of","explanation":"Ownership 不是條件；平板可由社團提供。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ability to use","explanation":"設備加上操作教學支持「能夠使用」的能力角度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission to","explanation":"Admission 指准入，未說懂得操作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"physical access into","explanation":"Physical access into 不自然地接應用程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"availability of","explanation":"應用程式可供下載仍不等於會員經教學後能使用其功能。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although members already had software accounts, the hands-on workshop gave them easy access to advanced editing tools that had previously baffled them; by the end, each member completed an edit without help.","zh":"會員本來已有軟件帳戶，但實作工作坊讓他們學會使用此前不懂的進階編輯工具；課程結束時，每人都能獨力完成一次編輯。","upgrade":"Although members already had software accounts, the hands-on workshop gave them the ability to use advanced editing tools that had previously baffled them; by the end, each member completed an edit without help.","answer":"ability to use","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permission to use","explanation":"會員原已有帳戶，缺的不是許可，而是使用進階工具的實際方法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ability to use","explanation":"每人課後都能獨力完成編輯，明確證明工作坊帶來實際使用進階工具的能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"entry to","explanation":"有帳戶本來就能進入軟件；entry 不表示已學會使用進階工具。"},{"letter":"D","text":"familiarity with","explanation":"熟悉工具介面仍可能不會操作；句尾說每人都能獨力完成編輯，證據強於熟悉感。"},{"letter":"E","text":"confidence with","explanation":"自信是心理感受；每人獨力完成編輯是可觀察的實際能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"availability of","explanation":"工具此前已在軟件內，供應沒有變；變的是會員會用了。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Internet Connectivity","meaning":"互聯網連線","note":"技術上有穩定連線的情況；只適合 internet access 的連線層面，不能代替原文同時提到的全部多媒體內容。","collocations":"internet connectivity; reliable connectivity; improve connectivity.","example":"The new network gave the village reliable internet connectivity.","exampleZh":"新網絡令村莊有穩定的互聯網連線。","contrast":"Connectivity 不表示有權看每一份付費內容，也不等於懂得操作網站。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After a fibre line reached the village, residents finally had easy access to the internet, although some paid sites still required subscriptions.","zh":"光纖線路接通村莊後，居民終於容易上網，但部分付費網站仍須訂閱。","upgrade":"After a fibre line reached the village, residents finally had internet connectivity, although some paid sites still required subscriptions.","answer":"internet connectivity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permission for all sites","explanation":"村落新接光纖只證明連上網；付費網站仍要訂閱，並非所有網站都可進入。"},{"letter":"B","text":"internet connectivity","explanation":"光纖提供網絡連接，且不聲稱可免費看所有付費內容。"},{"letter":"C","text":"data allowance","explanation":"光纖接通的是村莊固定網絡；句中沒有說居民手機數據配額改變。"},{"letter":"D","text":"availability of websites","explanation":"網站本來可能存在；新光纖改善的是居民的網絡連線。"},{"letter":"E","text":"broadband speed","explanation":"新光纖讓村莊能連上網，但句子未提供速率數據，不能把連線與速度混同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ability to browse","explanation":"居民或許會瀏覽網站，但新光纖首先提供的是物理網絡連線，技能和網站權限另論。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After a two-day router failure, technicians restored the school network and pupils regained easy access to the internet, although the subscription video library stayed locked.","zh":"路由器故障兩天後，技術員修復校園網絡，學生重新能上網；但付費影片庫仍無法開啟。","upgrade":"After a two-day router failure, technicians restored the school network and pupils regained internet connectivity, although the subscription video library stayed locked.","answer":"internet connectivity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"internet connectivity","explanation":"修好路由器後網絡重新連通；這不等於訂閱影片庫也解鎖。"},{"letter":"B","text":"unrestricted media access","explanation":"付費影片庫仍鎖住，明確否定對網上媒體不受限制地使用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"permission to browse","explanation":"網絡故障是技術連線問題，不是學校撤銷瀏覽許可。"},{"letter":"D","text":"connection speed","explanation":"路由器已恢復連線，但句子沒有比較修復前後的上網速度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"ability to use computers","explanation":"路由器故障與電腦操作技能不同；修復的是連線。"},{"letter":"F","text":"data allowance","explanation":"修復校園路由器不會改變學生手機數據配額，兩者是不同技術條件。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"access / entry：使用與進入","zh":"Access to the internet 指可連線使用；entry to a building 指實體進入。網頁可有 entry point，但原文並非在講大門或入場資格。","point":"Access here concerns use of a resource; entry usually names physical or formal admission."},{"word":"access / availability：人與資源角度","zh":"網上教程即使 available，沒有設備或網絡的學生仍可能 lack access。反過來，學生有網絡也不表示某份付費資料一定可取。改寫時要核查供應和實際使用條件。","point":"Availability describes the resource; access describes the user’s usable route to it."},{"word":"access / ownership：可用不等於擁有","zh":"圖書館電腦讓學生 have access to 互聯網，但電腦不是學生所有。原文也沒有說年輕人擁有所有媒體內容。","point":"Access to a resource does not entail owning it."},{"word":"permission / practical ability：允許與可行","zh":"獲准使用平台不等於有設備及連線；有設備也可能因權限被擋。Ability to use 若表示操作技能，需要上下文支持，不能把權限問題錯當成不懂操作。","point":"Permission, equipment and skill can each affect access but are not the same thing."},{"word":"internet connectivity：技術範圍","zh":"Connectivity 指網絡連接狀態，可替代特定情況的 internet access；它本身不包括圖片、影片、漫畫等 multimedia 的取得權利。","point":"Connectivity is narrower: it names the network link, not all multimedia resources."},{"word":"accessible / comprehensible：可得與易懂","zh":"資料 accessible to users 可指可取得，也可在某些語境指易理解或照顧無障礙需要。原文的 easy access 主要指資源可取得並使用，不能自動推論內容易明白。","point":"Accessible can concern obtaining, comprehension or disability accommodation, depending on context."}],"moduleNumber":18},{"id":"lesson-019","sourceId":19,"headword":"activity","title":"Activity","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 King of Comedy group prompt asks a school film club to discuss activities it could organise for a Stephen Chow festival. Activity is a planned thing participants can do or attend, not an organiser’s backstage task or a long-term hobby. The source uses plural activities; this lesson headword is its singular lemma.","sourceSense":"The 2012 King of Comedy group prompt asks a school film club to discuss activities it could organise for a Stephen Chow festival. Activity is a planned thing participants can do or attend, not an organiser’s backstage task or a long-term hobby. The source uses plural activities; this lesson headword is its singular lemma.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["pastime","false: continuing hobby, not scheduled item"],["pursuit","false: sustained interest or occupation"],["exercise","contextual subtype only: a practice activity"],["event","contextual: planned public occasion"],["task","false: backstage duty, not visitor activity"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Workshop 和 screening 是活動的具體類型，應在例子中教，不把每個下位類別重複算作通用同義詞。Pursuit 多指長期追求，非節目項。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["event","有計劃、供人參加的活動或場合，例如電影放映或問答賽。","活動須有可辨認的場合；幕後訂票工作不是參加者 event。"],["session","有起止時間的一節節目，如工作坊或討論時段。","整個電影節不是一個 session；須指其中一節。"],["programme item","寫在節目表上的一項安排；須有正式節目表語境。","Program(me) item 是節目表的一項，不泛指任何私人活動。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 面向觀眾安排的獨立活動可叫 event；有明確時段的討論或問答是 session；從節目表的排列角度看每一項是 programme item。個人長期嗜好 pastime 和籌辦者的工作 task 不等於整場電影節活動。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"event","meaning":"活動場合","note":"有計劃、供人參加的活動或場合，例如電影放映或問答賽。","collocations":"organise an event; festival events.","example":"The film club organised a costume event for the festival.","exampleZh":"電影社為電影節籌辦了一場服裝活動。","contrast":"活動須有可辨認的場合；幕後訂票工作不是參加者 event。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The club planned an activity for visitors: a public screening with a discussion afterwards.","zh":"社團為訪客規劃了一項活動：公開放映並在其後討論。","upgrade":"The club planned an event for visitors: a public screening with a discussion afterwards.","answer":"event","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"screening","explanation":"Screening 只涵蓋放映，不包括之後的公開討論。"},{"letter":"B","text":"workshop","explanation":"Workshop 通常要參加者動手學習，句中只有放映與討論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"meeting","explanation":"Meeting 可能有討論，卻不能概括對訪客開放的放映環節。"},{"letter":"D","text":"rehearsal","explanation":"Rehearsal 是正式活動前的排練，原句說訪客已可參加。"},{"letter":"E","text":"event","explanation":"Event 可把公開放映和映後討論視為同一項已籌辦活動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"routine","explanation":"Routine 是恆常程序，原句只說社團策劃一場訪客活動。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"One activity on the festival calendar was a Stephen Chow film quiz open to all pupils.","zh":"電影節日程上的一項活動是向所有學生開放的周星馳電影問答賽。","upgrade":"One event on the festival calendar was a Stephen Chow film quiz open to all pupils.","answer":"event","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"assignment","explanation":"Assignment 是交給某人的工作，不是日程表上供全校參加的問答活動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"screening","explanation":"Screening 是放映電影；句子描述的是問答比賽。"},{"letter":"C","text":"event","explanation":"Event 指這場向所有學生開放、列在電影節日程上的問答活動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"rehearsal","explanation":"Rehearsal 是彩排，不能把正式對外開放的問答活動改成排練。"},{"letter":"E","text":"exercise","explanation":"Exercise 可是課堂練習，卻沒有本句公開電影節活動的意味。"},{"letter":"F","text":"routine","explanation":"Routine 表示重複做的慣例，原句說的是日程上的一項活動。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"session","meaning":"一節活動","note":"有起止時間的一節節目，如工作坊或討論時段。","collocations":"a question-and-answer session; a festival session.","example":"The afternoon session featured a discussion of comedy films.","exampleZh":"下午場次安排了喜劇電影討論。","contrast":"整個電影節不是一個 session；須指其中一節。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The activity from 2 p.m. to 3 p.m. was a discussion of Stephen Chow’s films.","zh":"下午二時至三時的活動是一節周星馳電影討論。","upgrade":"The session from 2 p.m. to 3 p.m. was a discussion of Stephen Chow’s films.","answer":"session","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"whole festival","explanation":"Whole festival 是整個電影節，不會只佔下午二時至三時。"},{"letter":"B","text":"screening","explanation":"Screening 是播電影；這一小時安排的是討論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"workshop","explanation":"Workshop 通常有動手練習，句中沒有這類安排。"},{"letter":"D","text":"panel","explanation":"Panel 指座談嘉賓組或專題討論形式，原句沒有交代嘉賓席。"},{"letter":"E","text":"programme","explanation":"Programme 可指整張節目安排，範圍大於指定的一小時。"},{"letter":"F","text":"session","explanation":"Session 可指電影節中二時至三時的一段討論時段。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club scheduled an activity after the screening in which audience members asked questions.","zh":"社團在放映後安排一節讓觀眾發問的活動。","upgrade":"The club scheduled a question-and-answer session after the screening.","answer":"session","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"session","explanation":"映後讓觀眾提問是一段有安排的 session，不是整個電影節。"},{"letter":"B","text":"screening","explanation":"Screening 是播放影片，原句說的是播放後的提問環節。"},{"letter":"C","text":"rehearsal","explanation":"Rehearsal 是彩排；觀眾現場發問是正式節目。"},{"letter":"D","text":"programme","explanation":"Programme 是整體節目安排，不能精確表示映後單獨的時段。"},{"letter":"E","text":"workshop","explanation":"Workshop 一般有參與式練習，觀眾發問不足以確定是工作坊。"},{"letter":"F","text":"backstage task","explanation":"Backstage task 是幕後工作，原句說觀眾參與的公開問答。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"programme item","meaning":"節目項目","note":"寫在節目表上的一項安排；須有正式節目表語境。","collocations":"a programme item; list programme items.","example":"The quiz appeared as the final programme item.","exampleZh":"問答賽列為最後一項節目。","contrast":"Program(me) item 是節目表的一項，不泛指任何私人活動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The printed festival schedule listed each activity with its starting time.","zh":"印刷的電影節節目表列出每項活動及開始時間。","upgrade":"The printed festival schedule listed each programme item with its starting time.","answer":"programme item","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"programme booklet","explanation":"Programme booklet 是印製的節目冊，不能稱每一項有開始時間的活動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"programme schedule","explanation":"Programme schedule 是整張日程表，不是日程表列出的每項內容。"},{"letter":"C","text":"exercise","explanation":"Exercise 偏練習，不能概括電影節所有有時間的活動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"programme item","explanation":"Programme item 正是日程表中逐項列出並標示開始時間的活動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"venue","explanation":"Venue 是活動場地，句子列出的卻是每項活動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"performance","explanation":"Performance 只指演出；電影節節目還可能包括討論或問答。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The host announced the next activity on the festival programme: a short film quiz.","zh":"主持宣布電影節節目表上的下一項活動：短片問答賽。","upgrade":"The host announced the next programme item: a short film quiz.","answer":"programme item","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"programme booklet","explanation":"Programme booklet 是載有資訊的冊子，主持人宣布的是下一項活動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"festival venue","explanation":"Festival venue 是舉行地點，不是下一輪短片問答。"},{"letter":"C","text":"next performance","explanation":"Next performance 通常指演出，短片問答不必是演出。"},{"letter":"D","text":"programme schedule","explanation":"Programme schedule 是整份節目時間表，不是其中一項。"},{"letter":"E","text":"programme item","explanation":"Programme item 指節目表中的下一個活動，正好可接冒號後的短片問答。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ticketed event","explanation":"Ticketed event 暗示須買票，句子沒有提到票務。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"pastime / activity","zh":"中文辨析： Pastime 是平時的消閒嗜好；節目表上的單項活動未必是長期嗜好。","point":"A hobby is not necessarily an organised festival item."},{"word":"task / activity","zh":"中文辨析： Task 可指幕後工作，例如訂場；來源談的是供參加者參與的項目。","point":"Organiser duties and attendee activities differ."},{"word":"exercise / activity","zh":"中文辨析： Exercise 可指練習或運動；電影節活動不全是練習題。","point":"A quiz exercise may be one kind of activity, not the full category."},{"word":"event / session","zh":"中文辨析： Event 是可供參與的場合；session 特指一個有時間界線的場次。","point":"One festival can contain many sessions and events."}],"moduleNumber":19},{"id":"lesson-020","sourceId":18,"headword":"active","title":"Active","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2023 Night Owls passage says night owls are more awake and active at night. Active here means mentally awake and doing things during those hours; it does not necessarily mean exercising or being sociable.","sourceSense":"The 2023 Night Owls passage says night owls are more awake and active at night. Active here means mentally awake and doing things during those hours; it does not necessarily mean exercising or being sociable.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["energetic","contextual: stronger energy claim"],["physically engaged","false: source does not entail physical exercise"],["lively","false as general replacement: adds animated/social tone"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Lively 會增添活潑社交意味；up and about 偏身體走動；productive 斷言有效產出，都不是原文 active 的普遍等值詞。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["alert","夜間保持精神清醒、能注意事物；較偏心理狀態而非做事本身。","須有注意力或清醒線索；alert 不保證正在活動。"],["energetic","比 active 更強，指有充足精力去做事；練習須明示精力旺盛。","安靜但醒着不一定 energetic。"],["busy","若語境列明夜間有多項事情在進行，可指忙碌；不是單純清醒。","Busy 可有大量活動但不一定精力旺盛；原來源沒有說所有夜貓子都忙。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 夜裏仍清醒而注意細節是 alert；有精神和活動能量是 energetic；整晚在處理事情才是 busy。原文 active 可涵蓋其中幾項，但單一替換應依注意力、精力或工作量這個焦點來定。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"alert","meaning":"清醒警覺","note":"夜間保持精神清醒、能注意事物；較偏心理狀態而非做事本身。","collocations":"feel alert at night; remain alert.","example":"She felt alert after midnight and could follow the lecture closely.","exampleZh":"午夜後她仍很清醒，能專心聽講。","contrast":"須有注意力或清醒線索；alert 不保證正在活動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although it was midnight, the student was active enough to notice every detail in the film.","zh":"雖然已是午夜，學生仍精神清醒，注意到電影每個細節。","upgrade":"Although it was midnight, the student was alert enough to notice every detail in the film.","answer":"alert","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 說精力充沛，卻未必能察覺電影中的每個細節。"},{"letter":"B","text":"alert","explanation":"Alert 指深夜仍清醒且注意周圍細節，最貼合句末線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"athletic","explanation":"Athletic 是體能或運動能力，與看電影時是否留神不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"restless","explanation":"Restless 表示坐立不安，未必能仔細看電影。"},{"letter":"E","text":"occupied","explanation":"Occupied 表示正忙於某事，不表示能注意畫面細節。"},{"letter":"F","text":"lively","explanation":"Lively 可說氣氛或性格活躍，不能準確指出留神觀察。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although he had been tired at dinner, the night owl remained active at midnight and answered the emergency call immediately.","zh":"他晚飯時本來疲倦，但到了午夜仍然警覺，立即接聽緊急來電。","upgrade":"Although he had been tired at dinner, the night owl remained alert at midnight and answered the emergency call immediately.","answer":"alert","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"awake","explanation":"Awake 只表示沒睡着，未必能立即接聽午夜的緊急來電。"},{"letter":"B","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 說精力充足，卻不能直接表示對突發來電的即時警覺。"},{"letter":"C","text":"busy","explanation":"Busy 表示正在處理其他事情，不是立即接應緊急呼叫的狀態。"},{"letter":"D","text":"restless","explanation":"Restless 指坐立不安，未必有清晰、迅速的應急反應。"},{"letter":"E","text":"alert","explanation":"Alert 表示午夜仍保持清醒及應對準備，合乎立即接聽來電的細節。"},{"letter":"F","text":"available","explanation":"Available 只表示可聯絡，未必在疲倦後仍能立即而清醒地回應。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"energetic","meaning":"精力充沛","note":"比 active 更強，指有充足精力去做事；練習須明示精力旺盛。","collocations":"feel energetic; energetic at night.","example":"After sunset, Kai felt energetic enough to finish a long rehearsal.","exampleZh":"日落後，啟精力充沛，足以完成漫長綵排。","contrast":"安靜但醒着不一定 energetic。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Even after a full day, the night owl felt active, with plenty of energy for a two-hour dance rehearsal.","zh":"即使過了一整天，這名夜貓子仍精力充沛，足以排練兩小時舞蹈。","upgrade":"Even after a full day, the night owl felt energetic enough for a two-hour dance rehearsal.","answer":"energetic","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"alert","explanation":"Alert 可以清醒，但不足以表示還有精力跳兩小時舞。"},{"letter":"B","text":"busy","explanation":"Busy 說已有很多事情做，不表示身體精力仍充足。"},{"letter":"C","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 正好對應仍有很多體力參加長時間舞蹈排練。"},{"letter":"D","text":"restless","explanation":"Restless 是坐立不安，不等於有足夠體力排練。"},{"letter":"E","text":"athletic","explanation":"Athletic 指較持久的運動能力，並非當晚仍有精力的即時狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"productive","explanation":"Productive 指有成果，原句只說仍有體力，沒有交代排練成效。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At 11 p.m., she was still active during the club's planning meeting, leading the discussion without slowing down.","zh":"晚上十一時，她在社團策劃會議上仍很有精神，主持討論也沒有放慢節奏。","upgrade":"At 11 p.m., she was still energetic during the club's planning meeting, leading the discussion without slowing down.","answer":"energetic","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"alert","explanation":"Alert 是留神，可參與會議，卻不一定有主持討論的充沛精力。"},{"letter":"B","text":"busy","explanation":"Busy 只說會議佔用時間，沒有描述她十一時仍不減的活力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"agitated","explanation":"Agitated 是焦躁不安；句子描寫的是穩定地帶領討論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"athletic","explanation":"Athletic 是體能特質，與深夜主持策劃會議的精力不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"productive","explanation":"Productive 評價會議成果；原句只說她帶領討論沒有放慢節奏。"},{"letter":"F","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 可形容十一時仍充滿活力，持續領導社團討論。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"busy","meaning":"忙於做事","note":"若語境列明夜間有多項事情在進行，可指忙碌；不是單純清醒。","collocations":"busy at night; busy with projects.","example":"At midnight, she was busy editing the club video.","exampleZh":"午夜時她正忙着剪輯社團影片。","contrast":"Busy 可有大量活動但不一定精力旺盛；原來源沒有說所有夜貓子都忙。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She was active all evening, answering messages and editing the film-club programme.","zh":"她整晚忙着回覆訊息及剪輯電影社節目。","upgrade":"She was busy all evening, answering messages and editing the film-club programme.","answer":"busy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"busy","explanation":"Busy 指整晚接連回訊息和編節目，重點是有工作在身。"},{"letter":"B","text":"alert","explanation":"Alert 指留神，卻未必說她正處理多項任務。"},{"letter":"C","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 只說有精神，未表明整晚有事忙。"},{"letter":"D","text":"athletic","explanation":"Athletic 是運動能力，與編排電影社節目無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"restless","explanation":"Restless 是坐立不安，不能由回訊息及編排節目推出。"},{"letter":"F","text":"available","explanation":"Available 表示有空，與一整晚忙於兩項工作相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At midnight, the café staff were still active, serving the last customers while cleaning tables.","zh":"午夜時分，咖啡館員工仍在忙着招待最後一批客人，同時清理桌子。","upgrade":"At midnight, the café staff were still busy, serving the last customers while cleaning tables.","answer":"busy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"alert","explanation":"午夜仍 alert 可表示清醒，卻未說員工要同時接待客人和清理桌子。"},{"letter":"B","text":"energetic","explanation":"Energetic 描寫精力；本句重點是兩項工作同時在進行。"},{"letter":"C","text":"productive","explanation":"Productive 暗示已做出成果，原句只交代員工正在處理服務工作。"},{"letter":"D","text":"busy","explanation":"Busy 正好指咖啡館員工一邊服務末批客人、一邊清潔桌子。"},{"letter":"E","text":"restless","explanation":"Restless 是坐立不安，不等於正在執行兩項咖啡館工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"available","explanation":"Available 表示有空，與仍要接待客人及清潔相反。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"physically active / active","zh":"中文辨析： 原句沒有說夜貓子運動或身體活動量大；可以只是安靜讀書。","point":"Night-time activity need not be exercise."},{"word":"lively / active","zh":"中文辨析： Lively 偏向活潑、熱鬧或社交氣氛；一個獨自工作的人也可 active。","point":"Liveliness adds a social or animated nuance."},{"word":"awake / active","zh":"中文辨析： 醒着是狀態；active 還包含實際在做事。","point":"A person may be awake yet idle."},{"word":"productive / active","zh":"中文辨析： 做事不一定有成果；productive 額外斷言產出。","point":"Activity does not guarantee productivity."}],"moduleNumber":20},{"id":"lesson-021","sourceId":60,"headword":"alternative","title":"Alternative","titleZh":"非主流的／別具一格的","subtitle":"非主流的／別具一格的","description":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 8.1〈Outdoor Music Festivals〉有句「It could be what we did — an alternative music and arts festival.」這裏 alternative 是放在 music and arts festival 前的形容詞，描述活動的文化風格：不走一般大眾、傳統音樂節路線，可帶較小眾、不拘常規或新嘗試的特色。句子前半 It could be what we did 確有「一個可考慮做法」的語境，但不能因此把名詞片語裏的 alternative 當成名詞 an alternative / an option。原句本身沒有指明每一場表演都是實驗性、也沒有說活動由獨立機構主辦；這些較窄改寫須在教學例句另給條件。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 8.1〈Outdoor Music Festivals〉有句「It could be what we did — an alternative music and arts festival.」這裏 alternative 是放在 music and arts festival 前的形容詞，描述活動的文化風格：不走一般大眾、傳統音樂節路線，可帶較小眾、不拘常規或新嘗試的特色。句子前半 It could be what we did 確有「一個可考慮做法」的語境，但不能因此把名詞片語裏的 alternative 當成名詞 an alternative / an option。原句本身沒有指明每一場表演都是實驗性、也沒有說活動由獨立機構主辦；這些較窄改寫須在教學例句另給條件。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["option","false for the modifier sense","An option for a festival 指可選的方案；an option music and arts festival 不是正常形容詞改寫，也沒有交代活動風格。"],["substitute","false for this sense","A substitute festival 是代替另一場活動，暗示原定活動未能舉行或需要替代；原句未說這事。"],["different choice","false as a direct replacement","可說 a different choice of festival，但那描述選擇，不表示選中的活動非主流。"],["other choice","false as a direct replacement","Another choice 是另一個選項；other choice festival 不合搭配，也沒有非主流風格。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- 原文 alternative music and arts festival 的 alternative 形容活動非主流／不按慣例的文化風格；不是名詞「另一個選項」。\n- Unconventional 側重形式打破慣例；non-mainstream 側重小眾文化定位；offbeat 側重奇趣氣質；experimental 須有試行新方法的證據。\n- Option, substitute, different choice, other choice 屬另一個「選擇／替代」義；單用它們不能改寫本句的風格形容詞。\n- Independent, underground, alternative rock 各自加入營運、曝光或特定曲風條件；不能從原句自動推出。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"unconventional","meaning":"不拘傳統形式","note":"若節目安排、場地使用或藝術呈現打破一般音樂節慣例，可用 unconventional。它描述做法不按常規，未必表示活動不受歡迎或由小公司主辦。","collocations":"an unconventional festival; unconventional staging; unconventional art displays","example":"The organisers planned an unconventional festival with concerts inside a moving art installation.","exampleZh":"主辦者計劃舉辦一個不拘常規的音樂節，讓音樂會在移動藝術裝置內進行。","contrast":"Unconventional 指形式偏離常規；non-mainstream 指不屬於大眾主流。獨特舞台設計可不拘常規，即使觀眾仍很多。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisers called it an alternative music and arts festival because the concerts took place inside moving art installations instead of on a standard stage.","zh":"主辦者稱它為另類音樂藝術節，因為音樂會在移動藝術裝置內舉行，而非使用標準舞台。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The organisers called it an unconventional music and arts festival because the concerts took place inside moving art installations instead of on a standard stage.","answer":"an unconventional music and arts festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a substitute music and arts festival","explanation":"substitute 表代替另一活動，但句中沒有原活動取消。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an independently owned music and arts festival","explanation":"independently owned 說營運權，移動舞台不能證明主辦權。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an unconventional music and arts festival","explanation":"移動藝術裝置代替標準舞台，直接證明形式不拘常規。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a mainstream music and arts festival","explanation":"mainstream 與強調打破常規的安排方向不符。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an alternative-rock-only festival","explanation":"alternative-rock-only 把音樂與藝術節縮成單一搖滾曲風。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a music and arts festival held on an alternative date","explanation":"日期不同只是一個選擇差別，沒有解釋舞台形式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The organisers described an alternative festival with no fixed running order: performers chose their own spaces, and visitors discovered each show as it began.","zh":"主辦者形容這是另類藝術節：它沒有固定演出順序；表演者自行選擇場地，觀眾待演出開始才發現節目。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The organisers described an unconventional festival with no fixed running order: performers chose their own spaces, and visitors discovered each show as it began.","answer":"an unconventional festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a festival attended only by a niche audience","explanation":"觀眾是否小眾未交代；沒有固定演出順序說的是形式，不是受眾規模。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a festival using untested sound technology","explanation":"是否使用新聲音技術未交代；題句描述的是節目順序和場地選擇。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an experimental-music-only festival","explanation":"沒有固定時間表不表示只演實驗音樂。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an unconventional festival","explanation":"自選場地、觀眾即場發現節目，明確偏離慣常預排演出形式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a mainstream festival with a printed timetable","explanation":"印好的固定時間表與題句刻意不設演出順序相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a replacement festival for a cancelled event","explanation":"沒有提到另一場活動取消，replacement 無依據。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"non-mainstream","meaning":"非主流；不屬大眾口味","note":"若節目以主流媒體少播的藝人或風格為核心，觀眾較小但忠實，可用 non-mainstream；不等於活動一定非法、地下或無贊助。","collocations":"a non-mainstream music festival; non-mainstream artists; non-mainstream genres","example":"The festival introduced non-mainstream performers who rarely appeared on major radio stations.","exampleZh":"音樂節介紹了甚少在大型電台亮相的非主流表演者。","contrast":"Non-mainstream 說文化位置；independent 說製作或營運自主。大型公司也可能主辦小眾節目。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A major promoter funded the alternative festival, but its programme featured niche performers absent from the commercial charts.","zh":"大型主辦商資助了這個另類音樂節，但節目以沒有登上商業排行榜的小眾表演者為主。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"A major promoter funded the non-mainstream festival, but its programme featured niche performers absent from the commercial charts.","answer":"non-mainstream","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"independently funded","explanation":"題句明說由大型主辦商出資，不能說資金完全獨立。"},{"letter":"B","text":"non-mainstream","explanation":"小眾藝人未上商業排行榜，non-mainstream 準確描述節目定位。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an experimental event","explanation":"小眾藝人未上榜不表示活動在試驗新方法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mainstream","explanation":"主流定位與小眾、未上榜的節目焦點相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an offbeat event","explanation":"沒有描寫幽默怪趣的演出，offbeat 不是節目定位的最佳概括。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an event at an alternative venue","explanation":"換場地與藝人是否小眾、是否上榜是兩回事。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The alternative music and arts festival devoted its exhibition rooms to self-published comics and minority-language spoken-word artists rarely featured in major arts media.","zh":"這個另類音樂藝術節把展廳留給自行出版的漫畫，以及甚少獲大型藝術媒體介紹的少數語言口述藝術家。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The non-mainstream music and arts festival devoted its exhibition rooms to self-published comics and minority-language spoken-word artists rarely featured in major arts media.","answer":"a non-mainstream music and arts festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an independently owned music and arts festival","explanation":"自行出版的是漫畫，不能由作品的發行方式推斷藝術節的所有權。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a mainstream music and arts festival","explanation":"節目聚焦大型藝術媒體少見的創作者，與主流定位不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an experimental music and arts festival","explanation":"自行出版或媒體少報道不等於藝術節在試行新創作方法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a non-mainstream music and arts festival","explanation":"小眾出版與少數語言藝術家是節目的核心，直接支持非主流文化定位。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a music and arts festival in an alternative venue","explanation":"展廳本身不是重點，題句說的是展出對象而非換場地。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a music and arts festival featuring only rock music","explanation":"題句明列漫畫和口述藝術，不能縮成只有搖滾音樂。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"offbeat","meaning":"別具一格；帶輕鬆怪趣味","note":"當活動有古靈精怪、出人意表而有趣的表演或互動，可用較口語的 offbeat。它比 non-mainstream 更強調奇趣氣質，不適用於只是少人知道但嚴肅傳統的活動。","collocations":"an offbeat festival; offbeat performances; an offbeat arts programme","example":"The offbeat festival paired improvised music with playful puppet performances.","exampleZh":"這個別具一格的音樂節把即興音樂與趣味木偶表演結合。","contrast":"Offbeat 側重奇趣感；experimental 側重新技法的試驗，即使作品嚴肅也可實驗性。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The alternative festival made visitors laugh with a choir of toy robots and musicians dressed as enormous vegetables.","zh":"這個另類音樂節以玩具機械人合唱團，以及打扮成巨大蔬菜的音樂人逗得觀眾大笑。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The offbeat festival made visitors laugh with a choir of toy robots and musicians dressed as enormous vegetables.","answer":"an offbeat festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a formal festival","explanation":"formal 無法表達機械人合唱團與蔬菜服裝的奇趣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an offbeat festival","explanation":"怪趣而好玩的演出讓觀眾發笑，offbeat 語氣最貼合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an underground festival","explanation":"underground 指曝光度或文化場景；怪服裝不能證明地下性。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an experimental festival","explanation":"機械人合唱團和趣味服裝未必是在有系統地試驗新技法；笑點才是焦點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a traditional festival","explanation":"傳統節目與題句故意奇趣的演出方向不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a non-mainstream festival","explanation":"奇趣表演可在主流活動出現，不能只憑服裝判定觀眾或媒體定位。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the alternative arts festival, visitors voted for the next tune by placing coloured paper hats on a talking sculpture.","zh":"在這個另類藝術節，觀眾把彩色紙帽放在會說話的雕塑上，藉此投票決定下一首樂曲。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"At the offbeat arts festival, visitors voted for the next tune by placing coloured paper hats on a talking sculpture.","answer":"an offbeat arts festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a non-mainstream arts festival","explanation":"紙帽投票很奇趣，但題句未交代活動是否屬小眾文化圈。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a conventional arts festival","explanation":"這種遊戲式互動不屬常規音樂節安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an alternative-rock festival","explanation":"投票選樂曲不等於只演另類搖滾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an independently produced arts festival","explanation":"藝術節是否獨立製作未交代；觀眾投票方式不能證明營運結構。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an experimental arts festival","explanation":"題句沒有說在試驗方法或記錄結果；此處重在玩味十足的參與。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an offbeat arts festival","explanation":"會說話的雕塑與紙帽投票突出奇趣互動，offbeat 恰當。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"experimental","meaning":"實驗性的；試行新技法","note":"只有明確說藝術家試用未成熟或新穎的聲音、視覺或表演方法時，才把 alternative 縮成 experimental；原試卷句單獨不足以作此推斷。","collocations":"an experimental music and arts festival; experimental sound; experimental audience participation","example":"At the experimental festival, artists tested new ways to blend live instruments with projected images.","exampleZh":"在實驗性音樂藝術節，藝術家試驗把現場樂器與投影影像結合的新方法。","contrast":"Experimental 指試驗過程，不保證成功或受歡迎；alternative 可只是不走主流，而不一定使用新技術。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The alternative festival gave composers time to test untried ways of blending live strings with electronically generated sounds; the results were uncertain.","zh":"這個另類音樂節讓作曲家試驗現場弦樂與電子聲音的新結合方式，成效仍未確定。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The experimental festival gave composers time to test untried ways of blending live strings with electronically generated sounds; the results were uncertain.","answer":"an experimental festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an experimental festival","explanation":"未試過的混音方法及不確定結果，明確支持 experimental。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a festival featuring only alternative rock","explanation":"新聲音技法不限於另類搖滾，only 多加曲風限制。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a mainstream festival","explanation":"主流定位與此處的試驗目的並不相符，也非題句焦點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a substitute festival","explanation":"沒有另一場活動被替代。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an already standardised festival","explanation":"already standardised 與 test untried ways 矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an independently owned festival","explanation":"作品是否新技法，不能推斷活動所有權。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the alternative festival, composers invited the audience to change a new score during each performance and recorded which instructions produced useful results.","zh":"在這個另類音樂節，作曲家請觀眾在每場表演期間改動新樂譜，並記錄哪些指示產生有用結果。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"At the experimental festival, composers invited the audience to change a new score during each performance and recorded which instructions produced useful results.","answer":"at the experimental festival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"at the fully standardised festival","explanation":"每場讓觀眾改譜並比較效果，並非固定成熟流程。"},{"letter":"B","text":"at the festival with a different date","explanation":"換演出日期不能解釋作曲家讓觀眾改譜並記錄成效。"},{"letter":"C","text":"at the non-mainstream festival","explanation":"方法試驗本身不證明它只面向小眾，而非主流觀眾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"at the alternative-rock festival","explanation":"改譜和記錄效果不限於另類搖滾曲風。"},{"letter":"E","text":"at the experimental festival","explanation":"作曲家反覆試行新觀眾指示、記錄成效，明確是方法實驗。"},{"letter":"F","text":"at the offbeat festival","explanation":"沒有特別幽默怪趣的內容；記錄新指示效果更切合 experimental。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Option / another choice · 選項不是文化風格","zh":"中文辨析： An alternative to a concert 可是「另一個選擇」，但 an alternative festival 在本文是描述活動風格。選項可以非常主流；把 alternative 換成 option 既不合原句形容詞位置，也會漏掉非主流意味。","point":"A choice of events is different from an alternative-style event."},{"word":"Substitute / replacement · 替代事件需先有被取代物","zh":"中文辨析： 原有音樂節取消後，另辦一個 substitute/replacement festival 才有「代替」義；本文沒有取消或替代關係。新活動可以是替代選項，但不能由此推斷其文化風格。","point":"Replacement is a relationship between events, not a style label."},{"word":"Alternative rock · 特定音樂類型不等於整場藝術節","zh":"中文辨析： Alternative rock 是特定音樂類型；原句是音樂與藝術節，沒有說只演另類搖滾。即使有此類樂隊，也不應把整個活動縮成單一曲風。","point":"One music genre cannot represent the entire music-and-arts programme."},{"word":"Independent / underground · 營運方式或可見度未證實","zh":"中文辨析： Independent 常指不受大型機構控制；underground 暗示小型、低曝光或邊緣場景。原句沒有主辦或宣傳資料。若新例句明示這些條件，才可作較窄描述。","point":"Non-mainstream style does not prove independent ownership or underground status."},{"word":"Innovative / unusual / different · 相近但不足以單獨判斷","zh":"中文辨析： Innovative 需有新做法，unusual 只說少見，different 只說與另一活動不同。此三詞可在特定句子貼近原意，但不能一見 alternative 就認定創新、怪異或只是兩者不同。","point":"Difference, novelty and non-mainstream identity are related but distinct."},{"word":"Mainstream / conventional / traditional · 意義方向相反","zh":"中文辨析： 若節目走大眾熱門路線，可說 mainstream；沿用慣例可說 conventional；傳統藝術則可說 traditional。它們不是此處 alternative 的同義詞，雖然同一音樂節可同時包含傳統作品與另類安排。","point":"A festival can include tradition without being conventional overall."}],"moduleNumber":21},{"id":"lesson-022","sourceId":33,"headword":"advantage","title":"Advantage","titleZh":"交通選擇的優點","subtitle":"交通選擇的優點","description":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 4.2〈‘Take a Brake’ Low Carbon Action Scheme〉問：“What are the advantages of alternative modes of transport other than a car?” 來源用複數 advantages，本課以詞條單數 advantage 講一項有利特點，再按句子改成複數。問題請考生比較汽車以外交通方式的可取之處，並未聲稱任何方式在所有條件下都更好，也沒有給實際成效數據。以下指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 4.2〈‘Take a Brake’ Low Carbon Action Scheme〉問：“What are the advantages of alternative modes of transport other than a car?” 來源用複數 advantages，本課以詞條單數 advantage 講一項有利特點，再按句子改成複數。問題請考生比較汽車以外交通方式的可取之處，並未聲稱任何方式在所有條件下都更好，也沒有給實際成效數據。以下指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["benefit","主要近義","指乘客、社區或環境因選擇交通方式而可能得到的好處；須說清受惠對象或效果。"],["strength","有條件近義","指巴士、單車等方式本身相對其他選項的強項；在比較方案時自然。"],["positive aspect","主要近義","中性地說一個好的面向，未必已有可量度成效。"],["merits","詞形須調整","原圖列複數；談一項優點用 merit，談多項用 merits，較正式。"]],"note":"補充 upside，是口語談一項選擇有利之處的常用說法。Pro 與 plus 也是口語單項好處，已在 0034 的 pros and cons、pluses and minuses 教授其兩面權衡用法，故本課不重複兩組相同練習。Asset 多指有用的人、資源或特質，直接說 an asset of cycling 不如本課用語；gain 常暗示已得到結果，源題未給成效證據；selling point 偏推介或營銷，不是所有交通優點都在推銷。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","焦點","何時用"],"rows":[["advantage","一項有利特點","源題泛問其他交通方式的優點。"],["benefit","對人或環境的可能益處","說明受惠者或效果。"],["strength","方案本身的比較強項","有站點、容量等具體特點。"],["positive aspect","中性地指出好的一面","尚未量度實際成效。"],["merit","正式評鑑中的可取處","報告或聽證會；複數為 merits。"],["upside","口語的好處","朋友談話、個人網誌。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 先問「好在哪裏」：所得效果選 benefit，方案強項選 strength，尚待評估的正面選 positive aspect，正式評鑑選 merit，口語談得失可選 upside。單一優點不保證整種交通方式在所有條件下更好。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Benefit","meaning":"益處","note":"強調使用某交通方式對人或環境帶來的有利效果；可說潛在 benefit，不必假裝已證實。","collocations":"a benefit of cycling; benefits for commuters; environmental benefits.","example":"One potential benefit of cycling to school is that pupils get regular exercise.","exampleZh":"騎單車上學的一項潛在好處，是學生能定期運動。","contrast":"Benefit 偏受益效果；strength 偏交通方式的內在強項。若只說路線可達某處，未必能推斷健康效益。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"One possible advantage of walking to school is that pupils may get more daily exercise.","zh":"步行上學的一項可能好處，是學生每天或能多做運動。","upgrade":"One possible benefit of walking to school is that pupils may get more daily exercise.","answer":"benefit","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cost","explanation":"多運動是可能所得，不是要支付的金錢或時間代價。"},{"letter":"B","text":"benefit","explanation":"學生可能獲得健康相關益處，possible benefit 也保留未經保證的語氣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"guarantee","explanation":"May 已表不確定，不能說每位學生都保證多做運動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"route","explanation":"路線是步行經過的地方，不是運動效果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"obligation","explanation":"題句沒有要求學生必須步行。"},{"letter":"F","text":"disadvantage","explanation":"多運動在此被提出為有利結果，不是不利之處。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The council is studying whether a new bus lane could offer residents an advantage by reducing journey times.","zh":"議會正研究新巴士專線能否藉縮短車程，為居民帶來好處。","upgrade":"The council is studying whether a new bus lane could offer residents a benefit by reducing journey times.","answer":"benefit","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"benefit","explanation":"若新專線縮短車程，居民便可能受益；could 保留研究中的不確定性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"burden","explanation":"縮短車程在此是居民可能得到的好處，不是額外負擔。"},{"letter":"C","text":"certainty","explanation":"議會仍在研究，不可把可能效果說成確定事實。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fare","explanation":"車費是價格，題句談的是旅行時間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"timetable","explanation":"巴士時間表可能影響服務，但不是縮短車程帶來的益處本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"restriction","explanation":"巴士專線可能限制其他車輛，卻不是句中給居民的好結果。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Strength","meaning":"強項","note":"比較交通方案時指出某一方式特別做得好的地方，如班次密、可載多人或路線覆蓋好。","collocations":"a strength of the bus network; the strengths of rail travel; relative strength.","example":"A strength of the tram service is its frequent stops in busy districts.","exampleZh":"電車服務的一項強項，是在繁忙地區有密集車站。","contrast":"Strength 不等於乘客肌力，也不直接證明該方式沒有缺點；要有可比較的方案特點。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Compared with driving, one advantage of the tram network is its many stops in the city centre.","zh":"與駕車相比，電車網絡的一項強項，是市中心有很多車站。","upgrade":"Compared with driving, one strength of the tram network is its many stops in the city centre.","answer":"strength","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"physical strength","explanation":"電車網絡不是人，沒有需要量度的肌肉力量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"weakness","explanation":"市中心站點多在比較中被提出為優點，不是缺陷。"},{"letter":"C","text":"strength","explanation":"站點密是網絡本身相對駕車的有利特點，strength of the tram network 自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ticket price","explanation":"句子沒有提供票價資料，不能把車站密度換成價格。"},{"letter":"E","text":"result","explanation":"站點分布是服務特點，不是某項試驗的結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"legal right","explanation":"乘車權利與車站分布不是同一項方案強項。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The transport review named one advantage of the proposed ferry service: it could carry many passengers without using road space.","zh":"交通檢討指出擬議渡輪服務的一項優點：它可載很多乘客而不佔道路空間。","upgrade":"The transport review named one strength of the proposed ferry service: it could carry many passengers without using road space.","answer":"strength","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cost","explanation":"不佔道路而可載多人是方案特點，並非費用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"strength","explanation":"載客能力與不佔道路是渡輪方案的可比較強項，即使仍屬提案也可評估。"},{"letter":"C","text":"guarantee","explanation":"Could 表可能，並未保證每班船都會坐滿。"},{"letter":"D","text":"schedule","explanation":"檢討沒有說渡輪班次或開航時間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"passenger skill","explanation":"方案強項來自交通工具容量，不是乘客操作技能。"},{"letter":"F","text":"drawback","explanation":"此特點在檢討中被提出為有利面，而非不足。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Positive Aspect","meaning":"正面一面","note":"中性地指出一種交通安排好的面向，適合在尚待評估時避免誇大實際效益。","collocations":"a positive aspect of taking the bus; positive aspects of walking; note a positive aspect.","example":"A positive aspect of walking to school is the chance to talk with neighbours.","exampleZh":"步行上學的一個正面之處，是有機會與鄰居交談。","contrast":"Aspect 本身只指方面；加 positive 才表好的面向。這不等於已量度的健康或排放結果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A possible advantage of cycling to the station is that riders can enjoy fresh air along the river path.","zh":"騎單車到車站的一個可能正面之處，是騎車者可沿河道享受新鮮空氣。","upgrade":"A possible positive aspect of cycling to the station is that riders can enjoy fresh air along the river path.","answer":"positive aspect","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"neutral aspect","explanation":"新鮮空氣在句中被當作好的一面，不只是沒有評價的方面。"},{"letter":"B","text":"positive aspect","explanation":"保留對沿河騎行體驗的正面評價，沒有虛構已量度的效果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"proven medical result","explanation":"能享受新鮮空氣不等於已證明某項醫療結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"road hazard","explanation":"沿河新鮮空氣是正面體驗，不是路面危險。"},{"letter":"E","text":"parking rule","explanation":"題句沒有談單車泊位規則。"},{"letter":"F","text":"all-round solution","explanation":"一個好處不表示騎車解決所有交通問題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In a class discussion, the teacher asked for one advantage of taking the bus, even though the pupils had not measured travel times or pollution.","zh":"課堂討論中，老師請學生提出乘巴士的一項正面之處；學生尚未量度車程或污染。","upgrade":"In a class discussion, the teacher asked for one positive aspect of taking the bus, even though the pupils had not measured travel times or pollution.","answer":"positive aspect","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proven environmental gain","explanation":"未量度污染，不能稱已證實環境收益。"},{"letter":"B","text":"negative consequence","explanation":"老師要的是好的一面，不是不利後果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"positive aspect","explanation":"可先討論巴士好的面向，不必聲稱已有精確量度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"full solution","explanation":"一項正面特點不等於解決所有交通問題。"},{"letter":"E","text":"precise saving","explanation":"未量度車程，不能說節省了確切時間。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compulsory rule","explanation":"老師請學生提出觀點，沒有說所有人必須乘巴士。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Merit","meaning":"可取之處（較正式）","note":"正式評鑑交通方案時指出值得考慮的優點；單項用 merit，多項用 merits。","collocations":"a merit of the proposal; merits of public transport; assess the merits.","example":"One merit of the ferry proposal is that it could reduce road congestion.","exampleZh":"渡輪建議的一項可取之處，是它可能減少道路擠塞。","contrast":"Merit 評價方案有價值，不保證預測效果已發生；別把它誤解成考試分數或個人功績。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The planning report identified one advantage of the ferry proposal: it might reduce traffic at the bridge during peak hours.","zh":"規劃報告指出渡輪建議的一項可取之處：它可能在繁忙時間減少橋上的交通流量。","upgrade":"The planning report identified one merit of the ferry proposal: it might reduce traffic at the bridge during peak hours.","answer":"merit","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"demerit","explanation":"減少橋上交通被列為好處，不是方案缺點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"merit","explanation":"正式報告評價提案值得考慮的一面，並以 might 保留尚未驗證的效果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"certainty","explanation":"Might 不容許把預測說成已確定。"},{"letter":"D","text":"route number","explanation":"渡輪路線編號不等於減少交通的可取處。"},{"letter":"E","text":"complaint","explanation":"這是報告列出的潛在益處，不是乘客投訴。"},{"letter":"F","text":"penalty point","explanation":"Merit 在此評鑑方案，不是在給乘客記分。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the formal hearing, councillors discussed one advantage of a new cycle route: it would link two districts without requiring a car.","zh":"在正式聽證會上，議員討論新單車徑的一項優點：它將連接兩區，讓人不用駕車。","upgrade":"At the formal hearing, councillors discussed one merit of a new cycle route: it would link two districts without requiring a car.","answer":"merit","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merit","explanation":"正式聽證會評價路線的可取之處，單項用 merit，不把預定連接說成已實現。"},{"letter":"B","text":"legal offence","explanation":"單車徑連接兩區不是違法行為。"},{"letter":"C","text":"disadvantage","explanation":"不用駕車在此是有利特點，非缺陷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"restriction only","explanation":"單車徑增加出行選項，不是只有限制。"},{"letter":"E","text":"vote total","explanation":"議員是在討論方案優點，沒有點票數據。"},{"letter":"F","text":"physical strength","explanation":"路線可連接地區是方案價值，不是騎車者肌力。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Upside","meaning":"好的一面（口語）","note":"較口語地談某個交通選擇令人看好的地方，常與可能的不便對照。","collocations":"an upside of taking the train; the upside is that ...; a possible upside.","example":"An upside of taking the train is that I can read instead of driving.","exampleZh":"乘火車的一個好處，是我可以閱讀而不用駕車。","contrast":"Upside 在此不是地圖上方；正式政策報告可選 benefit 或 merit。有好的一面不表示全部都好。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"“My bus is sometimes late, but an advantage of taking it is that I can read on the way,” Kai told his friend.","zh":"啟對朋友說：「巴士有時會遲到，但乘巴士的好處是我可以在路上閱讀。」","upgrade":"“My bus is sometimes late, but an upside of taking it is that I can read on the way,” Kai told his friend.","answer":"upside","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"downside","explanation":"巴士遲到是壞處；可以閱讀才是這句轉折後的好處。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upside","explanation":"與朋友口語交談，以 upside 指乘巴士好的一面自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"route change","explanation":"路線有沒有改動並未提及。"},{"letter":"D","text":"obligation","explanation":"啟沒有說自己必須乘巴士。"},{"letter":"E","text":"guarantee","explanation":"可閱讀是一種個人可能性，不是巴士公司給出的保證。"},{"letter":"F","text":"fare increase","explanation":"句子沒有提票價提高。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In her travel vlog, Nora said an advantage of the ferry was seeing the harbour, even though the trip took longer than the train.","zh":"諾拉在旅遊網誌說，渡輪的好處是能欣賞海港，雖然船程比火車車程長。","upgrade":"In her travel vlog, Nora said an upside of the ferry was seeing the harbour, even though the trip took longer than the train.","answer":"upside","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"delay","explanation":"行程較長可能是不利之處；看海港不是延誤本身。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ticket rule","explanation":"題句沒有提購票規則。"},{"letter":"C","text":"timetable","explanation":"觀賞風景不是時刻表。"},{"letter":"D","text":"downside","explanation":"較長船程才是可能的壞處；看海港是好處。"},{"letter":"E","text":"upside","explanation":"網誌以輕鬆語氣把欣賞海港與較長車程對照，upside 正好指有利的一面。"},{"letter":"F","text":"obligation","explanation":"諾拉未說旅客必須乘渡輪。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Advantage / guarantee：可能的優點不等於保證","zh":"公共交通可能減少擠塞，但源題只要求討論優點，沒有保證每位乘客一定省時。English contrast: A possible advantage is not a guaranteed outcome.","point":""},{"word":"Benefit / cost：受益與付出","zh":"Benefit 指所得好處；票價、轉車時間可能是 cost 或 drawback。若題目只問優點，不能用成本代替。English contrast: Cost names a burden, not a benefit.","point":""},{"word":"Strength / physical strength：方案強項與肌力","zh":"The strength of the tram network 可指站點密；騎單車所需的 physical strength 是人的體力，不是同一個意思。English contrast: The strength of a transport option is its favourable feature.","point":""},{"word":"Positive aspect / aspect：評價不能漏","zh":"Aspect 只說「某方面」，可能好也可能壞；須有 positive 才可替代優點。English contrast: The adjective positive supplies the favourable judgment.","point":""},{"word":"Merit / demerit：優點與缺點","zh":"正式討論中 merit 是值得稱道之處，demerit 可指缺點；但學校紀律的記過點數又是 demerit 的另一義。English contrast: Merit evaluates a proposal's value, not a pupil's conduct record.","point":""},{"word":"Upside / downside：方向比喻與語體","zh":"交通討論中的 upside 是有利一面，downside 是不利一面；它不是路線上坡下坡。口語用得自然，正式報告則須考慮語體。English contrast: Upside and downside are figurative evaluations here.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":22},{"id":"lesson-023","sourceId":39,"headword":"advice","title":"Advice","titleZh":"給準實習生的建議","subtitle":"給準實習生的建議","description":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 1.1「An Intern in Hong Kong」問：「Any advice for potential interns?」題目要說話者向可能參加實習的人提出有幫助的做法或看法，沒有要求法律諮詢，也沒有說所有建議都是命令。以下指南與練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 1.1「An Intern in Hong Kong」問：「Any advice for potential interns?」題目要說話者向可能參加實習的人提出有幫助的做法或看法，沒有要求法律諮詢，也沒有說所有建議都是命令。以下指南與練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["guidance","教授","可指較持續的指引或輔導；比一條小貼士廣。"],["recommendations","教授","一項或多項值得採納的具體做法，常用複數。"],["counsel","不作本來源核心替換","作建議可用，但正式、常帶專業或慎重輔導語氣；對普通準實習生的日常提問過重。"]],"note":"補充 tips，適合可立即實行的小技巧；suggestions，適合保留選擇空間的提議。Pointers 接近 tips，若再開兩題會重複同一實用技巧；input 可指意見但不保證有指導作用；instructions 是較明確的操作指令，不一定容許選擇。Advice 本身通常不可數，不能說 an advice。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","最合適的情況","注意"],"rows":[["advice","一般有幫助的做法或看法","通常不可數。"],["guidance","持續方向與支援","不只一條小方法。"],["recommendations","可逐項採納的明確做法","可數；不自動等於硬性規定。"],["tips","簡短、具體的小技巧","語氣較輕。"],["suggestions","供對方考慮的提議","保留選擇空間。"],["counsel","較正式或專業的輔導","普通實習問題通常過重。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 持續指引用 guidance；列出多項較明確做法用 recommendations；可立即試用的小方法用 tips；讓對方自由考慮的提議用 suggestions。注意 advice 與 advise 的詞性及不可數用法。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Guidance","meaning":"指引／輔導","note":"給予方向和支援，可貫穿實習前準備或工作期間；通常不可數。","collocations":"guidance for interns; seek guidance from a supervisor; guidance on workplace conduct.","example":"New interns received guidance from a supervisor throughout their first month.","exampleZh":"新實習生在首個月持續得到主管指引。","contrast":"一條「帶筆記簿」的技巧更像 tip；跨數週的方向與支援更像 guidance。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"During their first month, new interns could seek advice from a supervisor whenever they were unsure how to handle a task.","zh":"新實習生首個月遇到不懂處理的工作時，都可以向主管尋求指引。","upgrade":"During their first month, new interns could seek guidance from a supervisor whenever they were unsure how to handle a task.","answer":"guidance","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a warning","explanation":"主管可在有風險時警告，但句子談各種工作疑問的持續支援。"},{"letter":"B","text":"guidance","explanation":"首個月遇到不確定工作便向主管請教，屬持續的工作指引。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an order","explanation":"實習生主動請教方法，不是在要求主管發命令。"},{"letter":"D","text":"information","explanation":"只獲得事實資訊未必能解決「如何處理工作」的方向問題。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an interview","explanation":"面試是甄選對話；這些人已在實習首月工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a rule","explanation":"固定規則未必回答多種不確定工作的處理方法。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before the placement began, the school offered advice on workplace conduct, reporting problems and asking for help.","zh":"實習開始前，學校就職場禮儀、匯報問題及求助方法提供指引。","upgrade":"Before the placement began, the school offered guidance on workplace conduct, reporting problems and asking for help.","answer":"guidance","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"guidance","explanation":"學校在三方面提供實習前方向，guidance on 是自然搭配。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a command","explanation":"內容包括求助方法及職場行為，不只是單一強制命令。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a rumour","explanation":"學校正式提供的準備資料不應無根據地叫傳聞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a contract","explanation":"合約約定權責；句子說學校提供實習前做事指引。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a warning only","explanation":"匯報問題可涉及風險，但職場禮儀和求助也屬正面指導。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a timetable","explanation":"時間表列安排，不會概括禮儀與問題處理方法。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Recommendations","meaning":"建議採取的做法","note":"可以逐項列出的較明確建議；說話者認為採納後會有益處，但未必強制。","collocations":"recommendations for future interns; make recommendations; follow a recommendation.","example":"Former interns made three recommendations: arrive early, ask questions and keep a work log.","exampleZh":"前實習生提出三項建議：提早到達、主動發問，以及記錄工作。","contrast":"Recommendation 可以數：one recommendation, three recommendations；advice 通常不可數。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The former intern's advice for newcomers came in three points: arrive early, write down instructions and ask when uncertain.","zh":"前實習生給新人的建議分為三點：提早到、記錄指示，以及不明白時發問。","upgrade":"The former intern's recommendations for newcomers came in three points: arrive early, write down instructions and ask when uncertain.","answer":"recommendations","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"requirements","explanation":"前實習生提出有益做法，不代表學校正式規定三點都必須遵守。"},{"letter":"B","text":"rumours","explanation":"三點是可操作做法，不是未經證實的傳聞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"recommendations","explanation":"三項可逐一採納的做法可稱複數 recommendations。"},{"letter":"D","text":"warnings","explanation":"記錄指示和主動發問不只是風險警告。"},{"letter":"E","text":"guarantees","explanation":"提早到和發問不能保證實習一定成功。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reports","explanation":"這些是給新人的行動提議，不是回報已發生事件的報告。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After learning each student's interests, the careers teacher sent advice to future interns on which of three placements would suit them best.","zh":"了解每名學生的興趣後，就業輔導老師就三種實習崗位中哪一種最適合他們提出建議。","upgrade":"After learning each student's interests, the careers teacher sent recommendations to future interns on which of three placements would suit them best.","answer":"recommendations","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a job offer","explanation":"老師幫學生比較三種崗位，沒有正式給任何人工作機會。"},{"letter":"B","text":"recommendations","explanation":"老師根據個人興趣建議最合適的實習崗位，屬可考慮的選擇建議。"},{"letter":"C","text":"instructions from the employer","explanation":"訊息由老師提供，不是接待機構規定每人必須選同一崗位。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an advertisement","explanation":"內容針對學生興趣比較崗位，並非向大眾公開招募。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a warning notice","explanation":"老師沒有提示某個崗位的危險，而是在比較合適程度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a review of past interns","explanation":"建議面向未來實習生，不是評核已完成實習的人。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Tips","meaning":"實用小貼士","note":"簡短、具體、可立即試用的小方法，語氣比正式建議輕。","collocations":"practical tips for interns; tips on travelling to work; share a few tips.","example":"The intern shared two tips: save the duty officer's number and leave extra travel time.","exampleZh":"實習生分享兩個小貼士：儲存當值主管電話，並預留額外交通時間。","contrast":"Tips 可數；若是涉及長期職涯方向，guidance 通常更合適。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The intern shared practical advice about saving the duty officer's number and leaving ten extra minutes for the bus.","zh":"實習生分享實用小貼士：儲存當值主管電話，以及為巴士預留多十分鐘。","upgrade":"The intern shared practical tips about saving the duty officer's number and leaving ten extra minutes for the bus.","answer":"tips","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"rules","explanation":"同輩分享的小方法沒有被說成機構強制規定。"},{"letter":"B","text":"facts","explanation":"電話號碼與巴士時間是資訊；「儲存」「預留」則是行動技巧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"warnings","explanation":"兩項正面準備方法不只是在提示危險。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tips","explanation":"短而立即可用的做法符合實用小貼士的語氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"formal counsel","explanation":"同輩分享通勤和聯絡方法，不是法律或專業輔導。"},{"letter":"F","text":"duties","explanation":"工作職責不是如何儲存電話及預留交通時間的建議。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"One piece of advice on Maya's interview blog was to check the route the night before so a late bus would not make an applicant panic.","zh":"瑪雅的面試網誌有一條建議：前一晚查好路線，以免巴士誤點令應徵者慌張。","upgrade":"One tip on Maya's interview blog was to check the route the night before so a late bus would not make an applicant panic.","answer":"tip","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"instruction","explanation":"網誌作者只分享可參考的準備方法，沒有向讀者發強制指令。"},{"letter":"B","text":"guarantee","explanation":"前晚查路可減低慌張風險，不能保證巴士準時或面試成功。"},{"letter":"C","text":"direction","explanation":"路線指示會說怎樣到達；此處建議的是何時查路與如何預先準備。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tip","explanation":"One tip 把一條可立即實行的小方法自然地數出來。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interview result","explanation":"面試尚未開始，網誌沒有公布錄取結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"employment rule","explanation":"查路線是面試前小方法，不是受聘後的正式工作守則。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Suggestions","meaning":"供考慮的提議","note":"提出可能有幫助的做法，讓對方判斷是否採用；比指令更有彈性。","collocations":"suggestions for potential interns; offer suggestions; ask for suggestions about a first day.","example":"The mentor offered several suggestions for introducing yourself to the team.","exampleZh":"導師提出幾個向團隊作自我介紹的建議，供實習生考慮。","contrast":"Suggestions 不代表已獲批准的正式規則；勿把可選提議當成必須服從的命令。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The mentor asked the new interns if they wanted any advice about how to introduce themselves to the team on day one.","zh":"導師問新實習生，是否想聽一些第一天向團隊自我介紹的建議。","upgrade":"The mentor asked the new interns if they wanted any suggestions about how to introduce themselves to the team on day one.","answer":"suggestions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"suggestions","explanation":"導師先問對方是否想聽，表示可考慮的自我介紹做法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"orders","explanation":"命令不會以「是否想聽」的自願方式提出。"},{"letter":"C","text":"guarantees","explanation":"沒人能保證某種自我介紹一定帶來理想結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"assessments","explanation":"句子是面對第一天的準備，不是在評核已做的介紹。"},{"letter":"E","text":"regulations","explanation":"沒有正式機構規條，只有導師可能提供的做法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"complaints","explanation":"導師不是在蒐集對團隊的不滿。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the placement schedule changed, the interns offered advice on rearranging their shared tasks, and the supervisor considered each idea.","zh":"實習時間表變動後，實習生提出如何重新分配共同工作的建議，主管逐一考慮。","upgrade":"When the placement schedule changed, the interns offered suggestions on rearranging their shared tasks, and the supervisor considered each idea.","answer":"suggestions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"final orders","explanation":"主管仍逐一考慮，實習生沒有直接下最終命令。"},{"letter":"B","text":"objections only","explanation":"他們提出可行的重新分工方法，不只是反對變動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suggestions","explanation":"多個可供主管評估的分工想法，符合 suggestions 的非強制語氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"results","explanation":"時間表剛變，句中尚未描述新安排的結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"complaints","explanation":"提出重排方法不等於抱怨。"},{"letter":"F","text":"instructions from management","explanation":"想法來自實習生，並非管理層已下的指示。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Advise / advice：詞性","zh":"Advise 是動詞，advice 是名詞；「give advice」不能寫成「give advise」。English contrast: She advises interns; she gives them advice.","point":""},{"word":"An advice：不可數名詞","zh":"在此義 advice 通常不可數；一條建議可說 a piece of advice 或 a recommendation。English contrast: Some advice; one recommendation.","point":""},{"word":"Instructions / orders：強制程度","zh":"實習生必須遵守安全指令；「可以早到十分鐘」則可能只是建議。English contrast: Follow safety instructions; consider a mentor's suggestions.","point":""},{"word":"Information：事實與行動方向","zh":"告知上班時間是資訊；建議預留交通時間才是行動建議。English contrast: The start time is information; leaving early is advice.","point":""},{"word":"Counsel：正式程度","zh":"法律或重大個人困難的輔導可叫 counsel；普通實習準備問題通常用 advice/guidance 自然。English contrast: Seek legal counsel; ask a former intern for practical tips.","point":""},{"word":"Warning：風險提醒與正面建議","zh":"提醒「不要在網上公開客戶資料」是警告的一部分，也可成為建議；單純 warning 不能概括所有幫助準實習生的做法。English contrast: A warning flags danger; advice can cover broader preparation.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":23},{"id":"lesson-024","sourceId":6,"headword":"ability","title":"Ability","titleZh":"能力；不同程度的能力","subtitle":"能力；不同程度的能力","description":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 2.1〈Apprenticeship Programmes in Switzerland〉說瑞士學徒制度吸納不同社經背景和 ability levels 的學生。這裏 ability 是學生一般的學習或做事能力，levels 說程度高低；原文沒有指某一門天生才能，也沒有把學生局限於一項技術。以下部分詞只在句子加入「潛力」、「已能執行」、「特定技能」或「達標程度」時成立。與 0007 able to watch 不同，0007 的電影觀賞是機會／可行性，不是學業或專業能力。","sourceSense":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 2.1〈Apprenticeship Programmes in Switzerland〉說瑞士學徒制度吸納不同社經背景和 ability levels 的學生。這裏 ability 是學生一般的學習或做事能力，levels 說程度高低；原文沒有指某一門天生才能，也沒有把學生局限於一項技術。以下部分詞只在句子加入「潛力」、「已能執行」、「特定技能」或「達標程度」時成立。與 0007 able to watch 不同，0007 的電影觀賞是機會／可行性，不是學業或專業能力。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["capacity","有條件","偏向可學、可承擔的潛力或容量；learning capacity 自然，不等於目前成績。"],["capability","有條件","指實際可以執行某項任務的能力；比原文籠統的 ability levels 更具體。"],["aptitude","有條件","對某門學科或工作有學習天分；不能把原文所有能力水平改成天生資質。"],["skill","有條件","經學習或練習形成的具體技能；skill levels 可用於特定項目，但窄於一般 ability levels。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["問的問題","較合適說法"],"rows":[["還未學但有潛力／可承擔更多嗎？","capacity"],["已能執行指定任務嗎？","capability"],["初學時顯出學得快的傾向嗎？","aptitude"],["練成了一項可觀察技巧嗎？","skill"],["表現達到要求標準嗎？","competence"],["特定領域的熟練程度有多高？","proficiency"]],"note":"快選規則： 原文 students of all ability levels 是包容不同一般程度的廣義說法，不能只用一項天資或技能重新界定所有學生。若改寫成這六個較窄詞，句子必須補上相應證據。0007 的 able to watch 則問觀賞是否可能，不能把 0006 的學習能力詞直接搬過去。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Capacity","meaning":"潛在能力；承擔能力","note":"適用於可學會某事或可承受工作量的潛力，不必證明當下已熟練。","collocations":"capacity to learn / improve / cope; learning capacity; capacity for extra work.","example":"The apprentice had the capacity to learn welding despite having no prior training.","exampleZh":"那名學徒雖然未受過相關訓練，仍有能力學會焊接。","contrast":"Capacity 也可指容納人數，本文不是該意思；別把可學會誤寫成已經會做。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The teacher recognised Nabil’s ability to learn coding with support, although he had never programmed before.","zh":"納比爾從未寫過程式，但老師看出他在支援下有學會編程的能力。","upgrade":"The teacher recognised Nabil’s capacity to learn coding with support, although he had never programmed before.","answer":"capacity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proficiency","explanation":"Nabil 從未編程，老師只是看到可學的潛力，不能稱他已有熟練程度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"aptitude","explanation":"Aptitude 通常接 for，不能直接替換 ability to learn 的名詞而保留 to；這裏也未特別證明某方面天資。"},{"letter":"C","text":"capacity","explanation":"Capacity to learn 指仍可學會，與沒有先前經驗並不矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"skill","explanation":"未上過編程課，句子尚未證明他已掌握具體編程技巧。"},{"letter":"E","text":"competence","explanation":"Competence 指現已能按標準執行；Nabil 尚未學過編程，老師只看到可學的潛力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"experience","explanation":"Experience 是過往經驗，句中明說沒有。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"With two placements already filling her timetable and leaving her exhausted, the trainee asked whether she had the ability to handle a third.","zh":"兩份實習已佔滿見習生的時間並使她疲憊，她因此問自己能否承擔第三份。","upgrade":"With two placements already filling her timetable and leaving her exhausted, the trainee asked whether she had the capacity to handle a third.","answer":"capacity","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aptitude","explanation":"她擔心的是時間已滿又疲憊，並非是否有學習第三份工作的天分；aptitude to handle 也不自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"capacity","explanation":"Capacity to handle 同時涵蓋時間與精力是否足以再負擔一份。"},{"letter":"C","text":"availability","explanation":"Availability 偏時段是否空閒；句子還明說她已疲憊，單說有空不足以回答能否負擔。"},{"letter":"D","text":"stamina","explanation":"Stamina 偏耐力，卻不能回答日程已被兩份實習佔滿的限制。"},{"letter":"E","text":"proficiency","explanation":"工作技巧熟練，也不能解決日程和精力不足。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permission","explanation":"是否獲准做第三份實習是另一問題；此處問她本人是否還承受得起。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Capability","meaning":"實際執行能力","note":"在訓練、工具和經驗已具備時，說人能實際完成某項清楚指明的任務。","collocations":"capability to perform / repair; technical capability; demonstrate capability.","example":"After training, the apprentices showed the capability to repair a bicycle safely.","exampleZh":"受訓後，學徒展示了安全維修單車的能力。","contrast":"Capability 可指系統功能，也可指人；原文一般 ability levels 並不保證每人已能完成同一技術任務。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After six weeks of practice, the apprentice demonstrated her ability to repair the pump without supervision.","zh":"練習六星期後，學徒展示她無須督導也能維修水泵。","upgrade":"After six weeks of practice, the apprentice demonstrated her capability to repair the pump without supervision.","answer":"capability","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"capability","explanation":"已實際示範獨立維修，capability 指可執行任務。"},{"letter":"B","text":"possibility","explanation":"Possibility 只是可能性，不等於她已示範能做。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intention","explanation":"Intention 是打算，不是實際維修能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"capacity to learn","explanation":"學徒已在無監督下修好水泵，句子證明的是現有執行能力，而非日後學會的可能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"certification","explanation":"Certification 是證書；句中只說實際表現。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aptitude","explanation":"六週實習後已完成維修；aptitude 偏重先天或早期學習潛質。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The new diagnostic tool gave the repair team the ability to identify faults on site, work it previously had to outsource.","zh":"新診斷工具讓維修隊能在現場找出故障；以前這項工作必須外判。","upgrade":"The new diagnostic tool gave the repair team the capability to identify faults on site, work it previously had to outsource.","answer":"capability","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aptitude","explanation":"診斷工具賦予維修隊現場找故障的實際手段，不是在測隊員是否有學習天分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"capability","explanation":"有了工具，維修隊現在能自行執行以前外判的特定任務，capability to identify 合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"competence","explanation":"工具使維修隊能在現場診斷，但未證明全隊經評核達到固定專業標準；此處說的是新增的執行能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"possibilities","explanation":"句子說維修隊已可在現場找故障，不只是抽象的多種可能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"know-how","explanation":"工具提供新的診斷手段，並未說隊員因此學得故障原理或操作知識；know-how to identify 也不如 capability to identify 自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"capacity to learn","explanation":"維修隊現在能直接識別故障，而非只是具有將來學會診斷的潛力。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Aptitude","meaning":"天資；學習潛質","note":"對某門工作或學科較易學會的傾向；在初接觸任務卻學得特別快的語境成立。","collocations":"aptitude for design / mathematics; show an aptitude for; aptitude test.","example":"Mei showed an aptitude for carpentry when she quickly learned to measure wood.","exampleZh":"阿美很快學會量度木材，顯示她有木工方面的學習天分。","contrast":"Aptitude 不等於已學會的 skill，也不可據此把所有程度學生都標成有天分。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"On her first day, Mei showed an unusual ability to pick up carpentry techniques quickly, although she had not trained before.","zh":"第一天接觸木工時，阿美雖未受過訓練，卻展現出異乎尋常的快速學習能力。","upgrade":"On her first day, Mei showed an unusual aptitude for picking up carpentry techniques quickly, although she had not trained before.","answer":"aptitude","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proficiency","explanation":"梅第一天尚未受訓，不能說她已有熟練的木工水平。"},{"letter":"B","text":"trained skill","explanation":"梅尚未受過正式訓練，這裏觀察到的是快速上手的潛質，而非已練成的技巧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"aptitude","explanation":"初次接觸卻學得很快，aptitude for 點出學習潛質；介詞須由 to 改為 for。"},{"letter":"D","text":"qualification","explanation":"Qualification 是正式資格，第一天尚無。"},{"letter":"E","text":"experience","explanation":"Experience 是既有經歷，句中明說沒有。"},{"letter":"F","text":"capacity","explanation":"Capacity 可泛指學習能力，但題句特別指出她異常快上手，aptitude 更精確。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The selection test measured each applicant’s ability to grasp unfamiliar mechanical principles before any training began.","zh":"甄選測驗在訓練開始前，評估每名申請人能否迅速理解陌生的機械原理。","upgrade":"The selection test measured each applicant’s aptitude for grasping unfamiliar mechanical principles before any training began.","answer":"aptitude","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aptitude","explanation":"甄選在訓練前評估理解陌生原理的傾向，aptitude for grasping 比已學成的技能準確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"proficiency","explanation":"尚未開始機械訓練，測驗並非量度申請人已有的操作熟練程度。"},{"letter":"C","text":"developed expertise","explanation":"面對陌生原理時的理解潛力，不等於已累積的專業知識。"},{"letter":"D","text":"confidence","explanation":"申請人可以很有信心卻不一定能理解陌生原理；甄選測的是上手潛質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"familiarity","explanation":"原理對申請人是 unfamiliar，測驗不是確認他們原已熟悉這些內容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"skill","explanation":"此處測的是訓練前的上手潛力，未證明申請人已練成機械技巧。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Skill","meaning":"經訓練形成的技巧","note":"可透過練習發展和觀察的某項具體能力，例如焊接、量度或溝通。","collocations":"develop a skill; welding skills; skill in using a tool; skill level.","example":"The apprentice developed the skill of checking electrical circuits safely.","exampleZh":"學徒培養了安全檢查電路的技能。","contrast":"Skill 常指特定學會的技巧；原文「各種能力水平」比單一 skill levels 廣泛。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After months of practice, the apprentice’s ability to join two metal pieces precisely had become reliable.","zh":"經過數月練習，那名學徒準確接合兩塊金屬的能力已變得可靠。","upgrade":"After months of practice, the apprentice’s skill in joining two metal pieces precisely had become reliable.","answer":"skill","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aptitude","explanation":"數月練習後能精準接合金屬，是習得的技巧，不只早期天分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"skill","explanation":"Skill in joining 指經訓練而能穩定執行的具體技巧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"capacity","explanation":"Capacity 可泛指承擔或發展能力；數月練習後的精準接合是特定已練成技巧，skill 更貼切。"},{"letter":"D","text":"certificate","explanation":"Certificate 是文件，不是動作本身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"proficiency","explanation":"Proficiency 說一個領域整體的熟練水平；句子聚焦接合兩塊金屬這項具體技巧，skill in joining 更直接。"},{"letter":"F","text":"competence","explanation":"Competence 可指達到安全標準；本句聚焦精準接合這項特定技巧，skill 更具體。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the repair course, trainees developed their ability to read circuit diagrams until they could spot wiring errors at a glance.","zh":"維修課程中，見習生反覆練習閱讀電路圖，直到能一眼看出接線錯誤。","upgrade":"During the repair course, trainees developed their skill in reading circuit diagrams until they could spot wiring errors at a glance.","answer":"skill","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"skill","explanation":"反覆練習把閱讀電路圖發展成可觀察的診斷技巧；skill in reading 自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"capacity","explanation":"Capacity 可說有讀圖潛力，但此句是反覆練習後已能一眼看出錯誤的具體技巧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"competence","explanation":"Competence 可概括達標表現；此句描述反覆練出的特定讀圖技巧，skill 更聚焦。"},{"letter":"D","text":"technique","explanation":"Technique 指採用的讀圖方法；原句要替代的是學生透過練習取得的能力，而非某套做法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"aptitude","explanation":"一眼識錯來自課程中的反覆讀圖練習，不能只說是先天上手傾向。"},{"letter":"F","text":"qualification","explanation":"課程讓學生讀圖更準確，並未說已取得正式資格；資格也不能替代一項具體技巧。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Competence","meaning":"足以勝任的能力","note":"指一個人能按要求完成任務，重點是達到適當標準，而非只具潛力。","collocations":"competence in a task; demonstrate competence; professional competence.","example":"The assessment confirmed her competence in handling the equipment safely.","exampleZh":"評核確認她有能力按標準安全操作設備。","contrast":"Competence 通常要有評核或表現證據；ability 可以籠統描述不同程度，未必人人都已達標。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The assessment confirmed his ability to perform the procedure safely and to the required standard.","zh":"評核證實他能按規定標準安全完成該程序。","upgrade":"The assessment confirmed his competence in performing the procedure safely and to the required standard.","answer":"competence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"confidence","explanation":"對程序有信心不等於評核證實能按標準安全完成。"},{"letter":"B","text":"competence","explanation":"已按標準完成程序，competence in 點出勝任程度。"},{"letter":"C","text":"capacity to learn","explanation":"Capacity to learn 只指將來可學，弱於已達標。"},{"letter":"D","text":"aptitude","explanation":"評核已證實他按規定安全完成程序，測的是現有勝任程度，不是入門時的學習天分。"},{"letter":"E","text":"qualification","explanation":"正式資格可由評核帶來，但題句要說明評核確認的操作能力，不是證書或資格本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"experience","explanation":"曾做過程序不保證這次按規定安全達標；評核確認的是現有勝任能力。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before allowing independent work, the instructor judged the trainee’s ability to choose a safe response when a machine unexpectedly jammed.","zh":"導師在准許學徒獨立工作前，評估他在機器突然卡住時能否選擇安全的應對方法。","upgrade":"Before allowing independent work, the instructor judged the trainee’s competence in choosing a safe response when a machine unexpectedly jammed.","answer":"competence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aptitude","explanation":"導師評估面對突發卡機能否作出安全判斷，而非推測學徒將來學得快不快。"},{"letter":"B","text":"competence","explanation":"能在突發故障時選對安全應對，顯示足以獨立工作的勝任能力；competence in choosing 自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"certificate","explanation":"資格文件不能代替對突發卡機應對判斷的實際評估。"},{"letter":"D","text":"aspiration","explanation":"想獨立工作不代表在機器卡住時知道安全做法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"confidence","explanation":"學徒可以自信地作決定，但導師要核查的是卡機時能否選對安全應對。"},{"letter":"F","text":"experience","explanation":"導師評估的是這次突發卡機時能否作出安全判斷，不是學徒過往經歷有多少。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"Proficiency","meaning":"熟練程度","note":"描述在某門語言、技術或明確領域中經學習後達到的熟練水平，常與 in 連用。","collocations":"proficiency in English / coding / a trade; high level of proficiency.","example":"The language test measured each apprentice’s proficiency in German.","exampleZh":"語言測驗量度每名學徒的德語熟練程度。","contrast":"Proficiency 較原文籠統的 ability 窄，通常要指定領域並有一定練習；不等於單純有機會學。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The exam measured the students’ ability to read German after two years of language lessons.","zh":"經過兩年語言課程，考試評估學生的德語閱讀能力。","upgrade":"The exam measured the students’ proficiency in reading German after two years of language lessons.","answer":"proficiency","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proficiency","explanation":"兩年課程後的考試量度已發展的閱讀水平；由 ability to read 改為自然的 proficiency in reading。"},{"letter":"B","text":"aptitude","explanation":"考試在兩年課後量度德文閱讀水平，非入門前學語言的天資。"},{"letter":"C","text":"confidence","explanation":"上了兩年課可能更有信心，但考試量度的是實際德語閱讀表現。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reading speed","explanation":"Reading speed 只說快慢；句子沒有計時證據，且要保留的是整體德語閱讀水平。"},{"letter":"E","text":"intelligence","explanation":"德語閱讀考試評估經學習形成的語言表現，不能直接等同學生的一般智力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"motivation","explanation":"學習動機可能影響進步，但閱讀考試直接量度的是表現，不是學習意願。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The final practical test demonstrated the trainees’ ability to use the workshop’s cutting machine with a high degree of accuracy.","zh":"期末實作測驗顯示，見習生能高度準確地使用工作坊的切割機。","upgrade":"The final practical test demonstrated the trainees’ proficiency in using the workshop’s cutting machine with a high degree of accuracy.","answer":"proficiency","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"possibility","explanation":"測驗已顯示高度準確的操作，possibility 只說可能做到。"},{"letter":"B","text":"proficiency","explanation":"高準確度的實作表現支持 proficiency in using，同時保留技術和表現兩層意思。"},{"letter":"C","text":"aptitude","explanation":"期末實作測試顯示現有操作水平，不是尚未訓練時的學習潛質。"},{"letter":"D","text":"familiarity","explanation":"熟悉切割機不保證能高度準確操作；familiarity in using 也不如 proficiency in using 自然。"},{"letter":"E","text":"confidence","explanation":"自信不等於實作測驗已顯示高度準確的表現。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ambition","explanation":"想學好切割機操作不等於已能高度準確地使用。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"capacity / capability：潛能與可執行","zh":"學徒未學過程式但可學會，是 capacity to learn；已能獨立修理機器，才可說有該項 capability。兩詞在別處可重疊，這裏用時間及證據區分。","point":"Capacity can foreground potential; capability can foreground demonstrated ability to do a task."},{"word":"aptitude / skill：天資與習得","zh":"Aptitude for design 是某方面較容易學會的傾向；design skills 是經練習具備的技巧。原文包容所有程度學生，不暗示人人有天資或已熟練。","point":"Aptitude concerns suitability to learn; skill concerns learned performance."},{"word":"competence / proficiency：達標與熟練程度","zh":"Competence 可說達到任務標準；proficiency 常說在語言或技術上的熟練程度。兩者比原文一般的 ability 更具體，不可無證據稱所有學徒都已熟練。","point":"Competence focuses on adequate performance; proficiency on developed command."},{"word":"ability / disability / inability：不要錯誤推論","zh":"Students of all ability levels 說接納不同程度的學生；不能改成 students with disabilities，因為「能力程度」不等於是否有殘疾。Inability 是不能做某事，也不等於能力較初階。","point":"A range of ability levels is not a statement about disability or total inability."},{"word":"capacity：非人的容量義","zh":"The classroom has a capacity of 30 指座位上限；本文講學生能力。詞形相同不表示這個物理容量義可用來描述學生的學習水平。","point":"Capacity of a room is maximum occupancy, a different sense from learning capacity."},{"word":"talent / qualification / achievement：不同對象","zh":"Talent 偏天分，qualification 是證書資格，achievement 是已取得成果；三者都不能單獨代表本文包容不同能力程度。","point":"A gift, credential and result are distinct from a general level of ability."}],"moduleNumber":24},{"id":"lesson-025","sourceId":91,"headword":"approach","title":"Approach","titleZh":"養育做法與理念","subtitle":"養育做法與理念","description":"2014 DSE Paper 4 set 10.1 says that some argue Sweden’s “child-centered approach has gone too far.” Approach is a count noun naming a broad manner or orientation in child-rearing. The criticism is reported opinion, not an established fact about all families. A narrower method or strategy needs concrete procedure or goal clues. All guide and practice sentences below are original.","sourceSense":"2014 DSE Paper 4 set 10.1 says that some argue Sweden’s “child-centered approach has gone too far.” Approach is a count noun naming a broad manner or orientation in child-rearing. The criticism is reported opinion, not an established fact about all families. A narrower method or strategy needs concrete procedure or goal clues. All guide and practice sentences below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["method","有條件近義","具體、可重複的方法；抽象育兒方針未必是方法。"],["strategy","有條件近義","為明確目標而設的計劃，原文未明說這層目的性。"],["way","直接廣義改寫","說成 way of raising children 才清楚保留育兒範圍。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： 補充 parenting style（持續的互動模式）和 child-rearing philosophy（支撐做法的理念）；後者指信念，若句子只描述執行細節便不可替換。Policy 偏機構規章，technique 偏單一技巧，attitude 只說心態；均不概括整個來源意思。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["看見的線索","最精確的說法"],"rows":[["一般養育方式，無固定程序","way of raising children"],["多年持續的親子互動模式","parenting style"],["明言關於兒童需要的信念","child-rearing philosophy"],["可重複的具體步驟","parenting method"],["為明確目標而設的安排","parenting strategy"]],"note":"原文的 child-centered approach 可寬可窄，必須按後文線索決定；這些近義說法不是每句都能機械替換。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"way of raising children","meaning":"養育子女的方式","note":"最廣、日常的改寫；用 of raising children 補回原文育兒範圍。","collocations":"a way of raising children; a different way of bringing up children","example":"The family discussed a gentler way of raising children.","exampleZh":"這家人討論了一種更溫和的養育子女方式。","contrast":"Way 本身太泛；method 暗示較具體做法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The parents described their approach as listening first and setting boundaries together, without following a fixed programme.","zh":"父母說自己的做法是先聆聽，再共同訂界線，並沒有依循固定方案。","upgrade":"The parents described their way of raising children as listening first and setting boundaries together, without following a fixed programme.","answer":"way of raising children","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"way of raising children","explanation":"全句概述父母如何養育孩子，且沒有固定程序，廣義 way 最合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parenting method","explanation":"method 暗示明確程序，題句說沒有固定方案。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"strategy 通常有預設目標與計劃，句中只描寫一般做法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school policy","explanation":"這是家庭相處方式，不是學校規章。"},{"letter":"E","text":"discipline technique","explanation":"聆聽與訂界線不只是一項管教技巧。"},{"letter":"F","text":"child-rearing result","explanation":"題句談做法，沒有交代成效。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A survey compared each family’s approach to bedtime, meals and schoolwork, rather than testing one specific technique.","zh":"一項調查比較各家庭如何處理睡眠、用餐和功課，而非測試某一項技巧。","upgrade":"A survey compared each family’s way of raising children in matters of bedtime, meals and schoolwork, rather than testing one specific technique.","answer":"way of raising children","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"single parenting trick","explanation":"涉及三個生活範疇，不是一個小訣竅。"},{"letter":"B","text":"official family policy","explanation":"家庭日常安排不等於正式政策。"},{"letter":"C","text":"way of raising children","explanation":"比較多個養育範疇的方式，way of raising children 保留廣度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有說家長為特定目標設計計劃。"},{"letter":"E","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"調查比較實際安排，未必探討背後理念。"},{"letter":"F","text":"educational outcome","explanation":"並非比較孩子最終成績。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"parenting style","meaning":"育兒風格","note":"指家長長期與子女互動的典型模式，例如如何聆聽、訂界線和回應。","collocations":"a child-centred parenting style; change one’s parenting style","example":"Her parenting style gives children room to explain their views.","exampleZh":"她的育兒風格容許孩子解釋自己的看法。","contrast":"Style 重複而持久；單次處理衝突的技巧不等於整體風格。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Over many years, the father’s approach remained warm but firm: he heard his children out and kept agreed limits.","zh":"多年來，父親的做法一直溫和而堅定：他聽孩子說話，也維持共同商定的界線。","upgrade":"Over many years, the father’s parenting style remained warm but firm: he heard his children out and kept agreed limits.","answer":"parenting style","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one-time technique","explanation":"題句強調多年一致，不是一次技巧。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parenting style","explanation":"多年持續的溫和而堅定互動模式，正是 parenting style。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有單一目標與階段計劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school policy","explanation":"父親的相處模式不是學校政策。"},{"letter":"E","text":"childhood result","explanation":"談的是家長如何做，不是孩子成長結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"parental mood","explanation":"mood 是一時情緒，不能概括多年模式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Her approach was consistently patient in everyday conversations with her children, even when she disagreed with them.","zh":"即使與孩子意見不同，她在日常對話中也一直保持耐心。","upgrade":"Her parenting style was consistently patient in everyday conversations with her children, even when she disagreed with them.","answer":"parenting style","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"family rule","explanation":"規則可寫在紙上，句中重點是每日互動方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"可能有理念，但句中直接描寫她持續的談話模式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting style","explanation":"一貫耐心的日常互動符合育兒風格。"},{"letter":"D","text":"negotiation trick","explanation":"不只一次協商技巧。"},{"letter":"E","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有為某目標而設的計劃。"},{"letter":"F","text":"temporary reaction","explanation":"consistently 表示持續，非一時反應。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"child-rearing philosophy","meaning":"育兒理念","note":"指一套關於兒童需要與家長角色的信念；必須有原則或觀念的線索。","collocations":"a child-rearing philosophy; a philosophy centred on children","example":"Their child-rearing philosophy treats listening as a sign of respect.","exampleZh":"他們的育兒理念認為聆聽是尊重的表現。","contrast":"Philosophy 是背後理念；method 是具體如何做。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The couple’s approach rests on the belief that children deserve explanations, not orders without reasons.","zh":"這對夫婦的做法立基於一項信念：孩子值得得到解釋，而不是毫無理由的命令。","upgrade":"The couple’s child-rearing philosophy rests on the belief that children deserve explanations, not orders without reasons.","answer":"child-rearing philosophy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting method","explanation":"具體方法會說如何操作；這裏是在說信念。"},{"letter":"B","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"句中明言 belief，是養育理念的根基。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有目標導向的步驟計劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"household rule","explanation":"一項原則不等於某條家規。"},{"letter":"E","text":"discipline technique","explanation":"沒有描述某個管教技巧。"},{"letter":"F","text":"school curriculum","explanation":"不是學校課程。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The author calls this approach a matter of respecting a child’s voice, rather than a checklist of steps for parents.","zh":"作者認為這種做法關乎尊重孩子的意見，而不是給父母執行的步驟清單。","upgrade":"The author calls this child-rearing philosophy a matter of respecting a child’s voice, rather than a checklist of steps for parents.","answer":"child-rearing philosophy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有為目標制定階段計劃。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parenting method","explanation":"文中明言不是步驟清單，method 過於程序化。"},{"letter":"C","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"核心是尊重兒童聲音的價值觀，屬育兒理念。"},{"letter":"D","text":"childcare procedure","explanation":"procedure 更強調規定次序，與題句相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"household routine","explanation":"routine 是日常重複安排，未表達尊重的原則。"},{"letter":"F","text":"parental reaction","explanation":"不是一次即時反應。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"parenting method","meaning":"具體育兒方法","note":"有清楚可重複的程序或技巧時用；比原文寬泛的 approach 窄。","collocations":"a parenting method for resolving disputes; try a different parenting method","example":"The parenting method asks each person to speak without interruption.","exampleZh":"這種育兒方法要求每個人發言時不受打斷。","contrast":"沒有具體程序時，不宜把整套理念硬稱 method。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The counsellor taught an approach in which parents take turns speaking, repeat what they heard, and then propose a compromise.","zh":"輔導員教授一種做法：父母輪流發言、覆述聽到的話，再提出折衷方案。","upgrade":"The counsellor taught a parenting method in which parents take turns speaking, repeat what they heard, and then propose a compromise.","answer":"parenting method","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting style","explanation":"style 指長期互動模式，不如具步驟的 method 準確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"philosophy 指理念，不描述三步程序。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting method","explanation":"輪流發言、覆述、提出建議構成可重複的方法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"family policy","explanation":"沒有制定正式家規。"},{"letter":"E","text":"desired outcome","explanation":"折衷可能是結果，但題句教的是程序。"},{"letter":"F","text":"parental attitude","explanation":"單靠心態不能表明三步做法。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For homework disputes, the parents tried an approach of writing down each child’s concern before discussing any solution.","zh":"遇到功課爭執，父母試行一種做法：先寫下每個孩子的顧慮，再討論解決辦法。","upgrade":"For homework disputes, the parents tried a parenting method of writing down each child’s concern before discussing any solution.","answer":"parenting method","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"沒有跨時期的總體目標計劃。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parenting method","explanation":"先記錄顧慮再討論，是可操作且可重複的方法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting style","explanation":"style 太廣，未突出這項做法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"沒有講解育兒價值體系。"},{"letter":"E","text":"school rule","explanation":"父母在家試行，並非校規。"},{"letter":"F","text":"final solution","explanation":"solution 是後續可能找到的答案，非這個做法。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"parenting strategy","meaning":"育兒策略","note":"家長為了明確目標制定一連串有意安排時用，例如逐步培養自主。","collocations":"a parenting strategy to build independence; plan a strategy","example":"Their parenting strategy gives the teenager one new responsibility each month.","exampleZh":"他們的育兒策略每月給青少年一項新的責任。","contrast":"Strategy 有目標和計劃；style 可以是習慣而沒有明訂目標。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Their approach to building independence gives the child one new responsibility each month and reviews progress at the end of the year.","zh":"他們為培養獨立性的做法是每月給孩子一項新責任，並在年底檢討進度。","upgrade":"Their parenting strategy for building independence gives the child one new responsibility each month and reviews progress at the end of the year.","answer":"parenting strategy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting style","explanation":"style 不如 strategy 表達明確目標及進度安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"single technique","explanation":"每月新責任和年底檢討超過單一技巧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"有培養獨立性的目標及時間安排，屬育兒策略。"},{"letter":"D","text":"family attitude","explanation":"attitude 只講心態，漏掉逐月安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"educational result","explanation":"獨立性是期望成果，不是安排本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"school timetable","explanation":"家庭責任計劃不是學校時間表。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"To help their son manage money, the parents adopted an approach: a small allowance now, then a larger budget once he could track his spending.","zh":"為幫兒子管理金錢，父母採取一種做法：先給少量零用錢，待他能記錄開支後再增加預算。","upgrade":"To help their son manage money, the parents adopted a parenting strategy: a small allowance now, then a larger budget once he could track his spending.","answer":"parenting strategy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"parenting method","explanation":"method 可描述一項程序，但題句聚焦理財目標和分階段安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parenting style","explanation":"不是一般親子互動風格。"},{"letter":"C","text":"child-rearing philosophy","explanation":"沒有專談背後信念。"},{"letter":"D","text":"parenting strategy","explanation":"以理財為目標、按進度調整預算，strategy 最準。"},{"letter":"E","text":"household policy","explanation":"不是針對全家的成文規章。"},{"letter":"F","text":"childhood result","explanation":"尚未說孩子已達成最終成果。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"technique / trick · 單項技巧","zh":"中文辨析： 一個勸說技巧或小訣竅可屬整體育兒 approach 的一部分，不能涵蓋一整套關係模式；在題句只問某一次談話技巧時才成立。","point":"One technique is smaller than an overall approach."},{"word":"policy / rule · 規章","zh":"中文辨析： 學校或政府可訂育兒政策；原文談家庭中的兒童為本取向，不是明文頒布的規則。若題句指正式規章，policy 才合適。","point":"A family orientation need not be a formal policy."},{"word":"attitude / belief · 心態與信念","zh":"中文辨析： 尊重兒童的信念可能支撐做法，但 approach 也包含實際相處模式；若只談內在看法，attitude 才可用。","point":"Belief alone does not describe the practical manner."},{"word":"solution / result · 處理方式與結果不同","zh":"中文辨析： Solution 是已找到的解答或結果；approach 是如何處理問題。即使某做法有效，不能因此把做法換成成果。","point":"An approach may lead to a solution; it is not the solution itself."},{"word":"child-centred / child-led · 以兒童為本不等於由兒童全權主導","zh":"中文辨析： Child-centred 指考慮兒童需要；child-led 暗示孩子決定方向。原文報道有人認為孩子權力過大，不代表每個 child-centred 做法都是 child-led。","point":"The source reports criticism; it does not equate the two labels."}],"moduleNumber":25},{"id":"lesson-026","sourceId":97,"headword":"argue","title":"Argue","titleZh":"主張某個有爭議的看法","subtitle":"主張某個有爭議的看法","description":"The 2013 DSE set 8.3 passage contrasts “some say...” with “others argue that...”, reporting different interpretations of appearance and beauty ideals. Argue that introduces a position being advanced, ordinarily with some reasoning; the excerpt does not prove that either group’s view is true or representative of all Asian people. It is not “quarrel with someone” here. All exercises below are original and avoid asserting the passage’s contested interpretation as fact.","sourceSense":"The 2013 DSE set 8.3 passage contrasts “some say...” with “others argue that...”, reporting different interpretations of appearance and beauty ideals. Argue that introduces a position being advanced, ordinarily with some reasoning; the excerpt does not prove that either group’s view is true or representative of all Asian people. It is not “quarrel with someone” here. All exercises below are original and avoid asserting the passage’s contested interpretation as fact.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["contend","近義","正式提出可辯論立場，通常有理由。"],["maintain","有條件","持續或面對反對仍堅持某立場；單次發言不一定有持續性。"],["claim","有條件","報道某人作出尚待驗證的斷言，不保證已有理由。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： Assert 是明確、肯定地說出主張；put forward the view 是中性明示「提出看法」的片語。Reason that 若明列推理步驟才可用；insist 強調強硬態度，believe 可只在心中相信，debate/quarrel 指互動行為，均不能無條件替換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["線索","優先動詞或片語"],"rows":[["有理由的正式辯論立場","contend that"],["面對質疑仍持續堅持","maintain that"],["可查證但尚未核實的說法","claim that"],["肯定而明確地斷言","assert that"],["中性提出一種觀點","put forward the view that"]],"note":"五項都報道別人的立場，並不替立場背書；來源的 argue that 不等於 quarrel 或 prove。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"contend","meaning":"主張；提出有爭議論點","note":"正式書面語，強調在不同意見中提出並通常試圖辯護的立場；常接 that。","collocations":"contend that the evidence is incomplete; critics contend that; contend that a proposal is fair","example":"Several teachers contend that later start times would help tired pupils.","exampleZh":"數名教師主張較遲上課有助疲倦的學生。","contrast":"Contend 比 say 更有辯論色彩；不等於與人吵架。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In the public debate, several historians argue that the old market should be preserved because its design shows how the district developed.","zh":"在公開辯論中，數名歷史學家主張保留舊街市，因為其設計顯示該區如何發展。","upgrade":"In the public debate, several historians contend that the old market should be preserved because its design shows how the district developed.","answer":"contend","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"contend","explanation":"公開辯論中提出保育理由，contend 突出有爭議立場及論證。"},{"letter":"B","text":"maintain","explanation":"maintain 常指持續堅持，句中只見這次辯論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"claim","explanation":"claim 可報道主張，但淡化已給出的歷史理由。"},{"letter":"D","text":"assert","explanation":"assert 強調肯定語氣，未如 contend 突出辯論和理由。"},{"letter":"E","text":"conclude","explanation":"conclude 暗示研究推導後得出結論，句中未交代完整研究過程。"},{"letter":"F","text":"allege","explanation":"allege 常指未證實的不當行為，這裏是保育建議。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Two scholars argue that the survey’s conclusion is premature, pointing to its small sample and missing age groups.","zh":"兩名學者指出樣本太小且漏掉一些年齡組別，主張調查結論言之過早。","upgrade":"Two scholars contend that the survey’s conclusion is premature, pointing to its small sample and missing age groups.","answer":"contend","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"insist","explanation":"insist 帶強硬堅持意味，題句只顯示學術辯論。"},{"letter":"B","text":"contend","explanation":"提出可辯論結論並列兩項樣本理由，contend 最合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"claim","explanation":"claim 可表主張，但沒有突出列證據來辯論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"assert","explanation":"assert 偏肯定斷言，未如 contend 呈現有據反駁。"},{"letter":"E","text":"conclude","explanation":"conclude 像研究者自己完成分析後定論，句中只是質疑別人的結論。"},{"letter":"F","text":"maintain","explanation":"maintain 需持續持有觀點的線索，題句沒有。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"maintain","meaning":"持續堅持某主張","note":"說話者在時間或質疑下繼續持有同一觀點時用，常接 that。","collocations":"maintain that the policy works; continue to maintain that; maintain a position","example":"Despite new criticism, the group maintains that its proposal is fair.","exampleZh":"儘管有新的批評，該團體仍堅持其建議公平。","contrast":"Maintain 有持續堅持意味；一個剛提出的新觀點宜用 put forward。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although several parents challenged the plan, the headteacher continued to argue that the new timetable would help students rest.","zh":"雖然多名家長質疑計劃，校長仍持續主張新時間表有助學生休息。","upgrade":"Although several parents challenged the plan, the headteacher continued to maintain that the new timetable would help students rest.","answer":"maintain","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"suggest for the first time","explanation":"continued 說明不是首次提出。"},{"letter":"B","text":"maintain","explanation":"家長質疑後仍持續持有立場，maintain 精確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"claim","explanation":"claim 可說出觀點，卻不表持續堅持。"},{"letter":"D","text":"assert","explanation":"assert 說話力度強，未表 continued 的時間線。"},{"letter":"E","text":"conclude","explanation":"conclude 是作出結論，不能表明面對反對仍持續。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concede","explanation":"concede 是讓步，與仍主張相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For three years, the committee has argued that the building can be repaired rather than demolished, even after repeated objections.","zh":"三年來，儘管不斷有人反對，委員會仍主張該樓可修復而非拆卸。","upgrade":"For three years, the committee has maintained that the building can be repaired rather than demolished, even after repeated objections.","answer":"maintained","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"suggested","explanation":"suggested 太弱，未涵蓋三年來持續的既定立場。"},{"letter":"B","text":"conceded","explanation":"conceded 指讓步，與反對後仍堅持相反。"},{"letter":"C","text":"maintained","explanation":"多年面對反對仍持有看法，maintained 最合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"asserted once","explanation":"once 與三年和 repeated objections 不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"concluded","explanation":"concluded 只說得出結論，未表不斷重申。"},{"letter":"F","text":"alleged","explanation":"alleged 常指不當行為的未證指控，這裏是可否修復。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"claim","meaning":"聲稱；提出尚待證實說法","note":"記述某人提出可被查證或質疑的說法，而敘述者不替它背書；常接 that。","collocations":"claim that results improved; claim without evidence; a disputed claim","example":"The company claims that its new filter removes most odours.","exampleZh":"該公司聲稱新過濾器能去除大部分異味。","contrast":"Claim 可不附理由，且語氣可能帶證據距離；contend 較像辯護論點。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The manufacturer argues that its bottle keeps water cold for twenty-four hours, but the article says no independent test has checked this.","zh":"製造商聲稱瓶子可讓水保持冰冷二十四小時，但文章說尚無獨立測試驗證。","upgrade":"The manufacturer claims that its bottle keeps water cold for twenty-four hours, but the article says no independent test has checked this.","answer":"claims","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proves","explanation":"沒有獨立測試，不能說 proves。"},{"letter":"B","text":"claims","explanation":"性能說法尚待驗證，claims 保持敘述者的證據距離。"},{"letter":"C","text":"asserts as established fact","explanation":"as established fact 把未經測試的說法錯當確立事實。"},{"letter":"D","text":"concludes from tests","explanation":"文中明說沒有測試，不能說從測試得結論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"maintains after repeated challenges","explanation":"沒有反覆受質疑後仍堅持的時間線。"},{"letter":"F","text":"alleges misconduct","explanation":"不是指控誰有不當行為。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A campaign leaflet argues that attendance doubled last month; it gives no figures, so the editor treats the statement as unverified.","zh":"宣傳單張聲稱上月出席人數翻倍，但沒有提供數據，因此編輯把這句話視作未經核實。","upgrade":"A campaign leaflet claims that attendance doubled last month; it gives no figures, so the editor treats the statement as unverified.","answer":"claims","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proves","explanation":"沒有數據支持，不能說證明。"},{"letter":"B","text":"maintains after repeated challenges","explanation":"沒有重複受質疑並堅持的歷程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"claims","explanation":"翻倍是可查證而未核實的說法，claims 精確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"concludes from data","explanation":"沒有數據，不能說從數據得結論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"asserts a verified result","explanation":"verified 與編輯視為 unverified 相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"suggests a possibility","explanation":"單張用肯定語氣說翻倍，不只是提出可能性。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"assert","meaning":"斷言；肯定地說","note":"明確而肯定地說某主張，可能尚未給出證據；常接 that。","collocations":"assert that a figure is correct; publicly assert that; assert a right","example":"The spokesperson asserted that the figures were accurate, but provided no data.","exampleZh":"發言人斷言數據準確，卻沒有提供資料。","contrast":"Assert 強調說話的肯定力度；claim 側重敘述者未核實內容。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At the meeting, the spokesperson argued that the figures were accurate, speaking with certainty but showing no supporting records.","zh":"發言人在會議上肯定地說數據準確，卻沒有展示支持紀錄。","upgrade":"At the meeting, the spokesperson asserted that the figures were accurate, speaking with certainty but showing no supporting records.","answer":"asserted","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proved","explanation":"沒有展示紀錄，不能說已證明。"},{"letter":"B","text":"asserted","explanation":"肯定地說主張但未展示證據，asserted 合語氣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suggested","explanation":"suggested 較保留，與 speaking with certainty 不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"conceded","explanation":"conceded 是讓步。"},{"letter":"E","text":"claimed tentatively","explanation":"tentatively 表猶豫，與肯定語氣不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"inferred from records","explanation":"沒有紀錄可供推導。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The director argued in a firm statement that the school had followed every required step, though auditors had not yet completed their review.","zh":"校長在一份語氣肯定的聲明中主張學校已遵照所有必要步驟，雖然審計人員尚未完成檢查。","upgrade":"The director asserted in a firm statement that the school had followed every required step, though auditors had not yet completed their review.","answer":"asserted","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"guessed","explanation":"firm statement 表明並非隨意猜測。"},{"letter":"B","text":"proved","explanation":"審計未完成，尚未證明。"},{"letter":"C","text":"asserted","explanation":"正式肯定地陳述立場，asserted 準確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admitted","explanation":"admitted 常指承認不利情況，此處是自我辯護。"},{"letter":"E","text":"suggested tentatively","explanation":"tentatively 與 firm statement 牴觸。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concluded after audit","explanation":"審計未完成，不能說已在審計後得結論。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"put forward the view","meaning":"提出看法","note":"較中性地呈現有人提出一種解釋；可接 that，或用 view that；不暗示真偽。","collocations":"put forward the view that; put forward an alternative view","example":"The researcher put forward the view that the survey needed a larger sample.","exampleZh":"研究員提出看法，認為調查需要更大的樣本。","contrast":"比 maintain 少持續性，比 assert 少強硬斷言色彩。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In her first article on the topic, the researcher argues that the survey may reflect sampling bias, offering it as one possible interpretation.","zh":"研究員首次就此題發表文章，提出調查可能受抽樣偏差影響，並把這視作一種可能解釋。","upgrade":"In her first article on the topic, the researcher puts forward the view that the survey may reflect sampling bias, offering it as one possible interpretation.","answer":"puts forward the view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"maintains","explanation":"first article 表示首次提出，maintains 的持續性未成立。"},{"letter":"B","text":"proves","explanation":"一種可能解釋不是已證明。"},{"letter":"C","text":"puts forward the view","explanation":"中性提出一種看法，puts forward the view 合適。"},{"letter":"D","text":"insists","explanation":"insists 強硬，與 possible interpretation 不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"concludes definitively","explanation":"definitively 與可能解釋相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"claims as a verified fact","explanation":"verified fact 與 possible interpretation 相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the discussion, a student argued that the club could hold shorter meetings; she presented this as a suggestion, not a demand.","zh":"討論期間，一名學生提出社團可縮短會議時間；她把這視作建議而非要求。","upgrade":"During the discussion, a student put forward the view that the club could hold shorter meetings; she presented this as a suggestion, not a demand.","answer":"put forward the view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proved","explanation":"建議尚未證實必定可行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"insisted","explanation":"句中明說不是強硬要求。"},{"letter":"C","text":"put forward the view","explanation":"提出可討論的看法，put forward the view 保留溫和語氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"maintained for years","explanation":"沒有多年持續主張的線索。"},{"letter":"E","text":"asserted as certain","explanation":"她說的是 suggestion，並未斷言必定如此。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concluded from data","explanation":"沒有列資料供推論出結論。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"quarrel / fight · 爭吵不是提出論點","zh":"中文辨析： Argue with someone 可是爭吵；來源的 argue that 引出命題，並無說雙方在現場吵架。若談激烈人際衝突才用 quarrel。","point":"A reporting clause about a position differs from an interpersonal dispute."},{"word":"prove / establish · 主張未必證實","zh":"中文辨析： 來源只報道某組人主張甚麼。Prove/establish 要有充分證據及結論，不能把爭議觀點升格為事實。","point":"An argument may be offered without being proved."},{"word":"believe / think silently · 內在看法未必公開提出","zh":"中文辨析： Believe 可只是某人私下想法；argue that 表有人把看法提出供討論。若文章明言公開發表，單說 believe 漏掉傳達行為。","point":"Private belief and public argument are not identical."},{"word":"reason / infer · 推理過程與主張行為不同","zh":"中文辨析： Reason 或 infer 可指從證據推導結論；來源沒有列出完整推理，只有報道主張。若題句真的展示推論過程，才可用 reason that。","point":"A conclusion can be argued without the excerpt showing every inferential step."},{"word":"insist / demand · 堅持與要求須有線索","zh":"中文辨析： Insist 暗示強硬或面對反對仍不退讓；demand 更是要求別人行動。來源只說 others argue，不能自行加上強硬語氣。","point":"A stated position need not be an insistence or demand."}],"moduleNumber":26},{"id":"lesson-027","sourceId":98,"headword":"argument","title":"Argument","titleZh":"辯論中的理由與論點","subtitle":"辯論中的理由與論點","description":"A reproduced 2013 DSE Paper 4 set 4.1 debate prompt asks students to discuss “arguments for the motion” and “arguments against the motion” about eating food from animals treated cruelly. The OCR elsewhere in the reproduction is noisy, but these two phrases are legible in the prompt. Here arguments is a plural count noun: reasons or cases advanced on either side, not a quarrel. The prompt does not itself endorse either side. [Reproduced 2013 Paper 4 examiner text](https://www.scribd.com/document/672533453/2013-HKDSE-ENG-Paper-4-Examiner). All guide and exercise scenarios below are original.","sourceSense":"A reproduced 2013 DSE Paper 4 set 4.1 debate prompt asks students to discuss “arguments for the motion” and “arguments against the motion” about eating food from animals treated cruelly. The OCR elsewhere in the reproduction is noisy, but these two phrases are legible in the prompt. Here arguments is a plural count noun: reasons or cases advanced on either side, not a quarrel. The prompt does not itself endorse either side. [Reproduced 2013 Paper 4 examiner text](https://www.scribd.com/document/672533453/2013-HKDSE-ENG-Paper-4-Examiner). All guide and exercise scenarios below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["reasoning","有條件整體改寫","不可數，偏從前提推到結論的推理過程；不能說 three reasonings。"],["case","有條件近義","一方完整的理由與證據組合，常比一個 argument 大。"],["line of reasoning","有條件近義","數個相扣的推理步驟；單一獨立理由未必是一條推論鏈。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： 補入常用可數 reason、辯論中可數的 supporting point，以及政策／決定背後的 rationale。Evidence 是支持論點的資料，不是論點本身；opinion 只有看法未必有理由；dispute/quarrel 是衝突；justification 與 rationale 高度重疊，故不重複計課。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["看到的結構","建議改寫"],"rows":[["一項「為何」","reason"],["辯論提綱中的一點","supporting point"],["一方多項理由與證據組成整體","case for/against"],["相扣的前提到結論","line of reasoning"],["決定／政策背後的目的和理由","rationale"],["整體推理品質，不能逐個數","reasoning"]],"note":"來源 arguments for/against the motion 是辯論正反論據；不是 quarrels。Reasoning 不可數，改寫時要連句法一起改。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"reason","meaning":"理由","note":"一項可數的「為何支持／反對」原因；最容易改寫 one argument for/against。","collocations":"a reason for the motion; reasons against the proposal; give a reason","example":"One reason against the ban is that small farms may need time to adapt.","exampleZh":"反對禁令的一項理由是小農場或需要時間適應。","contrast":"Reason 可以很簡短；case 可包含多項理由與證據。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"One argument against the proposal is that the nearest alternative canteen is a long bus ride away.","zh":"反對建議的一項理由是最近的其他飯堂要乘很久巴士才到。","upgrade":"One reason against the proposal is that the nearest alternative canteen is a long bus ride away.","answer":"reason","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reason","explanation":"句子提供一項為何反對的原因，reason 最直接。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the entire case","explanation":"整套 case 會有多項理由，原句只列一項。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one raw fact","explanation":"巴士距離已被用作反對原因，不只是孤立資料。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a rebuttal to a named speaker","explanation":"題句未指明針對哪名發言人作反駁。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the final motion","explanation":"動議是待辯題目，不是提出的原因。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a policy rationale","explanation":"rationale 通常指支持政策決定的整體理據，這裏只是一項反對原因。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A second argument for the motion is that clearer labels would let buyers compare the origins of food.","zh":"支持動議的第二項理由是更清晰的標籤可讓顧客比較食物來源。","upgrade":"A second reason for the motion is that clearer labels would let buyers compare the origins of food.","answer":"reason","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one example","explanation":"標籤益處已被說成第二項理由，不只是一個例子。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reason","explanation":"second 表示另一項獨立原因，reason 可數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"whole case","explanation":"整套 case 包含多項理由，不能只指第二項。"},{"letter":"D","text":"supporting evidence alone","explanation":"資料支持理由，但題句本身解釋為何支持動議。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a rebuttal to a previous point","explanation":"未說是在駁斥上一項論點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a conclusion","explanation":"這是支持動議的理由，非辯論結論。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"supporting point","meaning":"支持某立場的一個論點","note":"辯論或演講中一項可陳述、可展開的論點；要寫明支持哪一方。","collocations":"a supporting point for the motion; three supporting points; develop a point","example":"The team wrote a supporting point about the cost of inspection.","exampleZh":"小組寫下一項關於檢查成本的支持論點。","contrast":"比純 opinion 多了為立場服務的功能；仍可能需要證據支持。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The team listed three arguments for the motion on its debate card, each with a heading and one example.","zh":"小組在辯論卡上列出三項支持動議的論點，每項有標題及例子。","upgrade":"The team listed three supporting points for the motion on its debate card, each with a heading and one example.","answer":"three supporting points","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"three debate outcomes","explanation":"卡片列的是要發表的論點，不是辯論完畢的結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one overall case","explanation":"一套整體論證可包含三點，one 不能代替三個分列項目。"},{"letter":"C","text":"three sources of evidence alone","explanation":"每一標題本身是論點，例子才提供證據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"three supporting points","explanation":"三項有標題及例子的可展開論點，supporting points 最準。"},{"letter":"E","text":"three policy rationales","explanation":"沒有三項不同政策決定需要三套 rationale。"},{"letter":"F","text":"three rebuttals to named opponents","explanation":"沒有指定要逐一反駁哪名對手。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In her speech, the student added an argument that stricter checks could prevent misleading labels, then explained it with an example.","zh":"學生在演說中加入一項論點，認為更嚴格檢查可防止誤導標籤，並舉例解釋。","upgrade":"In her speech, the student added a supporting point that stricter checks could prevent misleading labels, then explained it with an example.","answer":"supporting point","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"supporting point","explanation":"演說中新加一項並舉例展開，supporting point 最精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"whole case","explanation":"整套 case 是全篇立場，不是新加的一點。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an unreasoned opinion","explanation":"她不只表態，還給例子解釋。"},{"letter":"D","text":"example alone","explanation":"例子是支持這一點的材料，不是這一點本身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"counterargument to a named speaker","explanation":"未說針對哪名發言人的論點反駁。"},{"letter":"F","text":"final verdict","explanation":"演說中的論點不是評判裁決。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"case","meaning":"一方整套論證","note":"一方把多項理由與證據組織成整體立場時用；常說 the case for/against。","collocations":"make the case for reform; the case against the ban; a strong case","example":"The students built a case against the proposal using cost and access data.","exampleZh":"學生利用成本及可達性數據，建立反對建議的整套論證。","contrast":"一個小 point 未必足以構成一方的整套 case。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The group’s argument against the ban combined cost figures, access concerns and interviews with small restaurant owners.","zh":"小組反對禁令的論證結合成本數字、可達性顧慮及小餐館東主訪談。","upgrade":"The group’s case against the ban combined cost figures, access concerns and interviews with small restaurant owners.","answer":"case","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"single reason","explanation":"句中結合成本、可達性及訪談，超過一項原因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"case","explanation":"多項理由與證據組成整體 case。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one piece of evidence","explanation":"成本數字只是其中一項材料。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one line of reasoning only","explanation":"only 將多面向反方立場錯縮成一條推理鏈。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the motion itself","explanation":"動議是討論題目，不是反方組合的論證。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a bare opinion","explanation":"已有三類證據與顧慮，不是空泛意見。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"By the end of practice, their argument for the motion had four reasons and evidence for each one.","zh":"練習結束時，他們支持動議的整套論證有四項理由，而且每項均有證據。","upgrade":"By the end of practice, their case for the motion had four reasons and evidence for each one.","answer":"case","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one supporting point","explanation":"四項理由不是單一支持點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one example","explanation":"四項理由各有證據，不只舉一例。"},{"letter":"C","text":"case","explanation":"四項理由與證據形成一方完整 case。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one inference only","explanation":"only 把多項可能獨立論點縮成單一步推論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the motion","explanation":"motion 是辯論命題，不是小組編成的正方論證。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unreasoned opinion","explanation":"有理由及證據，不是無據看法。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"line of reasoning","meaning":"相扣的一條推論","note":"前提、因果步驟及結論連成一線時用；可數但常指完整推論鏈。","collocations":"a line of reasoning; follow the line of reasoning; several lines of reasoning","example":"Her line of reasoning linked animal welfare standards to restaurant purchasing choices.","exampleZh":"她的推論把動物福利標準與餐廳採購選擇連起來。","contrast":"資料本身是 evidence；連結資料並推到結論才是 reasoning。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her argument began with the inspection data, linked poor labelling to uninformed choices, and ended by supporting a new rule.","zh":"她的論證從檢查數據開始，把標籤不足與顧客資訊不全連起來，最後支持訂立新規則。","upgrade":"Her line of reasoning began with the inspection data, linked poor labelling to uninformed choices, and ended by supporting a new rule.","answer":"line of reasoning","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"single statistic","explanation":"單一檢查數字沒有後續因果連結。"},{"letter":"B","text":"line of reasoning","explanation":"數據、推論與結論依次相扣，是 line of reasoning。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one supporting point without links","explanation":"without links 刪掉題句明列的連結。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the entire debate","explanation":"只說她的推理，不是整場辯論。"},{"letter":"E","text":"rationale for a policy decision","explanation":"她最後支持新規則，但句子重點是如何一步步推到它。"},{"letter":"F","text":"conclusion alone","explanation":"最後支持新規則只是結論，漏掉此前步驟。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The speaker’s argument was that fewer checks mean more false labels, which in turn makes informed buying harder.","zh":"發言人的論證是：檢查減少會令虛假標籤增加，而這又令顧客更難知情選購。","upgrade":"The speaker’s line of reasoning was that fewer checks mean more false labels, which in turn makes informed buying harder.","answer":"line of reasoning","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"two unrelated points","explanation":"兩個因果環節相扣，不是互不相干。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one statistic","explanation":"沒有單一統計資料作全句內容。"},{"letter":"C","text":"conclusion alone","explanation":"句中還有前提與中間環節，不是只有結論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a policy rationale","explanation":"這裏描寫推導過程，不只是政策決定背後的目的。"},{"letter":"E","text":"line of reasoning","explanation":"檢查到標籤再到知情選購，構成相扣推論。"},{"letter":"F","text":"whole team case","explanation":"只列一條連鎖推理，未交代全隊多項理由。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"rationale","meaning":"決定或政策背後的理據","note":"解釋為何採取某項措施或支持某決定時用；可說 rationale for the decision。","collocations":"the rationale for a rule; explain the rationale; policy rationale","example":"The committee explained the rationale for requiring clearer food labels.","exampleZh":"委員會解釋要求更清晰食品標籤的理據。","contrast":"比一般 reason 更常指一項決定或政策背後的整體理由；不是成效本身。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The council’s argument for requiring origin labels was that shoppers should know how their food was produced.","zh":"議會要求產地標籤的理據是顧客應知道食物如何生產。","upgrade":"The council’s rationale for requiring origin labels was that shoppers should know how their food was produced.","answer":"rationale","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"rationale","explanation":"顧客應知情是議會作出標籤要求的理據，rationale 合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one example","explanation":"不是只舉一個例子。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the resulting label","explanation":"標籤是要求的結果，非要求背後理由。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one supporting point only","explanation":"only 把決策背後整體目的縮成單一演說點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an unreasoned opinion","explanation":"已說明顧客知情的理由，不是空泛看法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"the debate motion","explanation":"動議是辯論命題，不等於議會立規理據。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school explained its argument for changing the lunch contract: it wanted suppliers to disclose animal-welfare standards.","zh":"學校解釋更改午餐合約的理據：希望供應商披露動物福利標準。","upgrade":"The school explained its rationale for changing the lunch contract: it wanted suppliers to disclose animal-welfare standards.","answer":"rationale","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"after-the-fact result","explanation":"題句在解釋更改的目的，尚未交代結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one isolated statistic","explanation":"沒有用單一數字作理由。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the lunch supplier","explanation":"供應商是要求對象，不是改約理據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one supporting point only","explanation":"only 太窄，這裏概括學校決策目的。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the new contract itself","explanation":"合約是被更改的文件，不是為何改的理由。"},{"letter":"F","text":"rationale","explanation":"要求披露福利標準是決策背後的 rationale。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"reasoning","meaning":"推理過程；整體論證方式","note":"不可數，指把前提、資料與結論連結的思路；若原句用複數 arguments，需整句改寫。","collocations":"sound reasoning; reasoning behind a claim; flawed reasoning","example":"The judge praised the team’s reasoning but questioned one piece of evidence.","exampleZh":"評判讚賞小組的推理方式，但質疑其中一項證據。","contrast":"不能說 three reasonings 來代替 three arguments；要說 three reasons 或 three lines of reasoning。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The judges praised the team’s arguments as careful, especially how it linked its evidence to the motion; they were not counting separate points.","zh":"評判讚賞小組的論證思路審慎，尤其是把證據與動議連結的方式；他們不是在數個別論點。","upgrade":"The judges praised the team’s reasoning as careful, especially how it linked its evidence to the motion; they were not counting separate points.","answer":"reasoning","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"separate reasons","explanation":"題句明言評判不是在數個別理由。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reasoning","explanation":"整體連接證據與動議的推理品質是 reasoning。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the evidence alone","explanation":"證據本身不同於如何連結證據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the verdict","explanation":"尚未提判決勝負。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unreasoned opinion","explanation":"有證據連結，不是沒有理由的看法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"several supporting points","explanation":"points 是可數論點，與不是在數點的線索相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The coach said the argument in the draft was weak because its conclusion did not follow from the evidence, although the facts themselves were correct.","zh":"教練說草稿中的論證薄弱，因為結論不能從證據推出，雖然事實本身正確。","upgrade":"The coach said the reasoning in the draft was weak because its conclusion did not follow from the evidence, although the facts themselves were correct.","answer":"reasoning","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"factual accuracy","explanation":"題句明說事實正確，問題不在準確性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one supporting point","explanation":"弱點是證據與結論的連接，不是一個獨立支持點。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reasoning","explanation":"證據不能推出結論，弱的是 reasoning。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the motion","explanation":"動議是辯題，不是推理品質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"evidence itself","explanation":"事實本身正確，問題在如何用它們。"},{"letter":"F","text":"conclusion itself","explanation":"結論可能有問題，但題句具體批評的是推導關係。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"quarrel / dispute · 人際爭執不是辯論論據","zh":"中文辨析： Argument 可指吵架，但來源的 arguments for/against the motion 明確指辯論理由。若題句談兩人互相叫罵才用 quarrel。","point":"A debate can contain arguments without any quarrel."},{"word":"opinion / assertion · 看法未必附理由","zh":"中文辨析： 「我不同意」只是立場；一項 argument 至少應給出支持或反對的理由。只有題句確實停留於主觀感受，才用 opinion。","point":"A claim becomes an argument when a reason is offered."},{"word":"evidence / example · 證據材料不是整個論點","zh":"中文辨析： 一個統計數字或個案可支持論點，卻仍需說明它如何支持提案。若題句只問資料來源，evidence 才對。","point":"Evidence supports a reasoned point; it is not the point itself."},{"word":"reasoning as a plural count noun · 可數性陷阱","zh":"中文辨析： 來源是 arguments（可數複數）；reasoning 通常不可數，不能不改句法就寫 three reasonings。要改成 the team’s reasoning 或 several lines of reasoning。","point":"Countable arguments require a grammatical recast into uncountable reasoning."},{"word":"counterargument / rebuttal · 反方論據與反駁動作不同","zh":"中文辨析： Argument against the motion 是反方的一項理由；counterargument 專指針對先前論點的反論；rebuttal 更強調駁斥。不是所有反方理由都在直接回應另一方。","point":"An opposing argument need not rebut a specific earlier point."},{"word":"result / conclusion · 理由與結論不同","zh":"中文辨析： 「成本會上升」可作反對理由；最後投票結果或最終結論不是提出理由的過程。若談辯論後決定才可說 conclusion。","point":"Arguments support a conclusion; they are not the vote or outcome."}],"moduleNumber":27},{"id":"lesson-028","sourceId":31,"headword":"adult","title":"Adult","titleZh":"成年人","subtitle":"成年人","description":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 1.1〈Life on HK$4 a Day an Eye-opener for Hong Kong Students〉寫道：“The high school students, accompanied by 20 adults, each paid HK$5000 for the trip”。Adults 是可數名詞複數，指與高中生同行的成年人士；原文沒有指明二十人全部是教師、家長或法定監護人，也沒有評價他們是否處事成熟。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 1.1〈Life on HK$4 a Day an Eye-opener for Hong Kong Students〉寫道：“The high school students, accompanied by 20 adults, each paid HK$5000 for the trip”。Adults 是可數名詞複數，指與高中生同行的成年人士；原文沒有指明二十人全部是教師、家長或法定監護人，也沒有評價他們是否處事成熟。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["grown-up","可教的口語近義名詞","Twenty grown-ups accompanied the students 保留年齡組別，但口語色彩比新聞稿的 adults 強。"],["mature person","在此不是年齡同義詞","Mature 通常評價判斷力或行為；成熟的學生仍可未成年，成年人也可能不成熟。"],["person of legal age","在此不宜替換","法定年齡須有某項法律行為及司法地區作參照；原文只作學生與成年同行者的區分。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","核心問題","本文可否使用？"],"rows":[["adult(s)","是否屬成年年齡組別？","原文的中性說法。"],["grown-up(s)","是否以口語稱呼大人？","可在非正式轉述中使用。"],["mature person","此人行為是否成熟？","不能單憑成年推定。"],["person of legal age","此人是否達某項法律行為的門檻？","原文無此法律問題。"],["teacher / parent / guardian","此人有甚麼角色？","須另有身分證據。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 先分清年齡、性格、法律資格及隊伍角色。原文只確認成年同行者；口語可說 grown-ups，不要自行增添其職務或性格。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Grown-up","meaning":"大人（較口語）","note":"作可數名詞時指成年人，常見於孩子、家庭或非正式敘述的語境。用 grown-ups 可重述旅行隊伍裏的成年同行者，但正式報道以 adults 較中性。","collocations":"a grown-up; ask a grown-up; three grown-ups and ten children; grown-ups accompanying a school group.","example":"A grown-up from our group waited with the children while the coach arrived.","exampleZh":"我們隊伍的一位大人陪孩子等候旅遊巴到來。","contrast":"Grown-up 命名年齡組別，沒有承諾那人是教師或監護人；mature 評價性格，elderly 指年紀較大的老人，都不能由 adult 自動推得。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"When the bus was delayed, an adult from our school group stayed with the younger pupils.","zh":"旅遊巴延誤時，我們學校隊伍的一位成年人留下來陪較年幼的學生。","upgrade":"When the bus was delayed, a grown-up from our school group stayed with the younger pupils.","answer":"grown-up","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"mature person","explanation":"延誤時留下陪學生是一次行動，不能由此把同行者的整體性格評為「成熟」。"},{"letter":"B","text":"legal guardian","explanation":"句子只說此人屬學校隊伍，沒有說他對這些學生有法定監護權。"},{"letter":"C","text":"grown-up","explanation":"與較年幼學生形成自然對照，口語地指一位成年同行者。"},{"letter":"D","text":"elderly passenger","explanation":"此人可能只是年輕成年人，句中沒有高齡資訊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"teacher","explanation":"學校隊伍亦可有家長或其他職員，不能把身分收窄為教師。"},{"letter":"F","text":"teenager","explanation":"青少年不一定成年，也不保留原句所標明的年齡類別。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At dinner, the child said that one adult and twelve pupils had travelled together.","zh":"晚飯時，孩子說有一位成年人和十二名學生一起出行。","upgrade":"At dinner, the child said that one grown-up and twelve pupils had travelled together.","answer":"grown-up","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"senior citizen","explanation":"這個說法特指長者，原句沒有交代同行者已到高齡。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parent","explanation":"這位成年同行者的親子關係未知；孩子未說他是家長。"},{"letter":"C","text":"legal adult","explanation":"雖可描述法定成年身分，但孩子只是口語對比大人和學生，法律門檻在此多餘。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mature person","explanation":"此人是否處事成熟無從得知，不能以個性評價代替年齡分類。"},{"letter":"E","text":"grown-up","explanation":"配合孩子在餐桌上的說法，準確保留「一位大人」與學生的對照。"},{"letter":"F","text":"instructor","explanation":"他可能帶隊，但句子沒有說此人負責教學或指導。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"成熟不等於成年 · Mature person","zh":"「成熟」是處事或判斷的評語，不是年齡類別。原文只知道二十人是 adults，不能聲稱他們全都 mature people。若另有證據說某位學生很穩重，a mature student 可成立，即使他尚未成年。English contrast: Mature describes conduct; adult classifies age.","point":""},{"word":"法律資格須有具體門檻 · Person of legal age / minor","zh":"Of legal age 要說清楚是有資格做甚麼，也可能因地區而異；原文沒有談簽約、投票或飲酒的法定年齡。Minor 是法律上的未成年人，亦不能拿來指二十位同行大人。English contrast: Legal capacity is a specific status, not the passage's broad school-trip category.","point":""},{"word":"同行角色不可憑空指定 · Teacher / parent / guardian","zh":"二十位成年人可能擔任不同角色；原文沒有逐一列出。把 adults 改為 teachers、parents 或 guardians 會增加未獲支持的身分主張。若另有資料證明其中某人是教師，才可專稱該人為 teacher。English contrast: A role can be held by an adult, but it is not the definition of adult.","point":""},{"word":"年齡程度與詞形 · Elderly / grown-up adjective","zh":"Elderly 通常指長者；成年人可以只有二十多歲。Grown-up 亦可作形容詞，如 a grown-up decision，但本課要替換的是可數名詞，二十人應寫 twenty grown-ups。English contrast: Elderly narrows the age range; the noun and adjective uses of grown-up need different grammar.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":28},{"id":"lesson-029","sourceId":70,"headword":"animal","title":"Animal","titleZh":"瀕危動物的保育語境","subtitle":"瀕危動物的保育語境","description":"來源核對： 2012 DSE Paper 4，5.2 Part B 問考生是否願意為保護 endangered animals 的機構工作，並問投放於拯救 endangered animals 的資源是否過多。來源實際用的是複數 animals；檔名的 animal 只是單數詞條形式。Part A 討論受威脅的海豚，但沒有把 animal 放進已核對的句子。這裏指面臨滅絕風險、受保育的非人類動物；不能由詞條擴成所有生命或寵物。[2012 Paper 4 set 5.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。以下題句均為原創。","sourceSense":"來源核對： 2012 DSE Paper 4，5.2 Part B 問考生是否願意為保護 endangered animals 的機構工作，並問投放於拯救 endangered animals 的資源是否過多。來源實際用的是複數 animals；檔名的 animal 只是單數詞條形式。Part A 討論受威脅的海豚，但沒有把 animal 放進已核對的句子。這裏指面臨滅絕風險、受保育的非人類動物；不能由詞條擴成所有生命或寵物。[2012 Paper 4 set 5.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。以下題句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["creature / creatures","可用","單數/複數要跟原句配合；原文是複數 endangered animals，練習用 creatures。"],["living being / living beings","太廣","可包括人，也可能涵蓋其他生命；只在強調道德地位而非保育分類時可另作改寫，故不當成本來源的直接同義詞。"],["wildlife","條件可用","集合不可數名詞；可說 protect endangered wildlife，但不可說 a wildlife。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： Endangered species 是談防止某些物種滅絕時的主要保育表達，但 species 是類別，可包括植物，不能在逐隻救援句中任意替換 animals。Fauna 是一地動物群的較技術性集合詞，適用於地區保育報告；不用來數一隻海豚。Marine life 可包括海洋植物或微生物，只有改成專指海洋生物時才用，非原題對全部瀕危動物的直接替換。Creatures 與 living creatures 高度重疊；後者強調有生命但可能變廣，故不重複設題。Wild animals 保留原 headword，不能作真正同義替換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Creatures 可指幾隻具體動物；wildlife 是野生動物的不可數集合詞。\n- Endangered species 着眼避免物種滅絕；fauna 是地區動物群的正式詞。\n- 原文為 endangered animals，不能無條件換成更廣的 living beings、organisms 或植物群。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"creatures","meaning":"動物；活生生的個體","note":"指幾隻具體的非人類動物、特別想突顯其生命與脆弱時用；原文複數 animals 應用複數 creatures。","collocations":"endangered creatures; sea creatures; protect these creatures","example":"The rescue centre cared for three endangered creatures after the storm.","exampleZh":"風暴過後，救援中心照顧了三隻瀕危動物。","contrast":"creature 也可指虛構怪物；需有保育或物種情境。談一整個棲地的動物群則 wildlife 更自然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The rescue centre treated three endangered animals after the storm: two turtles and a dolphin.","zh":"風暴過後，救援中心醫治了三隻瀕危動物：兩隻海龜與一條海豚。","upgrade":"The rescue centre treated three endangered creatures after the storm: two turtles and a dolphin.","answer":"creatures","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"species","explanation":"species 指物種類別，三隻被治療的是具體動物個體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"wildlife","explanation":"wildlife 是不可數集合詞，不可直接接 three。"},{"letter":"C","text":"creatures","explanation":"三隻具體海龜和海豚可稱 endangered creatures，保留個體與複數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fauna","explanation":"fauna 是地區動物群，不能數三隻個體。"},{"letter":"E","text":"organisms","explanation":"organisms 包括更多生命類別，沒有保留此處特指動物。"},{"letter":"F","text":"populations","explanation":"populations 是群體，不是三隻被治療的個體。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Volunteers found two endangered animals trapped in abandoned fishing nets and carried each one to safety.","zh":"義工發現兩隻瀕危動物被棄置的漁網困住，於是逐隻把牠們帶到安全地方。","upgrade":"Volunteers found two endangered creatures trapped in abandoned fishing nets and carried each one to safety.","answer":"creatures","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"wildlife","explanation":"wildlife 不可數，不能直接說 two wildlife 並逐隻搬走。"},{"letter":"B","text":"creatures","explanation":"兩隻被困並逐隻救出的動物，creatures 保留個體與數量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"animal species","explanation":"species 指種類，不是兩隻被搬走的動物。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fauna","explanation":"fauna 是動物群，非兩隻個體。"},{"letter":"E","text":"habitats","explanation":"habitats 是棲地，不會被逐隻從漁網救出。"},{"letter":"F","text":"marine life","explanation":"marine life 是集合性海洋生命，不能直接接 two。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"wildlife","meaning":"野生動物的集合稱呼","note":"談一片棲地或保育機構所保護的野生動物整體時用；不可數，通常配 protect, conserve, endangered。","collocations":"protect endangered wildlife; conserve local wildlife; wildlife in the reserve","example":"The charity works to protect endangered wildlife in coastal waters.","exampleZh":"這間慈善機構致力保護沿岸水域的瀕危野生動物。","contrast":"wildlife 是集合詞，不能說 three wildlife 或 a wildlife；也不包含家養寵物。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisation protects endangered animals throughout the coastal reserve, from seabirds to dolphins.","zh":"該機構保護沿岸保護區內的瀕危動物，包括海鳥與海豚。","upgrade":"The organisation protects endangered wildlife throughout the coastal reserve, from seabirds to dolphins.","answer":"wildlife","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"pets","explanation":"pets 指家養寵物，海鳥海豚是野生動物。"},{"letter":"B","text":"livestock","explanation":"livestock 是畜養牲口，與沿岸野生鳥類及海豚不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fauna","explanation":"fauna 可指地區動物群，但未直接保留 endangered 的保育對象；若用需說 threatened fauna。"},{"letter":"D","text":"wildlife","explanation":"整片保護區內的海鳥及海豚是野生動物整體，endangered wildlife 自然。"},{"letter":"E","text":"species","explanation":"species 指物種類別，也可能包含植物；句中重點是保護區野生動物。"},{"letter":"F","text":"organisms","explanation":"organisms 包含植物與微生物，範圍過廣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The coastal charity runs patrols to keep endangered animals safe from illegal hunting and harmful fishing gear.","zh":"沿岸慈善機構巡邏，防止瀕危動物受到非法捕獵及有害漁具傷害。","upgrade":"The coastal charity runs patrols to keep endangered wildlife safe from illegal hunting and harmful fishing gear.","answer":"wildlife","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"wildlife","explanation":"巡邏防捕獵及漁具傷害，endangered wildlife 合野生動物整體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"domestic animals","explanation":"domestic animals 是家養動物，不符非法捕獵的野生保育語境。"},{"letter":"C","text":"flora","explanation":"flora 是植物群，不能代替被捕獵的動物。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animal species","explanation":"animal species 說物種類別，這裏巡邏保護受威脅的野生個體。"},{"letter":"E","text":"marine organisms","explanation":"marine organisms 範圍包括非動物生命，且題句未限全在海裏。"},{"letter":"F","text":"fauna","explanation":"fauna 為生態報告中地區動物群；沒有地區限定或 threatened 修飾，不能直接替換 endangered animals。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"endangered species","meaning":"瀕危物種；從物種類別着眼","note":"當重點是避免一種或多種動物滅絕、資助物種保育計劃時，整個 endangered animals 可重寫為 endangered species。","collocations":"save endangered species; protect a species from extinction; conservation of species","example":"The fund supports projects that prevent endangered species from disappearing.","exampleZh":"該基金支持防止瀕危物種消失的計劃。","contrast":"species 是物種種類，不等於被救的個別動物；也可包含植物，因此上下文須已限定動物保育。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The charity funds breeding programmes for endangered animals so their kinds will not disappear forever.","zh":"慈善機構資助瀕危動物的繁殖計劃，使這些動物種類不致永遠消失。","upgrade":"The charity funds breeding programmes for endangered species so their kinds will not disappear forever.","answer":"endangered species","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"injured creatures","explanation":"injured 指受傷，但原句說瀕危與物種存續，未說受傷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"endangered species","explanation":"繁殖計劃要防止動物種類滅絕，endangered species 準確指物種層面。"},{"letter":"C","text":"wildlife","explanation":"wildlife 指野生動物整體，未保留特定瀕危物種不消失的焦點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"individual animals","explanation":"individual animals 是個體，the kinds will not disappear 明說物種。"},{"letter":"E","text":"local fauna","explanation":"local fauna 是某地動物群，句中沒有特定地區。"},{"letter":"F","text":"living beings","explanation":"living beings 範圍過廣，且不標示瀕危物種。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The committee allocated grants to protect endangered animals, assessing each species’ risk of extinction before approving a project.","zh":"委員會撥款保護瀕危動物，批准計劃前先評估各物種的滅絕風險。","upgrade":"The committee allocated grants to protect endangered species, assessing each species’ risk of extinction before approving a project.","answer":"endangered species","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"endangered species","explanation":"每個物種的滅絕風險決定資助，endangered species 保留類別層面。"},{"letter":"B","text":"three injured animals","explanation":"三隻受傷動物是個體救援，與逐個物種評估滅絕風險不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"all living beings","explanation":"all living beings 包含人及其他生命，範圍失控。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fauna","explanation":"fauna 是一地動物群，沒有精確指出各瀕危物種。"},{"letter":"E","text":"domestic pets","explanation":"domestic pets 不符滅絕風險的野生保育。"},{"letter":"F","text":"marine creatures","explanation":"marine creatures 限海洋且未指瀕危，原句無海洋限定。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"fauna","meaning":"一個地區的動物群；技術用語","note":"在生態報告中指某地所有動物或當地受威脅的動物類群，與 flora（植物群）成對；不是日常逐隻數動物的詞。","collocations":"local fauna; threatened fauna; coastal fauna and flora","example":"The survey documented threatened fauna in the coastal reserve.","exampleZh":"調查記錄了沿岸保護區內受威脅的動物群。","contrast":"fauna 較正式、集合性；一隻受傷海豚應說 a creature / an animal，不說 a fauna。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The ecological report lists the endangered animals of the reserve, including its rare mammals, birds and reptiles.","zh":"生態報告列出保護區的瀕危動物，包括當地罕見的哺乳類、鳥類和爬行類。","upgrade":"The ecological report lists the endangered fauna of the reserve, including its rare mammals, birds and reptiles.","answer":"fauna","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"flora","explanation":"flora 是植物群，不是哺乳類、鳥類及爬行類。"},{"letter":"B","text":"individual creatures","explanation":"individual creatures 指單隻個體，報告列的是地區動物群。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fauna","explanation":"在生態報告裏，一地的哺乳類、鳥類及爬行類可統稱 endangered fauna。"},{"letter":"D","text":"livestock","explanation":"livestock 是畜牧牲口，與保護區野生動物群不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"human residents","explanation":"human residents 是人類居民，不是列出的動物類別。"},{"letter":"F","text":"marine life","explanation":"marine life 只限海洋，句中有陸生哺乳類、鳥類和爬行類。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The island survey records endangered animals alongside its rare plants, keeping the two sections separate.","zh":"島嶼調查分別記錄瀕危動物和稀有植物，把兩類資料分開。","upgrade":"The island survey records endangered fauna alongside its rare plants, keeping the two sections separate.","answer":"fauna","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"creatures","explanation":"creatures 可指動物個體，但調查將一地動物與植物群分列，fauna 更合專業分類。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fauna","explanation":"動物群與植物群分開記錄，endangered fauna 是正式的地區動物群稱呼。"},{"letter":"C","text":"flora","explanation":"flora 是植物群，會與旁邊已列的 rare plants 重複而失去動物類別。"},{"letter":"D","text":"organisms","explanation":"organisms 包括動物和植物，不能保留兩欄分界。"},{"letter":"E","text":"wildlife","explanation":"wildlife 也可能指野生動物，但調查與植物群對列的技術搭配更自然是 fauna/flora。"},{"letter":"F","text":"species","explanation":"species 可同時指動物和植物物種，未保留兩欄的動物專指。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"living beings · 生命範圍太廣","zh":"中文辨析： 人在日常保育對比中也是 living beings，植物也有生命；用它代替題目專指的瀕危動物會放寬範圍。","point":"Living beings does not isolate threatened non-human animals."},{"word":"species / individual animals · 類別與個體有別","zh":"中文辨析： 拯救一隻受傷海豚，是救個體；防止海豚物種滅絕，才是 species-level 工作。句子有明確數量或個體時不可隨便換 species。","point":"A species is a category, not one rescued animal."},{"word":"wildlife / pet / livestock · 野生、家養及畜養動物","zh":"中文辨析： 野生動物可稱 wildlife；家養狗貓和畜牧牛羊仍是 animals，但不自動屬 wildlife。","point":"Wildlife is a narrower wild-animal subset."},{"word":"fauna / flora · 動物群與植物群","zh":"中文辨析： fauna 是動物群，flora 是植物群；兩字常並列，不能因都屬生態詞而互換。","point":"Fauna means animals; flora means plants."},{"word":"animal / human / organism · 日常保育用法與生物學範圍","zh":"中文辨析： 生物學上人類屬動物界，但題目問保護瀕危動物的機構，通常指非人類動物。organism 範圍更大，可含微生物。","point":"Use the source conversation’s practical animal category, not every living organism."}],"moduleNumber":29},{"id":"lesson-030","sourceId":63,"headword":"amazing","title":"Amazing","titleZh":"令人驚嘆的公益傳播","subtitle":"令人驚嘆的公益傳播","description":"原文： 2017 DSE Paper 4，2.2 的冰桶挑戰文章引述慈善機構代表：「It is certainly amazing to see how far and wide the campaign continues to spread, increasing both awareness and funds.」這裏的 amazing 是評價「活動傳播之廣和成效」的形容詞，帶正面驚歎；不表示網上影片好笑，也不是專指冰水的刺激。It is amazing to see... 這個句型可把評價對象放在 to see 後。以下例句和練習均屬原創。[2017 Paper 4 set 2.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2017-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2017 DSE Paper 4，2.2 的冰桶挑戰文章引述慈善機構代表：「It is certainly amazing to see how far and wide the campaign continues to spread, increasing both awareness and funds.」這裏的 amazing 是評價「活動傳播之廣和成效」的形容詞，帶正面驚歎；不表示網上影片好笑，也不是專指冰水的刺激。It is amazing to see... 這個句型可把評價對象放在 to see 後。以下例句和練習均屬原創。[2017 Paper 4 set 2.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2017-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["astonishing","直接但較強","活動的擴散幅度大到出乎預期時合用；不要在平凡成果上濫用。"],["remarkable","直接","成效值得注意、非同尋常；不必有強烈的瞬間震驚。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： Impressive 着重可量度的成果值得讚賞；extraordinary 用於明確超出一般水平的規模；inspiring 用於成果激勵別人行動，需有激勵線索。Phenomenal 可讚嘆異常傑出的正面成績；incredible 是常用的較口語熱烈讚歎；staggering 適合令人難以消化的大數字。三者在指南分別教其範圍。Astounding 與 astonishing 在此幾乎同義而無新的常見構式，故不另設兩題；striking 指特別顯眼，對公益擴散與捐款整體成效較弱，與 remarkable 的「值得注意」部分重疊。wonderful/fantastic 只說正面，容易漏掉原文的擴散幅度；surprising 可正可負，若只說預期落差而無讚賞，仍未完整表達原引語。Miraculous 暗示奇蹟，原文沒有超自然或不可能發生的意思。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Remarkable ＝值得記錄的顯著成果；astonishing ＝遠超預期的強烈驚訝。\n- Impressive 讚賞努力帶來的成績；extraordinary 須有一般或歷年水平作比較。\n- Inspiring 要看到別人受到鼓舞、願意行動。Amusing 只說好笑，shocking 可能轉成負面；兩者都不能無條件替代原引語的正面公益驚歎。\n- Phenomenal 強調正面非凡成就；incredible 可作可靠數據下的口語熱烈讚歎；staggering 特別搭配大得令人震驚的具體數字。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"remarkable","meaning":"值得注意的；非同尋常的","note":"當活動擴散或效果顯著到值得特別報道，可用 remarkable；比 astonishing 少一層強烈意外。","collocations":"remarkable reach; remarkable progress; remarkable fundraising result","example":"The student campaign achieved remarkable reach across several districts.","exampleZh":"這項學生發起的活動在多個地區取得了值得注意的傳播效果。","contrast":"Remarkable 說成果顯著；inspiring 則說它鼓舞其他人，需見後續行動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"It was amazing to see the small charity appeal reach every school in the district over the term; the organiser called this a result worth recording.","zh":"看到這項小型慈善呼籲在一學期內傳到區內每所學校，令人讚歎；主辦者認為這成果值得記錄。","upgrade":"It was remarkable to see the small charity appeal reach every school in the district over the term; the organiser called this a result worth recording.","answer":"remarkable to see","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"remarkable to see","explanation":"區內每校都接觸到、主辦者特別記錄這項成果，remarkable 突出值得注意。"},{"letter":"B","text":"astonishing to see","explanation":"astonishing 強調難以預料的震驚；此處說一學期逐步擴散，沒有一夜暴增。"},{"letter":"C","text":"impressive to see","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞成績，但「值得記錄」更直接指顯著、非同尋常。"},{"letter":"D","text":"inspiring to see","explanation":"inspiring 要交代有人因此展開行動；本句未提後續參與。"},{"letter":"E","text":"surprising to see","explanation":"surprising 只說意外，未必含主辦者對成果的正面評價。"},{"letter":"F","text":"amusing to see","explanation":"amusing 只說好笑，與傳到每所學校的成效不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After six months of steady work, the charity reported amazing growth in awareness and donations: both figures had risen every month, a rare combination it highlighted in its annual report.","zh":"持續工作六個月後，慈善機構公布認知度與捐款額有令人讚歎的增長：兩項數字每月都上升，這種少見的共同增長獲年報特別指出。","upgrade":"After six months of steady work, the charity reported remarkable growth in awareness and donations: both figures had risen every month, a rare combination it highlighted in its annual report.","answer":"remarkable growth","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"astonishing growth","explanation":"astonishing 需有劇烈超預期的數字，句中是穩定逐月上升。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impressive growth","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞表現，但年報特別指出的是兩項指標同時逐月增長這種少見現象。"},{"letter":"C","text":"remarkable growth","explanation":"兩項指標共同逐月增長而且屬少見情況、獲年報點名，remarkable 表值得注意最貼切。"},{"letter":"D","text":"extraordinary growth","explanation":"extraordinary 通常更強調超乎通常水平，句中只說少見並無極端幅度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"inspiring growth","explanation":"inspiring 需有人受這些數字鼓舞而行動，句中未提。"},{"letter":"F","text":"routine growth","explanation":"rare combination 且獲年報特別指出，routine 過弱。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"astonishing","meaning":"令人十分驚訝的","note":"傳播速度或數字遠超合理預期時用；強調觀看結果時的大出意料，語氣比 remarkable 強。","collocations":"astonishing spread; astonishing number of donors; astonishing growth","example":"It was astonishing to see the video reach ten schools overnight after organisers had invited only one.","exampleZh":"主辦者原本只邀請了一所學校，影片卻在一夜之間傳到十所學校，令人十分驚訝。","contrast":"Astonishing 需有明確的意外程度；impressive 可只因成果出色而成立。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisers invited one class, but clips reached a hundred schools overnight; they called that amazing spread impossible to predict.","zh":"主辦者只邀請了一個班，影片卻一夜傳到一百所學校；他們說這種擴散令人極為驚訝，事前無法預測。","upgrade":"The organisers invited one class, but clips reached a hundred schools overnight; they called that astonishing spread impossible to predict.","answer":"astonishing spread","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"impressive spread","explanation":"impressive 可稱讚觸及範圍，但「一班到一百校一夜間」更突出強烈意外。"},{"letter":"B","text":"astonishing spread","explanation":"一夜間遠超邀請規模，astonishing 說出不可預測的強烈落差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"remarkable spread","explanation":"remarkable 也說值得注意，但題句強調 impossible to predict 的震驚。"},{"letter":"D","text":"extraordinary spread","explanation":"extraordinary 說異於常態，但沒有過往活動數據可比較。"},{"letter":"E","text":"inspiring spread","explanation":"inspiring 需後續有人受激勵行動，本句只報傳播速度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ordinary spread","explanation":"一夜到一百校不是 ordinary。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The charity expected fifty responses, yet received five thousand; the chairperson said the amazing response had exceeded every forecast.","zh":"慈善機構預期收到五十個回應，結果卻有五千個；主席說這令人震驚的反應超出所有預測。","upgrade":"The charity expected fifty responses, yet received five thousand; the chairperson said the astonishing response had exceeded every forecast.","answer":"astonishing response","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"impressive response","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞五千人回應，但未直接說五十的預測被遠遠超過。"},{"letter":"B","text":"remarkable response","explanation":"remarkable 指值得注意，強度不及一百倍的預期落差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"astonishing response","explanation":"五十對五千的巨大差距，astonishing 最能表達超出所有預測。"},{"letter":"D","text":"inspiring response","explanation":"inspiring 要說有人因這些回應而採取新行動，題句沒有。"},{"letter":"E","text":"extraordinary response","explanation":"extraordinary 可說超常，但句中最鮮明的是預測錯得很遠，而非歷年基準。"},{"letter":"F","text":"routine response","explanation":"routine 與超出所有預測的五千人矛盾。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"impressive","meaning":"成果令人佩服的","note":"聚焦參與人數、募款或宣傳成績的品質或規模，表示值得讚賞；未必原先不相信會成功。","collocations":"impressive results; an impressive total; impressive fundraising effort","example":"The charity reported an impressive total after volunteers worked steadily for months.","exampleZh":"義工持續工作多個月後，慈善機構公布了令人佩服的募款總額。","contrast":"Impressive 評價成績；astonishing 特別指出超出預期。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After a year of careful planning, the volunteers produced an amazing fundraising total, which the charity praised as a strong achievement.","zh":"經過一年周詳計劃，義工籌得令人佩服的總額；慈善機構讚揚這是出色成績。","upgrade":"After a year of careful planning, the volunteers produced an impressive fundraising total, which the charity praised as a strong achievement.","answer":"an impressive fundraising total","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an astonishing fundraising total","explanation":"astonishing 強調預測落空；題句只交代一年計劃帶來好成績。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an impressive fundraising total","explanation":"一年努力後取得受讚賞的總額，impressive 強調成果品質。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an extraordinary fundraising total","explanation":"extraordinary 需和一般募款額比較，本句未給基準。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an inspiring fundraising total","explanation":"inspiring 重視激勵他人；機構是在表揚義工的既有成果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a remarkable fundraising total","explanation":"remarkable 亦可稱值得留意，但年報具體稱讚 strong achievement，impressive 更直接。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an uncertain fundraising total","explanation":"uncertain 與已公布總額矛盾。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The campaign achieved amazing reach through careful school partnerships, and the annual report praised the team’s effective work.","zh":"活動透過細心建立學校合作關係，取得令人佩服的觸及範圍；年報讚揚團隊工作卓有成效。","upgrade":"The campaign achieved impressive reach through careful school partnerships, and the annual report praised the team’s effective work.","answer":"impressive reach","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"astonishing reach","explanation":"astonishing 需有出乎預料的落差，句中顯示有計劃的學校合作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impressive reach","explanation":"年報讚揚有計劃取得的宣傳成果，impressive 最貼近。"},{"letter":"C","text":"remarkable reach","explanation":"remarkable 也可說值得留意，但此句的焦點是團隊有效工作的可佩成果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"extraordinary reach","explanation":"extraordinary 需與一般觸及範圍比較，句中未給基線。"},{"letter":"E","text":"inspiring reach","explanation":"inspiring 需有別人因此參與或捐助的線索，句中沒有。"},{"letter":"F","text":"doubtful reach","explanation":"doubtful 暗示成果可信度不足，年報卻稱讚團隊。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"extraordinary","meaning":"超乎尋常的","note":"有同類活動的通常範圍作比較，而成果明顯超出時用；比 remarkable 更明確說不普通。","collocations":"extraordinary scale; extraordinary response; extraordinary level of support","example":"An extraordinary number of schools joined the campaign compared with earlier local appeals.","exampleZh":"與過往本地募款呼籲相比，參與這次活動的學校數目超乎尋常。","contrast":"Extraordinary 需要「一般水平」可比較；inspiring 著重別人受到鼓舞，而不是統計異常。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"This year’s appeal reached eighty schools; previous annual appeals had never reached more than ten, so the organisers called the amazing response a new kind of success.","zh":"今年的募款呼籲傳到八十所學校；以往每年的活動從未超過十所，主辦者因此稱這次令人讚歎的回應是不同尋常的成功。","upgrade":"This year’s appeal reached eighty schools; previous annual appeals had never reached more than ten, so the organisers called the extraordinary response a new kind of success.","answer":"extraordinary response","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"impressive response","explanation":"impressive 表值得讚賞，但過往上限十校與今年八十校的明確差距更支持 extraordinary。"},{"letter":"B","text":"extraordinary response","explanation":"過往最高十校，今年八十校，extraordinary 直接表示超乎常態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"rapid response","explanation":"只知今年觸及八十校，沒有交代傳播速度；rapid 不能表達與歷年上限的異常差距。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enthusiastic response","explanation":"八十校參與並不直接交代各校的熱情程度；題句給的是規模比較。"},{"letter":"E","text":"remarkable response","explanation":"remarkable 也可說值得注意，但不如 extraordinary 明確對照常規。"},{"letter":"F","text":"routine response","explanation":"routine 與打破歷年上限的參與規模矛盾。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Teams of volunteers kept the appeal running for three days in shifts; earlier events had lasted only two hours, so the organisers called the effort amazing.","zh":"義工團隊輪班讓募款活動持續了三天；以往活動只維持兩小時，因此主辦者稱這番努力超乎尋常。","upgrade":"Teams of volunteers kept the appeal running for three days in shifts; earlier events had lasted only two hours, so the organisers called the effort extraordinary.","answer":"extraordinary","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"impressive","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞義工努力，但三天對兩小時的基準讓 extraordinary 更明確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"extraordinary","explanation":"輪班三天相對以前兩小時，extraordinary 精確說超出慣常長度。"},{"letter":"C","text":"astonishing","explanation":"astonishing 強調主辦者被驚嚇或震驚的程度，本句主軸是歷次活動的時間比較。"},{"letter":"D","text":"inspiring","explanation":"inspiring 需要有人因此受到鼓勵並行動，題句沒有交代。"},{"letter":"E","text":"remarkable","explanation":"remarkable 說值得留意，但未如 extraordinary 清楚說明遠超過往長度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ordinary","explanation":"ordinary 與三天相比以往兩小時的明顯差距相反。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"inspiring","meaning":"鼓舞人心的","note":"活動的廣泛參與與公益效果鼓勵旁觀者也參與或捐助時合用；它說的是他人反應，不只是數字驚人。","collocations":"an inspiring campaign; an inspiring response; inspiring people to donate","example":"The students found the campaign inspiring and organised a second collection for the charity.","exampleZh":"學生覺得這項活動鼓舞人心，於是為慈善機構籌辦第二次募捐。","contrast":"Inspiring 需有受激勵的人的行動或心志；amazing 可以只有驚歎，未必引發行動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The students found it amazing that a tiny school appeal had helped patients, and they immediately planned their own fundraiser.","zh":"學生得知一所小學校的募款活動幫到病人，覺得鼓舞人心，並立即計劃自己的募款活動。","upgrade":"The students found it inspiring that a tiny school appeal had helped patients, and they immediately planned their own fundraiser.","answer":"inspiring","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"remarkable","explanation":"remarkable 可說公益成果值得注意，未點出學生隨即效法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impressive","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞小校成果，但不是本題最重要的後續行動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"astonishing","explanation":"astonishing 強調驚訝；學生計劃募款顯示受激勵。"},{"letter":"D","text":"inspiring","explanation":"學生立即計劃自己的募款活動，inspiring 準確說明鼓舞作用。"},{"letter":"E","text":"extraordinary","explanation":"extraordinary 需和其他學校活動作常規比較，題句沒有。"},{"letter":"F","text":"surprising","explanation":"surprising 可說原先沒想到小校幫到病人，但未點出行動。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"It was amazing to hear that former donors had returned as volunteers because the campaign had given them hope.","zh":"得知昔日捐款者因活動給他們希望而回來當義工，令人鼓舞。","upgrade":"It was inspiring to hear that former donors had returned as volunteers because the campaign had given them hope.","answer":"inspiring to hear","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"inspiring to hear","explanation":"活動給予希望，昔日捐款者因此回來當義工，inspiring 捕捉激勵作用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impressive to hear","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞回流，但未明說希望促使人再參與。"},{"letter":"C","text":"remarkable to hear","explanation":"remarkable 指值得注意，卻沒有突出希望與回歸的因果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"astonishing to hear","explanation":"astonishing 偏強烈意外；題句主要說鼓舞人心。"},{"letter":"E","text":"surprising to hear","explanation":"surprising 只說沒預期，未保留公益故事的正面推動力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"amusing to hear","explanation":"amusing 指好笑，與捐款者轉為義工不合。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"phenomenal","meaning":"非凡卓越的；成果極出色","note":"宣傳或募款成果異常傑出、明確超越一般成功時可用；在公益成效中通常帶強烈正面評價。","collocations":"phenomenal success; phenomenal growth; a phenomenal response","example":"The volunteer drive enjoyed phenomenal success, collecting five times its target.","exampleZh":"義工招募活動取得非凡成功，招募人數達目標的五倍。","contrast":"Phenomenal 特別讚賞卓越成果；extraordinary 只說超常，未必正面。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The charity called its online drive amazing: it raised five times its target and reached communities that earlier campaigns had missed.","zh":"慈善機構稱網上活動成果非凡：募款達目標五倍，也接觸到過往活動未能接觸的社群。","upgrade":"The charity called its online drive phenomenal: it raised five times its target and reached communities that earlier campaigns had missed.","answer":"phenomenal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"extraordinary","explanation":"extraordinary 表超常，但句中同時強調募款與觸及新社群的卓越正面成果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"remarkable","explanation":"remarkable 可說值得記錄，卻不如 phenomenal 充分評價達目標五倍的成功。"},{"letter":"C","text":"phenomenal","explanation":"五倍募款兼拓展新社群，phenomenal 最能讚嘆多面向的非凡成功。"},{"letter":"D","text":"astonishing","explanation":"astonishing 重在意外程度，題句重在成果品質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"impressive","explanation":"impressive 可佩，但雙重突破與五倍目標令 phenomenal 更充分。"},{"letter":"F","text":"inspiring","explanation":"inspiring 需說有人因此受鼓舞行動，題句只報已取得成果。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The organisers described the campaign as amazing when 98 percent of pupils kept attending its weekly awareness sessions for the entire term, turning a one-day drive into lasting engagement.","zh":"原本只打算舉行一天的活動，結果百分之九十八的學生整個學期每週都出席認知教育活動；主辦者稱這種持續參與成績非凡。","upgrade":"The organisers described the campaign as phenomenal when 98 percent of pupils kept attending its weekly awareness sessions for the entire term, turning a one-day drive into lasting engagement.","answer":"phenomenal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"routine","explanation":"原本只有一天，卻有百分之九十八學生連續一學期參與，並非例行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"promising","explanation":"promising 只說前景可能好，題句已有完整學期的卓越實績。"},{"letter":"C","text":"astonishing","explanation":"astonishing 主要說預期落差；句中更重視極高而持久的正面參與成效。"},{"letter":"D","text":"phenomenal","explanation":"近乎全體持續一學期，且把一天活動轉成長期教育，phenomenal 強調非凡正面成功。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interesting","explanation":"interesting 表有趣，未能評價近乎全體長期參與。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impressive","explanation":"impressive 可稱可佩，但百分之九十八且持續一學期的雙重卓越程度以 phenomenal 更充分。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"incredible","meaning":"令人難以置信的；口語熱烈讚歎","note":"數字或成效有可靠根據，但大得令人難以相信時可在較親切、感嘆的語氣用；不是指數據虛假。","collocations":"incredible reach; incredible support; an incredible result","example":"The verified report showed incredible support for the small charity.","exampleZh":"核實後的報告顯示，這間小型慈善機構獲得令人難以置信的支持。","contrast":"Incredible 可是口語稱讚，亦可在別處指難以相信其真確性；正式年報通常以 remarkable/impressive 較穩妥。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After checking the platform data twice, the students exclaimed that the charity’s amazing reach extended to supporters in thirty countries.","zh":"學生兩次核對平台數據後，驚歎這間慈善機構的活動竟觸及三十個國家的支持者。","upgrade":"After checking the platform data twice, the students exclaimed that the charity’s incredible reach extended to supporters in thirty countries.","answer":"incredible reach","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"incredible reach","explanation":"數據兩次核實，學生仍以口語熱烈驚歎觸及三十國；incredible 非指造假。"},{"letter":"B","text":"astonishing reach","explanation":"astonishing 也可表意外，但 exclaimed 的熱烈口語評價更自然用 incredible。"},{"letter":"C","text":"impressive reach","explanation":"impressive 偏年報式的成果評價，不及現場感嘆的語氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"remarkable reach","explanation":"remarkable 較克制，未傳達學生的驚歎。"},{"letter":"E","text":"phenomenal reach","explanation":"phenomenal 讚卓越成功，但此句主線是三十國數據核實後仍令人難以相信。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unverified reach","explanation":"資料已核對兩次，unverified 與事實相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A former patient came to the school to confirm that its small online appeal had paid for the wheelchair she now used every day. “What an amazing result for one student project!” a volunteer exclaimed.","zh":"一名前病人到學校證實，學校的小型網上募款活動資助了她現在每天使用的輪椅。一名義工驚歎：「一個學生計劃竟有如此了不起的成果！」","upgrade":"A former patient came to the school to confirm that its small online appeal had paid for the wheelchair she now used every day. “What an incredible result for one student project!” a volunteer exclaimed.","answer":"an incredible result","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an admirable result","explanation":"admirable 可讚賞善行，但未呈現義工對小計劃產生具體幫助的熱烈驚歎。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a remarkable result","explanation":"remarkable 較克制，與義工感嘆語氣相比不夠熱烈。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an implausible result","explanation":"病人親自證實輪椅正在使用，implausible 不應質疑成果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a routine result","explanation":"已對病人生活產生具體改變，不是 routine。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an incredible result","explanation":"病人親自確認成果，義工仍興奮驚歎小計劃的效果，incredible 是可信而熱烈的口語稱讚。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an astonishing result","explanation":"astonishing 偏強調出乎意料，也可近義，但此處 “What an ...!” 的親切讚賞語氣以 incredible 更自然。"}]}]},{"order":8,"word":"staggering","meaning":"數字大得令人震驚的","note":"多與捐款總額、參與人數等具體大數字連用，表示大到令觀察者一時難以消化；不宜籠統修飾任何愉快活動。","collocations":"a staggering number of donors; a staggering amount; staggering figures","example":"The appeal received a staggering 80,000 donations in one weekend.","exampleZh":"這項募款呼籲在一個週末就收到驚人的八萬筆捐款。","contrast":"Staggering 特別搭配巨大數量；inspiring 說引發希望或行動，不能單憑數字大推斷。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The appeal recorded an amazing 80,000 separate donations in a single weekend, far beyond what its staff could process at once.","zh":"這項募款活動一個週末便收到驚人的八萬筆捐款，遠超員工能同時處理的數量。","upgrade":"The appeal recorded a staggering 80,000 separate donations in a single weekend, far beyond what its staff could process at once.","answer":"a staggering 80,000 separate donations","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a remarkable 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"remarkable 表值得注意，未突出員工一時無法處理的巨大數量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a staggering 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"八萬筆在一週末湧入並超出處理能力，staggering 最切合大數字。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an impressive 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"impressive 可讚賞募款，但未明說數量大得壓倒處理能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an incredible 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"incredible 可口語驚歎，但 staggering 專門與驚人的數量搭配。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an extraordinary 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"extraordinary 表超常，卻沒有 staggering 對龐大數字的具體力度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an inspiring 80,000 separate donations","explanation":"inspiring 要有受激勵的人和行動，筆數本身不足以證明。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The published accounts showed an amazing HK$12 million raised in two days, a figure the treasurer had to read twice.","zh":"公布的帳目顯示兩天籌得驚人的一千二百萬港元；司庫要看兩遍才確信數字。","upgrade":"The published accounts showed a staggering HK$12 million raised in two days, a figure the treasurer had to read twice.","answer":"a staggering HK$12 million","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an impressive HK$12 million","explanation":"impressive 可佩，但司庫看兩遍的重點是金額大得難以消化。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a remarkable HK$12 million","explanation":"remarkable 可說值得注意，未如 staggering 直接修飾驚人金額。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a staggering HK$12 million","explanation":"兩天籌得一千二百萬，司庫要看兩遍，staggering 最貼切。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an incredible HK$12 million","explanation":"incredible 可作口語讚歎，但這裏用已公布帳目描述大額數字，staggering 更精確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an extraordinary HK$12 million","explanation":"extraordinary 說超常，沒有明確比較往年基準。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an inspiring HK$12 million","explanation":"inspiring 需有因此被鼓舞的人的反應；司庫重看是震驚而非發起行動。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"amusing / entertaining · 好笑不等於成效驚人","zh":"中文辨析： 把冰水淋在頭上可能令觀眾發笑，但原引語評價的是傳播、認知與募款。Amusing 只表示有趣好笑，無法替代成果上的 amazing。","point":"A funny clip is not necessarily a remarkably effective campaign."},{"word":"beautiful / wonderful / fantastic · 泛泛稱讚少了焦點","zh":"中文辨析： 這些詞可作主觀讚賞，但未指出擴散之廣或成果之大。若只說活動「很棒」，讀者未必明白原文為何驚嘆。","point":"Praise alone may omit the scale and outcome being praised."},{"word":"surprising / shocking · 驚訝不必有正面讚賞","zh":"中文辨析： Surprising 可中性；shocking 甚至常指壞消息。原文代表對提升關注及籌款感到正面驚嘆。若活動以負面方式爆紅，兩詞可能合用，但不可無條件替換。","point":"A surprising result can be good or bad; this quotation admires the campaign."},{"word":"miraculous / unbelievable · 奇蹟與不可信過強","zh":"中文辨析： 文章有社交網絡傳播的實際機制，沒有說不可能發生。Miraculous 暗示奇蹟而過強；unbelievable 可是熱烈稱讚，但若在報告中說數字「不可信」，會引出真偽問題。","point":"Unexpected success need not be a miracle or implausible claim."},{"word":"amazing / amazed · 事物性質與人的感受","zh":"中文辨析： 活動的擴散 is amazing，看到的人 are amazed。不可寫 the campaign is amazed，除非擬人化；也不可把 It is amazing to see... 改成 It is amazed to see...。","point":"The spread is amazing; an observer is amazed."}],"moduleNumber":30},{"id":"lesson-031","sourceId":69,"headword":"angry","title":"Angry","titleZh":"合作受阻時的怒氣","subtitle":"合作受阻時的怒氣","description":"原文： 2013 DSE Paper 4，8.2 討論合作中的情緒陷阱：「We get angry and frustrated, falling into something which experts call an ‘emotional trap’ that prevents us from achieving success when working together.」這裏是人真正感到生氣，並與 frustrated 並列；原句沒有說怒氣有多強、是否因不公，或是否持續很久。以下五種替換均需原創練習中的額外線索。不可把 0068 公仔的印刷怒容套到人際情緒。[2013 Paper 4 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2013-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2013 DSE Paper 4，8.2 討論合作中的情緒陷阱：「We get angry and frustrated, falling into something which experts call an ‘emotional trap’ that prevents us from achieving success when working together.」這裏是人真正感到生氣，並與 frustrated 並列；原句沒有說怒氣有多強、是否因不公，或是否持續很久。以下五種替換均需原創練習中的額外線索。不可把 0068 公仔的印刷怒容套到人際情緒。[2013 Paper 4 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2013-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["furious","條件可用","暴怒，需激烈反應；原句只說 angry，不能自動升級。"],["irate","條件可用","惱怒，常見於因投訴、失約或受不公平對待；較正式。"],["annoyed","條件可用","較輕的生氣，可能把妨礙合作的怒氣說得太淡。"]],"note":"遺漏挑戰： Exasperated 結合憤怒與屢次受阻的厭煩，對原文 angry and frustrated 特別值得教，但不能用在單一突發事件。Indignant 指針對不公或失禮的義憤，須有道德評判線索。Irritated 與 annoyed 的輕度惱火高度重疊；cross 為常見英式口語亦大致落在此層，不重複設兩組相似題。Incensed / enraged 與 furious 的強烈怒意重疊，除非語體或激發原因是教點，這一來源不另設配額。Resentful 帶久積怨懟，與一時合作受阻不同；upset 可是傷心或憂慮。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Annoyed 通常較輕；exasperated 有屢次受阻的惱怒。\n- Indignant 源於不公；irate 常見正式投訴語境；furious 是極強怒意。\n- 原文的 angry and frustrated 只給一般情緒，不容自動增加強度、理由或持續時間。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"annoyed","meaning":"輕度生氣；有點煩","note":"組員的小干擾使人不快但仍能平靜對話時用；比 angry 通常溫和。","collocations":"annoyed by interruptions; annoyed with a teammate; slightly annoyed","example":"Mina was annoyed when the group kept starting late.","exampleZh":"小組一再遲開始，令美娜有點生氣。","contrast":"怒到大吼、摔門便不只是 annoyed；原文未交代程度，所以不能一律弱化。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Lena felt angry when her group started the meeting ten minutes late, but she calmly asked them to begin.","zh":"小組會議遲了十分鐘開始，蓮娜有點生氣，但她平靜地請大家開始。","upgrade":"Lena felt annoyed when her group started the meeting ten minutes late, but she calmly asked them to begin.","answer":"annoyed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 是暴怒，十分鐘延誤後仍平靜發言不支持。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"十分鐘延誤令人不快，仍可平靜發言，annoyed 合輕度惱火。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 指長期積怨，這是即時小插曲。"},{"letter":"D","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 要有不公或侮辱，遲到本身未構成。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 可指行程受阻，但題句要改寫的是她短暫的怒氣，annoyed 更精確。"},{"letter":"F","text":"exasperated","explanation":"exasperated 暗示同類延誤反覆令人受夠；題句只說這次遲了十分鐘。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Tom was angry when a teammate interrupted him once, then smiled as she apologised and let him finish.","zh":"隊友打斷湯姆一次，他有點生氣；她道歉讓他說完後，他便笑了。","upgrade":"Tom was annoyed when a teammate interrupted him once, then smiled as she apologised and let him finish.","answer":"annoyed","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 指因不公而憤慨，這是一次打斷且已道歉。"},{"letter":"B","text":"exasperated","explanation":"exasperated 通常受反覆問題磨光耐性，一次打斷不足以支持。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annoyed","explanation":"短暫受打斷，對方道歉即消氣，annoyed 強度最合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 是暴怒，立即微笑不支持。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 含長期介意，句中很快釋懷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 可以是難過或受驚，未精確表達被打斷後短暫的輕度怒氣。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"exasperated","meaning":"屢次受阻而又氣又煩","note":"同一問題一再出現，耐性逐漸耗盡，怒氣和挫折交織時用。","collocations":"exasperated by repeated delays; feel exasperated with someone; an exasperated reply","example":"After the third cancelled meeting, both partners were exasperated.","exampleZh":"第三次會議取消後，兩名合作夥伴都又氣又煩。","contrast":"frustrated 可只有受阻而未生氣；exasperated 通常加入受夠了的惱怒。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After her teammates cancelled the fourth planning session, Mei felt angry and fed up with trying to reschedule.","zh":"隊友第四次取消籌劃會議後，美怡既生氣又厭倦了重新安排時間。","upgrade":"After her teammates cancelled the fourth planning session, Mei felt exasperated and fed up with trying to reschedule.","answer":"exasperated","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"exasperated","explanation":"第四次取消令她氣憤又厭倦，exasperated 正是反覆受阻而惱怒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"merely disappointed","explanation":"disappointed 有失望，但 merely 刪去怒氣與受夠之感。"},{"letter":"C","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 要有不公理由，取消多次突出的是耐性耗盡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 只說不快，沒有交代第四次取消造成的怒氣與耐性耗盡。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hostile","explanation":"hostile 是對人懷敵意的態度，嘗試重新安排至受夠不表示她敵視組員。"},{"letter":"F","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 表暴怒，不如 exasperated 精確表又氣又煩。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The team felt angry after the fifth round of conflicting instructions; they sighed and said they could not keep revising the poster forever.","zh":"收到第五輪相互矛盾的指示後，小組既生氣又無奈；他們嘆氣說不可能永遠修改海報。","upgrade":"The team felt exasperated after the fifth round of conflicting instructions; they sighed and said they could not keep revising the poster forever.","answer":"exasperated","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 強調受到不公平冒犯；此處核心是反覆矛盾指示使人受夠。"},{"letter":"B","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 強調暴怒，不如 exasperated 包含嘆氣及無盡修改的疲憊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"exasperated","explanation":"第五輪矛盾指示造成怒氣及疲憊，exasperated 最精確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irritated","explanation":"irritated 可表示惱火，但不足以表達第五輪矛盾指示造成的受夠及疲憊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 偏長期積怨，題句着眼第五輪修改當下又氣又累。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 表工作受阻，但單獨一詞不如 exasperated 同時表嘆氣、怒氣和受夠。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"indignant","meaning":"因不公或失禮而憤慨","note":"人認為自己或別人受到不公平指責、剝奪或侮辱時用；有明確的正義或權利判斷。","collocations":"indignant about unfair treatment; indignant at an accusation; an indignant response","example":"The student was indignant when the leader claimed her ideas as his own.","exampleZh":"組長把她的主意據為己有，那名學生因而憤慨。","contrast":"一般不便或噪音使人 annoyed；indignant 必須有不公、冒犯等理由。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Sara was angry when the leader presented her work as his own and denied that she had contributed anything.","zh":"組長把莎拉的作品當作自己的，並否認她有任何貢獻，令她非常生氣。","upgrade":"Sara was indignant when the leader presented her work as his own and denied that she had contributed anything.","answer":"indignant","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 可說不快，但未突出遭奪功的不公。"},{"letter":"B","text":"indignant","explanation":"組長奪取其功勞並否認貢獻，indignant 表因不公而憤慨。"},{"letter":"C","text":"exasperated","explanation":"exasperated 重在反覆受阻，這裏是一宗不公行為。"},{"letter":"D","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 可說創作目標受阻，但題句核心是組長奪功的不公。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 可指其後長久記恨，句中聚焦發現奪功時的義憤。"},{"letter":"F","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 只說不快，未指出作品被據為己有的不公平原因。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The volunteers were angry when the organiser blamed them publicly for a mistake he had made himself.","zh":"主辦人公開把自己的錯誤歸咎於義工，令義工們憤怒。","upgrade":"The volunteers were indignant when the organiser blamed them publicly for a mistake he had made himself.","answer":"indignant","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 說極強怒意，句中明確的是不公而非暴怒程度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 可長期介懷，但此處是當下遭嫁禍。"},{"letter":"C","text":"indignant","explanation":"主辦人公開嫁禍，indignant 準確指出不公造成的義憤。"},{"letter":"D","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 較輕，且未突出遭公開錯怪。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 可是合作受阻，但不能精確說明主辦人公開嫁禍所引起的義憤。"},{"letter":"F","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 太廣，可是傷心；這句明確因遭錯怪而憤慨。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"irate","meaning":"惱怒的；正式語體","note":"在投訴、失約或受差劣對待的報導中描寫明顯生氣的人；通常比 annoyed 強，但不一定失控。","collocations":"an irate parent; irate about a delay; an irate complaint","example":"An irate parent demanded an explanation after the school lost her form.","exampleZh":"學校弄失一位家長的表格後，那位惱怒的家長要求解釋。","contrast":"irate 常用於較正式敘述投訴者；單純悲傷或輕微不便不足以支持。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"An angry parent filed a written complaint after the committee repeatedly ignored her requests for a meeting.","zh":"委員會一再無視家長要求會面的請求，一位惱怒的家長於是提出書面投訴。","upgrade":"An irate parent filed a written complaint after the committee repeatedly ignored her requests for a meeting.","answer":"irate","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irate","explanation":"因請求遭一再無視而正式投訴，irate 是自然的報導用語。"},{"letter":"B","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 表受阻，卻未保留 angry 的怒氣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 是暴怒，正式提出書面投訴並未顯示失控或怒喊。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 可以是不快或擔憂，未準確標示惱怒的正式投訴者。"},{"letter":"E","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 比 irate 較輕，與一再遭無視後提出書面投訴的報導語氣不如 irate 相符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 偏長期怨懟，句中突出的形式是當前的惱怒投訴。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The report described an angry customer who demanded an explanation after staff lost her booking twice.","zh":"報告描述一位憤怒的顧客：職員兩次弄失她的預約後，她要求解釋。","upgrade":"The report described an irate customer who demanded an explanation after staff lost her booking twice.","answer":"irate","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 表較輕惱火，報告裏兩次弄失預約又正式要求解釋更合 irate。"},{"letter":"B","text":"irate","explanation":"顧客因服務失當而生氣並要求解釋，irate customer 是自然正式搭配。"},{"letter":"C","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 需突出道德上的不公；這裏是服務失誤引致的投訴。"},{"letter":"D","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 可因預約失敗而受阻，但未保留顧客因服務失當而生氣的投訴態度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"furious","explanation":"furious 表極度暴怒，報告只說要求解釋，未提供這種強度線索。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 暗示長久積怨，句中是兩次服務失誤後的當前投訴。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"furious","meaning":"暴怒；極度生氣","note":"有強烈、激烈怒意，例如被嚴重背叛後高聲斥責；普通 angry 不必然達此程度。","collocations":"furious with a teammate; furious about deception; absolutely furious","example":"The captain was furious when she discovered that the final report had been falsified.","exampleZh":"隊長發現最終報告遭篡改後暴怒。","contrast":"frustrated 只表目標受阻；furious 表極強烈怒氣。小煩惱不宜誇大。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The team leader was angry when she discovered that a member had secretly falsified their final report; she shouted and demanded an immediate correction.","zh":"隊長發現隊員秘密竄改最終報告後暴怒，高聲斥責並要求立即更正。","upgrade":"The team leader was furious when she discovered that a member had secretly falsified their final report; she shouted and demanded an immediate correction.","answer":"furious","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 過輕，秘密竄改與高聲斥責顯示極強怒意。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upset","explanation":"upset 可指不快或難過，未精確表達發現蓄意篡改後高聲斥責的暴怒。"},{"letter":"C","text":"furious","explanation":"秘密竄改加上高聲斥責，furious 最貼合極強烈怒氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"irate","explanation":"irate 也可說生氣，但常見正式投訴者語境；高聲斥責使 furious 更貼強度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"exasperated","explanation":"exasperated 指反覆受阻而受夠，這是一宗嚴重背叛。"},{"letter":"F","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 也可因欺騙而憤慨，但題句強調高聲斥責的怒氣強度。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Jai was angry when a teammate published his private messages without consent; he slammed the table and yelled at the teammate.","zh":"隊友未經同意公布阿傑的私人訊息後，阿傑暴怒，拍桌並對隊友大喊。","upgrade":"Jai was furious when a teammate published his private messages without consent; he slammed the table and yelled at the teammate.","answer":"furious","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"indignant","explanation":"indignant 可指遭侵犯權益的義憤，但拍桌怒喊突出了更強的暴怒反應。"},{"letter":"B","text":"annoyed","explanation":"annoyed 過輕，不能表達拍桌怒喊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resentful","explanation":"resentful 表積怨，這句說即時激烈反應。"},{"letter":"D","text":"furious","explanation":"私訊被公開後拍桌怒喊，furious 表達極度生氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrated","explanation":"frustrated 表受阻，未涵蓋如此激烈的怒氣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hostile","explanation":"hostile 描寫對人的敵意態度；拍桌怒喊顯示的是當下暴怒，furious 更準確保留情緒強度。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"frustrated · 受阻不等於怒","zh":"中文辨析： 原句把 angry and frustrated 並列，兩種感受相關但不一樣；有人因問題解不開感到挫敗，仍未對任何人生氣。","point":"A blocked goal can produce frustration without anger."},{"word":"upset · 不快情緒太廣","zh":"中文辨析： upset 可是傷心、擔心或受驚；若要準確保留 angry，須有怒氣線索。","point":"Upset does not specify anger."},{"word":"resentful · 長期怨懟不等於一時怒氣","zh":"中文辨析： resentful 暗示不滿積累、記在心裏；原文沒有持續時間或舊怨證據。","point":"Resentment lasts or lingers; anger can be immediate."},{"word":"aggressive / violent · 行為與情緒不同","zh":"中文辨析： 有人感到很怒卻沒有威嚇或動手；aggressive、violent 會加入原句沒有的行為或態度。","point":"Feeling anger does not establish aggression or violence."},{"word":"irritated / cross / enraged / incensed · 重疊詞與強度","zh":"中文辨析： irritated、cross 很接近輕度 annoyed；enraged、incensed 很接近強烈 furious，且 incensed 往往含遭激怒。它們可在適當句中使用，但不能無線索地替換本原文。","point":"A near synonym may still change intensity, register or cause."}],"moduleNumber":31},{"id":"lesson-032","sourceId":52,"headword":"aim","title":"Aim","titleZh":"想達到的目標","subtitle":"想達到的目標","description":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 5.3〈Teaching Money Smarts to Kids via Cartoons〉： “A new cartoon show — Cha-Ching Money Smart Kids — features a band called Cha-Ching whose aim is to teach children the basic concepts about money in a fun and engaging way.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 5.3〈Teaching Money Smarts to Kids via Cartoons〉： “A new cartoon show — Cha-Ching Money Smart Kids — features a band called Cha-Ching whose aim is to teach children the basic concepts about money in a fun and engaging way.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["goal","close","想達成的結果；the band's goal is to teach... 自然。"],["objective","close, more formal","明確列於教育計劃中的目標；比日常 aim 正式。"],["purpose","contextual","交代節目或活動為何存在，焦點由追求的成果移向設立原因；常需改成 the purpose of...。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["goal","人或團隊追求的結果，可較廣或長遠；不代表已達成。"],["objective","正式教案或計劃中明確列出的預期成果；可具體、可核對。"],["purpose","節目、工具或活動為何存在；常用 the purpose of...。"],["intention","創作者或團隊本人打算做甚麼；可尚未實行，甚至後來改變。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 想達到的結果用 goal；文件中的具體目標用 objective；回答「為甚麼設計這節目或問卷」用 purpose；突出創作者當時的打算用 intention。方法與事後結果另有名稱。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"goal","meaning":"想達到的成果","note":"指人或團隊努力追求的結果，可用於長遠且較廣的教育目標；不表示結果已發生。","collocations":"a goal of teaching children; the goal is to explain; work towards a goal","example":"The club's goal is to help members understand how to plan a weekly budget.","exampleZh":"這個學會的目標是協助會員明白如何編製每週預算。","contrast":"Goal 偏向將來想達到的結果；method 是用甚麼方式達成，不是成果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The band's aim is to help children understand how to plan their weekly spending.","zh":"樂隊的目標是協助兒童明白怎樣編排每週開支。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The band's goal is to help children understand how to plan their weekly spending.","answer":"goal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"goal","explanation":"指樂隊想令兒童達到的學習成果，沒有聲稱他們已學會。"},{"letter":"B","text":"method","explanation":"歌曲或故事才是教學方法；題句說的是希望兒童學到甚麼。"},{"letter":"C","text":"observed result","explanation":"未提供課後測試，不能把預期成果改成已觀察到的結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"requirement","explanation":"題句沒有說外界強制樂隊必須達成此項任務。"},{"letter":"E","text":"lesson theme","explanation":"金錢管理可作主題，但「明白如何編排開支」是想達到的能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"performance measure","explanation":"題句沒有測量標準或數字，只交代教育目標。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Nina's aim is to save enough for a laptop by December, so she sets aside part of her pocket money each week.","zh":"妮娜的目標是在十二月前存夠錢買手提電腦，因此每週都撥出部分零用錢。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Nina's goal is to save enough for a laptop by December, so she sets aside part of her pocket money each week.","answer":"goal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"routine","explanation":"每週撥錢是她的做法，不是十二月前想達到的成果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"goal","explanation":"買電腦所需的儲蓄額是她正努力達到的個人結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"spending limit","explanation":"最高可花多少與她希望存夠多少不是同一件事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"saving method","explanation":"每週撥出零用錢是方法，買電腦的儲蓄額才是目標。"},{"letter":"E","text":"deadline","explanation":"十二月是期限，不是她打算存夠錢這項成果本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"past achievement","explanation":"她仍在儲蓄，題句沒有說已買到電腦。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"objective","meaning":"明確列出的目標；較正式","note":"常見於教案、項目建議書或評估表，指可清楚說明的預期成果；不必每次都有數字。","collocations":"a learning objective; the objective is to compare; meet an objective","example":"One objective of the lesson is for pupils to compare two saving plans.","exampleZh":"這課其中一項教學目標，是讓學生比較兩個儲蓄計劃。","contrast":"Objective 比日常 goal 正式、通常較具體；不能把主題 money 當成學習目標，應說學生預期能做甚麼。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In the lesson plan, one aim is for each child to compare the prices of two products by the end of class.","zh":"教案列出一項目標：每名兒童在下課前都應能比較兩件產品的價格。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"In the lesson plan, one objective is for each child to compare the prices of two products by the end of class.","answer":"objective","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"topic","explanation":"「購物價格」是主題；下課前能比較兩件產品才是具體學習成果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"teaching method","explanation":"用遊戲還是歌曲教學是方法，未表示學生最後應會甚麼。"},{"letter":"C","text":"objective","explanation":"在教案中明確列出可觀察的課堂末技能，符合正式教學目標。"},{"letter":"D","text":"prior result","explanation":"學生尚未上完課，不能說這項能力是已得結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"class instruction","explanation":"指令是要求學生當下做事；這裏是預期他們課末具備的能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"assessment score","explanation":"題句沒有任何分數或量度結果。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In the funding proposal, the team's first aim is to produce four short money lessons by June.","zh":"資助計劃書列明，團隊第一項目標是在六月前製作四節簡短理財課。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"In the funding proposal, the team's first objective is to produce four short money lessons by June.","answer":"objective","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"teaching style","explanation":"趣味教學或講課形式是做法，不是六月前製作四節課的成果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"broad mission","explanation":"使命通常較長遠；這裏有明確數量及期限，更適合具體 objective。"},{"letter":"C","text":"finished outcome","explanation":"計劃書說將要製作，不是已完成四節課。"},{"letter":"D","text":"objective","explanation":"資助文件中的首項可核對、有限期的成果，符合正式目標。"},{"letter":"E","text":"source of funding","explanation":"資金來源不等於團隊打算完成的工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"subject area","explanation":"理財是課題；「四節課、六月前」說明預期產出。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"purpose","meaning":"設立的原因／用途","note":"說明某節目或工具為何存在、用來做甚麼；改寫原文時常用 the purpose of the show is to...。","collocations":"the purpose of the cartoon; serve a purpose; be made for the purpose of teaching","example":"The purpose of the cartoon is to explain saving and spending to young viewers.","exampleZh":"這部卡通的製作目的，是向年幼觀眾解釋儲蓄與消費。","contrast":"Purpose 着重活動或物件的功能；一項可量度的招生數字更適合稱為 target 或 objective。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The aim of the cartoon is to explain saving and spending to young viewers, not to advertise a bank.","zh":"這部卡通的製作目的，是向年幼觀眾解釋儲蓄與消費，而非替銀行賣廣告。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The purpose of the cartoon is to explain saving and spending to young viewers, not to advertise a bank.","answer":"purpose","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"audience","explanation":"年幼觀眾是收看對象，不是卡通為何製作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"advertising method","explanation":"題句明說不是替銀行賣廣告，不能把教育原因改成宣傳手法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"achieved result","explanation":"節目要解釋概念，不代表所有觀眾已理解。"},{"letter":"D","text":"production budget","explanation":"製作費用與節目存在的教育用途不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"purpose","explanation":"在 purpose of the cartoon 結構中，清楚交代節目的創作原因。"},{"letter":"F","text":"viewing figure","explanation":"收視人數與教學用途是兩種資料，題句未給數字。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The aim of the school survey is to discover what children already know about spending before the lessons begin.","zh":"學校問卷的用途，是在課堂開始前了解兒童對消費已有甚麼認識。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The purpose of the school survey is to discover what children already know about spending before the lessons begin.","answer":"purpose","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"response rate","explanation":"回覆率說多少人填問卷，不是問卷用來查明甚麼。"},{"letter":"B","text":"survey method","explanation":"網上或紙本收集答案是方法；題句說的是調查用途。"},{"letter":"C","text":"final finding","explanation":"尚未完成調查，不能把預期用途當成最終發現。"},{"letter":"D","text":"deadline","explanation":"上課前是時間安排，不是問卷存在的原因。"},{"letter":"E","text":"topic","explanation":"消費是調查主題；了解孩子原有認識才是具體用途。"},{"letter":"F","text":"purpose","explanation":"問卷設計來了解教學前的知識狀況，正好回答「為何做問卷」。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"intention","meaning":"本人打算達成的事；視角轉換","note":"指創作者或團隊主觀上打算做甚麼；當句子明確指出他們的計劃時，可由 aim 轉述為 intention，但不保證已實行或成功。","collocations":"the team's intention is to teach; have every intention of explaining; an intention to help","example":"The producers' intention is to introduce children to simple saving habits through stories.","exampleZh":"製作團隊打算透過故事，向兒童介紹簡單的儲蓄習慣。","contrast":"Intention 聚焦創作者心中打算；goal 聚焦想達到的結果。若句子只談工具用途而未提人的計劃，purpose 比 intention 自然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The producers' aim was to invite parents into every episode, but they later changed that plan.","zh":"製作團隊原本打算每集都邀請家長參與，但其後改變了計劃。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The producers' intention was to invite parents into every episode, but they later changed that plan.","answer":"intention","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"obligation","explanation":"題句沒有說任何人強制製作團隊每集邀請家長。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intention","explanation":"說明團隊當時打算這樣做，並容許其後改變安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"outcome","explanation":"事後結果不是最初的計劃；題句更說他們改了計劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accident","explanation":"每集邀請家長是有意安排，不是意外。"},{"letter":"E","text":"instruction","explanation":"不見有人命令團隊這樣製作節目。"},{"letter":"F","text":"prediction","explanation":"預測某事會發生，與團隊自己打算實行的事不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When asked whether the show was meant to promote bank accounts, the writers said their aim was to explain saving without selling a product.","zh":"有人問節目是否為了推銷銀行戶口；編劇回答說，他們本意是解釋儲蓄，並非出售產品。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When asked whether the show was meant to promote bank accounts, the writers said their intention was to explain saving without selling a product.","answer":"intention","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"side effect","explanation":"意外帶來的影響不是編劇明說的創作本意。"},{"letter":"B","text":"commercial result","explanation":"題句否認推銷產品，亦未報告節目帶來的商業結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intention","explanation":"由編劇本人澄清當初打算教甚麼，並排除推銷目的。"},{"letter":"D","text":"audience reaction","explanation":"觀眾怎樣回應與編劇原本的打算不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"sponsor's instruction","explanation":"未提資助者命令；說話者是編劇本人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"lesson format","explanation":"用歌曲或動畫呈現才是形式；這裏談教學本意。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Method / approach · 方法不是目標","zh":"中文辨析： 歌曲和卡通是教理財的 方法；「教孩子基本金錢概念」是希望達到的 目標。句子若問 how，method 才合適。","point":"A method is how the band teaches; its aim is what it hopes to achieve."},{"word":"Result / outcome · 真正發生的結果未必是原先目標","zh":"中文辨析： 原文說樂隊 想 教孩子，沒有數據證明孩子已學會。Result/outcome 可用於事後報告，卻不能無端把打算改成已成事實。","point":"An aim is intended; a result is observed after the activity."},{"word":"Target · 具體指標需要相應語境","zh":"中文辨析： Reach 10,000 pupils 可稱為招生或觸及人數 target；原文廣義地說教孩子基本概念，沒有數量目標。Target 在有明確數字時可能有效，但不宜機械替換此處。","point":"A target often names a specified level; the passage states a broad teaching aim."},{"word":"Hope / wish · 願望與計劃的強度","zh":"中文辨析： 希望孩子喜歡節目只是願望；樂隊已以節目教學為創作方向，aim 表示有意追求的教育成果。單用 wish 會削弱計劃性。","point":"A wish may be passive; an aim guides the activity."},{"word":"Aim 的其他詞性與搭配","zh":"中文辨析： 原文是名詞 whose aim is to teach。動詞 aim a camera at the screen 是「瞄準」；aim to teach 雖也可表意圖，但須重寫句子，不可把動詞硬塞進名詞位置。","point":"Keep noun and verb patterns distinct: the aim is to teach; the band aims to teach."}],"moduleNumber":32},{"id":"lesson-033","sourceId":17,"headword":"achieve","title":"Achieve","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2025 company statement says it is working with partners to achieve a stated animal-welfare aim. Achieve means bring a goal about successfully; work to achieve this does not say the company has already succeeded.","sourceSense":"The 2025 company statement says it is working with partners to achieve a stated animal-welfare aim. Achieve means bring a goal about successfully; work to achieve this does not say the company has already succeeded.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["accomplish","contextual: a task or mission"],["attain","contextual: a standard or level"],["reach","contextual: a target or milestone"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Meet a requirement/target、realise an ambition/vision 和常用句法改寫 succeed in doing something 均已加入指南及練習。Get 過於寬泛，obtain/receive 偏取得物件；bring about 多接結果或變化，若沒有明確受詞便不能把原文 achieve this 機械替換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["attain","正式地達到一項水平或標準，或經努力取得資格。","配標準、資格自然；不能把「正努力」誤說成已取得。"],["reach","到達目標點、里程碑或共識；較一般、常見。","Reach a target 不保證更長遠的成效持續。"],["accomplish","成功完成一項具體任務或工作；不適合直接接抽象水平。","配 task/mission 最自然；與 attain a standard 要分開。"],["fulfil","使承諾、責任或願望得以實現；英式拼法 fulfil。","重點是承諾的履行；不能由 working to 推斷已履行。"],["meet","符合既定要求、標準或目標，常用於要求被滿足的語境。","Meet a requirement 不只是有所改善；仍須滿足所列門檻。"],["realise","使願望、理想或長期目標成為現實；英式拼法 realise。","Realise a vision 強調讓願景成真；不等於只想像或提出願景。"],["succeed in","把 achieve a goal of doing X 改寫為 succeed in doing X，說明成功完成的行動。","必須接 -ing，並與原句時態及「希望」或「已成功」狀態一致。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 達到水準用 attain，抵達目標或里程碑用 reach，完成艱難任務用 accomplish，履行承諾或合約條件用 fulfil，符合最低要求用 meet，把長遠抱負變成現實用 realise。若把「達成做某事的目標」改成動作句，可用 succeed in + -ing，但要保留尚在努力或已成功的時態差別。遇到 goal 等通用受詞時多個動詞可能同樣正確，須靠搭配與上下文選擇。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"attain","meaning":"達到","note":"正式地達到一項水平、標準或地位，也可指經努力取得資格。","collocations":"attain a standard; attain a qualification; attain a high level.","example":"The sanctuary worked to attain a recognised welfare standard.","exampleZh":"保護中心努力達到獲認可的動物福利標準。","contrast":"配標準自然；不能把「正努力」誤說成已達標。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The centre hopes to achieve the required welfare standard next year.","zh":"中心希望明年達到所需的福利標準。","upgrade":"The centre hopes to attain the required welfare standard next year.","answer":"attain","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish a task 可以，卻不自然接一項福利標準。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil a promise 自然；這裏接的是 required standard。"},{"letter":"C","text":"attainment","explanation":"Attainment 是名詞，不能接在 hopes to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"attain","explanation":"Attain a standard 是自然的正式搭配；hopes to 仍表示未完成。"},{"letter":"E","text":"attainable","explanation":"Attainable 是形容詞，不是動詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"improve","explanation":"Improve the standard 是修改標準，不是達到它。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The sanctuary hopes to achieve financial independence within five years by building a steady donation base.","zh":"保護中心希望藉着建立穩定的捐款來源，在五年內實現財務獨立。","upgrade":"The sanctuary hopes to attain financial independence within five years by building a steady donation base.","answer":"attain","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish 常接任務；此處要達到的是長期財務自主狀態，accomplish financial independence 不自然。"},{"letter":"B","text":"attain","explanation":"Attain financial independence 自然表示經努力達到財務自主；hopes to 保留尚未達成的狀態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil 常接承諾或責任，不自然說 fulfil financial independence。"},{"letter":"D","text":"attainment","explanation":"Attainment 是名詞，不能在 hopes to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"approach","explanation":"Approach financial independence 只表示接近財務自主，未保留五年內實際達成的目標。"},{"letter":"F","text":"attainable","explanation":"Attainable 是形容詞，不能在 hopes to 後作主要動詞。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"reach","meaning":"達到","note":"到達目標點、里程碑或共識；較一般、常見。","collocations":"reach a target; reach a milestone; reach an agreement.","example":"The team worked to reach its fundraising target.","exampleZh":"團隊努力達到籌款目標。","contrast":"Reach a target 不保證更長遠的成效持續。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisation aims to achieve its target of rehoming fifty animals.","zh":"機構希望達到為五十隻動物安排新家的目標。","upgrade":"The organisation aims to reach its target of rehoming fifty animals.","answer":"reach","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil a promise 是自然搭配，fulfil its target 在此不如 reach its target。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish 通常接任務，與數量 target 搭配不自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"attainment","explanation":"名詞不能在 aims to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"approach","explanation":"接近五十隻的目標，不等於到達該目標。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reach","explanation":"Reach a target 精確表示到達數量目標；aims to 仍未完成。"},{"letter":"F","text":"miss","explanation":"與 aims to 的達標目的相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After several rounds of talks, the two shelters hope to achieve an agreement on sharing veterinary staff.","zh":"經過數輪商談，兩間收容所希望就共用獸醫人員達成協議。","upgrade":"After several rounds of talks, the two shelters hope to reach an agreement on sharing veterinary staff.","answer":"reach","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil a commitment 自然；兩間收容所這裏仍在商討，還沒有一項已作出的承諾要履行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish a task 自然，卻不自然接雙方正在商議的 an agreement。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reach","explanation":"Reach an agreement 是「達成協議」的自然搭配；hope to 保留尚未達成的狀態。"},{"letter":"D","text":"attainable","explanation":"形容詞不能在 hope to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"approach","explanation":"Approach an agreement 只表示協議在望，未保留希望正式達成的意思。"},{"letter":"F","text":"miss","explanation":"Miss an agreement 不是這裏「達成協議」的自然說法。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"accomplish","meaning":"完成","note":"成功完成一項具體任務或工作；不適合直接接抽象水平。","collocations":"accomplish a task; accomplish a mission.","example":"The volunteers accomplished the task of moving the rescued animals.","exampleZh":"義工完成了轉移獲救動物的任務。","contrast":"配 task/mission 最自然；與 attain a standard 要分開。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The team hopes to achieve its goal of checking every shelter by Friday.","zh":"團隊希望星期五前完成檢查每間收容所的任務。","upgrade":"The team hopes to accomplish the task of checking every shelter by Friday.","answer":"accomplish","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"attempt","explanation":"Attempt 只表示嘗試檢查，未表達希望把所有收容所查完。"},{"letter":"B","text":"pursue","explanation":"Pursue a goal 是繼續朝目標努力，未必在星期五前完成全部檢查。"},{"letter":"C","text":"postpone","explanation":"Postpone 是延期，與希望星期五前完成的方向相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accomplishment","explanation":"Accomplishment 是名詞，不能放在 hopes to 後充當動詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"abandon","explanation":"Abandon 是放棄檢查工作，與團隊希望完成相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish 可改寫為 accomplish the task of checking every shelter，突出把具體工作做完。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The volunteers worked hard to achieve their mission of placing all the rescued dogs in safe homes.","zh":"義工努力完成把所有獲救狗隻安置在安全家庭的任務。","upgrade":"The volunteers worked hard to accomplish their mission of placing all the rescued dogs in safe homes.","answer":"accomplish","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish their mission 強調完成指定工作；worked hard 不單獨保證結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"attain","explanation":"Attain a standard 自然，但 attain their mission 不自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reach","explanation":"Reach a milestone 自然；mission 不是一個進度點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accomplishment","explanation":"這是名詞，不能接在 worked hard to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"attempt","explanation":"Attempt 只說嘗試，不能表達成功完成整項安置使命。"},{"letter":"F","text":"abandon","explanation":"放棄安置使命與努力完成相反。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"fulfil","meaning":"實現／履行","note":"使承諾、責任或願望得以實現；英式拼法 fulfil。","collocations":"fulfil a promise; fulfil a commitment.","example":"The agency worked to fulfil its promise to improve animal welfare.","exampleZh":"機構努力履行改善動物福利的承諾。","contrast":"重點是承諾的履行；不能由 working to 推斷已履行。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The company says it is working to achieve the goal set out in its promise to end harmful practices.","zh":"公司稱正努力實現停止有害做法的承諾。","upgrade":"The company says it is working to fulfil its promise to end harmful practices.","answer":"fulfil","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"announce","explanation":"Announce 只把承諾公開，不能表示公司已朝停止有害做法的承諾實行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"renew","explanation":"Renew 是重申或延續承諾，未表示把所承諾的事做成。"},{"letter":"C","text":"review","explanation":"Review 是檢討承諾或做法，不等於履行停止有害做法的承諾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil its promise 可把原句 goal set out in its promise 濃縮為履行承諾；working to 保留尚未完成。"},{"letter":"E","text":"break","explanation":"Break 是違背停止有害做法的承諾，方向相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"delay","explanation":"Delay 會推遲履行，不等於努力達成承諾目標。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The partners hope to achieve full compliance with the monthly welfare-check conditions in their contract.","zh":"合作夥伴希望完全符合合約中每月檢查動物福利的條件。","upgrade":"The partners hope to fulfil the monthly welfare-check conditions in their contract.","answer":"fulfil","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"outline","explanation":"Outline 只會概述合約條件，不表示每月檢查已按條件執行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reaffirm","explanation":"Reaffirm 可重申同意條件，卻不等於符合條件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"monitor","explanation":"Monitor 是監察每月檢查進度，不是達到合約的全部要求。"},{"letter":"D","text":"delay","explanation":"Delay 會推遲檢查，與希望完全符合合約條件相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"fulfil","explanation":"Fulfil the conditions 指實際滿足合約要求；hope to 保留尚未達成的狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"break","explanation":"Break 是違反條件，與追求 full compliance 相反。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"meet","meaning":"達到／符合","note":"符合既定要求、標準或目標，常用於要求被滿足的語境。","collocations":"meet a requirement; meet a target.","example":"The new policy must meet the agreed welfare requirements.","exampleZh":"新政策必須符合已商定的動物福利要求。","contrast":"Meet a requirement 不只是有所改善；仍須滿足所列門檻。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The rescue centre hopes to achieve the minimum welfare requirement this year.","zh":"救援中心希望今年達到最低動物福利要求。","upgrade":"The rescue centre hopes to meet the minimum welfare requirement this year.","answer":"meet","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish 常接任務，不自然接 requirement。"},{"letter":"B","text":"meet","explanation":"Meet a requirement 是自然搭配，hopes to 表示尚未達到。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fulfilment","explanation":"名詞不能在 hopes to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"approach","explanation":"接近最低要求不等於符合它。"},{"letter":"E","text":"improve","explanation":"改進要求本身不等於滿足要求。"},{"letter":"F","text":"receive","explanation":"收到要求不是遵守要求。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The partners are working to achieve the agreed target for veterinary checks.","zh":"合作夥伴正努力達到商定的獸醫檢查目標。","upgrade":"The partners are working to meet the agreed target for veterinary checks.","answer":"meet","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accomplish","explanation":"Accomplish a task 可用，與 target 的搭配不如 meet。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fulfilment","explanation":"這是名詞，不能接在 working to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approach","explanation":"接近檢查目標仍未滿足目標。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reset","explanation":"重設目標不是達成它。"},{"letter":"E","text":"receive","explanation":"目標不是被動收到的物品。"},{"letter":"F","text":"meet","explanation":"Meet a target 表達達標，working to 仍是努力方向。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"realise","meaning":"實現","note":"使願望、理想或長期目標成為現實；英式拼法 realise。","collocations":"realise an ambition; realise a vision.","example":"The sanctuary hopes to realise its vision of safer animal care.","exampleZh":"保護中心希望實現更安全動物照護的願景。","contrast":"Realise a vision 強調讓願景成真；不等於只想像或提出願景。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The founders still hope to achieve their long-held ambition of opening a rescue centre.","zh":"創辦人仍希望實現創立救援中心的長久抱負。","upgrade":"The founders still hope to realise their long-held ambition of opening a rescue centre.","answer":"realise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"envision","explanation":"Envision 是想像救援中心的未來，沒有讓長久抱負成真的意思。"},{"letter":"B","text":"pursue","explanation":"Pursue an ambition 是追求抱負，未必真正開成救援中心。"},{"letter":"C","text":"realise","explanation":"Realise an ambition 表示把開設救援中心的抱負變成現實；still hope to 保留未實現狀態。"},{"letter":"D","text":"announce","explanation":"Announce 是對外公布抱負，不等於建立中心。"},{"letter":"E","text":"realisation","explanation":"Realisation 是名詞，不能在 hope to 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"imagine","explanation":"Imagine 只是想像有救援中心，沒有完成開設。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"With every animal in its care now safely housed, the charity did achieve its vision of a secure home for each one.","zh":"由於照顧的每隻動物如今都有安全住處，這家慈善機構確實實現了讓牠們各有安身之所的願景。","upgrade":"With every animal in its care now safely housed, the charity did realise its vision of a secure home for each one.","answer":"realise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"realise","explanation":"Realise its vision 表把讓每隻獲救動物有安全家園的願景變成現實；now safely housed 交代目標已達成。"},{"letter":"B","text":"envision","explanation":"Envision 是構想願景，不等於把願景實現。"},{"letter":"C","text":"pursue","explanation":"Pursue a vision 只表示朝願景努力；句子說所有動物現在已有安全居所，重點是目標已實現。"},{"letter":"D","text":"announce","explanation":"Announce 只是公布願景，不能代替實現。"},{"letter":"E","text":"realisation","explanation":"Realisation 是名詞，不能接在 did 後作動詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"revise","explanation":"Revise 是修改願景內容，不是達成救援目標。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"succeed in","meaning":"成功做到【須改句法】","note":"以 succeed in + 動名詞 說明某人成功完成甚麼事；把 achieve a goal of doing X 改寫為 succeed in doing X 時，須保留原句的目標及完成狀態。","collocations":"succeed in finding homes; succeed in meeting a target; succeed in doing what was promised.","example":"After months of careful work, the volunteers succeeded in finding homes for all the rescued animals.","exampleZh":"經過數月細心努力，義工成功為所有獲救動物找到住處。","contrast":"Succeed in 後接 -ing，不接不定式；try to 只說嘗試，不能在已完成的句子中代替成功。原文 work to achieve 仍是目標，不可擅自改為已成功。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The shelter hopes to achieve its goal of finding homes for all twelve dogs by the end of the month.","zh":"收容所希望在月底前實現為十二隻狗全數找到住處的目標。","upgrade":"The shelter hopes to succeed in finding homes for all twelve dogs by the end of the month.","answer":"succeed in","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"succeed with","explanation":"這裏要接 finding homes 這項行動；標準搭配是 succeed in + -ing，不是 succeed with finding。"},{"letter":"B","text":"success in","explanation":"Success 是名詞，不能直接接在 hopes to 後充當動詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"try to","explanation":"Try to find 只說嘗試，未保留目標是為十二隻狗全數找到住處的「成功完成」方向。"},{"letter":"D","text":"succeed in","explanation":"Hopes to succeed in finding 保留「希望達成」而非「已達成」，亦正確接動名詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"come close to","explanation":"接近替十二隻狗全部找到家，仍可能有狗未獲安置。"},{"letter":"F","text":"fail to","explanation":"失敗與收容所希望達成全部安置的方向相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Despite early doubts, the team did achieve its aim of running the shelter without outside help for its first month.","zh":"儘管起初有人懷疑，團隊確實實現了首月不靠外援營運收容所的目標。","upgrade":"Despite early doubts, the team succeeded in running the shelter without outside help for its first month.","answer":"succeeded in","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"tried to","explanation":"Tried to 只說曾嘗試，不保證首個月真的獨立營運。"},{"letter":"B","text":"came close to","explanation":"Came close to 表示幾乎做到，弱化原句 achieved 已達成的事實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"success in","explanation":"名詞 success 不能直接接在主語 the team 後當作過去式動詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"failed to","explanation":"Failed to run 與原句已獨立營運首月相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"succeeded in","explanation":"過去式 succeeded in running 同時保留已完成的時間狀態和不靠外援營運這項行動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hoped to","explanation":"Hoped to 仍只是意願，沒有保留原句「首個月已達標」。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"attempt / achieve","zh":"中文辨析： Attempt 只說嘗試；achieve 才是達成。原文 to achieve 表目的，不表示結果已出現。","point":"Purpose must not be mistaken for completed success."},{"word":"receive / achieve","zh":"中文辨析： Receive 是收到，與經努力達成目標不同。","point":"A goal is pursued, not merely delivered to someone."},{"word":"accomplish / attain","zh":"中文辨析： Accomplish 常配任務，attain 常配標準或水平；搭配不可任換。","point":"Choose by object and collocation."},{"word":"succeed in / success in / succeed to","zh":"中文辨析： Succeed in doing 是動詞片語，表示成功完成；success in doing 是名詞片語，需要別的動詞承載句子；succeed to 通常不接「完成某事」的不定式。","point":"The useful recast is succeed in + -ing, with tense matching the original sentence."},{"word":"improve / achieve","zh":"中文辨析： Improve 表示變好，未必達到既定目標。","point":"Progress is not necessarily completion."}],"moduleNumber":33},{"id":"lesson-034","sourceId":42,"headword":"afford","title":"Afford","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2024 digital-museum material asks whether a reader can't afford a trip to Paris to see the Mona Lisa. Afford concerns financial capacity to bear a travel cost. The question does not assert that a particular reader is poor, and having enough cash or available credit does not always mean a trip is affordable after essential expenses.","sourceSense":"The 2024 digital-museum material asks whether a reader can't afford a trip to Paris to see the Mona Lisa. Afford concerns financial capacity to bear a travel cost. The question does not assert that a particular reader is poor, and having enough cash or available credit does not always mean a trip is affordable after essential expenses.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["have the money for","Contextual: available uncommitted funds; having cash reserved for rent does not establish affordability."],["be able to pay for","Close in a genuinely fundable purchase, but mere ability to swipe a credit card or borrow may leave the expense unaffordable."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Cover the cost of usefully specifies paying the whole stated cost; be beyond one's budget preserves the source's negative financial boundary with a subject recast. Both are taught. Have the means to pay for is a formal variant of be able to pay for and adds no new boundary here. Have enough money for is already covered by have the money for when essential commitments have been allowed for. Pay for reports a payment, not whether it can be borne; be worth the money evaluates value rather than capacity. Other senses, such as cannot afford to waste time, are outside this travel-cost source."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["have the money for","必要開支已預留，指定款項確實可用於門票或行程。","帳戶有現金但要付租金時，不能草率說有可用旅費。"],["be able to pay for","補助、利潤或其他已確定資金讓付款可行。","只因可刷卡或借款，未必表示消費可負擔。"],["cover the cost of","問某筆款能否付清全價或未付餘額。","著重帳單數額；不自動涵蓋付款後的其他生活壓力。"],["be beyond one's budget","費用超過已知可用預算，以物品或行程作主語改寫 cannot afford。","須有預算和價格線索；不能只因個人不喜歡某行程便說超出預算。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 已扣除必要開支仍有足夠款項，用 have the money for；補助或收入使付款可行，用 be able to pay for；強調付清某張帳單，用 cover the cost of；價格超過指定預算，用 be beyond one's budget。原題 can't afford a trip 說財務負擔，worth visiting 另問行程值不值得。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"have the money for","meaning":"有款項支付","note":"手上或預算內有可用款項支付指定物品；若另有必要開支，須先扣除才可與 afford 接近。","collocations":"have the money for a ticket; not have the money for a trip; have enough money left for transport.","example":"After setting aside her rent, Mei still had the money for a museum ticket.","exampleZh":"美已預留租金，仍有錢買一張博物館門票。","contrast":"只看銀行結餘可能誤判；本片語要貼近 afford，須交代那筆錢可用於該消費。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Mei can afford the HK$100 museum ticket: after setting aside money for rent and food, she has HK$120 left in her leisure envelope.","zh":"美負擔得起一百港元的博物館門票：預留租金及伙食費後，她的消閒預算仍有一百二十港元。","upgrade":"Mei has the money for the HK$100 museum ticket: after setting aside money for rent and food, she has HK$120 left in her leisure envelope.","answer":"have the money for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"owe the money for","explanation":"句子說她尚有消閒款項，沒有說已欠門票費。"},{"letter":"B","text":"have the money for","explanation":"預留必要開支後仍有一百二十元，足以支付一百元門票；has the money for 保留可用款項。"},{"letter":"C","text":"borrow the money for","explanation":"她已有足夠消閒資金，不必在改寫中增添借貸。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be short of money for","explanation":"一百二十元多於門票的一百元，沒有款項短缺。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have paid for","explanation":"句子只說她買得起，沒有說已買票。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have a discount on","explanation":"票價已說是一百元，沒有折扣資料；折扣也不是她已有可用錢的意思。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"If the charity sale raises HK$500, could the club afford group entry passes costing HK$450 without using its equipment fund?","zh":"如果慈善義賣籌得五百港元，社團能否購買總價四百五十港元的團體入場證，而不動用器材基金？","upgrade":"If the charity sale raises HK$500, would the club have the money for group entry passes costing HK$450 without using its equipment fund?","answer":"have the money for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"have already paid for","explanation":"慈善義賣仍屬假設，社團尚未買團體入場證。"},{"letter":"B","text":"have a voucher for","explanation":"句子只說義賣可能籌款，沒有折扣券。"},{"letter":"C","text":"need to borrow money for","explanation":"假如籌得五百元，已多於四百五十元總價，無須增添借貸。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have the money for","explanation":"Would ... have the money for 保留假設條件；義賣若籌得五百元，便可用其中四百五十元買票而不動用器材款。"},{"letter":"E","text":"have to use its equipment fund for","explanation":"五百元義賣收入若到手，便足夠買票，沒有必要挪用器材基金。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be short of money for","explanation":"假設籌款目標達成，五百元並不低於四百五十元票價。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"be able to pay for","meaning":"能夠支付","note":"有辦法支付某項費用，可來自自己的收入、補助或已確定的資助；重點在付款能力。","collocations":"be able to pay for travel; unable to pay for admission; able to pay for repairs.","example":"With the approved travel grant, the pupils were able to pay for the coach to the museum.","exampleZh":"獲批旅費補助後，學生能支付前往博物館的旅遊巴費用。","contrast":"靠借貸也可能一時 able to pay，卻不一定真正負擔得起；練習會交代穩妥的資金來源。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The class could afford the coach trip because an approved school grant covered the full fare.","zh":"全班負擔得起旅遊巴行程，因為已獲批的學校補助涵蓋全部車費。","upgrade":"The class was able to pay for the coach trip because an approved school grant covered the full fare.","answer":"be able to pay for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be billed for","explanation":"收到帳單不等於有辦法支付；句中補助已提供全額資金。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be willing to pay for","explanation":"學生願不願付款與補助使行程可支付是不同問題。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be required to pay for","explanation":"學校沒有說學生必須自行付款；資助已涵蓋全費。"},{"letter":"D","text":"have borrowed to pay for","explanation":"車費由已獲批補助支付，沒有借貸。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be able to pay for","explanation":"Was able to pay for 保留過去的支付能力，已獲批全額補助提供了可靠資金來源。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be reimbursed for","explanation":"Reimbursed 指先付款後獲償還；句子只說補助覆蓋費用，沒有這種程序。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Will the café be able to afford a new ordering tablet from this month's profit without touching its wages fund?","zh":"咖啡館能否用本月利潤支付新的點餐平板電腦，又不動用薪酬基金？","upgrade":"Will the café be able to pay for a new ordering tablet from this month's profit without touching its wages fund?","answer":"be able to pay for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be required to pay for","explanation":"問題不是咖啡館有否付款義務，而是利潤夠不夠又能保留工資。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be able to pay for","explanation":"Will ... be able to pay for 保留尚待確定的付款能力，亦保留不動用薪酬基金的限制。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be invoiced for","explanation":"收到平板電腦帳單不能回答本月利潤是否足以支付。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be willing to pay for","explanation":"願意購買不代表利潤足夠，題目問財務能力。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be reimbursed for","explanation":"退款或報銷不是咖啡館利潤能否直接支付新設備的問題。"},{"letter":"F","text":"have already paid for","explanation":"問句談未來能否買，沒有說已購買平板電腦。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"cover the cost of","meaning":"支付……的全部費用","note":"手頭資金足以應付指定費用；可明說全額、剩餘部分或費用來源。","collocations":"cover the cost of a ticket; cover the full cost of transport; cover the remaining cost of repairs.","example":"The sponsor's donation covered the full cost of hiring a bus for the exhibition.","exampleZh":"贊助人的捐款支付了聘請旅遊巴前往展覽的全部費用。","contrast":"Cover the cost 聚焦一筆帳單是否能付清；afford 亦可考慮付款後對其他生活費的壓力。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The club can afford the new projector because a donor has given it exactly the full purchase price.","zh":"社團負擔得起新投影機，因為捐贈者已提供正好相等於全額售價的款項。","upgrade":"The club can cover the cost of the new projector because a donor has given it exactly the full purchase price.","answer":"cover the cost of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"estimate the cost of","explanation":"已知捐款正好等於售價，句子重點是能支付，不是估算價格。"},{"letter":"B","text":"borrow the cost of","explanation":"社團收到捐款而非貸款，不能寫成借款。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cover the cost of","explanation":"Cover the cost of 表示有款項付清整部投影機；全額捐款正好支持此說法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recover the cost of","explanation":"Recover 是事後收回已花的錢，並非現在有資金付款。"},{"letter":"E","text":"divide the cost of","explanation":"句中只有捐贈者提供全價，沒有分攤買機費用的安排。"},{"letter":"F","text":"avoid the cost of","explanation":"投影機仍須付款；捐款只是替社團負擔，不是免除售價。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the insurance payout, the museum still could not afford the restoration work that the policy excluded.","zh":"收到保險賠款後，博物館仍無力負擔保單不承保的修復工程。","upgrade":"After the insurance payout, the museum still could not cover the cost of the restoration work that the policy excluded.","answer":"cover the cost of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"recover the cost of","explanation":"Recover 指收回已付的費用；博物館這裏是尚無力支付未承保工程。"},{"letter":"B","text":"estimate the cost of","explanation":"估算工程價格不表示能支付，原句關乎保險以外的負擔。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cover the cost of","explanation":"Could not cover the cost of 保留博物館無力支付保單排除的修復工程。"},{"letter":"D","text":"halve the cost of","explanation":"保險並未承保這部分工程，也沒有說博物館可把它的價格減半。"},{"letter":"E","text":"postpone the cost of","explanation":"延後支付不能代替「目前付不起」，句子沒有延期安排。"},{"letter":"F","text":"insure the cost of","explanation":"保單明說排除這部分工程，不能把它改成已受保項目。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"be beyond one's budget","meaning":"超出預算","note":"價格高於某人或團體可用於該用途的預算；可把否定的 cannot afford 改成「該項目超出預算」。","collocations":"be beyond the family's budget; be beyond the club's budget; a trip beyond our travel budget.","example":"The overseas tour was beyond the class's travel budget even after the fare reduction.","exampleZh":"即使車費減價，海外遊學團仍超出全班的旅費預算。","contrast":"Beyond budget 明說有預算上限；若沒有價錢或可用款項線索，不應憑空加進原句。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The family cannot afford the overseas museum tour: it costs twice their entire annual travel allowance.","zh":"這家人負擔不起海外博物館之旅：費用是他們全年旅遊預算的兩倍。","upgrade":"The overseas museum tour is beyond the family's budget: it costs twice their entire annual travel allowance.","answer":"be beyond one's budget","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be included in one's budget","explanation":"列進旅遊計劃不等於有錢支付，費用仍是全年可用款項的兩倍。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be worth the cost","explanation":"旅程可能值得參加，但費用仍是全年旅遊預算的兩倍。"},{"letter":"C","text":"use up one's budget","explanation":"Use up 是把預算耗盡；旅費達兩倍預算，單是耗盡仍付不清。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be below one's budget","explanation":"旅程要兩倍全年旅費，絕非低於預算。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be beyond one's budget","explanation":"Is beyond the family's budget 把「負擔不起」改述為旅費超過全年可用預算。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be eligible for a discount","explanation":"有資格折扣不等於折扣後能支付，原句只說現價為全年旅費兩倍。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Would the class be unable to afford the longer museum visit if half its trip fund must remain for textbooks?","zh":"如果班級必須保留一半活動經費購買課本，較長的博物館參觀會否超出他們可負擔的範圍？","upgrade":"Would the longer museum visit be beyond the class's budget if half its trip fund must remain for textbooks?","answer":"be beyond one's budget","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be within one's budget","explanation":"Within 問的是可支付，與原句 be unable to afford 的「是否超額」方向相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be beyond one's budget","explanation":"Would ... be beyond 保留條件疑問：扣起買課本的經費後，較長行程會否超過可用旅費。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be included in one's budget","explanation":"事先列入計劃不等於扣起課本費後仍有足夠旅費。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be worth the cost","explanation":"是否值得延長參觀不回答可用經費是否足夠。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be partly funded by one's budget","explanation":"題目問會否超出可用預算，部分資助不足以說明能支付全程。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be eligible for a refund","explanation":"沒有已付車費或退款安排；問題是預留課本經費後的負擔能力。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"pay for / afford","zh":"中文辨析： 已付款只表示交易完成；可能靠借貸或犧牲房租，因此不能自動推論負擔得起。","point":"Someone may pay for a trip and still be unable to afford it responsibly."},{"word":"have cash / have spare money","zh":"中文辨析： 帳戶中有足夠現金不代表可用於旅遊；若要繳租或買食物，have the money for the trip 仍可能誤導。","point":"Money committed to necessities is not necessarily money available for travel."},{"word":"affordable / afford","zh":"中文辨析： Affordable 是形容詞，說價格相對可負擔；來源 afford 是動詞，接 a trip 或 to travel。","point":"Compare can afford a trip with the trip is affordable."},{"word":"can afford to miss / can afford a trip","zh":"中文辨析： Cannot afford to miss 可指錯過機會的代價無法接受，不一定是金錢；巴黎之旅明確談旅費。","point":"The trip sentence uses the financial sense, not the “cannot risk losing” sense."},{"word":"worth the money / within budget","zh":"中文辨析： 值不值得買是價值判斷；是否在預算內是支付能力。值得的旅程仍可太貴。","point":"Good value and financial capacity are separate questions."}],"moduleNumber":34},{"id":"lesson-035","sourceId":43,"headword":"affordable","title":"Affordable","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2013 article says local designers benefited from affordable space, workshops, and retail experience. Space here means premises or workspace. Affordable says the cost was manageable for the intended users; it does not give an exact rent, say the shops were free, or prove that every designer could pay.","sourceSense":"The 2013 article says local designers benefited from affordable space, workshops, and retail experience. Space here means premises or workspace. Affordable says the cost was manageable for the intended users; it does not give an exact rent, say the shops were free, or prove that every designer could pay.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["reasonably priced","Contextual: judges a rent as fair/moderate against comparable space; a fair market rent may still exceed one designer's means."],["economical","Recast: describes a cost-saving choice or arrangement, often over time; economical workspace is possible but less direct than affordable space."],["within budget","Recast: requires a named designer or project and a spending ceiling; the rent can be within their budget."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Low-cost is a common label for space offered at a low rent; inexpensive describes a low price in ordinary language. Both are taught with comparison/evidence conditions. Cheap can imply poor quality or a subjective low price; it is discussed as a trap, not treated as a neutral universal swap. Budget-friendly overlaps low-cost in a more promotional register and adds no new construction here. Cost-effective evaluates value or results per dollar, which the source does not establish. No source candidate is silently dropped."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["reasonably priced","有同類場地的價格可比較，要評租金是否公平。","合理市價不保證每名設計師都付得起。"],["economical","共租或省電等安排降低相對租金或長期營運費。","需要比較基準；較省錢仍可超出個人預算。"],["within budget","已知某人或團體的支出上限，租金或總場地費不超標。","指明誰的預算；它不等於市場定價合理或場地便宜。"],["low-cost","有低於一般租金或較低設置成本的線索，可作空間前的形容詞。","低成本不等於免費或低品質。"],["inexpensive","已有不高的實際租用價格，普通語氣說空間不昂貴。","不要只憑「某人付得起」就斷言絕對價格低。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 比同類場地價格是否公平，用 reasonably priced；比較共租、電費或設置安排是否省錢，用 economical；對照指定使用者預算，用 within budget；說租金或建立費較低，用 low-cost；有實際低價並用一般語氣描述，用 inexpensive。來源的 affordable space 本身沒有免費、低品質或確切租金的意思。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"reasonably priced","meaning":"價格合理","note":"租金與附近同類單位相比公平或適中；重點是市場比較，不直接交代某設計師的收入。","collocations":"reasonably priced studio space; a reasonably priced shop; reasonably priced compared with similar units.","example":"The cooperative found a reasonably priced studio whose rent was below that of similar units nearby.","exampleZh":"合作社找到一間租金低於附近同類單位、價格合理的工作室。","contrast":"價格合理不保證每個設計師都負擔得起；affordable 更直接看使用者能否支付。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The cooperative called the studio affordable after comparing its HK$8,000 monthly rent with HK$12,000 for similar units nearby.","zh":"合作社比較附近同類單位每月一萬二千港元的租金後，認為這間月租八千港元的工作室價格合理。","upgrade":"The cooperative called the studio reasonably priced after comparing its HK$8,000 monthly rent with HK$12,000 for similar units nearby.","answer":"reasonably priced","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"free of charge","explanation":"工作室每月收八千元，並非免費。"},{"letter":"B","text":"within every designer's budget","explanation":"句子只比較租金，沒有每位設計師的收入或預算資料。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reasonably priced","explanation":"與附近同類單位的一萬二千元比較，八千元租金可支持「價格合理」的評價。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cost-effective","explanation":"比較租金沒有量度工作室帶來多少成果或收入，不能推定成本效益。"},{"letter":"E","text":"paid for already","explanation":"報價比較不表示合作社已交租。"},{"letter":"F","text":"overpriced","explanation":"在同類單位普遍收一萬二千元時，把八千元說成定價過高與線索相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Is the gallery room affordable in market terms if an independent survey says its daily fee matches comparable venues in the district?","zh":"若獨立調查顯示這間畫廊房間的日租與區內同類場地相若，從市場角度看，它的收費是否合理？","upgrade":"Is the gallery room reasonably priced in market terms if an independent survey says its daily fee matches comparable venues in the district?","answer":"reasonably priced","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"within the poorest artist's budget","explanation":"市場收費相若不表示收入最少的藝術家能付；調查沒有個人預算資料。"},{"letter":"B","text":"free to use","explanation":"有日租便不是免費。"},{"letter":"C","text":"subsidised","explanation":"調查只說價格與同類場地相若，沒有政府或私人補助。"},{"letter":"D","text":"underpriced","explanation":"與區內同類場地同價，不足以說它明顯定價過低。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reasonably priced","explanation":"Reasonably priced in market terms 精確問租金是否符合可比場地的正常水平。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more profitable","explanation":"句子沒有畫廊的收入或盈利，不能由日租判斷獲利。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"economical","meaning":"節省成本","note":"相較其他安排，某做法在租金或長期營運費上較節省；常修飾 choice/way/arrangement，必要時改寫 affordable space 的句法。","collocations":"an economical way to rent space; an economical workspace arrangement; more economical than renting alone.","example":"Sharing one empty shop was an economical way for three designers to show their work.","exampleZh":"三名設計師共用一間空置店舖，是較節省成本的作品展示方式。","contrast":"比另一方案省錢，仍可能超出個人預算；不要把 economical 當作每間低租工作室的直接形容詞。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Sharing an affordable shop allowed three designers to pay HK$2,000 each instead of HK$6,000 each for separate units.","zh":"三名設計師共用一間較可負擔的店舖，每人只需付二千港元，不必各自租獨立單位而支付六千港元。","upgrade":"Sharing one shop was an economical arrangement for the three designers: each paid HK$2,000 instead of HK$6,000 for a separate unit.","answer":"economical","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"profitable","explanation":"每人租金降低不表示設計師的作品一定帶來盈利。"},{"letter":"B","text":"economical","explanation":"共租令每人的租金由六千元降至二千元，正好表達與獨租相比更省錢。"},{"letter":"C","text":"free","explanation":"每人仍須付二千元，不是免費使用店舖。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more spacious","explanation":"共用店舖未必比各自租單位更寬敞，句子只提供費用比較。"},{"letter":"E","text":"within every budget","explanation":"即使比獨租省錢，二千元也未必在每名設計師的預算內。"},{"letter":"F","text":"cost-neutral","explanation":"Cost-neutral 表費用沒有變化；每人租金實際下降四千元。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The designers found the workspace affordable over a full year because its LED lighting cut electricity bills, although its rent matched other units.","zh":"設計師覺得這個工作空間一整年用下來較可負擔，因為 LED 照明降低電費，雖然租金與其他單位相同。","upgrade":"The designers found the workspace economical to use over a full year because its LED lighting cut electricity bills, although its rent matched other units.","answer":"economical","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"rent-free","explanation":"租金與其他單位相同，並非免租。"},{"letter":"B","text":"overpriced","explanation":"句子未說租金高於市價，反而說節電使全年使用費較低。"},{"letter":"C","text":"subsidised","explanation":"電費降低來自 LED 照明，沒有補助金。"},{"letter":"D","text":"economical","explanation":"Economical to use 突出相同租金下較低的長期電費，與共租減租的前一題不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more profitable","explanation":"電費減少未必令設計師收入或盈利增加。"},{"letter":"F","text":"within every budget","explanation":"全年較省電不代表任何設計師都付得起該租金。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"within budget","meaning":"在預算內","note":"指租金沒有超過某人或團體已知的可用上限；改寫時通常讓 rent/cost 作主語，並說明誰的預算。","collocations":"rent within the designers' budget; keep the venue cost within budget; a studio within our budget.","example":"The shop's monthly rent was within the students' exhibition budget.","exampleZh":"這間店舖的月租在學生的展覽預算之內。","contrast":"財力雄厚的團體可把昂貴場所列入預算；within budget 不自帶市場價格低的意思。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The studio is affordable for the illustrator, who has set aside HK$3,000 a month for rent; the quoted rent is HK$2,800.","zh":"這名插畫師負擔得起工作室：她每月預留三千港元租金，而報價是二千八百港元。","upgrade":"The studio's quoted rent is within the illustrator's budget of HK$3,000 a month: it costs HK$2,800.","answer":"within budget","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reasonably priced for the whole district","explanation":"只有插畫師預算與報價，沒有區內同類單位的租金資料。"},{"letter":"B","text":"free for the illustrator","explanation":"工作室收二千八百元，不是免費。"},{"letter":"C","text":"below the landlord's costs","explanation":"句子沒有業主成本，不能推定租金低於成本。"},{"letter":"D","text":"within budget","explanation":"二千八百元未超過插畫師已列明的三千元月租上限，必須說清是 her budget。"},{"letter":"E","text":"profitable to rent","explanation":"她能付租金不表示工作室會帶來盈利。"},{"letter":"F","text":"paid for in advance","explanation":"有預算不等於已預付租金。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school made the pop-up exhibition space affordable by booking it for one day instead of three; the shorter hire fitted its approved venue allowance.","zh":"學校只租用臨時展覽空間一天而非三天，使場地費用變得可負擔；較短的租期符合已獲批的場地預算。","upgrade":"By booking it for one day instead of three, the school brought the cost of the pop-up exhibition space within its approved venue budget.","answer":"within budget","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"within budget","explanation":"租用期由三天縮成一天，費用便落在已批准的場地預算內；改寫須說明是 the school's budget。"},{"letter":"B","text":"underpriced in the market","explanation":"縮短租期令總費下降，沒有同類場地的市場價格資料。"},{"letter":"C","text":"available free of charge","explanation":"學校仍要為一天的租用付款，只是付得起。"},{"letter":"D","text":"funded by ticket sales","explanation":"句子說的是獲批場地預算，沒有售票籌款。"},{"letter":"E","text":"worth more than its fee","explanation":"租期調整解決財務上限，沒有評估展覽成果是否物有所值。"},{"letter":"F","text":"beyond the approved allowance","explanation":"較短租期已使費用符合上限，並非超額。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"low-cost","meaning":"低成本","note":"相對一般選擇，使用或租用工作空間所需費用較低；常作名詞前形容詞。","collocations":"low-cost studio space; low-cost rental units; low-cost workshops.","example":"The arts centre offered low-cost studio space to newly established designers.","exampleZh":"藝術中心向新晉設計師提供低租金的工作室空間。","contrast":"Low-cost 是相對價錢標籤；即使低於市價，某人仍可能負擔不起。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The city project offered affordable studio units at one quarter of the usual rent for similar units in the area.","zh":"市府計劃提供較可負擔的工作室單位，租金只及區內同類單位一般租金的四分之一。","upgrade":"The city project offered low-cost studio units at one quarter of the usual rent for similar units in the area.","answer":"low-cost","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"free","explanation":"單位仍收租，只是租金是一般的四分之一。"},{"letter":"B","text":"low-cost","explanation":"四分之一的同類單位租金支持把這些工作室稱作 low-cost。"},{"letter":"C","text":"low-quality","explanation":"租金低不證明工作室品質差。"},{"letter":"D","text":"high-yield","explanation":"High-yield 說回報率，不是使用者所付租金低。"},{"letter":"E","text":"market-rate","explanation":"市府單位只收一般市場租金四分之一，並非市價水平。"},{"letter":"F","text":"within every artist's budget","explanation":"低租仍可能高於某些藝術家的可用款項；句子沒有每人的預算。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The community centre turned an unused room into affordable workshop space: by reusing shelves and tables, it kept the fee charged to designers low.","zh":"社區中心重用架子和桌子，把閒置房間改成設計師負擔得起的工作坊空間，並把向設計師收取的費用保持在低水平。","upgrade":"The community centre turned an unused room into low-cost workshop space: by reusing shelves and tables, it kept the fee charged to designers low.","answer":"low-cost","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"luxury","explanation":"重用現有桌架並降低設計師費用，沒有豪華裝潢的線索。"},{"letter":"B","text":"rent-free","explanation":"收費低不等於完全免收使用費。"},{"letter":"C","text":"high-maintenance","explanation":"沒有資料說日後保養費高；重點是重用家具並壓低使用費。"},{"letter":"D","text":"profitable","explanation":"降低使用者費用不保證社區中心會盈利。"},{"letter":"E","text":"low-cost","explanation":"重用桌架後，中心把節省的成本反映在設計師付的低費用上，故可稱 low-cost workshop space。"},{"letter":"F","text":"short-lived","explanation":"是否長期使用未交代，較低使用費不表示空間很快關閉。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"inexpensive","meaning":"不昂貴","note":"普通用語，表示一項租賃或使用費不高；需要價錢或比較線索，避免把僅僅「可負擔」誇成「便宜」。","collocations":"an inexpensive studio; inexpensive short-term space; inexpensive to rent.","example":"The designers chose an inexpensive display room that cost less than the other venues they visited.","exampleZh":"設計師選了一間租金比看過的其他場地低的展示室。","contrast":"Inexpensive 說價格不高；affordable 是價格與使用者可用資金之間的關係。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The tiny display room was affordable even for the school club: it cost only HK$30 for the entire afternoon.","zh":"即使對學校社團而言，這間小展示室也負擔得起：整個下午只收三十港元。","upgrade":"The tiny display room was inexpensive even for the school club: it cost only HK$30 for the entire afternoon.","answer":"inexpensive","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"spacious","explanation":"Tiny 已說房間很小，不能改說寬敞；大小也不是本句的價錢焦點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"free","explanation":"整個下午仍收三十元。"},{"letter":"C","text":"inexpensive","explanation":"一整個下午只收三十元，支持用一般詞 inexpensive 說租用費不高。"},{"letter":"D","text":"overpriced","explanation":"三十元的低費用與定價過高相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"cost-effective","explanation":"沒有活動成果與費用的比率資料，不能單憑三十元斷言成本效益。"},{"letter":"F","text":"prepaid","explanation":"句子只列收費，沒說社團事先付款。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During an off-peak week, the pop-up shop was affordable to rent at a modest fixed fee, with no extra charge for lighting.","zh":"在淡季的一星期，這間臨時店舖以不高的固定費用出租，照明也不另收費，因此租用起來不昂貴。","upgrade":"During an off-peak week, the pop-up shop was inexpensive to rent at a modest fixed fee, with no extra charge for lighting.","answer":"inexpensive","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"inexpensive","explanation":"Inexpensive to rent 對應淡季固定費不高、照明不加價的整體租用價格；此題練形容詞接 to rent。"},{"letter":"B","text":"free to rent","explanation":"店舖仍收固定費，只是照明不加收。"},{"letter":"C","text":"expensive to maintain","explanation":"原句談租用者付的費用，沒有維修保養成本。"},{"letter":"D","text":"already rented","explanation":"租金報價不表示已有租客租下店舖。"},{"letter":"E","text":"profitable to run","explanation":"低租不保證設計師開店會有盈利。"},{"letter":"F","text":"priced above market","explanation":"沒有市場價格比較，亦無線索支持「高於市價」。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"free / affordable","zh":"中文辨析： 可負擔的空間仍可收租；來源沒有說店舖免費提供。","point":"A manageable price is not a zero price."},{"word":"cheap / reasonably priced","zh":"中文辨析： Cheap 可說價低，亦可能帶品質差的語氣；reasonably priced 只評價格公平，原來源也沒有給品質判斷。","point":"Low price, fair price, and poor quality are different claims."},{"word":"economical / affordable","zh":"中文辨析： 共租相對獨租較省錢，但共租費用仍可能超出某設計師的預算；economical 需要比較基準。","point":"A cheaper arrangement need not be financially manageable for everyone."},{"word":"cost-effective / affordable","zh":"中文辨析： Cost-effective 指花費與得到的成果相比划算；來源只說設計師負擔得起空間，未量度成果效益。","point":"Value per dollar is not the same as capacity to pay rent."},{"word":"within budget / reasonably priced","zh":"中文辨析： 在某團體的預算內，不表示市場價格合理；市場價格合理，也可能超出一名新晉設計師的預算。","point":"An individual's ceiling and a market comparison answer different questions."}],"moduleNumber":35},{"id":"lesson-036","sourceId":82,"headword":"app","title":"App","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The reproduced 2023 Paper 4 set 2.2 article says teenagers use “social networking apps such as Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and Snapchat.” The plural count noun refers to user-facing software, specifically for social networking here. It does not specify a device for each app, and the named products can also be accessed as websites or wider services. Some original exercises extend the same software sense to other kinds of app, without presenting those examples as source facts. [2023 Paper 4, set 2.2](https://www.scribd.com/document/930902882/HKDSE-2023-P4).","sourceSense":"The reproduced 2023 Paper 4 set 2.2 article says teenagers use “social networking apps such as Facebook, Twitter, Instagram and Snapchat.” The plural count noun refers to user-facing software, specifically for social networking here. It does not specify a device for each app, and the named products can also be accessed as websites or wider services. Some original exercises extend the same software sense to other kinds of app, without presenting those examples as source facts. [2023 Paper 4, set 2.2](https://www.scribd.com/document/930902882/HKDSE-2023-P4).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["application","Close when it means a software program; application form is another sense and is false here."],["mobile software","Contextual, uncountable and device-specific. It cannot directly replace plural apps; one can recast as mobile applications only where phone/tablet use is stated."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Software programs is a broader but useful countable paraphrase for installed user-facing apps and is taught with the broader scope stated. Social networking applications preserves the source function and is taught. Mobile applications is also taught conditionally for explicit phone/tablet use, not asserted of every source platform. Platform/service may name the broader network rather than the installed app; website names a browser interface. Tool is too broad without its digital function. Application form and operating system are false."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["題句線索","合適表達"],"rows":[["只需把縮寫寫全","application(s)"],["強調可安裝／運行的電腦程式，功能已有交代","software program(s)"],["必須保留社交網絡功能","social networking application(s)"],["明說手機或平板","mobile application(s)"]],"note":"勿把軟件 application 讀成申請表；也勿把安裝在裝置上的程式直接當成整個平台或網站。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"applications","meaning":"應用程式（完整寫法）","note":"App 的完整形式，在軟件語境中可數；語氣稍正式，可指手機或電腦上的使用者程式。","collocations":"download applications; social networking applications; an application on a tablet.","example":"The school installed three applications on the tablets for class discussions.","exampleZh":"學校在平板電腦安裝了三款應用程式，供課堂討論使用。","contrast":"Application 另可指申請；要有安裝、使用、裝置等線索才是軟件。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The social networking apps on the class tablets let students share project photos with their teacher.","zh":"班級平板上的社交網絡應用程式讓學生與老師分享專題照片。","upgrade":"The social networking applications on the class tablets let students share project photos with their teacher.","answer":"applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"application forms","explanation":"申請表是提交資料的文件，並非平板上供分享照片的程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accounts","explanation":"帳戶讓使用者登入，但不是安裝在平板上的程式本身。"},{"letter":"C","text":"applications","explanation":"有平板及分享功能的線索，applications 是 apps 的完整軟件名稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"web pages","explanation":"網頁可在瀏覽器開啟，但原句說的是平板上的應用程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"operating systems","explanation":"作業系統支援整部平板，非專供班級分享照片的多個社交程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"notifications","explanation":"通知是程式顯示的訊息，不是讓學生分享照片的程式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before the workshop, the teacher checked that the two apps would open on every loan tablet.","zh":"工作坊開始前，老師檢查兩款應用程式能否在每部借用的平板上開啟。","upgrade":"Before the workshop, the teacher checked that the two applications would open on every loan tablet.","answer":"applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"application forms","explanation":"表格可以填寫或提交，但原句說兩款東西能在平板上啟動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"software licences","explanation":"授權可能影響使用權，但不是老師逐一開啟檢查的兩款程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"online accounts","explanation":"登入帳戶與程式能否在每部平板啟動是不同問題。"},{"letter":"D","text":"browser bookmarks","explanation":"書籤是網頁捷徑，原句沒有說瀏覽器中的網址。"},{"letter":"E","text":"applications","explanation":"兩款可在平板開啟的使用者程式，正式寫作 applications。"},{"letter":"F","text":"system updates","explanation":"系統更新是維護過程，並非老師要用的兩款應用程式。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"software programs","meaning":"軟件程式","note":"可數的上位名稱，指提供功能的電腦程式；在已清楚說明用途時可概括 apps，但比社交應用程式寬。","collocations":"install software programs; software programs for communication; run two programs.","example":"The library tested several software programs for group messaging.","exampleZh":"圖書館測試了幾款供群組傳訊使用的軟件程式。","contrast":"所有 apps 都是程式，但 software programs 也可能包括非社交、非手機的程式；需保留用途限定。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apps for group messaging had to be installed on each school computer before the discussion.","zh":"供群組傳訊的應用程式必須在討論前安裝到每部學校電腦。","upgrade":"The software programs for group messaging had to be installed on each school computer before the discussion.","answer":"software programs","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"messaging accounts","explanation":"帳戶用於識別使用者，通常不會逐部電腦安裝。"},{"letter":"B","text":"software programs","explanation":"句子明說要安裝供傳訊的程式，software programs 在用途限定下合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"device settings","explanation":"裝置設定可調整權限，但不是供群組傳訊的多款程式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"online services","explanation":"網上服務可由程式連接，卻不等於要安裝在每部電腦的軟件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"computer files","explanation":"一般電腦檔案不會因群組傳訊用途就成為應用程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"network connections","explanation":"網絡連線是通訊條件，並非可安裝的程式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A technician compared the apps students used to edit and send short video messages on their laptops.","zh":"技術員比較學生在手提電腦上用來編輯及傳送短片訊息的應用程式。","upgrade":"A technician compared the software programs students used to edit and send short video messages on their laptops.","answer":"software programs","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"social media accounts","explanation":"帳戶是使用者身分；技術員比較的是可編輯和傳送影片的程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"internet connections","explanation":"連線速度或穩定性不是技術員比較的兩款操作工具。"},{"letter":"C","text":"video files","explanation":"影片檔是程式編輯與傳送的內容，不是工具本身。"},{"letter":"D","text":"computer brands","explanation":"品牌是電腦製造者，不能表示學生使用的多款軟件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"message archives","explanation":"訊息存檔是結果資料，不能編輯和傳送新訊息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"software programs","explanation":"句中已限定電腦上的編輯與傳訊功能，較廣的 software programs 仍保留原意。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"social networking applications","meaning":"社交網絡應用程式","note":"明確指出建立連繫、分享及互動功能的完整軟件稱呼；最能保留來源片語 social networking apps 的功能限定。","collocations":"use social networking applications; social networking applications on a device.","example":"The club chose two social networking applications to coordinate its volunteers.","exampleZh":"社團選了兩款社交網絡應用程式來協調義工。","contrast":"Networking applications 是所用程式，social networking platforms 可能指整個服務或社群，不等於裝在裝置上的程式。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The social networking apps on students’ phones let them follow classmates and exchange photos within a shared network.","zh":"學生手機上的社交網絡應用程式讓他們在同一網絡內追蹤同學並交換照片。","upgrade":"The social networking applications on students’ phones let them follow classmates and exchange photos within a shared network.","answer":"social networking applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"social networking applications","explanation":"追蹤同學和在共同網絡分享照片，正是手機上的 social networking applications。"},{"letter":"B","text":"video-editing programs","explanation":"剪片程式處理影片，不必提供追蹤同學及社群互動功能。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school portals","explanation":"學校入口網站可供登入學習資源，沒有句中社交網絡功能的保證。"},{"letter":"D","text":"messaging records","explanation":"傳訊紀錄是過往內容，不能讓學生建立網絡或互相追蹤。"},{"letter":"E","text":"online communities","explanation":"網上社群是人及互動空間，非明確裝在手機上的應用程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"device contacts","explanation":"手機聯絡人名單是資料，不是用來互相追蹤及分享的程式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the school changed its device rules, teachers discussed which social networking apps pupils could install for a supervised project.","zh":"學校修改裝置規則時，老師討論學生可安裝哪些社交網絡應用程式參與受監督的專題。","upgrade":"When the school changed its device rules, teachers discussed which social networking applications pupils could install for a supervised project.","answer":"social networking applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"social media policies","explanation":"政策是規則本身；老師討論的是可安裝哪款軟件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"school websites","explanation":"網站可能經瀏覽器使用，句子明說安裝在裝置上的程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"student accounts","explanation":"帳戶是登入身分，不是獲准安裝的應用程式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"social networking applications","explanation":"既保留社交網絡用途，又可在裝置上安裝，social networking applications 最準確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"social circles","explanation":"社交圈是人際群體，不能在裝置上安裝。"},{"letter":"F","text":"content filters","explanation":"內容過濾器是管制功能，並非學生用來社交的程式。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"mobile applications","meaning":"流動裝置應用程式","note":"專指手機或平板上運行的應用程式；只有裝置被交代時才可用，不能從來源的社交網絡用途擅自推斷全部只限手機。","collocations":"mobile applications on smartphones; download a mobile application; update mobile apps.","example":"The teacher tested the mobile applications on both phones and tablets.","exampleZh":"老師在手機和平板電腦上測試了那些流動裝置應用程式。","contrast":"Mobile 限制裝置類型；電腦版社交程式和網頁版服務不一定屬於此類。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apps were downloaded to the students’ smartphones before they took part in the photo-sharing task.","zh":"學生參與分享照片的活動前，先把應用程式下載到智能手機。","upgrade":"The mobile applications were downloaded to the students’ smartphones before they took part in the photo-sharing task.","answer":"mobile applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"desktop programs","explanation":"桌面電腦程式不符合句中明示的手機安裝情況。"},{"letter":"B","text":"online profiles","explanation":"個人檔案是在服務中的身分頁，不等於下載的應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"websites","explanation":"網站可由手機瀏覽器打開，但原句說下載到手機的程式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"phone settings","explanation":"手機設定是裝置選項，不是參與分享活動的多款程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"mobile applications","explanation":"明說下載到智能手機，mobile applications 的裝置限定得到支持。"},{"letter":"F","text":"mobile networks","explanation":"流動網絡傳送數據，並非下載到手機的應用程式。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the tablet trial, the school counted how many apps could run without an internet connection.","zh":"在平板電腦試用期間，學校點算有多少款應用程式在沒有網絡連線時仍可運作。","upgrade":"During the tablet trial, the school counted how many mobile applications could run without an internet connection.","answer":"mobile applications","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"downloaded video files","explanation":"已下載的影片檔可離線播放，但它們是程式處理的內容，不是會自行運行的應用程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"device firmware","explanation":"裝置韌體是底層控制軟件，不是學校逐款測試的使用者應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mobile applications","explanation":"平板屬流動裝置，所點算的可運行使用者程式可稱 mobile applications。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cloud services","explanation":"雲端服務透過網絡提供功能，不是平板上可離線運行的多款程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"cached web pages","explanation":"快取網頁可能離線顯示內容，但網頁本身不是安裝並運行的應用程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"backup copies","explanation":"備份副本是儲存資料或程式的複本，不是正在逐款運行的應用程式。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"application / application form","zh":"中文辨析： Application 可以是程式，也可以是申請；此處有社交網絡及裝置語境，是軟件。Application form 只會在申請入學、工作等場合成立。","point":"Software and an application form share a spelling but not a function."},{"word":"app / platform / service","zh":"中文辨析： App 是使用者開啟的程式；platform/service 可指整個網絡、帳戶與伺服器。若談安裝、更新或手機版，應優先指明程式。","point":"A service may have several apps and a website."},{"word":"mobile software / plural apps","zh":"中文辨析： Mobile software 通常不可數；apps 是可數複數。若要保留「兩款」，可說 two mobile applications，但必須有手機或平板線索。","point":"Countability and device scope both change in this recast."},{"word":"website / application","zh":"中文辨析： 網站在瀏覽器中顯示；應用程式可安裝或啟動。某服務兩者兼備，不能因品牌相同就把媒介混為一談。","point":"The same social service can be used through a website or an app."},{"word":"operating system / app","zh":"中文辨析： 作業系統管理整部裝置及其他程式；社交 app 是在其上運行的一款使用者程式。","point":"An operating system supports apps; it is not one social-networking app."}],"moduleNumber":36},{"id":"lesson-037","sourceId":51,"headword":"AI","title":"AI","titleZh":"人工智能","subtitle":"人工智能","description":"原文： 2025 年 DSE 7.3〈An unusual career that may be one of the most desired jobs of the future〉： “As artificial intelligence or ‘AI’ becomes more widely used and starts replacing some traditional jobs, many young people worry about their future careers.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 年 DSE 7.3〈An unusual career that may be one of the most desired jobs of the future〉： “As artificial intelligence or ‘AI’ becomes more widely used and starts replacing some traditional jobs, many young people worry about their future careers.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["artificial intelligence","direct / exact expansion","AI 的正式全稱；適合原句談科技普及與工作的概括用法。"],["machine intelligence","contextual, more technical","可談機器展現的推理或辨識能力；不宜在每個產品名稱中機械地替換 AI。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["artificial intelligence","AI 的準確全稱；談整體技術或研究領域時最穩妥。"],["intelligent computer systems","有實際部署、分析或建議功能的具體系統時可用；通常需按單複數改寫。"],["machine intelligence","強調機器所展現的智能或與人類能力比較時可用；不是所有 AI 產品的日常稱呼。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 展開縮寫及談廣義領域用 artificial intelligence；句子指各地實際運作的系統用 intelligent computer systems；討論機器的認知能力與界限可用 machine intelligence。固定規則的自動化、機器學習方法和實體機械各有不同範圍。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"artificial intelligence","meaning":"人工智能；準確全稱","note":"AI 的標準展開形式。作廣義領域或技術名稱時通常不用複數；正式文章首次提及可寫 artificial intelligence (AI)。","collocations":"research in artificial intelligence; use artificial intelligence; artificial intelligence tools","example":"The careers talk explored how artificial intelligence might change office work.","exampleZh":"職業講座探討人工智能可能怎樣改變辦公室工作。","contrast":"全稱不縮窄為某一種方法或產品；machine learning 只是相關技術類別，並非 AI 兩個字母的展開。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The careers report introduces AI before discussing how it may change some office jobs.","zh":"這份職業報告先介紹人工智能，然後討論它可能怎樣改變部分辦公室工作。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The careers report introduces artificial intelligence before discussing how it may change some office jobs.","answer":"artificial intelligence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"artificial intelligence","explanation":"這是 AI 的準確全稱；首次介紹時可在後面加括號列出縮寫。"},{"letter":"B","text":"augmented intelligence","explanation":"可指以技術增強人的判斷，但不是原文縮寫 AI 的標準展開形式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"artificial information","explanation":"字首相似，卻不是文中談職業影響的 AI 技術名稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"machine learning","explanation":"只是一類相關方法，不能當成職業報告中 AI 的準確全稱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"automation technology","explanation":"固定規則的自動化也可存在，且不是 AI 的全稱。"},{"letter":"F","text":"intelligent machines","explanation":"是相關的機器描述，卻非 AI 的準確展開，也會縮窄原文的領域範圍。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Her university course examines the history of AI, from early research to current applications.","zh":"她的大學課程研究人工智能的歷史，由早期研究到現今應用。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Her university course examines the history of artificial intelligence, from early research to current applications.","answer":"artificial intelligence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"intelligent machines","explanation":"可指研究對象，卻把整個領域的歷史改成各台機器的歷史。"},{"letter":"B","text":"artificial intelligence","explanation":"作研究領域名稱時，AI 的全稱自然地接在 history of 後。"},{"letter":"C","text":"automatic devices","explanation":"自動裝置可以只按固定規則運作，範圍與人工智能史不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"machine-learning models","explanation":"特定方法及模型較窄，不能概括早期至今的整個 AI 領域。"},{"letter":"E","text":"computer programming","explanation":"寫程式是更廣的活動，不限於人工智能。"},{"letter":"F","text":"digital technology","explanation":"數碼科技包含許多非 AI 工具，範圍過闊。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"intelligent computer systems","meaning":"具智能功能的電腦系統；具體系統改寫","note":"當句子說的是實際部署的電腦系統，而非整個研究領域，可用此名詞詞組說明 AI 的具體載體。複數 systems 對應多個系統；單一系統須改為 an intelligent computer system。","collocations":"deploy intelligent computer systems; intelligent computer systems that analyse data","example":"The clinic is testing intelligent computer systems that help staff sort appointment requests.","exampleZh":"診所正測試具智能功能的電腦系統，協助職員整理預約申請。","contrast":"此說法把廣義 AI 具體化為系統；若原句談「人工智能這個研究領域」，不能無故換成一批系統。普通定時器雖是電腦控制，也未必有相關智能功能。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The clinic installed AI systems that sort appointment requests and flag missing details for staff.","zh":"診所安裝了人工智能系統，用來整理預約申請，並向職員標示缺漏資料。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The clinic installed intelligent computer systems that sort appointment requests and flag missing details for staff.","answer":"intelligent computer systems","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"computer hardware","explanation":"只說實體設備，未說明這些系統能分析預約內容並標示缺漏。"},{"letter":"B","text":"rule-based booking software","explanation":"固定規則的預約程式也可整理資料；原句明說是具智能功能的 AI 系統，不能無故收窄為固定規則。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intelligent computer systems","explanation":"原句說安裝並使用具體系統處理資料；複數系統改寫自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"machine-learning research","explanation":"研究活動不是診所已安裝的服務系統。"},{"letter":"E","text":"digital records","explanation":"紀錄是被處理的資料，不是負責整理及提示的系統。"},{"letter":"F","text":"appointment clerks","explanation":"職員接收系統提示；他們不是診所安裝的 AI 系統。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The museum lets visitors ask its AI systems questions about the collection in several languages.","zh":"博物館讓參觀者以多種語言向其人工智能系統詢問展品資料。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The museum lets visitors ask its intelligent computer systems questions about the collection in several languages.","answer":"intelligent computer systems","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"AI research projects","explanation":"研究計劃可展示成果，但題句明說參觀者可直接向系統用多種語言提問。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intelligent computer systems","explanation":"具體系統可接收多語言問題並作答，與原句的互動用途吻合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fixed audio recordings","explanation":"預錄聲帶只能播放固定內容，未必能回應不同語言的即場問題。"},{"letter":"D","text":"museum guides","explanation":"導賞員也能回答問題，但原句明說參觀者使用的是 AI 系統。"},{"letter":"E","text":"printed exhibit labels","explanation":"印刷標籤不能接收參觀者的即場提問。"},{"letter":"F","text":"internet connections","explanation":"網絡可供系統傳輸資料，本身不是回答展品問題的系統。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"machine intelligence","meaning":"機器智能；能力角度","note":"較專門地談機器在辨識、推理等任務中展現的智能，尤其與 human intelligence 對照或討論其能力界限時適用。","collocations":"human and machine intelligence; the limits of machine intelligence; research into machine intelligence","example":"The lecture compared human judgement with machine intelligence in recognising patterns.","exampleZh":"講座比較人類判斷與機器智能在辨識規律方面的表現。","contrast":"它強調能力而非一件產品；machine learning 指一類方法，不能直接當作全部 machine intelligence。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The lecture compares human intelligence with AI when recognising patterns in complex images.","zh":"講座比較人類智能與人工智能辨識複雜圖像中規律的能力。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The lecture compares human intelligence with machine intelligence when recognising patterns in complex images.","answer":"machine intelligence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"machine learning","explanation":"指機器學習方法，與 human intelligence 在句中的能力類別不平行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"algorithmic analysis","explanation":"強調分析程序，未概括與人類智能比較的機器認知能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"computer programming","explanation":"指編寫程式的活動，不是系統辨識規律時展現的能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"machine intelligence","explanation":"與 human intelligence 形成平行對照，聚焦兩者辨識圖像規律的能力。"},{"letter":"E","text":"automated pattern matching","explanation":"可指具體任務或方法，卻比題句的智能能力比較狹窄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"human intelligence","explanation":"會變成把人類智能與自己比較，失去機器一方。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The panel asks about the limits of AI: can a system judge a sensitive case without understanding its human context?","zh":"座談會探討人工智能的能力界限：系統若不理解個案背後的人情脈絡，能否判斷敏感個案？\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The panel asks about the limits of machine intelligence: can a system judge a sensitive case without understanding its human context?","answer":"machine intelligence","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"human judgement","explanation":"題句問電腦系統能否判斷，換成人的判斷便失去機器能力界限這個焦點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"automated case processing","explanation":"自動處理個案可只按既定步驟，未必涉及理解人情脈絡的能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"machine learning","explanation":"特定技術方法不等於題句所問的整體機器判斷能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"decision-support software","explanation":"可指輔助人作決定的產品；題句討論的是機器智能本身能理解到甚麼程度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"machine intelligence","explanation":"題句探討機器展現的判斷與理解能力有何限制。"},{"letter":"F","text":"data access","explanation":"能取用個案資料不保證能理解其人情脈絡並作適當判斷。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Machine learning · 方法不等於整個領域","zh":"中文辨析： 機器學習是一類利用數據改進表現的方法；原句廣泛談 AI 對職業的影響，不能把整個範圍縮成一種方法。若文章具體討論模型如何從數據學習，才可用 machine learning。","point":"Machine learning is a method within the wider AI area."},{"word":"Automation · 自動執行不必有智能","zh":"中文辨析： 定時開燈可屬 automation，卻不因「自動」便成為 AI。若只有預設時間或固定規則，不能憑此替換原文的人工智能。","point":"A fixed automatic rule does not itself establish AI."},{"word":"Robot / hardware · 實體機器不等於技術概念","zh":"中文辨析： 機械臂可能用 AI，也可能只按固定程式運作；原文談的是技術普及，不限於有形機器。若句子只指一台實體裝置，robot 才是相應名詞。","point":"A robot is a physical machine; AI names the technology or capability."},{"word":"Algorithm / software · 範圍不必相同","zh":"中文辨析： 算法是一套計算步驟，軟件是程式；兩者都可能用於 AI，也可能完全不涉及 AI。原文不能一概改成 algorithm 或 software。","point":"Not every algorithm or software program performs an AI task."},{"word":"Artificial / fake · 固定術語的詞義","zh":"中文辨析： Artificial intelligence 是固定技術名稱；artificial 在這裏指由人設計，不表示「虛假的智能」可作直接英文改寫。","point":"Artificial intelligence is the established full term, not “fake intelligence.”"}],"moduleNumber":37},{"id":"lesson-038","sourceId":8,"headword":"academic","title":"Academic","titleZh":"學業能力強的","subtitle":"學業能力強的","description":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 2.1〈Apprenticeship Programmes in Switzerland〉說雙軌職業教育的學生常是成績優秀者，因此 they are no less academic than students who chose university education。這裏 academic 形容學生的學業表現／學習能力，而不是說他們一定選大學、只會讀理論，或課程「具教育性」。比較式 no less ... than 不可被改成「較差」。","sourceSense":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 2.1〈Apprenticeship Programmes in Switzerland〉說雙軌職業教育的學生常是成績優秀者，因此 they are no less academic than students who chose university education。這裏 academic 形容學生的學業表現／學習能力，而不是說他們一定選大學、只會讀理論，或課程「具教育性」。比較式 no less ... than 不可被改成「較差」。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["scholastic","須改寫搭配","Scholastic achievement/performance 可指學業成績；the students are scholastic 在此不自然。"],["educational","錯義","形容有教育作用的活動、資源或制度，不表示學生學業能力強。"],["school-related","錯義","只表示與學校有關，不表示成績或學習能力。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["原句要說甚麼","選擇"],"rows":[["一般學業能力強","academically strong"],["能應付學業要求，未證明頂尖","academically capable"],["有分數、排名或獎項證明成績優異","high-achieving"],["正式比較學業成就，容許改寫主語","scholastic achievement"]],"note":"快選規則： 先確定 academic 在源句評價的是學生學業表現。若用 scholastic，把句子改成 scholastic achievement/performance；educational 和 school-related 不表示學生「學業能力強」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Academically Strong","meaning":"學業能力強的","note":"自然形容學生學業表現或能力強；保留「選職業路線也可以學業優秀」的中心意思。","collocations":"academically strong students / applicants; be academically strong.","example":"Several academically strong pupils chose apprenticeships instead of university courses.","exampleZh":"幾名學業能力強的學生選擇了學徒訓練，而非大學課程。","contrast":"學業強不保證每門實作技能已純熟；strong 在此不是體力強。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Although they chose apprenticeships, these pupils were no less academic than their classmates applying to university; both groups had strong grades.","zh":"雖然這些學生選擇學徒訓練，他們的學業表現不遜於申請大學的同學；兩組成績都很好。","upgrade":"Although they chose apprenticeships, these pupils were academically strong, like their classmates applying to university; both groups had strong grades.","answer":"academically strong","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"educational","explanation":"Educational 形容具教育作用的資源，不直接評價學生的成績。"},{"letter":"B","text":"academically strong","explanation":"兩組成績都好，academically strong 保留不遜於大學申請者的意思。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school-related","explanation":"School-related 只說與學校有關。"},{"letter":"D","text":"academically capable","explanation":"有能力應付學業仍可能成績一般；兩組的strong grades 支持更強的 academically strong。"},{"letter":"E","text":"academically gifted","explanation":"兩組成績都好，但並未證明所有學生有特別突出的天賦；strong 評價表現更審慎。"},{"letter":"F","text":"academic materials","explanation":"Academic materials 是教材或學術資料，不是學生。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The trainee was clearly academic despite preferring workshop training: in class, she explained complex scientific ideas and evaluated the evidence without notes.","zh":"那名學徒雖然偏好工作坊訓練，學業能力仍然很強：在課堂上，她能不看筆記解釋複雜科學概念並評估證據。","upgrade":"The trainee was clearly academically strong despite preferring workshop training: in class, she explained complex scientific ideas and evaluated the evidence without notes.","answer":"academically strong","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"academically strong","explanation":"能獨立解釋複雜概念並評估證據，支持對她學業能力強的判斷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"educational","explanation":"Educational 可形容課程有教育作用，不能描述她分析科學證據的學業表現。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school-related","explanation":"她展示的是解釋與評估能力，不只是做了與學校有關的事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"academically capable","explanation":"Capable 只說能應付；能不看筆記清楚解釋複雜概念並評估證據，支持更強的 academically strong。"},{"letter":"E","text":"high-achieving","explanation":"High-achieving 通常需要已取得的成績、獎項或排名；這題只有課堂上展示的強能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scholarly","explanation":"課堂分析科學概念不等於已有研究著述；scholarly 易轉向研究者風格。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Academically Capable","meaning":"有能力應付學業的","note":"指學生能處理學習要求，即使沒有證據說成績拔尖；比 academically strong 較審慎。","collocations":"academically capable learners / applicants; be academically capable of advanced study.","example":"The tutors found the apprentices academically capable of completing the theory units.","exampleZh":"導師發現學徒有能力完成理論課單元。","contrast":"Capable 不等於已得最高分；也不意味學生非得選大學。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apprentice had the academic ability to complete the demanding theory modules, although his grades were average rather than outstanding.","zh":"那名學徒的成績屬一般而非頂尖，但仍有足夠學業能力完成難度高的理論單元。","upgrade":"The apprentice was academically capable of completing the demanding theory modules, although his grades were average rather than outstanding.","answer":"academically capable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"high-achieving","explanation":"High-achieving 暗示成績優異，與一般成績衝突。"},{"letter":"B","text":"academically capable","explanation":"能完成高要求單元但未必高分，academically capable of 精準。"},{"letter":"C","text":"academically strong","explanation":"平均成績顯示能完成理論單元，但不足推斷整體學業表現『強』。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school-related","explanation":"School-related 不說他能否完成理論課。"},{"letter":"E","text":"academically incapable","explanation":"Incapable 與能完成相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scholarly","explanation":"修讀理論單元不等於具有研究學者的風格或產出。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The tutors said the vocational students had the academic ability to study advanced mathematics, even though none had chosen a university course.","zh":"導師說那些職業教育學生有足夠學業能力讀高等數學，雖然他們沒有人選大學課程。","upgrade":"The tutors said the vocational students were academically capable of studying advanced mathematics, even though none had chosen a university course.","answer":"academically capable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"academically strong","explanation":"導師只說學生有能力讀進階數學，未給成績證明他們在學業上特別強。"},{"letter":"B","text":"academically capable","explanation":"Capable of studying 保留能力判斷，沒有虛構高分。"},{"letter":"C","text":"high-achieving in exams","explanation":"High-achieving in exams 需要考試實績，句中沒給。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school-related","explanation":"School-related 只說關聯。"},{"letter":"E","text":"scholarly publications","explanation":"Scholarly publications 是研究出版品，不是學生能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"high-achieving","explanation":"沒有提到學生取得高分或獎項；能修讀進階課程不等於已表現卓越。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"High-Achieving","meaning":"成績優異的","note":"適用於已有考試分數、排名或其他實際成果，較單純 academic 加入「成績高」的含義。","collocations":"high-achieving students / pupils / applicants; high-achieving in school.","example":"The high-achieving apprentices had been near the top of their classes before training.","exampleZh":"這些成績優異的學徒在受訓前已名列前茅。","contrast":"原文另說學徒常是 high performers，所以這個詞有根據；若只知學生有潛力，就不可說已「成績優異」。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The students had strong academic records and had placed in the top five per cent of their school before entering vocational training.","zh":"這些學生學業能力強，在進入職業訓練前成績已排在全校首百分之五。","upgrade":"The students were high-achieving and had placed in the top five per cent of their school before entering vocational training.","answer":"high-achieving","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"academically capable","explanation":"能應付學習只是門檻；全校前百分之五是已證實的優異成績。"},{"letter":"B","text":"school-related","explanation":"School-related 不表示成績高。"},{"letter":"C","text":"high-achieving","explanation":"首百分之五的已取得成績，支持 high-achieving。"},{"letter":"D","text":"scholarly","explanation":"名列前茅屬學校成績，不等於研究型或學者式表現。"},{"letter":"E","text":"academically uncertain","explanation":"Academically uncertain 與明確高排名不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"research-minded","explanation":"Research-minded 是研究興趣，不能代替成績實績。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The trainee had an excellent academic record: she had won the school mathematics prize twice and passed every theory exam with distinction.","zh":"那名學徒學業成績優異：她曾兩度獲學校數學獎，每次理論考試都取得優異成績。","upgrade":"The trainee was high-achieving: she had won the school mathematics prize twice and passed every theory exam with distinction.","answer":"high-achieving","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"high-achieving","explanation":"數學獎與優異考試成績是已證實的高表現。"},{"letter":"B","text":"academically capable","explanation":"兩次數學獎及理論試優異成績，超越單純『能應付』的層次。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school-related","explanation":"School-related 只表示與學校相關。"},{"letter":"D","text":"academic resources","explanation":"Academic resources 是學習資源，不是她的特質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"merely capable","explanation":"Merely capable 只說能應付，弱於獲獎及優異成績。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scholarly","explanation":"獲學校數學獎不必然表示從事學術研究；此處說的是高成就學生。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Scholastic Achievement","meaning":"學業成就（正式改寫）","note":"Scholastic 常修飾 achievement / performance / record；要把原本形容學生的句子改寫成描述其學業表現。","collocations":"scholastic achievement / performance / record; strong scholastic record.","example":"The apprentices’ scholastic achievement was comparable to that of university applicants.","exampleZh":"學徒的學業成就與大學申請者相若。","contrast":"不能直接寫 the students are scholastic；這是名詞片語改寫，須調整主語與比較結構。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apprentices were no less academic than the university applicants; their examination records were equally strong.","zh":"學徒的學業表現不遜於大學申請者；雙方考試紀錄同樣出色。","upgrade":"The apprentices’ scholastic achievement was no lower than that of the university applicants; their examination records were equally strong.","answer":"scholastic achievement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"academic ability","explanation":"兩組不只是有學習能力，句子以考試紀錄比較實際成就。"},{"letter":"B","text":"educational","explanation":"Educational 不直接指學生學業成就。"},{"letter":"C","text":"scholastic achievement","explanation":"以 scholastic achievement 作新主語，正式地保留雙方成績不遜的比較。"},{"letter":"D","text":"scholastic students","explanation":"Scholastic students 搭配生硬，且不能直接表示成績紀錄。"},{"letter":"E","text":"scholarly achievement","explanation":"這裏比較學校考試成績，不是學術研究成果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"academic potential","explanation":"考試紀錄比較的是已取得的成績，potential 只說尚待發揮的能力。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The annual report praised the apprentices’ academic record because their examination results were consistently excellent across several subjects.","zh":"年報讚揚學徒的學業紀錄，因為他們在多門科目的考試中一直取得優異成績。","upgrade":"The annual report praised the apprentices’ scholastic achievement because their examination results were consistently excellent across several subjects.","answer":"scholastic achievement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"scholastic students","explanation":"Scholastic students 不能自然表示年報所強調的考試成果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"scholastic achievement","explanation":"把 academic record 改成 scholastic achievement，以持續優異的多科成績說明已取得的學業成果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"academic potential","explanation":"考試已顯示實際成就，不能只改寫成尚未發揮的潛力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school-related records","explanation":"與學校有關的紀錄可能是出席等資料；這裏明說多科考試成果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"scholarly style","explanation":"年報談的是考試表現，不是學徒的研究或文章風格。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scholarly achievement","explanation":"多科考試佳績是學校學業成果，沒有證據說學徒取得研究著述成就。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"academic / educational：人與資源","zh":"Academically strong students 是學業表現強的學生；educational films 是有教育作用的影片。形容影片的詞不能直接評價學徒的學業能力。","point":"Academic here evaluates learners; educational often describes something that teaches."},{"word":"academic / school-related：能力與關聯","zh":"School-related problems 只是與學校有關，可能包括交通或膳食；不能說 school-related students 來表示成績好。","point":"School-related indicates connection, not achievement."},{"word":"scholastic：常見搭配","zh":"Scholastic achievement / aptitude / performance 可用於學業成績；把 scholastic 直接放在原文 they are no less ... 後面會十分生硬，應改寫為名詞片語。","point":"Scholastic more naturally modifies a noun such as achievement or performance."},{"word":"high-achieving / academically capable：實績與潛力","zh":"High-achieving 表示已有較好成績；academically capable 只說有能力應付學業，未必是高分學生。原文另說 high performers，故某些練習可支持較強說法。","point":"High-achieving requires demonstrated results; capable can refer to ability without top marks."},{"word":"scholarly / academic：研究者與學生","zh":"Scholarly 常說學術研究及認真做學問的態度；本文是學徒的學業表現，不是說人人已做研究。","point":"Scholarly often concerns research-oriented work, not simply strong school performance."},{"word":"no less / less：比較方向","zh":"No less academic than 說學徒不比大學生差；刪去 no 就把比較方向反轉。改寫時可說「一樣學業能力強」，不可變成「較差」。","point":"No less than preserves equality or non-inferiority; less than reverses it."}],"moduleNumber":38},{"id":"lesson-039","sourceId":92,"headword":"appropriate","title":"Appropriate","titleZh":"對學生合適","subtitle":"對學生合適","description":"The 2025 DSE set 6.3 discussion asks, “Do you think adventure trips are appropriate for students?” This is a question about fit for student participants, not a statement that all such trips are safe or unsafe. The answer may depend on age, preparation, supervision, and purpose. The adjective takes for here. All examples below are original.","sourceSense":"The 2025 DSE set 6.3 discussion asks, “Do you think adventure trips are appropriate for students?” This is a question about fit for student participants, not a statement that all such trips are safe or unsafe. The answer may depend on age, preparation, supervision, and purpose. The adjective takes for here. All examples below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["suitable","直接近義","可說 suitable for students，保留對人群是否合適的問題。"],["fitting","有條件","常說 fitting for an educational purpose / fitting response；作一般安全判斷較不自然。"],["proper","有條件","須有規範、禮儀或既定標準；可合乎規矩但仍不適合某年齡學生。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： Right for 是常用口語改寫。Well suited to 與 suitable 高度重疊，不另計一課；advisable 表是否值得建議，需權衡益處風險；acceptable 只說過最低門檻，均不自動等於適合。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["語境重點","優先表達"],"rows":[["活動與學生能力或需要相配","suitable for"],["依個人情況作日常選擇","right for"],["與教育目的或場合相稱","fitting for / a fitting choice"],["明確規則、程序或行為規範","proper"]],"note":"Appropriate for students 是開放的判斷，不能自動變成「安全、合法、值得」其中任何一項。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"suitable","meaning":"適合的","note":"最直接描述活動與某類學生的需要、年齡或能力相配；用 suitable for。","collocations":"suitable for students; suitable for beginners; suitable for a school trip","example":"The short guided walk is suitable for first-year students.","exampleZh":"這段有導賞的短途步行適合一年級學生。","contrast":"與 appropriate for students 很接近；但是否合規需另作判斷。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The low-altitude trek is appropriate for beginners because the route is short and guides can adjust the pace.","zh":"這條低海拔步行路線適合初學者，因為路程短，導師亦可調整速度。","upgrade":"The low-altitude trek is suitable for beginners because the route is short and guides can adjust the pace.","answer":"suitable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"suitable","explanation":"路線短而可調整，整體配合初學者能力，suitable 最完整。"},{"letter":"B","text":"safe","explanation":"導師及短路線可能提高安全性，但 safe 只評危險程度，沒有概括能力與安排的配合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"advisable","explanation":"advisable 問是否值得推薦，句中只給出匹配初學者的條件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"permitted","explanation":"沒有說規則准許與否；獲准也不代表適合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adequate","explanation":"adequate 僅說勉強達最低要求，不能表達活動與初學者相配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"fitting","explanation":"fitting 較重與目的或場合相稱，這裏的核心是參加者能力。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The museum trip is appropriate for students who use wheelchairs because every gallery on the route has step-free access.","zh":"博物館旅程適合使用輪椅的學生，因為路線上每個展廳都有無障礙通道。","upgrade":"The museum trip is suitable for students who use wheelchairs because every gallery on the route has step-free access.","answer":"suitable","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"permitted","explanation":"沒有校規或場館規則說明是否獲准。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accessible","explanation":"無障礙通道使場館可進入，是其中一個具體條件；題句評估整個旅程對學生是否合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suitable","explanation":"旅程路線上各展廳均可到達，suitable for 保留對這群學生的整體適切性。"},{"letter":"D","text":"safe","explanation":"無障礙通道不能單獨證明整趟旅程絕對安全。"},{"letter":"E","text":"advisable","explanation":"advisable 表是否值得建議，未直接表達學生需要與路線相配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adequate","explanation":"adequate 只說最低程度夠用，語氣弱於整體適合。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"right for","meaning":"對某人合適","note":"日常口語說法，常用於依個人情況選擇旅程；必須補明對象。","collocations":"right for this group; right for younger pupils; not right for everyone","example":"The overnight hike may be right for students who have trained for it.","exampleZh":"通宵遠足或許適合受過相關訓練的學生。","contrast":"Right for 不表示唯一正確，更不保證零風險。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school offered three trips so each student could choose the one appropriate for their interests and stamina.","zh":"學校提供三個旅程，讓每名學生按興趣和體力選擇適合自己的活動。","upgrade":"The school offered three trips so each student could choose the one right for their interests and stamina.","answer":"right for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proper under the rules","explanation":"選擇依興趣和體力，沒有規章判斷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"right for","explanation":"right for their interests and stamina 明確對應每名學生的個別條件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"safe for","explanation":"安全是其中一面，但個人興趣也決定旅程是否合適。"},{"letter":"D","text":"advisable for","explanation":"是否值得推薦不等於每名學生都合身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"fitting for a lesson","explanation":"題句沒有指定哪一課的學習目標。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adequate for","explanation":"adequate for 只說勉強符合需要，未表達個人選擇。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although the climbing course suits older pupils, it may not be appropriate for Mina yet; she has only just begun training.","zh":"攀爬課程雖適合較年長學生，但未必已適合美娜；她才剛開始訓練。","upgrade":"Although the climbing course suits older pupils, it may not be right for Mina yet; she has only just begun training.","answer":"not right for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"not permitted for","explanation":"沒有說規則禁止美娜報名。"},{"letter":"B","text":"not proper for","explanation":"沒有說參加會違反禮儀或校規。"},{"letter":"C","text":"not right for","explanation":"她剛開始訓練，not right for Mina yet 準確表示目前能力未配合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"not safe for","explanation":"未提供攀爬課程的具體安全評估，只說她的訓練階段。"},{"letter":"E","text":"not worthwhile for","explanation":"課程可能有長期價值，只是現時未必適合她。"},{"letter":"F","text":"not accessible to","explanation":"句中沒有說她不能到達或進入課程場地。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"fitting","meaning":"與目的／場合相稱","note":"有清楚教育目標或場合時可說 a fitting activity/choice；比一般 suitable 帶「相稱」意味。","collocations":"fitting for a science course; a fitting choice for the occasion; a fitting activity","example":"A guided geology walk was a fitting activity for the earth-science class.","exampleZh":"有導賞的地質步行很符合地球科學課的學習目的。","contrast":"Fitting 側重與目的相稱，不能單靠它推斷安全和年齡適切。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"For a class studying rock formations, a supervised cave tour was an appropriate choice for the field trip.","zh":"對研究岩層的班級而言，有監督的洞穴導賞是一次相稱的實地考察選擇。","upgrade":"For a class studying rock formations, a supervised cave tour was a fitting choice for the field trip.","answer":"fitting","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"advisable","explanation":"參與或許值得建議，但句中明說選擇與岩層課程內容相稱。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fitting","explanation":"洞穴導賞與地球科學單元的岩層主題吻合，fitting choice 最準。"},{"letter":"C","text":"safe","explanation":"有監督仍不能推論活動完全安全。"},{"letter":"D","text":"proper","explanation":"沒有強調需遵守某規章程序。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adequate","explanation":"adequate 僅表示夠用，未表達內容與課程高度相配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permitted","explanation":"沒有說學校是否批准，批准亦非相稱的理由。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The local history teacher thought the heritage walk was appropriate for a unit on how the district had changed.","zh":"本地歷史老師認為古蹟步行活動很適合介紹該區變遷的單元。","upgrade":"The local history teacher thought the heritage walk was fitting for a unit on how the district had changed.","answer":"fitting for the unit","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proper under school rules","explanation":"題句不是在判斷是否符合校規。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fitting for the unit","explanation":"古蹟步行內容與地區變遷單元直接對應，fitting for the unit 最準。"},{"letter":"C","text":"safe for the class","explanation":"未提供安全評估，與課程主題相配才是理由。"},{"letter":"D","text":"advisable for the school","explanation":"值得推行與否仍需衡量其他條件；題句重點是課程內容。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adequate for the unit","explanation":"adequate 只說夠用，未突出高度吻合的主題。"},{"letter":"F","text":"permitted by the school","explanation":"校方准許不是老師認為相稱的理由。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"proper","meaning":"符合規範的；恰當的","note":"有明確校方守則、程序或禮儀標準時才可把 appropriate 解作 proper；日常判斷學生能力宜用 suitable。","collocations":"proper under school rules; proper conduct; a proper safety procedure","example":"It is proper to obtain parental consent before the overnight school trip.","exampleZh":"通宵學校旅行前取得家長同意，才符合恰當程序。","contrast":"Proper 著眼規範與程序；守規則的旅程仍可能不適合某些學生。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The principal said it was appropriate to obtain signed consent before taking pupils on an overnight trip, as the school rules required.","zh":"校長說按照校規，在帶學生通宵旅行前取得簽署同意才是恰當做法。","upgrade":"The principal said it was proper to obtain signed consent before taking pupils on an overnight trip, as the school rules required.","answer":"proper","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"suitable","explanation":"suitable 偏活動對學生需要相配；這裏是取得簽署同意的明確程序。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fitting","explanation":"fitting 偏與課程或場合相稱，沒有突出守規程序。"},{"letter":"C","text":"proper","explanation":"校規要求先取同意，proper 指合乎程序的恰當做法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"safe","explanation":"取得同意不等於通宵活動必然安全。"},{"letter":"E","text":"advisable","explanation":"advisable 說明智建議，但校規已明定必須遵守。"},{"letter":"F","text":"acceptable","explanation":"acceptable 只說最低限度可接受，未如 proper 表明合規。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The guide reminded the group that appropriate behaviour under the cave’s conservation rules included staying on marked paths and not touching the rock, even where stepping off the path posed no danger to visitors.","zh":"導師提醒一行人，按洞穴的保育規則，恰當行為包括走在標示路線上，以及不要觸摸岩石；即使離開路線不會危及訪客，仍須遵守。","upgrade":"The guide reminded the group that proper behaviour under the cave’s conservation rules included staying on marked paths and not touching the rock, even where stepping off the path posed no danger to visitors.","answer":"proper behaviour","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"safe behaviour","explanation":"洞穴守則旨在保護岩石，即使離開標示路線未必危及訪客，safe 只涵蓋人身安全。"},{"letter":"B","text":"fitting behaviour","explanation":"fitting 可指合場合，但不如 proper 明確指出須遵守保育規則。"},{"letter":"C","text":"proper behaviour","explanation":"走指定路線和不觸摸岩石是場地規範，proper behaviour 最準。"},{"letter":"D","text":"advisable behaviour","explanation":"advisable 是明智之舉，但題句說的是須遵守的守則。"},{"letter":"E","text":"acceptable behaviour","explanation":"acceptable 只表示可接受的最低水平，未突出明確規範。"},{"letter":"F","text":"suitable behaviour","explanation":"suitable 偏對用途或對象相配，較不直接指規矩。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"safe / risk-free · 合適不等於零風險","zh":"中文辨析： 活動可在充分訓練後適合學生，仍有可管理的風險；safe 只談危險程度，risk-free 更是不合理保證。","point":"Suitability is a broader judgment than absence of danger."},{"word":"legal / permitted · 合法或獲准只是其中條件","zh":"中文辨析： 法律或學校准許某活動，不代表它適合所有年齡和體能的學生。只有問題問規則許可時才用 permitted。","point":"Permission does not settle educational fit."},{"word":"advisable / worthwhile · 值得建議與合身不同","zh":"中文辨析： Advisable 涉及是否值得採用；worthwhile 涉及收益。某活動有教育價值，也可能超出個別學生能力。","point":"Value and recommendation are not identical to suitability."},{"word":"acceptable / adequate · 最低可接受不等於適切","zh":"中文辨析： 勉強合格的裝備可能 acceptable，但不等於對高風險活動 appropriate；adequate 也只達最低要求。","point":"Meeting a minimum standard may fall short of a good fit."},{"word":"proper / fitting without cues · 兩詞都須有界線","zh":"中文辨析： Fitting 要說明目的或場合；proper 要有規範標準。原文單問 adventure trips 是否適合學生，不能憑詞典把兩詞當作無條件可換。","point":"Context decides which narrower meaning is active."}],"moduleNumber":39},{"id":"lesson-040","sourceId":93,"headword":"approximately","title":"Approximately","titleZh":"數量大約","subtitle":"數量大約","description":"The 2014 DSE set 7.2 passage says that, on average, each person on Earth owns “approximately 75 LEGO bricks.” The quoted figure is a rounded estimate/average in a 2014 article, not an exact number owned by every person or a present-day statistic. Approximately modifies the number. All practice sentences are original.","sourceSense":"The 2014 DSE set 7.2 passage says that, on average, each person on Earth owns “approximately 75 LEGO bricks.” The quoted figure is a rounded estimate/average in a 2014 article, not an exact number owned by every person or a present-day statistic. Approximately modifies the number. All practice sentences are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["about","直接替代","中性，放數字前。"],["roughly","直接替代","暗示估算較粗略，仍在數字前。"],["around","直接替代","口語自然，數字前；此處不是空間「周圍」。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： or so 是常用口語近義片語，但在數字後面，所以須改寫句子。Some 75 亦可指「約 75」，偏新聞書面語，對本課不如前四項常用；an estimated 75 需把估算詞改成名詞片語，不視為單純副詞替換。Nearly / almost 傾向少於某數；at least / up to 是界線，不是約數。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"Approximately / about / around / roughly 都可表接近某數；roughly 較強調估算粗略，about 中性，around 口語自然，但不是嚴格互斥。Or so 放在數字片語後。記住 on average 說平均，approximately 說精確度；nearly 偏未達，at least 是下限，up to 是上限。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"about","meaning":"大約","note":"中性、常用的約數詞，放在數字、時間或金額前；不說明估算是否粗略。","collocations":"about 75 bricks; about an hour; about twenty people","example":"About forty visitors joined the guided tour.","exampleZh":"約四十名訪客參加了導賞團。","contrast":"數量語境常可與 around 換用；不能因語氣輕微差別硬說只有一個在所有句子成立。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organiser expected approximately 80 visitors and ordered enough chairs for a few more.","zh":"主辦者預計約有八十名訪客，並額外訂了數張椅子。","upgrade":"The organiser expected about 80 visitors and ordered enough chairs for a few more.","answer":"about","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"exactly","explanation":"exactly 表確認剛好八十，預計與額外預留不支持。"},{"letter":"B","text":"at least","explanation":"at least 設最低人數，句中沒有下限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"about","explanation":"about 置於數字前，保留中性約數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"no more than","explanation":"no more than 是上限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"nearly","explanation":"nearly 暗示未到八十，原句可能稍多。"},{"letter":"F","text":"on average","explanation":"on average 需綜合多次活動或多個群體，這裏只預計這場活動。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"It takes approximately half an hour to walk to the nature centre, depending on traffic lights.","zh":"步行到自然教育中心約需半小時，視乎交通燈情況。","upgrade":"It takes about half an hour to walk to the nature centre, depending on traffic lights.","answer":"about","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"at most","explanation":"at most 說最多半小時，但交通燈可能使時間稍長。"},{"letter":"B","text":"about","explanation":"about half an hour 表示可稍長或稍短。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more than","explanation":"more than 強加超過半小時的方向。"},{"letter":"D","text":"exactly","explanation":"exactly 不合交通燈帶來的變動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"almost","explanation":"almost 通常未到半小時，方向太窄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"at least","explanation":"at least 則把半小時當下限，原句亦無此保證。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"roughly","meaning":"粗略約為","note":"數量是粗略估計或四捨五入時用；放數字前，較突出精確度有限。","collocations":"roughly 75 bricks; roughly two hours; roughly a third","example":"The club counted roughly sixty entries before the deadline.","exampleZh":"截止前，社團粗略點算到約六十份報名。","contrast":"Roughly 更明示估算粗略；exactly 則相反。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After a quick count from the back of the hall, the teacher estimated approximately 120 people in the audience.","zh":"老師在禮堂後方快速點算後，估計觀眾約有一百二十人。","upgrade":"After a quick count from the back of the hall, the teacher estimated roughly 120 people in the audience.","answer":"roughly","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"precisely","explanation":"快速點算無法支持 precisely。"},{"letter":"B","text":"at least","explanation":"未說 120 是最低值。"},{"letter":"C","text":"nearly","explanation":"nearly 暗示不足 120；粗略點算可能多或少。"},{"letter":"D","text":"up to","explanation":"up to 是上限，不是中心估值。"},{"letter":"E","text":"on average","explanation":"on average 需要多場或多組數據，此處只點算一場觀眾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"roughly","explanation":"quick count 和 estimated 支持粗略估算 roughly。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The builder said the repairs would cost approximately $5,000, but the final price would depend on what was found behind the wall.","zh":"建築工人說維修約需五千元，但最終價格要看牆後發現甚麼問題。","upgrade":"The builder said the repairs would cost roughly $5,000, but the final price would depend on what was found behind the wall.","answer":"roughly","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"exactly","explanation":"最終價格尚未確定，不能說 exactly。"},{"letter":"B","text":"no more than","explanation":"沒有設定五千元上限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"roughly","explanation":"初步估價而未知牆後情況，roughly 表粗略估計。"},{"letter":"D","text":"almost","explanation":"almost 通常少於五千，原句沒有這個方向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"at least","explanation":"沒有設定最低價。"},{"letter":"F","text":"on average","explanation":"on average 要有多次維修價格，這裏只估一次工程。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"around","meaning":"大約；上下","note":"口語數字前的自然說法；表示接近該數，可能稍多或稍少。","collocations":"around 75 bricks; around noon; around fifty dollars","example":"Around thirty students attended the workshop.","exampleZh":"約三十名學生出席了工作坊。","contrast":"此處是數字範圍，不是 around the building 的空間位置。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The group reached the visitor centre at approximately 3 p.m.; nobody had recorded the exact minute.","zh":"一行人約於下午三時到達訪客中心；沒有人記錄確切分鐘。","upgrade":"The group reached the visitor centre at around 3 p.m.; nobody had recorded the exact minute.","answer":"at around 3 p.m.","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"at exactly 3 p.m.","explanation":"沒有記錄確切分鐘，at exactly 3 p.m. 過於精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"before 3 p.m.","explanation":"before 只說早於三時，原文沒有給單向資訊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"at around 3 p.m.","explanation":"at around 3 p.m. 表接近三時，可能早或晚。"},{"letter":"D","text":"no later than 3 p.m.","explanation":"no later than 把三時當最後期限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"after 3 p.m.","explanation":"after 只說晚於三時。"},{"letter":"F","text":"by 3 p.m.","explanation":"by 3 p.m. 表最遲三時到達，不是接近三時。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The student said her second-hand camera cost approximately $600, though she could not remember the exact amount.","zh":"學生說二手相機約花六百元，但她記不起確實金額。","upgrade":"The student said her second-hand camera cost around $600, though she could not remember the exact amount.","answer":"around","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"precisely","explanation":"記不起確實金額，precisely 不合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"around","explanation":"around $600 是自然口語約數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"at least","explanation":"沒有說六百是最低價。"},{"letter":"D","text":"less than","explanation":"less than 強加低於六百的方向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"no more than","explanation":"no more than 把六百變成上限。"},{"letter":"F","text":"as much as","explanation":"as much as 強調金額可高達六百，並非中性約數。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"or so","meaning":"左右","note":"置於數字片語之後，如 seventy-five or so；偏口語，改寫時必須移位。","collocations":"seventy-five or so; ten minutes or so; a dozen or so","example":"A dozen or so parents stayed for the final discussion.","exampleZh":"約有十多名家長留下參加最後的討論。","contrast":"與 about 的意義接近，主要差別在位置和語體；不能說 or so seventy-five。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"There were approximately twenty people waiting outside when the doors opened.","zh":"開門時，外面約有二十人等候。","upgrade":"There were twenty or so people waiting outside when the doors opened.","answer":"twenty or so","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"twenty or so","explanation":"twenty or so 在數字後表示約二十人。"},{"letter":"B","text":"at least twenty","explanation":"at least 設最低二十人。"},{"letter":"C","text":"exactly twenty","explanation":"exactly 把人數說成剛好二十，原句非精確計數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"twenty at most","explanation":"at most 設上限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"nearly twenty","explanation":"nearly 往往指未到二十人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"twenty on average","explanation":"on average 需要多次開門人數，原句只談一次。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The guide asked us to wait approximately ten minutes while she checked the weather forecast.","zh":"導師請我們等約十分鐘，期間她查閱天氣預報。","upgrade":"The guide asked us to wait ten minutes or so while she checked the weather forecast.","answer":"ten minutes or so","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"at most ten minutes","explanation":"at most 把十分鐘變成上限。"},{"letter":"B","text":"exactly ten minutes","explanation":"exactly 把等候時間說得過於精確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"up to ten minutes","explanation":"up to 也設十分鐘上限，原文沒有。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ten minutes or so","explanation":"ten minutes or so 將約數片語放後，保留大約意思。"},{"letter":"E","text":"at least ten minutes","explanation":"at least 設十分鐘下限。"},{"letter":"F","text":"nearly ten minutes","explanation":"nearly 傾向不足十分鐘。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"exactly / precisely · 準確數字","zh":"中文辨析： 原文 approximately 表示近似；exactly 和 precisely 表示數字經確認或指定精確值。若每人真有 75 塊才可用 exactly，平均值不能如此推斷。","point":"A rounded mean is not an exact individual count."},{"word":"nearly / almost · 接近但通常未達","zh":"中文辨析： Nearly 75 通常暗示低於 75；approximately 75 可略高或略低。若有證據顯示尚差一點達門檻，nearly 才合。","point":"Approximation does not imply the number is below the target."},{"word":"at least / more than · 下限","zh":"中文辨析： At least 75、more than 75 都把數字作下限或超過門檻；約 75 沒有這個方向。","point":"A lower bound is not a two-sided estimate."},{"word":"up to / at most · 上限","zh":"中文辨析： Up to 75 或 at most 75 可包括很小的數，表示上限；approximately 75 指接近 75。","point":"An upper cap is not a rounded central value."},{"word":"on average / approximately · 平均與約數不同","zh":"中文辨析： 原文同時有 on average 和 approximately：前者說如何綜合人群數量，後者說 75 是約數。可有精確平均值，也可有粗略的非平均數。","point":"Average describes aggregation; approximately describes precision."}],"moduleNumber":40},{"id":"lesson-041","sourceId":89,"headword":"appreciate","title":"Appreciate","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"A speaker in the 2013 exhibition passage hopes it will help Hongkongers “better appreciate our unique character.” The object is the city’s distinctive character, not a gift or favour. The context permits both understanding and favourable valuation; the exhibition’s hoped-for effect is not asserted as already achieved. [2013 Paper 4, set 9.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/963126936/2013-DSE-Paper-4-Examiner-Ver).","sourceSense":"A speaker in the 2013 exhibition passage hopes it will help Hongkongers “better appreciate our unique character.” The object is the city’s distinctive character, not a gift or favour. The context permits both understanding and favourable valuation; the exhibition’s hoped-for effect is not asserted as already achieved. [2013 Paper 4, set 9.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/963126936/2013-DSE-Paper-4-Examiner-Ver).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["value","Close when people regard the city’s distinctive quality as worth preserving or celebrating."],["recognise","Contextual for noticing or acknowledging a distinct quality; may lack the positive esteem in appreciate."],["be grateful for","False for this object: gratitude usually responds to a benefit, favour or person; the source asks people to understand and esteem a character."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Understand is taught when the exhibition supplies explanation of why a custom or trait matters. Admire is taught when the reaction is clearly positive praise of a specific quality, not mere recognition. Cherish adds affection and a wish to protect, stronger than the source alone; acknowledge can be neutral or reluctant; enjoy describes pleasure rather than discernment. Thank and be grateful for belong to another appreciate sense."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["題句有甚麼證據","選詞"],"rows":[["支持保存或認為值得重視","value"],["原本忽略，後來辨認出特色","recognise"],["解說揭示成因或重要性","understand"],["明確讚美某項能力或創意","admire"]],"note":"來源希望港人更深入認識並珍視城市獨特性，並非要求他們感謝一份個人恩惠。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"value","meaning":"重視；認為有價值","note":"看見特色值得保留或珍惜，著重價值判斷；比單純知道它存在更積極。","collocations":"value local heritage; value the city’s diversity; value a tradition.","example":"Residents value the neighbourhood’s small family-run shops and want them to survive.","exampleZh":"居民重視區內的小型家庭商店，並希望它們能繼續經營。","contrast":"Recognise 只需察覺；value 還包含認為值得保留或支持。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the exhibition, residents appreciated the old street signs enough to support a plan to preserve them.","zh":"參觀展覽後，居民更重視舊街道標誌，甚至支持保存計劃。","upgrade":"After the exhibition, residents valued the old street signs enough to support a plan to preserve them.","answer":"valued","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"understood","explanation":"理解標誌的來歷不一定會支持保存；這句明說居民認為它值得保留。"},{"letter":"B","text":"valued","explanation":"支持保存顯示認為其值得保留，valued 正確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"remembered","explanation":"記得標誌不等於認為它有文化價值。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enjoyed","explanation":"看着標誌覺得有趣，未必形成保育立場。"},{"letter":"E","text":"thanked","explanation":"標誌不是給居民恩惠的人，不能用感謝代替重視。"},{"letter":"F","text":"recognised","explanation":"認出舊標誌只證明知道其存在，未必會支持保存計劃。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The museum hopes visitors will appreciate the city’s mix of languages and defend its place in local culture.","zh":"博物館希望訪客重視這座城市多語並存的特色，並支持它在本地文化中的地位。","upgrade":"The museum hopes visitors will value the city’s mix of languages and defend its place in local culture.","answer":"value","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"observe","explanation":"觀察到多種語言不等於為其文化地位發聲。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be grateful for","explanation":"感謝某人幫助不同於重視城市的語言特色。"},{"letter":"C","text":"understand","explanation":"理解多語並存的背景未必會主動維護其文化地位。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admire","explanation":"欣賞多語特色可以是正面情緒，但此句更強調願意維護它的價值。"},{"letter":"E","text":"value","explanation":"支持多語特色的文化地位，需要認為其有價值，value 符合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"recognise","explanation":"承認多語存在仍可能態度中性；句中還有主動維護。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"recognise","meaning":"察覺並承認","note":"注意到某種特色確實存在，尤其原本容易被忽略；未必代表喜愛或願意保育。","collocations":"recognise a distinctive trait; recognise the city’s character; recognise a pattern.","example":"The photographs helped pupils recognise the market’s unusual mix of old and new shops.","exampleZh":"照片幫助學生察覺市場中新舊商店並存的獨特之處。","contrast":"Appreciate 常帶正面估值；recognise 可只表示看見或承認事實。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The photo display helped visitors appreciate a distinctive feature they had overlooked: tiny workshops hidden behind busy shopfronts.","zh":"照片展覽幫助訪客察覺一項過去忽略的特色：繁忙店面後隱藏着小工場。","upgrade":"The photo display helped visitors recognise a distinctive feature they had overlooked: tiny workshops hidden behind busy shopfronts.","answer":"recognise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"recognise","explanation":"由忽略到看見並承認特色，recognise 最準確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"admire","explanation":"照片可能令人欣賞，但句中明說重點是察覺以前忽略的工場。"},{"letter":"C","text":"value","explanation":"重視小工場比單純發現它們更進一步；原句只明說從忽略到看見。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enjoy","explanation":"訪客未必覺得小工場有娛樂性。"},{"letter":"E","text":"understand","explanation":"理解小工場的歷史或作用需要解說；照片這裏先幫助訪客察覺它們。"},{"letter":"F","text":"celebrate","explanation":"慶祝是表達讚賞的活動，超出首次留意到的事實。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the guide pointed out the rooflines, students began to appreciate which details made this district different from the neighbouring one.","zh":"導賞員指出屋頂線條後，學生開始察覺哪些細節令這區與鄰區不同。","upgrade":"After the guide pointed out the rooflines, students began to recognise which details made this district different from the neighbouring one.","answer":"recognise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cherish","explanation":"珍惜暗示情感和保護意願，句中只說看出差別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enjoy","explanation":"觀賞屋頂可能愉快，但題句重在辨認哪些細節不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"praise","explanation":"讚揚要有正面評價，原句沒有。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recognise","explanation":"導賞員指出可見細節後，學生開始辨別區域差異，recognise 合適。"},{"letter":"E","text":"understand","explanation":"深入理解屋頂設計原因比看出兩區差異多一步，原句沒有解說成因。"},{"letter":"F","text":"value","explanation":"重視某區屋頂特色包含價值判斷；原句只說辨別哪些細節不同。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"understand","meaning":"理解（特色的意思或成因）","note":"展覽、訪談或解說讓人明白一項本地特色的背景、作用或重要性；重在理解，不必已作價值承諾。","collocations":"understand the city’s character; understand why a tradition matters; better understand local culture.","example":"The oral histories helped teenagers understand why the harbour shaped the city’s working life.","exampleZh":"口述歷史幫助青少年理解海港為何塑造了這座城市的工作生活。","contrast":"Recognise 可只看見特色；understand 進一步掌握原因和含義。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"By hearing residents explain their family shops, visitors came to appreciate why those shops were important to the district.","zh":"聽居民解釋家族商店的故事後，訪客逐漸理解這些商店對社區為何重要。","upgrade":"By hearing residents explain their family shops, visitors came to understand why those shops were important to the district.","answer":"understand","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"spot","explanation":"看到商店位置不等於理解它對社區的作用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"enjoy","explanation":"喜歡逛店可能存在，但原句說的是透過講解掌握意義。"},{"letter":"C","text":"understand","explanation":"居民提供原因與背景，understand why 表達訪客理解其重要性。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recognise","explanation":"察覺商店存在不足以回答它們為何對社區重要；居民的講述提供了原因。"},{"letter":"E","text":"thank","explanation":"訪客不是在答謝居民的服務，而是學習商店背景。"},{"letter":"F","text":"value","explanation":"重視商店或許會隨理解而來，但「value why」不能自然替換此處的 appreciate why。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The exhibition captions helped newcomers appreciate how several migration waves had shaped the city’s food culture.","zh":"展覽說明文字幫助新來者理解幾波移民如何塑造這座城市的飲食文化。","upgrade":"The exhibition captions helped newcomers understand how several migration waves had shaped the city’s food culture.","answer":"understand","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"admire","explanation":"新來者可能欣賞飲食文化，但題句重點是說明文字解釋其形成過程。"},{"letter":"B","text":"recognise","explanation":"認出移民影響存在，未必理解各波移民如何塑造飲食文化的過程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"identify","explanation":"指出有哪些菜式，只及於辨認，未必懂形成過程。"},{"letter":"D","text":"value","explanation":"重視飲食文化未必明白展覽文字所解釋的形成過程。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be grateful for","explanation":"這不是感謝移民給予個人恩惠的句子。"},{"letter":"F","text":"understand","explanation":"文字解釋「如何塑造」，understand 準確表達對因果背景的理解。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"admire","meaning":"欣賞；讚賞","note":"對特定能力、創意或品格作明確正面評價；比中性察覺更強，但未必包含保育承諾。","collocations":"admire local creativity; admire the skill of craftsmen; admire the city’s resilience.","example":"Visitors admired the craft workers’ patience in restoring the old signs.","exampleZh":"訪客讚賞工匠修復舊招牌時展現的耐性。","contrast":"Admire 需要值得稱讚的具體特質；recognise 可純粹察覺，value 可能涉及保護。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At the exhibition, visitors appreciated the craft workers’ skill and praised the precision of every restored sign.","zh":"在展覽上，訪客欣賞工匠的手藝，並稱讚每塊修復招牌的精細工序。","upgrade":"At the exhibition, visitors admired the craft workers’ skill and praised the precision of every restored sign.","answer":"admired","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"identified","explanation":"認出是哪位工匠並不等於讚賞其技術。"},{"letter":"B","text":"admired","explanation":"訪客明確讚揚手藝精準，admired 表示積極欣賞這項能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"valued","explanation":"重視工匠手藝可以成立，但句中公開稱讚修復精細，admired 更直接說出讚賞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recognised","explanation":"察覺工匠有技術不及明確稱讚每塊招牌修復得精細。"},{"letter":"E","text":"enjoyed","explanation":"參觀愉快不及「讚賞手藝」具體。"},{"letter":"F","text":"thanked","explanation":"若工匠曾幫助訪客可道謝，但句中評的是專業技藝。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Residents appreciated the volunteers’ creativity in turning an empty lane into a lively exhibition and publicly praised their ideas.","zh":"居民欣賞義工把空巷變成熱鬧展覽的創意，並公開讚揚他們的構思。","upgrade":"Residents admired the volunteers’ creativity in turning an empty lane into a lively exhibition and publicly praised their ideas.","answer":"admired","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"recognised","explanation":"察覺有創意仍可態度中性，原句還明說公開讚揚。"},{"letter":"B","text":"understood","explanation":"理解義工如何設計展覽，不等於公開讚揚其創意。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cherished","explanation":"珍惜可以包含長久情感，但此句焦點是稱讚具體創意。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enjoyed","explanation":"享受展覽可與讚賞創意並存，卻未必直接評價義工想法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"admired","explanation":"對義工的創意作正面稱讚，admired 最貼切。"},{"letter":"F","text":"acknowledged","explanation":"承認義工有創意可以是中性評述；公開稱讚更貼近 admired。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"appreciate / be grateful for","zh":"中文辨析： Be grateful for 指因得到好處而心存感激；來源的賓語是城市的獨特性，重點是理解與珍視。若有人幫助舉辦展覽，才可說對其幫助心存感激。","point":"Valuing a city’s character is not the same as thanking a benefactor."},{"word":"recognise / understand / value","zh":"中文辨析： Recognise 是察覺特色，understand 是懂其成因及意義，value 是認為值得重視。看見、明白、珍惜可連續發生，不能在每句中無條件互換。","point":"Detection, explanation, and valuation are distinct cognitive steps."},{"word":"admire / acknowledge","zh":"中文辨析： Admire 明確讚賞；acknowledge 可以勉強承認一項事實，未必有正面評價。公開稱讚手藝時前者較準。","point":"Recognition of a fact need not imply praise."},{"word":"enjoy / appreciate","zh":"中文辨析： Enjoy 指愉快體驗；一個人可以喜歡看展覽，卻未理解其展示的城市特色。反之也可能尊重一段沉重歷史而不感到愉快。","point":"Pleasure and informed esteem do not always coincide."},{"word":"cherish / appreciate","zh":"中文辨析： Cherish 帶深厚感情和保護願望，較強於來源的 better appreciate。只有題句明說願保存或守護時，才可能適用。","point":"Cherishing adds an enduring protective attachment."}],"moduleNumber":41},{"id":"lesson-042","sourceId":83,"headword":"appeal","title":"Appeal","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 Paper 4 question asks, “Do 3D movies appeal more to younger people or older people?” This is a verb followed by to and an audience. It asks about relative attractiveness; it does not give the answer or concern a legal appeal. [2012 Paper 4, set 4.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2012 Paper 4 question asks, “Do 3D movies appeal more to younger people or older people?” This is a verb followed by to and an audience. It asks about relative attractiveness; it does not give the answer or concern a legal appeal. [2012 Paper 4, set 4.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["attract","Close: draw an audience’s attention or interest; takes a direct object rather than to."],["interest","Close when the feature arouses curiosity; takes a direct object."],["charm","Contextual only for a pleasing, endearing quality; 3D technology need not charm viewers, so not a general source replacement."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Be attractive to gives a direct adjective recast; draw is useful where appeal leads people to attend or watch. Both are taught with conditions. Be popular with reports actual favourable reception rather than a possible attraction, and entice suggests a stronger invitation to act; both are treated as contrasts. Engage requires attention or participation rather than attraction alone. Captivate and fascinate overstate intensity unless the reaction is evident. The legal verb appeal against belongs to another sense."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["語境","最合適的詞"],"rows":[["泛指作品吸引某群人","attract + 人"],["令人想了解題材","interest + 人"],["把 appeal to 改成「對……有吸引力」","be attractive to + 人"],["已把人吸引到場／觀看","draw + 人 + to 地點"]],"note":"2012 原題是開放式比較：別從題目推斷年輕或年長觀眾哪方一定更喜歡 3D 電影。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"attract","meaning":"吸引（某群觀眾）","note":"使人留意或想接觸電影；及物動詞直接接觀眾，不跟 to。","collocations":"attract younger viewers; attract a wide audience; attract attention.","example":"The film’s vivid underwater scenes attract viewers who enjoy visual effects.","exampleZh":"電影生動的海底畫面吸引喜歡視覺特效的觀眾。","contrast":"Appeal to 強調主觀吸引力；attract 可說作品把觀眾吸引過來，但不必證明票房。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The bright 3D animation may appeal to children who enjoy colourful screen effects.","zh":"鮮明的立體動畫可能吸引喜歡繽紛畫面效果的孩子。","upgrade":"The bright 3D animation may attract children who enjoy colourful screen effects.","answer":"attract","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"convince","explanation":"句子只說孩子可能被畫面吸引，沒有要說服他們接受某個論點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"attract","explanation":"畫面可能令這群孩子想觀看，attract 保留吸引力，並直接接人作受詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"entertain","explanation":"娛樂是觀看後的感受，未必解釋畫面為何先吸引他們。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charm","explanation":"討喜或可愛的魅力並非鮮明視覺效果必然具有的特質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"recruit","explanation":"招募通常用於成員或員工，不合動畫吸引觀眾的語境。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impress","explanation":"留下深刻印象可能發生在觀看後，較強於題句的可能吸引。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A lower ticket price for the 3D matinee could appeal to parents who usually avoid costly cinema trips.","zh":"較低的立體電影日場票價，可能吸引平日避免昂貴戲院活動的家長。","upgrade":"A lower ticket price for the 3D matinee could attract parents who usually avoid costly cinema trips.","answer":"attract","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"satisfy","explanation":"家長尚未購票或觀看，不能說低價已令他們滿意。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impress","explanation":"票價較低未必令人留下深刻印象；句子關心它能否吸引原本卻步者。"},{"letter":"C","text":"attract","explanation":"價錢降低可能吸引平日嫌貴的家長，attract 保留這種可能性。"},{"letter":"D","text":"persuade","explanation":"沒有論證要家長接受某個主張，只有較合適的價格。"},{"letter":"E","text":"engage","explanation":"Engage 指參與或保持投入，未必是低價令家長開始考慮觀影。"},{"letter":"F","text":"delight","explanation":"家長看完是否開心未知，不能把事前吸引改成觀後喜悅。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"interest","meaning":"引起興趣","note":"令特定觀眾想了解或觀看；及物動詞直連人，尤其當題句明示好奇心或題材興趣。","collocations":"interest younger viewers; interest science fans; interest an audience in a topic.","example":"A short film about coral reefs might interest students studying marine life.","exampleZh":"一套關於珊瑚礁的短片可能引起修讀海洋生物的學生的興趣。","contrast":"Interest 突出好奇或題材切合，不保證觀眾真的到戲院。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The science behind the 3D camera may appeal to students curious about how movies are made.","zh":"立體攝影機背後的科學可能引起好奇電影製作方法的學生的興趣。","upgrade":"The science behind the 3D camera may interest students curious about how movies are made.","answer":"interest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"entertain","explanation":"製作原理可以有趣，但未必旨在娛樂學生。"},{"letter":"B","text":"charm","explanation":"技術知識不是以可愛討喜為特徵的魅力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"persuade","explanation":"原句沒提出需要學生相信的主張，不是在說服他們。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reward","explanation":"獎勵是給予回報，與對攝影科學好奇無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interest","explanation":"學生對製作原理好奇，interest 直接指引起這方面興趣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reassure","explanation":"安撫焦慮不是句中的觀眾反應。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A 3D documentary about migrating sea turtles might appeal to biology students researching animal journeys.","zh":"一套講述海龜遷徙的立體紀錄片，可能引起正在研究動物遷徙的生物科學生的興趣。","upgrade":"A 3D documentary about migrating sea turtles might interest biology students researching animal journeys.","answer":"interest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"interest","explanation":"海龜遷徙正是學生的研究題材，interest 突出這種好奇與切合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"impress","explanation":"立體影像或令人印象深刻，但題句的關鍵是紀錄片題材切合研究方向。"},{"letter":"C","text":"occupy","explanation":"佔用學生時間不等於令他們想了解海龜遷徙。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charm","explanation":"海龜可能可愛，但原句沒有說學生被討喜外表吸引。"},{"letter":"E","text":"amuse","explanation":"紀錄片可能有娛樂性，題句卻著重研究興趣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"convince","explanation":"紀錄片未提出需要他們接受的爭議主張。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"be attractive to","meaning":"對……有吸引力","note":"把動詞 appeal to 改寫成形容詞結構；主語是電影或特色，後面用 to 接受眾。","collocations":"be attractive to older viewers; seem attractive to audiences; more attractive to one group than another.","example":"The shorter screening time may be attractive to families with young children.","exampleZh":"較短的放映時間可能對有年幼孩子的家庭有吸引力。","contrast":"Attractive 不等於外表漂亮；此處指作品或特點對一群人有吸引力，整句需補 be。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The interactive 3D exhibition might appeal to families who prefer hands-on activities.","zh":"互動式立體展覽可能對喜歡親手參與活動的家庭有吸引力。","upgrade":"The interactive 3D exhibition might be attractive to families who prefer hands-on activities.","answer":"be attractive to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be available to","explanation":"展覽開放給家庭不等於他們會被互動活動吸引。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be grateful to","explanation":"Grateful 描述人感謝別人，展覽不能感謝家庭。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be visible to","explanation":"能看見展覽不等於覺得它有吸引力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be attractive to","explanation":"親手參與正合這群家庭興趣，be attractive to 保留主觀吸引力。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be suitable for","explanation":"Suitable 說活動客觀上適合，但未必表示家庭因此有興趣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be familiar to","explanation":"對家庭來說熟悉，也不一定吸引他們參加。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The slow-paced 3D documentary may appeal more to older viewers than to teenagers, according to the organiser’s prediction.","zh":"按主辦方的預測，節奏較慢的立體紀錄片可能比起青少年更能吸引年長觀眾。","upgrade":"The slow-paced 3D documentary may be more attractive to older viewers than to teenagers, according to the organiser’s prediction.","answer":"be more attractive to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"be better known to","explanation":"較多人知道不等於對他們有較大吸引力。"},{"letter":"B","text":"be more popular with","explanation":"More popular with 常暗示已有實際反應；此處只是主辦方事前預測。"},{"letter":"C","text":"be more accessible to","explanation":"更容易接觸或觀看不等於更想看。"},{"letter":"D","text":"be more familiar to","explanation":"年長觀眾可能熟悉紀錄片形式，但原句比較的是興趣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"be more profitable for","explanation":"獲利對象不是觀眾的主觀喜好。"},{"letter":"F","text":"be more attractive to","explanation":"More attractive to 可保留「可能比較吸引」而不偷換成已證實受歡迎。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"draw","meaning":"吸引前來觀看","note":"當吸引力帶來到場或觀看行動時，用及物動詞 draw 接觀眾或人流；比單純覺得有趣更接近實際參與。","collocations":"draw young audiences; draw viewers to a screening; draw a crowd.","example":"The outdoor 3D screening drew families to the park on Saturday.","exampleZh":"週六的戶外立體電影放映吸引家庭到公園觀看。","contrast":"來源問題只問哪類人較受吸引，沒有公布入場結果；draw 只在原創題目明示觀眾前來時使用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The 3D film’s evening show appealed to teenagers strongly enough to bring them to the cinema despite the rain.","zh":"這套立體電影的晚場對青少年有足夠吸引力，令他們即使下雨也到戲院觀看。","upgrade":"The 3D film’s evening show drew teenagers to the cinema despite the rain.","answer":"drew","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"delighted","explanation":"題句證明他們到場，卻未說觀影後感到高興。"},{"letter":"B","text":"interested","explanation":"感興趣不必然到場；原句特別說下雨仍然去了。"},{"letter":"C","text":"drew","explanation":"吸引力帶來實際到戲院的行動，drew ... to the cinema 最完整。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charmed","explanation":"討喜魅力未必是這場電影吸引人到場的原因。"},{"letter":"E","text":"served","explanation":"Served 是提供服務，不表示吸引觀眾前來。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reached","explanation":"接觸到青少年不等於使他們冒雨入場。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The 3D film preview appealed to remote viewers so strongly that many clicked through to watch the full film online.","zh":"立體電影預告片十分吸引遠端觀眾，令很多人點擊觀看網上播放的完整電影。","upgrade":"The 3D film preview drew remote viewers to the full film online.","answer":"drew","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"amused","explanation":"點擊完整電影不證明他們已被預告片逗笑。"},{"letter":"B","text":"informed","explanation":"預告片可能提供資訊，但原句重點是促使觀眾從短片點入完整版。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reassured","explanation":"沒有疑慮被消除的線索。"},{"letter":"D","text":"targeted","explanation":"預告片可能面向遠端觀眾，targeted 只說受眾設定，不說他們真的點入。"},{"letter":"E","text":"drew","explanation":"觀眾實際點擊觀看網上完整版，drew ... to the full film 保留由吸引轉成行動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"pleased","explanation":"點擊不證明觀眾已對整部電影滿意。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"appeal to / legal appeal","zh":"中文辨析： Appeal to an audience 是吸引；appeal against a decision 是上訴，介詞與語義都不同。","point":"Audience attraction and a legal challenge are separate verb senses."},{"word":"attract / interest / draw","zh":"中文辨析： Attract 泛指吸引，interest 突出好奇，draw 通常暗示實際把人吸引到場。來源只問相對吸引力，沒有入場數據。","point":"A film may interest someone without drawing that person to a cinema."},{"word":"charm / captivate","zh":"中文辨析： Charm 帶討喜、親切的魅力；captivate 指強烈地迷住觀眾。立體效果未必具備這兩種情緒及強度。","point":"Not every appealing film is endearing or spellbinding."},{"word":"popular / attractive","zh":"中文辨析： Popular 常根據已有觀眾反應或普及程度說受歡迎；attractive 可作事前推測。原試題沒有公布年齡組喜好結果。","point":"Predicted appeal is not evidence of actual popularity."},{"word":"engage / entertain / appeal","zh":"中文辨析： Engage 指抓住注意或促使參與；entertain 指娛樂效果。它們可能由吸引力帶來，但不等於最初的吸引本身。","point":"Initial appeal, sustained attention, and enjoyment are distinct stages."}],"moduleNumber":42},{"id":"lesson-043","sourceId":86,"headword":"appearance","title":"Appearance","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 article says some fans think newcomers’ “appearance does not accurately resemble the manga character” they impersonate. The noun refers to how the cosplay looks in comparison with a drawn character. The passage separately mentions understanding the character, so visual fidelity and knowledge must not be collapsed. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2012 article says some fans think newcomers’ “appearance does not accurately resemble the manga character” they impersonate. The noun refers to how the cosplay looks in comparison with a drawn character. The passage separately mentions understanding the character, so visual fidelity and knowledge must not be collapsed. [2012 Paper 4, set 1.3](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["look","Close everyday noun for the visible combined effect of hair, costume, make-up and accessories."],["image","Ambiguous: a photograph, designed image, or public reputation; not a safe general replacement for a person’s cosplay appearance."],["outward form","Conditional for broad shape or physical form, but too limited for detailed costume fidelity; not taught as general equivalent."],["visual style","Conditional for aesthetic manner, but a style can differ from an exact character design; not a general replacement."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Visual presentation is useful when discussing how the whole cosplay is displayed or assessed and is taught with that boundary. Visual resemblance is taught when the comparison with a specific manga reference is explicit; it names similarity, not the whole appearance. Costume, wig, and make-up are components only. Likeness without visual can work, but the explicit phrase helps distinguish looks from personality. Physical appearance mostly repeats the headword, so it is not padded into the guide."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["問題焦點","選擇"],"rows":[["日常說整體扮相","look"],["評審或照片看到的整體展示效果","visual presentation"],["與指定漫畫原畫的相似程度","visual resemblance to + 角色"]],"note":"來源談的是可見的扮相與原角色是否吻合，不是參賽者的名聲、角色知識或只看服裝價格。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"look","meaning":"扮相；外觀","note":"日常說法，指角色扮演者整體呈現出來的樣子；可包括服裝、假髮、化妝。","collocations":"a convincing look; recreate the character’s look; her overall look.","example":"The cosplayer adjusted her wig until her look matched the drawing more closely.","exampleZh":"角色扮演者調整假髮，直到她的扮相更接近原畫。","contrast":"Look 是整體外觀，不只是單件 costume，也不代表演繹者理解角色。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The cosplayer’s appearance changed noticeably after she replaced the bright wig and adjusted her make-up.","zh":"角色扮演者換上鮮艷假髮並調整妝容後，扮相明顯改變。","upgrade":"The cosplayer’s look changed noticeably after she replaced the bright wig and adjusted her make-up.","answer":"look","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reputation","explanation":"名聲不會因即時換假髮和妝容而在鏡前改變。"},{"letter":"B","text":"look","explanation":"假髮與妝容共同改變可見的整體扮相，look 合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"performance","explanation":"表演包含動作和演技，題句只說靜態外觀的變化。"},{"letter":"D","text":"character knowledge","explanation":"是否理解漫畫角色與換假髮、化妝不是同一回事。"},{"letter":"E","text":"costume fabric","explanation":"布料只涉及服裝材質，不能涵蓋假髮及妝容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"photograph","explanation":"照片可記錄外觀，但不是人物本人被改變的扮相。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"From across the hall, the cosplayer’s appearance was recognisable because of the distinctive coat, hair shape and hat.","zh":"從展廳另一端望過去，角色扮演者憑着獨特外套、髮型輪廓和帽子，其扮相仍容易辨認。","upgrade":"From across the hall, the cosplayer’s look was recognisable because of the distinctive coat, hair shape and hat.","answer":"look","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"visual identity","explanation":"Visual identity 可以指整體設計特色，但較偏品牌或角色的識別系統，題句談扮演者眼前的外觀。"},{"letter":"B","text":"acting skill","explanation":"遠處看不出內在演技；外套、髮型和帽子是可見線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"wardrobe only","explanation":"只說衣櫥或服裝，漏掉髮型輪廓。"},{"letter":"D","text":"public image","explanation":"公眾形象是別人對人的印象或名聲，不是展廳內可見的造型。"},{"letter":"E","text":"look","explanation":"三項外觀線索合起來讓人認出扮相，look 最自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"face alone","explanation":"帽子和外套也幫助辨認，並非只看面容。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"visual presentation","meaning":"視覺呈現","note":"較正式地說服裝、化妝、姿態等如何被整體展示給觀眾或評審；焦點是呈現效果，不是私人名聲。","collocations":"assess the visual presentation; improve visual presentation; overall visual presentation.","example":"The judges praised the visual presentation of the costume but questioned the missing prop.","exampleZh":"評審稱讚服裝的視覺呈現，但質疑缺少了道具。","contrast":"Presentation 可以包含燈光或拍攝方法，故在題目中須明說評審或照片如何看到整體造型。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The judging sheet scored each entrant’s appearance as seen on stage, including costume, make-up and pose.","zh":"評分表按每名參賽者在台上展示的服裝、妝容及姿態，評核其視覺呈現。","upgrade":"The judging sheet scored each entrant’s visual presentation as seen on stage, including costume, make-up and pose.","answer":"visual presentation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"visual presentation","explanation":"評分項目是台上整體造型如何呈現，visual presentation 涵蓋服裝、妝容和姿態。"},{"letter":"B","text":"acting ability","explanation":"演技包含說話和動作演繹，題句只列外觀及站姿。"},{"letter":"C","text":"costume accuracy","explanation":"服裝是否準確只是其中一環，漏掉妝容及姿態。"},{"letter":"D","text":"visual resemblance to a character","explanation":"題句沒有指定要與哪個角色原畫作對照，不能只評相似程度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"stage charisma","explanation":"舞台魅力可以來自表演自信，未必等於服裝妝容呈現。"},{"letter":"F","text":"overall attractiveness","explanation":"主觀覺得漂亮與評分表列出的多項造型細節不是同一標準。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For the poster, the team checked how the cosplayer’s appearance would be presented under blue lighting in the final photograph.","zh":"製作海報時，團隊查看藍色燈光下，角色扮演者的扮相會如何在最終照片中呈現。","upgrade":"For the poster, the team checked the cosplayer’s visual presentation under blue lighting in the final photograph.","answer":"visual presentation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"costume fidelity","explanation":"服裝是否忠於原作可能重要，但題句關心藍光下整張照片的呈現。"},{"letter":"B","text":"visual style","explanation":"Visual style 可指設計風格，但題句檢查的是這個人在最終照片中如何被展示。"},{"letter":"C","text":"character likeness","explanation":"相似度須有指定角色圖像作比較；這裏未說要核對原畫。"},{"letter":"D","text":"visual presentation","explanation":"海報的燈光與拍攝改變整體可見效果，visual presentation 最準確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"public image","explanation":"公眾形象指長期名聲，不是單張海報的藍光效果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"fabric texture","explanation":"布料紋理只是照片中一個細節，不能概括整體扮相。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"visual resemblance","meaning":"視覺相似度","note":"當句子直接比較扮演者與漫畫原畫時，可把「外觀很相似／不像」改寫為視覺相似度高／低；它是關係而非整體外觀本身。","collocations":"a close visual resemblance to the character; little visual resemblance; assess visual resemblance.","example":"The blue wig gave the cosplayer a closer visual resemblance to the manga character.","exampleZh":"藍色假髮令角色扮演者的外觀更接近漫畫角色。","contrast":"Resemblance 必須有比較對象；服裝好看不代表與原角色相似。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The newcomer’s appearance was very similar to the manga drawing because the coat pattern and hairstyle matched it closely.","zh":"這名新參加者的外觀與漫畫原畫十分相似，因為外套花紋和髮型都高度吻合。","upgrade":"The newcomer showed a close visual resemblance to the manga drawing because the coat pattern and hairstyle matched it closely.","answer":"visual resemblance","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"individual style","explanation":"個人風格可以很獨特，卻未必忠於漫畫原畫。"},{"letter":"B","text":"costume quality","explanation":"服裝可能精良，但高品質不等於花紋和髮型與原畫吻合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"visual resemblance","explanation":"有原畫作對照，外套花紋與髮型都吻合，visual resemblance 表達可見的相似關係。"},{"letter":"D","text":"character knowledge","explanation":"了解角色故事不能單靠外觀證明。"},{"letter":"E","text":"public likeness","explanation":"Public likeness 不是此處常用的扮相比較詞，亦易與肖像權混淆。"},{"letter":"F","text":"artistic originality","explanation":"題句強調複製細節，而不是原創設計。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Even with an expensive costume, the cosplayer’s appearance did not resemble the character in the reference panel because the colours were reversed.","zh":"即使服裝昂貴，角色扮演者的扮相仍因顏色顛倒，而不像參考漫畫格中的角色。","upgrade":"Even with an expensive costume, the cosplayer showed little visual resemblance to the character in the reference panel because the colours were reversed.","answer":"visual resemblance","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"visual appeal","explanation":"扮相或許仍有吸引力，但題句評的是與參考畫格是否吻合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"costume expense","explanation":"價格已明示很高，卻不能決定外觀相似度。"},{"letter":"C","text":"acting style","explanation":"演技不涉及漫畫畫格的服裝配色。"},{"letter":"D","text":"personal image","explanation":"個人形象或名聲與參考角色的顏色比較無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"stage presence","explanation":"舞台存在感可以強，但扮相仍可能不像原畫。"},{"letter":"F","text":"visual resemblance","explanation":"顏色顛倒造成與畫格差異，little visual resemblance 準確表達不像。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"look / public image","zh":"中文辨析： Look 是眼前扮相；public image 指人們對參賽者的印象或聲譽。若談一張角色圖像，image 又指圖片，需看語境。","point":"Visible costume details and public reputation are different referents."},{"word":"appearance / understanding a character","zh":"中文辨析： 原文把外觀是否像角色和是否理解角色並列；扮相準確不證明熟悉人物設定，反之亦然。","point":"Visual fidelity and knowledge of the role are separate judgments."},{"word":"costume / full appearance","zh":"中文辨析： Costume 是服裝；來源的外觀還可能涉及假髮、妝容、道具等。不能因服裝吻合便稱整體扮相必然準確。","point":"A costume is one component of a cosplayer’s overall look."},{"word":"outward form / visual style","zh":"中文辨析： Outward form 偏形狀輪廓，visual style 偏美術風格；若原畫重在顏色、配件等細節，兩者不能自動代替外觀是否準確。","point":"General form and style may miss exact character-design details."},{"word":"presentation / resemblance","zh":"中文辨析： 造型呈現可以漂亮，但與指定角色未必相似。Visual resemblance 必須指定比較對象；visual presentation 不必。","point":"A polished presentation need not be a faithful likeness."}],"moduleNumber":43},{"id":"lesson-044","sourceId":87,"headword":"application","title":"Application","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2016 Paper 4 set 3.1 article introduces “four educational computer software applications” and discusses buying apps for school tablets. This explicitly identifies the software sense. The local mapping note about handwritten forms belongs to another sense and is contradicted by the passage. [2016 Paper 4, set 3.1](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2016-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2016 Paper 4 set 3.1 article introduces “four educational computer software applications” and discusses buying apps for school tablets. This explicitly identifies the software sense. The local mapping note about handwritten forms belongs to another sense and is contradicted by the passage. [2016 Paper 4, set 3.1](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2016-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["form","False: a document to fill in; the source names software for tablets."],["request form","False: administrative document, not learning software."],["written submission","False: student work or application document, not a program."],["apps","Close common shortened form of software applications; the source uses both."],["software tools","Contextual broad phrase for programs used for particular study tasks; not every software tool is a student-facing app."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Educational apps adds the passage’s school-purpose restriction and is taught. Computer/software programs is a broader valid countable substitute when installed functionality is clear; that broad paraphrase is developed in 0082 app, while this entry teaches the mapped functional recast software tools and the educational qualifier. Learning platforms can include a website, accounts, data and services beyond one application; not a direct synonym. Study resources may be books or worksheets. Applets often means small embedded programs and is not the normal term here. Application forms are a predictable false sense."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["需要表達","選擇"],"rows":[["日常簡稱一款程式","app(s)"],["明說教學或學習用途","educational app(s)"],["強調程式用來完成具體任務","software tool(s)"]],"note":"2016 原文明寫 computer software applications，所以原映射中的 form/request form/written submission 必須排除；不要再把這一課做成申請表練習。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"apps","meaning":"應用程式（簡稱）","note":"Applications 的常用縮寫；可數，源文正以 apps 談供學生使用的軟件。","collocations":"download apps; buy apps for tablets; use an app for revision.","example":"The club tested two apps for revising vocabulary on the school tablets.","exampleZh":"電腦學會在學校平板上測試了兩款溫習詞彙的應用程式。","contrast":"App 是軟件，不是申請表；此外，縮寫較口語，正式首次提及時可用 application。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school installed four applications on its tablets so pupils could revise formulas and vocabulary.","zh":"學校在平板電腦安裝了四款應用程式，讓學生溫習公式和詞彙。","upgrade":"The school installed four apps on its tablets so pupils could revise formulas and vocabulary.","answer":"apps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"apps","explanation":"四款可在平板上安裝、供溫習的軟件，日常可稱 apps。"},{"letter":"B","text":"application forms","explanation":"申請表是文件，不會作為四款溫習工具安裝。"},{"letter":"C","text":"online accounts","explanation":"帳戶讓學生登入服務，不是安裝在平板上的四款程式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"study files","explanation":"檔案可載有筆記，但原句說的是可安裝的軟件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"school portals","explanation":"入口網站也可能供學習，但未必是安裝到每部平板的程式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"software licences","explanation":"軟件授權決定使用權，與可直接溫習的四款程式不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A teacher compared the applications that give audio feedback when students practise pronunciation.","zh":"老師比較學生練習發音時會提供語音回饋的應用程式。","upgrade":"A teacher compared the apps that give audio feedback when students practise pronunciation.","answer":"apps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"spoken recordings","explanation":"錄音是程式可能播放的內容，未必會分析並回饋學生發音。"},{"letter":"B","text":"subscription plans","explanation":"訂閱計劃是付款安排，不是老師比較的回饋工具。"},{"letter":"C","text":"application forms","explanation":"申請表不能聽學生發音並回饋。"},{"letter":"D","text":"apps","explanation":"能在練習時提供語音回饋的軟件，簡稱 apps。"},{"letter":"E","text":"online profiles","explanation":"個人頁面記錄資料，未必有發音練習功能。"},{"letter":"F","text":"audio files","explanation":"音檔可播放聲音，卻不是提供互動回饋的完整程式。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"educational apps","meaning":"教育應用程式","note":"明確指出軟件的教學或學習用途；來源的四款程式屬此類，並非所有 app 都是教育 app。","collocations":"educational apps for tablets; choose educational apps; evaluate educational apps.","example":"The librarian recommended educational apps that help pupils practise reading.","exampleZh":"圖書館員推薦了幫助學生練習閱讀的教育應用程式。","contrast":"Educational 是用途限定；遊戲或社交程式不能只因學生使用便歸為教育軟件。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The applications in the school’s shortlist all taught maths or languages and were evaluated for classroom use.","zh":"學校候選清單上的應用程式都教授數學或語言，並經評估供課堂使用。","upgrade":"The educational apps in the school’s shortlist all taught maths or languages and were evaluated for classroom use.","answer":"educational apps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"student accounts","explanation":"學生帳戶是登入身分，並非教授數學或語言的軟件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"class schedules","explanation":"課表安排時間，不等於教授數學與語言的互動程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"educational apps","explanation":"每款程式都以教學為目的，educational apps 把來源的用途保留下來。"},{"letter":"D","text":"learning platforms","explanation":"學習平台可能包含網站、帳戶及多種服務；句中列的是逐款評估的應用程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"application packets","explanation":"申請文件組合不會教授兩科。"},{"letter":"F","text":"general entertainment apps","explanation":"娛樂程式不因被學校列出就自動成為教學軟件。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Parents checked whether the applications for reading practice had adjustable text sizes for younger pupils.","zh":"家長查看用於閱讀練習的應用程式，是否可以調整字體大小以方便較年幼的學生。","upgrade":"Parents checked whether the educational apps for reading practice had adjustable text sizes for younger pupils.","answer":"educational apps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reading assessments","explanation":"閱讀評估是測試活動，不能概括家長檢查的可調字體程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"digital textbooks","explanation":"電子課本可有字體設定，但原句說可供練習的多款應用程式，不只是課本。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school forms","explanation":"學校表格可有文字，卻不是閱讀練習軟件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"web subscriptions","explanation":"網站訂閱是服務權限，非家長逐款檢查字體設定的程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tablet settings","explanation":"平板系統字體設定可能影響顯示，但原句說的是應用程式各自的功能。"},{"letter":"F","text":"educational apps","explanation":"有閱讀練習功能的應用程式，educational apps 指明其學習用途。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"software tools","meaning":"軟件工具","note":"從功能角度稱可用來完成學習任務的程式；比 application 廣，須在句中指明可安裝或使用的具體功能。","collocations":"software tools for studying; compare software tools; use a software tool to organise homework.","example":"The students compared software tools for organising deadlines and revision notes.","exampleZh":"學生比較了用來整理限期和溫習筆記的軟件工具。","contrast":"Tool 也可指網站功能或系統模組；只有上下文清楚時才概括一款應用程式。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The applications helped students organise homework deadlines and send reminders on their tablets.","zh":"這些應用程式幫助學生在平板上整理功課限期並發出提醒。","upgrade":"The software tools helped students organise homework deadlines and send reminders on their tablets.","answer":"software tools","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"timetable entries","explanation":"時間表項目是被整理的資料，不是整理資料並提醒的程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"software tools","explanation":"原句交代了整理與提醒功能，software tools 可從工具用途概括這些程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"study instructions","explanation":"學習指示告訴學生做甚麼，不會自行處理限期及發提醒。"},{"letter":"D","text":"notification sounds","explanation":"提示音只是提醒的一部分，不能整理功課。"},{"letter":"E","text":"online lessons","explanation":"網上課堂可提供教學內容，不是此處的功課管理工具。"},{"letter":"F","text":"device accounts","explanation":"裝置帳戶識別使用者，不負責題句兩項具體功能。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A student with limited storage asked which applications could solve equations without saving large video files.","zh":"一名儲存空間有限的學生，詢問哪些應用程式能解方程式而不用儲存大型影片檔。","upgrade":"A student with limited storage asked which software tools could solve equations without saving large video files.","answer":"software tools","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worked examples","explanation":"例題可展示解法，但不會像程式般替學生處理新方程。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cloud accounts","explanation":"雲端帳戶能存資料，未說它本身會解方程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"video lessons","explanation":"影片課可教人解題，卻與避開大型影片檔的限制相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"storage plans","explanation":"儲存方案改善容量，不是解方程式的程式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"software tools","explanation":"題句要找能解方程式的程式工具，software tools 保留其功能。"},{"letter":"F","text":"written formulas","explanation":"紙上公式是資料，不是會計算輸入方程的軟件。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"software application / application form","zh":"中文辨析： 原文有電腦平板、程式功能與購買 app 的語境。Form、request form、written submission 是另一個「申請」詞義，不能安裝到平板。","point":"The source explicitly labels these applications computer software."},{"word":"app / account / licence","zh":"中文辨析： App 是程式，account 是使用者身分，licence 是使用權；有帳戶或授權不等於有某款程式。","point":"Access credentials and permission are not the software product."},{"word":"educational app / entertainment app","zh":"中文辨析： 學生可用娛樂程式，但來源特別說教育軟件。Educational 應由學習用途支持，不是由使用者年齡決定。","point":"The educational label describes the program’s learning function."},{"word":"software tool / platform","zh":"中文辨析： Software tool 可指一項程式功能，platform 可包括網站、帳戶及後台服務。談單款可安裝應用程式時，要小心範圍。","point":"A platform may contain or host several software tools and apps."},{"word":"program / worksheet / file","zh":"中文辨析： 程式可運行並處理輸入；工作紙和資料檔是學習材料，即使在平板上顯示也不自動成為應用程式。","point":"A file is content, while an application executes functions."}],"moduleNumber":44},{"id":"lesson-045","sourceId":14,"headword":"account","title":"Account","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2016 phone-scam article refers to hacked e-mail accounts whose owners’ contacts receive fraudulent pleas for money. Account means a digital sign-in identity with email functions, not a bank balance, a display profile, or an address alone.","sourceSense":"The 2016 phone-scam article refers to hacked e-mail accounts whose owners’ contacts receive fraudulent pleas for money. Account means a digital sign-in identity with email functions, not a bank balance, a display profile, or an address alone.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["user profile","false: visible profile is not the sign-in account"],["online account","contextual: broader than email account"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Mailbox 側重收件箱而非完整登入身分；login 可指登入程序或憑證，不等於帳戶。兩者在特定句子可改寫，但不作源句同義詞。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["e-mail account","特指電郵服務的登入身分，可收發訊息；與來源最吻合。","改寫時須保留電郵服務，不能泛化成任何網上帳戶。"],["online account","登入互聯網服務的身分，比電郵帳戶範圍廣；句子須另交代是電郵。","若刪去 used for email，會失去原文的服務種類。"],["user account","系統為某位用戶建立的登入身分；在郵件平台語境可用，但必須保留平台。","單說 user account 可能是任何系統，需加上 on the email service。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 原文的被盜帳戶是 e-mail account，最精確；online account 只說帳戶在網上，範圍較大；user account 着重平台分配給一名使用者的登入身分。E-mail address 是地址，mailbox 是信箱，login credentials 是登入資料，均非整個帳戶。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"e-mail account","meaning":"電郵帳戶","note":"特指電郵服務的登入身分，可收發訊息；與來源最吻合。","collocations":"a hacked e-mail account; access an e-mail account.","example":"The student secured her e-mail account after an unfamiliar login.","exampleZh":"學生發現陌生登入後加強保護電郵帳戶。","contrast":"改寫時須保留電郵服務，不能泛化成任何網上帳戶。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The scammer gained control of an account used to send the victim’s e-mails.","zh":"騙徒控制了用來寄出受害人電郵的帳戶。","upgrade":"The scammer gained control of the victim’s e-mail account.","answer":"e-mail account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"e-mail account","explanation":"E-mail account 直接指出被盜的是電郵登入帳戶。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bank account","explanation":"銀行戶口不能寄出受害人的電郵。"},{"letter":"C","text":"user profile","explanation":"可見資料頁不等於完整寄信登入身分。"},{"letter":"D","text":"email address","explanation":"知道地址不代表控制了可寄信的帳戶。"},{"letter":"E","text":"mailbox","explanation":"收件箱只是一項功能，未必包括整個登入帳戶。"},{"letter":"F","text":"login credentials","explanation":"憑證可用來登入，卻不是被控制的帳戶本身。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"She opened an account for e-mail so she could send her application to the museum.","zh":"她開設了一個電郵帳戶，以便把申請寄往博物館。","upgrade":"She opened an e-mail account so she could send her application to the museum.","answer":"e-mail account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"user profile","explanation":"個人資料頁可顯示姓名，卻未必能用來向博物館寄電郵。"},{"letter":"B","text":"email address","explanation":"地址是寄信時使用的識別字串；她開設的是整個服務帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mailbox","explanation":"信箱是郵件儲存區，不能概括新開帳戶的登入和寄送功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"password","explanation":"開設服務會設定密碼，但密碼本身不是電郵帳戶。"},{"letter":"E","text":"contact list","explanation":"通訊錄可儲存博物館地址，卻不能單獨寄出申請。"},{"letter":"F","text":"e-mail account","explanation":"E-mail account 指她新開、可用來寄出申請的電郵服務帳戶。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"online account","meaning":"網上帳戶","note":"登入互聯網服務的身分，比電郵帳戶範圍廣；句子須另交代是電郵。","collocations":"protect an online account; online account used for email.","example":"The phishing message tried to take over an online account used for email.","exampleZh":"釣魚訊息企圖盜取一個用於電郵的網上帳戶。","contrast":"若刪去 used for email，會失去原文的服務種類。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The account she used for email was one of several accounts she managed online.","zh":"她用作電郵的帳戶，是她使用的多項網上服務之一。","upgrade":"The online account she used for email was one of several accounts she managed.","answer":"online account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"bank account","explanation":"即使也是網上服務，仍與句中電郵用途不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"user profile","explanation":"可見檔案不等於登入服務的帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","text":"online account","explanation":"Online account 是上位類別；used for email 補回原本的特定功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"email address","explanation":"地址不足以表示一個有功能的網上帳戶。"},{"letter":"E","text":"mailbox","explanation":"收件箱是較窄的郵件區域，不是完整帳戶。"},{"letter":"F","text":"login details","explanation":"登入資料不是她所使用的服務帳戶本身。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The student could sign in to the account she used for e-mail through a web browser on any school computer.","zh":"學生可在學校任何一部電腦上，透過瀏覽器登入她的電郵帳戶。","upgrade":"The student could use a web browser on any school computer to sign in to her online account for e-mail.","answer":"online account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"email address","explanation":"地址只能識別郵件去向，不能作為可從各電腦登入的整個服務帳戶。"},{"letter":"B","text":"user profile","explanation":"個人資料頁不保證可經瀏覽器登入及使用電郵服務。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mailbox","explanation":"收件箱是帳戶功能之一，不能概括網上登入身分。"},{"letter":"D","text":"online account","explanation":"Online account 表示可從瀏覽器登入的網上帳戶；句中 used for e-mail 保留服務種類。"},{"letter":"E","text":"login credentials","explanation":"登入資料供學生使用，並非她登入後使用的帳戶本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"contact list","explanation":"通訊錄存聯絡人，不能單靠它登入電郵服務。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"user account","meaning":"用戶帳戶","note":"系統為某位用戶建立的登入身分；在郵件平台語境可用，但必須保留平台。","collocations":"create a user account; user account on the mail service.","example":"The school disabled the user account on its email service.","exampleZh":"學校停用了電郵服務中的用戶帳戶。","contrast":"單說 user account 可能是任何系統，需加上 on the email service。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The account assigned to that user on the mail platform was disabled after the breach.","zh":"資料外洩後，郵件平台上分配給該用戶的帳戶被停用。","upgrade":"The user account on the mail platform was disabled after the breach.","answer":"user account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"user profile","explanation":"資料頁不等於郵件平台可停用的登入身分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"user account","explanation":"User account 是系統登入身分，mail platform 保留電郵範圍。"},{"letter":"C","text":"email address","explanation":"地址是帳戶識別資訊，不是完整使用權限。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mailbox","explanation":"收件箱不涵蓋所有用戶登入設定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"login details","explanation":"登入資料與被停用的帳戶不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"contact card","explanation":"通訊錄中的人名卡片不是平台帳戶。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The help desk created an account for each new employee on the company e-mail system and issued separate login details.","zh":"服務台在公司電郵系統為每名新員工建立帳戶，並發出各自的登入資料。","upgrade":"The help desk created a user account for each new employee on the company e-mail system and issued separate login details.","answer":"user account","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"user profile","explanation":"服務台要為新員工建立可登入的系統身分，不只是展示個人資料頁。"},{"letter":"B","text":"email address","explanation":"電郵地址可隨帳戶發給員工，但不包括系統登入權限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mailbox","explanation":"收件箱只是帳戶中的郵件儲存功能，不能概括建立用戶身分。"},{"letter":"D","text":"login details","explanation":"句子把帳戶和另行發出的登入資料分開，兩者不可混同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"user account","explanation":"User account 指服務台在公司電郵系統為每名員工開立的登入身分。"},{"letter":"F","text":"contact entry","explanation":"通訊錄中的員工條目不提供系統登入權限。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"user profile / account","zh":"中文辨析： Profile 是可見的個人資料頁，不等於可登入寄信的帳戶。","point":"A profile page is not the full sign-in identity."},{"word":"email address / email account","zh":"中文辨析： 地址是收發信識別字串；帳戶包括登入憑證及服務功能。","point":"Knowing an address does not mean controlling an account."},{"word":"bank account / email account","zh":"中文辨析： 兩者都是 account，但銀行戶口不能用來寄詐騙電郵。","point":"Keep the service type when the source specifies email."},{"word":"mailbox / account","zh":"中文辨析： Mailbox 主要指收件箱或郵件儲存區；帳戶還包括登入和設定。","point":"A mailbox can be part of an email account."}],"moduleNumber":45},{"id":"lesson-046","sourceId":3,"headword":"a number of","title":"A Number Of","titleZh":"若干個；多個","subtitle":"若干個；多個","description":"2017 年 DSE Speaking 2.3〈Too Many Signals?〉說某項服務以前 had a number of roles，其中最重要的是提供準確天氣觀測和颱風警告。A number of 在這裏修飾複數可數名詞 roles，表示「有若干職能」，沒有給確切數目，也不必然說數目龐大。Had 是複數賓語前的動詞，不涉及「數目」作主語的單複數問題。","sourceSense":"2017 年 DSE Speaking 2.3〈Too Many Signals?〉說某項服務以前 had a number of roles，其中最重要的是提供準確天氣觀測和颱風警告。A number of 在這裏修飾複數可數名詞 roles，表示「有若干職能」，沒有給確切數目，也不必然說數目龐大。Had 是複數賓語前的動詞，不涉及「數目」作主語的單複數問題。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["several","近義","可表數個職能，通常暗示數目不大，需有複數可數名詞。"],["multiple","語境近義","強調同一服務有不止一項不同功能；數量未必很多。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["想強調甚麼","選擇"],"rows":[["只有幾項、數目不大","several roles"],["同一機構不只做一件事","multiple roles"],["職能的種類不同","various roles"],["工作橫跨不同範疇","a range of roles"]],"note":"快選規則： 先看 roles 是可數複數，再問句子重點是數量、超過一項、種類差異，還是範疇跨度。The number of roles 問「總數是多少」，不是原文「有若干職能」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Several","meaning":"好幾個","note":"表示不確定但相對有限的複數數量；在職能數目只有幾項時相當貼近原句。","collocations":"several roles / duties / functions; serve several purposes.","example":"The weather office performed several roles, including issuing warnings.","exampleZh":"氣象部門有好幾項職能，包括發出警告。","contrast":"Several 不報確切數目，也不表示「很多很多」；後面須接複數可數名詞。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The station had a number of roles: it measured rainfall, issued warnings and archived records.","zh":"該站有若干職能：測量雨量、發出警告及保存紀錄。","upgrade":"The station had several roles: it measured rainfall, issued warnings and archived records.","answer":"several","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"numerous","explanation":"句中只列三項職能；numerous 暗示數量很多，比已知數目誇大。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the number of","explanation":"The number of 指數目本身，後面不能在此保持 had ... roles 的意思。"},{"letter":"C","text":"several","explanation":"列出的三項職能支持「好幾項」，且直接接複數名詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"few","explanation":"Few 暗示職能少得不足，原句沒有這層評價。"},{"letter":"E","text":"much","explanation":"Much 只能修飾不可數名詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a couple of","explanation":"句中明列量度雨量、發警告和存檔三項，a couple of 通常只指兩項。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A number of the event team's six roles were behind the scenes—registration, equipment checks and record keeping—while the other three involved visitors.","zh":"活動團隊的六項職務中有幾項屬幕後工作——登記、檢查器材和保存紀錄；另外三項則要接觸訪客。","upgrade":"Several of the event team's six roles were behind the scenes—registration, equipment checks and record keeping—while the other three involved visitors.","answer":"several of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"most of","explanation":"六項中只有三項在幕後，恰好一半，不能說「大部分」。"},{"letter":"B","text":"several of","explanation":"三項屬於明確的六項職務之中，須用 several of the six roles 的部分結構。"},{"letter":"C","text":"all of","explanation":"另外三項要接觸訪客，幕後工作不可能是全部六項。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a couple of","explanation":"A couple of 通常指兩項，少於列明的三項幕後工作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"much of","explanation":"Roles 是可數複數，不能用 much of 來指三項職務。"},{"letter":"F","text":"numerous of","explanation":"Numerous of the roles 不是自然結構；即使改成 numerous roles，三項也不足稱為眾多。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Multiple","meaning":"多個；不止一項","note":"強調同一服務、人或事物有兩種或以上分立的職能，不一定說很多。","collocations":"multiple roles / purposes / functions; serve multiple purposes.","example":"The centre has multiple roles: it teaches skills and offers emergency shelter.","exampleZh":"中心有多項職能：教授技能，也提供緊急庇護。","contrast":"Multiple 著重「不只一個」，various 著重種類差異；在職能清單中兩者可能重疊，練習會用清楚的語境分開。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The warning system had a number of roles, issuing alerts and collecting weather readings.","zh":"該警報系統有多項職能，包括發出警報及收集天氣讀數。","upgrade":"The warning system had multiple roles, issuing alerts and collecting weather readings.","answer":"multiple","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"multiple","explanation":"明確強調同一系統有多於一項職能，與 roles 搭配。"},{"letter":"B","text":"multiplication","explanation":"Multiplication 是數學上的乘法或增加過程，不是修飾職能的形容詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a series of","explanation":"發警報及收集讀數是系統的職能，不是依次完成的一連串階段。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a quantity of","explanation":"A quantity of 不自然地描述一項服務的職能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"single","explanation":"Single 表示只有一項，與原句相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"numerous","explanation":"只列發警報與收集讀數兩項職能，numerous 的『眾多』超出數量。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the storm, the old signal played a number of roles at once: it reported weather to residents while telling ships when to seek shelter.","zh":"暴風雨期間，舊訊號同時肩負多項職能：向居民報告天氣，又告知船隻何時避風。","upgrade":"During the storm, the old signal played multiple roles at once: it reported weather to residents while telling ships when to seek shelter.","answer":"multiple","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a series of","explanation":"報告天氣與提醒船隻同時發生，並非依次完成的程序。"},{"letter":"B","text":"multiple","explanation":"At once 和 while 表明同一訊號同時肩負兩項職能，play multiple roles 搭配自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"multiples","explanation":"Multiples 是複數名詞，不能作此處的形容詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"less","explanation":"Less 不是可直接描述這些複數職能的量詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"one","explanation":"One 與明示的兩項職能矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"many","explanation":"句中明列同時進行的兩項職能，many 把數目誇大。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Various","meaning":"各種不同的","note":"當句子列出性質不同的職能時，強調種類差異；數量本身不必很大。","collocations":"various roles / duties / functions; serve various needs.","example":"The observatory performed various roles, from gathering data to warning the public.","exampleZh":"天文台履行多種不同職能，由收集資料到警告公眾。","contrast":"Various 不是「數量龐大」；也不要把它與 varying（在變動／程度不一）混同。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The agency had a number of roles, ranging from scientific observation to public education.","zh":"該機構有若干不同職能，由科學觀測到公眾教育。","upgrade":"The agency had various roles, ranging from scientific observation to public education.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"various","explanation":"不同範疇的職能正好支持 various roles。"},{"letter":"B","text":"changing","explanation":"機構兼具觀測與教育工作，句子未說它的職能正隨時間改變。"},{"letter":"C","text":"variable","explanation":"Variable 常指可變數值或不固定性，不自然修飾此處職能清單。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"句子展示跨類別職能，沒有證明職能數目眾多。"},{"letter":"E","text":"variety","explanation":"Variety 是名詞，若用須改為 a variety of roles。"},{"letter":"F","text":"identical","explanation":"科學觀測與公眾教育性質不同，不能說是相同職能。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The festival invited volunteers to apply for a number of roles, including interpreting, managing queues and operating lights.","zh":"文化節邀請義工申請不同崗位，包括傳譯、管理人龍和操作燈光。","upgrade":"The festival invited volunteers to apply for various roles, including interpreting, managing queues and operating lights.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"variation","explanation":"Variation 是名詞，不可直接修飾 roles。"},{"letter":"B","text":"various","explanation":"傳譯、管理人龍和燈光操作是性質不同的崗位，apply for various roles 自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"vary","explanation":"Vary 是動詞，不能放在名詞 roles 前。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"節目只舉三種崗位，沒有足夠依據稱為『眾多』。"},{"letter":"E","text":"identical","explanation":"傳譯、人龍管理與燈光操作工作不同，不能說崗位相同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an amount of","explanation":"An amount of 不可直接用於可數職能。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"A Range Of","meaning":"不同範疇的若干種","note":"強調職能橫跨不同範疇，適用於句子明示跨度的情況；比單純計數多一層「範圍」意思。","collocations":"a range of roles / services / functions; a range of duties from A to B.","example":"The public office performs a range of roles, from data collection to emergency advice.","exampleZh":"該公共機構處理不同範疇的職能，由收集資料到提供緊急建議。","contrast":"A range of 後接複數可數 roles；若原文只說有兩個相同類型的工作，未必需要強調範疇。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The observatory had a number of roles, from collecting scientific data to warning residents during storms.","zh":"天文台有若干職能，由收集科學數據到暴風雨期間警告居民。","upgrade":"The observatory had a range of roles, from collecting scientific data to warning residents during storms.","answer":"a range of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a series of","explanation":"資料收集與風暴警報是不同職能，並非必須依次完成的程序。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a range of","explanation":"From ... to ... 展示工作範疇的跨度，適合 a range of。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a range","explanation":"缺少 of，不能直接接 roles。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a number","explanation":"缺少 of，這個量詞片語不完整。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the range of","explanation":"The range of 指已特定的範圍，與句中首次介紹一系列職能的 had 搭配較不自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a multitude of","explanation":"原句只舉兩個跨度端點，沒有說職能數量龐大。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school performed a number of roles in the neighbourhood: it taught children, hosted weekend meetings and opened its hall as an emergency shelter.","zh":"學校在社區扮演多種角色：平日教導兒童，週末舉辦會議，並在緊急情況開放禮堂作庇護所。","upgrade":"The school performed a range of roles in the neighbourhood: it taught children, hosted weekend meetings and opened its hall as an emergency shelter.","answer":"a range of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a range of","explanation":"教育、社區活動及緊急庇護橫跨不同範疇，performed a range of roles 自然概括。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a series of","explanation":"三種職能隨需要提供，並非必須按一條預設次序完成。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a range","explanation":"缺少 of，片語不能直接接 roles。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a little","explanation":"A little 修飾不可數事物，不合複數職能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"one kind of","explanation":"One kind of 縮為一類，與兩種差異甚大的職能不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a multitude of","explanation":"列出的三種職能足以顯示跨度，卻沒有證據說數量龐大。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"a number of / the number of：主語一致","zh":"A number of roles are... 把職能視作複數；The number of roles is... 把「數目」視作單數。原文說服務「有若干職能」，不是在報告職能的總數。","point":"A number of plus a plural noun refers to the items; the number of refers to the count itself."},{"word":"number / amount：可數性","zh":"Roles 是可數複數，故可說 a number of roles；an amount of roles 不自然。不可數 information 則可說 an amount of information，不說 a number of information。","point":"Use number with countable plurals and amount with uncountable mass nouns."},{"word":"a few / few：語氣","zh":"A few roles 是「有幾項」，可作中性或正面陳述；few roles 常暗示「寥寥無幾／不足」。原文沒有說職能不足，不可把冠詞刪掉。","point":"A few asserts some exist; few often stresses scarcity."},{"word":"several / numerous：數量強度","zh":"Several 常指相對少量的幾項；numerous 明顯強調很多。原文只寫 a number of，沒有證據說職能極多。","point":"Numerous adds a stronger large-count claim than the source supplies."},{"word":"multiple / various / varying：重點","zh":"Multiple roles 強調多於一項；various roles 強調類型不同；varying roles 可指角色隨情況改變。原文列舉不同職能時前兩者可用，但不能無故說它們「正在改變」。","point":"Multiple marks plurality, various diversity, and varying change or differences in degree."}],"moduleNumber":46},{"id":"lesson-047","sourceId":5,"headword":"a variety of","title":"A Variety Of","titleZh":"多種不同科目","subtitle":"多種不同科目","description":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 9.3〈Study Time to Keep Kids Off the Streets〉說義工協助孩子學習 a variety of subjects，並舉英語及印尼語詞語翻譯活動為例。此處 subjects 是學校科目／學習領域，a variety of 表示不只一種；原文沒有證明所有科目都有輔導，也沒有給確切數目。0004 的 a range of 修飾遊學活動，本課則要檢查「科目種類」與「實際輔導範圍」的差別。","sourceSense":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 9.3〈Study Time to Keep Kids Off the Streets〉說義工協助孩子學習 a variety of subjects，並舉英語及印尼語詞語翻譯活動為例。此處 subjects 是學校科目／學習領域，a variety of 表示不只一種；原文沒有證明所有科目都有輔導，也沒有給確切數目。0004 的 a range of 修飾遊學活動，本課則要檢查「科目種類」與「實際輔導範圍」的差別。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["various","近義","Various subjects 可直接指不同科目，不加 of。"],["a range of","有條件近義","A range of subjects 強調跨科目範疇；源文只有例子，不能自行加 wide 誇大覆蓋。"],["different kinds of","有條件改寫","可明示科目類型，但 different kinds of subjects 略笨重；在面向初學者的解釋中，或改寫為 different kinds of schoolwork 更自然。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["語境焦點","較合適說法"],"rows":[["簡潔說不同類別（原文為科目）","various subjects / vegetables"],["由一類延伸到另一類的涵蓋範圍","a range of subjects / services"],["明說分類不同","different kinds of subjects / plants"],["只需說超過一項","multiple subjects / teas"],["類別差異顯著","diverse subjects / performers"]],"note":"快選規則： 先分清「不只一項」和「項目間差異大」。Multiple 只保證多於一；diverse 需有明顯跨類別證據。與 0004 一樣，range 需要範疇線索，不能憑一兩個同類例子加 wide。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Various","meaning":"不同的；各種的","note":"最簡潔地說義工幫忙不止一個科目類別，直接放在複數 subjects 前。","collocations":"various subjects / courses / school activities; help with various subjects.","example":"The volunteers help pupils with various subjects after school.","exampleZh":"義工放學後協助學生學習不同科目。","contrast":"Various 不帶 of，也不保證涵蓋每個科目；不要誤寫為 varying。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Volunteers help children with a variety of subjects, including English and art.","zh":"義工協助孩子學習多種科目，包括英語和美術。","upgrade":"Volunteers help children with various subjects, including English and art.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"variety","explanation":"Variety 是名詞，不能直接修飾 subjects。"},{"letter":"B","text":"numerous","explanation":"句中舉英語和美術兩科，numerous 的數量判斷過強；重點是科目不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"various","explanation":"英語與美術屬不同科目，various 是合適的簡短形容詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"diversity","explanation":"Diversity 是名詞，不是這裏需要的形容詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only one","explanation":"句中明列英語和美術兩科，only one 與事實不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"similar","explanation":"英語與美術不是相似科目；原句重點在不同學科。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The community garden grows a variety of vegetables, from leafy greens to root crops.","zh":"社區花園種植多種蔬菜，從葉菜到根莖類都有。","upgrade":"The community garden grows various vegetables, from leafy greens to root crops.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"various","explanation":"葉菜與根莖類是不同蔬菜種類；various 可直接修飾複數 vegetables。"},{"letter":"B","text":"numerous","explanation":"句子說種類不同，沒有給出大量蔬菜或植株的數目，numerous 會轉移焦點。"},{"letter":"C","text":"variation","explanation":"Variation 是名詞，不能直接放在複數 vegetables 前作這裏的形容詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"vary","explanation":"Vary 是動詞，不能填入 vegetables 前的形容詞位置。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a series of","explanation":"蔬菜類別同時種在花園，不是一件接一件的連續事件。"},{"letter":"F","text":"only one","explanation":"花園至少有葉菜與根莖兩類，不能說只種一種。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"A Range Of","meaning":"涵蓋若干科目的","note":"強調輔導橫跨不同科目範疇；若句子列出語文、科學、藝術，更能支持這種跨度。","collocations":"a range of subjects / disciplines / courses; cover a range of subjects.","example":"The centre offers tutoring in a range of subjects, from languages to science.","exampleZh":"中心提供不同科目的輔導，範圍由語文到科學。","contrast":"不要自動加 wide；只有例子確實跨得廣時才可說 a wide range of。0004 是活動選擇，這裏是學習領域。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The volunteers help with a variety of subjects, from languages to mathematics and science.","zh":"義工輔導多個科目，由語文到數學和科學。","upgrade":"The volunteers help with a range of subjects, from languages to mathematics and science.","answer":"a range of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a series of","explanation":"志願者可協助多個學科，並沒有要求按語言、數學、科學的順序教授。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a range of","explanation":"From ... to ... 顯示跨領域範圍，適合此片語。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an amount of","explanation":"An amount of 不修飾複數可數 subjects。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"語言、數學和科學是可同時支援的學科，並非必須依序完成。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a grade of","explanation":"A grade of 指級別。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a range for","explanation":"Range 後接被涵蓋的科目時須用 of；for 不能直接替代這個介詞。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The community clinic offers a variety of services, from vaccinations and nutrition advice to physical therapy.","zh":"社區診所提供多種服務，從疫苗接種、營養建議到物理治療都有。","upgrade":"The community clinic offers a range of services, from vaccinations and nutrition advice to physical therapy.","answer":"a range of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a range of","explanation":"由疫苗接種到物理治療，a range of 準確表達診所服務跨越不同類別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a range for","explanation":"Range 要用 of 連接所涵蓋的複數服務；for 不能直接放在此處。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an amount of","explanation":"Services 是可數複數，不能用計算不可數數量的 an amount of。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the amount of","explanation":"The amount of 也不合複數可數 services，更沒有表達服務類別的跨度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a series of","explanation":"三類服務不是必須按接種、建議、治療的順序完成的連續步驟。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a level of","explanation":"Level 指程度或服務水準，不能指診所提供的多種服務類別。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Different Kinds Of","meaning":"不同種類的（說明式）","note":"把「科目種類不同」說得非常明白，適合教學解說；與 subjects 連用稍長，可視句子改成 different kinds of schoolwork。","collocations":"different kinds of subjects / schoolwork; different kinds of lessons.","example":"The volunteers help pupils with different kinds of schoolwork, from reading to basic science.","exampleZh":"義工教授不同類型的課業，由閱讀到基礎科學。","contrast":"必須用複數 kinds 表示多類，並保留 of；改成 schoolwork 時已從科目名稱轉向課業內容，應向學習者說明。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The volunteers help with a variety of subjects, including languages and science.","zh":"義工輔導多種科目，包括語文和科學。","upgrade":"The volunteers help with different kinds of subjects, including languages and science.","answer":"different kinds of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different kind","explanation":"缺少 of，且單數 kind 不合多個類別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"different kinds of","explanation":"明確說明語文與科學分屬不同科目類型。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one kind of","explanation":"語言與科學分屬不同學科類別，不能說只有一類。"},{"letter":"D","text":"similar","explanation":"語言與科學的內容並不相近，原句特別列出兩種類型。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"語言與科學是不同學科類別，不是必須按順序教授的步驟。"},{"letter":"F","text":"each kind","explanation":"Each kind 指逐類各別描述，不能直接放入此句。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The nature centre groups a variety of plants into trees, shrubs and grasses for its visitor guide.","zh":"自然中心把多種植物分成樹木、灌木和草本植物，編入遊客指南。","upgrade":"The nature centre groups different kinds of plants into trees, shrubs and grasses for its visitor guide.","answer":"different kinds of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different kinds of","explanation":"樹木、灌木和草本植物是不同類別，different kinds of 明確表達分類差異。"},{"letter":"B","text":"several kind of","explanation":"Several 後須用複數 kinds，不能說 several kind of plants。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an amount of","explanation":"Plants 可數，an amount of 不能在此修飾複數植物。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a series of","explanation":"三類植物同時列在指南中，不是前後發生的連續事件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"each kinds of","explanation":"Each kinds of 單複數不合；即使改成 each kind of，也不是這裏的多種類概括。"},{"letter":"F","text":"identical","explanation":"樹木、灌木與草本植物分屬不同類別，不能稱為 identical。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Multiple","meaning":"多於一個的","note":"強調確有不止一個科目，但不必突出它們相差很大；常見於報告式語體。","collocations":"multiple subjects / disciplines / classes; study multiple subjects.","example":"One tutor supported pupils in multiple subjects during the term.","exampleZh":"一名導師在該學期協助學生學習多個科目。","contrast":"Multiple 是數量或多重性；若句子重點是從藝術到科學的差異，various 或 a range of 更清楚。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"One volunteer helps with a variety of language subjects: specifically, English, French and Spanish.","zh":"一名義工協助學生學習不止一門語言科目，具體包括英語、法語和西班牙語。","upgrade":"One volunteer helps with multiple language subjects: specifically, English, French and Spanish.","answer":"multiple","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a wide range of","explanation":"英、法、西三科都屬語言，不能稱學科範圍十分廣泛。"},{"letter":"B","text":"multiple","explanation":"明列三門語言科，multiple 準確表示不止一科。"},{"letter":"C","text":"single","explanation":"Single 只指一科，與列舉三門語言相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"Specifically 只列三科，numerous 會誇大數量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"diverse","explanation":"三科都屬語言，diverse 的跨領域意味沒有證據支持。"},{"letter":"F","text":"multiplied","explanation":"Multiplied 暗示科目經倍增，不是普通的多科。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The café offers a variety of related herbal teas—peppermint, spearmint and lemon balm—but each customer may sample only one.","zh":"咖啡店提供薄荷、留蘭香及香蜂草等數款相近的花草茶，但每位顧客只能試飲其中一款。","upgrade":"The café offers multiple related herbal teas—peppermint, spearmint and lemon balm—but each customer may sample only one.","answer":"multiple","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"single","explanation":"店裏有三款茶；即使每人只可試一款，也不能說咖啡店只提供單一款。"},{"letter":"B","text":"multiple","explanation":"Multiple 說店裏有不止一款，不會把顧客的試飲上限錯當成供應數目。"},{"letter":"C","text":"numerous","explanation":"句中只列三款，numerous 把茶款數量誇大了。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a broad range of","explanation":"三款都是相關花草茶，broad range 誇大了飲品類別的跨度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"multiplied","explanation":"Multiplied 暗示茶款數目經倍增，原句只說同時供應幾款。"},{"letter":"F","text":"diverse","explanation":"三款都屬相近的花草茶，缺乏 diverse 所強調的跨類別差異。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Diverse","meaning":"類別差異大的","note":"比一般「多種」更強調不同科目彼此差異明顯；要有跨領域例子支持。","collocations":"diverse subjects / disciplines; study diverse fields.","example":"The club offers support in diverse subjects, from music to mathematics.","exampleZh":"該學會輔導差異很大的科目，由音樂到數學。","contrast":"只舉英語與印尼語兩種語言活動時，不應自動加上 diverse；跨藝術、語文、科學等才較有根據。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The centre teaches a variety of subjects—music, biology, coding and literature.","zh":"中心教授多種科目，包括音樂、生物、編程及文學。","upgrade":"The centre teaches diverse subjects—music, biology, coding and literature.","answer":"diverse","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"closely related","explanation":"音樂、生物、程式設計和文學橫跨藝術、科學及科技，並非內容相近。"},{"letter":"B","text":"diversity","explanation":"Diversity 是名詞，不能直接作 subjects 的形容詞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"diverse","explanation":"從音樂到編程跨度明顯，diverse 突出類別差異。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"列四科可說有數科，卻不是數量眾多；焦點在科目跨度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"diversely","explanation":"Diversely 是副詞，不能直接修飾 subjects。"},{"letter":"F","text":"similar","explanation":"音樂與生物等領域明顯不同，不能形容為相似科目。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The festival brought together a variety of performers, from street dancers and opera singers to magicians and drummers.","zh":"節日活動匯聚各類表演者，從街舞舞者、歌劇歌手到魔術師和鼓手都有。","upgrade":"The festival brought together diverse performers, from street dancers and opera singers to magicians and drummers.","answer":"diverse","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"diverse","explanation":"街舞、歌劇、魔術與打鼓跨越不同表演類別，diverse 表達這種差異。"},{"letter":"B","text":"closely related","explanation":"舞蹈、歌唱和魔術的形式不同，不能說全部表演者做相近工作。"},{"letter":"C","text":"diversity","explanation":"Diversity 是名詞，不能直接放在 performers 前取代這裏的形容詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"原句列出四種表演類別，重點是類別差異，並未交代有大量表演者。"},{"letter":"E","text":"vary","explanation":"Vary 是動詞，不能直接修飾複數 performers。"},{"letter":"F","text":"uniform","explanation":"節目橫跨街舞、歌劇、魔術與打鼓，並非形式一致。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"various / varying：不同與變動","zh":"Various subjects 指不同科目；varying subjects 易暗示科目隨時間改變。原文只說輔導範圍有多種科目，未說課表每週改動。","point":"Various marks different categories; varying often suggests change or differing degree."},{"word":"a range / a wide range：不要擴大原文","zh":"A range of subjects 可說覆蓋若干學習範疇；a wide range of 更強調很廣，原文單舉語言相關例子，不足以保證廣及數理藝術。","point":"Wide adds a breadth claim requiring evidence."},{"word":"multiple / diverse：數量與差異","zh":"Multiple subjects 只說不止一科；diverse subjects 突出科目彼此差異大。兩科都屬語言也可算多科，但未必足以叫 diverse。","point":"Multiple marks plurality; diverse stresses substantial difference of kind."},{"word":"subjects / topics / objects：學校科目","zh":"原文義工教的是 subjects（如英語），不是隨意談論的 topics，也不是實物 objects。改成 different kinds of schoolwork 時須說清楚是課業，不要移到不相關的話題。","point":"Subjects are curricular areas here, not conversation topics or physical objects."},{"word":"a variety of / the variety of：陳述與比較","zh":"A variety of subjects 指有多種科目；the variety of subjects 把「多樣程度」當成名詞核心，常用於討論它有多廣。後者不可不經改寫就替代原句。","point":"A variety of introduces different items; the variety of names the diversity itself."}],"moduleNumber":47},{"id":"lesson-048","sourceId":4,"headword":"a range of","title":"A Range Of","titleZh":"多種不同的活動","subtitle":"多種不同的活動","description":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 3.2〈Oxford School of English Study Tour Programmes〉的活動介紹說 A range of sporting and recreational activities are provided two afternoons a week。此處 a range of 修飾複數可數的 activities，表示課程提供不同種類的運動與康樂選項；不一定承諾所有活動、固定先後次序或確切數目。原文以複數動詞 are 配合複數活動；改寫時按新句主語和語體檢查一致。","sourceSense":"2012 年 DSE Speaking 3.2〈Oxford School of English Study Tour Programmes〉的活動介紹說 A range of sporting and recreational activities are provided two afternoons a week。此處 a range of 修飾複數可數的 activities，表示課程提供不同種類的運動與康樂選項；不一定承諾所有活動、固定先後次序或確切數目。原文以複數動詞 are 配合複數活動；改寫時按新句主語和語體檢查一致。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["various","近義","直接修飾複數 activities；簡潔表達不同種類，但不明言跨度。"],["a variety of","近義","突顯活動種類的多樣性；與源句最接近的片語之一。"],["an assortment of","有條件","多用於有人選配或擺出的一批不同項目；原文的定期課程表未必是「混合拼盤」，須另有策劃選配的語境。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子重點","表達"],"rows":[["簡潔說活動不同","various activities"],["突出多樣種類","a variety of activities"],["一包／一桌的混合選配","an assortment of games and materials"],["清單供學員挑選","a selection of activities"],["平實說明類型差異","different kinds of activities"]],"note":"快選規則： 原文活動表最接近 various / a variety of。只有出現「配成一批」才用 assortment；只有明說「可從清單挑選」才用 selection。各說法都要跟複數可數名詞自然搭配。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Various","meaning":"各種不同的","note":"簡潔形容詞，直接放在複數可數名詞前，說有不同活動類別，但不特別宣稱範圍很廣。","collocations":"various activities / sports / workshops; choose from various options.","example":"Students tried various activities, including badminton and drama.","exampleZh":"學生嘗試了各種活動，包括羽毛球和話劇。","contrast":"Various 不需 of；不要寫 various of activities。它也不表示所有可能的活動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A range of activities is offered after class, including swimming, drama and drawing.","zh":"課後提供多種活動，包括游泳、話劇和繪畫。","upgrade":"Various activities are offered after class, including swimming, drama and drawing.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"numerous","explanation":"游泳、戲劇及繪畫展示不同類型；numerous 只說數量多，並未帶出類別之別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"various","explanation":"不同種類的三項活動可用單一形容詞 various 概括。"},{"letter":"C","text":"vary","explanation":"Vary 是動詞，不能作此處形容詞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an assortment","explanation":"An assortment 仍須 of，且不像普通課程活動清單。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an increasing number of","explanation":"句子只列游泳、戲劇及繪畫，沒有比較往年，不能推斷活動數目正在增加。"},{"letter":"F","text":"similar","explanation":"游泳、戲劇和繪畫分屬不同類型，不能說活動相似。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the holiday, Leila tried a range of sporting activities, including tennis, hiking and archery, before choosing her favourite.","zh":"假期期間，莉娜嘗試了網球、遠足和射箭等不同體育活動，然後才選出最喜歡的一項。","upgrade":"During the holiday, Leila tried various sporting activities, including tennis, hiking and archery, before choosing her favourite.","answer":"various","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"numerous","explanation":"莉娜只試了所列三項，numerous 暗示數量遠多於此。"},{"letter":"B","text":"assortment","explanation":"Assortment 是名詞，不能直接修飾這裏的 activities。"},{"letter":"C","text":"various","explanation":"網球、遠足和射箭是不同活動，形容詞可直接放在 sporting activities 前。"},{"letter":"D","text":"varying of","explanation":"Varying of 不能以這種形式修飾活動名詞。"},{"letter":"E","text":"seasonal","explanation":"假期期間嘗試活動，不等於各運動只在特定季節舉辦。"},{"letter":"F","text":"identical","explanation":"三種運動不同，不能稱為相同活動。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"A Variety Of","meaning":"多種不同的","note":"強調類別多樣，是原文「不同運動及康樂活動」的貼近改寫。","collocations":"a variety of activities / sports / games; offer a variety of options.","example":"The centre offers a variety of activities, from chess to dance.","exampleZh":"中心提供多種活動，由國際象棋到舞蹈都有。","contrast":"A variety of 不表示「全部種類」。後面通常接複數可數名詞；a variety of activity 在此不自然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A range of activities is offered at the centre: football, painting, music and coding.","zh":"中心提供多種活動：足球、繪畫、音樂和編程。","upgrade":"A variety of activities is offered at the centre: football, painting, music and coding.","answer":"a variety of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a series of","explanation":"足球、繪畫、音樂和編程同時供應，句中沒有指它們依次開辦。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an amount of","explanation":"An amount of 不自然地修飾複數可數活動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a variety of","explanation":"四個不同範疇的項目支持「種類多樣」。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a number for","explanation":"要接複數活動應說 a number of；for 不能在這裏連接數量與活動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a wide amount of","explanation":"Amount 通常量度不可數總量，不適合足球、繪畫等可數活動；wide 也不能補救搭配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a load of","explanation":"A load of 是口語數量，未點出類別不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the open day, visitors sampled a range of sporting and recreational activities, from canoeing to theatre games, in any order they liked.","zh":"開放日上，訪客按自己喜歡的次序嘗試不同體育及康樂活動，從獨木舟到戲劇遊戲都有。","upgrade":"At the open day, visitors sampled a variety of sporting and recreational activities, from canoeing to theatre games, in any order they liked.","answer":"a variety of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a variety of","explanation":"開放日讓訪客按喜好試不同類型活動，保留原句的多樣性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a selection for","explanation":"若指供選的活動，須用 a selection of activities；for 不能在此替代 of。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a series of","explanation":"訪客可按任何次序嘗試，series 所暗示的順序不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a programme of","explanation":"開放日可有活動安排，但此說法沒有明示從獨木舟到戲劇的種類差異。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a wide amount of","explanation":"Activities 是可數複數，amount 不合；wide 也不能表示活動種類的正確數量搭配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a number of","explanation":"只說有若干活動，弱化訪客跨體育與戲劇兩類的體驗。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"An Assortment Of","meaning":"一批不同類型的（選配）","note":"須有實際選配或集合的語境，如導師把不同遊戲和材料放在一盒；比原文的定期課程安排更具「混合一批」意味。","collocations":"an assortment of games / materials / activities; put together an assortment of items.","example":"The tutor placed an assortment of games and craft materials on each table.","exampleZh":"導師在每張桌上擺放了一批不同的遊戲及手工材料。","contrast":"源句的 a range of activities 未說活動被配成一批；若只講每週課表，assortment 不是優先選擇。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The tutor prepared a range of games and craft materials for each table, mixing cards, puzzles and drawing kits in one box.","zh":"導師為每張桌子準備了多種遊戲和手工材料，把紙牌、拼圖及繪畫工具混放在一個盒子裏。","upgrade":"The tutor prepared an assortment of games and craft materials for each table, mixing cards, puzzles and drawing kits in one box.","answer":"an assortment of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a variety of","explanation":"這說法可指不同物品，但句子特別說把遊戲和材料混裝在同一盒；an assortment of 更精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an assortment of","explanation":"一盒中刻意配搭不同實物，正合 assortment 的混合選配意味。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"卡牌、拼圖和畫材同放一盒，並不是須依次進行的步驟。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a set of","explanation":"Set 可指成套物品，但不突出這盒內容由不同遊戲和材料混搭。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a selection of","explanation":"沒有說學生要從卡牌、拼圖及畫材中挑選；此處是導師混合備妥一盒用品。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an amount of","explanation":"An amount of 不自然地接複數遊戲和材料。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The lost-property desk displayed a range of unrelated objects: one glove, a toy car and an old scarf.","zh":"失物認領處擺出一批互不相關的物品：一隻手套、一輛玩具車和一條舊頸巾。","upgrade":"The lost-property desk displayed an assortment of unrelated objects: one glove, a toy car and an old scarf.","answer":"an assortment of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a variety of","explanation":"也可籠統說物品不同，但手套、玩具車和頸巾雜放在一處，assortment 更精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an assortment of","explanation":"失物處混合擺放幾件互不相關的物品，正合 assortment 的語感。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a selection of","explanation":"這些是失物，不是經人精選供顧客挑選的商品。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"手套、玩具車和頸巾不是依先後次序發生的事情。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a uniform set of","explanation":"三件失物並不屬成套一致的物品。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an amount of","explanation":"這裏逐件列出可數物品，不能用 an amount of 概括這批混雜東西。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"A Selection Of","meaning":"一組供選擇的","note":"表示主辦者挑出一組可用項目，重點是學員可從中挑選；須有供選的安排。","collocations":"a selection of activities / courses / sports; choose from a selection of options.","example":"The programme offers a selection of afternoon sports from which pupils may choose.","exampleZh":"課程提供一組下午運動項目，讓學生自行選擇。","contrast":"Selection 未必表示涵蓋面廣，可能只是精選幾項；若源句只報有不同活動，勿憑空添加「任選」安排。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The camp offers a range of afternoon activities and asks each pupil to choose one from the list.","zh":"營地提供多種下午活動，並要求每名學生從清單中選一項。","upgrade":"The camp offers a selection of afternoon activities and asks each pupil to choose one from the list.","answer":"a selection of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a variety of","explanation":"這個說法也可指不同活動；然而學生須從清單挑一項，a selection of 更突出供選擇的性質。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an amount of","explanation":"營地清單列出多項可選的 activities，amount 量度不可數總量，不能表示這些活動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a selection of","explanation":"有清單並供學員挑選，selection 點出可選的子集。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a set of","explanation":"Set 可指一組活動，卻未清楚指出學生從清單選一項。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an assortment of","explanation":"Assortment 像混合備妥的物品；活動在這裏是有組織、可挑選的清單。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a wide range of","explanation":"句中沒有證據說選項範圍廣泛，只確認有多項供選。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The organisers approved a range of activities from more than fifty proposals and printed them in the final programme.","zh":"主辦方從五十多項提案中批准了一批活動，並把它們刊於最終節目表。","upgrade":"The organisers approved a selection of activities from more than fifty proposals and printed them in the final programme.","answer":"a selection of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a variety of","explanation":"活動可能有不同種類，但 from more than fifty proposals 表明主辦方挑選批准的過程，selection 更精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a selection of","explanation":"主辦方從五十多項提案挑出獲批活動，approved a selection of 保留精選結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an amount of","explanation":"活動是複數可數項目，不宜用修飾不可數名詞的 an amount of。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a set of","explanation":"Set 只說有一組活動，沒有表達從五十多項提案審選的結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"獲批活動沒有被說成須按節目表順序完成，sequence 不合這裏的挑選焦點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a wide range of","explanation":"只知從五十多項提案挑出一些，未說獲批活動本身範圍特別廣。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Different Kinds Of","meaning":"不同種類的","note":"直接明白地說活動類型不同，適合向一般讀者解釋；沒有 range 可能帶出的範疇廣度意味。","collocations":"different kinds of activities / sports / games; offer different kinds of lessons.","example":"The club runs different kinds of activities, including team games and painting.","exampleZh":"俱樂部舉辦不同種類的活動，包括團隊遊戲及繪畫。","contrast":"Kinds 後用 of；不可寫 different kind of activities 來說多種。若只是一項運動的不同時段，不算不同種類。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The centre offers a range of activities: some are sports and others are art workshops.","zh":"中心提供多種活動：有些是運動，另一些是藝術工作坊。","upgrade":"The centre offers different kinds of activities: some are sports and others are art workshops.","answer":"different kinds of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"numerous","explanation":"句中只證明活動有體育與藝術兩類，並沒有數量多到『眾多』的證據。"},{"letter":"B","text":"different kinds of","explanation":"明白地把運動與藝術分成不同活動種類。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a sequence of","explanation":"A sequence of 指先後，不是類別。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an amount of","explanation":"An amount of 不接複數可數活動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a selection of","explanation":"句子在分類活動，未說學員要從預設清單中挑選。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a large number of","explanation":"句子只提體育與藝術兩類，沒有數字證明活動總數非常多。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A range of activities suited different age groups: younger pupils tried finger painting, while older pupils built simple robots.","zh":"不同類型的活動適合不同年齡組：年幼學生玩手指畫，年長學生則製作簡單機械人。","upgrade":"Different kinds of activities suited different age groups: younger pupils tried finger painting, while older pupils built simple robots.","answer":"different kinds of","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different kind of","explanation":"Different kind of 的單數形式不合後面的複數 activities。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a series of","explanation":"手指畫與機械人製作分別適合不同年齡組，並非必須依序完成的一系列步驟。"},{"letter":"C","text":"different kinds of","explanation":"兩個年齡組參與性質不同的活動，different kinds of activities 直接點明類別差異。"},{"letter":"D","text":"numerous","explanation":"句中只舉兩組例子，沒有證明活動數目眾多。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a selection of","explanation":"題句談活動與年齡組的配合，不是提供一份由學生挑選的清單。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a wide range of","explanation":"兩種年齡適配例子不足以斷言活動範圍十分廣泛。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"range / series / sequence：廣度與次序","zh":"源句列出可選活動種類，未說必須按步驟先後進行；a series of 或 a sequence of 易令讀者以為活動依時間或程序排成一串。只有確有先後時才可用。","point":"Range expresses spread; series/sequence can imply ordered succession."},{"word":"variety / various / varying：詞性與意思","zh":"A variety of activities 與 various activities 都可指不同類別；裸名詞 variety activities 不對。Varying activities 較易理解為活動內容會變動，不是簡單列出種類。","point":"Variety is a noun phrase, various an adjective, and varying can suggest change."},{"word":"assortment / selection：選配程度","zh":"An assortment of 常像把不同物品配成一批；a selection of 暗示從較多可能項目中挑出供人選擇的一組。源句只是說課程有一個活動範圍，不能推斷是精心配盒或每人都可自選。","point":"Assortment suggests a mixed collection; selection a chosen subset of options."},{"word":"number / amount / range：數目與種類","zh":"A number of activities 只說有若干項；an amount of activities 不合複數可數名詞；a range of 才把焦點放在種類或涵蓋範圍。","point":"Number counts items; amount measures a mass; range points to variety or span."},{"word":"all / every / wide：不要誇大","zh":"All sports 表示全數，原文沒有這種承諾。A wide range of 比 a range of 更強調範圍廣，只有活動清單足夠廣時才加 wide。","point":"All and wide add scope that may exceed the brochure’s actual claim."}],"moduleNumber":48},{"id":"lesson-049","sourceId":1,"headword":"a few years ago","title":"A Few Years Ago","titleZh":"幾年前","subtitle":"幾年前","description":"2018 年 DSE Speaking 6.2〈Fake News - There's a LOT of It About〉在敘述一段關於雞塊影片的網上傳聞時，以 A few years ago 開頭。這是時間副詞片語，從2018 年作者寫作時向前數若干年，沒有說確切年份。它標示過去某件事發生的時間，不表示事情持續了若干年。今天寫新句時，ago 的起點是今天，不能仍然當成從 2018 年計算。","sourceSense":"2018 年 DSE Speaking 6.2〈Fake News - There's a LOT of It About〉在敘述一段關於雞塊影片的網上傳聞時，以 A few years ago 開頭。這是時間副詞片語，從2018 年作者寫作時向前數若干年，沒有說確切年份。它標示過去某件事發生的時間，不表示事情持續了若干年。今天寫新句時，ago 的起點是今天，不能仍然當成從 2018 年計算。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["several years earlier","有條件改寫","Earlier 通常以另一個已說明的過去事件為參照；必須把那個事件寫進句子，不能直接把原文的 ago 換掉。"],["some years back","口語近義","也從說話時往前回望，但語氣較口語，年數仍不精確。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["要表達的時間關係","用法","檢查"],"rows":[["從現在回看，年數模糊","some years ago","中性敘述，沒有給確切年份。"],["從現在回看，口語回憶","a few years back / some years back","a few 暗示較少幾年；some 更籠統。"],["從現在回看，約多於兩年","several years ago","仍非精確年數；若只有兩年可用 a couple of。"],["從另一個已說明的過去事件回看","several years earlier","先交代作為基準的年份或事件。"]],"note":"快選規則： 問「比甚麼時間早？」答案若是現在，用 ago/back；若是句中另一個過去事件，用 earlier。For 說時長，不可取代一次事件的日期。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Some Years Ago","meaning":"若干年前","note":"從說話或寫作的現在回望若干年；年數故意保持模糊。這是較中性的說法。","collocations":"some years ago, people believed...; I saw the clip some years ago.","example":"Some years ago, a misleading picture circulated among parents.","exampleZh":"若干年前，一張誤導圖片曾在家長之間流傳。","contrast":"與 a few years ago 一樣從現在計算，但 some 更不強調「只有幾年」；若要交代另一個過去年份，改用 earlier。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A few years ago, our class checked a rumour about a school closure; the teacher cannot recall the exact year.","zh":"幾年前，我們班核查過一則學校停課傳聞；老師記不起確切年份。","upgrade":"Some years ago, our class checked a rumour about a school closure; the teacher cannot recall the exact year.","answer":"some years ago","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"over the past few years","explanation":"老師說的是某次核查發生在幾年前，不是核查工作延續了幾年。"},{"letter":"B","text":"some years ago","explanation":"從現在回望一件過去的事，且不指定年份，合乎老師的記憶。"},{"letter":"C","text":"some years later","explanation":"Later 要有較早的事件作起點；本句沒有。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in some years","explanation":"In 在這裏較像將來的「若干年後」，與已核查矛盾。"},{"letter":"E","text":"since some years ago","explanation":"Since 需接一段延續狀態，不適合一次性的 checked。"},{"letter":"F","text":"some years earlier than the closure","explanation":"Earlier than 後面的停課只是傳聞內容，不是已知的過去時間錨點。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"I saw that edited photograph a few years ago, but I cannot place it in a particular year.","zh":"我幾年前見過那張經修改的照片，但說不出確切年份。","upgrade":"I saw that edited photograph some years ago, but I cannot place it in a particular year.","answer":"some years ago","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"some years ago","explanation":"以今天為時間起點，保留不確定的年份，與 saw 一次事件相配。"},{"letter":"B","text":"over some years","explanation":"Over 表示一段時間內持續發生，不合一次看見的動作。"},{"letter":"C","text":"some years ahead","explanation":"Ahead 把看見照片放在未來，與 saw 衝突。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several years earlier","explanation":"Earlier 需要另一個過去事件作比較；此句只說今天的回憶。"},{"letter":"E","text":"since some years","explanation":"Since 後面不能這樣接複數年數來定位一次看見。"},{"letter":"F","text":"before a few years","explanation":"這個片語沒有清楚的過去參照點，也不是自然定位一次見到照片的說法。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"A Few Years Back","meaning":"幾年前（口語）","note":"從現在回顧幾年前的事，比 ago 更像談話中引出一段回憶。","collocations":"a few years back, we...; I read that story a few years back.","example":"A few years back, my cousin sent me an invented news story.","exampleZh":"幾年前，表哥傳給我一則虛構新聞。","contrast":"Back 在此是口語時間副詞，不是地點的「後面」；正式、精確的年表宜直接寫年份。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"“A few years ago, I believed a fake headline about a new school rule,” Mei told her brother over dinner.","zh":"「幾年前，我曾相信一則關於學校新規的假標題。」阿美在晚飯時對弟弟說。","upgrade":"“A few years back, I believed a fake headline about a new school rule,” Mei told her brother over dinner.","answer":"a few years back","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a few years earlier","explanation":"Earlier 通常要比另一個已提及的過去時間更早；阿美在飯桌上是直接從當下回顧。"},{"letter":"B","text":"for a few years","explanation":"For 會說信了多久，不是最初在何時相信。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a few years back","explanation":"口語回憶過去的一件事，back 保留從現在回望的方向。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a few years later","explanation":"Later 必須由另一件事往後數；這裏沒有那個起點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"by a few years","explanation":"By 只可描述相差幾年等關係，不能單獨定位此事。"},{"letter":"F","text":"over the past few years","explanation":"阿美只說某一年曾相信一則假標題，不是多年來持續相信。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The little cinema near our flat closed a few years ago.","zh":"我們住所附近那間小戲院幾年前結業了。","upgrade":"The little cinema near our flat closed a few years back.","answer":"a few years back","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a few years earlier","explanation":"句中沒有另一件往事作參照；直接從現在回想戲院結業。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a few years after","explanation":"After 需要一件先前發生的事；本句沒有提供。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a few years before now","explanation":"Before now 可理解，但笨拙，沒有口語敘事的自然語感。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a few years back","explanation":"放在 closed 後，口語地定位戲院幾年前的一次結業事件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"over the past few years","explanation":"結業是某一過去時間的事件，不能寫成持續多年關閉。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a few years hence","explanation":"Hence 指將來，與已經結業的 closed 矛盾。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Several Years Ago","meaning":"數年前（可能較久）","note":"從現在回望不只一兩年；several 往往暗示多於兩年，但不報確切年數。","collocations":"several years ago, the rumour spread; a report from several years ago.","example":"Several years ago, a false health claim appeared on the forum.","exampleZh":"數年前，一則虛假的健康說法出現在該論壇。","contrast":"若上下文明確只有兩年，用 a couple of years ago；若起點是另一個過去事件，用 several years earlier。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"A few years ago, around 2020, the library first taught pupils to check image sources.","zh":"幾年前，大約在2020年，圖書館首次教學生核查圖片來源。","upgrade":"Several years ago, around 2020, the library first taught pupils to check image sources.","answer":"several years ago","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a couple of years ago","explanation":"A couple of 暗示約兩年，與約六年的距離不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"several years ago","explanation":"從2026年回望約六年，several 比原來的 a few 更貼合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"several years later","explanation":"Later 把首次教學移往2020年之後。"},{"letter":"D","text":"over several years","explanation":"Over 說活動持續多年，不能定位首次發生的一天或一年。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a few years ago","explanation":"2020 年距今約六年；several 比暗示相對少數幾年的 a few 更合這個時間距離。"},{"letter":"F","text":"several years earlier than 2020","explanation":"Earlier than 2020 會把教學放在2020年以前，與句中年份相矛盾。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The interview was recorded a few years ago, in late 2020, but the archivist only catalogued it this month.","zh":"那段訪問是在幾年前、即2020年年底錄製的，但檔案員到這個月才把它編目。","upgrade":"The interview was recorded several years ago, in late 2020, but the archivist only catalogued it this month.","answer":"several years ago","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"since several years","explanation":"Since 不可直接定位一次完成的 recorded；它通常引出延續至今的狀態。"},{"letter":"B","text":"several years ago","explanation":"訪問於2020年年底錄製，從2026年回望約六年，且可放在被動句動詞後。"},{"letter":"C","text":"for several years","explanation":"For 會說錄製持續多年，與一次完成的訪問錄影不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several years after","explanation":"句中本月編目發生在錄製之後，不能把錄製改成「在本月之後數年」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"several years from now","explanation":"From now 指未來，與已錄製並已編目的訪問矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a couple of years ago","explanation":"句子標明約 2020 年，距今約六年，不能說只有兩年前。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Some Years Back","meaning":"好些年前（口語）","note":"口語中籠統說過去若干年，常用來引出一段沒有精確日期的回憶。","collocations":"some years back, I...; I heard the claim some years back.","example":"Some years back, my aunt showed me a video that later proved false.","exampleZh":"好些年前，姨姨給我看過一段影片，後來證實是假的。","contrast":"與 a few years back 接近，但 some 不特別限制年數較少；不宜用於需要精確日期的記錄。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"“A few years ago, I heard that rumour at a family dinner,” she told her cousin.","zh":"「幾年前，我在家庭聚餐聽過那個傳聞。」她對表親說。","upgrade":"“Some years back, I heard that rumour at a family dinner,” she told her cousin.","answer":"some years back","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"for some years","explanation":"For 說聽聞持續多年；原句說一次聚餐。"},{"letter":"B","text":"some years back","explanation":"口語回憶沒有明確年份的過去事件，符合此處語氣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"some years ahead","explanation":"Ahead 指後來或未來，與 heard 不符。"},{"letter":"D","text":"some years earlier than the dinner","explanation":"聚餐就是聽到傳聞的時候，不是比它更晚的時間錨點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"over some years","explanation":"說話者只在某次家庭晚飯聽到傳言，不是在多年期間持續聽。"},{"letter":"F","text":"since some years","explanation":"Since 要引出持續至今的情況，不能直接修飾一次 heard。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"This is how the old cinema looked a few years ago.","zh":"這就是那間舊戲院幾年前的模樣。","upgrade":"This is how the old cinema looked some years back.","answer":"some years back","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"some years back","explanation":"從現在回看戲院往日模樣，口語時間說法與 looked 相配。"},{"letter":"B","text":"over some years","explanation":"句子顯示照片中的某個過去模樣，不是多年逐漸改變的過程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"some years later","explanation":"Later 需要一件更早往事作參照，這裏只是從今天回看。"},{"letter":"D","text":"during some years","explanation":"這個說法不能自然地定位戲院照片所示的某段過去時間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"some years from now","explanation":"From now 指未來，而戲院過去的模樣已經留在照片裏。"},{"letter":"F","text":"some years beforehand","explanation":"Beforehand 要有另一個過去事件；此句沒有指定那個錨點。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Several Years Earlier","meaning":"再早幾年（過去錨點）","note":"以另一件已提及的過去事件或年份為基準，再往前數幾年；屬有條件改寫。","collocations":"several years earlier, the team had...; several years earlier than the opening.","example":"The club opened in 2020; several years earlier, volunteers had tested a similar idea.","exampleZh":"俱樂部於2020年成立；在那之前幾年，義工已試行過類似構想。","contrast":"Ago 從說話時數；earlier 從另一個已指明的時間點數。要重寫原句並交代那個時間點，不能直接替換2018年原文。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisers tested the idea in two schools a few years ago, in 2022. The campaign launched in 2025.","zh":"主辦方幾年前在兩所學校試行這個構想，當時是2022年。計劃於2025年推出。","upgrade":"The campaign launched in 2025; several years earlier, in 2022, the organisers had tested the idea in two schools.","answer":"several years earlier","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"several years from now","explanation":"From now 指2026年以後，與試行已發生不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"for several years","explanation":"For 描述試行持續時間，不說它早於推出。"},{"letter":"C","text":"several years earlier","explanation":"重寫時先交代2025年推出，再用 earlier 以該過去事件為錨點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several years after 2025","explanation":"After 2025 顛倒試行與推出的先後。"},{"letter":"E","text":"since several years","explanation":"Since 不能自然修飾一次已完成的試行。"},{"letter":"F","text":"several years ago","explanation":"這個說法以今天作基準；改寫句先說 2025 年推出，再回述更早的 2022 年，earlier 明確連接兩件往事。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"“Residents proposed the park a few years ago, in 2021,” a planner wrote in a 2024 council report.","zh":"一名規劃師在2024年的議會報告中寫道：「居民幾年前、即2021年提出興建公園。」","upgrade":"The 2024 council report said residents had proposed the park several years earlier, in 2021.","answer":"several years earlier","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"several years later","explanation":"報告寫於2024年，提案卻在2021年；later 會顛倒先後。"},{"letter":"B","text":"since several years earlier","explanation":"Since 不能這樣修飾一次提出的建議，亦沒有延續狀態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"over several years","explanation":"Over 會說提案歷時多年；原文只指定2021年那次提出。"},{"letter":"D","text":"several years earlier","explanation":"轉述2024年報告時，以報告時間為過去錨點，回指約三年前的提案。"},{"letter":"E","text":"several years ago","explanation":"今天回望2021年也可如此說，但把2024年的引文轉為間接轉述時，earlier 更清楚保留報告的時間視角。"},{"letter":"F","text":"for several years","explanation":"For 描述持續時段，不適合只在2021年提出的一次建議。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"ago / earlier：時間起點","zh":"Ago 從說話或寫作的「現在」往回數；earlier 通常從另一個已交代的時間點往回數。例如 2026 年寫「2019 年開始；數年前已試行」，應以 2019 年為參照，不可含糊地寫成 ago。","point":"Ago is measured from the speaker’s present; earlier is measured from a stated or recoverable reference time."},{"word":"a few / several / a couple of：年數暗示","zh":"A couple of years ago 通常指大約兩年前；several years ago 常暗示多於兩年，可能比 a few years ago 略久。原文沒有給確切年數，不可把含糊說法誤寫成精確的「兩年前」。","point":"A couple of suggests about two; several allows a somewhat larger but still indefinite count."},{"word":"ago / for / since：事件與時段","zh":"「數年前看見影片」是在定位一次事件；for a few years 說一段持續時間，since a few years ago 要配合延續至今的狀態，不能機械替換一次性的 saw。","point":"Ago dates an event; for gives duration; since introduces a starting point for a continuing state."},{"word":"back / later / from now：方向與語體","zh":"Some years back 是從現在向過去回想，適合閒談；some years later 是從某事件向後推；in a few years / a few years from now 指未來。若句子說已發生的網上傳聞，後兩者會顛倒方向。","point":"Back is retrospective and informal; later is relative to another event; from now points forward."},{"word":"recently / long ago：距離不同","zh":"Recently 可能只指幾天或幾週，long ago 強調年代久遠；兩者都沒有原句「幾年前」的適中、含糊年距。只有上下文額外支持時才可另作描述。","point":"Neither recently nor long ago reliably retains an interval of a few years."}],"moduleNumber":49},{"id":"lesson-050","sourceId":99,"headword":"around the world","title":"Around the world","titleZh":"世界多地","subtitle":"世界多地","description":"The 2017 DSE set 1.3 book-fair passage reports a speaker saying martial-arts writers’ work is becoming more popular around the world. This is a developing international trend as reported in that passage, not proof that the work is popular in every country or equally popular everywhere. Around the world is an adverbial place phrase. All exercises below are original.","sourceSense":"The 2017 DSE set 1.3 book-fair passage reports a speaker saying martial-arts writers’ work is becoming more popular around the world. This is a developing international trend as reported in that passage, not proof that the work is popular in every country or equally popular everywhere. Around the world is an adverbial place phrase. All exercises below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["worldwide","直接替代","簡潔副詞；也可作形容詞修飾 audience。"],["across the globe","直接替代","稍有修辭色彩，仍只說廣泛分布，不是每處均有。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： 補 globally（較正式、常用於趨勢）、internationally（強調跨國，不必遍及整個地球）、in many parts of the world（明示多地而非每國）。All over the world 與本詞高度重疊，請看 0057；abroad/overseas 以某國為參照，everywhere 過強，around 單獨亦可指空間繞行，不合來源。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["要說的意思","可用表達"],"rows":[["簡潔的全球多地分布","worldwide"],["較正式的總體全球走勢","globally"],["強調跨國","internationally"],["有畫面感地說世界多處","across the globe"],["明言多地但不逐國全稱","in many parts of the world"]],"note":"幾項在自然英文中常重疊；練習的關鍵是避免把世界多地誤改成一國、一區或每一國，並保留 becoming more popular 的趨勢。參見 0057 all over the world。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"worldwide","meaning":"遍及世界多地","note":"簡潔地指讀者、銷量或關注度有國際分布；作副詞時可置句尾。","collocations":"gain readers worldwide; worldwide readership; become known worldwide","example":"The translation helped the novel reach readers worldwide.","exampleZh":"譯本幫助小說接觸世界各地讀者。","contrast":"不表示每個國家都有讀者；可與 globally 有很大重疊。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the translation appeared, the writer gained readers around the world, although no one had checked every country.","zh":"譯本推出後，作家在世界各地增加讀者，但並沒有人逐國核查。","upgrade":"After the translation appeared, the writer gained readers worldwide, although no one had checked every country.","answer":"worldwide","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worldwide","explanation":"worldwide 表廣泛跨國讀者，無須逐國覆蓋。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in every country","explanation":"沒有人逐國核查，不能說每國都有。"},{"letter":"C","text":"nationwide","explanation":"nationwide 只是一國內。"},{"letter":"D","text":"only overseas","explanation":"only overseas 錯排除本國讀者。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in one region","explanation":"one region 把範圍縮小。"},{"letter":"F","text":"world-leading","explanation":"world-leading 是排名最高，原句沒有比較排名。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The publisher said the series was reaching libraries around the world, with shipments to several continents.","zh":"出版社說該系列正送達世界多地圖書館，並運往數個大洲。","upgrade":"The publisher said the series was reaching libraries worldwide, with shipments to several continents.","answer":"worldwide","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in its home city","explanation":"數個大洲超過一座城市。"},{"letter":"B","text":"worldwide","explanation":"多洲圖書館的廣泛分布可稱 worldwide。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in every library","explanation":"沒有證據說每間圖書館都收到。"},{"letter":"D","text":"nationally","explanation":"nationally 只涵蓋一國。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only overseas","explanation":"only overseas 無端排除本國。"},{"letter":"F","text":"locally","explanation":"locally 與多洲運送不合。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"globally","meaning":"從全球範圍看","note":"較正式地描述跨多地的總體趨勢或分布，常用於出版、銷售、觀眾資料。","collocations":"sales rise globally; interest grows globally; global audience","example":"Interest in the author’s books grew globally after several translations appeared.","exampleZh":"幾個譯本出版後，全球多地對該作者作品的興趣有所增長。","contrast":"Globally 偏整體尺度；worldwide 可同義，無嚴格分界。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The distributor reported that interest in the books was increasing around the world, drawing on sales reports from several regions.","zh":"發行商根據多個地區的銷售報告指出，書籍在世界多地受到愈來愈多關注。","upgrade":"The distributor reported that interest in the books was increasing globally, drawing on sales reports from several regions.","answer":"globally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in every country without exception","explanation":"多地報告不等於逐國無例外。"},{"letter":"B","text":"globally","explanation":"根據多區資料說總體國際增長，globally 合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"only domestically","explanation":"domestically 只限本國。"},{"letter":"D","text":"within one region","explanation":"one region 縮小範圍。"},{"letter":"E","text":"at the highest level already","explanation":"原句是 increasing，未說已達最高。"},{"letter":"F","text":"overseas only","explanation":"only overseas 會排除本國銷售。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A review of sales in Asia, Europe and the Americas found that demand was rising around the world, though at different speeds.","zh":"對亞洲、歐洲和美洲銷售的檢視發現，需求在世界多地上升，速度卻不一。","upgrade":"A review of sales in Asia, Europe and the Americas found that demand was rising globally, though at different speeds.","answer":"globally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"globally","explanation":"跨三洲的總體升勢可稱 globally，並未說每地一樣快。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in one city","explanation":"資料來自三洲，不是一城。"},{"letter":"C","text":"uniformly everywhere","explanation":"句中明說上升速度不一。"},{"letter":"D","text":"in every country","explanation":"只看幾個地區，不能逐國斷言。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only nationally","explanation":"範圍超過單一國家。"},{"letter":"F","text":"at a fixed level","explanation":"demand was rising，非固定不變。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"internationally","meaning":"在多個國家；國際上","note":"重點是跨國，而非在某一國內；可修飾出版、流通或獲認識。","collocations":"published internationally; attract international readers; become popular internationally","example":"The series became popular internationally after publishers released several translations.","exampleZh":"出版社推出數個譯本後，該系列在多個國家受到歡迎。","contrast":"跨國不等於每一洲都有；worldwide 較突出整體全球範圍。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Once the novel was released in six countries, its audience began to grow around the world beyond its original home market.","zh":"小說在六個國家發行後，讀者群開始跨越原本的本土市場，在世界多地增長。","upgrade":"Once the novel was released in six countries, its audience began to grow internationally beyond its original home market.","answer":"internationally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"within one country","explanation":"六國發行超過單一國家。"},{"letter":"B","text":"only in its home market","explanation":"原句明說 beyond home market。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in every country","explanation":"六國不是每個國家。"},{"letter":"D","text":"internationally","explanation":"跨國並超出本土市場，internationally 準確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"across one district","explanation":"一個行政區太窄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"at one bookshop","explanation":"不只一間書店。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The prize helped the book attract readers around the world, including people in countries where it had never been sold before.","zh":"獎項幫助書籍在多個國家吸引讀者，包括一些此前未有發售的國家。","upgrade":"The prize helped the book attract readers internationally, including people in countries where it had never been sold before.","answer":"internationally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"domestically","explanation":"新增其他國家讀者，非只限本土。"},{"letter":"B","text":"internationally","explanation":"跨國吸引新讀者，internationally 合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in every nation","explanation":"沒有列出每一國。"},{"letter":"D","text":"only overseas","explanation":"獎項吸引多國新讀者，但句中未說本土讀者消失；only overseas 會無據排除他們。"},{"letter":"E","text":"regionally within one country","explanation":"一國內的區域仍未跨境。"},{"letter":"F","text":"uniformly everywhere","explanation":"沒有說各地情況完全一致。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"across the globe","meaning":"世界各處","note":"較有畫面感的片語，適合描述作品接觸遠距離、多個地點的讀者。","collocations":"readers across the globe; spread across the globe; festivals across the globe","example":"Readers across the globe shared reviews of the new translation.","exampleZh":"世界各地讀者分享了新譯本的評論。","contrast":"Globe 是地球，不是字面繞地球一圈；也不保證每個地方都有。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Readers around the world, from Hong Kong to Brazil and Sweden, exchanged reviews online.","zh":"世界多地讀者，包括香港、巴西和瑞典的讀者，在網上交流書評。","upgrade":"Readers across the globe, from Hong Kong to Brazil and Sweden, exchanged reviews online.","answer":"across the globe","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in one region","explanation":"香港、巴西、瑞典並非同一地區。"},{"letter":"B","text":"across the globe","explanation":"相距甚遠的多地讀者可說 across the globe。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in every country","explanation":"只列三地，不能說每國。"},{"letter":"D","text":"around one city","explanation":"不是一座城市周邊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only abroad from Hong Kong","explanation":"only abroad 錯把香港讀者排除。"},{"letter":"F","text":"across one border","explanation":"跨越的不只一條國界。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The online festival linked book clubs around the world, including groups on three continents.","zh":"網上節慶連繫了世界各地讀書會，包括三個大洲的小組。","upgrade":"The online festival linked book clubs across the globe, including groups on three continents.","answer":"across the globe","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"across the globe","explanation":"三洲讀書會分布廣泛，across the globe 合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"within one nation","explanation":"超過一國。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in every country","explanation":"只知三洲，不知每國都有。"},{"letter":"D","text":"around the venue","explanation":"網上活動連繫多地，不是場館周邊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only overseas","explanation":"only overseas 無本國參照且排除可能本地小組。"},{"letter":"F","text":"in one province","explanation":"一省太窄。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"in many parts of the world","meaning":"在世界許多地方","note":"明確降低全稱承諾，適合只知多個地區出現同一趨勢、未能逐國核實時。","collocations":"popular in many parts of the world; readers in many parts of the world","example":"The detective novels found readers in many parts of the world.","exampleZh":"這些偵探小說在世界許多地方找到讀者。","contrast":"比 everywhere 謹慎；與 around the world 的來源廣度相容。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The anthology became more popular around the world, with rising sales in a dozen markets on four continents, though the publisher had no figures for most countries.","zh":"選集在世界多地愈來愈受歡迎，四個大洲的十二個市場銷量上升；但出版社沒有大部分國家的數據。","upgrade":"The anthology became more popular in many parts of the world, with rising sales in a dozen markets on four continents, though the publisher had no figures for most countries.","answer":"in many parts of the world","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in every country","explanation":"大部分國家沒有數據，不能說每一國都上升。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in one city","explanation":"四洲十二個市場有升幅，不是一座城市。"},{"letter":"C","text":"only at home","explanation":"多洲市場有增長，並非只在本國。"},{"letter":"D","text":"uniformly everywhere","explanation":"各市場升幅未必相同，uniformly 是沒有證據的加強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in many parts of the world","explanation":"四洲十二個市場有升幅而非逐國全稱，in many parts of the world 謹慎準確。"},{"letter":"F","text":"in no foreign market","explanation":"已有四洲市場增長，不能說海外全無。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The author’s essays found readers around the world, especially in places where translations were available, but not in every language market.","zh":"作者的文章在世界多地找到讀者，尤其在有譯本的地方，但並非每個語言市場都有。","upgrade":"The author’s essays found readers in many parts of the world, especially in places where translations were available, but not in every language market.","answer":"in many parts of the world","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in one domestic market","explanation":"句中指出不同語言市場，不只本國一個。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in every language market","explanation":"明說並非每個語言市場都有。"},{"letter":"C","text":"in many parts of the world","explanation":"有譯本的多地讀者符合 in many parts of the world。"},{"letter":"D","text":"uniformly worldwide","explanation":"uniformly 錯加各地分布相同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only overseas","explanation":"only overseas 無端排除本地。"},{"letter":"F","text":"in the immediate region","explanation":"翻譯市場範圍不只附近一區。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"in every country / everywhere · 多地不等於每一國","zh":"中文辨析： 來源的 around the world 不提供逐國覆蓋證據。若有每個國家的完整資料，才可用 every country；否則是過度斷言。","point":"Wide reach does not prove universal coverage."},{"word":"abroad / overseas · 以某國為參照的海外","zh":"中文辨析： Abroad 要先知道出發國／本國；around the world 說分布範圍，不只是本國以外，還可能包含本國。","point":"Overseas is relative to a home location; global reach is not."},{"word":"nationwide / regionally · 全國或區域範圍太窄","zh":"中文辨析： 一國各地可稱 nationwide；鄰近數國可稱 regional。原文說多國／世界範圍，不可縮成一國或一區。","point":"A national or regional audience is narrower than worldwide reach."},{"word":"international / global as adjective · 詞性與位置","zh":"中文辨析： 可說 international readership 或 global trend；若在 became popular 後作狀語，要用 internationally/globally，不能寫 became popular global。","point":"Adjectives modify nouns; adverbs modify the popularity trend."},{"word":"popular / becoming more popular · 當前狀態與增長趨勢","zh":"中文辨析： 原文是 becoming more popular，說受歡迎程度上升；不能改寫成已在各地最暢銷或已完全普及。地點近義改寫仍須保留動態。","point":"Geographic paraphrase must preserve the reported trend."}],"moduleNumber":50},{"id":"lesson-051","sourceId":57,"headword":"all over the world","title":"All over the world","titleZh":"世界各地","subtitle":"世界各地","description":"原文： 2016 年 DSE 5.1〈Hong Kong’s Buskers the Good, the Bad and the Dreadful〉問：「Why do you think music is so important to people and cultures all over the world?」此處是地點範圍狀語，說音樂在世界很多地方、不同人群與文化中有重要性；不是一項統計結論，也不表示地球上每一個人都持相同看法。","sourceSense":"原文： 2016 年 DSE 5.1〈Hong Kong’s Buskers the Good, the Bad and the Dreadful〉問：「Why do you think music is so important to people and cultures all over the world?」此處是地點範圍狀語，說音樂在世界很多地方、不同人群與文化中有重要性；不是一項統計結論，也不表示地球上每一個人都持相同看法。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["worldwide","direct/close","可作副詞放在所修飾的活動或人群之後，如 listeners worldwide；也可作形容詞放在名詞前，如 worldwide interest。不要在原句直接寫成 all worldwide。"],["globally","contextual/recast","副詞通常修飾動詞或整個情況，如 music is valued globally；若硬貼在 people and cultures 後，句子較笨重，宜重排。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Worldwide 可後置作副詞，也可前置作形容詞；兩題分別練習這兩種位置。\n- Across the globe 可描述相距很遠的社群分布，也可配合 travel 說訊號跨洲傳播。\n- Globally 用於修飾 be valued 等情況或 examine 等研究動作；不要誇大為每個人、每個國家或每個城市無例外。\n- Around the world 同樣自然；完整教學見 0099 around the world，本課避免重複。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"worldwide","meaning":"遍及世界；世界各地的","note":"在名詞後可作副詞，或在名詞前作形容詞。改寫要維持這個位置差別；它指廣泛地理分布，不是逐一聲稱每個人都同意。","collocations":"fans worldwide; worldwide interest in music; broadcast worldwide","example":"The band's songs found listeners worldwide.","exampleZh":"這支樂隊的歌曲在世界各地找到聽眾。","contrast":"Worldwide 表地理涵蓋；international 往往強調跨國關係而非分布於世界各地。All worldwide 重複，不自然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The busker’s live stream reached listeners all over the world, with comments arriving from Hong Kong, Brazil, Kenya and many other places.","zh":"這位街頭藝人的直播傳到世界各地的聽眾，留言來自香港、巴西、肯尼亞及其他許多地方。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The busker’s live stream reached listeners worldwide, with comments arriving from Hong Kong, Brazil, Kenya and many other places.","answer":"listeners worldwide","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"listeners overseas","explanation":"overseas 以香港為立足點時會排除本地聽眾，但留言包含香港。"},{"letter":"B","text":"listeners worldwide","explanation":"worldwide 後置修飾 listeners，保留本地及遠方多地的廣泛分布。"},{"letter":"C","text":"listeners from a few foreign countries","explanation":"a few foreign countries 縮成少數境外國家，漏掉香港及 many other places。"},{"letter":"D","text":"listeners on every continent","explanation":"every continent 逐洲聲稱；列出的地方不足以證明每洲都有。"},{"letter":"E","text":"international listeners","explanation":"international listeners 常指國際觀眾或外國觀眾，未清楚涵蓋本地及世界多地。"},{"letter":"F","text":"listeners from every country","explanation":"every country 比 all over the world 更強，原句沒有逐國資料。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The street-music project received attention all over the world after one clip was shared by broadcasters on several continents.","zh":"一段影片獲多個大洲的廣播機構分享後，街頭音樂計劃得到世界各地關注。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The street-music project received worldwide attention after one clip was shared by broadcasters on several continents.","answer":"worldwide attention","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"universal attention","explanation":"universal 近乎人人關注，廣播機構跨洲分享不足以證明。"},{"letter":"B","text":"overseas attention","explanation":"overseas 只說境外，不能完整涵蓋本地及多洲。"},{"letter":"C","text":"attention from every country","explanation":"every country 要逐國都有關注，原句只說多洲。"},{"letter":"D","text":"international attention","explanation":"international 可能只指幾國，弱於原句的世界多地範圍。"},{"letter":"E","text":"worldwide attention","explanation":"worldwide 前置修飾 attention，保留跨洲的廣泛地理涵蓋。"},{"letter":"F","text":"national attention","explanation":"national 將原句收窄成一國。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"across the globe","meaning":"遍及全球；文體較生動","note":"名詞片語後的地理介詞片語，表示在相距很遠的多個地點；是 all over the world 的自然改寫，但不要誤讀成每個地方均已查證。","collocations":"communities across the globe; shared across the globe; audiences across the globe","example":"Musicians across the globe adapt familiar melodies to local styles.","exampleZh":"世界各地的音樂人把熟悉的旋律改編成當地風格。","contrast":"Globe 在此指地球；across the country 只限一國，on every continent 則加入原句未必支持的逐洲斷言。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Community choirs all over the world, from East Asia to South America, adapt the song to their local languages.","zh":"從東亞到南美洲，世界各地的社區合唱團把這首歌改編成當地語言。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Community choirs across the globe, from East Asia to South America, adapt the song to their local languages.","answer":"across the globe","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"in several nearby countries","explanation":"nearby countries 只表示鄰近幾國，與東亞至南美洲的廣泛分布不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"in communities overseas","explanation":"overseas 是相對本地的境外，也可能遺漏本地合唱團。"},{"letter":"C","text":"across the globe","explanation":"across the globe 描述相距遠的多地社群，符合跨洲例子。"},{"letter":"D","text":"on every continent","explanation":"every continent 要逐洲都有，原句舉例不能證明。"},{"letter":"E","text":"in countries across Asia","explanation":"across Asia 遺漏南美洲合唱團。"},{"letter":"F","text":"in international competitions","explanation":"international competitions 說活動性質，不是合唱團分布地點。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The festival broadcast travelled all over the world through partner radio stations on different continents.","zh":"音樂節廣播透過不同大洲的合作電台傳到世界各地。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The festival broadcast travelled across the globe through partner radio stations on different continents.","answer":"travelled across the globe","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"travelled across the globe","explanation":"across the globe 配合 travelled，保留訊號經多洲電台擴散的地理範圍。"},{"letter":"B","text":"travelled between two neighbouring countries","explanation":"兩個鄰國的傳播比不同大洲的電台網絡窄。"},{"letter":"C","text":"travelled to overseas stations only","explanation":"overseas only 排除可能的本地電台，原句沒有排除。"},{"letter":"D","text":"travelled on every radio frequency","explanation":"every radio frequency 是技術頻道範圍，不是世界地點範圍。"},{"letter":"E","text":"travelled through every country","explanation":"every country 要逐國覆蓋，不能從多洲合作電台推定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"travelled between international festivals","explanation":"between international festivals 說活動間傳遞，並非透過各洲電台向聽眾廣播。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"globally","meaning":"從全球範圍看；需配合動詞","note":"用副詞修飾 be valued, spread, be heard 等動詞或整個敘述；通常需把原句的「世界各地的人」重寫成「在全球受到重視」。","collocations":"valued globally; recognised globally; spread globally","example":"Traditional songs are heard globally through streaming services.","exampleZh":"傳統歌曲透過串流服務在全球都有人聆聽。","contrast":"Globally 在此表地理分布；universally 是「人人都／在所有情況下」的強斷言。Global 是形容詞，不能直接代替副詞。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Traditional music is valued all over the world, though each region performs it differently.","zh":"傳統音樂在世界各地受到重視，雖然不同地區的演奏方式各異。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Traditional music is valued globally, though each region performs it differently.","answer":"valued globally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"valued internationally by two groups","explanation":"兩個跨國群體不足以表達世界各地受重視。"},{"letter":"B","text":"valued globally","explanation":"globally 修飾 valued，保留多地重視而風格有差異的意思。"},{"letter":"C","text":"valued universal","explanation":"universal 是形容詞，不能作 valued 的副詞；也有無例外意味。"},{"letter":"D","text":"valued overseas only","explanation":"overseas only 排除本地，原句沒有此限制。"},{"letter":"E","text":"valued by every individual","explanation":"every individual 誇大為每個人都重視。"},{"letter":"F","text":"valued in several neighbouring countries","explanation":"數個鄰國比原句的世界多地狹窄。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The researchers examined street-music rules all over the world by comparing policy samples from cities on several continents.","zh":"研究人員比較多個大洲城市的政策樣本，藉此研究世界各地的街頭音樂規則。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The researchers examined street-music rules globally by comparing policy samples from cities on several continents.","answer":"examined street-music rules globally","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"examined street-music rules only overseas","explanation":"only overseas 排除本地樣本，而原句沒有這樣限制。"},{"letter":"B","text":"examined street-music rules internationally between two cities","explanation":"兩城跨國比較比多大洲樣本窄。"},{"letter":"C","text":"examined street-music rules universal","explanation":"universal 不是這裏的副詞，也會暗示所有規則相同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"examined street-music rules in every city","explanation":"every city 要逐城取樣；多洲城市樣本不等於所有城市。"},{"letter":"E","text":"examined street-music rules globally","explanation":"globally 修飾 examined，表明研究比較多洲城市的全球尺度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"examined street-music rules in neighbouring countries","explanation":"鄰國研究的地域範圍比多大洲樣本窄。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Everyone / universally · 範圍過度擴張","zh":"中文辨析： 原句說世界各地的「人與文化」，沒有說地球上每人都認為音樂重要。Universally 適用於真正無例外的普遍性主張，不能僅憑地理廣度推出。","point":"Geographic breadth does not prove every person agrees."},{"word":"Internationally / overseas · 跨國與海外","zh":"中文辨析： Internationally 可指跨國交流或多國活動，但不必遍及世界；overseas 依說話者所在地指境外。談樂隊到幾個外國演出時可用，不能完整傳達原句世界各地的範圍。","point":"Several foreign places are not automatically worldwide reach."},{"word":"Everywhere / every country / every continent · 過於籠統或過強","zh":"中文辨析： Everywhere 若無限定可只指一座城市內的每處；every country/continent 又變成逐一覆蓋的可查證主張。原句並未列證這些絕對範圍。","point":"The passage makes a broad claim, not an audited location count."},{"word":"Global versus globally / worldwide · 詞性與位置","zh":"中文辨析： Global 是形容詞，可說 global interest，不能寫 heard global。Worldwide 可前置修飾名詞或後置作副詞，globally 須放在適合修飾動詞／整句的位置。","point":"Similar scope does not license the same grammar."},{"word":"Across the country / locally · 地理範圍縮小","zh":"中文辨析： Across the country 可說一國多處，locally 可說某社區或地區；原句跨越世界多地，這些詞會把範圍縮窄。","point":"National and local reach are narrower than world reach."}],"moduleNumber":51},{"id":"lesson-052","sourceId":34,"headword":"advantages and disadvantages","title":"Advantages and Disadvantages","titleZh":"優點與缺點","subtitle":"優點與缺點","description":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 1.3〈The Magic of Outdoor Play〉請考生討論 “the advantages and disadvantages of allowing children to play at school”。這是尚待權衡的兩面問題，並不預設戶外玩耍必定有益或有害，也不要求正反理由數目相等。以下例句與練習均為原創。","sourceSense":"2016 年 DSE Speaking 1.3〈The Magic of Outdoor Play〉請考生討論 “the advantages and disadvantages of allowing children to play at school”。這是尚待權衡的兩面問題，並不預設戶外玩耍必定有益或有害，也不要求正反理由數目相等。以下例句與練習均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["pros and cons","口語直接近義","簡潔說正反理由，討論中自然；正式報告可用原片語。"],["benefits and drawbacks","有條件近義","分別強調實際所得與不利之處；談玩耍的具體效果時貼切。"]],"note":"另加入 positive and negative aspects（中性逐面分析）、strengths and weaknesses（方案本身的強弱）、upsides and downsides（口語的好壞後果）、pluses and minuses（逐項清單）及 merits and demerits（較正式的方案評鑑）。這些補充候選詞各有適用語境，不能機械地放入原句。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","主要用途","避免的誤解"],"rows":[["advantages and disadvantages","中性、較正式地談利弊","題目要求兩面，不是已作結論。"],["pros and cons","對話或討論中的贊成與反對理由","比原詞口語。"],["benefits and drawbacks","評估具體所得與限制","不要把未證實的益處說成保證。"],["positive and negative aspects","分析好與壞的不同面向","面向不一定是已量度的結果。"],["strengths and weaknesses","評鑑方案內部設計或運作","不等於外部機會或威脅。"],["upsides and downsides","口語談一項選擇的好壞後果","不宜硬放進極正式報告。"],["pluses and minuses","把正反點逐項列出或評分","不是數學正負號。"],["merits and demerits","較正式地評價建議兩面","Demerits 在此不是學生記過點數。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 先確認是否真的討論雙面。口頭簡述可用 pros and cons 或 upsides and downsides；表格逐項比較可用 pluses and minuses；方案內部評估用 strengths and weaknesses；具體效果用 benefits and drawbacks；中性逐面分析用 positive and negative aspects；正式政策討論可用 merits and demerits。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Pros and Cons","meaning":"利與弊（口語）","note":"談一個方案的贊成理由和反對理由，比 advantages and disadvantages 簡短、口語。","collocations":"weigh the pros and cons; discuss the pros and cons of outdoor play; list the pros and cons.","example":"The parents weighed the pros and cons of extending lunch playtime.","exampleZh":"家長們權衡延長午間玩耍時間的利與弊。","contrast":"Pros and cons 適合討論立場；benefits and drawbacks 更像具體效果，不要把尚未評估的方案說成已被證明有效。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Before voting on longer playground breaks, the parents discussed the advantages and disadvantages of the proposal.","zh":"家長在表決是否延長操場小息前，討論了這項建議的優點與缺點。","upgrade":"Before voting on longer playground breaks, the parents discussed the pros and cons of the proposal.","answer":"pros and cons","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"家長是在表決前權衡好壞，不是追查小息安排的起因與結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"pros and cons","explanation":"表決前的討論自然包括支持與反對理由，口語簡稱利弊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"costs only","explanation":"經費可能是一項缺點，卻沒有涵蓋建議的優點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"final decision","explanation":"表決尚未進行，句中討論的是判斷依據而非結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"benefits only","explanation":"只列好處，漏掉家長同時考慮的不利之處。"},{"letter":"F","text":"safety rules","explanation":"安全規則可能相關，但不能代替整項建議的兩面評估。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After a term of after-school play, the headteacher talked through its advantages and disadvantages on the school podcast: children made friends, but staff worked longer hours.","zh":"放學後玩耍安排試行一個學期後，校長在學校播客談到其利弊：孩子交到朋友，但職員工作時間更長。","upgrade":"After a term of after-school play, the headteacher talked through its pros and cons on the school podcast: children made friends, but staff worked longer hours.","answer":"pros and cons","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"benefits alone","explanation":"交朋友是好處，但職員工時延長是不利之處，不能只列單邊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"staff rules","explanation":"校長談的是試行一學期後的結果，不是職員守則。"},{"letter":"C","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"播客同時評價正反結果，並非研究延長工時的原因鏈。"},{"letter":"D","text":"risks and remedies","explanation":"工作時間延長是負擔；只談風險與補救會漏掉孩子交朋友的益處。"},{"letter":"E","text":"pros and cons","explanation":"播客的口語回顧涵蓋孩子社交得益及員工負擔，完整保留兩面。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a final verdict","explanation":"校長說明試行利弊，題句沒有交代校董會最後的政策決定。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Benefits and Drawbacks","meaning":"好處與不足","note":"同時點出可能帶來的益處和實際限制；可接 of + 活動／方案。","collocations":"assess the benefits and drawbacks of play; potential benefits and drawbacks; benefits for pupils and drawbacks for staff.","example":"The report compares the benefits and drawbacks of giving pupils more time in the playground.","exampleZh":"報告比較讓學生有更多操場活動時間的好處和不足。","contrast":"Benefit 往往指所得的好結果，drawback 指方案的不利特點；若只是羅列支持或反對的論點，pros and cons 更直接。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The trial report describes the advantages and disadvantages of daily outdoor play: pupils moved more, but teachers needed extra supervision time.","zh":"試行報告描述每日戶外玩耍的利弊：學生多了活動，但教師需要額外監督時間。","upgrade":"The trial report describes the benefits and drawbacks of daily outdoor play: pupils moved more, but teachers needed extra supervision time.","answer":"benefits and drawbacks","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"benefits and drawbacks","explanation":"多活動是具體好處，額外監督時間是不利之處，兩面都保留。"},{"letter":"B","text":"benefits and guarantees","explanation":"報告沒有保證玩耍一定成功；教師的時間負擔也不是「保證」。"},{"letter":"C","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"後半句列的是一好一壞，重點不在分析兩者的因果鏈。"},{"letter":"D","text":"gains without costs","explanation":"額外監督時間正是一項成本，without costs 與報告相矛盾。"},{"letter":"E","text":"rules and punishments","explanation":"試行報告提活動量和人手，沒有列懲罰。"},{"letter":"F","text":"risks alone","explanation":"只談風險會漏掉學生多了活動這個好處。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school compared the advantages and disadvantages of opening its playground at lunchtime, including exercise opportunities and cleaning costs.","zh":"學校比較午飯時間開放操場的利弊，包括運動機會和清潔費用。","upgrade":"The school compared the benefits and drawbacks of opening its playground at lunchtime, including exercise opportunities and cleaning costs.","answer":"benefits and drawbacks","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"safety instructions","explanation":"句子比較運動機會和清潔成本，並非教學生如何安全玩耍。"},{"letter":"B","text":"advantages only","explanation":"清潔費用是不利項，不能只寫好處。"},{"letter":"C","text":"benefits and drawbacks","explanation":"運動機會屬潛在利益，清潔成本屬實際負擔，組成雙面比較。"},{"letter":"D","text":"profits and losses","explanation":"學校操場安排不一定以金錢利潤衡量；運動機會亦非「利潤」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"causes and results","explanation":"學校權衡方案兩面，而非追問開放操場的成因。"},{"letter":"F","text":"final verdict","explanation":"比較正在進行，句中沒有說學校已作決定。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Positive and Negative Aspects","meaning":"正反面","note":"中性地檢視同一安排的好與壞方面，不必聲稱各方面已有可量度的結果。","collocations":"examine positive and negative aspects; positive and negative aspects of outdoor play; consider both aspects.","example":"The committee examined the positive and negative aspects of holding games during breaks.","exampleZh":"委員會檢視在小息舉辦遊戲的正面與負面之處。","contrast":"Aspects 只是「方面」，可涵蓋氣氛、安全與時間安排；benefits and drawbacks 對利弊評價較明確。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The committee recorded the advantages and disadvantages of the new play area, from fresh air to the shortage of shade.","zh":"委員會記錄新遊樂區的正反面，包括新鮮空氣和遮蔭不足。","upgrade":"The committee recorded the positive and negative aspects of the new play area, from fresh air to the shortage of shade.","answer":"positive and negative aspects","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"positive aspects alone","explanation":"遮蔭不足也是記錄內容，不能只保留正面。"},{"letter":"B","text":"positive and negative aspects","explanation":"新鮮空氣與遮蔭不足是場地兩個不同面向，尚未必有可量度的成果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"causes of bad weather","explanation":"遮蔭不足是設施問題，句中沒有討論天氣成因。"},{"letter":"D","text":"proven health outcomes","explanation":"新鮮空氣不等於報告已證實健康效益，說法過強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"rules of the area","explanation":"記錄的是場地特點，並非使用規則。"},{"letter":"F","text":"repairs needed","explanation":"增加遮蔭可能是改善方向，但不能涵蓋正面特點。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In her presentation, Mina explained the advantages and disadvantages of outdoor lessons, including a lively atmosphere and distracting noise.","zh":"美娜在匯報中解釋戶外課堂的正反面，包括活潑氣氛和令人分心的噪音。","upgrade":"In her presentation, Mina explained the positive and negative aspects of outdoor lessons, including a lively atmosphere and distracting noise.","answer":"positive and negative aspects","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"benefits only","explanation":"令人分心的噪音是負面一面，不可略去。"},{"letter":"B","text":"final decision","explanation":"美娜解釋課堂特點，未說學校最後是否採用戶外課。"},{"letter":"C","text":"lesson timetable","explanation":"氣氛與噪音不是上課時間表。"},{"letter":"D","text":"causes of noise","explanation":"句子提到噪音的不利影響，沒有研究噪音從何而來。"},{"letter":"E","text":"positive and negative aspects","explanation":"中性地涵蓋活潑氣氛與噪音兩個面向，保留雙面討論。"},{"letter":"F","text":"health risks","explanation":"分心不必然是健康風險，也漏掉活潑氣氛的好處。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Strengths and Weaknesses","meaning":"方案的強項與弱項","note":"評價一項已設計或試行的安排本身在哪些方面做得好、哪些方面不足；比泛談玩耍後果更偏方案內部特點。","collocations":"assess the strengths and weaknesses of a policy / programme; identify strengths and weaknesses.","example":"The pilot review identified the strengths and weaknesses of the supervised-play programme.","exampleZh":"試行檢討指出有督導玩耍計劃的強項與弱項。","contrast":"Strengths 可是安排清晰、師資配合等；weaknesses 可是人手不足。它不自動涵蓋所有外部風險或利益，因此需要方案評估語境。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The pilot review examined the advantages and disadvantages of the supervised-play scheme: clear activity rotations worked well, but too few staff watched the gate.","zh":"試行檢討審視有督導玩耍計劃的長處與不足：活動輪換清晰，但看守大門的人手太少。","upgrade":"The pilot review examined the strengths and weaknesses of the supervised-play scheme: clear activity rotations worked well, but too few staff watched the gate.","answer":"strengths and weaknesses","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"opportunities and threats","explanation":"輪換安排與大門人手是方案內部設計，不是外在市場機會或威脅。"},{"letter":"B","text":"strengths and weaknesses","explanation":"檢討同時指出運作良好的安排和人手不足，正是方案的強弱項。"},{"letter":"C","text":"benefits and guarantees","explanation":"輪換清晰不是保證；人手不足更不是保證的另一面。"},{"letter":"D","text":"staff skills and pupil abilities","explanation":"題句談輪換設計與崗位人數，沒有評核員工或學生的個人技能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"causes and results","explanation":"檢討是在評價方案本身好壞，並非單純追蹤因果鏈。"},{"letter":"F","text":"successes only","explanation":"大門人手不足是明確弱點，不能只保留成功面。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before adopting the proposed play policy, planners listed its advantages and disadvantages: the timetable was flexible, but its rain-day procedure was unclear.","zh":"規劃者在採納玩耍政策前列出其強弱項：時間表靈活，但雨天程序不清楚。","upgrade":"Before adopting the proposed play policy, planners listed its strengths and weaknesses: the timetable was flexible, but its rain-day procedure was unclear.","answer":"strengths and weaknesses","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"profits and losses","explanation":"學校政策的時間表與雨天程序不是營業利潤及虧損。"},{"letter":"B","text":"strengths and weaknesses","explanation":"提案尚未採納，但已有靈活設計和不清楚的程序，可評估其內部強弱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"two strengths","explanation":"雨天程序不清楚是弱點，不能當作第二個優點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"external opportunities and threats","explanation":"兩項都在政策文本內，不是外部環境因素。"},{"letter":"E","text":"rules and penalties","explanation":"雨天程序是規則，但題句還評價靈活時間表，沒有談懲罰。"},{"letter":"F","text":"implementation steps","explanation":"雨天程序可能要補寫，但句子先評價政策的靈活處與缺陷，並非列實施步驟。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Upsides and Downsides","meaning":"好處與不利之處（口語）","note":"口頭討論或輕鬆文字中說一個選擇可能帶來的正反後果；比 pros and cons 更像「做了之後會怎樣」。","collocations":"talk about the upsides and downsides; upsides and downsides of longer breaks.","example":"Over lunch, the teachers talked about the upsides and downsides of a longer play break.","exampleZh":"教師在午飯時談論延長玩耍小息的好處與不利之處。","contrast":"這是口語詞組；正式政策報告宜用 benefits and drawbacks 或原片語。不能只取 upsides 而漏掉另一面。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At pickup, a parent said, “Let's talk about the advantages and disadvantages of opening the courtyard at lunch: children could exercise, but nearby classes might be noisier.”","zh":"接孩子時，一名家長說：「我們談談午飯時開放庭院的好壞吧：孩子可運動，但附近課室可能更嘈。」","upgrade":"At pickup, a parent said, “Let's talk about the upsides and downsides of opening the courtyard at lunch: children could exercise, but nearby classes might be noisier.”","answer":"upsides and downsides","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upsides and downsides","explanation":"家長在閒談中說可能多運動也可能增噪，口語詞組保留正反後果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"rules and restrictions","explanation":"是否開庭院的規則不是句中比較的運動機會和噪音後果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"benefits only","explanation":"課室更嘈是可能的不利之處，不能只談好處。"},{"letter":"D","text":"hazards only","explanation":"噪音不等於全部風險，且會漏掉運動機會。"},{"letter":"E","text":"profits and losses","explanation":"學校午飯安排沒有在計算金錢盈利。"},{"letter":"F","text":"rights and duties","explanation":"家長談的是安排的結果，不是學生權利與義務清單。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After a week of longer play breaks, Mei told her friend about the advantages and disadvantages: she saw friends more often but had less time to finish lunch.","zh":"延長玩耍小息試行一星期後，美兒向朋友說起其好壞：她更常見到朋友，卻少了時間吃完午飯。","upgrade":"After a week of longer play breaks, Mei told her friend about the upsides and downsides: she saw friends more often but had less time to finish lunch.","answer":"upsides and downsides","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upward and downward directions","explanation":"題句沒有描述上下移動，而是在談小息改動後的好壞。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upsides and downsides","explanation":"向朋友回顧實際一週的得失，口語說法自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"見朋友與吃午飯的時間是正反後果，不是要找改動的原因。"},{"letter":"D","text":"gains without costs","explanation":"少了吃午飯時間正是她付出的代價。"},{"letter":"E","text":"punishments and rewards","explanation":"沒有學生受罰或獲獎；這是日程帶來的兩面影響。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a final verdict","explanation":"美兒報告個人體驗，沒有對政策作最後表決。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"Pluses and Minuses","meaning":"加分點與扣分點（非正式清單）","note":"把選項的正反項目逐條列出或評分時自然，語氣較輕便；不是數學的正負號。","collocations":"list the pluses and minuses; weigh the pluses and minuses of an option.","example":"The class put the pluses and minuses of extra outdoor play in two columns.","exampleZh":"全班把額外戶外玩耍的加分點和扣分點分列兩欄。","contrast":"Pluses and minuses 適合表格或快速比較；若要談已量度的健康效果，benefits and drawbacks 更明確。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"On the whiteboard, the class wrote the advantages and disadvantages of an extra play period in two columns before comparing them.","zh":"全班先在白板上分兩欄寫出額外玩耍時段的加分點和扣分點，再作比較。","upgrade":"On the whiteboard, the class wrote the pluses and minuses of an extra play period in two columns before comparing them.","answer":"pluses and minuses","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"mathematical signs","explanation":"白板兩欄是列出政策好壞，不是練習算術正負號。"},{"letter":"B","text":"pluses and minuses","explanation":"逐項分欄的非正式比較，適合簡稱加分點與扣分點。"},{"letter":"C","text":"rules and penalties","explanation":"題句沒有列玩耍守則或違規懲罰。"},{"letter":"D","text":"positive points only","explanation":"兩欄中有不利之處，不能只列加分項。"},{"letter":"E","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"同學比較的是安排好壞，不是繪製因果圖。"},{"letter":"F","text":"final decisions","explanation":"比較尚未完成，白板列的是判斷材料。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the trial, teachers rated the advantages and disadvantages of outdoor breaks on a simple score sheet, giving each point a number from one to five.","zh":"試行後，教師在簡易評分表上評估戶外小息的正反項目，並逐項給一至五分。","upgrade":"After the trial, teachers rated the pluses and minuses of outdoor breaks on a simple score sheet, giving each point a number from one to five.","answer":"pluses and minuses","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"costs and profits","explanation":"小息的好壞不一定能換算成金錢盈虧。"},{"letter":"B","text":"causes and effects","explanation":"評分表逐項衡量正反點，不是追查安排的起因。"},{"letter":"C","text":"pluses and minuses","explanation":"試行後把有利與不利項逐項評分，符合清單式的輕便說法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"marks without reasons","explanation":"分數是給每個正反點，並非沒有評分對象的數字。"},{"letter":"E","text":"benefits alone","explanation":"評分表也包括不利點，不能只評好處。"},{"letter":"F","text":"attendance figures","explanation":"有沒有出席人數沒有提及；教師評的是戶外小息的正反項。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"Merits and Demerits","meaning":"優點與缺點（較正式）","note":"在某些正式、考試或政策討論中評鑑一項建議的長處與短處；語氣比 pros and cons 書面。Merits and drawbacks 在一般現代英文也很自然。","collocations":"examine the merits and demerits of a proposal; debate its merits and demerits.","example":"The school board examined the merits and demerits of opening the playground after lessons.","exampleZh":"校董會審視放學後開放操場這項建議的優點與缺點。","contrast":"這裏的 demerits 指方案的不足，不是學校紀律制度中的「記缺點」。只談獎懲記錄時不能直接替代利弊。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school board's formal report assessed the advantages and disadvantages of keeping the playground open after lessons before making a recommendation.","zh":"校董會在提出建議前，於正式報告中評估放學後繼續開放操場的優點與缺點。","upgrade":"The school board's formal report assessed the merits and demerits of keeping the playground open after lessons before making a recommendation.","answer":"merits and demerits","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merits and demerits","explanation":"正式報告在建議前評價開放方案兩面，這裏的 demerits 是方案不足。"},{"letter":"B","text":"disciplinary points","explanation":"報告沒有給學生記過；這裏評的是操場政策。"},{"letter":"C","text":"final recommendation","explanation":"校董會尚在評估，結論要在權衡後才作出。"},{"letter":"D","text":"benefits alone","explanation":"只說好處會漏掉開放操場的可能缺點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"legal offences","explanation":"政策短處不是法律犯罪。"},{"letter":"F","text":"causes and consequences","explanation":"報告評價方案好壞，不只是列因果次序。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In the council debate, each speaker had to address the advantages and disadvantages of the proposed school-play policy, even if they supported one side.","zh":"在議會辯論中，每名發言者即使支持其中一方，也必須論及擬議校園玩耍政策的優點與缺點。","upgrade":"In the council debate, each speaker had to address the merits and demerits of the proposed school-play policy, even if they supported one side.","answer":"merits and demerits","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merits and demerits","explanation":"正式辯論要求發言者涵蓋方案好壞兩面，即使本人有立場也不能漏一面。"},{"letter":"B","text":"speaker penalties","explanation":"Demerits 在此不是給發言者記過，辯論規則要求評價政策。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one-sided arguments","explanation":"題句明定每位發言者都須談正反兩面。"},{"letter":"D","text":"strengths and threats","explanation":"Strengths 是方案內部強項，threats 通常指外部風險；混用兩套框架不能準確保留一般優缺點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"dissent and consensus","explanation":"發言者可能有不同立場，但題目要他們評價政策特點，不是統計分歧與共識。"},{"letter":"F","text":"benefits and penalties","explanation":"政策有潛在好處與缺點，缺點不等於學生要受紀律處罰。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"只寫單邊 · Benefits / drawbacks alone","zh":"原題要求正反兩面。只說 benefits 會漏掉潛在風險，只說 drawbacks 會漏掉可能的好處；若問題改為只問玩耍如何幫助健康，才可單談 benefits。English contrast: One side does not preserve a two-sided request.","point":""},{"word":"因果與評估 · Causes and effects","zh":"Causes and effects 問原因和結果，不自動比較好壞。若題目問「延長小息為何令學生更活躍」，才適合因果分析；本題要評估安排的利弊。English contrast: Causation is a different analytical task from weighing merits.","point":""},{"word":"正反論點與最後決定 · Conclusion / verdict","zh":"列出 pros and cons 是討論過程，verdict 或 conclusion 是權衡後的決定。原題沒有預先作出結論；不能用「應該全面禁止」代替利弊討論。English contrast: The outcome of a debate is not the two-sided evidence.","point":""},{"word":"利弊不等於危險與安全 · Risks and safety","zh":"安全可能是一項考慮，但玩耍的優點還可能包括社交和活動量，缺點也可能是時間與空間限制。若新題專問意外風險及防護，risks and safety measures 才合題。English contrast: A specific safety pair is narrower than all advantages and disadvantages.","point":""},{"word":"Strengths / external opportunities：內部表現與外部條件","zh":"一項玩耍方案的人手安排可說是 strength 或 weakness；天氣、政策資助等外部條件未必是方案本身的強弱。若在分析外部機會與威脅，不可只換詞不換分析框架。English contrast: Internal strengths and weaknesses are not the same as external opportunities and threats.","point":""},{"word":"Demerits：方案缺點與記過","zh":"Demerits of a proposal 是建議的不足；校規裏的 demerits 可指學生被記的缺點或過失。原題不是要求列出學生犯規紀錄。English contrast: The policy-evaluation sense differs from disciplinary demerit points.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":52},{"id":"lesson-053","sourceId":30,"headword":"adopt","title":"Adopt","titleZh":"開始採用環保駕駛習慣","subtitle":"開始採用環保駕駛習慣","description":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 4.2〈‘Take a Brake’ Low Carbon Action Scheme〉說計劃 “encourages people to drive less and adopt green driving habits”。原文說的是鼓勵，沒有報告每位司機已採用。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 4.2〈‘Take a Brake’ Low Carbon Action Scheme〉說計劃 “encourages people to drive less and adopt green driving habits”。原文說的是鼓勵，沒有報告每位司機已採用。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["take up","near, object-sensitive","可說 take up a greener driving practice；take up habits 較不自然。"],["embrace","contextual / stronger","接受並熱心支持，比中性的 adopt 多了積極態度。"],["start following","recast","較自然接 guidelines；若受詞是 habits，可說 start practising。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["take up","開始做某活動或做法：Take up a habit 不如 adopt a habit 自然；只說開始，不保證已堅持多年。"],["start practising","開始實踐一種習慣：start practising 指開始實踐；若前面是 agreed to 或 encourages，則仍只表示承諾或鼓勵，不能當作已實行。"],["embrace","欣然採納；更強態度：中性 adopt 不必然 enthusiasm；原文計劃鼓勵採用，未證明人人熱心支持。"],["switch to","轉而使用；有舊新對比：單獨 adopt 不一定表示完全拋棄舊做法；若沒有舊新對比，switch to 可能過度指定。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 受詞是 practice 可用 take up；強調開始實際養成習慣可用 start practising；有熱心認同證據才用 embrace；已交代舊新做法對比才用 switch to。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"take up","meaning":"開始做某活動或做法","note":"由未做過轉為開始某種可重複的環保駕駛實踐；受詞宜是 practice / activity。","collocations":"take up a greener driving practice; take up car-sharing","example":"Several drivers decided to take up car-sharing after attending the scheme.","exampleZh":"數名司機參加計劃後決定開始共乘。","contrast":"Take up a habit 不如 adopt a habit 自然；只說開始，不保證已堅持多年。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the workshop, some drivers decided to adopt a new practice of planning shorter routes.","zh":"工作坊後，一些司機決定採用預先規劃較短路線的新做法。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After the workshop, some drivers decided to take up a new practice of planning shorter routes.","answer":"take up","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"take up","explanation":"後接 a new practice，自然表達司機決定開始這項做法；不宣稱他們已實行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"look into","explanation":"只研究是否可行，未開始實踐新做法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"consider adopting","explanation":"只考慮，原句說決定開始採用。"},{"letter":"D","text":"keep up","explanation":"表示維持已在做的事，與題句由此開始不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"pass on","explanation":"把建議傳給別人，不等於自己開始。"},{"letter":"F","text":"phase out","explanation":"逐步停止，方向與採用相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The scheme invited taxi drivers to adopt the practice of switching off engines while parked.","zh":"計劃邀請的士司機採用停車時關掉引擎的做法。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The scheme invited taxi drivers to take up the practice of switching off engines while parked.","answer":"take up","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consider","explanation":"只考慮做法，計劃邀請司機開始實踐關引擎。"},{"letter":"B","text":"take up","explanation":"可接 the practice of...，指計劃邀請司機開始實踐停車關引擎，未說每人已做。"},{"letter":"C","text":"recommend","explanation":"可以向別人建議，未表示受邀司機自己做。"},{"letter":"D","text":"keep up","explanation":"表示繼續既有做法，原句重點是開始新習慣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"test briefly","explanation":"短暫試一下未表達養成停車關引擎的做法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"phase out","explanation":"表示淘汰一項做法，而不是開始採用它。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"start practising","meaning":"開始實踐一種習慣","note":"清楚把提議轉成日常行動；適合 green driving habits，拼寫用英式 practising。","collocations":"start practising greener driving habits; practise smoother driving","example":"The trainees agreed to start practising smoother driving after the training session.","exampleZh":"受訓者同意在培訓後開始實踐較平穩的駕駛方法。","contrast":"start practising 指開始實踐；若前面是 agreed to 或 encourages，則仍只表示承諾或鼓勵，不能當作已實行。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The campaign encourages drivers to adopt green driving habits such as smoother acceleration.","zh":"活動鼓勵司機採用較平穩加速等環保駕駛習慣。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The campaign encourages drivers to start practising green driving habits such as smoother acceleration.","answer":"start practising","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consider practising","explanation":"只是考慮，未明確要求開始實踐。"},{"letter":"B","text":"recommend to others","explanation":"向他人建議不等於自己養成駕駛習慣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"start practising","explanation":"後接 green driving habits，保留活動鼓勵司機開始實踐的語氣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"start discussing","explanation":"討論做法未保留實際駕駛行動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"start measuring","explanation":"量度省油成效與開始駕駛做法不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"start advertising","explanation":"宣傳做法未表示司機親自實踐。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The trainer watched the trainees adopt smoother braking during their supervised road session; they continued using it afterward.","zh":"教練看到受訓者在路面練習中採用較平穩的煞車方式；他們之後也繼續使用。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The trainer watched the trainees start practising smoother braking during their supervised road session; they continued using it afterward.","answer":"start practising","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"consider practising","explanation":"只是考慮，不能解釋教練已看到受訓者在路面練習中使用新方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"evaluate","explanation":"評估煞車做法不是自己在練習中開始使用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"recommend to classmates","explanation":"向同學推薦與受訓者親自做是兩回事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"start practising","explanation":"教練親眼看到開始實踐，而且之後延續，和第一題的「鼓勵」不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"describe","explanation":"只描述做法，不能保留在車上實際煞車的行為。"},{"letter":"F","text":"continue practising","explanation":"單說繼續，略去了教練看見的開始時點。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"embrace","meaning":"欣然採納；更強態度","note":"在有熱心支持、主動倡議的線索時，表示不只開始做，也認同這套做法。","collocations":"embrace green driving habits; embrace a low-carbon approach","example":"The drivers enthusiastically embraced greener driving habits and urged colleagues to join.","exampleZh":"司機熱心採納較環保的駕駛習慣，還鼓勵同事加入。","contrast":"中性 adopt 不必然 enthusiasm；原文計劃鼓勵採用，未證明人人熱心支持。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The drivers welcomed the idea and chose to adopt green driving habits, then urged colleagues to join them.","zh":"司機歡迎這個理念，決定採用環保駕駛習慣，並敦促同事加入。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The drivers welcomed the idea and chose to embrace green driving habits, then urged colleagues to join them.","answer":"embrace","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accept","explanation":"可以勉強接受，未包含題句的熱心支持。"},{"letter":"B","text":"tolerate","explanation":"只忍受做法，與積極推廣語氣不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"approve of","explanation":"只表示贊成，未必開始做並鼓勵別人。"},{"letter":"D","text":"consider","explanation":"只是思考，未到承諾與推廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"embrace","explanation":"歡迎理念並主動推廣，支持更強的欣然採納語氣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"follow","explanation":"可以照做，但未明確表達熱情認同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At its annual meeting, the taxi association voted to adopt greener driving habits as a central policy and publicly praised drivers who followed them.","zh":"的士協會在周年會議上投票把更環保的駕駛習慣列為核心政策，並公開表揚遵循的司機。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"At its annual meeting, the taxi association voted to embrace greener driving habits as a central policy and publicly praised drivers who followed them.","answer":"embrace","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accept","explanation":"單純接受未必會投票列為核心政策並公開表揚實踐者。"},{"letter":"B","text":"put up with","explanation":"勉強容忍與協會公開支持新做法不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"consider","explanation":"只作考慮，與已投票作出政策決定不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"follow","explanation":"可指照做，但協會此處是把做法立為政策並積極倡導。"},{"letter":"E","text":"approve of","explanation":"口頭贊成仍未必代表投票採納並公開推廣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"embrace","explanation":"核心政策表決加上公開讚賞，支持協會積極採納的意思。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"switch to","meaning":"轉而使用；有舊新對比","note":"已交代以前的做法和新的綠色做法時，表示從舊習慣轉向新習慣。","collocations":"switch to greener driving habits; switch from idling to turning off the engine","example":"The drivers agreed to switch to greener habits after the course.","exampleZh":"司機上完課後同意轉而採用較環保的習慣。","contrast":"單獨 adopt 不一定表示完全拋棄舊做法；若沒有舊新對比，switch to 可能過度指定。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Instead of idling while waiting, the driver chose to adopt a greener habit of switching off the engine.","zh":"司機不再在等候時讓引擎空轉，而選擇採用停車關引擎的環保習慣。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Instead of idling while waiting, the driver chose to switch to a greener habit of turning off the engine.","answer":"switch to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"switch to","explanation":"句子明列舊的空轉與新的關引擎習慣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"add to","explanation":"可能只是保留舊做法再加新項，未說轉換。"},{"letter":"C","text":"consider","explanation":"只作思考，原句已選擇或計劃改換。"},{"letter":"D","text":"return to","explanation":"說以前曾做新方法，題句未提供。"},{"letter":"E","text":"follow","explanation":"可照新方法做，但未凸顯由舊轉新。"},{"letter":"F","text":"look into","explanation":"只是研究新方法，尚未計劃或決定轉換。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The fleet used to brake sharply at stops; it now plans to adopt a smoother braking practice.","zh":"車隊以前停車時急煞；現在計劃採用更平穩的煞車做法。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The fleet used to brake sharply at stops; it now plans to switch to a smoother braking practice.","answer":"switch to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"add to","explanation":"可能保留急煞再加入另一做法，沒有清楚表示改用較平穩煞車。"},{"letter":"B","text":"switch to","explanation":"有明確舊做法，新計劃是轉換；仍保留 plans to。"},{"letter":"C","text":"look into","explanation":"只研究可能性，與車隊已計劃轉換的程度不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"continue with","explanation":"繼續急煞，與車隊計劃改用平穩煞車相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"return to","explanation":"暗示以前已用新方法，題句沒有這層背景。"},{"letter":"F","text":"combine with","explanation":"表示急煞與平穩煞車並行，而非由舊做法轉換。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Adopt a child · 同字異義","zh":"中文辨析： 領養孩子是 adopt 的另一義；本段受詞是 green driving habits，談的是開始採用做法。","point":"Adopt a child and adopt a practice are different senses."},{"word":"Embrace · 積極認同非必然","zh":"中文辨析： 熱心歡迎與鼓勵同事可用 embrace；只是嘗試一項綠色習慣不能自動加上熱情。","point":"Embrace adds enthusiastic acceptance beyond neutral adopt."},{"word":"Take up habits · 搭配問題","zh":"中文辨析： Take up a practice 或 take up car-sharing 自然；take up habits 較彆扭，應說 adopt habits 或 start practising habits。","point":"Choose a suitable object after take up."},{"word":"Encourage / actually do · 語氣差別","zh":"中文辨析： 原文說計劃 encourages people，沒有說每個人已採用；改寫也必須保留鼓勵或計劃，而非改成已完成事實。","point":"An invitation to adopt does not prove that adoption occurred."}],"moduleNumber":53},{"id":"lesson-054","sourceId":56,"headword":"alert","title":"Alert","titleZh":"提醒／發出通知","subtitle":"提醒／發出通知","description":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.1〈Wearable smart devices are here!〉列舉「smart swimsuits that alert the user to apply sunscreen」。這裏 alert 是動詞：智能泳衣向穿着者發出提示，使他們知道該塗防曬霜；句子沒有說它代替人塗抹，也沒有說穿着者一定照做。前文列舉其他可監測或震動的穿戴裝置，但沒有指定泳衣用聲響、燈光、震動還是手機訊息發提示。","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.1〈Wearable smart devices are here!〉列舉「smart swimsuits that alert the user to apply sunscreen」。這裏 alert 是動詞：智能泳衣向穿着者發出提示，使他們知道該塗防曬霜；句子沒有說它代替人塗抹，也沒有說穿着者一定照做。前文列舉其他可監測或震動的穿戴裝置，但沒有指定泳衣用聲響、燈光、震動還是手機訊息發提示。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["warn","contextual","若提示明確指出陽光、紫外線或曬傷風險，可說 warn someone to apply sunscreen；中性提示未必是警告。"],["notify","close","向用戶送達通知；若題句說的是裝置提供資訊而非強調危險，可用 notify someone that... 或 notify someone to...，後者在裝置指示語境自然。"],["signal to","recast / not a direct swap","Signal to the wearer that it is time to apply sunscreen 可用，但 signal to the wearer to apply sunscreen 較累贅，不能當作一詞對一詞替換。若只是技術訊號送至另一裝置，亦不等於穿着者收到提示。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Notify：把要塗防曬霜的通知送達用戶；不表示已塗。\n- Warn：提示同時明確指出危險或曬傷風險。\n- Remind：喚回用戶已知的補塗計劃或先前指示。\n- Prompt：介面或語音助理提示下一步行動；不保證執行。\n- Signal to 需完整句法和明確接收者；單靠裝置間的技術訊號，不等於人收到防曬提示。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"notify","meaning":"通知；傳達訊息","note":"裝置向人送達可見、可聽或其他能察覺的提示；說的是通知的傳送，不暗示用戶已採取行動。較適合通知欄、手機訊息或系統提示。","collocations":"notify the wearer to apply sunscreen; notify users that UV exposure is high; send a notification","example":"The wristband notified its wearer to reapply sunscreen after swimming.","exampleZh":"手環在使用者游泳後通知他補塗防曬霜。","contrast":"Notify 重在消息送達；warn 要有較明確的危險訊息；inform 可只是提供一般資料，未必要求行動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The smart swimsuit alerts Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen before the outdoor lesson.","zh":"智能泳衣在諾拉的手機上提示她於戶外課前塗防曬霜。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The smart swimsuit notifies Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen before the outdoor lesson.","answer":"notifies Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"notifies Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"手機通知的送達是題句確定的事，notify 準確保留要塗防曬霜的訊息。"},{"letter":"B","text":"warns Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"原句只說上課前的通知，沒有說紫外線已達危險水平；warn 多添風險意味。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"沒有交代諾拉先前打算塗防曬霜，remind 多加已知計劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reports Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"report 不能按此句法直接接 Nora，且報告資料不等於提示行動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"alarms Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"alarm 在此處不自然且比普通手機通知強烈。"},{"letter":"F","text":"signals to Nora on her phone to apply sunscreen","explanation":"signal to 接這個人和 to apply 的重疊結構累贅；應改為 signal to Nora that it is time。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The app connected to the swimsuit alerts its wearer to apply sunscreen, then records whether the notice has been opened.","zh":"連接泳衣的應用程式通知穿着者塗防曬霜，然後記錄通知是否已被打開。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The app connected to the swimsuit notifies its wearer to apply sunscreen, then records whether the notice has been opened.","answer":"notifies its wearer to apply sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"prompts its wearer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"prompt 可指要求下一步的介面提示，但題句特別追蹤「通知」是否打開，notify 對訊息送達更精準。"},{"letter":"B","text":"notifies its wearer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"通知被打開與否是題句焦點，notify 保留發出通知而未假設已塗抹。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds its wearer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"沒有先前塗抹時間或用戶設定，remind 暗示的既定任務未獲支持。"},{"letter":"D","text":"informs its wearer about sunscreen","explanation":"只告知防曬霜資料，沒有保留「要塗」這個行動提示。"},{"letter":"E","text":"warns its wearer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"題句沒有明說日曬風險或危險水平，warn 額外強調危險。"},{"letter":"F","text":"notifies sunscreen to its wearer","explanation":"notify 的常用形式是 notify someone to do something，不能把 sunscreen 當直接受通知者。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"warn","meaning":"警告；提示風險","note":"題句說明過度日曬、紫外線或曬傷等風險時，可用 warn；它比中性的 alert 更明顯帶有危險意味，不宜用於純例行通知。","collocations":"warn the wearer to apply sunscreen; warn users about strong UV radiation; warn of sunburn risk","example":"The swimsuit warned the swimmer to apply sunscreen when the UV level became dangerous.","exampleZh":"當紫外線水平升至危險程度時，泳衣警告泳客塗防曬霜。","contrast":"Warn 把風險置於前景；alarm 通常表示更強烈的驚恐或警報，不是所有防曬提示都達到那個程度。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"When the UV reading reaches a dangerous level, the swimsuit alerts the swimmer to apply sunscreen before returning to the beach.","zh":"當紫外線讀數達到危險水平，泳衣警示泳客回到海灘前塗防曬霜。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the UV reading reaches a dangerous level, the swimsuit warns the swimmer to apply sunscreen before returning to the beach.","answer":"warns the swimmer to apply sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"notifies the swimmer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"notify 也可能傳達訊息，但沒有如 warn 一樣直接反映「危險水平」所帶的風險。"},{"letter":"B","text":"warns the swimmer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"危險紫外線讀數使這項防曬提示具有明確警告性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds the swimmer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"原句沒有預設泳客已計劃塗防曬霜，所以提醒並非最精確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"informs the swimmer of sunscreen","explanation":"告知防曬霜資料沒有表達必須在回海灘前塗抹。"},{"letter":"E","text":"prompts the swimmer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"prompt 可描述介面下一步，但較少體現危險 UV 讀數這個關鍵。"},{"letter":"F","text":"alarms the swimmer to apply sunscreen","explanation":"alarm someone to do something 在此不自然，也過度渲染警報強度。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The sensor detects prolonged direct sun and alerts the wearer to put on sunscreen because the risk of sunburn has risen.","zh":"感測器發現持續直曬，警示穿着者塗防曬霜，因為曬傷風險已上升。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The sensor detects prolonged direct sun and warns the wearer to put on sunscreen because the risk of sunburn has risen.","answer":"warns the wearer to put on sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reminds the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"沒有之前的塗抹安排，remind 的「記得做」前提未交代。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reports the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"report the wearer 意思可能是舉報該人，並非給他防曬警示。"},{"letter":"C","text":"notifies the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"notify 能送達消息，但沒有充分突出因直曬而上升的曬傷風險。"},{"letter":"D","text":"signals the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"signal the wearer to... 在某些手勢語境可用，這裏感測器的風險警告以 warn 更清楚。"},{"letter":"E","text":"warns the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"題句明說曬傷風險增加，warn 最準確表達防護警告。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frightens the wearer to put on sunscreen","explanation":"frighten 說的是使人害怕；泳衣不必把人嚇到才發出警示。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"remind","meaning":"提醒；喚回已知事項","note":"用戶已知道或預先設定要塗、補塗防曬霜，裝置在適當時間提示其記得做，便可用 remind。若首次告知一項新風險，未必是「提醒」。","collocations":"remind the wearer to reapply sunscreen; set a reminder; remind someone of an earlier instruction","example":"An hour after the first application, the watch reminded Maya to put on more sunscreen.","exampleZh":"第一次塗防曬霜一小時後，手錶提醒瑪雅再塗一些。","contrast":"Remind 預設已有計劃、記憶或先前塗抹；notify 只說訊息送達，不必有這個先決條件。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Nora sets a two-hour reapplication timer, and her swimsuit alerts her to put on more sunscreen when the timer ends.","zh":"諾拉設定兩小時後補塗的計時器；時間一到，泳衣便提醒她再塗防曬霜。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Nora sets a two-hour reapplication timer, and her swimsuit reminds her to put on more sunscreen when the timer ends.","answer":"reminds her to put on more sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"warns her to put on more sunscreen","explanation":"沒有新的危險讀數；計時器到時更像提醒既定補塗計劃。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reminds her to put on more sunscreen","explanation":"兩小時補塗是諾拉先設定的任務，remind 精確表達喚回既定事項。"},{"letter":"C","text":"notifies her about more sunscreen","explanation":"notify her about more sunscreen 只泛指相關消息，沒有明示補塗。"},{"letter":"D","text":"informs her to put on more sunscreen","explanation":"inform her to... 在此不自然，inform 通常接 of/that 引出資訊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"signals her about putting on more sunscreen","explanation":"signal her about... 搭配彆扭，也不如 remind 點明預設計時器。"},{"letter":"F","text":"forces her to put on more sunscreen","explanation":"泳衣只發提示，沒有能力強迫諾拉塗抹。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the coach has told the team to use sunscreen before practice, the swimsuit alerts each player to apply it as they leave the changing room.","zh":"教練先告訴隊員練習前要塗防曬霜；隊員走出更衣室時，泳衣提醒各人塗上。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After the coach has told the team to use sunscreen before practice, the swimsuit reminds each player to apply it as they leave the changing room.","answer":"reminds each player to apply it","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"informs each player to apply it","explanation":"inform someone to... 不是自然搭配，且教練已先給出指示。"},{"letter":"B","text":"warns each player to apply it","explanation":"沒有紫外線危險讀數；原句重在讓隊員記起剛才的指示。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds each player to apply it","explanation":"先前教練已明確說明，泳衣再次提示正是 remind 的情況。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reports each player to apply it","explanation":"report each player 會像舉報隊員，並非向其提示。"},{"letter":"E","text":"prompts each player to apply it","explanation":"prompt 可描述下一步提示，但弱於 remind 對先前指示的對應。"},{"letter":"F","text":"alarms each player to apply it","explanation":"alarm 表示使人驚恐，與更衣室出口的例行提示不相稱。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"prompt","meaning":"提示採取下一步","note":"當裝置顯示或發出一個要求用戶接着行動的提示，可說 prompt someone to do something。此處指介面提示，並不保證用戶真的塗了防曬霜。","collocations":"prompt the wearer to apply sunscreen; a screen prompt; prompt users to take action","example":"The swim tracker prompted Leo to apply sunscreen before he went back into the water.","exampleZh":"游泳追蹤器提示利奧在回到水裏前塗防曬霜。","contrast":"Prompt 突出即時下一步操作；cause/force someone to apply 會把提示誇大為必然行動。若只說向感測器傳送訊號，不能推斷人已收到 prompt。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The swimsuit app displays “Apply sunscreen now” and alerts the wearer to do so before starting the swim session.","zh":"泳衣應用程式顯示「現在塗防曬霜」，提示穿着者在開始游泳前這樣做。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The swimsuit app displays “Apply sunscreen now” and prompts the wearer to do so before starting the swim session.","answer":"prompts the wearer to do so","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"notifies the wearer to do so","explanation":"notify 可指傳達訊息，但顯示即時操作指令時 prompt 更能突出下一步行動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"informs the wearer about doing so","explanation":"inform about doing so 只泛指相關資訊，不能保留畫面上的指令。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds the wearer to do so","explanation":"沒有先前計劃或指示，remind 多加既定任務。"},{"letter":"D","text":"prompts the wearer to do so","explanation":"螢幕明確給出下一步指令，prompt the wearer to do so 最切合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"causes the wearer to do so","explanation":"cause 表示已促成實際塗抹，原句只保證介面出現提示。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reports the wearer to do so","explanation":"report the wearer 在這句可能是舉報此人，並非提供操作提示。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the wearer asks the swimsuit’s voice assistant how to prepare for a swim, it alerts her to apply sunscreen, then waits for her reply before naming the next step.","zh":"穿着者問泳衣的語音助理游泳前該如何準備；助理提示她塗防曬霜，然後等她回應才說下一步。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the wearer asks the swimsuit’s voice assistant how to prepare for a swim, it prompts her to apply sunscreen, then waits for her reply before naming the next step.","answer":"prompts her to apply sunscreen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"warns her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"語音助理回答準備步驟時沒有提及危險 UV 程度，warn 的風險意味不是焦點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reports her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"report her to... 會變成舉報穿着者，句法和意思均不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reminds her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"對話沒有交代她先前設定補塗計劃，remind 的已知計劃前提不足。"},{"letter":"D","text":"informs her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"inform her to... 搭配不自然，且此處是互動步驟而非單純資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"prompts her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"語音助理把塗防曬霜當成回應前須處理的下一步，prompt 比中性的 notify 更準確；也不保證她真有塗。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compels her to apply sunscreen","explanation":"compel 表示強迫她實際塗抹，語音提示沒有這樣的能力。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Inform / report · 資訊與行動提示","zh":"中文辨析： Inform 或 report 可以只報告紫外線指數。原句要的是用戶「該塗防曬霜」的提示；只有明示行動時才接近 alert。","point":"Reporting a reading is not necessarily cueing sunscreen application."},{"word":"Alarm / frighten · 強度過高","zh":"中文辨析： Alarm 可指強烈警報或使人驚恐；原文沒有交代那樣的強度。若真有緊急危險警報，才可能用此字。","point":"An alert need not be an alarming emergency."},{"word":"Signal to · 句法及接收者","zh":"中文辨析： Signal to someone that... 可作完整改寫，但不能將原句的 alert 直接換成 signal to 而保留全部結構；向手機發訊號也不自動等於向人提示。","point":"A signal needs a clear recipient and a complete construction."},{"word":"Remind versus first notification · 已知與新知","zh":"中文辨析： 用戶若先前已有補塗計劃，remind 正確；若裝置第一次偵測未知風險並告知用戶，說「提醒」會多加一項未交代的前提。","point":"A reminder presupposes an earlier intention or awareness."},{"word":"Apply / protect / force · 提示不等於完成動作","zh":"中文辨析： 泳衣只是發出提示，不會替穿着者塗防曬霜；protect 或 force 也會把作用及結果說得過滿。","point":"Giving a cue does not establish that sunscreen was applied."}],"moduleNumber":54},{"id":"lesson-055","sourceId":76,"headword":"annoying","title":"Annoying","titleZh":"令人煩厭的","subtitle":"令人煩厭的","description":"原文： 2023 DSE Speaking 6.1〈Super Bowl〉的討論問題問：“Do you think advertisements are annoying?” 這裏是問廣告會否令觀眾煩厭；問題沒有指定廣告吵鬧、重複、阻路或侵犯私隱，這些只可在另有線索的原創練習句中用較窄近詞。Annoying 是形容詞，通常描述造成煩擾的事物；annoyed 描述感到煩擾的人。以下例句皆為原創。","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 DSE Speaking 6.1〈Super Bowl〉的討論問題問：“Do you think advertisements are annoying?” 這裏是問廣告會否令觀眾煩厭；問題沒有指定廣告吵鬧、重複、阻路或侵犯私隱，這些只可在另有線索的原創練習句中用較窄近詞。Annoying 是形容詞，通常描述造成煩擾的事物；annoyed 描述感到煩擾的人。以下例句皆為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["irritating","近義","突出反覆或尖銳刺激引起惱火；一般廣告句可用，具體情境更有辨別力。"],["bothersome","近義，通常較輕","突出不便或打擾，不一定使人強烈生氣。"],["frustrating","有條件","只有當廣告妨礙觀眾完成目標（如閱讀文章）時才精確；單純不喜歡廣告未必「挫敗」。"]],"note":"補充候選覆核： Intrusive 指不受歡迎地闖入注意力或私人空間，適合遮住內容、打斷活動的廣告；不等於所有令人煩的廣告。Aggravating/exasperating 比 annoying 強，多是程度變化，未另設兩組高度重複問題；tedious 要有乏味拖長線索，offensive 要有冒犯內容，均於第 4 節處理。Disturbing 可能是令人不安而不只是煩，不能籠統代換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["明確線索","較準確的說法","不要擅自加上"],"rows":[["尖銳、閃爍、反覆刺激","irritating","冒犯內容"],["小型但實際的麻煩","bothersome","完全無法完成任務"],["目標被廣告阻住","frustrating","只是聲音難聽"],["未邀請而佔據閱讀／聆聽空間","intrusive","必然侵犯數據私隱"]],"note":"原文只問廣告會否 annoying。若沒有上述額外線索，應保留這個較廣的詞，不把所有廣告強行說成 frustrating 或 intrusive。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"irritating","meaning":"刺激得令人惱火","note":"對尖銳聲音、閃爍畫面或反覆出現的訊息所引起的惱火尤其貼切。可說 an irritating advertisement；人則 feel irritated。","collocations":"an irritating jingle; an irritating pop-up ad; find repeated adverts irritating","example":"The advert's shrill jingle became irritating after it played five times in one programme.","exampleZh":"那首廣告歌在同一節目中播了五遍後，尖銳的聲音令人煩躁。","contrast":"比泛稱 annoying 更突出刺激感；不表示廣告必然在道德上 offensive。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The advertisements were annoying because the same high-pitched jingle played loudly between every short segment.","zh":"那些廣告令人煩躁，因為每個短節目段落之間都大聲播放同一段尖銳廣告歌。","upgrade":"The advertisements were irritating because the same high-pitched jingle played loudly between every short segment.","answer":"irritating","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irritating","explanation":"尖銳廣告歌在短段落之間反覆大聲播放，強調感官刺激造成的惱火。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bothersome","explanation":"也可泛指小麻煩，但比 irritating 少了本句尖銳聲音造成的惱火感。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intrusive","explanation":"插播可能打斷節目，但此句突出聲音尖銳、反覆，而非廣告闖入私人畫面。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tedious","explanation":"若廣告很長且乏味才特別貼切；此句沒有說內容冗長。"},{"letter":"E","text":"offensive","explanation":"冒犯需有侮辱內容；聲音尖銳本身不能支持這個判斷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrating","explanation":"若廣告阻住觀眾完成觀看目標才特別合適；此句重點是刺激耳朵。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"I found the advertisement annoying when its bright border flashed repeatedly beside an otherwise readable page.","zh":"那個網頁本來可正常閱讀，但廣告的鮮亮邊框不斷閃動，令我煩躁。","upgrade":"I found the advertisement irritating when its bright border flashed repeatedly beside an otherwise readable page.","answer":"irritating","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"distracting","explanation":"閃動確會分散注意，但此題說的是反覆亮光引起的煩躁感，irritating 更精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"irritating","explanation":"亮邊在可閱讀頁面旁反覆閃動，正是視覺刺激引起惱火。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intrusive","explanation":"若廣告突然佔據閱讀空間可說 intrusive；這裏它仍在頁旁。"},{"letter":"D","text":"frustrating","explanation":"頁面可以閱讀，沒有任務被阻住而產生的挫敗。"},{"letter":"E","text":"monotonous","explanation":"單調指乏味或千篇一律，不是亮邊反覆閃爍的刺激。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unsettling","explanation":"令人不安比一般煩躁更強；原句沒有恐懼或不祥感。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"bothersome","meaning":"造成小麻煩或打擾","note":"指雖未必激怒觀眾，卻使觀看或閱讀變得不方便。常跟 to someone；用於小而反覆的不便很自然。","collocations":"bothersome ads; bothersome interruptions; find the pop-ups bothersome","example":"The small banner was bothersome because it covered the final line of each paragraph.","exampleZh":"那條小型橫幅遮住每段最後一行，因此造成困擾。","contrast":"Bothersome 強調麻煩，未必像 irritating 那樣有強烈情緒刺激；若廣告完全阻止讀者完成任務，frustrating 更能說出挫敗。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The small advertisement was annoying because I had to move the page slightly to see the last word of each line.","zh":"那則小廣告令人困擾，因為我須稍微移動頁面，才看得見每行最後一個字。","upgrade":"The small advertisement was bothersome because I had to move the page slightly to see the last word of each line.","answer":"bothersome","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irritating","explanation":"廣告也可能令某人惱火，但只需稍移頁面的細小麻煩較貼合 bothersome。"},{"letter":"B","text":"frustrating","explanation":"若整篇閱讀目標無法完成才更像 frustrating；此處仍能稍作調整繼續讀。"},{"letter":"C","text":"bothersome","explanation":"每行末字需稍移頁面才看見，正是輕微但實際的不便。"},{"letter":"D","text":"intrusive","explanation":"廣告沒有突然接管全屏，只是小幅遮住行末文字。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tedious","explanation":"乏味評述內容或長度，不能說明這個小廣告造成的操作麻煩。"},{"letter":"F","text":"distracting","explanation":"遮字確會影響注意，但具體麻煩是每行都要移動頁面，bothersome 更完整。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The advertisements were mildly annoying because I had to dismiss a small notification a few times, though the text remained visible.","zh":"我須數次關掉小型廣告通知；雖然文字一直看得見，仍覺得有點麻煩。","upgrade":"The advertisements were bothersome because I had to dismiss a small notification a few times, though the text remained visible.","answer":"bothersome","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"intrusive","explanation":"通知未接管整個閱讀空間，而且可迅速關掉；說 intrusive 會加重其侵擾程度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"irritating","explanation":"有人也可能因多次彈出而惱火，但原句明說只是有點麻煩。"},{"letter":"C","text":"distracting","explanation":"通知可能短暫分散注意，但文字仍可見；此句更着重數次關掉通知的操作麻煩。"},{"letter":"D","text":"bothersome","explanation":"數次關掉小通知是輕微、重複的不便，最貼合 bothersome。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrating","explanation":"閱讀目標仍能完成，沒有被擋住造成的挫敗。"},{"letter":"F","text":"exasperating","explanation":"Exasperating 表強烈惱怒，與原句 mildly 及可輕易關掉的通知不符。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"frustrating","meaning":"令人因受阻而沮喪","note":"觀眾想完成某件事，卻被廣告阻住，例如倒數、無法關閉的畫面。須有明確的受阻目標；frustrated 形容人。","collocations":"a frustrating delay; a frustrating unskippable advert; find the blocked page frustrating","example":"The unskippable advert was frustrating because it stopped her from opening the lesson video on time.","exampleZh":"那段無法略過的廣告阻止她準時打開教學影片，令她感到挫敗。","contrast":"Annoying 可只是煩；frustrating 需要目標受阻。廣告聲音難聽卻不妨礙任何事時，irritating 可能更準。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The unskippable advertisement was annoying because it prevented me from opening the lesson video before class began.","zh":"那段無法略過的廣告阻止我在上課前打開教學影片，令我感到挫敗。","upgrade":"The unskippable advertisement was frustrating because it prevented me from opening the lesson video before class began.","answer":"frustrating","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irritating","explanation":"廣告可能令人惱火，但原句的關鍵是課前無法開到需要的教學影片。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bothersome","explanation":"小麻煩一詞弱於影片開啟目標被無法略過的廣告阻止。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intrusive","explanation":"廣告確實闖入觀看流程，但此句特別說明了被阻住的課前目標。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tedious","explanation":"乏味可描述廣告內容，卻未解釋為何不能準時開影片。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrating","explanation":"無法略過而趕不上課前開片的目標，精確表達挫敗。"},{"letter":"F","text":"worrying","explanation":"Worrying 指擔心可能發生壞事；此句是已發生的操作障礙。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The advertisement was annoying because it covered the Submit button during the final minute before the application deadline, leaving no time to submit.","zh":"廣告在申請截止前最後一分鐘遮住「提交」按鈕，令我來不及提交，十分挫敗。","upgrade":"The advertisement was frustrating because it covered the Submit button during the final minute before the deadline, leaving no time to submit.","answer":"frustrating","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"bothersome","explanation":"Bothersome 只說麻煩，未充分表達申請在截止前完全交不出的結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intrusive","explanation":"廣告遮住按鈕也可說 intrusive，但這題最重要的是提交目標失敗。"},{"letter":"C","text":"irritating","explanation":"Irritating 可說惱火，卻沒有指出截止時間過去後不能提交的挫敗。"},{"letter":"D","text":"stressful","explanation":"截止前被卡住或會有壓力，但 stressful 偏向受壓感而非目標受阻本身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"upsetting","explanation":"失去申請機會可能令人難過，但 upsetting 沒有準確說出受阻的操作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frustrating","explanation":"截止前最後一分鐘按鈕被遮，來不及提交，明確目標落空，frustrating 最切合。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"intrusive","meaning":"侵入注意力／空間的","note":"指廣告未經邀請地闖入閱讀、觀看或私密體驗，例如突然全屏覆蓋文章。它評述呈現方式，不必然說內容侮辱人或違法收集數據。","collocations":"intrusive advertising; intrusive pop-ups; an intrusive full-screen advert","example":"The full-screen advert felt intrusive because it covered the article without warning.","exampleZh":"那則全屏廣告毫無預警地遮住文章，令人覺得它侵擾了閱讀。","contrast":"Intrusive 比一般 annoying 更重視邊界被闖入；小小一則靜態廣告可能令人厭煩，卻未必構成侵擾。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The advertisement felt annoying when it suddenly covered the entire article without warning, though I could close it straight away.","zh":"廣告毫無預警地突然遮住整篇文章，雖然我可以立即關掉，仍覺得閱讀空間受到侵擾。","upgrade":"The advertisement felt intrusive when it suddenly covered the entire article without warning, though I could close it straight away.","answer":"intrusive","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"distracting","explanation":"遮蓋會分心，但關鍵是無預警佔滿閱讀空間，而非一般注意力飄移。"},{"letter":"B","text":"irritating","explanation":"突然遮住文章也可能令人生氣；intrusive 更準確指出它闖入整個閱讀界面。"},{"letter":"C","text":"intrusive","explanation":"即使可立即關掉，全屏無預警接管文章仍是侵擾式呈現。"},{"letter":"D","text":"bothersome","explanation":"Bothersome 能泛指不便，但不足以突顯全屏接管的方式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frustrating","explanation":"因能立即關掉，原句未說閱讀目標最終被阻止，故挫敗不是最佳焦點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"invasive","explanation":"Invasive 可暗示更深的侵犯或私隱問題；原句只有短暫的畫面遮蓋。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The advertisement was annoying because it began playing loudly without permission while the user was reading a quiet memorial page.","zh":"使用者正閱讀一個安靜的紀念網頁，廣告卻未經同意突然大聲播放，令人覺得受到侵擾。","upgrade":"The advertisement was intrusive because it began playing loudly without permission during the user’s quiet reading of a memorial page.","answer":"intrusive","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"irritating","explanation":"突然大聲播出當然也可能惱人，但本句更突出未經同意闖入原本安靜的場合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"distracting","explanation":"聲音可分散注意，但廣告強行進入紀念頁的安靜體驗，intrusive 更完整。"},{"letter":"C","text":"bothersome","explanation":"Bothersome 是泛稱不便，弱於未經同意的大聲闖入。"},{"letter":"D","text":"intrusive","explanation":"未經同意地在寧靜紀念頁播出巨響，正是侵擾閱讀空間。"},{"letter":"E","text":"jarring","explanation":"Jarring 可指突兀刺耳，抓住瞬間感卻少了未獲邀請侵入體驗的邊界。"},{"letter":"F","text":"invasive","explanation":"Invasive 可能暗示深層侵犯或資料取得；原句沒有該種證據。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Annoyed / irritated / frustrated · 人與事的形容詞","zh":"中文辨析： 廣告 is annoying/irritating/frustrating；觀眾 is annoyed/irritated/frustrated。若原句主語是 advertisements，不能直接換成描述觀眾情緒的 -ed 形容詞。","point":"The advert causes the feeling; the viewer experiences it."},{"word":"Frustrating versus merely irritating · 目標有否受阻","zh":"中文辨析： 刺耳廣告可令觀眾煩，但若沒有阻住他閱讀或觀看，未必造成 frustration。若影片被無法略過的廣告卡住，frustrating 就有明確根據。","point":"Frustrating normally implies a blocked goal; irritating need not."},{"word":"Offensive / disturbing · 冒犯或不安不是普通煩擾","zh":"中文辨析： Offensive 要有冒犯或侮辱內容；disturbing 可指令人不安的畫面。原文只問廣告是否煩，沒有說內容涉及歧視或令人恐懼。若具體例句提及侮辱性內容，才應選 offensive。","point":"An ad can be annoying without being offensive or disturbing."},{"word":"Tedious / boring · 乏味與受打擾","zh":"中文辨析： 長而乏味的廣告可以 tedious，但突然打斷閱讀的短廣告雖 annoying，不一定乏味。題目若強調重複冗長，乏味詞才有根據。","point":"Boredom and irritation can coexist but are not identical."},{"word":"Intrusive / invasive · 呈現侵擾與私隱侵害","zh":"中文辨析： 全屏廣告可 intrusive，指打斷與遮蓋；invasive 往往更強，可指侵犯私隱或過度闖入。若沒有蒐集資料的證據，不應把一則遮擋畫面的廣告說成追蹤私隱。","point":"Intrusive placement does not by itself prove invasive data practices."}],"moduleNumber":55},{"id":"lesson-056","sourceId":77,"headword":"annual","title":"Annual","titleZh":"每年的","subtitle":"每年的","description":"原文： 2012 DSE Speaking 3.1〈The Race Is On!〉說主辦者希望把維港橫渡泳賽變成 “an annual event”。此處 annual 修飾 event，指計劃每年舉行，不表示一次活動持續全年，也不保證未來每年必定成事。下列練習為原創教學句。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 DSE Speaking 3.1〈The Race Is On!〉說主辦者希望把維港橫渡泳賽變成 “an annual event”。此處 annual 修飾 event，指計劃每年舉行，不表示一次活動持續全年，也不保證未來每年必定成事。下列練習為原創教學句。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["yearly","直接","可作形容詞說 a yearly event；與每年重複的原義貼近。"],["once-a-year","有條件的形容詞","強調每年一次，作名詞前修飾語；若一年舉行多場，不能使用。"],["each year","需重組句子","副詞片語，須說 the race is held each year；不能直接寫 an each year event。"]],"note":"覆核後的範圍： Every year 是 each year 的近義變體，不另計一項；annually 是對應副詞，亦需改寫成 the race will be held annually；其用法與本課的 held each year 重疊，故不另計。Year-long 指持續一整年；biannual/biennial 的頻率不同；seasonal 只說某季節，均不是此處同義詞。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["想說明的資訊","合適說法","限制"],"rows":[["名詞前形容詞：按年重複","yearly","不表示單次活動長一年"],["用動詞子句說每年舉行","held each year","保留「希望／將會」或「已成慣例」時態"],["特別確定一年只有一次","once-a-year","一年多場不能用"]],"note":"原文是主辦者的 hope。若改寫試卷句，不能把尚在期望中的年度安排說成已有多年的固定賽事。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"yearly","meaning":"每年的；逐年重複","note":"作形容詞放在名詞前，最直接改寫 annual event；用於活動、報告、預算等按年重複的安排。Yearly 也可作副詞，但本課主要練形容詞。","collocations":"a yearly race; yearly celebrations; a yearly report","example":"The club hopes to make the open-water race a yearly event.","exampleZh":"俱樂部希望把公開水域游泳比賽辦成每年一度的活動。","contrast":"Yearly 說重複頻率，不保證任何一次賽事會持續一年；原文的 hope 也仍是計劃而非已實現紀錄。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After the first race, organisers hoped to turn the harbour swim into an annual event.","zh":"首屆賽事之後，主辦者希望把維港泳賽辦成每年舉行的活動。","upgrade":"After the first race, organisers hoped to turn the harbour swim into a yearly event.","answer":"a yearly event","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a year-long event","explanation":"把「每年再舉行」錯改成單次泳賽持續十二個月。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a yearly event","explanation":"作名詞前形容詞，保留主辦者希望每年舉行的頻率。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a monthly event","explanation":"每月一場比原句的年度計劃頻密。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a one-off event","explanation":"只辦一次與主辦者想繼續舉辦相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an event held every two years","explanation":"隔年舉行，不是每年。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an event held twice in the same year","explanation":"一年兩場又比原句頻密。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The race committee publishes an annual safety report after reviewing incidents from that year's event.","zh":"賽事委員會檢視該年活動的事故後，發布一份年度安全報告。","upgrade":"The race committee publishes a yearly safety report after reviewing incidents from that year's event.","answer":"a yearly safety report","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a report covering every month separately","explanation":"逐月分類資料可能出現在報告內，卻不等於報告按年發布。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a report that takes a full year to write","explanation":"寫作需時一年是持續時間，不是年度發布頻率。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a yearly safety report","explanation":"保留每年就當年賽事檢視後發布報告的安排。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a report issued twice a year","explanation":"一年兩份比原句的年度報告頻密。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a report issued only after the first race","explanation":"原句是按年處理各年事故，不只首屆後一份。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a report for events held every two years","explanation":"把每年賽事與報告錯換成隔年活動。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"held each year","meaning":"每年舉行","note":"動詞被動詞組加頻率片語，適合把 annual race/event 改寫成完整子句；each year 也可換 every year。若活動仍只是計劃，須保留 will be/hope to be held，不可改成已確定歷年舉行。","collocations":"a race held each year; hope the event will be held each year; events held each year","example":"The organisers hope the harbour swim will be held each year.","exampleZh":"主辦者希望維港泳賽日後每年都會舉行。","contrast":"與 yearly 意思相近，但句法要重組；held each year 若不加 hope/will，會暗示已形成慣例。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisers said they hoped the cross-harbour race would become an annual competition.","zh":"主辦者說，他們希望維港橫渡賽事日後成為每年舉行的比賽。","upgrade":"The organisers said they hoped the cross-harbour race would be held each year.","answer":"would be held each year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"would be held each year","explanation":"把年度形容詞改成舉辦子句，亦保留「希望」而非已確立的事實。"},{"letter":"B","text":"had already been held every year for decades","explanation":"無據地加入已辦數十年的歷史，與原句未來意向不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"would last for an entire year","explanation":"賽事持續一年不是每年舉行一次。"},{"letter":"D","text":"would be held once every two years","explanation":"隔年舉行不符合主辦者的年度意向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"would be held monthly from now on","explanation":"每月一場改變了原句的頻率。"},{"letter":"F","text":"would be cancelled after its first edition","explanation":"首屆後取消與希望繼續舉辦相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The annual charity swim has taken place in the bay every summer since 2016.","zh":"這項年度慈善泳賽自二零一六年起，每個夏天都在海灣舉行。","upgrade":"The charity swim has been held each year in the bay during summer since 2016.","answer":"is held each year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was once planned but never held","explanation":"原句明說自二零一六年起每夏都有賽事，不只是未實行計劃。"},{"letter":"B","text":"is held twice every summer","explanation":"一夏兩次超過原句的每年一次。"},{"letter":"C","text":"lasts through every month of the year","explanation":"每夏舉行與全年持續不一樣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"is held each year","explanation":"保留自二零一六年起按年舉辦這個已成慣例的事實。"},{"letter":"E","text":"takes place every two summers","explanation":"隔年夏季舉行會與「每個夏天」矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"has happened only in 2016","explanation":"把連續多年舉行縮成只有一年。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"once-a-year","meaning":"每年一次的","note":"複合形容詞置於名詞前，突出每年只有一次該活動。若一年有多輪賽事，雖然活動按年舉行，也不能稱整體為 once-a-year。","collocations":"a once-a-year race; a once-a-year gathering; a once-a-year celebration","example":"The village holds a once-a-year swimming festival on the first Sunday in July.","exampleZh":"村莊每年七月第一個星期日舉辦一次游泳節。","contrast":"比 yearly 多了「一年一次」的數量限制；它不等於 year-long 的「持續一年」。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The club's annual race takes place on one Saturday each August; it does not hold a second race that year.","zh":"俱樂部的年度賽事每年八月只在一個星期六舉行，該年不會再辦第二場。","upgrade":"The club's once-a-year race takes place on one Saturday each August; it does not hold a second race that year.","answer":"once-a-year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"year-long","explanation":"一個星期六的賽事不會持續整年。"},{"letter":"B","text":"twice-yearly","explanation":"原句明說當年沒有第二場。"},{"letter":"C","text":"biennial","explanation":"每兩年一次與每年八月不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"seasonal but held every weekend","explanation":"每個週末舉行比一年一場頻密得多。"},{"letter":"E","text":"once-a-year","explanation":"強調每年只有這一場，吻合八月單日賽事。"},{"letter":"F","text":"one-time-only","explanation":"此詞指只辦一次，以後也不再辦；原句每年重複。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The annual registration window for the school's swim opens for one week every April and does not reopen until the following year.","zh":"學校泳賽每年的報名時段在四月開放一星期，其後要到下一年才再次開放。","upgrade":"The once-a-year registration window for the school's swim opens for one week every April and does not reopen until the following year.","answer":"once-a-year","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"year-long","explanation":"報名只開放一星期，不是全年開放；年度重開不等於持續一年。"},{"letter":"B","text":"monthly","explanation":"若每月開放，四月之後便不必等到翌年。"},{"letter":"C","text":"twice-yearly","explanation":"一年兩次與句子明說「下一年才再次開放」相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"once-a-year","explanation":"說明報名每年只開放一次，同時保留每次可持續一星期。"},{"letter":"E","text":"biennial","explanation":"每兩年一次與每年四月開放不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"one-time-only","explanation":"只開放一次後永不再開，與翌年重開不同。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Year-long / all-year · 持續時間不是出現頻率","zh":"中文辨析： 原文希望比賽每年再辦；一場泳賽本身不會持續整年。Year-long 適合一年期課程，all-year 適合全年開放服務；不能代替 annual event。","point":"Annual describes recurrence; year-long describes duration."},{"word":"Biannual / biennial / semiannual · 次數或隔年","zh":"中文辨析： Semiannual 通常指每年兩次，biennial 指每兩年一次；biannual 有時被人理解為一年兩次，也有歧義，正式語境應說清楚。原文是一年一次的意向，不能憑這些詞替換。","point":"Twice a year and every two years are not the same as once each year."},{"word":"Seasonal / monthly · 時間單位不同","zh":"中文辨析： Seasonal 說與某季節有關，不必然只辦一次；monthly 是每月一次。若泳賽每月辦一場，不能稱為一次 annual race。某活動雖每年夏季舉行，可同時是 seasonal 和 annual，但兩詞各自說明不同方面。","point":"Seasonality can coexist with annual recurrence, but it does not entail it."},{"word":"Anniversary / calendar year · 日期與時間跨度","zh":"中文辨析： Anniversary 是某事發生滿一年的紀念日，不必然有新賽事；calendar year 指一月到十二月的時段。原句要說未來的泳賽按年舉行，不是界定紀念日或報告年度。","point":"A date or a year-long period is not itself a recurring event."}],"moduleNumber":56},{"id":"lesson-057","sourceId":84,"headword":"appealing","title":"Appealing","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2023 Paper 4 article contrasts commercials “creating laughter” with those “appealing to the heart.” It calls one advertisement heartwarming and describes emotional connection to viewers. The source uses appealing as a participle in a verb phrase, not as the adjective an appealing advertisement meaning attractive. [2023 Paper 4, set 6.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/887877008/2023-Paper-4-2).","sourceSense":"The 2023 Paper 4 article contrasts commercials “creating laughter” with those “appealing to the heart.” It calls one advertisement heartwarming and describes emotional connection to viewers. The source uses appealing as a participle in a verb phrase, not as the adjective an appealing advertisement meaning attractive. [2023 Paper 4, set 6.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/887877008/2023-Paper-4-2).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["attractive","Adjective for general appeal; false as a direct substitute for participial appealing to the heart."],["enticing","Adjective suggesting temptation to act or buy; lacks the source’s emotional mechanism."],["inviting","Adjective for a welcoming prospect; also fails to express being emotionally moved."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Touching viewers’ hearts, moving viewers, and creating an emotional connection with viewers are central recasts and are taught. Resonating with viewers is taught only when the story reflects a recognisable experience or value. Stirring emotions largely overlaps with moving viewers; tugging at heartstrings adds a stronger, possibly sentimental idiom and is contrasted rather than padded into the guide. Persuading can be a commercial aim without describing the emotional route. Appealing as an adjective belongs to another grammatical construction."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["觀眾反應或廣告做法","佳用表達"],"rows":[["溫情故事令觀眾受感動","touching viewers’ hearts"],["強調觀眾的情緒反應","moving viewers"],["觀眾認出自身經驗或共同價值","resonating with viewers"],["故事逐步令觀眾關心人物／主題","creating an emotional connection with viewers"]],"note":"這四種表達均需有情感線索；不要只見 appealing 就改作一般「吸引人」的形容詞。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"touching viewers’ hearts","meaning":"打動觀眾的心","note":"故事令觀眾有溫暖、同情或感動的情緒反應；可把動詞片語 appealing to the heart 改寫為 touching viewers’ hearts。","collocations":"touch viewers’ hearts; a story that touches the audience’s heart.","example":"The story of a lost dog finding its family touched viewers’ hearts.","exampleZh":"走失的狗尋回家人的故事打動了觀眾的心。","contrast":"此詞強調觀眾受感動，不只是覺得廣告好看或好笑；heart 不是實際身體器官。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The short film was appealing to the heart by showing a child welcome a rescued dog home; the scene brought quiet smiles and tears.","zh":"這套短片展示孩子迎接獲救狗兒回家的一幕，令觀眾默默微笑、眼眶泛淚，以此打動人心。","upgrade":"The short film was touching viewers’ hearts by showing a child welcome a rescued dog home; the scene brought quiet smiles and tears.","answer":"touching viewers’ hearts","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"charming viewers","explanation":"狗兒或許討喜，但題句重點是重聚一幕帶來溫暖和淚水，而不只是可愛魅力。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reassuring viewers","explanation":"觀眾未表現先前的焦慮，不能把感動改成疑慮得到安撫。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resonating with viewers","explanation":"題句沒有說觀眾有相同走失狗兒經歷，未足以指特定的個人共鳴。"},{"letter":"D","text":"touching viewers’ hearts","explanation":"重聚令觀眾微笑又落淚，touching viewers’ hearts 指這種溫情感動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"evoking nostalgia","explanation":"沒有共同往昔的回憶線索，不能把眼淚歸為懷舊。"},{"letter":"F","text":"inspiring viewers to act","explanation":"畫面或許令人願意幫助動物，但原句沒有觀眾採取或想採取行動。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The advertisement was appealing to the heart when a new pupil unfolded a welcome note signed by classmates she had not yet met.","zh":"廣告展示一名新同學打開從未見面的同班同學聯名寫的歡迎字條，以此打動人心。","upgrade":"The advertisement was touching viewers’ hearts when a new pupil unfolded a welcome note signed by classmates she had not yet met.","answer":"touching viewers’ hearts","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"touching viewers’ hearts","explanation":"陌生同學主動歡迎新生的善意令人感動，touching viewers’ hearts 最貼切。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reassuring viewers about safety","explanation":"歡迎字條表達接納，但廣告沒有安全疑慮需要安撫。"},{"letter":"C","text":"evoking viewers’ nostalgia","explanation":"故事發生在新同學剛入班時，未提供觀眾懷念自身往昔的線索。"},{"letter":"D","text":"amusing viewers with wordplay","explanation":"字條或許友善，但沒有文字遊戲或笑話。"},{"letter":"E","text":"persuading viewers with proof","explanation":"沒有事實論證，不能把溫暖情景改作證據式說服。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resonating with former classmates","explanation":"題句未說觀眾曾經歷相同入學故事，不能假設特定校友共鳴。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"moving viewers","meaning":"令觀眾感動","note":"強調廣告使觀眾產生較深的情感反應；move 作及物動詞時可說 move viewers。","collocations":"move viewers; a moving commercial; be moved by a story.","example":"The reunion scene moved viewers because the family had been apart for years.","exampleZh":"團聚一幕令觀眾感動，因為這家人已分隔多年。","contrast":"Move 不是指把觀眾移動到另一處；也不等於已說服他們購買。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Rather than making jokes, the commercial was appealing to the heart by showing a father quietly support his daughter through a difficult year; several viewers said they cried.","zh":"廣告沒有說笑，而是展示父親在艱難的一年裏默默支持女兒；數名觀眾說自己哭了，廣告藉此訴諸情感。","upgrade":"Rather than making jokes, the commercial was moving viewers by showing a father quietly support his daughter through a difficult year; several viewers said they cried.","answer":"moving viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"charming viewers","explanation":"父親或可親，但觀眾哭泣顯示的情緒強度超過一般討喜。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reassuring viewers","explanation":"故事沒有提出讓觀眾安心的疑慮或解決辦法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"inspiring viewers to compete","explanation":"父親支持女兒不是鼓勵觀眾參加競賽。"},{"letter":"D","text":"evoking nostalgia","explanation":"沒有過去共同年代或回憶線索，哭泣未必是懷舊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"merely attracting attention","explanation":"吸引注意只是初步反應，不能概括題句明示的眼淚。"},{"letter":"F","text":"moving viewers","explanation":"觀眾直接說自己哭了，moving viewers 保留這個明確的感動反應。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The public-service video was appealing to the heart by showing both a farmer’s loss after a flood and neighbours helping rebuild; viewers described grief and hope together.","zh":"公益短片展示農夫在洪水後的損失，以及鄰居協助重建；觀眾說自己同時感到悲傷和希望，短片藉此訴諸情感。","upgrade":"The public-service video was moving viewers by showing both a farmer’s loss after a flood and neighbours helping rebuild; viewers described grief and hope together.","answer":"moving viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"evoking sympathy only","explanation":"同情農夫只是其中一面，不能保留鄰居重建帶來的希望。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reassuring viewers that nothing was lost","explanation":"農夫明明遭受損失，不能說影片保證沒有任何損失。"},{"letter":"C","text":"moving viewers","explanation":"觀眾同時感到悲傷和希望，moving viewers 能涵蓋這個深刻而混合的情緒反應。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charming viewers with cuteness","explanation":"可愛逗趣不是洪水損失與重建的情緒核心。"},{"letter":"E","text":"inspiring viewers only to donate","explanation":"原句未說觀眾捐款，亦不只描述行動號召。"},{"letter":"F","text":"evoking childhood nostalgia","explanation":"洪水與重建沒有個人童年回憶線索，不能指定懷舊。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"resonating with viewers","meaning":"令觀眾產生共鳴","note":"觀眾從故事中認出自身經驗或共同價值而產生情感聯繫；只有題句提供這種可辨認的連結才合適。","collocations":"resonate with viewers; resonate with parents; a message that resonates.","example":"The story about caring for an ageing parent resonated with viewers who had faced the same challenge.","exampleZh":"照顧年邁父母的故事，令曾面對同樣難題的觀眾產生共鳴。","contrast":"Resonate 不只是令人傷感；強調觀眾與故事之間的相似經驗或價值。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The ad was appealing to the heart because its story of balancing school and family work mirrored many teenagers’ own lives.","zh":"廣告以兼顧學業和家庭工作的故事，呼應不少年輕人的生活經驗，因而打動人心。","upgrade":"The ad was resonating with viewers because its story of balancing school and family work mirrored many teenagers’ own lives.","answer":"resonating with viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"moving viewers with tragedy","explanation":"題句沒有悲劇；單說被感動也不及「映照自身經歷」具體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reassuring viewers about exams","explanation":"兼顧家務和學業不是保證考試順利。"},{"letter":"C","text":"evoking nostalgia for childhood","explanation":"觀眾正是青少年，故事是他們當下生活，不是懷念童年。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charming viewers with humour","explanation":"沒有幽默線索，不能把貼近生活改成被笑料逗樂。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resonating with viewers","explanation":"故事直接映照青少年自己的生活，resonating with viewers 最準確指出共鳴來源。"},{"letter":"F","text":"inspiring viewers to buy","explanation":"原句沒有購買行為或鼓勵下單。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The rehabilitation ad was appealing to the heart for former athletes because its scene of learning to walk again reminded them of their own recoveries.","zh":"康復廣告中重新學習走路的一幕，令曾當運動員的觀眾想起自己康復的經歷，因此打動他們。","upgrade":"The rehabilitation ad was resonating with former athletes because its scene of learning to walk again reminded them of their own recoveries.","answer":"resonating with viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merely charming viewers","explanation":"重新學習走路不是單靠可愛、討喜來吸引。"},{"letter":"B","text":"resonating with viewers","explanation":"曾受傷的運動員從畫面認出自己的康復經歷，resonating with viewers 點出共享經驗。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reassuring all viewers","explanation":"廣告未保證所有觀眾都會康復，不能說全面安撫。"},{"letter":"D","text":"moving viewers through an unfamiliar tragedy","explanation":"對這群人而言經歷並不陌生；只說悲劇也漏掉自身經驗的對應。"},{"letter":"E","text":"evoking nostalgia for old sports victories","explanation":"畫面喚起的是康復過程，不是舊日勝利的懷舊感。"},{"letter":"F","text":"creating immediate pressure to donate","explanation":"沒有立即捐款的訊息或壓力。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"creating an emotional connection with viewers","meaning":"與觀眾建立情感連繫","note":"廣告透過故事使觀眾對人物、主題或品牌產生情感連結；比一次性「感動」更強調關係的建立。","collocations":"create an emotional connection with viewers; build a connection through storytelling.","example":"The campaign created an emotional connection with viewers by following one family over several years.","exampleZh":"這項宣傳透過多年追蹤一個家庭的故事，與觀眾建立情感連繫。","contrast":"Emotional connection 不保證買賣或忠誠；它描述感受與故事之間的連結。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The campaign was appealing to the heart through a series of stories that helped viewers care about the same characters over time.","zh":"宣傳活動透過連續故事，令觀眾逐漸關心同一批角色，以此建立情感連繫。","upgrade":"The campaign was creating an emotional connection with viewers through a series of stories that helped them care about the same characters over time.","answer":"creating an emotional connection with viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"evoking a brief feeling of sympathy","explanation":"短暫同情不足以表達觀眾隨時間持續關心同一角色。"},{"letter":"B","text":"charming viewers with one cute image","explanation":"單張可愛圖片可能令人喜歡，但不能代表連續故事累積的情感投入。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reassuring viewers with a promise","explanation":"題句沒有承諾，也不是解除顧慮。"},{"letter":"D","text":"creating an emotional connection with viewers","explanation":"連續故事令觀眾逐步關心角色，creating an emotional connection with viewers 強調持續建立的關係。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resonating through a shared memory","explanation":"沒有說觀眾與角色共享相同回憶；其關心是隨故事進展形成。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stirring surprise at each ending","explanation":"驚喜結尾可以帶來即時情緒，但不能解釋觀眾長期關心角色。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The community ad was appealing to the heart by inviting viewers to share their own stories and then showing how those stories shaped later campaign messages.","zh":"社區廣告邀請觀眾分享自身故事，之後展示這些故事如何影響往後的宣傳訊息，以此與觀眾建立情感連繫。","upgrade":"The community ad was creating an emotional connection with viewers by inviting them to share their own stories and then showing how those stories shaped later campaign messages.","answer":"creating an emotional connection with viewers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"evoking sympathy for strangers only","explanation":"觀眾不只同情陌生人，還親自分享並影響後續內容。"},{"letter":"B","text":"inspiring a one-time donation","explanation":"沒有一次性捐款要求；後續宣傳展示持續關係。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reassuring viewers that nothing will change","explanation":"宣傳內容正因觀眾故事而改變，不能說一切保持不變。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charming viewers with a mascot","explanation":"沒有吉祥物；情感來自參與及故事被採納。"},{"letter":"E","text":"appealing to nostalgia alone","explanation":"觀眾分享的是各自經歷，題句不把情感限定為懷舊。"},{"letter":"F","text":"creating an emotional connection with viewers","explanation":"觀眾參與並看見自己的故事延續到後續訊息，creating an emotional connection with viewers 說明雙向、持續的連結。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"appealing to the heart / appealing adjective","zh":"中文辨析： 來源的 appealing 是現在分詞，搭配 to the heart；an appealing ad 的形容詞只說廣告吸引，未必訴諸情感。","point":"A participial emotional appeal is narrower than a generally attractive advertisement."},{"word":"attractive / enticing / inviting","zh":"中文辨析： 三個原映射形容詞分別偏向吸引、誘惑行動、令人想參與；皆沒有保留「打動內心」這種情緒機制。若另有情緒線索，可寫完整改句，不能逐字替換分詞。","point":"A general invitation or temptation does not itself express heartfelt impact."},{"word":"touch / resonate / emotional connection","zh":"中文辨析： Touch 重感動一刻；resonate 要有觀眾認得的經驗或價值；connection 可隨故事逐漸建立。題句沒有共鳴線索時，不應硬用 resonate。","point":"Emotional impact, shared experience, and an ongoing bond overlap but differ."},{"word":"laughter / sentiment / purchase","zh":"中文辨析： 來源刻意對比笑聲與溫情；令人感動不等於製造笑聲，也不等於已令觀眾購買。過度煽情的 tug at heartstrings 又較強。","point":"The emotion in the ad is a method, not proof of a sales outcome."},{"word":"persuade / inform","zh":"中文辨析： 廣告可用事實說明或理由說服，但這兩種做法不一定令觀眾感動；來源說的是故事建立情感連繫。","point":"Informing or persuading can occur without appealing to the heart."}],"moduleNumber":57},{"id":"lesson-058","sourceId":90,"headword":"apprenticeship","title":"Apprenticeship","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2013 set 2.1 article defines an apprenticeship as “a formal, on-the-job training programme” in which a trainee learns a craft or trade under a skilled master. It then describes a Swiss dual track combining vocational education with paid work training. The word is a count noun for the whole structured programme, not merely any day spent working. [2013 Paper 4, set 2.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/963126936/2013-DSE-Paper-4-Examiner-Ver).","sourceSense":"The 2013 set 2.1 article defines an apprenticeship as “a formal, on-the-job training programme” in which a trainee learns a craft or trade under a skilled master. It then describes a Swiss dual track combining vocational education with paid work training. The word is a count noun for the whole structured programme, not merely any day spent working. [2013 Paper 4, set 2.1](https://www.scribd.com/document/963126936/2013-DSE-Paper-4-Examiner-Ver).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["work-based training","Contextual: preserves the workplace basis, but needs a programme and supervised trade focus to capture the full source."],["vocational training","Contextual broader occupational training; can occur only in class, so workplace context must remain."],["on-the-job learning","Contextual process, not necessarily formal; recast as a structured programme when replacing apprenticeship."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Dual education and training programme is taught for the Swiss passage’s alternating school/work route; it is not universal to every apprenticeship. Traineeship is broader and can be shorter or less structured; internship often emphasises work experience instead of trade mastery. Trade school is a school, not the whole supervised work arrangement. Work placement is a component, not necessarily a full training programme. Earn-while-you-learn captures pay plus training in the Swiss example but not the formal master-guided trade structure, so it is explained as a near phrase rather than a guide term."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子強調","改寫選擇"],"rows":[["在真實工作場所接受正式指導","work-based training programme"],["做實際工作時練習並獲回饋","on-the-job training programme"],["培養特定可就業職業技能，且句中保留在職部分","vocational training programme"],["職校課與僱主處訓練交替","dual education and training programme"]],"note":"學徒制是整段有組織的受訓路徑；不能只憑「有工作」、「有課堂」或「有薪水」便認定完全等同。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"work-based training programme","meaning":"以工作場所為本的訓練計劃","note":"強調技能訓練主要在實際工作場所進行；需補出正式計劃與師傅指導，才足以代替來源的學徒訓練。","collocations":"a work-based training programme; work-based training under a mentor; join a work-based programme.","example":"The young carpenter joined a work-based training programme supervised by a master craftsperson.","exampleZh":"這名年輕木匠參加由資深工匠指導、以工作場所為本的訓練計劃。","contrast":"單說在工作中學習可以很隨意；來源的 apprenticeship 還有正式安排及可售技能。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The carpentry apprenticeship placed each trainee in a workshop with an experienced craftsperson for a formal two-year course.","zh":"木工學徒計劃安排每名學員在工場由資深工匠指導，完成兩年的正式課程。","upgrade":"The work-based carpentry training programme placed each trainee in a workshop with an experienced craftsperson for a formal two-year course.","answer":"work-based training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"work-based training programme","explanation":"正式兩年課程以工場及工匠指導為核心，work-based training programme 合適。"},{"letter":"B","text":"brief work observation","explanation":"短暫旁觀沒有兩年的實際技能訓練。"},{"letter":"C","text":"classroom-only course","explanation":"原句明說學員在工場由工匠指導，不是只上課室課。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unpaid holiday job","explanation":"臨時工作可能有收入，卻不等於正式的木工訓練。"},{"letter":"E","text":"short work placement","explanation":"短期工作見習有實地接觸，卻未必有題句明說的兩年正式木工課程和師傅指導。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unsupervised workshop job","explanation":"在工場無人指導地工作，缺少原句資深工匠帶領的系統訓練。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Under the electrical apprenticeship, trainees repair equipment beside qualified technicians and follow a documented skills plan.","zh":"在電工學徒計劃中，學員跟合資格技術員一起修理設備，並按有記錄的技能訓練計劃學習。","upgrade":"Under the work-based electrical training programme, trainees repair equipment beside qualified technicians and follow a documented skills plan.","answer":"work-based training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"technical lecture series","explanation":"講座可以教授理論，卻不涵蓋並肩修理設備。"},{"letter":"B","text":"informal job shadowing","explanation":"單純跟看沒有明確技能計劃，也未必親手操作。"},{"letter":"C","text":"temporary technician job","explanation":"臨時技術員職位可涉及維修，但未必按記錄的技能計劃接受指導。"},{"letter":"D","text":"work-based training programme","explanation":"與技術員實作加上有記錄的技能計劃，支持 work-based training programme。"},{"letter":"E","text":"technical college course only","explanation":"只在技術學院上課未保留題句與合資格技術員在工場一同修理的安排。"},{"letter":"F","text":"employment trial without teaching","explanation":"沒有教學的試用工作與記錄在案的技能訓練相反。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"on-the-job training programme","meaning":"在職訓練計劃","note":"強調學員在執行真實工作時受教、練習和回饋；需有正式計劃才足以表示完整的學徒安排。","collocations":"an on-the-job training programme; receive on-the-job training; supervised on-the-job practice.","example":"The bakery’s on-the-job training programme let trainees practise dough preparation under a baker’s supervision.","exampleZh":"麵包店的在職訓練計劃讓學員在麵包師監督下練習準備麵糰。","contrast":"On-the-job learning 可以是偶然學到東西；training programme 明確有安排及監督。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"During her baking apprenticeship, Rosa learned each technique while working at the counter and received daily feedback from the head baker.","zh":"在烘焙學徒訓練期間，羅莎一邊在店內工作一邊學習各項技術，並每日獲首席麵包師回饋。","upgrade":"During her on-the-job training programme in baking, Rosa learned each technique while working at the counter and received daily feedback from the head baker.","answer":"on-the-job training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"independent study course","explanation":"自主學習沒有題句明說的師傅每日回饋。"},{"letter":"B","text":"work experience only","explanation":"純工作體驗可讓人觀看，但不足以表達有系統地教授各項技術。"},{"letter":"C","text":"on-the-job training programme","explanation":"工作同時學技術且每日獲師傅回饋，on-the-job training programme 點出邊做邊受訓。"},{"letter":"D","text":"classroom skills course","explanation":"課室技能課程或能教烘焙理論，卻沒有她在櫃檯工作時每天得到師傅回饋的環節。"},{"letter":"E","text":"remote tutorial package","explanation":"遠端教程缺少店內實作及首席麵包師現場指導。"},{"letter":"F","text":"paid bakery shift without instruction","explanation":"受薪烘焙輪班若沒有每天的教導和回饋，仍不是題句的在職訓練計劃。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The mechanics’ apprenticeship required trainees to service real vehicles under supervision and record what each shift taught them.","zh":"機械維修學徒計劃要求學員在監督下維修真車，並記錄每更學到的知識。","upgrade":"The mechanics’ on-the-job training programme required trainees to service real vehicles under supervision and record what each shift taught them.","answer":"on-the-job training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"school-only theory course","explanation":"純課堂理論不會讓學員在真車上逐更維修。"},{"letter":"B","text":"informal weekend hobby","explanation":"週末興趣活動沒有此處的正式督導和每更學習紀錄。"},{"letter":"C","text":"work experience placement","explanation":"工作體驗可以接觸真實車輛，但未必有按班次記錄所學和受監督的正式訓練。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unsupervised repair job","explanation":"無監督的修車工作漏掉題句導師指導和每班學習紀錄。"},{"letter":"E","text":"one-time safety briefing","explanation":"一次性簡介無法涵蓋逐更練習與記錄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"on-the-job training programme","explanation":"在真車上實作、有人監督並按更記錄所學，on-the-job training programme 符合。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"vocational training programme","meaning":"職業技能訓練計劃","note":"強調為特定職業或工藝培養可就業技能；比 apprenticeship 廣，可只有課堂訓練，故此課改寫需保留工作場所及導師。","collocations":"a vocational training programme in plumbing; vocational skills; workplace-based vocational training.","example":"The plumbing vocational training programme combines college lessons with guided work on real building sites.","exampleZh":"水管維修職業技能訓練計劃結合學院課堂與真實建築工地上的指導實習。","contrast":"只上學校職業課也可叫 vocational training；來源學徒計劃另有在職實習。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The Swiss apprenticeship prepared trainees for a skilled trade through workshops, assessed practice and supervised work with an employer.","zh":"瑞士學徒計劃透過工場課、受評核的練習和在僱主督導下工作，培養學員從事技術行業。","upgrade":"The Swiss vocational training programme prepared trainees for a skilled trade through workshops, assessed practice and supervised work with an employer.","answer":"vocational training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"general academic degree","explanation":"一般學術學位不一定包括工藝實作和僱主督導。"},{"letter":"B","text":"vocational training programme","explanation":"工藝技能、評核及僱主督導把這項計劃界定為 vocational training programme，句子保留在職部分。"},{"letter":"C","text":"internship focused on observation","explanation":"只以旁觀為主的實習未能涵蓋工藝訓練、評核實作和僱主監督。"},{"letter":"D","text":"temporary work placement only","explanation":"短期工作安排只是一部分，漏掉工場課與評核。"},{"letter":"E","text":"trade school without workplace practice","explanation":"單在職校讀書可以培養職業知識，但漏掉題句與僱主一同受訓的部分。"},{"letter":"F","text":"trade licensing exam","explanation":"牌照考試是結果考核，不是整個技能培訓計劃。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For adults changing careers, the machinery apprenticeship combined a technical course with supervised factory shifts so trainees could qualify as machine technicians.","zh":"這項機械學徒計劃供轉行成年人參加，結合技術課程與受督導的工廠輪班，讓學員取得機械技術員資格。","upgrade":"For adults changing careers, the vocational training programme in machinery combined a technical course with supervised factory shifts so trainees could qualify as machine technicians.","answer":"vocational training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"brief machine induction","explanation":"短暫機器操作簡介不足以培養取得技術員資格的完整技能。"},{"letter":"B","text":"short factory placement","explanation":"短期廠房見習未必包括資格課程與受監督輪班的完整訓練。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unsupervised work trial","explanation":"無督導試工與原句明示的課程及監督相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"equipment sales course","explanation":"設備銷售課重在銷售，不是培養機械技術員的維修和操作技能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"vocational training programme","explanation":"轉行者透過課堂與受督導實作取得技術員資格，vocational training programme 抓住職業技能目標。"},{"letter":"F","text":"technical lecture series only","explanation":"只聽技術講座沒有題句機械廠內受監督的實作輪班。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"dual education and training programme","meaning":"學校與工作場所雙軌訓練","note":"僅在明說一部分時間於職業學校上課、另一部分在僱主處受訓時使用；是來源瑞士例子的制度特點，不是所有學徒制的必要名稱。","collocations":"a dual education and training programme; alternate classroom study with paid workplace training.","example":"The dual education and training programme sends trainees to college two days a week and to workshops on other weekdays.","exampleZh":"這項學校與工作場所雙軌訓練計劃安排學員每週兩天到學院上課，其餘工作天到工場實習。","contrast":"Dual 指兩個互補學習場域，不是同時讀兩個無關課程；沒課堂部分時不應硬稱雙軌。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In this Swiss apprenticeship, trainees study in a vocational school on Mondays and Tuesdays and train with a paid employer for the rest of the week.","zh":"在這項瑞士學徒計劃中，學員每週一、二於職業學校上課，其餘日子受薪在僱主處受訓。","upgrade":"In this Swiss dual education and training programme, trainees study in a vocational school on Mondays and Tuesdays and train with a paid employer for the rest of the week.","answer":"dual education and training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"dual education and training programme","explanation":"每週同時安排職校課與受薪在職訓練，dual education and training programme 準確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"school-only vocational course","explanation":"只上職校課會漏掉其餘工作天的僱主訓練。"},{"letter":"C","text":"two unrelated internships","explanation":"這是同一職業計劃的兩個場域，不是兩份互不相關的實習。"},{"letter":"D","text":"paid work without lessons","explanation":"只說受薪工作會漏掉週一、二的正式課堂。"},{"letter":"E","text":"vocational course followed by an unrelated job","explanation":"先讀職課再做無關工作，不等於題句一周內學校與同一僱主訓練互相配合的雙軌計劃。"},{"letter":"F","text":"work placement without school study","explanation":"只有工作見習會漏掉題句每周一、二在職業學校上課。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The furniture-making apprenticeship alternates a term of college design lessons with a term of paid supervised work in a furniture workshop.","zh":"家具製作學徒計劃一學期在學院學習設計，下一學期則在家具工場接受有薪督導訓練，兩者交替進行。","upgrade":"The furniture-making dual education and training programme alternates a term of college design lessons with a term of paid supervised work in a furniture workshop.","answer":"dual education and training programme","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"classroom-only design course","explanation":"只學設計課會漏掉下一學期受督導的工場工作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"paid work without study","explanation":"只說有薪工作會漏掉正式學院設計課。"},{"letter":"C","text":"two unrelated college majors","explanation":"學院課與工場訓練服務同一家具工藝，不是兩個無關主修。"},{"letter":"D","text":"dual education and training programme","explanation":"這次以整個學期輪換學院及有薪工場，dual education and training programme 仍指出雙場域學習。"},{"letter":"E","text":"work placement without supervision","explanation":"單獨工作安排未必有學院學期和正式督導。"},{"letter":"F","text":"workplace course without college study","explanation":"只有工場課程未保留與學院設計課交替的雙軌安排。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"apprenticeship / internship","zh":"中文辨析： Internship 常為短期工作體驗；來源的 apprenticeship 是正式、受師傅指導、培養可就業工藝的計劃。某實習也可有訓練，但不能自動當成學徒制。","point":"Work exposure alone does not establish a structured trade apprenticeship."},{"word":"training programme / casual learning","zh":"中文辨析： On-the-job learning 可偶然發生；來源定義明說 formal programme。改寫須保留計劃、指導與職業技能。","point":"Informal experience is narrower evidence than an organised programme."},{"word":"vocational school / apprenticeship","zh":"中文辨析： 職校教授職業技能，但來源的學徒安排還有僱主處的在職訓練。單說 trade school 會漏掉工作場所部分。","point":"Schooling is one component of the Swiss dual track."},{"word":"dual track / all apprenticeships","zh":"中文辨析： 瑞士段落描述學校與受薪工作並行的雙軌安排；其他地方或計劃形式可能不同，不可說每個學徒制都有同一時間表。","point":"Dual education describes the documented Swiss structure, not a universal schedule."},{"word":"paid job / supervised training","zh":"中文辨析： 受薪工作不一定教授技能；來源的學徒制有師傅指導及可就業工藝目標。Earn-while-you-learn 可概括薪酬與學習，但本身仍不足以說明正式結構。","point":"Payment does not by itself make a job an apprenticeship."}],"moduleNumber":58},{"id":"lesson-059","sourceId":20,"headword":"actors","title":"Actors","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 King of Comedy individual-response question asks whether famous actors should be paid a lot. Actors here are people who portray characters in film or on stage; in this film context the pay question is about screen acting.","sourceSense":"The 2012 King of Comedy individual-response question asks whether famous actors should be paid a lot. Actors here are people who portray characters in film or on stage; in this film context the pay question is about screen acting.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["performers","contextual: wider category, acting clue needed"],["players","false in contemporary film-pay question"],["cast members","contextual: requires a specified production"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Film stars 因來源明說 famous actors 而加入；thespians 偏舞台及文藝書面語，不適合本口語提問；players 在現代用法容易誤作運動員。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["performers","表演藝術工作者的廣義名稱；若要專指演戲，句子須維持電影角色線索。","單說 performers 也包括歌手等；原題的 actors 更精確。"],["cast members","屬於某一指定電影或製作演出班底的人；比泛稱 actors 多了歸屬。","沒有指定製作時，不能把所有知名演員稱為其 cast members。"],["screen actors","在電影或電視鏡頭前飾演角色的人，保留電影語境。","比 actors 更窄：舞台演員未必是 screen actor。"],["film stars","在電影中演出而且知名度高的演員；比一般 actors 加入成名程度。","不是每個演員都是明星；來源問 famous actors，才容許這個較窄說法。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 只需泛稱演出者用 performers；特定一部電影的演員集合用 cast members；要與舞台演員對比可用 screen actors；原句明說知名電影演員才適用 film stars。Director 管導演工作，viewer 看電影，均非演員。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"performers","meaning":"表演者","note":"表演藝術工作者的廣義名稱；若要專指演戲，句子須維持電影角色線索。","collocations":"screen performers; pay performers.","example":"The film’s performers brought its characters to life.","exampleZh":"影片的表演者令角色栩栩如生。","contrast":"單說 performers 也包括歌手等；原題的 actors 更精確。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The actors in the film portrayed the main characters, rather than singing on stage.","zh":"片中演員飾演主要角色，並非在舞台唱歌。","upgrade":"The performers in the film portrayed the main characters, rather than singing on stage.","answer":"performers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"singers","explanation":"句子明說演員演主要角色而非台上唱歌，singers 把演出種類改了。"},{"letter":"B","text":"directors","explanation":"Directors 指導拍攝，未必親自演出片中主要角色。"},{"letter":"C","text":"performers","explanation":"Performers 可泛稱在電影中演出角色的人，保留本句的演出動作。"},{"letter":"D","text":"stunt doubles","explanation":"Stunt doubles 代演危險動作，不能概括所有演主要角色的人。"},{"letter":"E","text":"viewers","explanation":"Viewers 是看電影的人，不是片中扮演角色的人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"producers","explanation":"Producers 負責製作安排，與扮演主角的工作不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The animated film used actors to voice its animal characters, although none appeared on camera.","zh":"這部動畫電影由演員為動物角色配音，雖然他們都沒有在鏡頭前出現。","upgrade":"The animated film used performers to voice its animal characters, although none appeared on camera.","answer":"performers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"players","explanation":"Players 在現代英語多指球員或遊戲參與者，不能清楚表示動畫配音演員。"},{"letter":"B","text":"directors","explanation":"Directors 指導配音及製作，不一定親自為動物角色獻聲。"},{"letter":"C","text":"scriptwriters","explanation":"Scriptwriters 編寫角色對白，與把對白演出來不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"editors","explanation":"Editors 剪接聲畫，並非動畫角色的聲音表演者。"},{"letter":"E","text":"film presenters","explanation":"Film presenters 介紹影片，不表示為動畫動物角色配音。"},{"letter":"F","text":"performers","explanation":"Performers 可包括只用聲線演出角色的人；句中 voice its animal characters 保留演員身分。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"cast members","meaning":"演出班底成員","note":"屬於某一指定電影或製作演出班底的人；比泛稱 actors 多了歸屬。","collocations":"the film’s cast members; cast members in the comedy.","example":"Several cast members attended the film’s premiere.","exampleZh":"幾名演出班底成員出席了該片首映禮。","contrast":"沒有指定製作時，不能把所有知名演員稱為其 cast members。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The actors in this particular comedy attended its premiere together.","zh":"這部喜劇的演員一同出席其首映禮。","upgrade":"The cast members of this particular comedy attended its premiere together.","answer":"cast members","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cast members","explanation":"Cast members 明確指同一部喜劇的演員，配合他們一起出席首映禮。"},{"letter":"B","text":"film critics","explanation":"Film critics 可以出席首映，但不是片中演員。"},{"letter":"C","text":"audience members","explanation":"Audience members 參加首映並觀影，不表示參與演出。"},{"letter":"D","text":"crew members","explanation":"Crew members 泛指幕後製作人員，與這部片的演員陣容不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"directors","explanation":"導演也可能到場，但 directors 不能統稱該片所有演員。"},{"letter":"F","text":"producers","explanation":"Producers 管製作，不能取代這部喜劇的表演陣容。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The closing credits listed the actors from the school's short film in the order they appeared.","zh":"片尾字幕按出場次序列出校園短片的演員。","upgrade":"The closing credits listed the cast members from the school's short film in the order they appeared.","answer":"cast members","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"audience members","explanation":"Audience members 是短片觀眾，不會以演員身分列在片尾字幕。"},{"letter":"B","text":"film editors","explanation":"Film editors 可能另列在幕後名單，但不是原句的角色演員。"},{"letter":"C","text":"crew members","explanation":"Crew members 包括攝影等幕後人員，與按出場次序排列的演員名單不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"cast members","explanation":"Cast members 指這部指定短片的演員，合乎片尾按出場次序列名的情境。"},{"letter":"E","text":"ticket holders","explanation":"Ticket holders 是有入場資格的人，不是影片角色的演出者。"},{"letter":"F","text":"journalists","explanation":"Journalists 可報道短片，卻不因採訪而列作演員。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"screen actors","meaning":"影視演員","note":"在電影或電視鏡頭前飾演角色的人，保留電影語境。","collocations":"famous screen actors; screen actors in comedies.","example":"The panel discussed pay for screen actors in Hong Kong films.","exampleZh":"座談會討論香港電影演員的薪酬。","contrast":"比 actors 更窄：舞台演員未必是 screen actor。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The question concerns famous actors in films, not performers in stage plays.","zh":"問題關乎電影中的知名演員，而不是舞台劇表演者。","upgrade":"The question concerns famous screen actors, not performers in stage plays.","answer":"screen actors","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"stage actors","explanation":"原句特意排除舞台劇表演者，stage actors 正好是對照組。"},{"letter":"B","text":"film directors","explanation":"Film directors 可拍電影，但不等於在電影中表演的人。"},{"letter":"C","text":"voice actors","explanation":"Voice actors 可能為角色配音，卻未必是這裏泛指的銀幕演員。"},{"letter":"D","text":"camera operators","explanation":"Camera operators 在鏡頭後工作，不是片中演員。"},{"letter":"E","text":"screen actors","explanation":"Screen actors 限定電影或其他銀幕演出，符合本句與舞台劇的對比。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scriptwriters","explanation":"Scriptwriters 負責劇本，不能取代受薪電影演員。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club invited actors seen portraying characters in streamed television dramas to a workshop instead of performers heard only in radio plays.","zh":"社團邀請了在串流電視劇中出鏡飾演角色的演員參加工作坊，而不是只在廣播劇中獻聲的表演者。","upgrade":"The club invited screen actors seen portraying characters in streamed television dramas to a workshop instead of performers heard only in radio plays.","answer":"screen actors","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"stage directors","explanation":"Stage directors 管理舞台演出，不是串流電視劇中扮演角色的人。"},{"letter":"B","text":"screen actors","explanation":"Screen actors 包括在電視鏡頭前飾演角色的人，與聲音廣播劇的表演者形成對比。"},{"letter":"C","text":"voice actors","explanation":"Voice actors 可在廣播劇中演出；本句特意選串流電視劇中可見的演員。"},{"letter":"D","text":"film crew","explanation":"Film crew 是幕後製作人員，不能表示電視劇中的角色演員。"},{"letter":"E","text":"cinema audiences","explanation":"Cinema audiences 是觀看者，不是受邀參加工作坊的影視表演者。"},{"letter":"F","text":"producers","explanation":"Producers 可製作劇集，卻不等於在其中飾演角色。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"film stars","meaning":"電影明星","note":"在電影中演出而且知名度高的演員；比一般 actors 加入成名程度。","collocations":"famous film stars; pay film stars.","example":"The film stars drew large crowds to the premiere.","exampleZh":"電影明星吸引大批人出席首映禮。","contrast":"不是每個演員都是明星；來源問 famous actors，才容許這個較窄說法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The debate was about famous actors in films and whether their high pay was fair.","zh":"辯論談的是電影中的知名演員，以及他們的高薪是否公平。","upgrade":"The debate was about film stars and whether their high pay was fair.","answer":"film stars","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cast members","explanation":"Cast members 可以是任何一部片的演員，沒有保留 famous 這個條件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"performers","explanation":"Performers 範圍更廣，還可能包括非電影表演者。"},{"letter":"C","text":"screen actors","explanation":"Screen actors 保留銀幕媒介，卻未必是辯論中的知名演員。"},{"letter":"D","text":"directors","explanation":"Directors 不等於受討論的電影演員，工作職責不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"celebrities","explanation":"Celebrities 保留名氣，但名人未必是電影演員。"},{"letter":"F","text":"film stars","explanation":"Film stars 同時保留電影演員及知名度，符合高薪是否公平的辯題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Fans queued for autographs from actors whose faces appeared on posters for several hit films.","zh":"影迷排隊向幾位演員索取簽名；他們的肖像曾登上多部賣座電影的海報。","upgrade":"Fans queued for autographs from film stars whose faces appeared on posters for several hit films.","answer":"film stars","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"cast members","explanation":"Cast members 只表示屬於某部電影，未保留多部賣座片海報及影迷排隊所顯示的知名度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"performers","explanation":"Performers 太廣，可包括其他演藝工作者，未點出電影明星。"},{"letter":"C","text":"film stars","explanation":"Film stars 同時保留電影演員身分與海報、簽名隊伍反映的知名度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"screen actors","explanation":"Screen actors 指鏡頭前演員，但未必是影迷爭取簽名的明星。"},{"letter":"E","text":"film directors","explanation":"Film directors 可能有影迷，卻不等於句中上過電影海報的演員。"},{"letter":"F","text":"theatre stars","explanation":"Theatre stars 是舞台明星；這些演員的知名度線索來自多部賣座電影海報。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"performer / actor","zh":"中文辨析： Performer 範圍較廣，可包括歌手及舞蹈員；原題明確問演員。","point":"An actor is a performer, but not every performer acts."},{"word":"player / actor","zh":"中文辨析： Player 今日常指運動員或遊戲參與者；在原題容易誤讀。","point":"The theatrical player sense is specialised or old-fashioned."},{"word":"cast member / famous actor","zh":"中文辨析： Cast member 屬某一製作的演出班底；原題泛問知名演員。","point":"Membership in a named production is extra information."},{"word":"director / actor","zh":"中文辨析： 導演指導製作，並不必親自飾演角色；周星馳可兼任，但職務仍不同。","point":"One person can hold both roles without making the nouns synonymous."}],"moduleNumber":59},{"id":"lesson-060","sourceId":54,"headword":"airport","title":"Airport","titleZh":"機場／接機地點","subtitle":"機場／接機地點","description":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 3.2〈Oxford School of English Study Tour Programmes〉： “You will be picked up from the airport and taken to our centre where you will be introduced to your host family.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 年 DSE 3.2〈Oxford School of English Study Tour Programmes〉： “You will be picked up from the airport and taken to our centre where you will be introduced to your host family.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["air terminal","contextual / less natural","可指乘客辦理登機、抵埗的航站樓，較自然的現代說法是 airport terminal；它只是機場的一部分，原文未指明接人點。"],["aviation hub","conditional","指航線匯聚、轉機繁忙的重要機場；原文只說接機，不能推斷樞紐地位。"],["airfield","false for pickup sense","偏向飛機起降及滑行區或較簡單的機場設施，不是一般乘客接送的自然地點名。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["airport terminal","明確指客運建築、入口或樓內集合點時可用；比整個 airport 窄。"],["arrivals hall","有抵埗旅客走入公共接機大堂的線索才可用；又比 terminal 窄。"],["air transport hub","有多航線匯聚、轉機或航空公司網絡中心的證據才可用；不能由一般接機推斷。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 原文只說機場接人時保留 airport 最穩妥；有航站樓入口資料時可說 airport terminal；明示入境出口外的公共接機區才說 arrivals hall；講多航線轉機功能才用 air transport hub。Airfield 和 runway 不適合一般乘客接送。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"airport terminal","meaning":"機場客運航站樓；較窄","note":"指旅客辦理手續、抵埗及離開的客運建築；若句子交代接送在樓內或樓門口進行，可把籠統的 airport 說得更具體。","collocations":"meet at the airport terminal; leave the airport terminal; terminal entrance","example":"The driver waited at the airport terminal entrance with the students' names on a sign.","exampleZh":"司機在機場客運航站樓入口舉着寫有學生姓名的牌子等候。","contrast":"Airport 包括航站樓及其他設施；terminal 只是一部分。原文沒有說接人點在樓內，因此不能硬改成航站樓。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school driver will meet the students at the airport, inside the passenger building near the information desk.","zh":"學校司機會在機場的客運建築內、資訊櫃檯附近與學生會合。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The school driver will meet the students at the airport terminal, near the information desk.","answer":"airport terminal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airfield","explanation":"偏飛機運作區，不能自然指客運建築內的資訊櫃檯。"},{"letter":"B","text":"runway","explanation":"跑道供飛機起降，司機不會在那裏與抵埗學生會合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"check-in hall","explanation":"辦理離境登機手續的區域只是航站樓一部分；題句只確定在客運建築的資訊櫃檯附近。"},{"letter":"D","text":"baggage conveyor","explanation":"行李輸送帶可在航站樓內，卻不是資訊櫃檯所在的整個客運建築。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport terminal","explanation":"題句明說會合點在客運建築內，此較窄地點名有根據。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aircraft stand","explanation":"飛機停泊位不在乘客資訊櫃檯旁，也不是一般接機區。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the airport, students should wait at the passenger terminal's main entrance, where the coach will stop.","zh":"學生在機場應在客運航站樓正門等候，旅遊巴會在那裏停靠。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"At the airport terminal, students should wait at its main entrance, where the coach will stop.","answer":"airport terminal","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"aircraft parking bay","explanation":"飛機泊位屬禁區，不是旅遊巴停在航站樓正門的地方。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport terminal","explanation":"passenger terminal's main entrance 明確把等候地點縮窄到客運航站樓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airport runway","explanation":"跑道與地面旅遊巴停靠的正門不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"check-in counter","explanation":"櫃檯在樓內，不能代表大樓正門及外面停靠的巴士。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airfield boundary","explanation":"飛行區邊界不是乘客按牌走向的航站樓正門。"},{"letter":"F","text":"departure gate","explanation":"登機閘口通常在保安檢查後，不是巴士停靠的建築入口。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"arrivals hall","meaning":"入境大堂；接機點改寫","note":"指抵埗旅客完成相關手續後走出的公共區域；只有句子明說接人在此處發生才可用，是比 airport 更精確的地點名。","collocations":"wait in the arrivals hall; meet someone at the arrivals hall","example":"A teacher met the exchange students in the arrivals hall after they collected their luggage.","exampleZh":"交換生領取行李後，一名老師在入境大堂與他們會合。","contrast":"飛機降落機場不等於接人就在入境大堂；若原句只說 at the airport，必須有額外位置線索才能縮窄。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After collecting their luggage, the students met the teacher at the airport in the public area beyond the arrival exit.","zh":"學生領取行李後，在入境出口外的機場公共區域與老師會合。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After collecting their luggage, the students met the teacher in the arrivals hall beyond the arrival exit.","answer":"arrivals hall","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"departures lounge","explanation":"供離境旅客候機，與領行李後的入境出口不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"baggage carousel","explanation":"旅客先在行李帶取行李，題句說在出口外的公共區域會合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"arrivals hall","explanation":"入境出口外的公共接機區正是入境大堂。"},{"letter":"D","text":"security checkpoint","explanation":"安檢處不是領行李後的公開接機區。"},{"letter":"E","text":"boarding gate","explanation":"登機閘口供登機，不是抵埗旅客與老師會合的地點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"runway apron","explanation":"停機坪是飛機活動區，並非公開接送區。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Parents waiting at the airport should stand by the marked meeting point where arriving passengers enter the public hall.","zh":"在機場等候的家長應站在指定集合點，即抵埗旅客進入公共大堂的位置。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Parents waiting in the arrivals hall should stand by the marked meeting point where arriving passengers enter the public area.","answer":"arrivals hall","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"departures hall","explanation":"供離境旅客辦理手續，不是抵埗旅客走出的公共接機大堂。"},{"letter":"B","text":"baggage reclaim belt","explanation":"行李帶在旅客進入公共大堂之前，家長一般不在該受限區等候。"},{"letter":"C","text":"aircraft stand","explanation":"飛機停泊位置不能作普通家長的公開集合點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"arrivals hall","explanation":"題句明確描寫抵埗旅客走入的公共接機區。"},{"letter":"E","text":"check-in area","explanation":"登機辦理區服務離境旅客，不是入境出口的會合點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"immigration counter","explanation":"入境檢查櫃檯在公開大堂之前，與家長等候區不同。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"air transport hub","meaning":"航空交通樞紐；功能角度","note":"指有多條航線匯集、轉機及旅客流量大的機場；只有句子本身強調這種連接功能時才可用。","collocations":"a major air transport hub; fly through an air transport hub","example":"The city has become an air transport hub where travellers change planes for many destinations.","exampleZh":"該城市已成為航空交通樞紐，旅客可在此轉機前往許多目的地。","contrast":"樞紐必然涉及航線連接角色；一個小機場也能接送學生，卻未必是 hub。Aviation hub 是原始候選，但在普通旅行說明中 air transport hub 較明確指客運功能。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The students changed planes at the airport, a major connection point for flights across Asia.","zh":"學生在一個機場轉機；那裏是亞洲多條航線的重要轉接點。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The students changed planes at the air transport hub serving flights across Asia.","answer":"air transport hub","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"air transport hub","explanation":"多條亞洲航線匯聚並供轉機，明確支持機場樞紐的功能說法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport terminal","explanation":"航站樓是建築；題句強調整個機場在航線網絡中的連接角色。"},{"letter":"C","text":"regional airfield","explanation":"較小飛行場未必有多條跨亞洲的定期轉機航線。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airline office","explanation":"航空公司辦公室不是學生轉機的整個場地。"},{"letter":"E","text":"arrival gate","explanation":"一個抵埗閘口不能代表多航線轉機中心。"},{"letter":"F","text":"aircraft depot","explanation":"維修或停泊設施不是供旅客轉機的航線樞紐。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Several airlines use the airport as the centre of their route networks, bringing travellers from smaller cities to connect with long-haul flights.","zh":"多間航空公司以該機場為航線網絡中心，讓小城市旅客在此轉乘長途航班。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Several airlines route travellers through the air transport hub from smaller cities to long-haul flights.","answer":"air transport hub","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"terminal entrance","explanation":"一個入口不能代表多間航空公司的航線網絡中心。"},{"letter":"B","text":"air transport hub","explanation":"多間航空公司在此集中短途及長途轉機航線，符合樞紐功能。"},{"letter":"C","text":"private airstrip","explanation":"私人短跑道未必有這種大規模轉機服務。"},{"letter":"D","text":"boarding lounge","explanation":"候機室只是旅客等候的室內區域，不是整個航線連接點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"aircraft manufacturer","explanation":"製造商是企業，不能代替旅客轉機的機場。"},{"letter":"F","text":"city bus station","explanation":"巴士站可轉乘地面交通，卻不是航班路線的航空樞紐。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Terminal / arrivals hall · 部分不能自動代替整體","zh":"中文辨析： 接機可在航站樓大堂，也可在指定出口或其他集合點。原文只說 airport，不能自行補出終端樓或入境大堂；練習若有明確地點線索才可縮窄。","point":"The airport is the site; a terminal or arrivals hall is a specified part of it."},{"word":"Airfield / runway · 飛機活動區不是一般接送地點","zh":"中文辨析： Runway 是跑道，airfield 偏飛機運作區；一般家長或學校接學生不會在跑道會合。航空操作文本可能用 airfield，但本段的乘客接送語境不合適。","point":"Student pickup belongs to passenger facilities, not the runway or airfield."},{"word":"Hub · 樞紐地位須有航線證據","zh":"中文辨析： Aviation hub 或 air transport hub 要有多航線連接或轉機功能。只知學生從一個機場抵達，不代表那裏是樞紐。","point":"A hub has a connecting role; an airport need not be one."},{"word":"Airport versus airline / aircraft","zh":"中文辨析： Airline 是航空公司，aircraft 是飛機；airport 是飛機起降及旅客出入的地點。接送地點不能寫成公司或飛機本身。","point":"An airport is a place; an airline is a company and an aircraft is a vehicle."},{"word":"Air terminal 的用法","zh":"中文辨析： Air terminal 可見於某些用法，但現代旅遊說明通常較清楚寫 airport terminal，並指出是第幾號航站樓或哪個入口。它仍不表示整個機場。","point":"An air/airport terminal is a passenger building within an airport."}],"moduleNumber":60},{"id":"lesson-061","sourceId":11,"headword":"accidents","title":"Accidents","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2016 text quotes a speaker saying that preventing accidents was not the reason for the smartphone walking lanes. Here accidents are unplanned unwanted events involving pedestrians. The quotation states motive; it does not prove whether the lanes worked.","sourceSense":"The 2016 text quotes a speaker saying that preventing accidents was not the reason for the smartphone walking lanes. Here accidents are unplanned unwanted events involving pedestrians. The quotation states motive; it does not prove whether the lanes worked.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["mishaps","contextual: mild accidents"],["unintended incidents","recast: broader; add outcome if needed"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Crash 偏向車輛猛烈相撞，原文行人意外不一定涉及車輛；injury 是結果，mistake 是失誤，均不列為通用替換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["mishaps","指未料到而不太嚴重的失誤或小事故；用於擦碰、跌倒等輕微事情。","嚴重受傷或死亡的事故不宜輕描淡寫為 mishap。"],["unintended incidents","正式而較中性的描述，突出事件並非故意；incident 本身不保證有傷害。","若原句特別要求傷害結果，須補上 caused injury/damage；不可只說 incidents。"],["collisions","當意外確實涉及人或物互相撞擊時可用；它比 accidents 指得更窄。","跌倒但沒有相撞的 accident 不能改成 collision。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 遇到輕微、非故意的小意外可用 mishap；需要不預設受傷或類型的中性總稱，用 unintended incident；句子明說人或物實際相撞才用 collision。Injury 是傷勢，near miss 是險些發生，均不可當作已發生事故的通稱。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"mishaps","meaning":"小意外","note":"指未料到而不太嚴重的失誤或小事故；用於擦碰、跌倒等輕微事情。","collocations":"minor mishaps; a few mishaps.","example":"The walk ended with two minor mishaps but no injuries.","exampleZh":"步行活動出了兩宗小意外，但沒有人受傷。","contrast":"嚴重受傷或死亡的事故不宜輕描淡寫為 mishap。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school walk had two minor accidents: a dropped bottle and a harmless stumble.","zh":"學校步行活動有兩宗小意外：有人掉了水樽，另有人絆倒但沒有受傷。","upgrade":"The school walk had two minor mishaps: a dropped bottle and a harmless stumble.","answer":"mishaps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"injuries","explanation":"瓶子掉下與輕微絆倒均未造成受傷，injuries 把事件誤說成傷勢。"},{"letter":"B","text":"collisions","explanation":"兩件事都沒有與人或物相撞，collisions 過於具體。"},{"letter":"C","text":"near misses","explanation":"瓶子已掉下、學生已絆倒；這些是實際發生的小意外，不只是差點發生的 near misses。"},{"letter":"D","text":"mishaps","explanation":"Mishaps 恰好概括這兩宗輕微、非故意的小意外，也符合學校步行活動的語氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"mistakes","explanation":"Mistakes 偏重判斷或操作上的錯誤；原句沒有說有人做錯決定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"incidents","explanation":"Incidents 可泛指事件，但沒有 mishaps 對輕微失手意外的明確提示。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Despite a few small accidents with props, the festival rehearsal finished on time.","zh":"雖然道具出了幾宗小意外，電影節綵排仍準時完成。","upgrade":"Despite a few small mishaps with props, the festival rehearsal finished on time.","answer":"mishaps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"technical faults","explanation":"道具出的小意外不一定由設備故障造成，technical faults 擅自指定原因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"mishaps","explanation":"Mishaps 自然指排練時的幾宗小意外，亦配合活動仍準時完成。"},{"letter":"C","text":"injuries","explanation":"原句沒有說演員受傷，injuries 把意外誤作人身傷害。"},{"letter":"D","text":"near misses","explanation":"小意外已在道具使用時發生，並非只差點發生的 near misses。"},{"letter":"E","text":"setbacks","explanation":"Setbacks 可指排練進度受阻，但原句只說道具出小意外，沒有實質延誤。"},{"letter":"F","text":"breakages","explanation":"Breakages 只指物件破損；道具小意外可能是掉落或擺放失誤。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"unintended incidents","meaning":"非蓄意事件","note":"正式而較中性的描述，突出事件並非故意；incident 本身不保證有傷害。","collocations":"record unintended incidents; unintended incidents involving pedestrians.","example":"The council recorded unintended incidents near the crossing, including one minor collision.","exampleZh":"區議會記錄了行人過路處附近的非蓄意事件，包括一宗輕微碰撞。","contrast":"若原句特別要求傷害結果，須補上 caused injury/damage；不可只說 incidents。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The report recorded accidents ranging from harmless bumps to serious falls in its section on unplanned events.","zh":"報告在「非預期事件」一節記錄了意外，從無傷大雅的碰撞到嚴重跌倒都有。","upgrade":"The report recorded unintended incidents ranging from harmless bumps to serious falls in its section on unplanned events.","answer":"unintended incidents","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"near misses","explanation":"Near misses 是差點發生的意外，不能概括報告已記錄的碰撞及跌倒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"intentional acts","explanation":"報告明說沒有人預先計劃這些事，故 intentional acts 相反。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unintended injuries","explanation":"其中包括無害碰撞，injuries 暗示每宗都有傷勢，範圍過窄。"},{"letter":"D","text":"safety violations","explanation":"Safety violations 指違反規則；原句沒有判定有人違規。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unintended incidents","explanation":"Unintended incidents 可涵蓋無傷碰撞與嚴重跌倒，也符合報告的「非預期事件」分類。"},{"letter":"F","text":"collisions","explanation":"Collisions 只指相撞，不能把句中嚴重跌倒也一併涵蓋。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The council logged accidents involving pedestrians, specifying separately whether anyone was hurt.","zh":"區議會記錄涉及行人的非蓄意事件，另行註明是否有人受傷。","upgrade":"The council logged unintended incidents involving pedestrians, specifying separately whether anyone was hurt.","answer":"unintended incidents","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"unintended incidents","explanation":"議會另行記錄是否有人受傷，unintended incidents 可先統稱這些非故意事件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"injuries","explanation":"Injuries 只指傷害；本句刻意把意外與有沒有受傷分開。"},{"letter":"C","text":"collisions","explanation":"Collisions 限於相撞；行人意外還可能是跌倒等其他類型。"},{"letter":"D","text":"near misses","explanation":"Near misses 指險些發生事故，不能取代已被記錄的意外。"},{"letter":"E","text":"safety breaches","explanation":"Safety breaches 表示違規或保安漏洞，句中沒有此結論。"},{"letter":"F","text":"casualties","explanation":"Casualties 指傷亡者，不是議會記錄的事故本身。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"collisions","meaning":"碰撞事故","note":"當意外確實涉及人或物互相撞擊時可用；它比 accidents 指得更窄。","collocations":"pedestrian collisions; collisions at a crossing.","example":"The camera recorded two pedestrian collisions at the crossing.","exampleZh":"鏡頭拍到行人過路處兩宗行人碰撞。","contrast":"跌倒但沒有相撞的 accident 不能改成 collision。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Two accidents at the crossing involved pedestrians bumping into cyclists.","zh":"過路處有兩宗意外，均涉及行人與單車騎士相撞。","upgrade":"Two collisions at the crossing involved pedestrians bumping into cyclists.","answer":"collisions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"stumbles","explanation":"Stumbles 是絆了一下；原句明說行人撞到單車人士。"},{"letter":"B","text":"near misses","explanation":"既然雙方已碰到，便不是尚未相撞的 near misses。"},{"letter":"C","text":"collisions","explanation":"Collisions 指兩方實際相撞，準確概括過路處這兩宗意外。"},{"letter":"D","text":"falls","explanation":"Falls 指跌倒；相撞後是否跌倒並未交代。"},{"letter":"E","text":"injuries","explanation":"Injuries 指傷勢，原句只確認碰撞而未說有人受傷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"missteps","explanation":"Missteps 可指踏錯步或失策，沒有說出行人與單車人士相撞。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the exhibition, three accidents involved visitors walking into a glass door.","zh":"展覽期間有三宗意外，都是參觀者走路時撞上玻璃門。","upgrade":"At the exhibition, three visitors were involved in collisions with a glass door.","answer":"collisions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"stumbles","explanation":"Stumbles 指絆了一下；三名參觀者是實際撞上玻璃門。"},{"letter":"B","text":"near misses","explanation":"Near misses 表示差點撞到卻避開；句中三人都已碰到玻璃。"},{"letter":"C","text":"collisions","explanation":"Collisions 可指人撞上固定物件，準確概括參觀者與玻璃門的三次碰撞。"},{"letter":"D","text":"falls","explanation":"Falls 是跌倒，原句沒有說撞門後任何人跌在地上。"},{"letter":"E","text":"distractions","explanation":"Distractions 可是撞門原因，卻不是三宗已發生的意外本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"injuries","explanation":"Injuries 是可能的傷勢；句中沒有交代有沒有人受傷。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"incident / accident","zh":"中文辨析： Incident 只表示事件，未必有人受傷或財物受損；accident 在安全討論中通常是不想發生的意外。","point":"An incident may be harmless; an accident is an unwanted event."},{"word":"injury / casualty","zh":"中文辨析： Injury 是傷害結果，casualty 是傷亡者；兩者都不是事故本身。","point":"An injury can result from an accident; it is not the event."},{"word":"mishap / disaster","zh":"中文辨析： Mishap 語氣輕，不能淡化嚴重車禍；disaster 則會誇大小碰撞。","point":"Check severity before replacing accident with either word."},{"word":"mistake / offence","zh":"中文辨析： Mistake 是錯誤決定，offence 是違法行為；意外未必有錯或犯罪。","point":"An accident does not itself establish fault or crime."}],"moduleNumber":61},{"id":"lesson-062","sourceId":12,"headword":"accommodation","title":"Accommodation","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"In the 2012 study-tour brochure, homestay accommodation is the temporary place and arrangement for students living with a host family. British-English accommodation in this sense is normally uncountable; the lesson does not treat it as a permanent home.","sourceSense":"In the 2012 study-tour brochure, homestay accommodation is the temporary place and arrangement for students living with a host family. British-English accommodation in this sense is normally uncountable; the lesson does not treat it as a permanent home.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["lodging","contextual: short-term accommodation"],["place to stay","recast: countable phrase"],["housing","false for short homestay; usually longer-term"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Housing 是長期住屋概念；residence 可指住處或住宿設施，但不特指寄宿家庭。Host-family stay 可作解釋性改寫，與 homestay 意義重疊，故不另重複兩題。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["lodging","旅行或短期逗留時的住處，語氣可較正式；不必是寄宿家庭。","Homestay lodging 可理解，但 lodging 本身不保證文化交流或寄宿形式。"],["a place to stay","通俗說法，說明學生暫住哪裏；由不可數 accommodation 改成可數短語時須改句法。","短語只交代有住處；若要表達寄宿家庭，須加 with a host family。"],["homestay","特指住在接待家庭中的住宿模式；比一般 accommodation 範圍窄。","若學生住酒店或宿舍，就不能稱為 homestay。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 短期遊學的「住宿」可概括為 lodging；只需要日常說法時用 a place to stay；只有學生確實住在接待家庭並參與家庭生活時才用 homestay。Host family 是接待者，hospitality 是款待，兩者不直接指住宿。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"lodging","meaning":"臨時住宿","note":"旅行或短期逗留時的住處，語氣可較正式；不必是寄宿家庭。","collocations":"arrange lodging; overnight lodging.","example":"The organiser arranged lodging with local families.","exampleZh":"主辦方安排學生住在當地家庭。","contrast":"Homestay lodging 可理解，但 lodging 本身不保證文化交流或寄宿形式。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The summer course included accommodation with host families for fourteen nights.","zh":"暑期課程包括在寄宿家庭住宿十四晚。","upgrade":"The summer course included lodging with host families for fourteen nights.","answer":"lodging","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"housing","explanation":"Housing 常指較長期的居住安排；這裏只說十四晚的遊學住宿。"},{"letter":"B","text":"lodging","explanation":"Lodging 正好指旅程期間提供的住宿，不改變寄宿家庭這項安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"residence","explanation":"Residence 可指住處或居留，卻不如 lodging 準確表達短期旅遊住宿。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a private room","explanation":"學生住在接待家庭，原句沒有保證各人獲得 a private room。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hospitality","explanation":"Hospitality 是接待態度或款待，不是十四晚的住宿安排本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"board","explanation":"Board 往往涉及膳食，卻不能單獨清楚取代這裏的住宿。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The hiking club reserved accommodation in a small guesthouse for one night.","zh":"遠足社在一間小型旅館預訂了一晚住宿。","upgrade":"The hiking club reserved lodging in a small guesthouse for one night.","answer":"lodging","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"housing","explanation":"Housing 多指住房或較長期安排；這裏只預訂旅館一晚。"},{"letter":"B","text":"residence","explanation":"Residence 可指居所，但不像 lodging 明確表示旅程中的短期留宿。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a room","explanation":"A room 只是一間房，原句未說團體預訂的是一間房而非多個床位。"},{"letter":"D","text":"board","explanation":"Board 常包括膳食，句中只說遠足社預訂一晚住宿。"},{"letter":"E","text":"lodging","explanation":"Lodging 自然概括旅館提供的一晚短期住宿，也說明不一定要住接待家庭。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hospitality","explanation":"Hospitality 是款待，不能代替遠足社預訂的過夜住宿。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"a place to stay","meaning":"住宿地方","note":"通俗說法，說明學生暫住哪裏；由不可數 accommodation 改成可數短語時須改句法。","collocations":"find a place to stay; a place to stay with a family.","example":"The students found a place to stay near the language school.","exampleZh":"學生在語言學校附近找到住宿地方。","contrast":"短語只交代有住處；若要表達寄宿家庭，須加 with a host family。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organiser promised each student accommodation with a local family.","zh":"主辦方承諾為每名學生安排在當地家庭的住宿地方。","upgrade":"The organiser promised each student a place to stay with a local family.","answer":"a place to stay","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a place to stay","explanation":"A place to stay with a local family 保留學生在當地家庭過夜的安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a room to rent","explanation":"A room to rent 暗示學生自己租房；原句只說主辦方承諾安排住宿。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a student residence","explanation":"A student residence 會把寄宿家庭改成宿舍。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a hotel room","explanation":"A hotel room 也改變了 with a local family 這個關鍵條件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a host family","explanation":"A host family 指接待者，不直接指主辦方提供的住宿地方。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a place to visit","explanation":"A place to visit 只供參觀，不表示學生可在當地家庭留宿。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the exchange, accommodation was arranged for the visiting pupils.","zh":"交流期間，來訪學生獲安排住宿地方。","upgrade":"During the exchange, a place to stay was arranged for each visiting pupil.","answer":"a place to stay","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a permanent home","explanation":"交換生只是短期到訪，a permanent home 把暫住改成永久住處。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a student residence","explanation":"A student residence 指特定宿舍，原句沒有說安排在宿舍。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a family visit","explanation":"A family visit 可以當天結束，不等於為到訪學生安排過夜住宿。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a rented flat","explanation":"A rented flat 擅自指定租住單位，來源只說已安排住宿。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a housing policy","explanation":"A housing policy 是規則或政策，不是學生實際可住的地方。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a place to stay","explanation":"A place to stay 可概括交換期間安排給學生的暫時住處。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"homestay","meaning":"寄宿家庭住宿","note":"特指住在接待家庭中的住宿模式；比一般 accommodation 範圍窄。","collocations":"arrange a homestay; a two-week homestay.","example":"A two-week homestay helped Mei practise English at dinner.","exampleZh":"兩星期的寄宿家庭生活讓美在晚餐時練習英語。","contrast":"若學生住酒店或宿舍，就不能稱為 homestay。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The brochure offered accommodation with a host family, including shared evening meals.","zh":"小冊子提供與寄宿家庭同住、包括共進晚餐的住宿。","upgrade":"The brochure offered a homestay, including shared evening meals with the host family.","answer":"homestay","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a hotel stay","explanation":"A hotel stay 不會包含與接待家庭一起吃晚飯的寄宿安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a student residence","explanation":"A student residence 是宿舍，並非與當地家庭同住。"},{"letter":"C","text":"homestay","explanation":"Homestay 同時包含住在接待家庭及參與家庭生活，最切合句中細節。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a rented flat","explanation":"A rented flat 只表達租住單位，沒有 host family 的共同生活。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a family visit","explanation":"A family visit 可指短暫拜訪，不保證學生在該家過夜。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a boarding-school place","explanation":"A boarding-school place 是寄宿學校學位，不是遊學團的接待家庭住宿。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For the first week of the language trip, her accommodation was in a teacher’s family home; the second week was spent in a hotel.","zh":"語言遊學首週，她住在一名教師的家中；第二週則住酒店。","upgrade":"For the first week of the language trip, her homestay was with a teacher’s family; the second week was spent in a hotel.","answer":"homestay","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a hotel booking","explanation":"A hotel booking 只適用第二週，不能表示第一週住在教師家中。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a student apartment","explanation":"A student apartment 把第一週教師家庭住宿改成公寓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a day visit","explanation":"A day visit 只是一日拜訪，不能表示整個第一週的過夜安排。"},{"letter":"D","text":"homestay","explanation":"Homestay 準確指第一週在教師家庭同住；它不會把第二週的酒店也錯稱寄宿家庭。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a host-family visit","explanation":"A host-family visit 可能只是探訪，沒有清楚表示第一週在該家留宿。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a boarding-school place","explanation":"A boarding-school place 是學校宿位，與首週住教師家、次週住酒店不同。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"housing / accommodation","zh":"中文辨析： Housing 多指長期房屋供應或居所；短期遊學寄宿家庭較自然稱 accommodation。","point":"Housing is often a long-term or policy category."},{"word":"room / homestay","zh":"中文辨析： Room 只說房間，未必包括與寄宿家庭同住的安排。","point":"A room is part of some accommodation, not the whole arrangement."},{"word":"home / accommodation","zh":"中文辨析： Home 帶有自己的家或長期歸屬之意；遊學住宿是暫時安排。","point":"A study-tour host house is not necessarily the student’s home."},{"word":"an accommodation / accommodation","zh":"中文辨析： 在英式旅遊語境，accommodation 通常不可數；不說 an accommodation。","point":"Use accommodation is provided, or a place to stay."}],"moduleNumber":62},{"id":"lesson-063","sourceId":35,"headword":"adventure","title":"Adventure","titleZh":"不尋常的探索旅程","subtitle":"不尋常的探索旅程","description":"一份[2025 年 DSE Speaking 6.3 次級逐字轉錄](https://www.scribd.com/document/942988550/English-Oral)把題目列為 School Adventure Trip，列出澳洲與海龜同游、冰島探索火山洞、摩洛哥觀星三個選項，並問：「Which of the three adventure trips is the most appealing?」[另一題目索引](https://dsetreasure.com/dse-english-paper-4-%E9%A1%8C%E7%9B%AE/)獨立記錄相同主題和三種活動。校內來源索引對應的句子被截斷，本課不把截斷文字重建成試卷引文；官方試卷影像尚未核對。這裏 adventure 的可核實語境是學生參與新奇、探索或具挑戰的旅行；它不必然等於危險或胡鬧。以下所有指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"一份[2025 年 DSE Speaking 6.3 次級逐字轉錄](https://www.scribd.com/document/942988550/English-Oral)把題目列為 School Adventure Trip，列出澳洲與海龜同游、冰島探索火山洞、摩洛哥觀星三個選項，並問：「Which of the three adventure trips is the most appealing?」[另一題目索引](https://dsetreasure.com/dse-english-paper-4-%E9%A1%8C%E7%9B%AE/)獨立記錄相同主題和三種活動。校內來源索引對應的句子被截斷，本課不把截斷文字重建成試卷引文；官方試卷影像尚未核對。這裏 adventure 的可核實語境是學生參與新奇、探索或具挑戰的旅行；它不必然等於危險或胡鬧。以下所有指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["exciting experience","有條件近義","可說旅程令學生興奮；單獨此片語也能指演唱會，須保留旅行或探索語境。"],["expedition","有條件近義","有組織地前往洞穴等地方考察，常帶明確探索／研究目的；不是每次好玩的旅行都算考察。"],["escapade","源語境不宜教作近義","常指一段衝動、冒失甚至淘氣的插曲，會把有監督的學校旅行說得不穩重。"]],"note":"補充 journey of discovery，可同時說旅行與從陌生事物中學習，但需要旅程確實帶來觀察或新知。Thrilling experience 與 exciting experience 的情緒差別太細，會重複練習；excursion 是短程遊覽，未必有探索或挑戰；quest 通常有明確追尋目標，不能套到所有校外旅行。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","適用焦點","必須有的線索"],"rows":[["adventure","新奇、探索或具挑戰的旅程","旅程及不尋常體驗。"],["exciting experience","參加者的興奮感受","仍保留旅行線索，勿保證人人喜歡。"],["expedition","有目的的有組織考察","探索、觀察或研究任務。"],["journey of discovery","旅途中發現新知","實際出行及新觀察／學習。"],["escapade","冒失或淘氣插曲","不宜無根據地指有監督的校外旅行。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 只說參與者感到興奮，可用 exciting experience；有明確考察目標，可用 expedition；旅程實際帶來新發現，可用 journey of discovery。不要把學校安排的探險活動自動說成危險事故或胡鬧。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Exciting Experience","meaning":"令人興奮的經歷","note":"從參加者感受說旅行新奇、有趣或激動；要在句子保留旅行及探索線索，才接近 adventure。","collocations":"an exciting experience for pupils; an exciting travel experience; describe the trip as an exciting experience.","example":"Exploring the cave with a guide was an exciting experience for the school group.","exampleZh":"在導遊帶領下探索洞穴，對學校團體來說是令人興奮的經歷。","contrast":"一場演唱會也可以令人興奮，卻不一定是探險；冒險亦可能令人害怕，不保證每人喜歡。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The pupils called their first guided walk inside a volcanic cave an adventure they would remember for years.","zh":"學生說，首次在導遊帶領下走進火山洞，是一段多年後仍會記得的新奇經歷。","upgrade":"The pupils called their first guided walk inside a volcanic cave an exciting experience they would remember for years.","answer":"exciting experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"exciting experiment","explanation":"洞穴步行是親身經歷，句中沒說學生在進行科學實驗；experiment 亦不能代替 experience。"},{"letter":"B","text":"exciting experience","explanation":"學生多年難忘首次探索洞穴，句子保留旅行內容及個人體驗。"},{"letter":"C","text":"dangerous experience","explanation":"原句強調首次探索令人難忘，沒有證據說旅程危險。"},{"letter":"D","text":"exciting experiences","explanation":"原句以 an 指一次經歷，複數 experiences 與冠詞不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"mischievous escapade","explanation":"學生參與的是有導遊的活動，沒有胡鬧或擅自行動線索。"},{"letter":"F","text":"exciting opportunity","explanation":"學生已完成首次洞穴步行並回顧經歷；opportunity 著重尚可把握的機會。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school hopes its desert stargazing adventure will give pupils a new view of the night sky, though the trip has not happened yet.","zh":"學校希望沙漠觀星之旅讓學生以新角度看夜空，但旅程尚未發生。","upgrade":"The school hopes its desert stargazing trip will be an exciting experience that gives pupils a new view of the night sky, though it has not happened yet.","answer":"exciting experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"completed exciting experience","explanation":"觀星旅程尚未發生，不能說已完成的興奮經歷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"guaranteed success","explanation":"學校只是希望學生有新體驗，沒有保證人人一定覺得成功。"},{"letter":"C","text":"exciting experiment","explanation":"觀星可令人興奮，但句子說旅行體驗，沒有科學實驗的設定。"},{"letter":"D","text":"exciting experience","explanation":"整句改寫為學校希望旅程會令人興奮，仍保留沙漠觀星和未來的不確定性。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reckless incident","explanation":"學校計劃的觀星之旅不等於冒失事故。"},{"letter":"F","text":"exciting experiences","explanation":"主語是單一觀星之旅，改寫需要單數補語 an exciting experience，不是複數。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Expedition","meaning":"有計劃的考察旅程","note":"有組織地到不熟悉或較難到的地方探索、觀察或研究；比一般 adventure 更強調目的與準備。","collocations":"an expedition to a volcanic cave; a marine expedition; join an expedition; conduct a field expedition.","example":"The class joined a guided expedition to study rock formations inside the cave.","exampleZh":"全班參加有導遊帶領的考察旅程，研究洞內的岩層。","contrast":"由老師帶去附近商場看電影是 outing，通常不是 expedition；有趣不等於有研究或探索目標。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school organised an adventure into the volcanic cave to record its rock layers with a trained guide.","zh":"學校安排由受訓導遊帶領進入火山洞，記錄其岩層。","upgrade":"The school organised an expedition into the volcanic cave to record its rock layers with a trained guide.","answer":"expedition","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"escapade","explanation":"有學校安排和受訓導遊，並非學生冒失地闖進洞內。"},{"letter":"B","text":"excursion","explanation":"Excursion 可指一般短程遊覽，但這裏有進洞記錄岩層的明確研究任務，expedition 更準確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"expedition","explanation":"有組織地進洞記錄岩層，具明確探索與研究目的。"},{"letter":"D","text":"sightseeing trip","explanation":"此行不是只為欣賞景色；學生帶着記錄岩層的研究任務。"},{"letter":"E","text":"expeditionary","explanation":"這是形容詞，不能單獨作 an 後面的名詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"expedition to","explanation":"原句已有 into the volcanic cave；再加 to 會破壞介詞結構。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Pupils joined an adventure across unfamiliar desert terrain to chart a safe path for next year's school group.","zh":"學生參加穿越陌生沙漠路線的旅程，為明年的學校團體繪製安全路徑。","upgrade":"Pupils joined an expedition across unfamiliar desert terrain to chart a safe path for next year's school group.","answer":"expedition","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"guided tour","explanation":"可以有導遊，但這裏的學生須自行勘查陌生路線並繪製後續團體可走的路徑，超出一般參觀。"},{"letter":"B","text":"expedition","explanation":"有組織地穿越陌生沙漠路線，完成勘路任務，符合有目的的探索旅程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"sightseeing excursion","explanation":"Sightseeing 著重觀光；繪製安全路徑的實地任務不只是看風景。"},{"letter":"D","text":"route map","explanation":"學生是參加旅程去製作地圖，不能說他們「參加一張路線圖」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"escapade","explanation":"勘查供明年團體使用的安全路徑是有計劃的任務，沒有胡鬧意味。"},{"letter":"F","text":"exploratory","explanation":"這是形容詞，不能獨自放在 an 後面作旅程名稱。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Journey of Discovery","meaning":"發現新事物的旅程","note":"強調旅途讓參加者認識陌生地方或知識；可有實際移動，也可帶學習的比喻意味。","collocations":"a journey of discovery through the desert; a journey of discovery for pupils; turn a trip into a journey of discovery.","example":"The stargazing trip became a journey of discovery as pupils learned to identify constellations.","exampleZh":"學生學會辨認星座，令觀星之旅成了發現新知的旅程。","contrast":"需要真有新觀察或學習；若只是重遊熟悉地方、沒有新體驗，不能為了換詞而誇稱「發現之旅」。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The Iceland trip became an adventure as pupils explored unfamiliar rock formations and learned how the cave was formed.","zh":"學生探索陌生岩層並學習火山洞如何形成，令冰島之旅成了一段發現新知的旅程。","upgrade":"The Iceland trip became a journey of discovery as pupils explored unfamiliar rock formations and learned how the cave was formed.","answer":"journey of discovery","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"journey of recovery","explanation":"Recovery 指恢復，原句談首次了解陌生岩層與洞穴成因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"journey of discovery","explanation":"實際走訪冰島並學到此前不懂的地質知識，兩個要素都成立。"},{"letter":"C","text":"journey of rediscovery","explanation":"Rediscovery 表示重新發現已知事物，句子強調學生新學會洞穴成因。"},{"letter":"D","text":"dangerous voyage","explanation":"洞穴探索沒有遇險證據，voyage 也通常指較長的海上或太空旅程。"},{"letter":"E","text":"journey to discovery","explanation":"固定說法是 a journey of discovery；to discovery 在此處不自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"discovery journey","explanation":"這種名詞並置不如慣用的 journey of discovery 自然。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For Lena, the Morocco adventure changed more than her route: after several wrong turns, she learned to navigate an unfamiliar town independently.","zh":"摩洛哥之旅不只改變了莉娜的路線：走錯幾次路後，她學會在陌生城鎮獨自認路。","upgrade":"For Lena, the Morocco trip was a journey of discovery: after several wrong turns, she learned to navigate an unfamiliar town independently.","answer":"journey of discovery","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"journey of recovery","explanation":"莉娜獲得新能力，句中沒說她從疾病或挫折中復原。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accidental detour","explanation":"走錯路是經歷的一部分，但整段旅行帶來的是獨立認路的新能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"journey of rediscovery","explanation":"她是在陌生地方第一次學會獨立認路，並非重新發現早已掌握的能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"journey of discoveries","explanation":"雖可談多項 discoveries，但本句的慣用概括說法是單數不可數意義的 journey of discovery。"},{"letter":"E","text":"journey of discovery","explanation":"旅途中她發現自己能獨立應付陌生地方，既有實際出行也有自我認識。"},{"letter":"F","text":"dangerous voyage","explanation":"多次轉錯彎不等於遇險；在城鎮找路也不屬典型的 voyage。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Escapade：冒失插曲與有監督旅行","zh":"Escapade 常帶衝動或淘氣意味；有導遊與教師帶隊的火山洞考察不應無根據地說成一次胡鬧。English contrast: An escapade is a daring episode, often with a mischievous tone; an expedition is planned exploration.","point":""},{"word":"Excursion / outing：短程遊覽不必然冒險","zh":"Excursion 或 outing 可指外出活動，卻不表明有陌生環境、挑戰或探索；若只坐車去看熟悉景點，不宜說成來源語境的冒險。English contrast: An outing names a trip; adventure adds novelty or challenge.","point":""},{"word":"Thrill / danger：興奮不等於危險","zh":"去摩洛哥觀星可令人興奮，卻不能推斷安排不安全。Dangerous incident 說真的遇險，比原題強得多。English contrast: Excitement is an emotion; danger is a risk or harmful event.","point":""},{"word":"Expedition / holiday：目的性","zh":"Expedition 偏有計劃的考察；純放鬆的海灘假期雖然可以很愉快，卻未必有探索目的。English contrast: An expedition has an exploratory purpose; a holiday may not.","point":""},{"word":"Experience / trip：感受與行程","zh":"Exciting experience 著重參與者的感受，trip 只稱旅程；換詞時仍要保留原句的旅行內容，不可改成與實際出行無關的娛樂。English contrast: The experience describes how the journey felt, not just its itinerary.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":63},{"id":"lesson-064","sourceId":22,"headword":"adapt","title":"Adapt","titleZh":"適應新環境","subtitle":"適應新環境","description":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “Can you adapt to new environments quickly?”","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “Can you adapt to new environments quickly?”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["adjust","near / 搭配要完整","adjust to a new environment 指調整做法以配合環境。"],["accommodate","false for this grammar","accommodate a need/person 常是提供方便；accommodate to an environment 並非自然替換。"],["respond to change","contextual / 需補結果","只表示對變化有所回應；要加 effectively/constructively 才保留成功適應的意思。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["adjust to","調整以配合：Adjust to 著重改變做法；單獨 adjust 不交代適應甚麼。"],["acclimatise to","逐漸習慣陌生環境：這個詞暗示逐步熟悉；若原句強調立即改變一個做法，adjust to 較自然。"],["get used to","習慣起來；口語：重點是熟悉感，未必指出具體改變了甚麼做法；to 在此為介詞。"],["respond effectively to change","有效應對變化；需改寫：單獨 respond to change 可能是抱怨或拒絕；effectively 加上有效應對的結果。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 人主動改變作息配合新條件，可用 adjust to；經時間逐步習慣氣候或地方，用 acclimatise to；強調熟悉感時用 get used to；若要描述具體有效回應變化，可用 respond effectively to change。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"adjust to","meaning":"調整以配合","note":"改變習慣、時間表或做法，以便在新的環境中運作；需接 to。","collocations":"adjust to a new school; adjust to a different timetable","example":"The new pupils adjusted to the school’s unfamiliar timetable.","exampleZh":"新生調整了作息，以適應學校陌生的時間表。","contrast":"Adjust to 著重改變做法；單獨 adjust 不交代適應甚麼。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After changing schools, Lam had to adapt to a different timetable.","zh":"轉校後，阿林需要適應不同的時間表。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After changing schools, Lam had to adjust to a different timetable.","answer":"adjust to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adjust to","explanation":"表示因應新學校的時間安排而改變自己的作息。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adjust","explanation":"缺少 to，沒有自然接上 a different timetable。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accommodate","explanation":"通常是安排去照顧他人的需要，不是學生適應時間表。"},{"letter":"D","text":"resist","explanation":"是抗拒新時間表，與因應它改變做法相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"observe","explanation":"只表示留意時間表，沒有調整作息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"accept","explanation":"可能表示同意，未必實際改變行為。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After joining a new team, Eva had to adapt to its quieter coaching style by asking for feedback privately.","zh":"加入新隊伍後，伊娃改為私下請教意見，以適應較安靜的教練指導方式。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After joining a new team, Eva had to adjust to its quieter coaching style by asking for feedback privately.","answer":"adjust to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"become aware of","explanation":"知道新教練較安靜，未表示伊娃因此改為私下請教。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adjust to","explanation":"她改變取得意見的方法以配合新指導風格，保留適應行為。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accommodate","explanation":"通常是教練或隊伍照顧隊員需要，而非伊娃適應指導方式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"endure","explanation":"勉強忍受安靜教學，沒有表達她主動更改溝通方式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"react to","explanation":"可作任何反應，包括抱怨，未必是有效配合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"approve of","explanation":"贊同教練做法不等於自己改成私下請教。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"acclimatise to","meaning":"逐漸習慣陌生環境","note":"經過一段時間，慢慢適應陌生氣候、地方或生活條件；英式拼法可寫 acclimatise。","collocations":"acclimatise to a new climate; acclimatise to a new setting","example":"It took the exchange students two weeks to acclimatise to the colder city.","exampleZh":"交換生花了兩星期才逐漸習慣那座更冷的城市。","contrast":"這個詞暗示逐步熟悉；若原句強調立即改變一個做法，adjust to 較自然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The exchange students needed several weeks to adapt to the colder climate.","zh":"交換生花了數星期適應更寒冷的氣候。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The exchange students needed several weeks to acclimatise to the colder climate.","answer":"acclimatise to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adjust the climate","explanation":"學生不能把氣候本身調整掉，受詞關係錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accommodate the climate","explanation":"accommodate 不自然地表示人體逐步習慣氣候。"},{"letter":"C","text":"acclimatise to","explanation":"數星期慢慢適應新氣候，是這個詞的典型語境。"},{"letter":"D","text":"react against","explanation":"表示反對或抵抗，不是逐步習慣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"become familiar with","explanation":"說已熟悉，卻沒有呈現逐步適應的過程。"},{"letter":"F","text":"endure","explanation":"可能只是忍受寒冷，未必習慣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Jin needed a month in the mountain village to adapt to its thin air.","zh":"在山村住了一個月後，阿進已適應當地稀薄的空氣。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Jin needed a month in the mountain village to acclimatise to its thin air.","answer":"acclimatise to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"insist on","explanation":"表示堅持某物，與空氣條件不合。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accommodate","explanation":"缺少恰當受詞，亦不表示身體逐漸習慣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"recognise","explanation":"只表示識別稀薄空氣，不是適應。"},{"letter":"D","text":"acclimatise to","explanation":"經過一個月逐步習慣稀薄空氣，保留原句時間與結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"accept","explanation":"心理接受不等於身體適應空氣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"comply with","explanation":"通常接規則或命令，不接薄空氣。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"get used to","meaning":"習慣起來；口語","note":"經接觸一段時間後，對陌生環境或安排不再感到不適應；to 後接名詞或動名詞。","collocations":"get used to a new campus; get used to working at night","example":"Mira got used to the new campus after a few weeks.","exampleZh":"過了幾星期，米拉習慣了新校園。","contrast":"重點是熟悉感，未必指出具體改變了甚麼做法；to 在此為介詞。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Pong needed three weeks in the dormitory to adapt to sharing a room.","zh":"在宿舍住了三星期後，阿邦適應了與人同房。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Pong needed three weeks in the dormitory to get used to sharing a room.","answer":"get used to sharing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"get used to sharing","explanation":"三星期後習慣與人同房；to 後的 sharing 是動名詞。"},{"letter":"B","text":"get used to share","explanation":"to 是介詞，後面不能在此直接接動詞原形。"},{"letter":"C","text":"become dependent on sharing","explanation":"說成依賴與人同房，超出原句。"},{"letter":"D","text":"approve of sharing","explanation":"只說贊成共住，沒有表示已習慣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"become aware of sharing","explanation":"只知道共住一事，沒有適應結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"respond to sharing","explanation":"只說有反應，不一定已習慣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The pupils needed until midterm to adapt to the school’s early start.","zh":"到了學期中段，學生已適應學校很早開始上課的安排。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The pupils needed until midterm to get used to the school’s early start.","answer":"get used to","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"protest against","explanation":"可以抗議早開課，但不表示過了一段時間後已習慣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"get used to","explanation":"一段時間後熟悉早開課安排，語氣自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accommodate","explanation":"學校可滿足學生需要；學生在此不是安排時間表去照顧它的需要。"},{"letter":"D","text":"memorise","explanation":"記住開課時間不等於已習慣這種早起作息。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tolerate","explanation":"可以勉強忍受早開課，卻仍未必習慣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"plan for","explanation":"可預先計劃應付，但題句描述的是到了學期中段已習慣。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"respond effectively to change","meaning":"有效應對變化；需改寫","note":"描述人在環境變化後採取有用的新做法。比 adapt 長，也可能不如 adapt 明確指出適應了哪個環境。","collocations":"respond effectively to change; respond constructively to new demands","example":"The team responded effectively to change by reorganising shifts for the new timetable.","exampleZh":"團隊重新編排輪班，有效應對新時間表。","contrast":"單獨 respond to change 可能是抱怨或拒絕；effectively 加上有效應對的結果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"When the school timetable changed, the club had to adapt by moving its meeting online so all members could still attend.","zh":"學校時間表改變時，社團須把會議轉到網上，讓所有會員仍可出席。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the school timetable changed, the club had to respond effectively to the change by moving its meeting online so all members could still attend.","answer":"respond effectively to the change","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"notice the change","explanation":"只留意時間變動，沒有表達社團如何繼續開會。"},{"letter":"B","text":"resist the change","explanation":"抗拒與實際把會議改到網上不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"respond to the change","explanation":"有回應但未說是否有效；搬到網上且能繼續開會才是題句重點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"respond effectively to the change","explanation":"網上開會使社團在新時間表下仍能開會，保留有效調整的意思。"},{"letter":"E","text":"make the change","explanation":"表示社團自己發動改變；題句是學校先改時間表，社團隨後調整開會方式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"predict the change","explanation":"預測是事前判斷，原句交代變動後的安排。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When a storm closed the community hall, the organisers managed to adapt by moving the workshops to a nearby school; every session still ran.","zh":"暴風雨令社區會堂關閉後，主辦者成功把工作坊移到附近學校，所有場次仍如期進行。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When a storm closed the community hall, the organisers managed to respond effectively to the change by moving the workshops to a nearby school; every session still ran.","answer":"respond effectively to the change","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"respond randomly to the change","explanation":"隨機改動不能解釋主辦者找到可用場地並讓每場照常進行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"notice the change","explanation":"察覺會堂關閉沒有包括安排附近學校作替代場地。"},{"letter":"C","text":"tolerate the change","explanation":"忍受取消風險，不等於成功保住全部工作坊。"},{"letter":"D","text":"welcome the change","explanation":"歡迎暴風雨或場地關閉既非題意，也沒有表達有效安置活動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"respond effectively to the change","explanation":"另找場地後每場仍能舉行，結果證明應對有效。"},{"letter":"F","text":"prepare for the change","explanation":"事前預備不能代替題句已發生的場地轉移及成功結果。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Accommodate · 動詞主客體","zh":"中文辨析： 學校可 accommodate pupils’ needs，意思是作出安排滿足學生需要；學生適應學校通常說 adjust to 或 adapt to。","point":"A school accommodates a pupil’s needs; a pupil adapts to a school."},{"word":"Respond / react · 回應不足","zh":"中文辨析： 有人對變化投訴也算 respond 或 react；若要保留成功適應，必須交代有效改變的做法。","point":"A response can resist change; adaptation requires a suitable adjustment."},{"word":"Accept / tolerate · 接受或忍受","zh":"中文辨析： 接受規則或忍受環境未必已改變自己的日常做法。","point":"Acceptance and tolerance do not by themselves show behavioural adaptation."},{"word":"Adjustable · 詞性與受事","zh":"中文辨析： Adjustable 常形容可調節的物件，如桌椅；不能用來說學生已適應新學校。","point":"Adjustable describes a modifiable object, not a person adapting."}],"moduleNumber":64},{"id":"lesson-065","sourceId":25,"headword":"adaptable","title":"Adaptable","titleZh":"善於適應的","subtitle":"善於適應的","description":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “Why being adaptable is becoming more important nowadays”","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “Why being adaptable is becoming more important nowadays”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["flexible","near","形容人願意或能改變計劃，未必已在新環境中成功安頓。"],["adjustable","false for person","通常形容椅子、設定等可由人調節的物件，不能自然地形容一名學生善於適應。"],["able to respond to change","conditional","只說有能力回應仍不足；需指出能有效改變做法。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["flexible","靈活的；可改變做法：Flexible 不保證每次改動有效；若強調已成功安頓，able to adjust 更明確。"],["able to adjust","能作出調整；能力改寫：這是形容詞性詞組，與 adaptability 這個名詞不同；只有有回應卻未調整時不足以成立。"],["versatile","多才多藝；跨角色應變：只會在一個新學校調整作息，未能證明 versatile；比 adaptable 多了多種任務能力。"],["quick to adapt","迅速適應；有速度條件：Adaptable 本身不承諾速度；若原句只說終能適應，不能無故加 quick。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 人在新情況改計劃可說 flexible；具體說能調整可說 able to adjust；多種角色皆勝任才說 versatile；只有原句明示速度才加 quick to adapt。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"flexible","meaning":"靈活的；可改變做法","note":"形容人願意按情況更改計劃或方法，尤其有可見的選擇與行動時。","collocations":"a flexible learner; be flexible about plans","example":"The flexible coach changed the training plan when it rained.","exampleZh":"那位靈活的教練下雨時修改訓練計劃。","contrast":"Flexible 不保證每次改動有效；若強調已成功安頓，able to adjust 更明確。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The adaptable tutor changed her teaching plan when the pupils needed more practice.","zh":"學生需要更多練習時，那位善於適應的導師修改了教學計劃。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The flexible tutor changed her teaching plan when the pupils needed more practice.","answer":"flexible","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"flexible","explanation":"她按學生需要修改計劃，突顯做法靈活。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adjustable","explanation":"通常指椅子或設定可調，不自然地修飾導師。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resistant","explanation":"表示抗拒改變，與她修改計劃相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"receptive","explanation":"表示樂意接納意見，但未如題句指出已能改動教學計劃。"},{"letter":"E","text":"patient","explanation":"有耐性可能幫助教學，但原句證據是她實際改變教學計劃。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resilient","explanation":"題句沒有受挫後恢復，韌性不如靈活精準。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"An adaptable organiser can move activities indoors if the weather changes.","zh":"善於適應的活動籌辦者能在天氣變化時把活動移到室內。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"A flexible organiser can move activities indoors if the weather changes.","answer":"flexible","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"rigid","explanation":"表示缺乏變通，與天氣變化時改地點相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"flexible","explanation":"能按天氣修改活動地點，正是安排靈活。"},{"letter":"C","text":"adjustable","explanation":"通常說 adjustable schedule，不自然地直接指籌辦者。"},{"letter":"D","text":"open-minded","explanation":"願意接納改變，卻未像題句那樣指出可實際更改活動地點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resilient","explanation":"受挫後復原並非題句的天氣應變重點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"versatile","explanation":"擅長多種任務未由改一次場地證明。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"able to adjust","meaning":"能作出調整；能力改寫","note":"形容人有能力按新條件改動習慣或工作方式；需要交代調整所對應的變化。","collocations":"able to adjust to new routines; able to adjust quickly","example":"She is able to adjust to different classroom routines.","exampleZh":"她能適應不同的課室日常安排。","contrast":"這是形容詞性詞組，與 adaptability 這個名詞不同；只有有回應卻未調整時不足以成立。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"An adaptable new employee learns the revised booking system and changes her routine.","zh":"一名善於適應的新員工學會修訂後的預訂系統，並改變日常做法。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The new employee is able to adjust to the revised booking system: she learns it and changes her routine.","answer":"able to adjust","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"allowed to adjust","explanation":"表示獲准改動，未必有能力實際做到。"},{"letter":"B","text":"willing to adjust","explanation":"願意配合是態度；題句還證實她學會系統並改變流程。"},{"letter":"C","text":"able to adjust","explanation":"學懂新系統並改變工作流程，顯示有能力調整。"},{"letter":"D","text":"quick to adjust","explanation":"題句沒有說她多快學會，不能加上「迅速」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"expected to adjust","explanation":"被要求配合不等於已具備並運用了調整能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adjustable","explanation":"可調節的物件用形容詞，不宜形容員工。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The adaptable guide altered her route when a path closed.","zh":"小徑關閉時，善於適應的嚮導改變了路線。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The guide was able to adjust her route when a path closed.","answer":"able to adjust","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"willing to adjust","explanation":"願意改路是態度；題句顯示她已改路，故能力說法更準確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"quick to adapt","explanation":"她改了路線，但原句沒有說關閉後多久才改。"},{"letter":"C","text":"able to stay calm","explanation":"保持鎮定可有助應變，卻沒有說明她能重訂路線。"},{"letter":"D","text":"able to adjust","explanation":"小徑關閉後改走別路，說明嚮導能調整做法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adjustable","explanation":"不能自然形容嚮導如物件般可調。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ready to adapt","explanation":"準備好改變不等於題句中已成功改走別路。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"versatile","meaning":"多才多藝；跨角色應變","note":"形容能在數種不同工作或角色中有效發揮的人；須有多方面技能的證據。","collocations":"a versatile performer; a versatile team member","example":"The versatile volunteer can design posters and speak to visitors.","exampleZh":"這名多才多藝的義工既能設計海報，也能向訪客解說。","contrast":"只會在一個新學校調整作息，未能證明 versatile；比 adaptable 多了多種任務能力。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The adaptable volunteer can translate, design flyers and organise the event timetable.","zh":"那名善於適應的義工能翻譯、設計傳單及編排活動時間表。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The versatile volunteer can translate, design flyers and organise the event timetable.","answer":"versatile","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"resilient","explanation":"沒有受挫後恢復；題句列出多種技能。"},{"letter":"B","text":"obedient","explanation":"順從與勝任三類工作不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"adjustable","explanation":"用於可調節物件，不自然地指人。"},{"letter":"D","text":"consistent","explanation":"一貫做法未突出不同角色。"},{"letter":"E","text":"versatile","explanation":"能翻譯、設計及編排，是跨任務能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"passive","explanation":"被動與積極勝任多項工作相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the interpreter fell ill, the adaptable festival worker moved from selling tickets to interpreting the guest's speech.","zh":"口譯員病倒時，那名善於應變的節慶工作人員由售票轉去為嘉賓演說口譯。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the interpreter fell ill, the versatile festival worker moved from selling tickets to interpreting the guest's speech.","answer":"versatile","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adjustable","explanation":"可指設備能由他人調節；題句說的是職員能做兩類工作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"patient","explanation":"願意耐心等口譯員康復，不代表能即時頂替口譯。"},{"letter":"C","text":"conventional","explanation":"按慣常安排工作，不能概括由售票轉為口譯的能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"resistant","explanation":"抗拒改變職務與她實際頂替口譯員不符。"},{"letter":"E","text":"recovering","explanation":"病倒的是口譯員，該職員並非在康復。"},{"letter":"F","text":"versatile","explanation":"原本售票，後來又能口譯，顯示具備跨職務本領。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"quick to adapt","meaning":"迅速適應；有速度條件","note":"當句子明說能很快改變做法、安頓於新情況時，突出速度的形容詞性改寫。","collocations":"quick to adapt to changes; quick to adapt in a new role","example":"The newcomer was quick to adapt to the unfamiliar timetable.","exampleZh":"新來者很快適應了陌生的時間表。","contrast":"Adaptable 本身不承諾速度；若原句只說終能適應，不能無故加 quick。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The adaptable intern learned the unfamiliar booking system within a day.","zh":"那名善於適應的實習生一天內學會陌生的預訂系統。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The intern was quick to adapt, learning the unfamiliar booking system within a day.","answer":"quick to adapt","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"quick to adapt","explanation":"一天內學會新系統，原句有迅速適應的證據。"},{"letter":"B","text":"slow to comply","explanation":"又慢又只是遵從，與一天內學會不符。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reluctant to change","explanation":"不願改變與已快速學會新系統相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"able to recover","explanation":"沒有挫敗後復原。"},{"letter":"E","text":"easy to adjust","explanation":"像被人調節的物件，不自然地形容實習生。"},{"letter":"F","text":"bound to succeed","explanation":"保證成功，原句只談一項學習表現。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the projector failed moments before her talk, the adaptable student switched to printed diagrams without delaying her presentation.","zh":"投影機在演講前一刻故障，那名善於應變的學生立即改用印刷圖表，沒有延誤報告。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the projector failed moments before her talk, the student was quick to adapt: she switched to printed diagrams without delaying her presentation.","answer":"quick to adapt","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"able to wait","explanation":"題句強調立即轉用紙本圖表，並非耐心等待修理。"},{"letter":"B","text":"quick to adapt","explanation":"投影機臨場故障後迅速轉用後備方法，明確顯示應變速度。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resistant to change","explanation":"抗拒改變便不會立刻轉用紙本圖表。"},{"letter":"D","text":"merely flexible in theory","explanation":"她已實際更改呈示方法，不只是口頭上願意變通。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adjustable by others","explanation":"表示由別人調節她，與她主動換方法不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resilient after failure","explanation":"投影機故障是設備問題；題句重點是即時應變，不是受挫後長期復原。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Adjustable · 人與物件","zh":"中文辨析： Adjustable 常形容椅子高度、屏幕亮度等可調節物件；本課 adaptable 指人能主動改做法。","point":"An adjustable chair can be altered; an adaptable person alters behaviour."},{"word":"Willing / open to change · 願意不等於能做到","zh":"中文辨析： 願意聽新安排是態度；能否實際學懂新系統及改習慣仍需證據。","point":"Willingness is an attitude, not proven ability to adapt."},{"word":"Resilient · 復原不等於適應","zh":"中文辨析： 受挫後重新振作可說 resilient；題句若只談改變做法，無須假設有挫敗。","point":"Resilience concerns recovery after difficulty; adaptability can occur without a setback."},{"word":"Versatile · 多技能須證明","zh":"中文辨析： 多才多藝可在跨多種任務的句子中替換，但只適應一項新日程不保證多技能。","point":"Versatile implies varied capabilities, not one adjustment."}],"moduleNumber":65},{"id":"lesson-066","sourceId":26,"headword":"addicted","title":"Addicted","titleZh":"對使用優惠券難以自控","subtitle":"對使用優惠券難以自控","description":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 4.2〈Couponing — Job, Hobby, or Necessity?〉： “Do you think some people could become addicted to couponing?”","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 4.2〈Couponing — Job, Hobby, or Necessity?〉： “Do you think some people could become addicted to couponing?”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["dependent","conditional","dependent on couponing 可能只指經濟上依賴折扣；必須另有失控證據。"],["hooked","informal near","hooked on couponing 是口語吸引力很強的說法，不是醫學診斷。"],["compulsively attached","false / unnatural","不自然的英語搭配；應說 feel compelled to keep couponing 等行為描述。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["hooked on couponing","沉迷使用優惠券；口語：Hooked on 可較輕鬆地形容強烈興趣；若缺少失控或問題證據，不應視作確診。"],["unable to stop couponing","難以停止；行為改寫：沒有停止嘗試的證據時，不可無端聲稱 unable to stop；喜歡優惠券不等同不能停。"],["compelled to keep couponing","感到非繼續不可；依語境：Compelled 可來自外在命令；本課必須清楚是個人的難以控制衝動。"],["obsessed with couponing","思緒常被優惠券佔據；只有明顯反覆想着並影響其他活動時才可作有條件改寫。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 有失控線索時，口語可說 hooked on couponing；停止多次失敗可直接說 unable to stop couponing；強調內心衝動可說 feel compelled to keep couponing；思緒持續被折扣佔據可說 obsessed with couponing。保留 could/might 的假設語氣。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"hooked on couponing","meaning":"沉迷使用優惠券；口語","note":"非正式說法，表示很難抗拒繼續蒐集或使用優惠券；保留原題的可能性時要寫 could become。","collocations":"be hooked on couponing; become hooked on couponing","example":"She worried that she was becoming hooked on couponing after spending hours clipping coupons.","exampleZh":"她花數小時剪優惠券後，擔心自己愈來愈沉迷其中。","contrast":"Hooked on 可較輕鬆地形容強烈興趣；若缺少失控或問題證據，不應視作確診。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If he keeps collecting coupons after promising himself to stop, could he become addicted to couponing?","zh":"若他答應自己停止後仍不停收集優惠券，他會否可能對此上癮？\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"If he keeps collecting coupons after promising himself to stop, could he become hooked on couponing?","answer":"hooked on couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"hooked on couponing","explanation":"與可能逐漸難以抗拒的行為吻合，仍保留疑問。"},{"letter":"B","text":"keen on couponing","explanation":"只有興趣，未包含題句想停卻繼續的失控線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fond of bargains","explanation":"喜愛便宜貨不等於難以抗拒重複購券。"},{"letter":"D","text":"dependent on discounts","explanation":"可能是經濟上需要優惠，與行為失控不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preoccupied with savings","explanation":"心裏常想省錢，未必已反覆進行購券。"},{"letter":"F","text":"reluctant to stop couponing","explanation":"不願停止是選擇；題句暗示想停仍難停。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The discussion asks whether shoppers who cannot resist buying unneeded items with coupons might become addicted to couponing.","zh":"討論問難以抗拒以優惠券購買不需要物品的顧客，會否沉迷使用優惠券。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The discussion asks whether shoppers who cannot resist buying unneeded items with coupons might become hooked on couponing.","answer":"hooked on couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a bargain enthusiast","explanation":"愛找便宜貨只說偏好，不能說明題句購買不需要物品時仍難以抗拒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"hooked on couponing","explanation":"保留可能沉迷的口語語氣，並有難以抗拒的行為線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reliant on coupon savings","explanation":"若生活費緊張而靠優惠省錢，是經濟需要；題句問的是無法抵擋購買。"},{"letter":"D","text":"habitual coupon users","explanation":"經常使用未必有購買多餘物品的失控傾向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"eager to compare prices","explanation":"樂於比價仍屬主動選擇，不必然停不了。"},{"letter":"F","text":"attracted by coupons","explanation":"被優惠吸引較輕，未涵蓋難以抗拒的程度。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"unable to stop couponing","meaning":"難以停止；行為改寫","note":"直接描述嘗試停止仍繼續的行為，比一個上癮標籤更審慎；視語境保留 could / might。","collocations":"be unable to stop couponing; find it hard to stop couponing","example":"He tried to cut back but found himself unable to stop couponing.","exampleZh":"他試圖減少使用優惠券，卻發現自己難以停止。","contrast":"沒有停止嘗試的證據時，不可無端聲稱 unable to stop；喜歡優惠券不等同不能停。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Could a person become addicted to couponing if she repeatedly tries to quit but cannot?","zh":"若一個人多次嘗試停止使用優惠券卻做不到，她會否可能對此上癮？\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Could a person be unable to stop couponing if she repeatedly tries to quit but cannot?","answer":"unable to stop couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reluctant to stop couponing","explanation":"不願意停與嘗試停止卻做不到不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"accustomed to couponing","explanation":"習慣做未必有停止失敗的情況。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unable to stop couponing","explanation":"多次嘗試仍不能停，直接說明困難，且可保留疑問。"},{"letter":"D","text":"dependent on discounts","explanation":"經濟依賴未必表示控制不了自己的行為。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interested in coupons","explanation":"有興趣不能涵蓋題句反覆想停止的困難。"},{"letter":"F","text":"obsessed with bargains","explanation":"可能只是不斷想着折扣，未明說停不了購券。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The article asks whether someone who keeps sorting coupons through family meals and says she cannot make herself put them away might be addicted to couponing.","zh":"文章問有人連與家人吃飯時也不停整理優惠券，並說自己無法放下它們，會否可能對此上癮。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The article asks whether someone who keeps sorting coupons through family meals and says she cannot make herself put them away might be unable to stop couponing.","answer":"unable to stop couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a regular coupon user","explanation":"經常用券未必會在家庭聚餐時也放不下整理工作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a money-conscious shopper","explanation":"節省意識不能解釋她自述無法收起優惠券。"},{"letter":"C","text":"dependent on lower prices","explanation":"財務需要與吃飯時不能停止整理優惠券是兩回事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unable to stop couponing","explanation":"她在家庭聚餐仍整理優惠券，並明說自己無法放下，行為改寫有根據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"someone reluctant to quit","explanation":"不情願與明說「做不到」不同；題句指控制困難。"},{"letter":"F","text":"someone who enjoys coupons","explanation":"喜歡優惠券可以自行選擇整理時間，未涵蓋聚餐時仍停不下來。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"compelled to keep couponing","meaning":"感到非繼續不可；依語境","note":"強調主觀上有難以抵擋的衝動；可用 feel compelled to keep couponing，不把假設當診斷。","collocations":"feel compelled to keep couponing; become compelled to keep couponing","example":"She felt compelled to keep couponing even after the savings became tiny.","exampleZh":"即使省下的錢很少，她仍感到非繼續使用優惠券不可。","contrast":"Compelled 可來自外在命令；本課必須清楚是個人的難以控制衝動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If someone feels an uncontrollable urge to continue, could that person become addicted to couponing?","zh":"若某人感到無法控制的衝動要繼續使用優惠券，那人會否可能上癮？\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"If someone feels an uncontrollable urge to continue, could that person feel compelled to keep couponing?","answer":"compelled to keep couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"compelled to keep couponing","explanation":"與題句明說的難以控制衝動吻合，仍是可能性提問。"},{"letter":"B","text":"willing to coupon","explanation":"願意做是選擇，不是題句難以抵擋的衝動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"persuaded to coupon","explanation":"被他人勸說是外因，原句說自己的內心衝動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"used to couponing","explanation":"熟習一種做法不等於感到非做不可。"},{"letter":"E","text":"dependent on discounts","explanation":"可能為生活成本而依賴，未證實內心衝動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"keen to find bargains","explanation":"熱衷找優惠較輕，沒有不能控制的迫切感。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The speaker wonders whether people who keep searching for coupons despite wanting to sleep could be addicted to couponing.","zh":"說話者想知道，有人明明想睡覺卻繼續找優惠券，會否可能沉迷其中。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The speaker wonders whether people who keep searching for coupons despite wanting to sleep could be compelled to keep couponing.","answer":"compelled to keep couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"keen to save on purchases","explanation":"想省錢是普通動機，未能解釋想睡仍繼續找券。"},{"letter":"B","text":"compelled to keep couponing","explanation":"想睡卻持續搜尋，支持難以抗拒的衝動描述。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accustomed to checking offers","explanation":"習慣查看不等於題句內心難以抗拒。"},{"letter":"D","text":"persuaded by a discount alert","explanation":"外來通知可能引起查看，卻非題句描述的內在衝動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"paid to collect coupons","explanation":"受薪責任會使人繼續，但題句沒有工作安排。"},{"letter":"F","text":"willing to stay up late","explanation":"自願熬夜不等於想睡卻覺得非做不可。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"obsessed with couponing","meaning":"腦中總想着優惠券；有條件","note":"強調優惠券佔據思緒，甚至打斷日常活動；若只有偶爾想到折扣，強度不足。它是普通用語，不表示已獲臨床診斷。","collocations":"be obsessed with couponing; become obsessed with finding coupons","example":"He was obsessed with couponing and kept planning bargains even during a family meal.","exampleZh":"他對使用優惠券着迷，連與家人吃飯時也不停盤算優惠。","contrast":"Obsessed 着重腦中反覆想着；hooked on 和 unable to stop 更着重實際行為難以停下。需有明顯的思緒佔據線索才可用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The class wonders whether a pupil who talks about coupons during every lesson and misses assignments might be addicted to couponing.","zh":"全班想知道，有學生每節課都談優惠券，還因此漏交功課，會否可能對使用優惠券着迷。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The class wonders whether a pupil who talks about coupons during every lesson and misses assignments might be obsessed with couponing.","answer":"obsessed with couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fascinated by couponing","explanation":"感到好奇或着迷，未必會每節課都談及，更未必因此漏交功課。"},{"letter":"B","text":"financially dependent on coupons","explanation":"可能只是家庭需要折扣；題句着重思緒佔據課堂。"},{"letter":"C","text":"obsessed with couponing","explanation":"課課談優惠券並忽略功課，支持其思緒過度集中於此的有條件改寫。"},{"letter":"D","text":"experienced in couponing","explanation":"熟練使用優惠券與上課時不停談論是兩回事。"},{"letter":"E","text":"keen on saving money","explanation":"樂於省錢較弱，未涵蓋已影響課業的反覆談論。"},{"letter":"F","text":"persuaded to collect coupons","explanation":"受人勸說不等於自己一直想着優惠券。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Her friend worries that she may be addicted to couponing: even on holiday, far from any shops, she keeps thinking about future coupon deals.","zh":"朋友擔心她可能對使用優惠券過度着迷：即使在遠離商店的假期裏，她仍不斷想着將來的優惠券折扣。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Her friend worries that she may be obsessed with couponing: even on holiday, far from any shops, she keeps thinking about future coupon deals.","answer":"obsessed with couponing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"hooked on shopping","explanation":"把焦點擴成購物行為；題句只說她不斷想着優惠券折扣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"obsessed with couponing","explanation":"沒有商店可用券時仍反覆想着未來折扣，突出難擺脫的思緒。"},{"letter":"C","text":"reliant on discounts","explanation":"財務依賴不必令人在遠離商店時持續想着優惠券。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unusually frugal","explanation":"節儉是花費習慣，未涵蓋題句持續佔據心思的情況。"},{"letter":"E","text":"used to clipping coupons","explanation":"習慣剪券不表示假期中也不停想着未來優惠。"},{"letter":"F","text":"worried about prices","explanation":"擔心價格可能是原因，但題句沒有說她焦慮，而是反覆想着用券。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Dependent · 依賴有兩種","zh":"中文辨析： Dependent on discounts 可以只是收入有限而需要省錢；若要表示行為失控，必須給出停止失敗等證據。","point":"Financial dependence on discounts is not proof of behavioural compulsion."},{"word":"Obsessed / interested · 程度差異","zh":"中文辨析： Interested 太弱；obsessed 可形容反覆想某事，但未必已出現難以停止的實際行為。","point":"Interest and preoccupation do not automatically establish addiction."},{"word":"Compulsively attached · 不自然搭配","zh":"中文辨析： Attached 通常接對象而非表示持續使用優惠券的行為；可改為 feel compelled to keep couponing。","point":"Describe the behaviour: feel compelled to keep couponing."},{"word":"Clinical diagnosis · 不可由題目推斷","zh":"中文辨析： 原文只問 could；新例句也只能說可能或難以控制，不能確診某個人患有疾病。","point":"A hypothetical discussion question is not a diagnosis."},{"word":"Obsessed · 着迷不必然是失控","zh":"中文辨析： 若人常想着優惠券並因此忽略正事，obsessed with couponing 可作有條件的口語改寫；只因喜歡省錢便說 obsessed 則過強。","point":"Obsession suggests persistent preoccupation, which must be supported by the context."}],"moduleNumber":66},{"id":"lesson-067","sourceId":28,"headword":"addicts","title":"Addicts","titleZh":"標題中的手機沉迷者","subtitle":"標題中的手機沉迷者","description":"原文： 2016 年 DSE 9.3 標題為〈Text Walking Lanes for Smartphone Addicts〉；可核對的正文片語是 “a culture of walking and texting” on the Utah Valley University campus。標題與片語分別呈現稱呼和可觀察的行為，並無提供臨床診斷。","sourceSense":"原文： 2016 年 DSE 9.3 標題為〈Text Walking Lanes for Smartphone Addicts〉；可核對的正文片語是 “a culture of walking and texting” on the Utah Valley University campus。標題與片語分別呈現稱呼和可觀察的行為，並無提供臨床診斷。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["compulsive users","conditional","要說明是 compulsive smartphone users，且有難以控制的反覆使用證據；走路發訊息一次不足夠。"],["dependent users","conditional","應完整說 people dependent on their phones；可能是實用依賴，須交代不良影響。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["heavy smartphone users","大量使用手機的人；中性：Heavy 只說使用量，不保證有傷害或失控；原標題的貶義會減弱。"],["compulsive smartphone users","難以自控的手機使用者；有條件：走路時發一則訊息或用導航，不足以證明 compulsive；不是臨床診斷詞的替身。"],["people dependent on smartphones","依賴手機的人；須交代依賴性質：工作或求助必須用手機可造成實用依賴，但不等於失控；須看文章實際證據。"],["people who text while walking","只在談邊走邊發訊息的可觀察行為時適用；是文章語境的改寫，不是 addicts 的通用同義詞。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 文章只有大量使用證據時稱 heavy smartphone users；有反覆想停失敗才稱 compulsive smartphone users；有離開手機便難處理生活的線索才稱 people dependent on smartphones；若只證實邊走邊發訊息，直接說 people who text while walking。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"heavy smartphone users","meaning":"大量使用手機的人；中性","note":"在只觀察到使用頻繁、沒有控制能力證據時，是較審慎的標題改寫。","collocations":"heavy smartphone users; heavy phone use","example":"The survey described heavy smartphone users without calling any participant an addict.","exampleZh":"調查描述大量使用手機的人，卻沒有把任何參加者稱為上癮者。","contrast":"Heavy 只說使用量，不保證有傷害或失控；原標題的貶義會減弱。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The article’s headline calls walkers who check their phones often “smartphone addicts”, but reports no evidence that they cannot stop.","zh":"文章標題把經常用手機的人稱為「手機沉迷者」，卻沒有提供他們無法停止的證據。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The article’s headline calls walkers who check their phones often “heavy smartphone users”, but reports no evidence that they cannot stop.","answer":"heavy smartphone users","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"heavy smartphone users","explanation":"只證實頻繁使用，這個中性稱呼符合證據強度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"clinically diagnosed users","explanation":"原文未有診斷，不能把標題用語當醫學結論。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compulsive smartphone users","explanation":"只有使用頻繁，未證實難以控制。"},{"letter":"D","text":"people dependent on phones","explanation":"依賴程度不能單靠用量或走路查看推斷。"},{"letter":"E","text":"occasional phone users","explanation":"偶爾使用與題句所述頻繁使用不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"skilled smartphone users","explanation":"操作技巧與用量是兩個不同問題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The writer uses “smartphone addicts” for people who use their phones for many hours, without discussing loss of control.","zh":"作者用「手機沉迷者」稱呼每天用手機多個小時的人，卻沒有討論他們是否失控。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The writer uses “heavy smartphone users” for people who use their phones for many hours, without discussing loss of control.","answer":"heavy smartphone users","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"people reliant on phones","explanation":"多小時使用不足以判定沒有手機便無法生活。"},{"letter":"B","text":"heavy smartphone users","explanation":"「多個小時」支持使用量大，不推斷失控。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compulsive phone checkers","explanation":"題句特別沒有談能否停下，不能加上失控。"},{"letter":"D","text":"phone enthusiasts","explanation":"喜歡手機也許存在，但作者只報告使用時數。"},{"letter":"E","text":"occasional app users","explanation":"偶爾使用與多小時用手機不符。"},{"letter":"F","text":"diagnosed technology addicts","explanation":"沒有診斷，不能把標題修辭改成醫學身份。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"compulsive smartphone users","meaning":"難以自控的手機使用者；有條件","note":"只有文字描述多次嘗試停止卻不斷查看手機時，才能由標題的 addicts 轉述為此說法。","collocations":"compulsive smartphone users; compulsive phone checking","example":"The report describes compulsive smartphone users who keep checking their phones despite repeated attempts to stop.","exampleZh":"報告描述難以自控的手機使用者：他們多次嘗試停止，仍不斷查看手機。","contrast":"走路時發一則訊息或用導航，不足以證明 compulsive；不是臨床診斷詞的替身。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In a separate case study, the “smartphone addicts” tried repeatedly to put their phones away but kept checking them.","zh":"在另一項個案研究中，那些被稱為「手機沉迷者」的人多次嘗試收起手機，卻仍不斷查看。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"In a separate case study, the “compulsive smartphone users” tried repeatedly to put their phones away but kept checking them.","answer":"compulsive smartphone users","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"heavy smartphone users","explanation":"只說用量，未反映題句多次想停卻失敗。"},{"letter":"B","text":"phone enthusiasts","explanation":"喜愛手機不足以說明不能按決定收起。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compulsive smartphone users","explanation":"反覆嘗試仍不停查看，支持難以自控的行為描述。"},{"letter":"D","text":"people dependent on phones","explanation":"依賴可能出於工作；題句着重行為控制。"},{"letter":"E","text":"frequent phone checkers","explanation":"只說查看頻率，沒有意願與行為衝突。"},{"letter":"F","text":"skilled app users","explanation":"技巧高低與停不了無關。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When researchers silenced all alerts, the study’s “smartphone addicts” still unlocked their phones every few minutes without intending to.","zh":"研究員關掉所有提示後，研究中被稱為「手機沉迷者」的人仍每隔幾分鐘便不自覺地解鎖手機。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When researchers silenced all alerts, the study’s “compulsive smartphone users” still unlocked their phones every few minutes without intending to.","answer":"compulsive smartphone users","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"heavy app users","explanation":"用量大未必表示沒有通知也不自覺地反覆解鎖。"},{"letter":"B","text":"curious smartphone owners","explanation":"好奇想看手機是自願選擇，較難解釋沒有意圖仍頻繁查看。"},{"letter":"C","text":"people reliant on phone maps","explanation":"題句沒有導航需要；研究員也已關掉所有提示。"},{"letter":"D","text":"compulsive smartphone users","explanation":"沒有提示仍每隔幾分鐘不自覺解鎖，支持難以自控的重複行為。"},{"letter":"E","text":"enthusiastic gamers","explanation":"原句沒有說他們正在玩遊戲或因遊戲而解鎖。"},{"letter":"F","text":"habitual screen users","explanation":"習慣可有意識地維持；題句特別說他們並非有意解鎖。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"people dependent on smartphones","meaning":"依賴手機的人；須交代依賴性質","note":"完整的名詞詞組；當人離開手機便難以處理正常生活，且有不良影響時可用。","collocations":"people dependent on their phones; dependence on smartphones","example":"The interviewees were people dependent on smartphones who felt unable to manage daily tasks without constant access.","exampleZh":"受訪者是依賴手機的人，覺得不能持續使用手機便難以處理日常事務。","contrast":"工作或求助必須用手機可造成實用依賴，但不等於失控；須看文章實際證據。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The interview calls them “smartphone addicts” because they feel unable to manage ordinary tasks without checking their phones.","zh":"訪問把他們稱為「手機沉迷者」，因為他們覺得不查看手機便無法處理普通事務。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The interview describes them as people dependent on smartphones because they feel unable to manage ordinary tasks without checking their phones.","answer":"people dependent on smartphones","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"people who own smartphones","explanation":"擁有裝置遠弱於覺得不能短暫離開。"},{"letter":"B","text":"heavy smartphone users","explanation":"只說大量使用，未表示生活上非帶不可。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compulsive smartphone users","explanation":"題句呈現依賴感，未明說多次想停卻失敗。"},{"letter":"D","text":"people familiar with smartphones","explanation":"熟悉操作不等於離開便難處理事情。"},{"letter":"E","text":"people dependent on smartphones","explanation":"正常事務也覺得非查看不可，支持依賴描述。"},{"letter":"F","text":"people carrying smartphones","explanation":"帶手機是行為描述，未說明依賴程度。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The article labels some walkers “smartphone addicts” after they say they cannot leave home without a phone, even for a short safe walk.","zh":"一些行人說即使只是短暫、安全的散步也不能不帶手機，文章便把他們稱為「手機沉迷者」。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The article describes some walkers as people dependent on smartphones after they say they cannot leave home without a phone, even for a short safe walk.","answer":"people dependent on smartphones","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"frequent phone carriers","explanation":"常帶電話只描述頻率，不說明短暫散步也非帶不可的感受。"},{"letter":"B","text":"experienced app users","explanation":"熟練操作與散步時不能離開手機無關。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compulsive phone checkers","explanation":"原句只說不能不帶，沒有說散步中反覆查看。"},{"letter":"D","text":"phone users at work","explanation":"工作需要合理，但題句明說是安全短途散步。"},{"letter":"E","text":"people interested in phones","explanation":"有興趣太弱，不能涵蓋非帶不可的依賴感。"},{"letter":"F","text":"people dependent on smartphones","explanation":"「短暫安全散步也不能不帶」可描述依賴感，但仍非臨床診斷。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"people who text while walking","meaning":"邊走邊發訊息的人；文章行為改寫","note":"當句子專指文章提到的邊走邊輸入訊息者，可用可觀察的行為取代標題的修辭稱呼；這不是 addicts 在所有語境的字典同義詞。","collocations":"people who text while walking; pedestrians texting as they walk.","example":"The campus signs remind people who text while walking to watch the stairs.","exampleZh":"校園告示提醒邊走邊發訊息的人留意樓梯。","contrast":"此說法不推斷使用時間、依賴或診斷；只有句子確實談「走路時發訊息」才可用，不能拿來概括所有手機使用者。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The campus notice calls pedestrians who type messages as they walk “smartphone addicts”, but says nothing about their use at other times.","zh":"校園告示把走路時輸入訊息的行人稱為「手機沉迷者」，但沒有談他們在其他時間怎樣使用手機。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The campus notice calls pedestrians who type messages as they walk “people who text while walking”, but says nothing about their use at other times.","answer":"people who text while walking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"heavy smartphone users","explanation":"告示沒有提供整天用手機的時數或使用量。"},{"letter":"B","text":"compulsive smartphone users","explanation":"走路時發訊息不足以證明多次想停卻做不到。"},{"letter":"C","text":"people dependent on smartphones","explanation":"未知行人離開手機是否難以處理日常事務。"},{"letter":"D","text":"people who text while walking","explanation":"只陳述告示確實記錄的邊走邊輸入訊息行為。"},{"letter":"E","text":"people who use maps while walking","explanation":"看地圖可用手機，但原句明說輸入訊息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"people who text while seated","explanation":"地點與原句「走路時」相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The campus planned a marked lane for “smartphone addicts” who send messages as they walk between buildings; it made no claim about clinical addiction.","zh":"校園計劃劃設一條通道，供在建築物之間邊走邊發訊息、被稱為「手機沉迷者」的人使用；計劃沒有提出臨床上癮的判斷。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The campus planned a marked lane for people who text while walking between buildings; it made no claim about clinical addiction.","answer":"people who text while walking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"people who carry phones while walking","explanation":"帶手機經過通道未必邊行邊發訊息，範圍過闊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"people who read messages while seated","explanation":"坐着閱讀與通道服務的邊走邊發訊息者不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"people unable to stop texting","explanation":"加入自控困難；計劃明言沒有作成癮判斷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"people dependent on phone navigation","explanation":"導航需要與此處輸入短訊不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"people who text while walking","explanation":"直接指出通道面向邊行邊發訊息的人，不推斷醫學狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"people who use phones for work","explanation":"工作用途沒有交代，亦不是這條通道的界定條件。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Headline addicts · 標題修辭","zh":"中文辨析： 標題用 addicts 吸引注意；正文只見走路發訊息，未證明個別行人有病或難以自控。","point":"A provocative headline does not establish a diagnosis."},{"word":"Heavy / frequent · 用量不等於失控","zh":"中文辨析： 使用時間長與停不下來是不同判斷；若沒有控制能力資料，用 heavy users 較穩妥。","point":"Frequency alone does not prove compulsive behaviour."},{"word":"Compulsive · 需停止失敗證據","zh":"中文辨析： 單次在樓梯發訊息可算危險，但不表示多次想停卻停不了。","point":"Compulsive use needs evidence of hard-to-control repetition."},{"word":"Dependent · 實用需要也可能依賴","zh":"中文辨析： 手機作導航或聯絡家人可能是實用需要；若用 dependent，要說清是哪一種依賴。","point":"Practical reliance differs from problematic dependence."},{"word":"Behaviour / label · 行為描寫與標籤","zh":"中文辨析： 標題的 addicts 暗示沉迷；若只證明某人邊走邊發訊息，較嚴謹的改寫是 people who text while walking，但不能推廣至所有被稱為 addicts 的人。","point":"A walking-and-texting description reports an observed action, not a general dependence or diagnosis."}],"moduleNumber":67},{"id":"lesson-068","sourceId":80,"headword":"anxiety","title":"Anxiety","titleZh":"焦慮感","subtitle":"焦慮感","description":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 3.3〈The art of self-care〉所摘錄的 [Tatler Asia 原文](https://www.tatlerasia.com/lifestyle/wellbeing/hk-self-care-mental-health-advice) 引述 Odile Thiang 談心理健康時說，anxiety or depression 有增加的情況；文章稍後亦提及 feelings of anxiety and depression。這裏把 anxiety 與 depression 分開列出；本課教名詞 anxiety 表示憂慮、不安的感受或狀態，不把一個詞自動當成對任何人的診斷。來源索引句在後半截有截斷，故本課只引述已可核對的短語，不重建缺失文字。所有練習均為原創。 [Cambridge Dictionary](https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/anxiety) 對一般語義的解釋亦把它連於 nervousness/worry 的不舒服感。","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 3.3〈The art of self-care〉所摘錄的 [Tatler Asia 原文](https://www.tatlerasia.com/lifestyle/wellbeing/hk-self-care-mental-health-advice) 引述 Odile Thiang 談心理健康時說，anxiety or depression 有增加的情況；文章稍後亦提及 feelings of anxiety and depression。這裏把 anxiety 與 depression 分開列出；本課教名詞 anxiety 表示憂慮、不安的感受或狀態，不把一個詞自動當成對任何人的診斷。來源索引句在後半截有截斷，故本課只引述已可核對的短語，不重建缺失文字。所有練習均為原創。 [Cambridge Dictionary](https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/anxiety) 對一般語義的解釋亦把它連於 nervousness/worry 的不舒服感。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文語境中的理由"],"rows":[["worry","有條件的近義","當焦慮圍繞一件可說出的事情，例如結果或健康，尤其自然；也可指「所擔心的事」。"],["unease","有條件的近義","指說不清原因的隱約不安，比強烈恐慌輕；不可把所有嚴重焦慮都縮成微弱不安。"],["apprehension","有條件、較正式","指對將來可能不如意的事感到擔憂；沒有未來事件線索時不宜一概替換。"]],"note":"補充候選覆核： Nervousness 適合臨場緊張；concern 常指理性關切，未必含不舒服的焦慮；fear 常有較明確威脅；panic 程度更強；stress 可指壓力來源或受壓狀態；depression 是原文另列的不同概念。後六項中的緊張感本課另教，其餘放在第 4 節辨明。這四個詞覆蓋此處最有用、且能以線索區分的日常近義說法；不把各種臨床診斷當作同義詞。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子明確提供的線索","可用說法","不可推斷"],"rows":[["擔心一個具體結果或親友情況","worry","必然有診斷"],["不清楚原因的隱約不安","unease","一定發生恐慌"],["對尚未發生之事的不利預期","apprehension","壞事已發生"],["演講、面試、比賽前的臨場緊張","nervousness","長期心理疾病"]],"note":"原文把 anxiety 與 depression 並列而分開。這些詞語是按語境選擇的日常近義說法，不應用來替人作心理健康診斷。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"worry","meaning":"對特定事情的擔憂","note":"名詞可數或不可數；當人為結果、親友或未來事項反覆擔心時，可用 worry about/over。它也可指某一個「擔心的問題」，不像 anxiety 一定着重整體感受。","collocations":"worry about exam results; cause worry; a source of worry","example":"The long wait for the test result caused worry for the whole family.","exampleZh":"漫長的檢查結果等待令全家人擔憂。","contrast":"較明確指向一件擔心的事；若句子只說無由來的不安，unease 更能保留朦朧感。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Waiting for the examination results caused anxiety because the students feared they might not meet the entry requirement.","zh":"等待考試成績令學生焦慮，因為他們擔心自己可能達不到入學要求。","upgrade":"Waiting for the examination results caused worry about whether the students would meet the entry requirement.","answer":"worry about whether they would meet the entry requirement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry about whether they would meet the entry requirement","explanation":"成績未出且學生擔心是否達到入學要求，worry 指向這個具體結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"apprehension before sitting the examination","explanation":"Apprehension 也可涉及未來壞結果，但選項錯置成應考之前；原句已考完在等成績。"},{"letter":"C","text":"nervousness while answering the examination questions","explanation":"Nervousness 在考場答題時可用，原句卻說考後等候結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unease without a named concern","explanation":"不安的原因已明說是入學要求能否達到，並非無從辨明。"},{"letter":"E","text":"stress from revising for the examination","explanation":"溫習壓力可能存在，但時間線已到等放榜，不是溫習階段。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concern about the wording of the entry rules","explanation":"學生怕自己未達標，並非質疑入學規則的文字。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"His anxiety grew when the hospital said his mother's test result would not be ready until next week.","zh":"醫院說他母親的檢查結果下星期才有，他的擔憂因而加深。","upgrade":"His worry about his mother's pending test result grew when the hospital said it would not be ready until next week.","answer":"worry about his mother’s pending test result","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"concern about hospital visiting hours","explanation":"醫院探訪時間或會令人關切，卻不是原句延遲公布的檢查結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"worry about his mother’s pending test result","explanation":"結果要到下星期才有，明確指出他擔心母親的待出結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"apprehension before the test was booked","explanation":"檢查已做完而等結果，選項卻改成預約檢查前的疑懼。"},{"letter":"D","text":"nervousness during his mother’s appointment","explanation":"原句不是母親正在就診時的臨場緊張，而是等待報告。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unease with no identifiable focus","explanation":"焦點非常清楚：母親的檢查結果；不是說不出原因的不安。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stress from arranging transport to the hospital","explanation":"交通安排的壓力與醫院延遲結果這個觸發因素不同。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"unease","meaning":"隱約不安","note":"通常不可數，指說不清為何卻感到不安；可說 a sense of unease 或 unease about something。程度未必很強，不可用來淡化嚴重症狀。","collocations":"a sense of unease; growing unease; unease about the silence","example":"She felt a sense of unease when the normally busy corridor was silent.","exampleZh":"平日繁忙的走廊突然一片寂靜，令她隱約感到不安。","contrast":"比 worry 少了具體擔心的問題，也不像 panic 那樣強烈或突然。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She felt anxiety in the quiet waiting room, although she could not identify what exactly was troubling her.","zh":"她在安靜的候診室感到不安，卻說不出究竟是甚麼令她心緒不寧。","upgrade":"She felt unease in the quiet waiting room, although she could not identify what exactly was troubling her.","answer":"unease without a clearly identified cause","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry about a result the staff had just announced","explanation":"原句未有已宣布的結果；她更說不清困擾自己的具體事情。"},{"letter":"B","text":"unease without a clearly identified cause","explanation":"保留安靜候診室中難以指明原因的不舒服感。"},{"letter":"C","text":"apprehension about a scheduled procedure tomorrow","explanation":"若已知明天有程序，apprehension 很合適；此句沒有該未來事件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"nervousness before speaking to the doctor","explanation":"沒有說她即將與醫生對話，不能將模糊感鎖定為談話前緊張。"},{"letter":"E","text":"concern about the hospital’s visiting policy","explanation":"探訪政策是明確的關注對象，但她並未指出這項政策。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stress caused by filling in a difficult form","explanation":"原句沒有填表任務，且她說不出不安來源。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Anxiety spread through the group when their normally talkative friend answered only briefly, though nobody knew whether anything was wrong.","zh":"平日很健談的朋友突然只簡短回話，雖然沒人知道是否出了甚麼事，團體中仍瀰漫一股不安。","upgrade":"Unease spread through the group when their normally talkative friend answered only briefly, though nobody knew whether anything was wrong.","answer":"unease at the unexplained change in the friend’s replies","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry about a known argument with the friend","explanation":"若已知道發生爭執，worry 可指具體問題；原句沒人知道是否有事。"},{"letter":"B","text":"apprehension about a planned difficult conversation","explanation":"若已約好艱難談話，apprehension 適合，但這裏沒有未來會談安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unease at the unexplained change in the friend’s replies","explanation":"朋友異常簡短回話而原因不明，最切合模糊的不安。"},{"letter":"D","text":"nervousness before asking the friend a question","explanation":"沒說組員正準備發問；情緒來自已觀察到的異常回覆。"},{"letter":"E","text":"concern about a specific message the friend had sent","explanation":"沒有提及任何內容明確的訊息，不宜補出特定關注對象。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stress caused by the group’s school workload","explanation":"學校工作量沒有出現，不是本句的觸發線索。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"apprehension","meaning":"對未來不利事情的疑懼","note":"較正式的名詞，通常指尚未發生的事可能不順利而感到不安；常用 apprehension about/over。此處不是「拘捕」或「理解」的其他詞義。","collocations":"apprehension about the interview; growing apprehension over changes; feel apprehension before a trip","example":"He felt apprehension before the interview because he did not know what questions to expect.","exampleZh":"他不知道面試會問甚麼，因此在面試前感到疑懼。","contrast":"比一般 worry 更突出未來的不確定或壞結果預期；[Cambridge Dictionary](https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/apprehension) 也記錄這個未來憂慮義。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"He felt anxiety before tomorrow's interview because he did not know whether the questions would be difficult.","zh":"明天面試前，他不知道問題會否很難，因此感到焦慮。","upgrade":"He felt apprehension about the coming interview because he did not know whether the questions would be difficult.","answer":"apprehension about the coming interview","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry that the interview had already gone badly","explanation":"面試在明天，尚未發生；不能說已答得不好。"},{"letter":"B","text":"nervousness while answering questions in the interview room","explanation":"面試中答題也可緊張，但原句是面試前預想問題會否難。"},{"letter":"C","text":"concern about the interview venue rather than its questions","explanation":"他擔心提問難度，而非面試地點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"apprehension about the coming interview","explanation":"對明天尚未發生、問題難度未知的面試感到疑懼，正是此詞的重點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unease with no identifiable reason","explanation":"原句有清楚的未來事件，並非原因不明的不安。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stress from arranging transport after the interview","explanation":"交通安排不在句中，也不是他擔心的面試問題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The volunteers expressed anxiety about next month's route change because they feared some participants might get lost.","zh":"義工對下個月的路線更改感到擔憂，因為他們怕部分參加者會迷路。","upgrade":"The volunteers expressed apprehension about the forthcoming route change because they feared some participants might get lost.","answer":"apprehension about the forthcoming route change","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"apprehension about the forthcoming route change","explanation":"路線下月才改，義工預想參加者可能迷路，符合未來疑慮。"},{"letter":"B","text":"worry that participants had already become lost","explanation":"原句只是怕將來有人迷路，沒有說現在已有人迷失。"},{"letter":"C","text":"concern about the cost of printing the new route map","explanation":"印製地圖成本可能值得關切，但義工說的是改路後的迷路風險。"},{"letter":"D","text":"nervousness during an emergency already under way","explanation":"原句沒有現場緊急事故，只是在提前討論下月安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unease without any expected future change","explanation":"下月改路是明確事件，不能稱沒有可預期的變化。"},{"letter":"F","text":"stress from logging last month’s attendance","explanation":"上月點名工作與下月的路線風險無關。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"nervousness","meaning":"臨場緊張","note":"通常不可數，指面對演講、比賽或新場合時的緊張感；可隨事件結束而減退，不應由此推論為焦慮症。","collocations":"nervousness before a speech; hide one's nervousness; nervousness on the first day","example":"A little nervousness before the debate made her rehearse her opening more carefully.","exampleZh":"辯論前略感緊張，令她更仔細地練習開場白。","contrast":"比廣義 anxiety 更明確指向臨場緊張；nervous 是形容詞，不能直接放進名詞位置。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her anxiety before speaking on stage made her hands shake slightly, but she still gave the speech.","zh":"上台演說前的緊張令她雙手微微顫抖，但她仍完成演說。","upgrade":"Her nervousness before speaking on stage made her hands shake slightly, but she still gave the speech.","answer":"nervousness before speaking on stage","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry about the speech’s results after it ended","explanation":"演說尚未開始，並非事後對成績的擔憂。"},{"letter":"B","text":"nervousness before speaking on stage","explanation":"上台前略微手抖、最後仍能演說，精確表示臨場緊張。"},{"letter":"C","text":"apprehension about a different event next month","explanation":"Apprehension 可形容對未來事件疑懼，但選項說的是下月另一件事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unease with no identifiable occasion","explanation":"她的緊張情境已明確是即將上台，不是無由來不安。"},{"letter":"E","text":"stress from preparing the presentation slides","explanation":"準備投影片可能有壓力，卻不是句中臨上台時手抖的線索。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concern about whether the stage was structurally safe","explanation":"沒有舞台安全問題，不能將緊張改成對結構的理性關切。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The new employee's anxiety showed as she introduced herself at her first team meeting, but it faded when her colleagues welcomed her.","zh":"新員工在第一次團隊會議上自我介紹時顯得緊張，但同事歡迎她後，緊張感便漸漸消退。","upgrade":"The new employee's nervousness showed as she introduced herself at her first team meeting, but it faded when her colleagues welcomed her.","answer":"nervousness during her first introduction to the team","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"worry about a later review of the employee's work","explanation":"原句沒有之後的工作評估，情緒發生在首次自我介紹當刻。"},{"letter":"B","text":"apprehension about a future transfer to another team","explanation":"未提將來調職，不能把眼前會議緊張移到另一事件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"nervousness during her first introduction to the team","explanation":"首次向團隊介紹自己時緊張，獲歡迎後消退，符合臨場情緒。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unease that continued after the welcome","explanation":"同事歡迎後情緒已緩和，與持續不安相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"stress from a heavy workload at the meeting","explanation":"工作量並未提及，無法解釋自我介紹時的短暫反應。"},{"letter":"F","text":"concern about the team’s written rules","explanation":"她不是在討論團隊規則，而是在新同事面前介紹自己。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Depression · 原文另列，不可互換","zh":"中文辨析： 原文寫 anxiety or depression，明確把兩者區分。擔憂和不安不是 depression 的英語替換；不能因同屬心理健康話題便合併。若文章具體說情緒低落等另一狀態，才使用相應詞。","point":"The source lists anxiety and depression separately."},{"word":"Stress / pressure · 壓力與焦慮感","zh":"中文辨析： 考試或工作可帶來 pressure/stress；anxiety 指可能出現的憂慮感受。壓力來源可以存在而某人未感焦慮，也可在沒有明確外在壓力時感到不安。","point":"Pressure can contribute to anxiety, but cause and feeling are not identical."},{"word":"Fear / panic · 威脅明確與程度差異","zh":"中文辨析： Fear 常指對具體危險的害怕；panic 是突發、強烈的恐慌。原文只列一般 anxiety，沒有說讀者正在遭遇緊急危險或恐慌發作。若原創題目明說突然無法控制地驚慌，才考慮 panic。","point":"Fear and panic can overlap with anxiety, but neither is a blanket replacement."},{"word":"Concern / caution · 關切不一定是焦慮","zh":"中文辨析： 人可冷靜地 express concern 或小心採取 caution，而沒有不舒服的緊張感。若句子只說理性關注一項政策，不能硬稱心理上的 anxiety。","point":"Concern may be reasoned attention; caution is behaviour, not necessarily anxiety."},{"word":"Anxious / anxiety / nervous · 詞性陷阱","zh":"中文辨析： Anxiety、nervousness 是名詞；anxious、nervous 是形容詞。She felt anxiety 可改成 She felt nervous，但不可說 She felt nervousness 並把所有位置都當成無需改寫。","point":"A related meaning still needs the correct grammatical form."}],"moduleNumber":68},{"id":"lesson-069","sourceId":81,"headword":"apartments","title":"Apartments","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2016 Paper 4 article begins, “Hong Kong apartments are well-known for being tiny – the average is only 450 square feet.” A speaker then describes living in a 400-square-foot apartment; Part B asks about flats in Hong Kong. Here the plural noun names separate homes, not buildings, hotel rooms or an abstract amount of floor space. The figures are historical statements in the passage, not current housing data. [2016 Paper 4, set 1.2](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2016-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceSense":"The 2016 Paper 4 article begins, “Hong Kong apartments are well-known for being tiny – the average is only 450 square feet.” A speaker then describes living in a 400-square-foot apartment; Part B asks about flats in Hong Kong. Here the plural noun names separate homes, not buildings, hotel rooms or an abstract amount of floor space. The figures are historical statements in the passage, not current housing data. [2016 Paper 4, set 1.2](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2016-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf).","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for the source sense"],"rows":[["flats","Close in Hong Kong/British English for self-contained homes in apartment blocks; the paper itself uses flats in Part B."],["residential units","Contextual formal count term. It can also include houses, so a block or development context must retain the apartment sense."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Dwellings adds a useful formal term for places people live, though broader than high-rise flats; taught with its boundary. Homes is natural but centres occupants and may include houses; here it adds little beyond dwellings. Housing units largely duplicates residential units. Condos implies a form of ownership; studios is a smaller layout subtype. Neither is a general synonym. Residences is broad and sometimes means whole buildings or institutions; not selected."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["需要保留的重點","選擇"],"rows":[["香港／英式日常說法，樓內一戶","flat(s)"],["正式說可居住的地方，且上下文已限定樓宇單位","dwelling(s)"],["規劃或建築文件逐個計算住處","residential unit(s)"]],"note":"來源的 apartments 指獨立住處。選用較廣的正式字時，須在句中保留「在住宅大廈內」等限定；不得變成整座大廈、樓層或居住的人。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"flats","meaning":"樓宇住宅單位","note":"英式及香港英語的日常複數名詞，指大廈內獨立居住的單位；最貼近原文的 apartments。","collocations":"small flats; flats in a high-rise; rent a flat.","example":"The family turned one wall of their flat into storage shelves.","exampleZh":"這家人把住宅單位的一面牆改作儲物架。","contrast":"Flat 是一個住戶單位；block of flats 才是整座樓，floor 是樓層。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apartments in this tower each have their own kitchen and entrance, even though the rooms are compact.","zh":"這座大廈的住宅單位雖然房間細小，但每個都有自己的廚房和入口。","upgrade":"The flats in this tower each have their own kitchen and entrance, even though the rooms are compact.","answer":"flats","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"floors","explanation":"每個樓層可有多戶，原句指各個有廚房的住處。"},{"letter":"B","text":"flats","explanation":"大廈內各自有廚房及入口的獨立住處，就是英式英語的 flats。"},{"letter":"C","text":"bedrooms","explanation":"睡房只是單位的一部分，不能承擔各自有廚房的意思。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tenancies","explanation":"租約是法律關係，不是有入口和廚房的實體住處。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hotel suites","explanation":"酒店套房涉及短期住宿；句子說住宅大廈中的住處。"},{"letter":"F","text":"tower blocks","explanation":"整幢高樓不是每個住戶所住的一個單位。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Residents complained that the apartments above the bakery had little room for storing winter clothes.","zh":"居民投訴麵包店樓上的住宅單位幾乎沒有空間存放冬衣。","upgrade":"Residents complained that the flats above the bakery had little room for storing winter clothes.","answer":"flats","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"storage rooms","explanation":"儲物房只是用途特定的房間，不是居民居住的完整單位。"},{"letter":"B","text":"leaseholds","explanation":"Leasehold 指租賃權益，無法自然表示居民所住的實際空間。"},{"letter":"C","text":"flats","explanation":"麵包店樓上供居民居住的獨立單位，香港英語自然稱 flats。"},{"letter":"D","text":"apartment blocks","explanation":"原句可在同一幢樓內有多個單位，並非指整幢住宅樓。"},{"letter":"E","text":"upper storeys","explanation":"樓層是位置；每層可以分成多個住宅單位。"},{"letter":"F","text":"guest rooms","explanation":"客房不一定是長住住宅，亦不能保留居民的單位含義。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"dwellings","meaning":"住處；住宅","note":"正式或統計語域中的可居住單位，尤其從居住功能看一處地方；可包括屋或樓宇單位，因此要保留原句的樓宇限定。","collocations":"compact dwellings; dwellings in the block; count occupied dwellings.","example":"The survey counted 90 occupied dwellings in the older residential block.","exampleZh":"調查點算了舊住宅大廈內九十個有人居住的住宅單位。","contrast":"Dwelling 強調供人居住的場所，範圍比 apartment 廣；household 指住在其中的人。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The apartments in the old block were listed as separate places to live in the housing survey.","zh":"房屋調查把舊大廈的住宅單位逐個列作獨立住處。","upgrade":"The dwellings in the old block were listed as separate places to live in the housing survey.","answer":"dwellings","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"households","explanation":"住戶是居住的人或家庭；調查列的是各個住處本身。"},{"letter":"B","text":"dwellings","explanation":"有舊大廈及獨立居住場所的限定，正式統計可稱 dwellings。"},{"letter":"C","text":"tenancies","explanation":"租住關係不是居住場所；業主自住的單位也可能列入。"},{"letter":"D","text":"buildings","explanation":"一幢舊樓可包含多個單位，不能把單位變成多幢樓。"},{"letter":"E","text":"premises","explanation":"Premises 可指商業處所等，沒有把「可住」的性質說清楚。"},{"letter":"F","text":"floors","explanation":"一層可能有數個單位，不能按樓層取代各個住處。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the fire, inspectors checked whether the apartments on the upper three floors were still safe to live in.","zh":"火警後，檢查員查看上面三層的住宅單位是否仍然適合居住。","upgrade":"After the fire, inspectors checked whether the dwellings on the upper three floors were still safe to live in.","answer":"dwellings","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"residents","explanation":"檢查對象是可否居住的地方，不是居民本身。"},{"letter":"B","text":"dwellings","explanation":"句子明確限定在樓宇上層、以可否居住為焦點，dwellings 合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"lease agreements","explanation":"租約是否有效與單位是否安全可住是兩回事。"},{"letter":"D","text":"residential buildings","explanation":"Residential buildings 指整座住宅樓，不是樓內上層的多個住處。"},{"letter":"E","text":"storeys","explanation":"樓層容納單位，不能直接代指每個受檢住處。"},{"letter":"F","text":"vacancies","explanation":"空置狀態不說明地方是否安全可住，也未見原句說空置。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"residential units","meaning":"住宅單位（規劃用語）","note":"建築、規劃或樓宇統計中計算的個別住宅；保留「每個單位」的數量重點，但單獨使用比 apartments 廣。","collocations":"residential units in a tower; 120 residential units; average floor area per residential unit.","example":"The plan shows 120 residential units in two new towers.","exampleZh":"圖則顯示兩座新大廈共有一百二十個住宅單位。","contrast":"Residential units 是正式分類，可以涵蓋屋；在本課題目中以大廈或樓層限定，避免把它誤作整座樓。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The development plan lists 180 apartments across two residential towers, with each home counted separately.","zh":"發展計劃列出兩座住宅大廈共有一百八十個住宅單位，每個住處均獨立計算。","upgrade":"The development plan lists 180 residential units across two residential towers, with each home counted separately.","answer":"residential units","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"residential units","explanation":"規劃文件逐一計算兩座大廈內的住處，正式稱 residential units。"},{"letter":"B","text":"residential blocks","explanation":"兩座大廈不可能在這句被改說成一百八十座樓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"households","explanation":"一戶可由多人組成；規劃數字是在算單位，不是入住家庭。"},{"letter":"D","text":"tenancies","explanation":"租約數不必等於建成單位數，亦不一定全部出租。"},{"letter":"E","text":"building plots","explanation":"地段是土地，不是兩座大廈內各個住宅。"},{"letter":"F","text":"floor areas","explanation":"樓面面積是量度值，不能取代一百八十個可數的住處。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After the approved conversion of the old office building, the plan shows 24 apartments with kitchens and no commercial space.","zh":"舊辦公樓獲准改建後，圖則顯示有二十四個附設廚房的住宅單位，沒有商業樓面。","upgrade":"After the approved conversion of the old office building, the plan shows 24 residential units with kitchens and no commercial space.","answer":"residential units","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"office suites","explanation":"原來是辦公樓，但改建後圖則列的是附設廚房的住處，不是辦公套間。"},{"letter":"B","text":"commercial units","explanation":"句子明說沒有商業樓面，不能把二十四個住處稱作商業單位。"},{"letter":"C","text":"residential units","explanation":"在改建規劃中逐一計算附設廚房的住處，residential units 正好與原來的商業用途對比。"},{"letter":"D","text":"building plots","explanation":"地段是土地的劃分，不是樓宇內改建出的二十四個住宅。"},{"letter":"E","text":"business premises","explanation":"商業處所與改建後的居住用途相反，且原句排除商業空間。"},{"letter":"F","text":"tenancy agreements","explanation":"租賃合約是法律文件，圖則展示的是建成的住宅單位。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"flat / floor / block","zh":"中文辨析： Flat 指樓內一戶；floor 是層數，block 是整座樓。只有說 a block of flats 時才指一棟樓。","point":"One building can have many floors, and one floor can contain several flats."},{"word":"dwelling / household","zh":"中文辨析： Dwelling 是可住的場所；household 是同住的人。統計兩者可能有不同計算方式，不可因中文都涉及「住戶」就互換。","point":"The place is a dwelling; the people living there form a household."},{"word":"residential unit / room","zh":"中文辨析： 住宅單位通常是可獨立使用的一戶；單個睡房或儲物室只是單位的一部分。","point":"A room is a component of a home, not automatically a complete residential unit."},{"word":"condo / studio / serviced apartment","zh":"中文辨析： Condo 常帶分層業權概念，studio 是開放式小戶型，serviced apartment 帶服務及住宿安排。原文只說公寓單位，沒有這些額外條件。","point":"A subtype or ownership model cannot replace the broad headword without evidence."},{"word":"tenancy / residence","zh":"中文辨析： Tenancy 是租住關係；residence 可以是住所，也可能指整座宿舍或法定居住身分。須核對語法與範圍。","point":"Legal occupancy and an individual self-contained apartment are different things."}],"moduleNumber":69},{"id":"lesson-070","sourceId":73,"headword":"animation","title":"Animation","titleZh":"動畫製作（軟件語境）","subtitle":"動畫製作（軟件語境）","description":"原文： 2023 DSE Speaking 7.2 的暑期實習招聘要求申請人「have good knowledge of graphic design and animation programmes」，工作涉及製作遊戲的即時視覺效果。Animation 在這裏修飾 programmes，指用來製作活動影像的電腦程式類別；這不是在招聘看過很多卡通的人。來源文字的具體職務為視覺效果；以下所有情境句均為原創，沒有冒充試卷原句。","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 DSE Speaking 7.2 的暑期實習招聘要求申請人「have good knowledge of graphic design and animation programmes」，工作涉及製作遊戲的即時視覺效果。Animation 在這裏修飾 programmes，指用來製作活動影像的電腦程式類別；這不是在招聘看過很多卡通的人。來源文字的具體職務為視覺效果；以下所有情境句均為原創，沒有冒充試卷原句。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文語境中的理由"],"rows":[["animated film","錯置產物","是完成的電影，不是應徵者需熟悉的製作程式。"],["cartoon filmmaking","過窄且詞組性質不同","可指製作卡通片的活動，不能概括用於遊戲視覺效果的軟件知識。"],["moving drawings","過窄","某些動畫由圖畫構成，遊戲視效也可用模型、文字或粒子；此詞不能替代程式類別。"],["cartoons","作品類型，不是工具","看卡通不等於懂動畫製作軟件。"]],"note":"補充候選覆核： animation software 是此搭配的最直接改寫；software for creating moving images 向一般讀者說明功能；motion-design tools 只在處理動態視覺設計而非任何動畫工作時成立。Visual-effects software 可包含合成、調色等非動畫工作，不能無限制等同；3D modelling software 可生成靜態模型，不一定處理動作。沒有把 program/programme 美英拼字變體重算成新項。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["原句焦點","較準確的說法","限制"],"rows":[["對一般讀者說明程式用途","software for creating moving images","說的是工具，非成品"],["招聘或訓練中的電腦工具名稱","digital animation software","不等於只會 3D 電影"],["動態文字、圖示、版面效果","motion-design tools","比所有動畫程式窄"]],"note":"原文是 animation programmes 這個軟件搭配。若其他句子單獨說「看一部 animation」，那是作品義，需另作判斷。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"software for creating moving images","meaning":"製作活動影像的軟件","note":"用功能解釋 animation programmes。適合對不熟悉術語的人說明；software 通常不可數，若要數個產品可說 software programs/applications。","collocations":"learn software for creating moving images; use software for creating moving images; experience with software for creating moving images","example":"The intern used software for creating moving images to make a character's walk cycle.","exampleZh":"實習生使用製作活動影像的軟件，製作角色步行循環動作。","contrast":"描述的是工具功能，並非已完成的 animated film；它也不暗示影像一定以手繪卡通製成。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The careers adviser explained that interns needed knowledge of animation programmes for character-motion tasks in games.","zh":"職業顧問解釋，實習生需要懂得動畫製作程式，才能處理遊戲角色動作的工作。","upgrade":"The careers adviser explained that interns needed to know how to use software for creating moving images when animating game characters.","answer":"software for creating moving images","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"software for creating moving images","explanation":"以軟件功能說明應徵者須懂得怎樣製作角色動作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"video-editing software used only to cut recorded character footage","explanation":"剪接已有片段不等於能製作角色的新動作。"},{"letter":"C","text":"graphic-design software used only for still character posters","explanation":"可畫角色但沒有題目要求的活動影像功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a game engine that plays premade movement clips but does not create them","explanation":"播放預製動作與製作角色動作是不同技能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"3D modelling software used only to build still character meshes","explanation":"會建立靜態模型，未必會令角色動起來。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a library of finished character-animation clips","explanation":"成品片段可供使用，但不是應徵者需懂得操作的創作軟件。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For the trial task, candidates opened animation programmes and built a short moving sequence from still shapes.","zh":"在試作任務中，應徵者開啟動畫製作程式，利用靜態形狀製作一段短小的活動影像。","upgrade":"For the trial task, candidates opened software for creating moving images and built a short moving sequence from still shapes.","answer":"software for creating moving images","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"video-editing software limited to trimming completed clips","explanation":"裁剪已有片段，不能按題目要求由靜態形狀製作新動作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"software for creating moving images","explanation":"可開啟並把靜態形狀變成短動態片段，保留原句的工具與功能。"},{"letter":"C","text":"graphic-design software limited to drawing the still shapes","explanation":"能準備素材，但沒有把形狀隨時間移動的功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a compositing tool limited to combining already moving clips","explanation":"合成現成動態片段，沒有從靜態形狀創造題目所說的動作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"3D modelling software limited to building static objects","explanation":"建模可供後續動畫使用，單靠靜態模型並未完成短動態片段。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a game engine set to play only prebuilt animation sequences","explanation":"播放已製成的動作，不等於應徵者自己由形狀製作序列。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"digital animation software","meaning":"數碼動畫軟件","note":"用簡明技術名稱指電腦動畫程式，適合招聘要求或工具清單。Digital 說明電腦化；不等於只會製作 3D 電影。","collocations":"proficiency in digital animation software; digital animation software for games; training in digital animation software","example":"The studio trained new staff in digital animation software before asking them to build game effects.","exampleZh":"工作室先訓練新員工使用數碼動畫軟件，然後才要求他們製作遊戲效果。","contrast":"很接近原文 animation programmes，但詞組整體作名詞；不能把 software 轉寫成 cartoons 這種作品名稱。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The job advert lists animation programmes among the computer tools that interns should be able to use for game visuals.","zh":"招聘廣告把動畫製作程式列為實習生應懂得用來製作遊戲畫面的電腦工具之一。","upgrade":"The job advert lists digital animation software among the computer tools that interns should be able to use for game visuals.","answer":"digital animation software","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a library of completed animation clips for games","explanation":"動作素材庫可供取用，但不表示會操作製作視效的程式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a manual about animation software without hands-on operation","explanation":"懂說明書內容仍與招聘要求的實際使用工具不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"digital animation software","explanation":"直接把招聘中的 programmes 說成可操作的數碼動畫軟件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"video-editing software limited to cutting recorded gameplay","explanation":"只剪接已有遊戲影片，沒有保留招聘所需的動畫創作工具。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a game engine configured only to import premade effects","explanation":"匯入預製特效與操作動畫製作程式不一樣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"graphic-design software limited to static game illustrations","explanation":"可做靜態素材，但廣告另要求動畫工具知識。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before the intern made a moving logo, the studio trained her to use its animation programmes on a computer.","zh":"實習生製作活動標誌前，工作室先訓練她在電腦上使用其動畫程式。","upgrade":"Before the intern made a moving logo, the studio trained her to use its digital animation software on a computer.","answer":"its digital animation software","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"its digital animation software","explanation":"符合「在電腦上使用程式」的技能訓練，亦可用來製作活動標誌。"},{"letter":"B","text":"its sprite editor used only to draw separate still logo frames","explanation":"會畫分開的畫格，未必懂得安排時間讓標誌實際動起來。"},{"letter":"C","text":"its motion-capture tool used only to record actors' gestures","explanation":"人體動作擷取與製作文字標誌的畫面動態不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"its file converter used only to export completed logo animations","explanation":"格式轉換處理完成品，不是訓練她創作新標誌動作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"its game-engine previewer used only to play imported logo motions","explanation":"可預覽匯入效果，但不等於製作原來的動作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"its library of already completed moving logos","explanation":"現成標誌素材庫不是教她操作創作程式。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"motion-design tools","meaning":"動態視覺設計工具","note":"只在工作具體涉及動態文字、圖像或遊戲介面效果時，作較窄的工具類別改寫。Tools 可指多個軟件或軟件功能；不保證涵蓋所有角色動畫。","collocations":"motion-design tools for title sequences; learn motion-design tools; use motion-design tools for interface effects","example":"The designer used motion-design tools to animate the game's menu icons.","exampleZh":"設計師使用動態視覺設計工具，為遊戲選單圖示製作動態效果。","contrast":"焦點是圖像元素的動態設計；若題目說角色骨骼動作或完整動畫電影，須另看工具類型，不能一律用這個較窄名稱。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"For the game's menu, the intern used animation programmes to make icons slide and change colour when selected.","zh":"實習生利用動畫程式，讓遊戲選單圖示在被選取時滑動及變色。","upgrade":"For the game's menu, the intern used motion-design tools to make icons slide and change colour when selected.","answer":"motion-design tools","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"graphic-design software limited to painting still menu icons","explanation":"可畫圖示，但題目要設計被選取時的滑動與變色。"},{"letter":"B","text":"3D-rigging software used for character skeletons, not interface icons","explanation":"角色骨架工具不針對原句的選單圖示動態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"motion-design tools","explanation":"選單圖示的滑動與變色是具體動態視覺設計任務。"},{"letter":"D","text":"video-editing software used only to cut a recording of the menu","explanation":"剪已有畫面與設計玩家選取時的即時圖示動作不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a game-engine viewer that only plays already designed icon motions","explanation":"播放預製效果，未完成實習生在句中製作新動態的工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"visual-effects compositing software used only on the game's trailer","explanation":"處理預告片合成，對象不是互動選單圖示。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The designer opened animation programmes to create a short moving title for the game's loading screen.","zh":"設計師開啟動畫程式，為遊戲載入畫面製作一段短小的活動標題。","upgrade":"The designer opened motion-design tools to create a short moving title for the game's loading screen.","answer":"motion-design tools","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"tools for static 3D title models with no timeline","explanation":"雖能建立立體文字，沒有時間軸便不能製作其動作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"video-editing software used only to trim an exported loading-screen clip","explanation":"修剪已輸出的片段，並非創作載入畫面的活動標題。"},{"letter":"C","text":"compositing software used only to colour-grade an already moving title","explanation":"調整既有動態標題的顏色，沒有製作題目要求的新動作。"},{"letter":"D","text":"motion-design tools","explanation":"活動標題屬動態圖像設計，這個較窄工具名稱有明確語境支持。"},{"letter":"E","text":"game-engine software set only to display imported title animations","explanation":"顯示預製標題，與設計師製作新動態標題不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"graphic-design software used only to create still title cards","explanation":"靜態文字卡沒有載入畫面所需的移動效果。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Animated film / cartoons · 作品不是程式","zh":"中文辨析： 原文要求懂 animation programmes，是懂操作軟件；animated film 和 cartoons 是觀眾看到的作品。若句子談播放一部動畫電影，它們才可能適用。","point":"A finished cartoon is an output, not the software used to make it."},{"word":"Graphic design software · 靜態設計與動畫工具","zh":"中文辨析： 招聘句把 graphic design 與 animation programmes 並列，不能把兩類知識合併；平面設計程式可製作靜態圖，但未必能處理時間軸上的動作。若工作只做海報，平面設計軟件才精確。","point":"The advert names graphic design and animation as separate software-related skills."},{"word":"Visual-effects / 3D-modelling software · 相交而不等同","zh":"中文辨析： 遊戲視效軟件可能用於合成或調色，3D 建模軟件可能只建立靜態模型；兩者都可與動畫製作合作，卻不能單憑名稱判定有製作動作的能力。具體題目若說粒子、時間軸或圖示移動，才選相應工具。","point":"Visual effects and modelling can involve animation, but each covers other tasks too."},{"word":"Moving drawings / cartoon filmmaking · 限制媒介與成品","zh":"中文辨析： Moving drawings 暗示圖畫素材；cartoon filmmaking 暗示卡通影片製作。原句的遊戲即時視效範圍較廣，可包括動態圖示及粒子效果，不應縮窄成畫卡通片。","point":"Game animation tools need not produce hand-drawn cartoons or films."}],"moduleNumber":70},{"id":"lesson-071","sourceId":74,"headword":"anime","title":"Anime","titleZh":"日本動畫","subtitle":"日本動畫","description":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 4.1〈Why Spirited Away Changed Animation Forever〉寫道：“In 2001, one of the most celebrated anime movies hit theatres in Japan.” 這裏的 anime 修飾 movies，指日本動畫電影這類作品；《千與千尋》是當中的例子。單獨的 anime 可作類別名稱，涵蓋電影與電視動畫；改寫原句時必須保留 movies，不能把一部電影改成一套電視劇。以下練習句皆為原創。","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 4.1〈Why Spirited Away Changed Animation Forever〉寫道：“In 2001, one of the most celebrated anime movies hit theatres in Japan.” 這裏的 anime 修飾 movies，指日本動畫電影這類作品；《千與千尋》是當中的例子。單獨的 anime 可作類別名稱，涵蓋電影與電視動畫；改寫原句時必須保留 movies，不能把一部電影改成一套電視劇。以下練習句皆為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["Japanese animation","直接類別改寫","可解釋 anime，但在 anime movies 中須改成 Japanese animated movies/films 才保留電影媒介。"],["animated Japanese film","過窄的單數作品改寫","適合指一部日本動畫電影，不可等同單獨的類別詞 anime。這個詞組在 0075 電影條目討論。"]],"note":"覆核後的範圍： Japanese cartoons 容易暗示兒童向或短篇作品，不宜概括這部長片；manga 是漫畫媒介；Japanese-style animation 可由日本以外製作，不能憑風格推定來源。Animated works from Japan 是在確知來源時有用的類別改寫。單獨的 Japanese animation 和 animated works from Japan 已覆蓋此狹窄原文義；拼字／詞序變體不再湊數。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["語境","用法","邊界"],"rows":[["談日本動畫作為媒介與產業","Japanese animation","類別名詞，通常不可數"],["同時談多部日本來源的電影／電視／網上動畫","animated works from Japan","指作品來源，不只是日式風格"]],"note":"原文是 anime movies；如果要改寫那一句，須寫 Japanese animated films 一類保留電影身分的詞組，這由 0075 條目專門處理。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Japanese animation","meaning":"日本動畫","note":"最簡明地說明 anime 所屬的日本動畫類別；animation 作類別名稱通常不可數。若指一部作品，用 a Japanese animated film/series，不說 an animation 來機械替換。","collocations":"Japanese animation studios; the history of Japanese animation; a Japanese animation festival","example":"The exhibition traced the development of Japanese animation from television series to feature films.","exampleZh":"展覽追溯日本動畫由電視系列發展至長篇電影的歷程。","contrast":"Japanese animation 是類別／媒介；anime movie 指該類別中的電影。若句子計算電影數量，須把類別改為可數的 films。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The lecture placed anime such as Spirited Away within the history of films and television series made in Japan.","zh":"講座把《千與千尋》等日本動畫放在日本製作的電影與電視系列發展史中討論。","upgrade":"The lecture placed Japanese animation such as Spirited Away within the history of films and television series made in Japan.","answer":"Japanese animation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese animation","explanation":"可涵蓋講座所談的日本動畫電影與電視系列，也保留《千與千尋》的作品類別。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese live-action cinema","explanation":"真人拍攝的電影不是題目的動畫類別。"},{"letter":"C","text":"manga published in Japan","explanation":"漫畫是印刷／數碼閱讀的圖像敘事，不能代替放映的動畫。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animation made outside Japan in a Japanese style","explanation":"把作品來源改成日本以外，只保留風格相似。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only Japanese animated television series","explanation":"漏掉題目明說的電影及《千與千尋》。"},{"letter":"F","text":"every film shown in Japanese cinemas","explanation":"在日本戲院上映的真人或外國電影也包括在內，範圍過廣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The streaming service uses anime as a category for feature films, serial shows and short videos produced by Japanese studios.","zh":"串流平台把日本動畫設為一個類別，收錄日本工作室製作的長篇電影、連續劇集和短片。","upgrade":"The streaming service uses Japanese animation as a category for feature films, serial shows and short videos produced by Japanese studios.","answer":"Japanese animation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese animated feature films only","explanation":"目錄還收錄連續劇集和短片，不能只寫長篇電影。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese animation","explanation":"作為串流類別名稱，可同時涵蓋日本工作室的三種動畫格式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese comic books that were never animated","explanation":"未動畫化的漫畫不會作為這批串流影片播放。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animated shows made abroad in a Japanese style","explanation":"只保留仿日風格，與目錄標示的日本工作室來源不符。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Japanese live-action programmes","explanation":"真人節目缺少這個目錄類別必需的動畫特徵。"},{"letter":"F","text":"animation from all countries regardless of origin","explanation":"動畫範圍過廣，不能保留目錄限定的日本來源。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"animated works from Japan","meaning":"來自日本的動畫作品","note":"以複數可數名詞強調作品來源，適合同時談電影、電視系列等多種日本動畫成品。若原句只說一部電影，應改成單數 an animated work from Japan 並保留電影資訊。","collocations":"screen animated works from Japan; compare animated works from Japan; animated works from Japan for different audiences","example":"The festival screened animated works from Japan, including films and television shorts.","exampleZh":"影展放映來自日本的動畫作品，包括電影和電視短片。","contrast":"此說法強調製作來源，不只說有日本風格；也比 anime movies 範圍廣，若題目限定電影，不能無故加入電視作品。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The festival will show anime from several Japanese studios, including two films and three television shorts.","zh":"影展將放映數間日本工作室製作的動畫，包括兩部電影及三部電視短片。","upgrade":"The festival will show animated works from Japan produced by several studios, including two films and three television shorts.","answer":"animated works from Japan","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"live-action works from Japanese studios","explanation":"保留日本來源，但把動畫錯改為真人拍攝。"},{"letter":"B","text":"manga volumes from Japan","explanation":"漫畫卷冊不能在影展以電影和電視短片形式放映。"},{"letter":"C","text":"animated works from Japan","explanation":"保留日本工作室來源，又可涵蓋電影與電視短片兩類作品。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animated films from Japan only","explanation":"漏掉原句明說的三部電視短片。"},{"letter":"E","text":"works in a Japanese style made entirely abroad","explanation":"風格相似卻改了製作來源。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Japanese television shorts only","explanation":"漏掉原句明說的兩部電影。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The awards archive lists anime made in Japan in three formats: a feature film, a television episode and a web short.","zh":"獎項檔案列出在日本製作、分屬三種格式的動畫作品：一部長篇電影、一集電視動畫和一部網上短片。","upgrade":"The awards archive lists animated works from Japan in three formats: a feature film, a television episode and a web short.","answer":"animated works from Japan","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese feature films only, whether animated or live-action","explanation":"檔案另有電視集數和網上短片，亦限定動畫作品。"},{"letter":"B","text":"works made outside Japan in a Japanese style","explanation":"把「在日本製作」改成只是風格相似。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese manga titles with no moving-image version","explanation":"未動畫化的漫畫不是檔案列出的電影、電視集數和網上短片。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animated works from Japan","explanation":"同時保留動畫性質、日本來源及三種可數作品格式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"animated cinema releases from Japan without television or web entries","explanation":"只留下長篇電影，漏掉電視及網上項目。"},{"letter":"F","text":"animated television episodes from Japan without films or web shorts","explanation":"只留下電視一集，漏掉電影和網上短片。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Manga · 漫畫不是動畫","zh":"中文辨析： Manga 一般指日本漫畫，頁面本身不會像動畫那樣連續播放畫面。漫畫可以被改編成 anime；原文談的是在戲院上映的動畫電影，不是漫畫出版。","point":"Manga is a comics medium; anime is animated screen work."},{"word":"Japanese-style animation · 風格不保證來源","zh":"中文辨析： 日本以外也有人製作受日本動畫影響的作品。Japanese-style animation 說風格，animated works from Japan 說來源；原文以日本上映的《千與千尋》為例，不能把來源悄悄換成模仿風格的外國作品。","point":"A work can resemble anime without being made in Japan."},{"word":"Cartoon / Japanese film · 類別過廣或語感偏移","zh":"中文辨析： Cartoon 可泛指動畫，常令讀者想到兒童節目；Japanese film 包含真人電影。若只需說「一部日本電影」，後者成立；若要保留原句的動畫性質，兩者都不夠準確。","point":"Japanese film does not entail animation; cartoon may carry a narrower register."},{"word":"Anime movie versus anime series · 成品媒介要保留","zh":"中文辨析： 單獨 anime 可包含電影和電視系列；原文卻明說 movies 並在戲院上映。改寫整句時不能只寫 series。若句子說每週播出一集，anime series 才恰當。","point":"Anime is a category; a film and a television series are different formats within it."}],"moduleNumber":71},{"id":"lesson-072","sourceId":100,"headword":"arrested","title":"Arrested","titleZh":"被警方拘捕","subtitle":"被警方拘捕","description":"The reproduced 2018 DSE Paper 4 set 6.1 article reports that a 51-year-old man accused of flying a drone in an airport restricted area was arrested upon returning to Hong Kong; it also says he “was picked up at the airport” and was arrested on suspicion of breaking a flight-safety rule. These are reports of police action and allegation, not a charge or conviction. [Reproduced 2018 Paper 4 text](https://www.scribd.com/document/980567264/HKDSE-Paper-4-2018-Examiner). Hong Kong Police guidance distinguishes arrest, detention while investigating, and a possible later charge; it says an arrested person may be released if further detention is not justified. [Hong Kong Police, Guidance to an Arrested Person](https://www.police.gov.hk/info/doc/pol/en/Pol-1128.pdf). All exercises below are original, not additional claims about the airport case.","sourceSense":"The reproduced 2018 DSE Paper 4 set 6.1 article reports that a 51-year-old man accused of flying a drone in an airport restricted area was arrested upon returning to Hong Kong; it also says he “was picked up at the airport” and was arrested on suspicion of breaking a flight-safety rule. These are reports of police action and allegation, not a charge or conviction. [Reproduced 2018 Paper 4 text](https://www.scribd.com/document/980567264/HKDSE-Paper-4-2018-Examiner). Hong Kong Police guidance distinguishes arrest, detention while investigating, and a possible later charge; it says an arrested person may be released if further detention is not justified. [Hong Kong Police, Guidance to an Arrested Person](https://www.police.gov.hk/info/doc/pol/en/Pol-1128.pdf). All exercises below are original, not additional claims about the airport case.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["detained","不可直接替換來源的正式拘捕","指不能自由離開；可能是拘捕後留置，也可能未正式拘捕。單說 detained 會失去原文確定的法律行動。"],["taken into custody","不可單獨直接替換","描述被警方控制的結果；本身不能證明正式拘捕。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： Placed under arrest 是最明確的法律改寫，雖然保留 arrest 字根，不能為追求詞形不同而丟失法律狀態。Apprehended 指警方找到並控制嫌疑人；picked up by police 是來源新聞也使用的口語表述。後兩者都不單獨證明正式拘捕，所以練習的完整改寫會明說隨後正式拘捕。Held by police 與 detained 重疊；charged/convicted 是後續不同階段。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"Placed under arrest 是來源 was arrested 的直接法律改寫。Apprehended 說追查後抓獲，picked up by police 說新聞口語的找到並帶走；後兩者練習均另外明說正式拘捕。來源映射中的 detained 與 taken into custody 可描述拘捕後狀態，卻不能單獨取代已知的正式拘捕。Charged 是可能的後續落案，convicted 是法院定罪；來源只說涉嫌與拘捕。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"placed under arrest","meaning":"被正式拘捕","note":"直接而清楚地指警方採取正式拘捕行動；被動結構與 was arrested 對應。","collocations":"was placed under arrest; placed under arrest on suspicion; formally placed under arrest","example":"After identifying the suspect, officers placed him under arrest at the station.","exampleZh":"警員確認疑犯身分後，在車站正式拘捕他。","contrast":"與 detained 或 taken into custody 相比，明確保留正式拘捕身分；並不暗示已落案或定罪。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Officers identified the wanted man at the arrivals hall and arrested him on suspicion of breaching a flight-safety rule.","zh":"警員在抵港大堂認出被通緝男子，並因懷疑他違反飛行安全規例而拘捕他。","upgrade":"Officers identified the wanted man at the arrivals hall and placed him under arrest on suspicion of breaching a flight-safety rule.","answer":"placed him under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merely stopped him","explanation":"只截停不能表達原句確定的拘捕。"},{"letter":"B","text":"detained him without recording an arrest","explanation":"明說 without recording an arrest，與原文正式拘捕矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","text":"placed him under arrest","explanation":"placed him under arrest 保留正式拘捕，也不擅稱有罪。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charged him in court","explanation":"原句只有涉嫌與拘捕，沒有落案起訴資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"convicted him of the offence","explanation":"拘捕遠未等於法院定罪。"},{"letter":"F","text":"questioned him as a witness","explanation":"他是涉嫌違規者，不是只作證人問話。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After confirming the warrant, officers arrested the suspect at the flat and told her why; no charge had yet been laid.","zh":"警員確認拘捕令後，在單位拘捕疑犯並告知原因；當時尚未落案起訴。","upgrade":"After confirming the warrant, officers placed the suspect under arrest at the flat and told her why; no charge had yet been laid.","answer":"placed her under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"took her into custody without stating a formal arrest","explanation":"受控制不等於明言正式拘捕；原句還有拘捕令及告知原因。"},{"letter":"B","text":"placed her under arrest","explanation":"確認拘捕令並告知原因，placed her under arrest 保留原句程序。"},{"letter":"C","text":"found her guilty","explanation":"沒有法院有罪裁決。"},{"letter":"D","text":"invited her for voluntary questioning","explanation":"自願問話與被執行拘捕令不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"filed a charge against her","explanation":"題句明說尚未落案。"},{"letter":"F","text":"released her without further action","explanation":"並非告知原因後立即放人。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"apprehended","meaning":"被尋獲並抓獲","note":"警方追查後找到及控制嫌疑人時用；可描述正式拘捕過程中的抓獲一環，但若要保留法律身分，須另說 placed under arrest。","collocations":"apprehended after a search; apprehended by officers; apprehended at a checkpoint","example":"Officers apprehended the wanted man at the border and placed him under arrest.","exampleZh":"警員在邊境截獲該名被通緝男子，並正式拘捕他。","contrast":"抓獲側重找到並控制；正式拘捕是另須交代的法律行動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After searching three train platforms, officers arrested the suspect at the final exit before he could leave the station.","zh":"警員搜查三個月台後，在疑犯離開車站前於最後一個出口拘捕他。","upgrade":"After searching three train platforms, officers apprehended the suspect at the final exit and placed him under arrest before he could leave the station.","answer":"apprehended and placed under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"apprehended and placed under arrest","explanation":"搜查後在出口找到並控制疑犯，並明說正式拘捕，兩個事實都保留。"},{"letter":"B","text":"only stopped and released","explanation":"只截停及放走與拘捕相反。"},{"letter":"C","text":"detained without formal arrest","explanation":"without formal arrest 刪掉原句確定的法律行動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"charged and brought to court","explanation":"尚無落案及上庭資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"convicted after trial","explanation":"沒有法庭審訊結果。"},{"letter":"F","text":"questioned as a witness","explanation":"疑犯不是僅以證人身分問話。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The wanted man was arrested at the border checkpoint after officers recognised him from a notice and prevented him from walking away.","zh":"警員根據通告在邊境檢查站認出被通緝男子，阻止他離開並拘捕他。","upgrade":"The wanted man was apprehended and placed under arrest at the border checkpoint after officers recognised him from a notice and prevented him from walking away.","answer":"was apprehended and placed under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was only questioned and allowed to leave","explanation":"警員阻止離開並拘捕，非問話後放行。"},{"letter":"B","text":"was apprehended and placed under arrest","explanation":"在檢查站尋獲、控制並正式拘捕，兩層資訊都保留。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was detained but not arrested","explanation":"but not arrested 與原句相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was charged in court","explanation":"沒有落案資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was convicted of the offence","explanation":"沒有法院定罪資料。"},{"letter":"F","text":"was released after identification","explanation":"認出後沒有放行。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"picked up by police","meaning":"被警方找到並帶走","note":"新聞語體指警方到某處找到並帶走一人；來源文章亦說疑犯在機場 was picked up。正式拘捕須在完整改寫中保留。","collocations":"picked up by police at the airport; picked up by officers after a tip","example":"The suspect was picked up by police near the ferry terminal and placed under arrest.","exampleZh":"疑犯在渡輪碼頭附近被警方找到並帶走，隨後被正式拘捕。","contrast":"若沒有 police 或正式拘捕線索，picked up 也可只是普通接送，不能獨立證明拘捕。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The report says the wanted man was arrested at the airport after officers identified him near the arrivals exit and took him away.","zh":"報道稱警方在入境出口附近認出被通緝男子並把他帶走，隨後拘捕。","upgrade":"The report says the wanted man was picked up by police and placed under arrest at the airport after officers identified him near the arrivals exit and took him away.","answer":"was picked up by police and placed under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was picked up by police and placed under arrest","explanation":"警方找到帶走，並明說正式拘捕；這是來源新聞的 picked up 用法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"was only picked up by a friend","explanation":"朋友接送不涉及警方拘捕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was merely stopped and released","explanation":"mere stop and release 與被帶走及拘捕不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was charged before a court","explanation":"沒有法庭落案資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was convicted after trial","explanation":"沒有審訊及定罪。"},{"letter":"F","text":"was detained without an arrest","explanation":"without an arrest 與原句正式拘捕矛盾。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Acting on a neighbour’s tip, officers found the suspect at a rented flat before dawn. She was arrested there and taken to the station.","zh":"警員依據鄰居提供的線索，天亮前在一個租住單位找到疑犯。她在那裏被拘捕，然後被帶到警署。","upgrade":"Acting on a neighbour’s tip, officers found the suspect at a rented flat before dawn. She was picked up by police and placed under arrest there, then taken to the station.","answer":"was picked up by police and placed under arrest","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was only questioned at home","explanation":"警員把她帶到警署，並非只在家中問話。"},{"letter":"B","text":"was picked up by police and placed under arrest","explanation":"警員按線索找到並帶走她，同時保留正式拘捕狀態。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was detained without a formal arrest","explanation":"without a formal arrest 刪掉原句明確的拘捕。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was charged at trial","explanation":"題句未說落案或審訊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was convicted","explanation":"沒有法院有罪裁定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"was released after a warning","explanation":"她被帶到警署，非警告後釋放。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"accused / suspected · 被指控或懷疑不等於被拘捕","zh":"中文辨析： 一人可被指涉嫌違規但尚未被捕；來源分別說 accused of、arrested on suspicion。不要把指控當成警方已採取的實際拘捕行動。","point":"Allegation and suspicion concern a possible offence; arrest is an action."},{"word":"stopped / questioned · 截停或問話不必然拘捕","zh":"中文辨析： 警方可截停及詢問一人而不正式拘捕。來源先說被截停／查到物件，後另說被拘捕，兩步不可合併成同一狀態。","point":"A stop or interview can precede an arrest."},{"word":"detained / custody without status · 留置與拘捕有重疊但不等同","zh":"中文辨析： 香港警方官方資料說拘捕後可留置調查；但 detained 只說不能自由離開，taken into custody 只說受警方控制。兩者皆可能描述拘捕後情況，單獨改寫來源 was arrested 卻會失去正式拘捕這個已知事實。","point":"Custody and detention describe what happens to a person; arrest names a formal action."},{"word":"charged · 落案起訴是後續程序","zh":"中文辨析： 香港警方指若調查後證據足夠，才可能落案起訴。來源只報道涉嫌與拘捕，沒有證實 charge。","point":"Arrest may be followed by a charge, but does not itself establish one."},{"word":"convicted / found guilty · 定罪須有司法裁定","zh":"中文辨析： 被捕或落案也不等於法院已判有罪。來源沒有審訊結果，不能用 convicted。","point":"A court conviction is a later and different outcome."},{"word":"released / cleared · 獲釋也不是原文拘捕的同義","zh":"中文辨析： 被捕後可能獲釋，不等於之前沒有拘捕；cleared 表嫌疑已排除，也不能由來源自行推斷。","point":"Release and clearance are possible later outcomes, not the arrest event."}],"moduleNumber":72},{"id":"lesson-073","sourceId":40,"headword":"aerial","title":"Aerial","titleZh":"從空中俯瞰的","subtitle":"從空中俯瞰的","description":"2023 年 DSE Speaking 2.3「Graduation ideas」介紹直升機觀光，可讓乘客欣賞維多利亞港的「unbeatable aerial view」。Aerial 在這個名詞片語中修飾 view，指從直升機空中看到的景色；原句還提到地質公園及香港島海灘，但不保證乘客每一刻都垂直俯視。以下指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2023 年 DSE Speaking 2.3「Graduation ideas」介紹直升機觀光，可讓乘客欣賞維多利亞港的「unbeatable aerial view」。Aerial 在這個名詞片語中修飾 view，指從直升機空中看到的景色；原句還提到地質公園及香港島海灘，但不保證乘客每一刻都垂直俯視。以下指南例句及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["from the air","教授為 view from the air","用片語改寫整個 aerial view，清楚保留乘直升機在空中觀看的來源。"],["overhead","本來源不教作直接替換","常暗示觀察點在目標正上方或從上往下；觀光飛行也可能斜向望海港。"],["airborne","假同義","形容飛機、人或微粒在空中，不自然修飾此處的景色方向。"]],"note":"補充 bird's-eye view 表高處看見整體格局；view from above 表從較高位置向下看，可由飛機、無人機或建築物取得，未必限定在空中飛行。Panoramic view 強調視野寬廣，可能由地面山頂取得；high-angle shot 是攝影術語，指鏡頭角度，不是一般旅客的所見。這些候選均在下文辨析，教學詞數以不同視角資訊決定，非固定配額。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","主要資訊","在來源語境的界限"],"rows":[["aerial view","從飛行器空中看到景色","原題是直升機觀光。"],["view from the air","明確說觀看位置在空中","改寫整個名詞片語。"],["bird's-eye view","從高處看整體格局","不限定實際乘飛行器。"],["view from above","從較高處往下看","可來自高樓或無人機，不一定正上方。"],["overhead view","從正上方俯視的暗示較強","原觀光句未保證垂直俯視。"],["airborne","在空中飛行／飄浮","不能自然代替景色視角。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 要保留乘直升機觀看，選 view from the air；要說海港或地區全貌，選 bird's-eye view；要突出從較高位置看清形狀或屋頂細節，選 view from above。勿把「景色」錯寫成「在空中飛的東西」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"View from the Air","meaning":"從空中所見景色","note":"把 aerial view 改寫成完整名詞片語，明確表示觀看位置在飛行器上方空域。","collocations":"a view from the air; see the harbour from the air; a view from the air of the islands.","example":"The helicopter passengers enjoyed a view from the air of the harbour at sunset.","exampleZh":"直升機乘客欣賞到夕陽下從空中所見的海港景色。","contrast":"不要直接把形容詞 aerial 換成介詞片語 from the air 而留下不通順的詞序；須重寫整個名詞片語。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The aerial view during the helicopter flight showed passengers the harbour and the islands beyond it.","zh":"從直升機俯瞰，乘客看到海港及其外的島嶼。","upgrade":"The view from the air during the helicopter flight showed passengers the harbour and the islands beyond it.","answer":"view from the air","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"view from the air","explanation":"直升機乘客在飛行中看海港和島嶼，完整片語自然說明視角來源。"},{"letter":"B","text":"view from a rooftop","explanation":"屋頂也能從高處看海港，但這些乘客是在直升機飛行中觀看。"},{"letter":"C","text":"satellite image","explanation":"他們親眼從飛機窗外看景色，不是在讀太空影像。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airborne view","explanation":"Airborne 形容飛行器在空中，不自然用來表示景色從何處看見。"},{"letter":"E","text":"overhead map","explanation":"句中是乘客現場視野，不是地圖；亦未說直升機正好在港上方。"},{"letter":"F","text":"panorama from a hilltop","explanation":"山頂可提供廣闊景色，卻不是這趟直升機所提供的空中視角。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Back at school, the pupils studied a photograph showing an aerial view; they had taken it over the harbour during their helicopter flight.","zh":"返校後，學生研究一張記錄空中景色的照片；那是他們乘直升機飛越海港時拍的。","upgrade":"Back at school, the pupils studied a photograph showing a view from the air; they had taken it over the harbour during their helicopter flight.","answer":"view from the air","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"view from a high tower","explanation":"高樓也能俯瞰海港，但照片是在直升機飛越海港時拍攝。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airborne photograph","explanation":"照片可在飛行時拍攝，但 airborne 不自然代替所見景色的視角片語。"},{"letter":"C","text":"view from the air","explanation":"照片記錄的是學生在直升機上親眼見過的空中景色。"},{"letter":"D","text":"bird's-eye drawing","explanation":"這是學生在飛行時拍下的照片，不是繪製的俯瞰圖。"},{"letter":"E","text":"drone image","explanation":"照片由乘坐直升機的學生拍攝，並非無人機拍攝。"},{"letter":"F","text":"vertical map","explanation":"學生研究的是實際空中景色照片，不是把地貌抽象化的垂直地圖。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Bird's-Eye View","meaning":"俯瞰全貌","note":"從高處看見地區整體布局或寬闊景色；可從直升機或其他高處取得，不必真的有鳥。","collocations":"a bird's-eye view of the harbour; get a bird's-eye view; a bird's-eye view of the school grounds.","example":"From the helicopter, the class got a bird's-eye view of the harbour, islands and shoreline in one sweep.","exampleZh":"全班從直升機上一眼俯瞰海港、島嶼和海岸線的全貌。","contrast":"此說法突出整體布局；若句子只講飛機窗外一座樓的局部細節，未必需要用「全貌」。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"From the helicopter, the class saw an aerial view that took in Victoria Harbour, the skyline and nearby islands in one sweep.","zh":"全班從直升機上一眼望見維港、天際線及附近島嶼的全貌。","upgrade":"From the helicopter, the class saw a bird's-eye view that took in Victoria Harbour, the skyline and nearby islands in one sweep.","answer":"bird's-eye view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"close-up view","explanation":"一眼包括海港、天際線與島嶼，並非只看局部細節。"},{"letter":"B","text":"panoramic street view","explanation":"雖然景色寬廣，乘客卻在直升機上而非街道觀景。"},{"letter":"C","text":"bird's-eye view","explanation":"從高處同時看見多個地標的整體布局，符合俯瞰全貌。"},{"letter":"D","text":"panorama from a hilltop","explanation":"山頂也可一覽地標，但全班當時在直升機上。"},{"letter":"E","text":"satellite diagram","explanation":"這是人在直升機上現場觀看，不是衛星製作的圖解。"},{"letter":"F","text":"overhead view","explanation":"直升機看到天際線與遠處島嶼，說明這是斜向廣角俯瞰；overhead 容易誤示正上方向下看。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A drone's aerial view helped the school planners see how the classrooms, sports field and bus entrance fit together.","zh":"無人機從空中拍攝，幫學校規劃者看清課室、運動場及巴士入口的相對位置。","upgrade":"A drone's bird's-eye view helped the school planners see how the classrooms, sports field and bus entrance fit together.","answer":"bird's-eye view","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"overhead diagram","explanation":"圖解可標示布局，但句子說無人機提供的實際俯瞰畫面，沒有畫成示意圖。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bird's-eye view","explanation":"無人機從高處顯示各處的相對位置，適合概括學校整體布局。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ground-level route","explanation":"地面路線只顯示走法，不能同時呈現三處的高處布局。"},{"letter":"D","text":"close-up of the sports field","explanation":"單拍球場不能看清它與課室、巴士入口如何相連。"},{"letter":"E","text":"window view","explanation":"普通窗口視角不一定能看見課室、球場與入口的整體關係。"},{"letter":"F","text":"panoramic ground photograph","explanation":"地面照片即使寬廣，也不如無人機俯瞰能顯示課室、球場和入口的相對位置。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"View from Above","meaning":"從上方看見的景色","note":"強調觀察點較高，往下看某地或物；可由直升機、無人機或高樓取得。","collocations":"a view from above; a view of the roof from above; study the coastline from above.","example":"The drone gave the engineers a view from above of the damaged roof.","exampleZh":"無人機讓工程師從上方看到受損屋頂。","contrast":"比 view from the air 寬，因為人在高樓也能向下看；不一定表示剛好在物件正上方。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The drone's live aerial view revealed cracks in the roof that the engineers could not see from the street.","zh":"無人機從上方拍攝，顯示工程師站在街上看不到的屋頂裂縫。","upgrade":"The drone's live view from above revealed cracks in the roof that the engineers could not see from the street.","answer":"view from above","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"view from the street","explanation":"工程師正是站在街上看不到裂縫，視角須在更高處。"},{"letter":"B","text":"distant panorama of the site","explanation":"遠景可能顯示整個工地，卻難以辨認屋頂裂縫細節。"},{"letter":"C","text":"satellite image","explanation":"影像來自無人機，不能推成衛星拍攝。"},{"letter":"D","text":"view from above","explanation":"無人機在屋頂較高處拍攝，讓工程師看見地面視角看不到的裂縫。"},{"letter":"E","text":"archived aerial photograph","explanation":"原句說無人機傳來的即時畫面，不能改成過往已存檔的照片。"},{"letter":"F","text":"roof plan","explanation":"屋頂平面圖可標示設計，卻不是即時拍到的實際裂縫。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The helicopter's aerial view let the visitors trace the curve of the coastline before landing.","zh":"直升機降落前，乘客從上方看清海岸線的彎曲形狀。","upgrade":"The helicopter's view from above let the visitors trace the curve of the coastline before landing.","answer":"view from above","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"view from a hilltop","explanation":"山上也可看海岸，但乘客此時仍在直升機上，來源不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"view from above","explanation":"降落前的空中高處視角讓人辨認海岸線的彎曲走向。"},{"letter":"C","text":"close-up of one bay","explanation":"乘客要追看整段海岸線的彎曲走向，不只看單一海灣近鏡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airborne view","explanation":"Airborne 形容直升機飛行狀態，不能自然指這個觀看方向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"route map","explanation":"他們是親眼看海岸線，不是在看標示飛行路徑的地圖。"},{"letter":"F","text":"overhead view","explanation":"直升機尚在飛行，句子沒有保證它正好從海岸線正上方垂直俯視；from above 不要求嚴格垂直。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Overhead：正上方的暗示","zh":"Overhead view 尤其適合地圖式俯視或直接在目標上方觀察；觀光直升機沿岸飛行時可斜向望維港，不能自動說成正上方視角。English contrast: An overhead plan looks down; a scenic aerial view may be oblique.","point":""},{"word":"Airborne：在空中不等於從空中看到","zh":"Airborne 可形容直升機正在飛，或微粒在空氣中漂浮；an airborne view 在這裏不自然。English contrast: The helicopter is airborne; the passengers see an aerial view.","point":""},{"word":"Panoramic：寬廣與高度","zh":"Panoramic 指視野遼闊，可以在太平山頂取得；它不保證觀看者身在飛行器。English contrast: A hilltop panorama is wide but not necessarily aerial.","point":""},{"word":"Satellite Image：來源不同","zh":"衛星影像由太空攝取，不是直升機乘客親眼看到的現場海港景色。English contrast: A satellite image is recorded remotely; passengers see the harbour from their aircraft.","point":""},{"word":"Aerial Photograph：影像與現場視野","zh":"An aerial photograph 是照片，可記錄空中景色；原題強調直升機乘客當下欣賞的 view，不必然拍照。English contrast: A photograph can capture a view, but the view is not necessarily a photograph.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":73},{"id":"lesson-074","sourceId":67,"headword":"analysts","title":"Analysts","titleZh":"分析科技趨勢的人","subtitle":"分析科技趨勢的人","description":"原文可核對的範圍： 2025 DSE Paper 4，1.3 的文章題為 As PC ownership declines, smartphones are on the rise；在「Not quite, say analysts」中，複數名詞指對個人電腦與智能手機趨勢作出判斷的人。現有摘錄沒有交代他們的僱主、學歷、是否親自蒐集數據或是否預測未來；以下相應詞只在練習補充了角色證據時使用，不冒稱那些事實來自原文。練習句均為原創。[2025 Paper 4 sample](https://www.hkeaa.edu.hk/DocLibrary/HKDSE/Subject_Information/eng_lang/2025-Sample-ENG-Paper4-S633.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文可核對的範圍： 2025 DSE Paper 4，1.3 的文章題為 As PC ownership declines, smartphones are on the rise；在「Not quite, say analysts」中，複數名詞指對個人電腦與智能手機趨勢作出判斷的人。現有摘錄沒有交代他們的僱主、學歷、是否親自蒐集數據或是否預測未來；以下相應詞只在練習補充了角色證據時使用，不冒稱那些事實來自原文。練習句均為原創。[2025 Paper 4 sample](https://www.hkeaa.edu.hk/DocLibrary/HKDSE/Subject_Information/eng_lang/2025-Sample-ENG-Paper4-S633.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["候選","範圍判定","原文界線"],"rows":[["experts","可用但較廣","在相關科技領域有公認知識時；原摘錄未證明資格。"],["commentators","條件可用","公開評論趨勢；不必親自分析或蒐集數據。"],["researchers","條件可用","親自進行系統研究時；不能從 say analysts 推斷。"]],"note":"遺漏挑戰： Forecasters 專指利用現有跡象預測未來；原句只表示反駁或修正，沒有明說預測，故練習明確加入預測。Industry observers 是持續追蹤科技業、描述動向者；比 analyst 弱化分析方法。Market analysts / industry analysts 可作更專門的職銜，但加入 market 或 industry 會假定原文未交代的機構或研究範圍；練習可作搭配，本來源不直接宣稱。Specialists 與 experts 在本課主要意義重疊，無新增獨立考點。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Experts 強調相關專長；researchers 親自進行研究。\n- Commentators 公開提出解讀；forecasters 預測未來；industry observers 持續留意業界。\n- 原文只稱 analysts，所以無證據時應保留這個較準確的角色詞。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"experts","meaning":"相關領域專家","note":"當這些人因持續的專業知識和經驗而有權解說科技趨勢時用；它強調知識，不保證他們正做市場數據分析。","collocations":"technology experts; experts in computing; experts say","example":"Technology experts explained why hospitals still rely on desktop computers.","exampleZh":"科技專家解釋了醫院為何仍依賴桌上型電腦。","contrast":"Analysts 以分析工作命名；experts 以知識或專長命名。單憑 say analysts 不可推斷學歷。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The analysts invited to the hospital were senior computer engineers; they explained why the wards still used desktop machines.","zh":"獲醫院邀請的分析人士是資深電腦工程師；他們解釋病房為何仍使用桌上型電腦。","upgrade":"The experts invited to the hospital were senior computer engineers; they explained why the wards still used desktop machines.","answer":"experts","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"experts","explanation":"他們是資深電腦工程師，experts 突出有根據的專門知識。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reporters","explanation":"reporters 負責採訪報導；句中說的是工程師解釋技術用途。"},{"letter":"C","text":"survey respondents","explanation":"survey respondents 是答問卷的人，並非受邀講解的工程師。"},{"letter":"D","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 預測未來；此處解釋現有病房設備。"},{"letter":"E","text":"critics","explanation":"critics 暗示批評立場，句中只作解說。"},{"letter":"F","text":"data collectors","explanation":"data collectors 蒐集資料，沒有涵蓋工程師的專門解釋。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The analysts on the panel had spent decades designing mobile processors, and their technical advice guided the school purchase.","zh":"小組中的分析人士有數十年設計手機處理器的經驗，他們的技術意見指導了學校採購。","upgrade":"The experts on the panel had spent decades designing mobile processors, and their technical advice guided the school purchase.","answer":"experts","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"industry observers","explanation":"industry observers 可追蹤業界，但未表這些人的數十年設計專長。"},{"letter":"B","text":"commentators","explanation":"commentators 著眼公開評論，不是小組提供的技術建議身份。"},{"letter":"C","text":"research assistants","explanation":"research assistants 協助研究，未能表達資深設計經驗。"},{"letter":"D","text":"experts","explanation":"數十年處理器設計經驗令 experts 最貼合其專門權威。"},{"letter":"E","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 預測走勢，題句是採購技術建議。"},{"letter":"F","text":"customers","explanation":"customers 是買家，不是提供技術建議的人。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"researchers","meaning":"研究人員","note":"有明確證據顯示他們設計調查、蒐集資料或進行系統研究時用；研究人員也可能分析結果，但兩個稱號不同。","collocations":"researchers surveyed households; university researchers; researchers compared device use","example":"Researchers surveyed 2,000 households about the devices used for schoolwork.","exampleZh":"研究人員訪問了二千個家庭，了解他們做功課使用哪些裝置。","contrast":"報導既有數據的 analyst 不一定親自做調查；researchers 需有研究行動支持。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The analysts designed a questionnaire, interviewed 1,800 households and published the method with their findings.","zh":"這些分析人士設計問卷、訪問了一千八百個家庭，並把研究方法與結果一同發表。","upgrade":"The researchers designed a questionnaire, interviewed 1,800 households and published the method with their findings.","answer":"researchers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"commentators","explanation":"commentators 可討論已發表結果，卻不指出親自設計及進行調查。"},{"letter":"B","text":"researchers","explanation":"設計問卷、訪問家庭並公布方法是系統研究，researchers 最準確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 預測未來，題句是調查設計及發表結果。"},{"letter":"D","text":"editors","explanation":"editors 修改或編排文章，非必然執行調查。"},{"letter":"E","text":"industry observers","explanation":"industry observers 可能留意趨勢，但未表親自訪問家庭。"},{"letter":"F","text":"survey respondents","explanation":"survey respondents 是被訪者，而非設計問卷的團隊。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The analysts recruited volunteers, measured how they completed the same task on a phone and a PC, and reported the results.","zh":"這些分析人士招募義工，量度他們分別用手機及個人電腦完成同一任務的表現，然後報告結果。","upgrade":"The researchers recruited volunteers, measured how they completed the same task on a phone and a PC, and reported the results.","answer":"researchers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reporters","explanation":"reporters 可以報道研究，句中人員卻自己招募及量度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"statisticians","explanation":"statisticians 可能處理數據，但句中直接證實的是執行研究而非其專業職銜。"},{"letter":"C","text":"researchers","explanation":"招募受試者、量度表現、報告結果構成研究程序，researchers 最明確。"},{"letter":"D","text":"commentators","explanation":"commentators 主要公開討論，不表示進行比較研究。"},{"letter":"E","text":"customers","explanation":"customers 使用產品，沒有執行此量度設計。"},{"letter":"F","text":"industry observers","explanation":"industry observers 追蹤動態，未指出親自進行受控測試。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"commentators","meaning":"公開評論人士","note":"在報章、電台、影片或公開討論中就科技發展提出解讀或意見時用；不宣稱其做了正式研究。","collocations":"technology commentators; commentators on the phone market; commentators argue","example":"Technology commentators debated whether tablets could replace laptops.","exampleZh":"科技評論人士討論平板電腦能否取代手提電腦。","contrast":"Commentators 指發言方式；analysts 指分析角色。專業研究員也可公開評論，但不能由評論推斷原創研究。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The analysts spent the radio programme debating whether phones would make home PCs less necessary.","zh":"這些分析人士在電台節目中討論手機會否令家用個人電腦變得較不必要。","upgrade":"The commentators spent the radio programme debating whether phones would make home PCs less necessary.","answer":"commentators","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 重在具體未來預測；此處重點是電台公開辯論多方看法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"researchers","explanation":"researchers 暗示系統研究，電台討論本身不能證明。"},{"letter":"C","text":"commentators","explanation":"在電台公開討論趨勢，commentators 最能指其發言角色。"},{"letter":"D","text":"statisticians","explanation":"statisticians 是統計專業，句中沒有方法證據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"survey respondents","explanation":"survey respondents 是被詢問的人，非節目討論者。"},{"letter":"F","text":"computer engineers","explanation":"computer engineers 是職業推斷，節目未交代技術背景。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The analysts wrote weekly newspaper columns interpreting why families increasingly shared one computer but owned several phones.","zh":"這些分析人士每星期在報章專欄解讀為何家庭愈來愈常共用一部電腦，卻擁有多部手機。","upgrade":"The commentators wrote weekly newspaper columns interpreting why families increasingly shared one computer but owned several phones.","answer":"commentators","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"commentators","explanation":"定期寫公開專欄解讀趨勢，commentators 最符合角色。"},{"letter":"B","text":"field researchers","explanation":"field researchers 須親赴現場蒐集研究資料，寫專欄不能證明。"},{"letter":"C","text":"data collectors","explanation":"data collectors 只說蒐集資料，忽略公開解讀。"},{"letter":"D","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 須預測未來，句中解讀的是已有家庭習慣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"retailers","explanation":"retailers 是零售商，寫專欄不構成此身份。"},{"letter":"F","text":"survey respondents","explanation":"survey respondents 是受訪家庭，非寫專欄的人。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"forecasters","meaning":"預測人士","note":"當其主要任務是根據銷售或擁有率資料推算將來走勢，而非只描述目前情況時用。","collocations":"sales forecasters; forecasters expect growth; market forecasters predict","example":"Forecasters predict that second-hand laptop sales will rise next year.","exampleZh":"預測人士估計明年二手手提電腦銷量會上升。","contrast":"Analysts 可以解讀現在或過去；forecasters 必須指向未來。原文的 Not quite 並不自行構成預測。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The analysts used this year’s sales figures to predict how many smartphones households would buy next year.","zh":"這些分析人士根據今年的銷售數據，預測家庭明年會買多少智能手機。","upgrade":"The forecasters used this year’s sales figures to predict how many smartphones households would buy next year.","answer":"forecasters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"commentators","explanation":"commentators 指公開評論，句中核心工作是定量預測。"},{"letter":"B","text":"industry observers","explanation":"industry observers 追蹤動向，未明示會推算明年銷量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"forecasters","explanation":"根據當年數字預測明年購買量，forecasters 最貼切。"},{"letter":"D","text":"reporters","explanation":"reporters 會報導數據，未必推算未來。"},{"letter":"E","text":"statisticians","explanation":"statisticians 是方法專業；預測行為本身更直接支持 forecasters。"},{"letter":"F","text":"retail customers","explanation":"retail customers 購物，並非根據數據作預測的人。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The analysts projected that PC ownership would fall by another five percentage points over the next three years.","zh":"這些分析人士推算未來三年個人電腦擁有率會再下降五個百分點。","upgrade":"The forecasters projected that PC ownership would fall by another five percentage points over the next three years.","answer":"forecasters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"researchers","explanation":"researchers 可能提供資料，但句中給的是明確未來推算而非研究方法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"forecasters","explanation":"推算未來三年的擁有率變化，forecasters 正好指預測者。"},{"letter":"C","text":"critics","explanation":"critics 指批評立場；下降預測不等於批評。"},{"letter":"D","text":"industry observers","explanation":"industry observers 可留意市場，卻未必作明確三年預測。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reporters","explanation":"reporters 可能報導推算，句中是提出推算的人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"technicians","explanation":"technicians 維修或操作技術設備，與擁有率預測不同。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"industry observers","meaning":"持續留意業界動向的人","note":"當這些人定期追蹤電腦及手機業界，從產品與銷售變化作一般觀察時用；比 analysts 弱化正式分析方法。","collocations":"technology industry observers; industry observers noticed; observers of the market","example":"Industry observers noticed that more shops offered phone repair services.","exampleZh":"業界觀察人士注意到愈來愈多店舖提供手機維修服務。","contrast":"Observers 可以只是留意並報告動向；analysts 暗示進一步拆解證據並作判斷。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The analysts who followed local phone shops for years noticed that repair desks had become more common.","zh":"這些分析人士多年來留意本地手機店，發現維修櫃檯變得更普遍。","upgrade":"The industry observers who followed local phone shops for years noticed that repair desks had become more common.","answer":"industry observers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"industry observers","explanation":"多年追蹤商店變化並指出動向，industry observers 合其持續觀察角色。"},{"letter":"B","text":"survey respondents","explanation":"survey respondents 是接受訪問者，非長期追蹤商店的人。"},{"letter":"C","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 說將來，題句注意到已發生的轉變。"},{"letter":"D","text":"retail customers","explanation":"retail customers 可能進店，但未表多年系統留意行業動向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"laboratory researchers","explanation":"laboratory researchers 指實驗室研究，題句是留意實體商店。"},{"letter":"F","text":"critics","explanation":"critics 指批評者，注意到服務增加未含批評。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The analysts regularly visited trade fairs and noticed that fewer exhibitors brought desktop PCs than before.","zh":"這些分析人士定期參觀貿易展覽，發現帶桌上型電腦參展的商家比以前少。","upgrade":"The industry observers regularly visited trade fairs and noticed that fewer exhibitors brought desktop PCs than before.","answer":"industry observers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"forecasters","explanation":"forecasters 預測未來，句中描述展覽上已觀察到的變化。"},{"letter":"B","text":"journalists","explanation":"journalists 可能報導展覽，但題句未說採訪或寫新聞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"industry observers","explanation":"定期看展並留意參展產品變化，industry observers 最貼近。"},{"letter":"D","text":"data collectors","explanation":"data collectors 只說記錄，未突出持續追蹤業界動向。"},{"letter":"E","text":"statisticians","explanation":"statisticians 暗示統計專業，題句沒有統計方法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"computer designers","explanation":"computer designers 設計產品，非必然定期觀察展覽趨勢。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"data collectors / survey respondents · 資料蒐集者與受訪者","zh":"中文辨析： 蒐集問卷或回答問題的人不一定解讀結果；如果句子只說他們記錄回答或受訪，不能概稱 analysts。","point":"Collecting or providing data is not the same act as interpreting it."},{"word":"statisticians · 統計學家","zh":"中文辨析： 統計學家擅長數據方法，可能同時是分析員；原摘錄沒有證據顯示這些人從事統計學工作。","point":"Statisticians identifies a technical profession that the source does not establish."},{"word":"journalists / reporters · 採訪與報導人士","zh":"中文辨析： 記者報導 analysts 的說法，不一定自己提出分析；將兩者混同會改變說話者身份。","point":"A reporter may quote analysts without being one."},{"word":"critics · 批評者","zh":"中文辨析： analysts 說「不盡然」不代表敵意批評或負面評價；critics 會把中性分析轉成反對立場。","point":"Correcting a claim does not automatically mean opposing it as a critic."},{"word":"forecasters / commentators · 預測與公開評論的額外條件","zh":"中文辨析： 兩者皆可能與分析員重疊，但原句未說未來預測或公開媒體職責；練習只有在補上可信的情境證據時才選用。","point":"Use the narrower label only when the sentence supplies its defining activity."}],"moduleNumber":74},{"id":"lesson-075","sourceId":68,"headword":"angrier","title":"Angrier","titleZh":"公仔的怒容比較","subtitle":"公仔的怒容比較","description":"來源界線： 2014 DSE Paper 4，7.2 的材料題目問 Are LEGO Figures Getting Angrier?；這是問題，不能把它寫成考卷已證明的結論。公仔臉上的印刷表情可呈現怒氣，塑膠本身不會感到生氣。與此議題相關的[Bartneck 等人 2013 年原研究](https://bartneck.de/publications/2013/agentsWithFaces/bartneckLEGOAgent.pdf)統計不同年份表情類別，指出笑臉比例下降及怒容類別出現；研究的群體比例與單一公仔表情強度是兩種不同比較。考卷全文未在現有摘錄中逐字核對，以下原創題不冒充引文。","sourceSense":"來源界線： 2014 DSE Paper 4，7.2 的材料題目問 Are LEGO Figures Getting Angrier?；這是問題，不能把它寫成考卷已證明的結論。公仔臉上的印刷表情可呈現怒氣，塑膠本身不會感到生氣。與此議題相關的[Bartneck 等人 2013 年原研究](https://bartneck.de/publications/2013/agentsWithFaces/bartneckLEGOAgent.pdf)統計不同年份表情類別，指出笑臉比例下降及怒容類別出現；研究的群體比例與單一公仔表情強度是兩種不同比較。考卷全文未在現有摘錄中逐字核對，以下原創題不冒充引文。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["more irate","近義，未獨立教","對人自然；描寫塑膠公仔宜說 more irate-looking，但語體正式，與下列 furious/irritated 的強度教點重疊。"],["more furious","條件可用","極強怒意時可說 more furious-looking；不能用在輕微怒容。"],["more upset","假近義","可能是難過、擔心或震驚；不保證臉孔呈怒氣。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： More angry-looking 直接澄清外觀；more irritated-looking 是較輕微的不耐煩；more furious-looking 是更強烈的暴怒表情。Showing a higher proportion of angry faces 则只在比較一批新舊款公仔時保留研究所說的分布趨勢。More scowling 描寫皺眉可能表示思考或厭惡，並非每次都是怒意；more aggressive-looking / more threatening 說攻擊性或威脅感，不能只憑怒容推出；less cheerful 也可能只是平靜。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- More angry-looking 清楚說公仔外觀；more irritated-looking 是輕度惱火；more furious-looking 是極強怒容。\n- Showing a higher proportion of angry faces 說不同系列的表情分布，須有比例證據。\n- More upset、less cheerful、more aggressive 均不足以單獨證明怒氣。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"more angry-looking","meaning":"看起來更生氣","note":"比較印在兩個公仔臉上的怒容強度；加 looking 明確指外觀，不假設公仔真的有情緒。","collocations":"a more angry-looking face; look more angry than before; more angry-looking figures","example":"The newer pirate face is more angry-looking than the old smiling design.","exampleZh":"新款海盜臉孔看起來比舊款微笑設計更生氣。","contrast":"angrier 可省略外觀標記；對玩具用 angry-looking 更準確。它仍要有比較基準。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The new guard figure looks angrier than the old one: its printed eyebrows tilt down and its mouth is set in a firm line.","zh":"新款守衛公仔看起來比舊款更生氣：它印上的眉毛向下傾斜，嘴巴抿成一條緊繃的線。","upgrade":"The new guard figure is more angry-looking than the old one: its printed eyebrows tilt down and its mouth is set in a firm line.","answer":"more angry-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more angry-looking","explanation":"眉毛下壓、嘴巴抿緊呈怒容，angry-looking 指印刷外觀而非真實情緒。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more frightened-looking","explanation":"frightened 偏驚恐，沒有害怕線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more tired-looking","explanation":"tired 需疲態，不由緊閉嘴與怒眉得出。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more cheerful-looking","explanation":"cheerful 與怒眉和緊閉嘴不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more surprised-looking","explanation":"surprised 通常睜大眼或張口，而非眉毛下壓、嘴巴抿緊。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more worried-looking","explanation":"worried 重在憂慮，這裏突出的不是憂慮表情。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The older hero had a broad smile, but the redesigned hero has a deep frown, making the new face angrier.","zh":"舊版英雄露出燦爛笑容，新設計的英雄則深深皺眉，使新臉孔看起來更生氣。","upgrade":"The older hero had a broad smile, but the redesigned hero has a deep frown, making the new face more angry-looking.","answer":"more angry-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more irate in real life","explanation":"in real life 把印刷臉孔錯當有真實情緒的生命。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more angry-looking","explanation":"笑容改為明顯皺眉，new face more angry-looking 清楚比較外觀。"},{"letter":"C","text":"less detailed","explanation":"less detailed 說繪畫細節，皺眉未必較少細節。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more confident-looking","explanation":"confident 指自信，深皺眉不能直接證明。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more frightened-looking","explanation":"frightened 是恐懼，題句呈現的是怒容轉變。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more solemn-looking","explanation":"solemn 可為嚴肅，但沒有保留由笑到生氣的特定情緒。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"more irritated-looking","meaning":"看起來更不耐煩、更惱火","note":"臉部只呈輕度不滿或不耐煩，例如嘴角下垂、微皺眉，而非暴怒時用。","collocations":"a more irritated-looking figure; look slightly more irritated; an irritated-looking face","example":"The new librarian figure looks more irritated than the old one because of its slight frown.","exampleZh":"新款圖書館員公仔微微皺眉，看起來比舊款更惱火。","contrast":"Irritated 比 furious 輕；只是疲倦或難過的表情不可擅自說成 anger。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The new shopkeeper figure has a slight frown instead of a neutral mouth, so it appears angrier than the old version.","zh":"新款店主公仔由中性嘴形變成微微皺眉，因此看起來比舊款更生氣。","upgrade":"The new shopkeeper figure has a slight frown instead of a neutral mouth, so it is more irritated-looking than the old version.","answer":"more irritated-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more furious-looking","explanation":"furious 是暴怒，微皺眉不足以支持。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more upset-looking","explanation":"upset 可是難過或困擾，未準確說出輕度惱火。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more irritated-looking","explanation":"微微皺眉較像輕度不耐煩，irritated-looking 保留輕微怒意。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more frightened-looking","explanation":"frightened 要有恐懼線索。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more aggressive","explanation":"aggressive 指攻擊姿態或行為，非輕度臉部怒意。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more cheerful-looking","explanation":"cheerful 與皺眉不符。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The old robot face looked neutral; the new one has slightly narrowed eyes and faintly pressed lips, so it looks angrier.","zh":"舊款機械人臉孔看起來中性；新款眼睛略微瞇起，嘴唇輕輕抿着，因此看起來更生氣。","upgrade":"The old robot face looked neutral; the new one has slightly narrowed eyes and faintly pressed lips, so it is more irritated-looking.","answer":"more irritated-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more violent","explanation":"violent 指暴力；輕微瞇眼抿嘴不能顯示攻擊行為。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more frightened-looking","explanation":"frightened 說害怕，題句沒有驚恐細節。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more furious-looking","explanation":"furious 是激烈暴怒，略微瞇眼與輕抿嘴唇未達此強度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more irritated-looking","explanation":"相對中性舊臉，輕微瞇眼與抿嘴只顯些許不耐煩，irritated-looking 合適。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more delighted-looking","explanation":"delighted 是高興，與題句輕微瞇眼、抿嘴的不耐煩神情不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more sorrowful-looking","explanation":"sorrowful 是悲傷，沒有眼淚或哀傷線索。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"more furious-looking","meaning":"看起來更暴怒","note":"兩款臉都呈強烈憤怒，新款又有露齒、緊眉等誇張暴怒線索時用；語氣比一般 angrier 強。","collocations":"a more furious-looking villain; look more furious; a furious-looking expression","example":"With clenched teeth and sharply lowered brows, the new villain looks more furious than the earlier one.","exampleZh":"新款反派咬緊牙關、眉毛急劇下壓，看起來比早期款式更暴怒。","contrast":"輕微皺眉只支持 more irritated-looking，不能誇成 furious-looking。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The newer villain bares its teeth and has sharply V-shaped brows; beside the older angry face, it looks angrier.","zh":"新款反派公仔露出牙齒、眉毛呈尖銳的 V 形；與舊款怒容相比，它看起來更生氣。","upgrade":"The newer villain bares its teeth and has sharply V-shaped brows; beside the older angry face, it is more furious-looking.","answer":"more furious-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more disappointed-looking","explanation":"disappointed 偏失望，不解釋露齒的激烈怒容。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more irritated-looking","explanation":"irritated 程度輕，不足以形容比舊怒臉更激烈的咬牙眉形。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more furious-looking","explanation":"兩張本來都生氣，新款露齒兼尖銳怒眉，furious-looking 最能表達暴怒升級。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more frightened-looking","explanation":"frightened 是害怕，露齒與怒眉在此並無受驚背景。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more worried-looking","explanation":"worried 說憂慮，不合誇張怒容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"less cheerful-looking","explanation":"less cheerful 只說笑少，削弱強烈怒氣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The old warrior face was already scowling, but the new printed face has a wide shouting mouth and an intense glare, making it angrier.","zh":"舊款戰士臉孔本已怒視，新款印刷臉孔更有大張的吼叫嘴形與凌厲目光，使它看起來更生氣。","upgrade":"The old warrior face was already scowling, but the new printed face has a wide shouting mouth and an intense glare, making it more furious-looking.","answer":"more furious-looking","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"more serious-looking","explanation":"serious 不一定怒，未保留從怒視到更激烈的變化。"},{"letter":"B","text":"more irritated-looking","explanation":"irritated 較輕，舊款已怒視，新款還大口吼叫，強度更高。"},{"letter":"C","text":"more confused-looking","explanation":"confused 表困惑，與怒視咬牙不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"more surprised-looking","explanation":"surprised 可張口，但舊款已怒視、加上凌厲目光使怒氣解釋更強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"more furious-looking","explanation":"舊款已怒視，新款大口吼叫兼凌厲目光，furious-looking 表暴怒升級。"},{"letter":"F","text":"more upset-looking","explanation":"upset 可指難過，不能精確呈現怒氣。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"showing a higher proportion of angry faces","meaning":"怒容款式所佔比例較高","note":"比較兩批不同年份推出的公仔時用，說的是怒容在全部表情中所佔的比例，而非同一個塑膠臉孔逐漸變怒。","collocations":"a higher proportion of angry faces; more figures with angry faces; the share of angry expressions rose","example":"The later collection showed a higher proportion of angry faces than the earlier one.","exampleZh":"較後期的系列中，怒容所佔的比例高於早期系列。","contrast":"更多公仔有怒容，不等於每個怒容的強度都上升；必須有兩批及比例資料。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The later LEGO collection seemed angrier than the earlier one: 40% of its printed faces were classified as angry, compared with 12% before.","zh":"較後期的 LEGO 系列看起來比早期更生氣：其中百分之四十的印刷臉孔被歸類為怒容，早期則為百分之十二。","upgrade":"The later LEGO collection showed a higher proportion of angry faces than the earlier one: 40% of its printed faces were classified as angry, compared with 12% before.","answer":"showing a higher proportion of angry faces","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"showing a higher proportion of angry faces","explanation":"四成對一成二是群體比例比較，higher proportion of angry faces 精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"making each face more furious","explanation":"百分比變化不證明每張臉都更暴怒。"},{"letter":"C","text":"giving the figures real anger","explanation":"塑膠公仔不會有真實怒氣，數據只分類印刷表情。"},{"letter":"D","text":"showing fewer kinds of faces","explanation":"資料是怒容比例，未說表情種類變少。"},{"letter":"E","text":"making every face scowl","explanation":"四成不是全部，每張臉都怒視與數據矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"showing a higher proportion of sad faces","explanation":"分類是 angry 而不是 sad，不可換成悲傷比例。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Across the two catalogues, the figures became angrier in the aggregate: angry faces made up one in ten earlier designs but nearly one in three newer designs.","zh":"比較兩份產品目錄，公仔整體上看起來更生氣：怒容在早期設計中佔十分之一，新設計中則接近三分之一。","upgrade":"Across the two catalogues, the newer figures showed a higher proportion of angry faces: one in ten earlier designs were angry, compared with nearly one in three newer designs.","answer":"showing a higher proportion of angry faces","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"becoming more violent in play","explanation":"violent in play 涉及玩耍時的行為，目錄只統計面部表情。"},{"letter":"B","text":"showing a higher proportion of angry faces","explanation":"十分之一升至近三分之一，正是怒容款式比例增加。"},{"letter":"C","text":"appearing more upset overall","explanation":"upset 不特指生氣，不能取代已明確分類的 angry。"},{"letter":"D","text":"making individual brows darker","explanation":"沒有逐個量眉色，比例數字不能推出眉毛更深。"},{"letter":"E","text":"showing fewer smiling mouths in every face","explanation":"題句列的是怒容比例，未證明每張臉的笑容都減少。"},{"letter":"F","text":"giving every new figure a furious face","explanation":"近三分之一不是每個新公仔都有暴怒臉。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"more upset · 難過或困擾未必是生氣","zh":"中文辨析： 嘴角下垂或哭泣可能是傷心；如果沒有怒眉、咬牙等證據，upset 不能忠實改寫怒容。","point":"Upset is broader than anger."},{"word":"more aggressive / more violent · 攻擊行為不是臉部怒容","zh":"中文辨析： 刀劍、武器或打鬥動作可令人感到具攻擊性，卻不是臉上真的印有較怒的表情。","point":"A threatening pose does not establish an angry facial expression."},{"word":"less cheerful / more serious · 少笑不等於怒","zh":"中文辨析： 中性、嚴肅的臉也少笑，不能因笑容減少便逐個斷定更生氣。","point":"A neutral face can be less cheerful without being angry."},{"word":"single face intensity / group proportion · 兩種比較不能混為一談","zh":"中文辨析： 一張新臉畫得更怒，是強度比較；新系列有更高比例的怒臉，是分布比較。兩者都能使新聞標題說 angrier，但證據不同。","point":"A greater share of angry faces does not imply that each angry face is more intense."},{"word":"feel angrier · 玩具並無真實情緒","zh":"中文辨析： 除非明說是在虛構故事中把公仔當角色，描述印刷臉孔應用 look、appear、show，而非斷言塑膠感到怒氣。","point":"Printed expressions depict feelings; plastic toys do not experience them."}],"moduleNumber":75},{"id":"lesson-076","sourceId":47,"headword":"age discrimination","title":"Age discrimination","titleZh":"年齡歧視","subtitle":"年齡歧視","description":"The 2017 letter is headed “It is important to fight age discrimination.” It discusses older people losing work or opportunities because of age, and the discussion questions also ask whether young people suffer it. Here the phrase concerns age-based unequal treatment. The writer advocates action; the article does not establish a legal ruling against a named employer.","sourceSense":"The 2017 letter is headed “It is important to fight age discrimination.” It discusses older people losing work or opportunities because of age, and the discussion questions also ask whether young people suffer it. Here the phrase concerns age-based unequal treatment. The writer advocates action; the article does not establish a legal ruling against a named employer.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["age-based prejudice","Near miss: a biased belief about an age group can precede an unfair decision, but a private assumption alone is not the same as unequal treatment. Retained as a contrast, not taught as a direct synonym."],["ageism","Broad social term covering age stereotypes, prejudice and discriminatory conduct; usable for a pattern of the treatment described, with its wider scope made explicit."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Age-based discrimination is the closest transparent equivalent. Unfair treatment because of age is a plain-language causal paraphrase useful when a specific action is known. Ageism adds the wider pattern. Discrimination on the grounds of age is a formal variant of age-based discrimination and largely duplicates it. Age bias can name a tendency or attitude without proving treatment; generational conflict is a disagreement between generations, not necessarily discrimination. The lesson does not suggest every age-based distinction is automatically unlawful."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["ageism","描述跨個案的年齡成見、態度和不公平做法。","廣義標籤本身不證明某個人遭遇哪次具體決定。"],["age-based discrimination","有因歲數而作出的較差待遇或拒絕。","只有心裏成見或純粹歲數不同仍不足夠。"],["unfair treatment because of age","要平實講明待遇較差與其年齡原因。","不能省略 because of age，否則可指其他不公原因。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 先找清楚年齡是否導致不公平待遇。已有拒聘、拒訓或差別派工，可用 age-based discrimination 或具體地說 unfair treatment because of age；若討論針對年輕與年長人士的成見及制度性做法，ageism 較能概括整體。單有偏見、歲數差異或代際分歧，不能自動說已有歧視行為。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"ageism","meaning":"年齡主義／年齡偏見與歧視","note":"涵蓋對年輕或年長人士的年齡成見、偏見及歧視做法；特別適合談制度或社會上的廣泛模式。","collocations":"fight ageism; ageism in hiring; challenge ageism against young and older workers.","example":"The campaign challenged ageism in hiring by comparing applicants' skills rather than their birthdays.","exampleZh":"該運動以求職者的能力而非出生日期作比較，藉此對抗招聘中的年齡偏見與歧視。","contrast":"Ageism 可比一次歧視行為更廣；要報告具體事件，仍應說明誰因年齡受到甚麼不公平對待。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The review called the firm's repeated jokes about older staff, refusal to train them, and age-targeted hiring age discrimination across the whole workplace.","zh":"調查把公司反覆取笑年長員工、不讓他們受訓及針對年齡招聘的做法，稱為遍及整個工作場所的年齡歧視。","upgrade":"The review called the firm's repeated jokes about older staff, refusal to train them, and age-targeted hiring ageism across the whole workplace.","answer":"ageism","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age-based prejudice alone","explanation":"不止有成見和笑話，還有拒絕培訓及針對年齡的招聘行為；alone 把範圍收窄了。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a single age limit","explanation":"句子列出多種反覆做法，不是一條單一歲數界線。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ageism","explanation":"Ageism 可概括遍及公司的年齡成見及實際不公平做法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a generation gap","explanation":"問題不是兩代意見不同，而是年長員工受訓和求職機會受限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unequal seniority pay","explanation":"原句沒有提按年資計薪，而是笑話、培訓和招聘。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ordinary skills assessment","explanation":"公司按年齡對待員工，沒有描述逐一評核能力。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The campaign described the firm's age discrimination as part of a wider culture: managers denied older staff training and also called younger staff careless, although no young employee had yet been refused a role.","zh":"宣傳活動把公司的年齡歧視視為更廣泛文化的一部分：經理不讓年長員工受訓，也說年輕員工粗心，雖然尚未有年輕員工因此被拒絕職位。","upgrade":"The campaign described the firm's ageism as part of a wider culture: managers denied older staff training and also called younger staff careless, although no young employee had yet been refused a role.","answer":"ageism","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a seniority scale","explanation":"按任職年資排列薪級不能概括對年輕及年長員工的兩種成見。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a retirement age rule","explanation":"活動討論兩端年齡的刻板印象，沒有提出退休歲數條例。"},{"letter":"C","text":"one rejected application","explanation":"年長員工被拒受訓，年輕員工被貼標籤；沒有說有一宗被拒的求職申請。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ageism","explanation":"Ageism 可同時概括拒絕年長者受訓的行動及針對年輕人的成見。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an age difference","explanation":"歲數不同不能概括拒絕培訓或說年輕人一概粗心的做法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"generational cooperation","explanation":"活動反對刻板印象，並非把這些成見稱為合作。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"age-based discrimination","meaning":"基於年齡的歧視","note":"因一個人的歲數而給予較差機會或待遇；在本課例句中須見到具體決定，不能只有心裏成見。","collocations":"age-based discrimination in recruitment; report age-based discrimination; prevent age-based discrimination.","example":"Rejecting the qualified applicant solely because she was 62 was age-based discrimination.","exampleZh":"只因那名合資格求職者六十二歲便拒絕她，是基於年齡的歧視。","contrast":"Age-based 指原因是年齡；如果決定有與年齡無關的實際資格理由，不能只因結果涉及年長者便推定歧視。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After confirming that the two candidates had the same qualifications, the employer refused the 62-year-old an interview solely because of her age; the complaint called this age discrimination.","zh":"僱主確認兩名求職者資格相同後，只因其中一人六十二歲便拒絕面試她；投訴把這稱為年齡歧視。","upgrade":"After confirming that the two candidates had the same qualifications, the employer refused the 62-year-old an interview solely because of her age; the complaint called this age-based discrimination.","answer":"age-based discrimination","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age-based prejudice without action","explanation":"已有拒絕面試的實際決定，不能說只有心裏偏見而無行動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a fair qualification check","explanation":"兩人資格相同，拒絕理由明說只是六十二歲，不是技能差異。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a neutral retirement plan","explanation":"這是求職面試決定，不是中立的退休計劃。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a generation gap","explanation":"僱主不是描述兩代看法不同，而是拒絕給一人面試機會。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age-based discrimination","explanation":"Age-based discrimination 精確表示因年齡而作出的不公平拒絕面試決定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a voluntary withdrawal","explanation":"求職者沒有自行退出；是僱主拒絕她。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club let older members enter the open photography contest but turned away a qualified 19-year-old solely for being young, despite having published no age rule; its committee investigated the age discrimination.","zh":"攝影會准許年長會員參加公開比賽，卻只因一名合資格參賽者十九歲便拒絕他，事前亦未公布年齡規則；委員會調查這宗年齡歧視。","upgrade":"The club let older members enter the open photography contest but turned away a qualified 19-year-old solely for being young, despite having published no age rule; its committee investigated the age-based discrimination.","answer":"age-based discrimination","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age-based discrimination","explanation":"十九歲合資格參賽者只因年輕而被拒，已有具體的不公平待遇。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a published age requirement","explanation":"題目明說事前沒有公布年齡規則；這是後來的拒絕行為。"},{"letter":"C","text":"lack of photographic skill","explanation":"參賽者明說合資格，拒絕原因是年輕而非攝影能力。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a private stereotype alone","explanation":"攝影會已把他拒之門外，並非只有尚未付諸行動的想法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a seniority ranking","explanation":"比賽參賽資格不是按會員任職年資排序。"},{"letter":"F","text":"an equal entry policy","explanation":"年長會員可參賽而合資格的年輕會員被拒，不是平等入場。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"unfair treatment because of age","meaning":"因年齡而受到不公平對待","note":"用日常語言把兩件事都講清楚：待遇較差，以及真正原因是年齡。適合改寫具體事件。","collocations":"face unfair treatment because of age; describe unfair treatment because of age.","example":"The older trainees faced unfair treatment because of age when the manager denied them the same course offered to younger colleagues.","exampleZh":"經理不讓年長實習員上年輕同事可上的同一課程，使他們因年齡而受到不公平對待。","contrast":"Unfair treatment 單獨可由其他原因造成；要與來源相符，because of age 不能省略。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The training centre described the age discrimination in plain terms: it gave the same course to younger staff but denied it to older staff because they were over 60, regardless of their ability.","zh":"培訓中心直白地描述這種年齡歧視：它給年輕員工上同一課程，卻只因其他員工超過六十歲便不讓他們上，完全不考慮能力。","upgrade":"The training centre described the unfair treatment because of age in plain terms: it gave the same course to younger staff but denied it to older staff because they were over 60, regardless of their ability.","answer":"unfair treatment because of age","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different ages in one course","explanation":"年長員工被拒，並未和年輕員工一起上課。"},{"letter":"B","text":"unfair treatment because of age","explanation":"年長者因超過六十歲而失去同一培訓機會，兩部分意思都保留。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a justified skills test","explanation":"中心不考慮能力，只按年齡決定，沒有公平技能測試。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unequal treatment because of seniority","explanation":"差別依據是六十歲以上，不是任職年資。"},{"letter":"E","text":"prejudice without a decision","explanation":"中心已拒絕培訓，不只是心裏成見。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a published course timetable","explanation":"原句談誰可參加，不是課程何時舉行。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In her appeal, the young volunteer described it as age discrimination when a charity assigned her only clerical work because she was 18, although she had passed the same fieldwork training as older volunteers.","zh":"年輕義工在申訴中把此事稱為年齡歧視：慈善機構只因她十八歲便只派文書工作給她，儘管她通過了和年長義工相同的實地工作培訓。","upgrade":"In her appeal, the young volunteer described it as unfair treatment because of age when a charity assigned her only clerical work because she was 18, although she had passed the same fieldwork training as older volunteers.","answer":"unfair treatment because of age","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fair task rotation","explanation":"義工因十八歲而只獲派文書工作，並非大家公平輪換任務。"},{"letter":"B","text":"lack of fieldwork training","explanation":"她已通過和年長義工一樣的實地工作培訓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a harmless age difference","explanation":"歲數差異已帶來較差工作安排，不只是無影響的不同年齡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a private belief with no action","explanation":"機構已作出只派文書工作的決定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"unequal treatment because of rank","explanation":"題目明說原因是十八歲，沒有職級差異的資料。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unfair treatment because of age","explanation":"Unfair treatment 點出任務不平等，because of age 保留真正原因是十八歲。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"prejudice / discriminatory action","zh":"中文辨析： 心裏假定年長者學不會軟件，是偏見；因此拒絕合資格者受訓，才有具體歧視行為。","point":"A stereotype may exist before any decision is made."},{"word":"ageism / one incident","zh":"中文辨析： Ageism 可以概括制度、態度和做法；若題目只描述一次拒聘，須能指出該次行為，不能憑廣義標籤虛構整個制度。","point":"A broad label does not specify which decision was unfair."},{"word":"different age / age discrimination","zh":"中文辨析： 兩名僱員年齡不同本身不是歧視；須有因年齡而來的不公平待遇。","point":"A difference in age is not an unfair decision."},{"word":"legal age rule / unfair exclusion","zh":"中文辨析： 有年齡界線不自動等於歧視；要看規則的目的、適用背景及實際效果。本課不作法律裁決。","point":"The word discrimination requires more than the presence of a number."},{"word":"generation gap / discrimination","zh":"中文辨析： 年輕與年長人士意見不合是代際分歧；若沒有因此剝奪機會，就不能當作年齡歧視。","point":"Disagreement alone is not unequal access to work."}],"moduleNumber":76},{"id":"lesson-077","sourceId":48,"headword":"age limit","title":"Age limit","titleZh":"年齡限制","subtitle":"年齡限制","description":"The 2019 set asks, “Should there be an age limit for political leaders?” The surrounding discussion weighs strengths and limitations of older leaders and whether age should affect selection. An upper limit is a plausible proposal in that setting; the question alone does not choose a number, establish a rule, or prove that a maximum rather than a minimum has been adopted.","sourceSense":"The 2019 set asks, “Should there be an age limit for political leaders?” The surrounding discussion weighs strengths and limitations of older leaders and whether age should affect selection. An upper limit is a plausible proposal in that setting; the question alone does not choose a number, establish a rule, or prove that a maximum rather than a minimum has been adopted.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["age cap","Good only for an upper age limit: a cap is a maximum, not a minimum. The source's older-leader topic makes it relevant, but the bare title does not settle the direction."],["maximum permitted age","Transparent upper-bound paraphrase where a definite ceiling is stated or proposed; too specific if age limit means a minimum."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Age restriction is the broad natural alternative, preserving an unspecified age-based rule. Age cap is concise and maximum permitted age explicit when a ceiling is stated. Upper age limit is also valid but largely duplicates age cap and is not separately drilled. Age requirement can be a minimum, maximum, or exact criterion, so it is broader than a specified cap. Retirement age is when someone leaves work, not necessarily the maximum age for becoming a leader. Age bracket is a category of people, not an eligibility boundary."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["age restriction","原句問應否有年齡資格限制，尚未指定最高或最低。","不憑一般限制推定已有某個數值或現行規則。"],["age cap","說明最高可申請歲數，尤其討論建議、提高或撤銷上限。","不能用於「至少十八歲」等最低門檻。"],["maximum permitted age","需要正式說出一條規則容許的最高年齡。","不等於平均年齡、退休歲數或建議偏好。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 原題只問應否有 age limit 時，用較廣的 age restriction；當句子明說超過某歲數不得申請，才可說 age cap；表格或規則需填明可接受的最高歲數，用 maximum permitted age。Proposed 與 enacted 不能互換，下限也不能寫成上限。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"age restriction","meaning":"年齡限制","note":"泛指按年齡限制資格，可指最低或最高歲數；在原題尚未指定方向時最穩妥。","collocations":"impose an age restriction; question an age restriction; age restriction for candidates.","example":"The debate asked whether an age restriction should apply to committee candidates, without suggesting a number.","exampleZh":"辯論問委員會候選人應否受年齡限制，卻沒有提出歲數。","contrast":"Restriction 表有資格門檻，不表示已確定為最高歲數，也不等於年齡歧視的法律結論。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The panel asked whether any age limit should apply to candidates, without deciding whether a future rule would set a minimum or a maximum.","zh":"小組問候選人應否受到任何年齡限制，卻未決定將來的規則會定最低還是最高歲數。","upgrade":"The panel asked whether any age restriction should apply to candidates, without deciding whether a future rule would set a minimum or a maximum.","answer":"age restriction","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"retirement age","explanation":"小組談候選人資格，沒有討論任職者何時退休。"},{"letter":"B","text":"age recommendation","explanation":"題目問是否應有實際限制，不只是給一項沒有約束力的建議。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age restriction","explanation":"Age restriction 可泛指最低或最高年齡限制，符合尚未決定方向的討論。"},{"letter":"D","text":"upper age cap","explanation":"小組尚未決定是最低或最高界線，upper 過早指定上限。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age bracket","explanation":"年齡組別可用於分類，不一定限制任何人參選。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age prejudice","explanation":"問句在討論應否制定規則，不是斷言小組已有年齡偏見。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The proposed age limit would require candidates to be at least 18; it sets no upper boundary, and the council has not voted on it yet.","zh":"建議的年齡限制要求候選人至少十八歲，沒有設定最高年齡；議會尚未表決。","upgrade":"The proposed age restriction would require candidates to be at least 18; it sets no upper boundary, and the council has not voted on it yet.","answer":"age restriction","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age cap","explanation":"十八歲是下限，cap 卻指最高歲數。"},{"letter":"B","text":"retirement age","explanation":"候選人至少十八歲不是退休規定。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age range","explanation":"句子只給最低資格門檻，沒有給上下兩端的年齡跨度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enacted age rule","explanation":"議會尚未表決，不能說已頒布。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age restriction","explanation":"這個較廣的片語可指最低歲數限制，也保留只是建議的狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age-based prejudice","explanation":"這裏有具體建議門檻；單說偏見既不表規則，也不能由門檻本身斷定偏見。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"age cap","meaning":"年齡上限","note":"簡潔說最高允許歲數，常用於討論是否設上限或調整數值。","collocations":"propose an age cap; lift the age cap; age cap of 75.","example":"The club lifted its age cap from 65 to 70, allowing more older candidates to apply.","exampleZh":"該會把年齡上限由六十五歲提高至七十歲，容許更多年長候選人申請。","contrast":"Cap 是最高點，不能用來表示只准十八歲以上參加的下限。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If adopted, the proposed age limit of 70 would stop a 71-year-old from applying while allowing a 69-year-old to apply.","zh":"如獲通過，建議的七十歲年齡上限會令七十一歲的人不能申請，但容許六十九歲的人申請。","upgrade":"If adopted, the proposed age cap of 70 would stop a 71-year-old from applying while allowing a 69-year-old to apply.","answer":"age cap","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"age cap","explanation":"七十歲是容許申請的最高界線，cap 保留上限方向及具體數值。"},{"letter":"B","text":"minimum age","explanation":"六十九歲可申請、七十一歲不可申請，方向是上限不是下限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age bracket","explanation":"此數字用來排除超齡者，不是只把人分類的年齡組別。"},{"letter":"D","text":"retirement age","explanation":"句子談能否提出申請，不是當選後何時退職。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age preference","explanation":"規則若通過會直接禁止七十一歲者，不只是偏好年輕候選人。"},{"letter":"F","text":"current age rule","explanation":"If adopted 表示尚未生效，不可稱為現行規則。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The association lifted its age limit from 65 to 72, so a 68-year-old who was previously too old may now stand for chair.","zh":"協會把年齡上限由六十五歲提高至七十二歲，因此原本超齡的六十八歲人士現在可以競選主席。","upgrade":"The association lifted its age cap from 65 to 72, so a 68-year-old who was previously too old may now stand for chair.","answer":"age cap","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"lower age threshold","explanation":"提高最高歲數讓原本太年長的人可參選，並非改動最低年齡。"},{"letter":"B","text":"preferred age range","explanation":"原本六十八歲不能參選，是硬性資格而非協會的偏好區間。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age average","explanation":"六十五及七十二歲是規則界線，不是候選人平均歲數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"age cap","explanation":"Lifted its age cap 自然表示把最高允許歲數由六十五提高至七十二。"},{"letter":"E","text":"retirement date","explanation":"這是主席參選資格，不是某人離職日期。"},{"letter":"F","text":"birth-year cohort","explanation":"協會改最高歲數，沒有按出生年份重劃世代。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"maximum permitted age","meaning":"最高准許年齡","note":"正式、明確地說規則容許的最高歲數；要有已頒布或明確假設的規則。","collocations":"maximum permitted age for entry; state the maximum permitted age; raise the maximum permitted age.","example":"Under the proposed rule, the maximum permitted age for a new chair would be 72.","exampleZh":"根據建議規則，新任主席的最高准許年齡是七十二歲。","contrast":"Maximum 說明上界；若尚無具體規則，不能把開放問題寫成已有定案。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Under the enacted club rules, the age limit for a new chair is 72: a person aged 73 cannot register, but someone aged 72 can.","zh":"根據已生效的會章，新任主席的最高准許年齡為七十二歲：七十三歲不能登記，七十二歲則可以。","upgrade":"Under the enacted club rules, the maximum permitted age for a new chair is 72: a person aged 73 cannot register, but someone aged 72 can.","answer":"maximum permitted age","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"youngest eligible age","explanation":"七十二歲是最高准許歲數，不是最年輕可參選歲數。"},{"letter":"B","text":"suggested retirement age","explanation":"已生效規則限制新主席登記，並非建議何時退休。"},{"letter":"C","text":"average applicant age","explanation":"規則給資格上限，沒有計算申請人平均歲數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"preferred age bracket","explanation":"七十三歲不能登記，屬硬性上限，不只是偏好某年齡組。"},{"letter":"E","text":"proposed age factor","explanation":"會章已生效，且超齡者不得登記，不只是建議考慮年齡。"},{"letter":"F","text":"maximum permitted age","explanation":"Maximum permitted age 精確說明七十二歲仍可登記、七十三歲不可的現行最高界線。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The application form asks staff to enter the age limit in the new rules; because applicants must be 70 or younger, staff write “70” in that box.","zh":"申請表要求職員填入新規則准許的最高年齡；由於申請人須為七十歲或以下，職員在該欄填上「70」。","upgrade":"The application form asks staff to enter the maximum permitted age in the new rules; because applicants must be 70 or younger, staff write “70” in that box.","answer":"maximum permitted age","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"minimum applicant age","explanation":"70 or younger 指最高界線，不是至少七十歲。"},{"letter":"B","text":"maximum permitted age","explanation":"表格要填准許的最高數值；七十歲以下及七十歲本身均可申請。"},{"letter":"C","text":"average age of applicants","explanation":"表格填的是規則中的「70」，不需要先統計申請人平均歲數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"preferred age range","explanation":"表格只填一個最高數字，不是沒有強制力的偏好跨度。"},{"letter":"E","text":"expected retirement year","explanation":"「70」是年齡，不是退休的曆年。"},{"letter":"F","text":"age-group label","explanation":"表格問最高准許歲數，沒有要求選二十至二十九等分類標籤。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"cap / minimum","zh":"中文辨析： Age cap 只說最高歲數；十八歲才可申請是最低年齡要求，不能稱為上限。","point":"A minimum age of 18 does not cap the age of older applicants."},{"word":"proposed / enacted","zh":"中文辨析： 原題問「應否」，不能把建議的上限說成已生效的規則。","point":"Discussing a limit does not create one."},{"word":"retirement age / candidacy limit","zh":"中文辨析： 退休年齡涉及何時離職，參選資格上限涉及能否申請；兩者可能不同。","point":"Leaving one job does not necessarily bar a candidacy."},{"word":"age bracket / age boundary","zh":"中文辨析： Age bracket 把人分類，並不必然排除任何人；limit 是資格界線。","point":"A survey band can include 70-year-olds without barring them."},{"word":"age factor / age rule","zh":"中文辨析： 考慮候選人年齡是一個因素，並不等於設硬性年齡限制。","point":"A panel may discuss age without imposing a cutoff."}],"moduleNumber":77},{"id":"lesson-078","sourceId":49,"headword":"age limits","title":"Age limits","titleZh":"年齡限制","subtitle":"年齡限制","description":"The 2017 set's article says people under 18 generally cannot get tattoos, with a stated medical exception, and gives different legal ages for other activities. The group prompt asks why the government has age limits for tattoos, why limits differ by activity, and whether any should change. Here these are mainly minimum legal ages for permission, not maximum ages. The lesson does not infer extra exceptions or treat the source's activity table as an explanation of why every law exists.","sourceSense":"The 2017 set's article says people under 18 generally cannot get tattoos, with a stated medical exception, and gives different legal ages for other activities. The group prompt asks why the government has age limits for tattoos, why limits differ by activity, and whether any should change. Here these are mainly minimum legal ages for permission, not maximum ages. The lesson does not infer extra exceptions or treat the source's activity table as an explanation of why every law exists.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["age restrictions","Good broad alternative for rules based on age, including lower thresholds. It does not by itself identify whether the boundary is minimum or maximum."],["age caps","Wrong direction for the tattoo example: a cap is a maximum, whereas under-18s are barred and older people are eligible. It would fit a separately stated upper limit, not this source sense."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Minimum legal ages makes the direction and legal status explicit. Legal age thresholds highlights the crossing point for permission and works for different activities with different numbers. Age restrictions keeps the broad rule sense. Age requirements is also natural but overlaps age restrictions and can include other criteria. Age cutoffs is less formal and can be upper or lower; the lesson uses the more explicit threshold term. Age caps is recorded as a false synonym here. A rule that requires parental permission at one age may differ from an outright minimum; examples must state which applies."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["age restrictions","泛指各活動按年齡限制參與資格的規則。","本身未說最低還是最高，也不交代例外。"],["minimum legal ages","法律規定未滿某歲數不能參與，且可比較多項活動。","不等於最高上限或只有建議性的歲數。"],["legal age thresholds","焦點是跨過某個法定歲數後取得資格。","門檻不是平均歲數或年齡組別標籤。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 概括不同活動的規則，用 age restrictions；明說「未滿某歲數不得參與」且有法律效力，用 minimum legal ages；強調到達某個生日便取得資格，用 legal age thresholds。原文紋身例子的方向是最低歲數，所以不能用 age caps；醫療例外也不能擴寫成所有未滿十八歲者均可紋身。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"age restrictions","meaning":"年齡限制","note":"按歲數限制某活動資格的規則，可概括不同活動的年齡界線。","collocations":"age restrictions for tattoos; review age restrictions; different age restrictions for different activities.","example":"The council compared age restrictions for several activities before discussing whether any should change.","exampleZh":"議會比較多項活動的年齡限制，再討論有沒有規則需要修改。","contrast":"Restriction 不自動表示上限、家長同意例外或某條法律的目的；須看句子補充。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The class compared age limits for tattoos, driving and other activities rather than assuming every activity had the same rule.","zh":"全班比較紋身、駕駛和其他活動的年齡限制，沒有假設每項活動都採用同一規則。","upgrade":"The class compared age restrictions for tattoos, driving and other activities rather than assuming every activity had the same rule.","answer":"age restrictions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upper age caps","explanation":"來源活動主要設定最低准許歲數；caps 卻指最高上限。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parental-consent rules","explanation":"各活動的年齡規則不一定都以家長同意為條件；本題要比較的是年齡本身如何限制資格。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age restrictions","explanation":"Age restrictions 可概括不同活動各自按年齡限定資格的規則。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one uniform age rule","explanation":"原句特意說不能假設每項活動都用同一規則。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age categories for a survey","explanation":"班上比較的是各活動可否參與，不是調查如何把人分組。"},{"letter":"F","text":"non-binding age advice","explanation":"來源討論政府設定的限制，而非只供參考的建議。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The article asks why age limits stop people under 18 from getting tattoos in ordinary circumstances, while noting a narrow medical exception.","zh":"文章問為何年齡限制一般阻止未滿十八歲的人紋身，同時指出有一個狹窄的醫療例外。","upgrade":"The article asks why age restrictions stop people under 18 from getting tattoos in ordinary circumstances, while noting a narrow medical exception.","answer":"age restrictions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an upper tattoo-age cap","explanation":"被限制的是未滿十八歲者，方向是最低門檻而非最高上限。"},{"letter":"B","text":"parental-consent permission","explanation":"一般情況下家長同意也不能讓未滿十八歲者紋身；題目只指出狹窄醫療例外。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an unrestricted medical exemption","explanation":"醫療例外只限指定情況，不能把它寫成無條件豁免。"},{"letter":"D","text":"age restrictions","explanation":"Age restrictions 表達按年齡限制一般紋身資格，仍容許句子另述狹窄醫療例外。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a suggested tattoo age","explanation":"十八歲是一般法律限制，不只是建議紋身的歲數。"},{"letter":"F","text":"one absolute ban with no exception","explanation":"來源明說有狹窄醫療例外，不能描述成毫無例外的禁令。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"minimum legal ages","meaning":"法定最低年齡","note":"法律容許參與某活動的最低歲數；低於門檻的人通常不得參加，例外須另說。","collocations":"minimum legal ages for different activities; raise a minimum legal age; compare minimum legal ages.","example":"The poster listed minimum legal ages for two activities so pupils could see why a 16-year-old qualified for one but not the other.","exampleZh":"海報列出兩項活動的法定最低年齡，讓學生明白十六歲人士為何可參加其中一項，卻不能參加另一項。","contrast":"Minimum 不能換成 cap；legal 亦不能由單純家長建議推論。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In the fictional town's licensing law, the age limits are 16 for one activity and 18 for another; anyone younger than the listed age must wait.","zh":"在這個虛構城鎮的發牌法例中，一項活動的年齡限制是十六歲，另一項是十八歲；低於各項指定歲數的人須等待。","upgrade":"In the fictional town's licensing law, the minimum legal ages are 16 for one activity and 18 for another; anyone younger than the listed age must wait.","answer":"minimum legal ages","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"upper eligibility ages","explanation":"低於十六或十八歲的人要等，說的是最低而不是最高界線。"},{"letter":"B","text":"minimum legal ages","explanation":"規則冊列出兩項活動各自的法定最低歲數，低於者不可參與。"},{"letter":"C","text":"minimum ages suggested by parents","explanation":"這兩個數字列於虛構發牌法例，並非家長個別建議。"},{"letter":"D","text":"one legal age for every activity","explanation":"一項十六歲、另一項十八歲，不能說所有活動只用同一歲數。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age categories without permission rules","explanation":"低於各數字的人必須等候，數字決定資格而非只供分類。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ages at which licences expire","explanation":"達到十六或十八歲後才可參與，並非到該歲數牌照便失效。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The fictional council proposed raising the age limits for two licensed activities from 16 to 17 and from 18 to 19; younger applicants would have to wait longer if the changes became law.","zh":"虛構議會建議把兩項須持牌活動的年齡限制分別由十六提高至十七歲、由十八提高至十九歲；若修例成法，較年輕申請人須等待更久。","upgrade":"The fictional council proposed raising the minimum legal ages for two licensed activities from 16 to 17 and from 18 to 19; younger applicants would have to wait longer if the changes became law.","answer":"minimum legal ages","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"voluntary age advice","explanation":"Became law 和申請人必須等待，均表示討論的是法定門檻。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upper age caps","explanation":"提高門檻令較年輕的人須多等，符合最低歲數而非最高上限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parental-consent thresholds","explanation":"題目沒說滿十七或十九歲仍需家長同意；提議改的是法律准入最低歲數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enacted minimum ages","explanation":"十七及十九歲是建議的新門檻，尚未成法，不能稱為已生效。"},{"letter":"E","text":"minimum legal ages","explanation":"Minimum legal ages 指兩項活動各自最低准許歲數；proposed 保留修例未生效。"},{"letter":"F","text":"one general age of majority","explanation":"題目分別改兩項活動的門檻，不是在改所有權利通用的單一成年歲數。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"legal age thresholds","meaning":"法定年齡門檻","note":"強調跨過哪個法定歲數便改變資格；多項活動可有不同門檻。","collocations":"cross a legal age threshold; compare legal age thresholds; legal age thresholds for activities.","example":"The guide marked different legal age thresholds, explaining that permission changed at 16 for one activity and at 18 for another.","exampleZh":"指南標示不同法定年齡門檻，說明一項活動的資格在十六歲改變，另一項則在十八歲改變。","contrast":"Threshold 指門檻點，句子須說清楚達到門檻後可做甚麼；不等於把人按年齡分組。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The poster marks the age limits at which two legal permissions begin: one starts on a person's sixteenth birthday and the other on the eighteenth.","zh":"海報標示兩項法律許可開始生效的年齡門檻：一項從十六歲生日開始，另一項從十八歲生日開始。","upgrade":"The poster marks the legal age thresholds at which two legal permissions begin: one starts on a person's sixteenth birthday and the other on the eighteenth.","answer":"legal age thresholds","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"legal age thresholds","explanation":"海報標的是兩項許可各從哪個生日開始生效，thresholds 突出跨過門檻的時點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upper age caps","explanation":"生日到達後才取得資格，沒有說超過該歲數反而被禁止。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parental-consent milestones","explanation":"海報說的是法律許可從哪個生日開始，沒有說是家長同意才生效。"},{"letter":"D","text":"suggested ages to start","explanation":"兩項法律許可正式生效，不只是建議何時開始。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age brackets for pupils","explanation":"海報沒有把學生編組，而是標示各活動取得許可的生日。"},{"letter":"F","text":"licence-expiry ages","explanation":"許可在十六或十八歲開始，不是到該歲數便終止。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the applicant turned 18 at midnight, she crossed one of the age limits in the fictional licensing rules and could submit her application for the first time.","zh":"申請人在午夜滿十八歲時，跨過虛構發牌規則的一項年齡門檻，首次可以提交申請。","upgrade":"When the applicant turned 18 at midnight, she crossed one of the legal age thresholds in the fictional licensing rules and could submit her application for the first time.","answer":"legal age thresholds","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"the general age of majority","explanation":"句子只給一項虛構發牌活動的具體准入門檻，沒有說所有法律權利都在十八歲開始。"},{"letter":"B","text":"upper age caps","explanation":"達到十八歲後能申請，是最低准入門檻而非年長者上限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"parental-consent thresholds","explanation":"發牌規則說她一滿十八歲便可申請，沒有附加家長同意條件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"suggested coming-of-age milestones","explanation":"她首次取得法律申請資格，不只是象徵成年的建議時點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"age bands used for surveys","explanation":"申請資格即時改變，並非轉入另一統計年齡組。"},{"letter":"F","text":"legal age thresholds","explanation":"Crossed 配合 thresholds，表示一滿十八歲便跨過法定門檻而首次可申請。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"age cap / minimum age","zh":"中文辨析： 紋身例子阻止未滿十八歲的人；cap 卻是超過某歲數不能參加的最高上限。","point":"A rule excluding younger people is not an upper cap."},{"word":"law / advice","zh":"中文辨析： 法定年齡有法律效力；家長說「最好等到十八歲」只是建議，除非另有法律規定。","point":"Advice does not become a legal age solely by mentioning 18."},{"word":"age category / permission threshold","zh":"中文辨析： 「十三至十七歲」是分類；「滿十八歲才准參加」是資格界線。","point":"A survey band need not permit or forbid an activity."},{"word":"one rule / different activities","zh":"中文辨析： 來源列不同活動的不同歲數，不能把紋身十八歲搬到每一項活動。","point":"Distinct activities may have distinct legal ages."},{"word":"exception / general rule","zh":"中文辨析： 來源提到醫生因醫療理由施行紋身的例外；有例外不代表一般未滿十八歲者都可紋身。","point":"A narrow exception does not erase the general minimum."}],"moduleNumber":78},{"id":"lesson-079","sourceId":55,"headword":"airport ambassadors","title":"Airport ambassadors","titleZh":"機場服務大使","subtitle":"機場服務大使","description":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 1.2〈Airport Ambassadors〉廣告說，香港國際機場招募 18 至 24 歲青年成為 Airport Ambassadors；同篇說他們駐守機場繁忙位置，即時協助有需要的人，並列出迎接旅客、回答查詢與指路、協助有需要旅客及推廣旅客安全等工作。","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 1.2〈Airport Ambassadors〉廣告說，香港國際機場招募 18 至 24 歲青年成為 Airport Ambassadors；同篇說他們駐守機場繁忙位置，即時協助有需要的人，並列出迎接旅客、回答查詢與指路、協助有需要旅客及推廣旅客安全等工作。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["airport greeters","contextual, narrower","只突出迎接旅客；若句子說的是全部查詢、安全及協助職責，會漏掉其他面向。"],["airport representatives","ambiguous / unsafe alone","可指代表機場發言或處理商務事宜的人；原文沒有賦予青年大使這種官方代表權。須另明說服務職能才可重寫。"],["airport guides","contextual, narrower","在指路或介紹機場設施的句子可用；不能概括所有迎賓及安全工作。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["airport customer-service assistants","說明多種機場查詢與服務問題時，可概括大使的顧客服務職能。"],["airport greeters","句子特別談抵埗或活動入口的歡迎接待時可用；不能概括所有職責。"],["airport guides","句子特別談指路或改道時可用；不代表旅行團導遊或入境人員。"],["passenger assistance staff","明確對旅客提供即時實際支援時可用；比協助 anyone in need 稍窄。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 看句子突出哪項工作：多類問題是 customer-service assistants；迎接是 greeters；指路是 guides；對有需要旅客作實際支援是 passenger assistance staff。泛指整個官方計劃仍以 airport ambassadors 最準確。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"airport customer-service assistants","meaning":"機場顧客服務助理；職能概括","note":"以幫助旅客、回答問題等顧客服務工作概括大使的主要職能；是普通職能描述，不是計劃的正式職銜。","collocations":"airport customer-service assistants; customer-service assistance at the airport","example":"Airport customer-service assistants answered travellers' questions near the information desk.","exampleZh":"機場顧客服務助理在資訊櫃檯附近回答旅客問題。","contrast":"此說法可概括多種服務，但 ambassador 職稱的迎賓及推廣形象意味會減弱；airline staff 則可能只屬某航空公司，僱主範圍不同。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Airport ambassadors answered travellers' questions about facilities, explained directions and helped with service enquiries.","zh":"機場大使回答旅客對設施的查詢、講解路線，並協助處理服務問題。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Airport customer-service assistants answered travellers' questions about facilities, explained directions and helped with service enquiries.","answer":"airport customer-service assistants","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airport customer-service assistants","explanation":"設施查詢、指路與服務疑問合起來，適合用廣義顧客服務職能概括。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"只突出歡迎抵埗旅客，未概括設施、路線與服務查詢三類工作。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airport guides","explanation":"指路是其中一項工作，但題句也有設施及服務問題。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airline customer-service agents","explanation":"通常服務某間航空公司的旅客，原句講機場範圍的多種查詢。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport security officers","explanation":"保安有檢查及秩序職責；題句說的是一般顧客服務。"},{"letter":"F","text":"official airport representatives","explanation":"可能暗示正式對外發言，原句只說前線服務。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The recruitment notice says airport ambassadors will staff busy information points and help visitors solve a range of travel-service problems.","zh":"招聘告示說，機場大使將在繁忙的資訊站值勤，協助訪客解決各類旅遊服務問題。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The recruitment notice says airport customer-service assistants will staff busy information points and help visitors solve a range of travel-service problems.","answer":"airport customer-service assistants","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airport tour guides","explanation":"帶參觀團遊覽機場與資訊站處理不同旅遊服務問題不一樣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport customer-service assistants","explanation":"招聘說明列的是資訊站服務與多種訪客問題，適合職能概括。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airline check-in agents","explanation":"只替某航空公司辦理登機，範圍比機場資訊站的問題窄。"},{"letter":"D","text":"official airport spokespeople","explanation":"對外發言權未見於原句，資訊站員工不等於官方發言人。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport retail assistants","explanation":"店員可回答商品問題，但題句說的是整個機場的旅遊服務查詢。"},{"letter":"F","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"迎接訪客只是部分工作，未包含資訊站的一系列問題。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"airport greeters","meaning":"機場迎賓人員；只突出迎接","note":"當題句明確說大使站在抵埗位置迎接旅客、讓人感到受歡迎時可用；不能把指路、安全推廣等所有職責都縮成問候。","collocations":"airport greeters at the arrivals area; greeters welcome passengers","example":"The airport greeters welcomed arriving passengers and helped them find the information desk.","exampleZh":"機場迎賓人員歡迎抵埗旅客，並協助他們找到資訊櫃檯。","contrast":"Greeter 強調抵埗時的接待；guide 強調指引路線。若只說大使處理複雜顧客投訴，greeter 太窄。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Airport ambassadors stood near the arrivals exit to welcome passengers as soon as they entered the public hall.","zh":"機場大使站在入境出口附近，旅客一進入公共大堂便迎接他們。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Airport greeters stood near the arrivals exit to welcome passengers as soon as they entered the public hall.","answer":"airport greeters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airport guides","explanation":"指路可在迎賓後發生，但題句只描述出口外的歡迎接待。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airline check-in assistants","explanation":"辦理登機手續屬離境流程，與公共入境大堂迎賓不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"站在入境出口歡迎旅客，正好突出大使的迎賓職能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"passenger service coordinators","explanation":"可統籌多項服務，卻未如 greeters 準確指出只在出口迎接的動作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport information assistants","explanation":"解答資訊問題可能是另一職責，題句沒有查詢內容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"security screeners","explanation":"安檢工作不是旅客進入公共大堂時的歡迎接待。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"On the opening day of a new terminal, airport ambassadors welcomed the first visitors and handed them maps at the entrance.","zh":"新航站樓啟用當天，機場大使在入口歡迎首批訪客，並派發地圖。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"On the opening day of a new terminal, airport greeters welcomed the first visitors and handed them maps at the entrance.","answer":"airport greeters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airport guides","explanation":"派地圖可協助指路，但題句主軸是啟用日迎接首批訪客。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airline check-in assistants","explanation":"辦理登機手續與入口歡迎訪客不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"official media spokespeople","explanation":"向媒體發言需要另有正式權限，題句只說迎賓及派地圖。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"開幕日於入口歡迎訪客，並提供基本地圖，符合迎賓人員說法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport information assistants","explanation":"可提供地圖，但未如 greeters 突出開幕日歡迎首批訪客。"},{"letter":"F","text":"passenger transport coordinators","explanation":"安排交通服務與入口迎賓派圖不同。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"airport guides","meaning":"機場導向人員；只突出指路","note":"當大使主要回答位置查詢，指引旅客往閘口、車站或服務櫃檯時可用；這是功能改寫而非正式職稱。","collocations":"airport guides give directions; ask an airport guide for help","example":"The airport guides showed new arrivals the way to the city-bound train.","exampleZh":"機場導向人員向剛抵埗的旅客指出前往市區列車的路。","contrast":"Guide 不表示他們會檢查護照或帶領付費旅行團；此處是機場內指路。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Airport ambassadors showed new arrivals which corridor led to the city-bound train.","zh":"機場大使向剛抵埗的旅客指出哪條走廊通往市區列車。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Airport guides showed new arrivals which corridor led to the city-bound train.","answer":"airport guides","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"可以先歡迎旅客，但題句集中在解釋通往列車的走廊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"railway platform staff","explanation":"在月台服務的人未必在機場走廊為新抵埗旅客指路。"},{"letter":"C","text":"terminal information clerks","explanation":"櫃檯職員也可回答方向，但題句描述在現場帶出明確路線的導向職能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airline booking agents","explanation":"處理機票訂位，不是講解機場內走廊的位置。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport guides","explanation":"題句集中在向旅客指出通往交通工具的路。"},{"letter":"F","text":"airport map designers","explanation":"設計地圖與在現場向旅客指出哪條走廊不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When construction closed the usual passage, airport ambassadors directed passengers along a temporary route to their gates.","zh":"工程封閉了慣常通道後，機場大使引導旅客沿臨時路線前往登機閘口。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When construction closed the usual passage, airport guides directed passengers along a temporary route to their gates.","answer":"airport guides","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"terminal repair workers","explanation":"可能負責施工，卻不一定在現場向旅客講解改道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"迎接旅客不是題句重點；這裏須引導他們沿新路到閘口。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airline gate agents","explanation":"通常處理某航班的閘口事務；題句說為沿臨時通道走的旅客指全段路線。"},{"letter":"D","text":"passenger assistance staff","explanation":"可提供一般支援，但 guides 更準確標出此處的臨時路線指引。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport security guards","explanation":"保安或可協助改道，但題句沒有保安或執法職能，guides 更精準。"},{"letter":"F","text":"airport guides","explanation":"舊通道關閉後提供新的閘口路線，正是導向職能。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"passenger assistance staff","meaning":"旅客支援人員；協助角度","note":"當句子強調為有需要旅客提供即時、實際幫助時可用；比原文的 anyone in need 略窄，只指旅客。","collocations":"passenger assistance staff help travellers; ask passenger assistance staff for directions","example":"Passenger assistance staff helped a traveller find the lost-property counter.","exampleZh":"旅客支援人員協助一名旅客找到失物認領櫃檯。","contrast":"Staff 表示工作人員，不等同所有人都具有醫療、保安或移民官員的專業權力；若題句也涉及非旅客，須改用更廣說法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Airport ambassadors helped a lost passenger locate the correct airline desk and contact her family.","zh":"機場大使協助一名迷路旅客找到正確的航空公司櫃檯，並聯絡家人。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Passenger assistance staff helped a lost passenger locate the correct airline desk and contact her family.","answer":"passenger assistance staff","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"passenger assistance staff","explanation":"對象明確是一名旅客，工作是即時協助她解決兩項實際需要。"},{"letter":"B","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"迎接旅客不足以涵蓋找櫃檯及協助聯絡家人兩項實際支援。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airport guides","explanation":"可指往櫃檯的路，但未必涵蓋協助聯絡家屬。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airline check-in agents","explanation":"只處理登機手續；迷路旅客未必搭乘其航空公司。"},{"letter":"E","text":"airport security officers","explanation":"題句沒有保安事件或執法需要，只有服務性協助。"},{"letter":"F","text":"official airport representatives","explanation":"可能暗示對外發言權，題句是前線個別旅客支援。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After a flight was cancelled, airport ambassadors helped stranded passengers find the airline's service counter and explained where to seek further help.","zh":"航班取消後，機場大使協助滯留旅客找到航空公司的服務櫃檯，並解釋到哪裏尋求進一步協助。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After a flight was cancelled, passenger assistance staff helped stranded passengers find the airline's service counter and explained where to seek further help.","answer":"passenger assistance staff","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"airline rebooking agents","explanation":"可替旅客改票，但題句說大使把人帶到航空公司櫃檯，沒有親自處理改票。"},{"letter":"B","text":"passenger assistance staff","explanation":"對象是滯留旅客，職能是協助找服務櫃檯與後續求助地點。"},{"letter":"C","text":"airport spokespeople","explanation":"官方對外解說事故不同於直接向旅客提供個別支援。"},{"letter":"D","text":"airport guides","explanation":"可指路到櫃檯，但題句還說向滯留旅客解釋進一步求助的方法，支援範圍較廣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"terminal information clerks","explanation":"櫃檯職員也可給資料，但原句說大使主動協助滯留旅客找櫃檯並作轉介。"},{"letter":"F","text":"airport greeters","explanation":"迎賓角色未能概括航班取消後的個別支援。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Diplomatic ambassador / official spokesperson · 職稱比喻不是外交或發言權","zh":"中文辨析： 這些青年大使在機場服務旅客；原文沒有說他們代表國家、替機場發佈政策或接受媒體訪問。Airport representatives 若不加限定，容易誤指有正式代表權的人。","point":"A service ambassador is not automatically a diplomat or official spokesperson."},{"word":"Greeter / guide / assistant · 單一職能不等於全部職責","zh":"中文辨析： 迎賓、指路及支援都是原文職責之一；句子只談其中一項時可用相應名稱，概括整個計劃則應保留較廣的職能描述或正式職稱。","point":"Each functional label highlights part of the ambassador role."},{"word":"Security officer / immigration officer · 權力與專業不同","zh":"中文辨析： 大使可提醒旅客注意安全，卻不因此成為保安或入境審查官；兩者有不同權責及訓練。","point":"Promoting passenger safety does not confer security or immigration authority."},{"word":"Airline staff · 機場服務與航空公司職員","zh":"中文辨析： 大使在機場協助不同旅客，未必隸屬某間航空公司。若句子談一間航空公司處理登機票的職員，才用 airline staff。","point":"Airport-wide visitor assistance differs from service for one airline."},{"word":"Volunteers / paid workers · 不可猜僱用形式","zh":"中文辨析： 原文招募青年，官方計劃包含在職培訓及工作機會；不能因「大使」二字便當成所有人無薪。另一個長者大使計劃可以是義工，但不可混成同一群。","point":"The title alone does not establish whether a particular ambassador is paid or volunteering."}],"moduleNumber":79},{"id":"lesson-080","sourceId":65,"headword":"ambassadors","title":"Ambassadors","titleZh":"宣傳計劃的學生大使","subtitle":"宣傳計劃的學生大使","description":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，4.2 的環保計劃說學生會成為「Young Ambassadors」，邀請公眾支持減碳計劃及多用公共交通。後文說這些學生已向駕駛者積極推廣「不開車」概念。這裏的 ambassadors 是獲計劃指定、代表計劃對外接觸和倡議的學生，不是外交大使，也不只是迎賓。以下練習都是原創。[2012 Paper 4 set 4.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2012 DSE Paper 4，4.2 的環保計劃說學生會成為「Young Ambassadors」，邀請公眾支持減碳計劃及多用公共交通。後文說這些學生已向駕駛者積極推廣「不開車」概念。這裏的 ambassadors 是獲計劃指定、代表計劃對外接觸和倡議的學生，不是外交大使，也不只是迎賓。以下練習都是原創。[2012 Paper 4 set 4.2 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2012-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","此處的界線"],"rows":[["representatives","直接／偏角色身分","學生代表環保計劃對外活動，但未必可發布官方政策。"],["envoys","此處不宜","通常帶正式派遣、外交或機構間傳達訊息的語氣；街頭邀請公眾用公共交通時太正式。"],["greeters","假近義","迎接訪客只是可能的一小項工作，不能概括主動勸說公眾減碳。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： Outreach volunteers 指走進社區親自接觸公眾；campaign promoters 指積極擴大認識與參與；student spokespeople 只有獲授權對媒體或公眾正式發言時才成立。Champions 可在宣傳文中指熱心支持者，與 advocates 高度重疊且語氣較宣傳化；activists 暗示更強烈的社會運動與抗議手段，原文沒有；recruiters 只指招募人員，忽略理念教育。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- 原文 Young Ambassadors 是環保計劃指定的學生推廣者。\n- Student representatives 看正式代表身分；campaign advocates 看提出理由勸說；outreach volunteers 須明示自願無薪，並看是否直接接觸社區；campaign promoters 看海報、短片等宣傳。\n- Student spokespeople 必須獲授權代表計劃正式發言。Envoys 過度外交化，greeters 只迎賓而漏掉減碳倡議。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"student representatives","meaning":"學生代表","note":"計劃正式指定學生在活動中代表其身分、回答基本問題或交代計劃內容時用；不自動表示有權決定政策。","collocations":"student representatives of the scheme; represent the programme at a booth; official student representatives","example":"Student representatives of the scheme explained its aims at the school fair.","exampleZh":"計劃的學生代表在校園展覽會上解釋計劃宗旨。","contrast":"Representatives 突出受委任的身分；advocates 突出積極支持主張，兩者可由同一人兼任。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The programme appointed two ambassadors from each school to report how pupils were responding to its campaign and relay the organisers’ next steps back to their classmates.","zh":"計劃從每校委任兩名大使，向主辦者報告同學對活動的反應，再向同學轉達主辦者的下一步安排。","upgrade":"The programme appointed two student representatives from each school to report how pupils were responding to its campaign and relay the organisers’ next steps back to their classmates.","answer":"student representatives","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"student representatives","explanation":"計劃正式委任學生作雙向聯絡，student representatives 最能說明代表計劃在學校傳訊的身分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 側重為減碳立場辯護，這裏報告同學反應及轉達主辦者安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 直接接觸公眾，這裏是計劃與學校之間的正式聯絡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 致力提升計劃知名度；這裏主要轉達意見和安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"spokespeople 通常代表計劃正式對外發言；兩人是在計劃與本校之間傳訊。"},{"letter":"F","text":"youth envoys","explanation":"envoys 帶使節語氣，學校與計劃的常規聯絡不需這稱呼。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The scheme gave its ambassadors official badges so visitors to the community fair would know which students could explain the programme on its behalf.","zh":"計劃給大使正式徽章，讓社區展覽會的訪客知道哪些學生可代表計劃作介紹。","upgrade":"The scheme gave its student representatives official badges so visitors to the community fair would know which students could explain the programme on its behalf.","answer":"student representatives","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"community greeters","explanation":"greeters 可迎接訪客，但徽章顯示的是獲指定代表計劃介紹的身分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"student representatives","explanation":"官方徽章和 on its behalf 明示授權代表計劃，student representatives 最精確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"campaign donors","explanation":"沒有說學生出資。"},{"letter":"D","text":"environmental advocates","explanation":"advocates 可積極支持理念，但題句重點是獲授權代表計劃。"},{"letter":"E","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 也會接觸訪客，但徽章與代計劃介紹更直接指代表角色。"},{"letter":"F","text":"media spokespeople","explanation":"media spokespeople 需指定對媒體正式發言，展覽會訪客介紹未到此層。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"campaign advocates","meaning":"活動倡議者","note":"學生解釋減碳理由並勸公眾改變出行習慣時用；強調有立場的倡導，不只是轉遞資訊。","collocations":"campaign advocates for low-carbon travel; advocate public transport; youth advocates","example":"The campaign advocates explained why taking the bus could reduce car use.","exampleZh":"活動倡議者解釋為何乘巴士可以減少開車。","contrast":"Advocates 強調說服人接受理念；promoters 可只集中提高活動知名度。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The young ambassadors used evidence about emissions to persuade drivers to try public transport instead of dismissing the no-car idea.","zh":"青年大使用排放數據說服駕駛者嘗試乘公共交通，而不是把不開車理念置之不理。","upgrade":"The young campaign advocates used evidence about emissions to persuade drivers to try public transport instead of dismissing the no-car idea.","answer":"campaign advocates","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 可宣傳活動，但本句特別寫以排放證據勸人接受理念。"},{"letter":"B","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 說身分，不如 advocates 說清楚有立場的說服。"},{"letter":"C","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"提出環境證據、勸人改變習慣，campaign advocates 最合功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 說接觸方式，未概括以數據辯護的倡議。"},{"letter":"E","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"沒有記者會或官方政策發言授權。"},{"letter":"F","text":"event greeters","explanation":"greeters 只迎人，未涵蓋論證與勸說。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When residents said one car-free day would make no difference, the ambassadors defended the idea by explaining how many small choices add up.","zh":"居民說一天不駕車不會帶來改變，大使便解釋眾多小選擇如何累積成效，為理念辯護。","upgrade":"When residents said one car-free day would make no difference, the campaign advocates defended the idea by explaining how many small choices add up.","answer":"campaign advocates","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach 可描述與居民直接交流，但未突出他們回應質疑的立場。"},{"letter":"B","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"面對反對意見提出理由維護理念，advocates 最切合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 會擴散消息，題句主線是為理念辯論而非知名度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 可能是學生身分，但未說明他們提出理據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"policy spokespeople","explanation":"沒有獲正式政策發言授權，亦非單純讀官方立場。"},{"letter":"F","text":"community hosts","explanation":"hosts 迎接來客，不會概括反駁居民質疑。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"outreach volunteers","meaning":"社區外展義工","note":"學生自願、無薪地走出校園，到街頭、住戶或透過電話與公眾直接交流時，可稱 outreach volunteers；原試卷沒有交代學生是否無薪，因此這是有條件的角色改寫。","collocations":"outreach volunteers at a station; community outreach volunteers; volunteers doing public outreach","example":"Outreach volunteers spoke with commuters outside the bus station.","exampleZh":"外展義工在巴士站外與通勤者交談。","contrast":"Outreach 說向外接觸公眾；representatives 說計劃授予的身分。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The ambassadors volunteered after school to go door to door in nearby buildings, asking residents how they travelled and explaining the scheme in person.","zh":"大使放學後自願逐戶走訪附近樓宇，詢問居民出行方式，並親身解釋計劃。","upgrade":"The outreach volunteers went door to door after school in nearby buildings, asking residents how they travelled and explaining the scheme in person.","answer":"outreach volunteers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 可能提出理念理由，但題句最鮮明的是自願逐戶接觸的外展方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 可宣傳，卻未如 outreach 指出直接走到居民住處。"},{"letter":"C","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"自願逐戶拜訪、詢問與面談，是義工的直接社區外展。"},{"letter":"D","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"spokespeople 要有正式代表計劃發言授權，題句未說。"},{"letter":"E","text":"school representatives","explanation":"representatives 說被指定身分，未描寫逐戶行動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"survey analysts","explanation":"analysts 會分析問卷，這些學生是在現場解釋計劃。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The ambassadors volunteered to phone households that had requested more information, listen to commuting concerns and explain how the pledge would work.","zh":"大使自願致電曾要求更多資料的住戶，聆聽其通勤顧慮，並解釋承諾計劃如何運作。","upgrade":"The outreach volunteers phoned households that had requested more information, listened to commuting concerns and explained how the pledge would work.","answer":"outreach volunteers","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 著重擴大知名度；這裏自願直接跟進個別住戶的疑問。"},{"letter":"B","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 說身分，不如 outreach 描述主動聯絡公眾。"},{"letter":"C","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 強調捍衛理念，電話中主要是聆聽及解釋參與方法。"},{"letter":"D","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"自願致電住戶、聆聽並解答，是電話形式的外展義工工作。"},{"letter":"E","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"沒有授權發布官方聲明或接待記者。"},{"letter":"F","text":"telephone survey clerks","explanation":"電話中不只收集出行資料，還聆聽問題並解釋承諾計劃，超過 survey clerks 的記錄工作。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"campaign promoters","meaning":"活動宣傳者","note":"學生透過海報、短片、傳單等方法使更多人知道並參與環保活動時用；promoter 在此不是必然收費的商業推銷員。","collocations":"campaign promoters; promote the no-car concept; promoters distributing leaflets","example":"The campaign promoters shared short videos about travelling by train.","exampleZh":"活動宣傳者分享了有關乘搭火車出行的短片。","contrast":"Promoters 聚焦擴散消息；advocates 偏重為理念提出理由。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Before the launch, the ambassadors created short videos and shareable graphics so more families would hear about the no-car pledge.","zh":"活動推出前，大使製作短片及可分享圖片，讓更多家庭知道不開車承諾。","upgrade":"Before the launch, the campaign promoters created short videos and shareable graphics so more families would hear about the no-car pledge.","answer":"campaign promoters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach 偏直接接觸特定住戶；這裏是設計大量分享的宣傳媒體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 會為理念提出理由，題句只說提升認識。"},{"letter":"C","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 說正式身分，不是這些短片的宣傳功能。"},{"letter":"D","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"spokespeople 需正式代表計劃發言，短片圖像製作本身不足以證明。"},{"letter":"E","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"製作可分享短片與圖片擴大知名度，campaign promoters 最直接。"},{"letter":"F","text":"community greeters","explanation":"greeters 迎接現場訪客，不能概括線上傳播。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the town festival, the ambassadors organised a public trial of a car-free day and handed out sign-up cards to encourage participation.","zh":"市鎮節慶時，大使籌辦公開的一日不駕車體驗，並派發登記卡鼓勵參與。","upgrade":"At the town festival, the campaign promoters organised a public trial of a car-free day and handed out sign-up cards to encourage participation.","answer":"campaign promoters","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"沒有正式媒體或政策發言任務。"},{"letter":"B","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"策辦體驗並派登記卡擴大參與，promoters 聚焦把計劃推廣出去。"},{"letter":"C","text":"school representatives","explanation":"representatives 可是其身分，但此句突出的是真正推動報名。"},{"letter":"D","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 側重論證減碳理念；此處主要安排活動吸引參與。"},{"letter":"E","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 也可現場接觸人，卻未如 promoters 概括策辦體驗及推動報名。"},{"letter":"F","text":"festival hosts","explanation":"hosts 負責節慶安排，但未必推動減碳承諾。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"student spokespeople","meaning":"學生發言人","note":"計劃明確授權學生代表它向記者、校方或公眾正式解釋立場時用；不是每位宣傳大使都可自稱發言人。","collocations":"student spokespeople for the scheme; a designated spokesperson; speak on behalf of the programme","example":"Two student spokespeople answered reporters’ questions on behalf of the campaign.","exampleZh":"兩名學生發言人代表活動回答記者提問。","contrast":"Spokespeople 需正式發言授權；一般 outreach volunteers 可邀請公眾，但未必代表計劃作權威聲明。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The organisers authorised two ambassadors to answer journalists’ questions at a press conference and state the scheme’s official position.","zh":"主辦者授權兩名大使在記者會回答記者問題，並陳述計劃的正式立場。","upgrade":"The organisers authorised two student spokespeople to answer journalists’ questions at a press conference and state the scheme’s official position.","answer":"student spokespeople","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 表受委任身分，但對記者發布正式立場需要更特定的發言人身分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 接觸公眾，未必獲記者會答問授權。"},{"letter":"C","text":"campaign advocates","explanation":"advocates 可捍衛理念，但不是每人能代表計劃說正式立場。"},{"letter":"D","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 擴大參與，與官方記者答問有別。"},{"letter":"E","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"明確授權、記者會、官方立場都支持 student spokespeople。"},{"letter":"F","text":"media coordinators","explanation":"media coordinators 安排媒體事務，這兩人則親自向記者說明計劃正式立場。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Only three ambassadors were assigned to read the programme’s approved statement at the school assembly, while other volunteers staffed the information table.","zh":"只有三名大使獲指派在學校集會宣讀計劃已核准的聲明；其他義工則在詢問桌協助。","upgrade":"Only three student spokespeople were assigned to read the programme’s approved statement at the school assembly, while other volunteers staffed the information table.","answer":"student spokespeople","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"statement editors","explanation":"這三人獲指派公開宣讀核准聲明，題句沒有說他們負責編輯文字。"},{"letter":"B","text":"event greeters","explanation":"greeters 可能在詢問桌迎賓，並非這三人的正式發言任務。"},{"letter":"C","text":"outreach volunteers","explanation":"outreach volunteers 更接近其他在詢問桌協助的人；三人特別獲授權發言。"},{"letter":"D","text":"student spokespeople","explanation":"只有三人宣讀獲核准聲明，spokespeople 突出正式對外傳訊。"},{"letter":"E","text":"campaign promoters","explanation":"promoters 可辦宣傳，未必能代表計劃讀聲明。"},{"letter":"F","text":"student representatives","explanation":"representatives 是較廣的授權角色，spokespeople 更準確命名正式發言。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"diplomatic ambassadors / envoys · 官方使節角色過窄","zh":"中文辨析： 外交大使或使節代表政府、組織進行正式任務。原文小學生向公眾推廣少開車理念；若是兩個機構正式派人談判，才可考慮 envoys。","point":"Public campaign representation is not diplomatic appointment."},{"word":"greeters / hosts · 迎賓不能概括倡議","zh":"中文辨析： Greeters 可能在攤位迎接人；原文學生還要邀請公眾支持計劃、改乘公共交通。只寫 greeters 漏掉宣傳與說服。","point":"Greeting visitors is narrower than explaining and advocating a campaign."},{"word":"tour guides / escorts · 帶路不等於減碳宣傳","zh":"中文辨析： 學生若帶人參觀展覽可稱 guides；若陪同來賓可稱 escorts。原文沒有導覽路線或護送任務，重點是傳遞環保訊息。","point":"Guiding a route and promoting a cause are different jobs."},{"word":"activists / protesters · 倡議不一定抗議","zh":"中文辨析： Activists 可大力推動社會改變，但有時暗示組織行動、示威等。原文沒有抗議，而是教育公眾及邀請改變日常交通。","point":"An ambassador may advocate without protesting."},{"word":"volunteers / spokespeople · 一般義工與正式發言權不同","zh":"中文辨析： 只說 volunteers 太籠統，可能做後勤；spokespeople 又需明確授權。原文的共同核心是對外推廣，因此練習要看學生是否在社區宣傳、還是被指定回答媒體。","point":"Tasks and authorization determine the narrower role word."}],"moduleNumber":80},{"id":"lesson-081","sourceId":36,"headword":"advertise","title":"Advertise","titleZh":"為產品做廣告","subtitle":"為產品做廣告","description":"2023 年 DSE Speaking 6.1「Super Bowl」的任務寫道：「Your Business Studies teacher wants your group to use storytelling to advertise a new sports drink called ‘Champion’.」學生要用故事把新飲品介紹給可能購買的人，並引起興趣。題目只要求構思宣傳，沒有說飲品已上市或已有銷量。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2023 年 DSE Speaking 6.1「Super Bowl」的任務寫道：「Your Business Studies teacher wants your group to use storytelling to advertise a new sports drink called ‘Champion’.」學生要用故事把新飲品介紹給可能購買的人，並引起興趣。題目只要求構思宣傳，沒有說飲品已上市或已有銷量。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["promote","教授","推動人們認識、嘗試或購買飲品；範圍比一則廣告廣。"],["market","有條件教授","涵蓋定位、價格、渠道和推廣等較完整的市場工作；單寫故事廣告不足以證明做了全套。"],["publicise","有條件教授","讓消息廣為人知；公告推出日期尤其自然，但不必然有勸購意味。"]],"note":"補充候選：plug 是口語、常指節目或談話中順帶推介；pitch 是向特定對象提出產品主張，重點在提案而非公開刊登；put the word out about 是口語的「傳開消息」，語域與本題正式任務不同。這些不增加獨立教學價值，故不另開重複練習。Sell 可指實際成交，不能由「構思廣告」直接推論。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","主要焦點","在本文語境的限制"],"rows":[["advertise","用公開訊息吸引潛在顧客","題目指定用故事推介新飲品。"],["promote","以一種或多種方法提高興趣","比單一廣告廣，可包含試飲與合作。"],["market","把產品定位並推向目標顧客","須有較完整的市場安排，不能由一則文案直接推論。"],["publicise","使產品或消息廣為人知","只公布日期也可，不必勸購。"],["sell","完成出售或主動售貨","原題沒有銷售結果。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 故事影片加試飲等方式可說 promote；選定客群、定位和渠道可說 market；公布推出日期或供應消息可說 publicise。只有實際售貨證據，才可把「做廣告」改成「賣出」。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Promote","meaning":"推廣","note":"透過廣告、試飲、贊助等方式增加產品關注或購買意願；比 advertise 廣。","collocations":"promote a new drink; promote a product through a story; promote a brand at a sports event.","example":"The class promoted its new drink with a short film and free samples at the match.","exampleZh":"全班以一段短片及球賽上的免費試飲推廣新飲品。","contrast":"Promote exercise 可指鼓勵運動，未必涉及出售商品；須看賓語及情境。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The class will advertise its sports drink through a story video, free samples and a local team partnership.","zh":"全班將以故事影片、免費試飲及與本地球隊合作等方式宣傳運動飲品。","upgrade":"The class will promote its sports drink through a story video, free samples and a local team partnership.","answer":"promote","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"announce","explanation":"宣布一則消息不足以概括影片、試飲與球隊合作三種持續推廣方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"endorse","explanation":"可能由球隊推薦飲品，但全班的影片及試飲不等於全班公開為產品背書。"},{"letter":"C","text":"promote","explanation":"此詞涵蓋透過三種方式增加飲品關注與試用意願。"},{"letter":"D","text":"sell","explanation":"句子說未來的宣傳安排，沒有實際成交或售貨資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"survey","explanation":"問卷調查會收集意見；列出的活動旨在提高興趣。"},{"letter":"F","text":"sponsor","explanation":"球隊合作可能涉及贊助，但不能概括故事影片和免費試飲。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The short film advertises the new drink by ending with an invitation to try it after the race.","zh":"短片在結尾邀請觀眾賽後試飲，以此宣傳新飲品。","upgrade":"The short film promotes the new drink by ending with an invitation to try it after the race.","answer":"promotes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"reviews","explanation":"影評式評測須評估產品優缺點；短片的結尾是邀請試飲。"},{"letter":"B","text":"promotes","explanation":"邀請觀眾試用指定產品有提高興趣的勸說作用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"stocks","explanation":"Stock 是店舖備貨；影片不能把飲品放到貨架上。"},{"letter":"D","text":"compares","explanation":"句子沒有把此飲品與其他飲品比較。"},{"letter":"E","text":"announces","explanation":"短片不只是公布存在；賽後試飲邀請旨在推動觀眾行動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"samples","explanation":"試飲的是人，不是短片；影片只是發出試飲邀請。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Market","meaning":"把產品推向目標市場","note":"為產品選目標顧客、定位、價格、銷售渠道及宣傳方式。廣告通常只是其中一環。","collocations":"market a drink to young athletes; market a product as low-sugar; market a new brand online.","example":"The company marketed the drink to runners through sports shops, race sponsorship and targeted adverts.","exampleZh":"公司透過運動用品店、賽事贊助及定向廣告，把飲品推向跑手市場。","contrast":"若只寫一則故事廣告，說 advertise/promote 更精確；market 要有較全面的面向顧客安排。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The firm wants to advertise the drink to runners, and will coordinate its price, bottle design, shops and campaign channels before launch.","zh":"上市前，公司一併決定價格、瓶身設計、店舖及宣傳渠道，把飲品推向跑手。","upgrade":"The firm wants to market the drink to runners, and will coordinate its price, bottle design, shops and campaign channels before launch.","answer":"market","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"label","explanation":"瓶身標籤只關乎包裝，沒有涵蓋價格、店舖和宣傳渠道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"distribute","explanation":"分銷關乎供貨地點，不能涵蓋定價和產品定位。"},{"letter":"C","text":"market","explanation":"公司協調多項產品與顧客決策，符合整套市場工作。"},{"letter":"D","text":"announce","explanation":"公告飲品推出不等於制定價格與銷售安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"endorse","explanation":"句中沒有代言人公開推薦此飲品。"},{"letter":"F","text":"sample","explanation":"試飲只是一種接觸顧客的活動，不能概括全套安排。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The company will advertise the low-sugar drink as a recovery option for hikers, then place it in outdoor shops rather than supermarkets.","zh":"公司會把低糖飲品定位為遠足後補充體力的選擇，並在戶外用品店而非超市出售。","upgrade":"The company will market the low-sugar drink as a recovery option for hikers, then place it in outdoor shops rather than supermarkets.","answer":"market","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"market","explanation":"選定遠足人士、產品定位和專門店渠道，構成面向目標顧客的市場安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"bottle","explanation":"裝瓶不表達「作為遠足恢復飲品」的定位或店舖選擇。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicise","explanation":"公布產品資訊不必然包括選擇目標群及銷售渠道。"},{"letter":"D","text":"discount","explanation":"原句沒有減價；定價折扣亦不足以概括定位和渠道。"},{"letter":"E","text":"recommend","explanation":"推薦可由個人提出；公司在句中還決定產品定位及售賣地點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"review","explanation":"評測是評價產品，不是把產品放入特定市場。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Publicise","meaning":"公布並使廣為人知","note":"把產品、活動或推出消息傳給公眾；著重傳播資訊，未必勸人購買。","collocations":"publicise a launch date; publicise a new product; publicise an event on social media.","example":"The club publicised the drink's launch date on its website before the tasting event.","exampleZh":"社團在試飲活動前，於網站公布飲品推出日期。","contrast":"簡單公告日期可 publicise，但不等於以賣點說服觀眾買飲品。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The club will advertise the drink's launch date on its website so families know when the tasting event begins.","zh":"社團會在網站公布飲品推出日期，讓家庭知道試飲活動何時開始。","upgrade":"The club will publicise the drink's launch date on its website so families know when the tasting event begins.","answer":"publicise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"endorse","explanation":"公布日期不表示社團公開保證飲品品質或推薦購買。"},{"letter":"B","text":"market","explanation":"句子只講把日期通知家庭，沒有產品定位、價格或渠道決策。"},{"letter":"C","text":"sell","explanation":"網站發布日期不是出售飲品，也沒有成交訊息。"},{"letter":"D","text":"publicise","explanation":"在網站向公眾傳播推出日期，與後面的「讓家庭知道」一致。"},{"letter":"E","text":"review","explanation":"公布活動時間沒有評估飲品好壞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"sponsor","explanation":"社團沒有出資支持別人的活動；它是在傳遞自己活動的消息。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although no sales pitch has been prepared, the school will advertise the fact that a new sports drink is available at the charity match.","zh":"雖然尚未準備勸購內容，學校仍會告知公眾慈善賽上有新運動飲品供應。","upgrade":"Although no sales pitch has been prepared, the school will publicise the fact that a new sports drink is available at the charity match.","answer":"publicise","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"price","explanation":"句子沒有設定售價，而是要讓公眾知道有飲品供應。"},{"letter":"B","text":"endorse","explanation":"學校沒有公開推薦品質；只是傳遞供應消息。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicise","explanation":"Publicise the fact that... 可表示把供應資訊廣泛告知他人，不要求已有勸購文案。"},{"letter":"D","text":"market","explanation":"沒有目標市場、渠道或定位策略；單一事實公告不足以用此詞概括。"},{"letter":"E","text":"sell","explanation":"句子說未來公布消息，沒有指學校在此時完成售貨。"},{"letter":"F","text":"test","explanation":"學校不是在檢驗飲品，而是在傳達它可於慈善賽取得。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Sell：宣傳與成交","zh":"寫好故事廣告並不證明已賣出飲品；sell 若指完成交易，會加上來源沒有的結果。English contrast: Advertise the drink before selling any bottles.","point":""},{"word":"Announce：宣布與勸購","zh":"Announce 可以公布上市日期，但不能概括影片、試飲和球隊合作等一整套推廣。English contrast: Announce a launch; promote a product.","point":""},{"word":"Endorse：名人推薦與一般宣傳","zh":"Endorse 通常指有人公開表示支持；沒有代言人時不能把任何廣告稱作代言。English contrast: A player may endorse a drink; a student may advertise it without an endorsement.","point":""},{"word":"Market / advertise：整套策略與單一訊息","zh":"Market 涉及顧客與渠道等決策。若句子只說寫一段故事文案，不能假設已制定價格和銷售方案。English contrast: Advertising is one possible part of marketing.","point":""},{"word":"Publicise / persuade：知曉與購買理由","zh":"公布活動消息不一定提出產品好處；敘述跑手如何使用飲品並邀請試飲，則帶勸說目的。English contrast: Publicise the date; persuade viewers to try the drink.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":81},{"id":"lesson-082","sourceId":37,"headword":"advertisement","title":"Advertisement","titleZh":"招募廣告","subtitle":"招募廣告","description":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 9.1 的材料寫道：「Below is an extract from an advertisement for the Hong Kong Police Force Post-Secondary School Summer Internship Programme.」Advertisement 是供人閱讀的實習計劃招募訊息。片段屬文字摘錄；不能無根據地改稱電視廣告、已完成的申請表或實習合約。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceSense":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 9.1 的材料寫道：「Below is an extract from an advertisement for the Hong Kong Police Force Post-Secondary School Summer Internship Programme.」Advertisement 是供人閱讀的實習計劃招募訊息。片段屬文字摘錄；不能無根據地改稱電視廣告、已完成的申請表或實習合約。以下指南及練習句均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["ad","教授","Advertisement 的常用簡稱，可指紙本或網上招募廣告。"],["commercial","不教作本來源直接替換","通常指廣播或電視等視聽廣告；原材料只是文字摘錄。"],["promotion","不教作直接替換","可指整體推廣活動或優惠，不一定是一則可供摘錄的廣告文字。"],["advert","教授","英式英語常見的簡稱，尤其可指紙本或網上招聘廣告。"]],"note":"補充 recruitment notice：強調有一份邀請合資格人士申請的文字公告，貼合實習招募；不包括所有產品廣告。Job posting 常指正式職位空缺，實習計劃未必屬有薪工作；flyer/poster 指版面或載體形式，原句未說材料印成哪一種；announcement 可只告知消息，不一定邀請申請。這些界限避免把媒介、目的和整項活動混為一談。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","適用焦點","注意界限"],"rows":[["advertisement","一則宣傳或招募訊息","原材料是可閱讀的實習招募文字。"],["ad","日常簡稱","同樣可指網站或雜誌中的單則廣告。"],["advert","英式英語簡稱","仍是單則訊息，並不暗示視聽播放。"],["recruitment notice","招募與申請方法","需有明確邀請申請或資格資訊。"],["commercial","電視／廣播等視聽廣告","文字摘錄不能直接推論此媒介。"],["promotion","較廣的推廣活動或優惠","不一定是可供引用的一則廣告。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 普通簡稱用 ad，英式簡稱可用 advert；強調資格與申請步驟的文字用 recruitment notice。勿把廣告本身寫成申請表、實習職位或已播出的電視廣告。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Ad","meaning":"廣告的常用簡稱","note":"Advertisement 的簡短日常形式；這裏仍指一則可閱讀的實習招募訊息。","collocations":"an ad for an internship; read an ad online; place an ad in a student magazine.","example":"Mei read an ad for a summer internship on the college website.","exampleZh":"美怡在學院網站讀到一則暑期實習廣告。","contrast":"Ad 是訊息，不是申請表；讀到廣告不等於已獲錄取。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The college website displayed an advertisement for the police summer internship, including eligibility and an application deadline.","zh":"學院網站展示一則警隊暑期實習廣告，列明資格和申請截止日期。","upgrade":"The college website displayed an ad for the police summer internship, including eligibility and an application deadline.","answer":"ad","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"application form","explanation":"列出資格和截止日供人閱讀，不等於要求填寫個人資料的表格。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ad","explanation":"這是網站上一則招募訊息，ad 是 advertisement 的自然簡稱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"vacancy","explanation":"空缺是可申請的機會本身，不是網站展示的整則文字。"},{"letter":"D","text":"commercial","explanation":"網頁文字沒有電視或廣播片段的證據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interview","explanation":"面試是甄選環節，不是網站上的招募文字。"},{"letter":"F","text":"promotion","explanation":"可指整項推廣活動，這裏明確是網站展示的一則有內容的廣告。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Kai responded to the advertisement in the student magazine by sending his CV before the internship deadline.","zh":"啟仔回應學生雜誌的實習廣告，在截止日期前寄出履歷。","upgrade":"Kai responded to the ad in the student magazine by sending his CV before the internship deadline.","answer":"ad","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"placement","explanation":"啟仔是回應招募訊息去爭取實習，不能說他「回應職位本身」。"},{"letter":"B","text":"poster","explanation":"訊息刊在學生雜誌，沒有張貼成海報的證據。"},{"letter":"C","text":"application","explanation":"他寄出履歷是提出申請，不能說他在此之前「回應申請」。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ad","explanation":"Respond to an ad 是自然搭配，表示看到雜誌招募廣告後採取申請行動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"contract","explanation":"尚未錄用，沒有合約可供回應。"},{"letter":"F","text":"campaign","explanation":"啟仔針對雜誌內一則實習廣告寄履歷，並非回應整項推廣活動。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Advert","meaning":"英式英語的廣告簡稱","note":"英式英語常用 advert 指一則廣告；香港的英語學習語境可見此寫法。和 ad 意義近，但語域及地區使用習慣不同。","collocations":"an advert for an internship; a newspaper advert; an online advert.","example":"The college printed an advert for the internship in its weekly bulletin.","exampleZh":"學院在每週通訊刊出一則實習廣告。","contrast":"這是英式縮寫詞，不等於動詞 advertise；也不能因為出現 advert 就假定有電視影片。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In its weekly newsletter, a London school printed an advertisement for the internship beside notices about student clubs.","zh":"一間倫敦學校在每週通訊中，把實習廣告刊於學生社團通告旁。","upgrade":"In its weekly newsletter, a London school printed an advert for the internship beside notices about student clubs.","answer":"advert","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"advert","explanation":"英式英語用 advert 指單則紙本或網上廣告，適合通訊中的招募文字。"},{"letter":"B","text":"advertorial","explanation":"這是仿編輯文章形式的付費宣傳；原句只說一般實習廣告。"},{"letter":"C","text":"advertisement campaign","explanation":"宣傳活動是一連串安排，不是通訊中印出的一則文字。"},{"letter":"D","text":"advertisement form","explanation":"不是慣用的廣告簡稱，也會錯把招募訊息當作表格。"},{"letter":"E","text":"applicant","explanation":"申請人是讀者或應徵者，不是學校刊出的訊息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"commercial","explanation":"文字通訊中沒有播出的影片或音訊廣告。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At a careers fair, a visiting British speaker told students to check the advertisement for a summer placement on the college website before applying.","zh":"在升學就業展，一位英國嘉賓提醒學生，申請前要查看學院網站上的暑期實習廣告。","upgrade":"At a careers fair, a visiting British speaker told students to check the advert for a summer placement on the college website before applying.","answer":"advert","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"advertiser","explanation":"指刊登廣告的人或機構，不是嘉賓叫學生查看的網站訊息。"},{"letter":"B","text":"advertising","explanation":"通常指做廣告的活動或行業，不能代替此處的一則實習訊息。"},{"letter":"C","text":"advert","explanation":"英國嘉賓談的是可供學生在申請前查看的單則網站廣告，advert 自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"application","explanation":"嘉賓叫學生在申請前先看訊息；申請文件是後一步。"},{"letter":"E","text":"promotion","explanation":"可泛指整項推廣，不能精確指網站上這則列明實習條件的文字。"},{"letter":"F","text":"job vacancy","explanation":"指空缺本身；學生要查看的是介紹暑期實習機會的網站廣告。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Recruitment Notice","meaning":"招募公告","note":"一份告知對象、資格及申請方法的書面通知；比一般 advertisement 更明確指招募。","collocations":"a recruitment notice for interns; publish a recruitment notice; read a recruitment notice.","example":"The recruitment notice invited post-secondary students to apply before Friday.","exampleZh":"招募公告邀請專上學生在星期五前提出申請。","contrast":"若只是推介運動飲品，不能改稱 recruitment notice；須真有招募對象或申請訊息。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The advertisement invited post-secondary students to apply for the summer internship and stated the closing date.","zh":"這則廣告邀請專上學生申請暑期實習，並列出截止日期。","upgrade":"The recruitment notice invited post-secondary students to apply for the summer internship and stated the closing date.","answer":"recruitment notice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"programme announcement","explanation":"只說公布計劃未必邀請特定對象申請；本句同時列明對象及截止日。"},{"letter":"B","text":"application guide","explanation":"指導填表的文件可有說明，但此句的主要作用是公開招募專上學生。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicity campaign","explanation":"多項宣傳活動並非這一則邀請申請的具體文字。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recruitment notice","explanation":"明確招募學生並列截止日，符合招募公告功能。"},{"letter":"E","text":"application form","explanation":"表格用於填寫資料；此文字先邀請學生提出申請並列期限。"},{"letter":"F","text":"interview invitation","explanation":"面試邀請只會發給進入甄選程序的人，這裏面向全部合資格學生。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school posted an advertisement inviting students to apply for five volunteer guide positions at its museum.","zh":"學校刊登一則廣告，邀請學生申請博物館的五個義務導賞員名額。","upgrade":"The school posted a recruitment notice inviting students to apply for five volunteer guide positions at its museum.","answer":"recruitment notice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"event notice","explanation":"這不是通知博物館活動時間，而是招募五名學生導賞員。"},{"letter":"B","text":"vacancy list","explanation":"單列五個空缺名稱不足以表達句中向學生發出的申請邀請。"},{"letter":"C","text":"volunteer handbook","explanation":"手冊通常指導已加入的義工；學校此刻仍在徵集申請。"},{"letter":"D","text":"recruitment notice","explanation":"Posted a recruitment notice inviting students to apply 自然表明公開招募五個義務職位。"},{"letter":"E","text":"volunteer application form","explanation":"表格供學生填資料；學校先貼出的是邀請申請的招募訊息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"publicity campaign","explanation":"宣傳活動是多項行動的總稱，不是學校貼出的一則具體招募文字。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Commercial：媒介","zh":"Commercial 常指電視、電台或串流平台上的視聽商業廣告；文字摘錄不證明存在影片。English contrast: Read a printed ad; watch a television commercial.","point":""},{"word":"Promotion：活動與單一訊息","zh":"Promotion 可指整個招募宣傳或限時優惠；an extract from a promotion 不如 an extract from an advertisement 精確。English contrast: The campaign is a promotion; its written notice is an ad.","point":""},{"word":"Application Form：申請文件與招募訊息","zh":"廣告邀請學生申請，申請表則收集申請人的資料，兩者用途不同。English contrast: Read the advertisement before filling in the application form.","point":""},{"word":"Vacancy / Job Posting：職位與實習機會","zh":"Vacancy 是空缺本身；job posting 通常是職位廣告，但實習計劃未必等於正式職位。English contrast: A notice may advertise an internship without offering a permanent vacancy.","point":""},{"word":"Flyer / Poster：載體與訊息","zh":"廣告可能印在海報或傳單上，原句只說文字摘錄，沒有確認具體排版或紙張。English contrast: A flyer can carry an ad; the ad need not be a flyer.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":82},{"id":"lesson-083","sourceId":38,"headword":"advertising","title":"Advertising","titleZh":"廣告宣傳","subtitle":"廣告宣傳","description":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 7.3 的標題是「Is There Truth in Advertising?」。[2014 題目逐字轉錄](https://www.scribd.com/document/1013097967/Eng-Notes-4)載有句子：「The success of a product does not rely only on its advertising but also on its quality.」[另一題目索引](https://dsetreasure.com/dse-english-paper-4-%E9%A1%8C%E7%9B%AE/)亦記錄廣告聲稱與產品品質的對比。此處 advertising 是企業製作並傳播促銷說法的活動，不是單獨一則 advertisement；原段落還討論誇大廣告與首次購買，不能把未付費新聞曝光直接當成這裏的廣告。逐字轉錄屬次級來源，官方試卷影像尚未核對。以下例句和練習均為原創。","sourceSense":"2014 年 DSE Speaking 7.3 的標題是「Is There Truth in Advertising?」。[2014 題目逐字轉錄](https://www.scribd.com/document/1013097967/Eng-Notes-4)載有句子：「The success of a product does not rely only on its advertising but also on its quality.」[另一題目索引](https://dsetreasure.com/dse-english-paper-4-%E9%A1%8C%E7%9B%AE/)亦記錄廣告聲稱與產品品質的對比。此處 advertising 是企業製作並傳播促銷說法的活動，不是單獨一則 advertisement；原段落還討論誇大廣告與首次購買，不能把未付費新聞曝光直接當成這裏的廣告。逐字轉錄屬次級來源，官方試卷影像尚未核對。以下例句和練習均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["promotion","教授，視乎範圍","可指提高產品關注和銷售的活動，可能包括廣告、優惠及試用；比廣告廣。"],["publicity","不教作直接近義","著重產品或活動獲得公眾注意，可來自未付費報道；標題的 advertising 特指商家製作及傳播的促銷說法。"],["marketing","有條件教授","涵蓋研究顧客、定位、定價、渠道和廣告；須有較完整商業策略才可替換。"]],"note":"補充候選：commercial communication 是較正式的總稱，但在日常 DSE 答案中生硬；advertising campaign 指一項特定宣傳活動，不能概括整個行業；adverts/ads 是一則則訊息，不能無條件代替不可數的活動名詞。Publicity 在其他語境可泛指曝光，但不能把未付費新聞報道當成廣告，因此列為辨析詞而非練習目標。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","重點","界限"],"rows":[["advertising","製作並傳播促銷訊息的活動","原標題關心訊息真實性。"],["promotion","提高興趣的一組活動","可包括試用及折扣，範圍較廣。"],["publicity","取得公眾注意","可來自免費報道；不能直接代替標題中的商業廣告說法。"],["marketing","研究、定位、價格、渠道與宣傳","不可從單一廣告推斷整套策略。"],["an advertisement / an ad","一則訊息","可數，與活動名詞不同。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 跨媒介推廣可稱 promotion；涉及顧客、價格及渠道的更廣工作可稱 marketing。由報道或分享帶來的 publicity 並不是商家自己製作的廣告。判斷說法是否真實時，先查明究竟是單一廣告、跨媒介宣傳，還是整個市場說法。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Promotion","meaning":"推廣活動","note":"以廣告、試用、折扣等方法鼓勵人認識或購買產品；比純廣告活動廣。","collocations":"product promotion; promotion of a new drink; a promotional campaign.","example":"The drink's promotion combined posters, free samples and a launch discount.","exampleZh":"該飲品的推廣結合了海報、免費試飲及上市折扣。","contrast":"單說一則海報內容是否真實，用 advertising claim 更精確；promotion 可能也包括優惠。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The drink's advertising appeared on posters, in short videos and on sports websites throughout the city.","zh":"該飲品在全市以海報、短片及體育網站進行廣告宣傳。","upgrade":"The drink's promotion appeared on posters, in short videos and on sports websites throughout the city.","answer":"promotion","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"advertising claim","explanation":"一項廣告說法不能概括海報、短片與體育網站三類宣傳渠道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"publicity stunt","explanation":"Stunt 暗示吸睛噱頭；原句只說正常的跨媒介宣傳。"},{"letter":"C","text":"promotion","explanation":"海報、短片及網站上的廣告活動都可用較廣的 promotion 概括。"},{"letter":"D","text":"sales record","explanation":"句中沒有銷量數據，也不能把活動當成銷售紀錄。"},{"letter":"E","text":"sponsorship","explanation":"沒有資助賽事或機構的訊息。"},{"letter":"F","text":"commercial","explanation":"一段播出短片不能概括海報及體育網站上的文字宣傳。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The library's advertising of its new reading club appeared on posters and its website, each inviting readers to a trial session.","zh":"圖書館為新閱讀會所做的廣告出現在海報和網站上，兩者都邀請讀者參加體驗活動。","upgrade":"The library's promotion of its new reading club appeared on posters and its website, each inviting readers to a trial session.","answer":"promotion","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"promotion","explanation":"海報與網站共同邀請讀者試參加閱讀會，屬多渠道推廣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"paid commercial","explanation":"沒有電視或廣播短片，海報及網站文字也不限於一則播出廣告。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicity claim","explanation":"原句談海報和網站邀請，不是在核對某個待查證的聲稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"membership fee","explanation":"句中沒有會費，焦點是邀請讀者試參加。"},{"letter":"E","text":"press release","explanation":"圖書館自行於海報和網站發邀請，未提及向媒體發新聞稿。"},{"letter":"F","text":"poster","explanation":"海報只是其中一種載體，原句還包括圖書館網站上的邀請。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Marketing","meaning":"市場推廣工作","note":"分析目標顧客並決定產品定位、價格、銷售渠道與宣傳；比 advertising 範圍廣。","collocations":"marketing a new product; a marketing strategy; truth in marketing claims.","example":"The firm's marketing plan linked its target audience, price, shops and advertising messages.","exampleZh":"公司的市場推廣計劃把目標顧客、價格、店舖及廣告訊息連在一起。","contrast":"一則不實海報是廣告問題；不能由一張海報推斷整套市場策略的每個部分。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The firm's advertising plan linked its poster messages to customer research, product pricing and the shops chosen to sell the drink.","zh":"公司的廣告計劃把海報訊息與顧客研究、產品定價及銷售店舖連起來。","upgrade":"The firm's marketing plan linked its poster messages to customer research, product pricing and the shops chosen to sell the drink.","answer":"marketing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"poster design","explanation":"只涵蓋海報外觀，不能連同顧客研究、定價和店舖選擇一起描述。"},{"letter":"B","text":"marketing","explanation":"計劃明確連接顧客研究、價格、渠道及海報訊息，marketing plan 能概括這些決策。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicity","explanation":"公眾曝光不涵蓋定價及貨架安排。"},{"letter":"D","text":"sales","explanation":"句子是計劃如何向顧客推介，沒有實際成交或銷量。"},{"letter":"E","text":"sponsorship","explanation":"沒有資助任何賽事或機構。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a commercial","explanation":"一段視聽廣告不能成為涵蓋定價、研究和分銷的整體計劃。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The consumer group asked whether the drink company's advertising in online videos and sponsored posts made truthful claims about the drink.","zh":"消費者組織質疑飲品公司在網上短片及贊助帖文中是否如實描述飲品。","upgrade":"The consumer group asked whether the drink company's marketing in online videos and sponsored posts made truthful claims about the drink.","answer":"marketing","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"journalism","explanation":"這些短片與贊助帖文出自飲品公司，不是新聞機構的獨立報道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"market research","explanation":"市場研究用來了解顧客，不是公司在短片及帖文中對飲品作出的說法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"sales","explanation":"銷售交易不是網上短片及贊助帖文中產品聲稱的名稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"marketing","explanation":"公司透過兩種網上渠道推介飲品；marketing in online videos and sponsored posts 在此可指這些商業說法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"sponsorship","explanation":"Sponsored posts 是付費發布的帖文，sponsorship 本身不是帖文中的產品說法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a poster","explanation":"句中是網上短片及帖文，單張海報既不合渠道也不合不可數名詞結構。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Advertisement / ad：一則訊息與整項活動","zh":"An advertisement 可數，advertising 通常不可數。An advertising 在此義不自然。English contrast: The ad is one message; advertising is the practice.","point":""},{"word":"Public relations：聲譽管理","zh":"Public relations 包括與媒體、社群及持份者建立關係，不等於產品廣告。English contrast: A press interview may build public relations without being a paid ad.","point":""},{"word":"Propaganda：帶立場的宣傳","zh":"Propaganda 常帶政治或操控意味；不能把一般商品廣告一概貼上這個判斷。English contrast: A persuasive drink advert is not automatically propaganda.","point":""},{"word":"Sponsorship：資助與宣傳","zh":"公司贊助賽事可帶來曝光，卻不等於它製作或刊登了廣告。English contrast: Sponsorship can support promotion, but it is a distinct activity.","point":""},{"word":"Sales：宣傳與交易","zh":"看到宣傳不證明有人購買；sales 指出售或銷量。English contrast: Advertising may precede sales.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":83},{"id":"lesson-084","sourceId":15,"headword":"accounting","title":"Accounting","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2012 article says a student joined an accounting firm as an unpaid summer intern. Accounting names the firm’s professional field; the article does not specify that the intern personally kept books or that the firm offered only bookkeeping.","sourceSense":"The 2012 article says a student joined an accounting firm as an unpaid summer intern. Accounting names the firm’s professional field; the article does not specify that the intern personally kept books or that the firm offered only bookkeeping.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["bookkeeping","false for firm label: a narrower service"],["financial record-keeping","false for firm label: task description"],["accountancy","close: British professional field"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： 來源是 accounting firm，故只教授同等專業領域的 accountancy。Bookkeeping 和 financial record-keeping 是較窄任務，不把來源公司擅自縮窄；accounting practice/accountancy practice 是 firm 的近乎同義公司標籤，放在指南搭配，不重複算作另一個概念。單一教學替代詞需獨立覆核。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["accountancy","英式英語常用於專業或行業名稱；accountancy firm 與 accounting firm 在此最接近。","不應由公司名稱推斷實習生具專業資格。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 原文的 accounting firm 只界定公司的會計專業領域，英式英語可改稱 accountancy firm。Bookkeeping 是較窄的記帳工作；auditing 和 tax advisory 只指出其中一類服務，不能在沒有證據時代替整家公司。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"accountancy","meaning":"會計專業","note":"英式英語常用於專業或行業名稱；accountancy firm 與 accounting firm 在此最接近。","collocations":"an accountancy firm; the accountancy profession.","example":"Mira spent the summer at an accountancy firm.","exampleZh":"美拉暑假在一家會計師行度過。","contrast":"不應由公司名稱推斷實習生具專業資格。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"She applied for an internship at an accounting firm that served local businesses.","zh":"她申請在一家為本地企業服務的會計師行實習。","upgrade":"She applied for an internship at an accountancy firm that served local businesses.","answer":"accountancy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"bookkeeping","explanation":"簿記行可能為企業記帳，但原句只說會計師行，沒有把業務限於簿記。"},{"letter":"B","text":"banking","explanation":"銀行可服務本地企業，卻不是原句所指的會計專業公司。"},{"letter":"C","text":"auditing","explanation":"審計行是較窄的服務類別；原句未說這家公司只做審計。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accountability","explanation":"這個字指問責，不能用來命名原句的會計師行。"},{"letter":"E","text":"financial advisory","explanation":"財務顧問也可能服務企業，但不能據此把會計師行改作顧問公司。"},{"letter":"F","text":"accountancy","explanation":"Accountancy firm 在英式英語中保留會計專業公司的範圍，與原句最貼近。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The accounting firm handled both tax returns and independent audits for the charity.","zh":"這家會計師行為慈善機構處理報稅，也進行獨立審計。","upgrade":"The accountancy firm handled both tax returns and independent audits for the charity.","answer":"accountancy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"bookkeeping","explanation":"簿記只涵蓋交易記錄，不能概括報稅與獨立審計兩類專業工作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"tax advisory","explanation":"稅務顧問行可處理報稅，但原句還明說獨立審計，範圍較廣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accountancy","explanation":"Accountancy firm 可同時處理報稅和審計，保留原句的專業領域。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accountability","explanation":"問責是另一概念；處理報稅與審計也不能令「問責」變成會計業務。"},{"letter":"E","text":"financial planning","explanation":"理財規劃不是慈善機構的報稅和獨立審計兩項工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"auditing","explanation":"審計只涵蓋其中一項服務，不能取代同時辦理報稅的會計師行。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"bookkeeping / accounting","zh":"中文辨析： 簿記是記錄交易的一部分；會計行業可包括審核、稅務及分析。","point":"Bookkeeping is narrower than accounting."},{"word":"accountability / accounting","zh":"中文辨析： Accountability 是問責，字形相近卻不是會計。","point":"Similar spelling does not preserve the profession."},{"word":"auditing / accounting","zh":"中文辨析： 審計可屬會計相關專業，但會計師行不一定只做審計。","point":"Auditing is a particular service, not the whole field."},{"word":"banking / accounting","zh":"中文辨析： 銀行業處理金融服務，並非會計專業的同義詞。","point":"A bank and an accounting firm have different primary roles."}],"moduleNumber":84},{"id":"lesson-085","sourceId":23,"headword":"adaptability","title":"Adaptability","titleZh":"適應能力","subtitle":"適應能力","description":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “AQ stands for adaptability quotient.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “AQ stands for adaptability quotient.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["flexibility","near","願意改變方法；可支持適應，但未必證明能在新環境成功運作。"],["ability to adjust","direct paraphrase","清楚說出適應能力；應交代 adjust to 甚麼。"],["resilience","contextual, narrower","受挫後復原的能力；只在變化伴隨挫折而且談及恢復時重疊。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["flexibility","靈活變通：有人能靈活改一次時間，仍未必能在全新環境長期適應。"],["ability to adjust","能作調整的能力：表達能力，而不是某一次已完成的調整；若寫成 adjustment，可能只指一項改動。"],["versatility","多方面應變能力：適應力未必要求已有多項技能；若只談習慣新氣候，不應用 versatility。"],["resilience","受挫後恢復的適應力；有條件：Resilience 不等於一般 adaptability；一個人可以快速換方法，卻未曾面對挫敗。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 描述願意換方法用 flexibility；明說能力用 ability to adjust；跨多種角色技能用 versatility；句子有挫敗後恢復才可用 resilience。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"flexibility","meaning":"靈活變通","note":"名詞，指願意或能夠修改計劃、做法；適應力的一個重要面向。","collocations":"show flexibility; flexibility in changing plans","example":"Her flexibility helped her change study plans after moving schools.","exampleZh":"她的靈活變通使她轉校後能修改讀書計劃。","contrast":"有人能靈活改一次時間，仍未必能在全新環境長期適應。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her adaptability showed when she changed her study plan after the timetable shifted.","zh":"時間表改變後，她修改讀書計劃，顯示出適應能力。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Her flexibility showed when she changed her study plan after the timetable shifted.","answer":"flexibility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"flexibility","explanation":"修改讀書計劃直接顯示變通能力。"},{"letter":"B","text":"resilience","explanation":"沒有挫折後重新站穩的情節，不能精準表達這次變通。"},{"letter":"C","text":"versatility","explanation":"可指多方面本領，但句子只展示一項計劃調整。"},{"letter":"D","text":"willingness to change","explanation":"願意修改計劃是態度，題句則已指出她實際改了計劃。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tolerance of change","explanation":"能忍受變動不等於主動調整讀書方法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"題句沒有測驗或分數，不能把可見的變通說成評分。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The committee’s adaptability showed when it offered both in-person and online workshops after members requested different formats.","zh":"會員希望有不同參與方式，委員會於是同時提供實體和網上工作坊，顯示其應變能力。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The committee’s flexibility showed when it offered both in-person and online workshops after members requested different formats.","answer":"flexibility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"willingness to listen","explanation":"願意聽會員意見不等於已能提供實體與網上兩種形式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"flexibility","explanation":"委員會按會員需要改變原有活動形式，顯示做法靈活。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resilience","explanation":"題句沒有指出活動曾失敗而後恢復，只說委員會配合不同需要。"},{"letter":"D","text":"versatility","explanation":"可指組織具備多方面能力；此處更直接呈現按要求改變活動安排。"},{"letter":"E","text":"compliance","explanation":"單純遵從指令未能說明委員會自行設計兩種參與形式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability rating","explanation":"沒有正式量度委員會表現或給它評級。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"ability to adjust","meaning":"能作調整的能力","note":"白話名詞詞組，表明人能按新環境要求更改做法；常接 to a new situation。","collocations":"the ability to adjust to change; an ability to adjust quickly","example":"Her ability to adjust to the new classroom helped her settle in.","exampleZh":"她能適應新課室環境，因而較快融入。","contrast":"表達能力，而不是某一次已完成的調整；若寫成 adjustment，可能只指一項改動。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"His adaptability to the new school helped him find a workable routine.","zh":"他適應新學校的能力有助找到可行的日常安排。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"His ability to adjust to the new school helped him find a workable routine.","answer":"ability to adjust","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adjustment","explanation":"可指已作的一項改動，未完整表示他的持續能力。"},{"letter":"B","text":"willingness to adjust","explanation":"願意改做法是態度；題句說他已找到可行的新日常安排。"},{"letter":"C","text":"ability to adjust","explanation":"能力名詞可接 to the new school，並解釋可行安排。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ability to recover","explanation":"偏重受挫後復原，題句未提挫折。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"沒有評估或分數，不能把能力說成量化成績。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ability to tolerate change","explanation":"能忍受轉校未必表示能調整生活安排並安頓下來。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The volunteer’s adaptability to changing tasks made her useful at the event.","zh":"義工能適應不斷改變的工作，因此在活動中很有幫助。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The volunteer’s ability to adjust to changing tasks made her useful at the event.","answer":"ability to adjust","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"ability to resist change","explanation":"抗拒工作變動與適應正好相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"willingness to change tasks","explanation":"願意轉任務不保證能實際做好新工作；題句則說她確實有用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"experience across roles","explanation":"過去做過多項工作也未必表示能隨當下變動即時調整。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ability to adjust","explanation":"可接 to changing tasks，指能按任務改變工作方式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"single adjustment","explanation":"只是一項修改，不足以表達持續能力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability rating","explanation":"沒有測量她或給應變能力評級。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"versatility","meaning":"多方面應變能力","note":"具備多種可轉換使用的本領，可在不同任務或角色中發揮；屬較窄的情境替換。","collocations":"versatility across roles; show versatility in different tasks","example":"Her versatility let her help with both planning and translation.","exampleZh":"她的多方面才能使她既能協助籌劃，也能協助翻譯。","contrast":"適應力未必要求已有多項技能；若只談習慣新氣候，不應用 versatility。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her adaptability across several roles let her coordinate, translate and design posters.","zh":"她能適應多種崗位，既可協調、翻譯，也可設計海報。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Her versatility across several roles let her coordinate, translate and design posters.","answer":"versatility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"resilience","explanation":"沒有受挫後復原；題句是多種崗位與本領。"},{"letter":"B","text":"broad interests","explanation":"對多種工作有興趣，不等於已能協調、翻譯和設計。"},{"letter":"C","text":"single-role expertise","explanation":"擅長單一工作不足以概括協調、翻譯及設計。"},{"letter":"D","text":"willingness to learn","explanation":"願意學習不能說明已能勝任三項不同任務。"},{"letter":"E","text":"versatility","explanation":"協調、翻譯及設計三種任務突出多方面應變。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"沒有任何評分，不能換成量化指標。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the host fell ill, the volunteer’s adaptability let her move from editing the programme to introducing speakers on stage.","zh":"主持人患病時，義工憑應變能力由編輯活動手冊轉為在台上介紹講者。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"When the host fell ill, the volunteer’s versatility let her move from editing the programme to introducing speakers on stage.","answer":"versatility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"enthusiasm","explanation":"熱心也許促使她頂替，但不能說明她可做編輯及主持兩種工作。"},{"letter":"B","text":"confidence","explanation":"在台上有自信或許有幫助，卻未概括她也能編輯活動手冊的跨職務能力。"},{"letter":"C","text":"resilience","explanation":"患病的是主持人，義工並非從自己的挫敗中恢復。"},{"letter":"D","text":"single-role expertise","explanation":"她能由幕後編輯轉到台前介紹講者，並非只擅長單一職務。"},{"letter":"E","text":"willingness to switch roles","explanation":"願意頂替是態度，題句更說她實際能完成兩種工作。"},{"letter":"F","text":"versatility","explanation":"從幕後編輯轉到台前主持，顯示她能勝任不同工作。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"resilience","meaning":"受挫後恢復的適應力；有條件","note":"遇到挫敗後重新站穩及繼續應對；只有句子同時說明挫折與恢復才可作有限近義。","collocations":"show resilience after a setback; resilience in the face of change","example":"After her first plan failed, her resilience helped her try a new one.","exampleZh":"第一個計劃失敗後，她憑韌性嘗試新方案。","contrast":"Resilience 不等於一般 adaptability；一個人可以快速換方法，卻未曾面對挫敗。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After two failed attempts, her adaptability helped her recover and try a different approach.","zh":"兩次嘗試失敗後，她靠適應力重整狀態並嘗試不同方法。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After two failed attempts, her resilience helped her recover and try a different approach.","answer":"resilience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"resilience","explanation":"題句同時有失敗及恢復，韌性成為合適的局部改寫。"},{"letter":"B","text":"flexibility","explanation":"可表示改用新方法，但未如 resilience 聚焦兩次失敗後恢復並再試。"},{"letter":"C","text":"versatility","explanation":"題句未顯示多種角色或技能，只談失敗後再試。"},{"letter":"D","text":"willingness to try","explanation":"願意嘗試是態度；題句也有受挫後重新站穩的過程。"},{"letter":"E","text":"endurance","explanation":"可指忍受困難，卻未必表示失敗後復原並改用新方法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"沒有數字或正式測試，不能把人的應對說成評分。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The group’s adaptability mattered after its first event was cancelled: it regrouped and planned another.","zh":"首次活動取消後，小組的適應力很重要：他們重新組隊並籌辦另一場。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The group’s resilience mattered after its first event was cancelled: it regrouped and planned another.","answer":"resilience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"flexibility","explanation":"可表修改計劃，但題句特別指出取消後重新振作，韌性更精準。"},{"letter":"B","text":"resilience","explanation":"活動取消是挫折；重新組隊籌辦另一場是恢復。"},{"letter":"C","text":"versatility","explanation":"沒有各種工作技能的證據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"persistence","explanation":"持續努力可描述再辦活動，但未如 resilience 強調取消這次挫折後重新組織。"},{"letter":"E","text":"willingness to restart","explanation":"願意再開始是態度；題句明說小組已重整並籌辦另一場。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability rating","explanation":"沒有測量小組表現或給予應變能力評級。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Resilience · 韌性不等於一般適應","zh":"中文辨析： 韌性強調受挫後恢復；若只有新時間表而沒有挫敗，應優先談 flexibility 或 ability to adjust。","point":"Resilience is recovery after difficulty; adaptability also covers ordinary change."},{"word":"Adaptability quotient / score · 指標不等於能力","zh":"中文辨析： AQ 可能是描述能力的指標，但題句若無測驗或數字，不應以 score 代替能力名詞。","point":"A score represents an assessment, not the ability itself."},{"word":"Adjustment · 一次修改不等於持續能力","zh":"中文辨析： Adjustment 可以是一項時間表改動；adaptability 是作出適當改動的能力。","point":"An adjustment is a change made; adaptability is a capacity to change."},{"word":"Versatility · 多能須有證據","zh":"中文辨析： 可勝任多種不同角色時可談 versatility；只適應一個新環境不保證多項技能。","point":"Versatility requires varied capabilities, not merely one successful adaptation."}],"moduleNumber":85},{"id":"lesson-086","sourceId":24,"headword":"adaptability quotient","title":"Adaptability quotient","titleZh":"AQ 名稱與指標","subtitle":"AQ 名稱與指標","description":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “AQ stands for adaptability quotient.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2023 年 DSE 4.2〈Adaptability quotient〉： “AQ stands for adaptability quotient.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["adaptability score","conditional","只有真的測得或報告分數時才可描述評分結果；不能推斷原文已有分數。"],["ability to adjust","false","這是被評估的能力，不是 AQ 的名稱或結果。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["AQ","縮寫；同一名稱：AQ 是字母縮寫，不是 ability to adjust；首次使用應先給讀者全稱。"],["measure of adaptability","適應力的衡量指標；解釋性改寫：原文只給縮寫全稱；此說法是解釋性重述，不可用來回答 AQ 的字母逐字代表甚麼。"],["adaptability score","適應力分數；有條件：原始 DSE 句子沒有分數；本詞只適用於新例句已交代測驗及結果時。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 問縮寫全稱可說 AQ；解釋評估用途可說 measure of adaptability；只有語境明確測得數值才說 adaptability score。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"AQ","meaning":"縮寫；同一名稱","note":"在已先寫出全稱並清楚定義的文章中，以 AQ 指代 adaptability quotient。","collocations":"AQ stands for adaptability quotient; an AQ assessment","example":"The article defines AQ as adaptability quotient before using the abbreviation.","exampleZh":"文章先把 AQ 定義為適應力商數，然後才使用縮寫。","contrast":"AQ 是字母縮寫，不是 ability to adjust；首次使用應先給讀者全稱。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The handout defines adaptability quotient on page one. Later, it mentions adaptability quotient again.","zh":"講義在第一頁定義「適應力商數」，其後又提及這個名稱。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The handout defines adaptability quotient on page one. Later, it mentions AQ again.","answer":"AQ","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"AQ","explanation":"已提供全稱，後文用 AQ 可指同一名稱。"},{"letter":"B","text":"IQ","explanation":"指智力相關縮寫，不是本段的適應力商數。"},{"letter":"C","text":"adaptability","explanation":"只指能力，沒有 quotient 的評估名稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"resilience","explanation":"指受挫後復原能力，並非這個縮寫。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adjustment","explanation":"指一次調整，不是縮寫。"},{"letter":"F","text":"score","explanation":"泛指分數，未指明是哪種指標。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The lecturer explains adaptability quotient, then writes “adaptability quotient” as the heading on a short class questionnaire.","zh":"講者解釋了「適應力商數」，然後把「適應力商數」寫成一份簡短課堂問卷的標題。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The lecturer explains adaptability quotient, then writes “AQ” as the heading on a short class questionnaire.","answer":"AQ","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"EQ","explanation":"是另一種商數縮寫，不能標示這份關於 adaptability quotient 的問卷。"},{"letter":"B","text":"AQ","explanation":"全稱已在課堂解釋，簡短標題可用其字母縮寫。"},{"letter":"C","text":"adaptability","explanation":"只說適應能力，漏掉問卷要沿用的 quotient 名稱。"},{"letter":"D","text":"ability to adjust","explanation":"解釋人的能力，卻不是此標題所要求的名稱縮寫。"},{"letter":"E","text":"IQ","explanation":"指另一種商數，不能把問卷題目改成智力。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resilience","explanation":"指受挫後恢復的能力，範圍及名稱都變了。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"measure of adaptability","meaning":"適應力的衡量指標；解釋性改寫","note":"當句子解釋 AQ 的用途，而非逐字展開縮寫時，可說這是一種衡量適應力的指標；不保證某種量表。","collocations":"a measure of adaptability; a proposed measure of adaptability","example":"The researcher described the questionnaire as a measure of adaptability.","exampleZh":"研究者把問卷描述為一種衡量適應力的工具。","contrast":"原文只給縮寫全稱；此說法是解釋性重述，不可用來回答 AQ 的字母逐字代表甚麼。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The lecturer explained that an adaptability quotient is intended to assess how people handle change.","zh":"講者解釋，「適應力商數」旨在評估人如何應對變化。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The lecturer explained that a measure of adaptability is intended to assess how people handle change.","answer":"measure of adaptability","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"ability to adjust","explanation":"只是人的能力，沒有保留「用來衡量」這層意思。"},{"letter":"B","text":"numerical score","explanation":"題句未說此評估必定產生數字。"},{"letter":"C","text":"measure of adaptability","explanation":"講者談評估用途，這是謹慎的解釋性改寫。"},{"letter":"D","text":"single adjustment","explanation":"只是一項行動，非評估工具。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resilience","explanation":"只描述受挫後恢復，範圍太窄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"school grade","explanation":"學校分級並非題句所指適應力評估。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"For a small study of changing tasks, the researcher selected adaptability quotient as one way to assess how participants adjusted; she specified no universal formula.","zh":"在一項研究任務變動的小型調查中，研究者選用「適應力商數」作為評估參加者如何調整的一種方法；她沒有訂出通用公式。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"For a small study of changing tasks, the researcher selected a measure of adaptability as one way to assess how participants adjusted; she specified no universal formula.","answer":"measure of adaptability","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"proven universal scale","explanation":"研究者明說沒有通用公式，不能把所選方法說成普世量尺。"},{"letter":"B","text":"personal willingness","explanation":"是參加者的態度，並非研究者選來評估調整能力的工具。"},{"letter":"C","text":"score out of ten","explanation":"研究句沒有報告十分制，也沒有給個人分數。"},{"letter":"D","text":"measure of adaptability","explanation":"研究者選一種評估調整能力的方法，不擅自補入固定量尺。"},{"letter":"E","text":"ability to adjust","explanation":"是受評估的能力，不是研究者所選的衡量方式。"},{"letter":"F","text":"degree of resilience","explanation":"只聚焦受挫後恢復，研究句談一般任務變動。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"adaptability score","meaning":"適應力分數；有條件","note":"在明確存在評估結果和數值時，指某人得到的分數，而非任何地方都通行的一套 AQ 量尺。","collocations":"receive an adaptability score; compare adaptability scores","example":"The survey gave each participant an adaptability score from zero to twenty.","exampleZh":"調查給每名參加者一個零至二十的適應力分數。","contrast":"原始 DSE 句子沒有分數；本詞只適用於新例句已交代測驗及結果時。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In a classroom survey, each pupil received an adaptability quotient shown as a number out of twenty.","zh":"在一項課堂調查中，每名學生取得一個以二十分為滿分的適應力商數數值。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"In a classroom survey, each pupil received an adaptability score out of twenty.","answer":"adaptability score","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adaptability","explanation":"只指能力，不表示所取得的二十分制數值。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adjustment","explanation":"表示調整行為，不是測驗結果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"AQ definition","explanation":"是名稱解釋，不是個別學生所得數值。"},{"letter":"D","text":"measure of adaptability","explanation":"可指評估工具，但題句聚焦每名學生獲得的數值結果。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"明確有調查及二十分制數值，稱為分數自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"resilience","explanation":"另一種能力，沒有數值結果。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After six weeks of training, the centre reported that each trainee’s adaptability quotient had risen by three points on its own scale.","zh":"六星期培訓後，中心報告每名學員的適應力商數在其自訂量尺上升了三分。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After six weeks of training, the centre reported that each trainee’s adaptability score had risen by three points on its own scale.","answer":"adaptability score","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"universal AQ","explanation":"原句明說是中心自己的量尺，不能因三分變化就推成普世標準。"},{"letter":"B","text":"ability to adapt","explanation":"能力本身不是能在同一量尺上「上升三分」的數值。"},{"letter":"C","text":"adaptability measure","explanation":"可能指評估工具，但題句報告的是每名學員前後的個人得分。"},{"letter":"D","text":"adjustable rating","explanation":"adjustable 是可調節，不表示這裏量到的適應力分數變化。"},{"letter":"E","text":"resilience grade","explanation":"改成挫折復原能力，與中心測量的適應力不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adaptability score","explanation":"「上升三分」明確指同一量尺上的分數變化，而非只說有評估工具。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Ability to adjust · 特質不是指標","zh":"中文辨析： 人能作出調整是能力；AQ 是可用來談或衡量該能力的名稱。兩者不能互換。","point":"The ability is what may be assessed; the quotient names an assessment concept."},{"word":"IQ / EQ · 字母相近不等同","zh":"中文辨析： 商數縮寫可能形式相似，但 AQ 的 A 對應 adaptability；不能任意改成另一種商數。","point":"Similar two-letter labels refer to different concepts."},{"word":"Score · 分數須有實際評分","zh":"中文辨析： 只有明確測量及數字時才可說 adaptability score；原文的縮寫解釋沒有提供數值。","point":"A score needs a stated assessment result; the source only expands an abbreviation."},{"word":"Universal quotient · 不可虛構量尺","zh":"中文辨析： 原文沒有證明 AQ 有全球統一的計算公式。新例句若用自訂量尺，須明說其限定範圍。","point":"Do not infer a standard numerical scale from an expanded term alone."}],"moduleNumber":86},{"id":"lesson-087","sourceId":27,"headword":"addicted to technology","title":"Addicted to technology","titleZh":"科技使用失控的疑慮","subtitle":"科技使用失控的疑慮","description":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 8.3〈Warning Signs You Are Addicted to Technology〉： “Why some Hong Kong teenagers are addicted to technology”","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 8.3〈Warning Signs You Are Addicted to Technology〉： “Why some Hong Kong teenagers are addicted to technology”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["dependent on technology","conditional","也可指上課或工作實際依賴科技；須有不良依賴或失控線索。"],["compulsively using devices","contextual","描寫難控制的重複使用，但把廣義 technology 縮窄至 devices。"],["hooked on digital media","informal, narrower","口語且偏向網絡內容，不涵蓋所有科技用途。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["dependent on technology","依賴科技；須有不良線索：學校規定網上交功課也會造成實際依賴，但不能據此說學生上癮。"],["using devices compulsively","難以自控地反覆使用裝置：Device 比 technology 範圍窄；若原句談整個科技環境，須先確定焦點確是裝置使用。"],["hooked on digital media","沉迷數碼內容；口語且較窄：Digital media 是內容，不等於所有科技；對電子教學平台的正常使用不應套用。"],["struggling to control technology use","難以控制科技使用；審慎改寫：必須有可見的失控線索；每天為上課用平板並不足以支持這說法。"],["hooked on technology","廣義的非正式說法，須有難抽身的線索，不能當成確診。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 有不良依賴證據可說 dependent on technology；具體反覆使用裝置可說 using devices compulsively；聚焦網上內容可說 hooked on digital media，泛指科技則可說 hooked on technology；需審慎描述行為可說 struggling to control technology use。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"dependent on technology","meaning":"依賴科技；須有不良線索","note":"在已指明離開裝置便焦躁、影響日常生活時，可指不健康的依賴。","collocations":"become dependent on technology; unhealthy dependence on devices","example":"Some pupils became dependent on technology and felt unable to function without constant screen access.","exampleZh":"有些學生變得依賴科技，覺得離開屏幕便無法正常生活。","contrast":"學校規定網上交功課也會造成實際依賴，但不能據此說學生上癮。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The discussion describes teenagers who panic whenever their devices are unavailable as addicted to technology.","zh":"討論把一離開裝置便驚慌的青少年形容為沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The discussion describes teenagers who panic whenever their devices are unavailable as dependent on technology.","answer":"dependent on technology","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"dependent on technology","explanation":"焦躁而無法離開裝置，支持不良依賴的描述。"},{"letter":"B","text":"comfortable with technology","explanation":"熟悉使用不表示離開裝置便焦躁或不能過日子。"},{"letter":"C","text":"interested in technology","explanation":"興趣不等於題句強烈依賴。"},{"letter":"D","text":"skilled with devices","explanation":"操作能力與無法短暫離開是兩回事。"},{"letter":"E","text":"reliant on school software","explanation":"學校使用的實際需要不能解釋題句的情緒或生活困難。"},{"letter":"F","text":"frequent technology users","explanation":"只說使用次數，沒有不良依賴。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Some teenagers may be addicted to technology if they feel they cannot manage a normal day without checking a screen constantly.","zh":"若一些青少年覺得不持續查看屏幕便無法正常生活，他們可能過度依賴科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Some teenagers may be dependent on technology if they feel they cannot manage a normal day without checking a screen constantly.","answer":"dependent on technology","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"curious about devices","explanation":"好奇程度太弱，與題句不能不用的感覺不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"dependent on technology","explanation":"「沒有持續查看便難以過日子」是依賴線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"accustomed to carrying phones","explanation":"習慣隨身攜帶不等於不能正常過一天。"},{"letter":"D","text":"afraid of missing messages","explanation":"怕漏訊息是一種擔心，未完整表達生活依賴。"},{"letter":"E","text":"digitally literate","explanation":"懂用數碼工具不等於無法停止查看。"},{"letter":"F","text":"using apps for homework","explanation":"功課用途可合理需要設備，與題句整日離不開不同。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"using devices compulsively","meaning":"難以自控地反覆使用裝置","note":"以行為描述反覆查看或使用裝置的衝動；適合具體談手機、平板等，語氣不作診斷。","collocations":"use devices compulsively; compulsive device use","example":"She was using devices compulsively, reopening the app despite deciding to stop.","exampleZh":"她難以自控地使用裝置，明明決定停止卻仍反覆打開應用程式。","contrast":"Device 比 technology 範圍窄；若原句談整個科技環境，須先確定焦點確是裝置使用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The question calls pupils who repeatedly check phones despite trying to stop addicted to technology.","zh":"問題把想停止卻仍不斷查看手機的學生形容為沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The question says that pupils who repeatedly check phones despite trying to stop are using devices compulsively.","answer":"using devices compulsively","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"using devices frequently","explanation":"使用頻密未必表示想停卻停不了。"},{"letter":"B","text":"using devices for lessons","explanation":"功課用途不能解釋題句反覆使用的失控。"},{"letter":"C","text":"using devices compulsively","explanation":"手機是裝置；想停卻反覆查看支持難自控。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enjoying mobile games","explanation":"喜歡遊戲未必會違背自己的停止決定。"},{"letter":"E","text":"accustomed to devices","explanation":"習慣使用與難以控制頻率不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"keeping devices nearby","explanation":"把裝置放附近不等於不斷重開。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The article asks whether pupils who repeatedly open unrelated apps on their tablets during paper-based revision, without intending to, are addicted to technology.","zh":"文章問有學生在用紙本資料溫習時，不自覺地反覆打開平板上無關的程式，是否沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The article asks whether pupils who repeatedly open unrelated apps on their tablets during paper-based revision, without intending to, are using devices compulsively.","answer":"using devices compulsively","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"choosing to use devices","explanation":"題句說他們並非有意開程式，不能概括成自願選用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"using devices by habit","explanation":"習慣可按計劃維持；這裏是在紙本溫習中不自覺反覆開無關程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"using devices to relax","explanation":"題句沒有安排休息，也沒有說開程式是為放鬆。"},{"letter":"D","text":"using devices compulsively","explanation":"無意間反覆開啟無關程式，支持難以自控地使用平板。"},{"letter":"E","text":"using devices for homework","explanation":"溫習使用紙本資料，打開的程式與之無關。"},{"letter":"F","text":"using devices with permission","explanation":"是否獲准使用，與不自覺反覆打開程式是不同問題。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"hooked on digital media","meaning":"沉迷數碼內容；口語且較窄","note":"當題句具體談網上影片、社交媒體或遊戲內容難以抽身時，這個非正式說法可用。","collocations":"be hooked on digital media; get hooked on online videos","example":"He became hooked on digital media and kept watching short videos after bedtime.","exampleZh":"他沉迷數碼內容，過了睡覺時間仍一直觀看短片。","contrast":"Digital media 是內容，不等於所有科技；對電子教學平台的正常使用不應套用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The speaker describes teens who keep watching short videos long after bedtime as addicted to technology.","zh":"說話者把過了睡覺時間仍一直看短片的青少年形容為沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The speaker describes teens who keep watching short videos long after bedtime as hooked on digital media.","answer":"hooked on digital media","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"hooked on digital media","explanation":"短片屬數碼內容，深夜仍難停止符合口語描述。"},{"letter":"B","text":"interested in digital media","explanation":"有興趣較輕，未包含題句深夜或停不了的持續觀看。"},{"letter":"C","text":"familiar with online content","explanation":"熟悉內容不等於難以抽身。"},{"letter":"D","text":"studying digital media","explanation":"研究內容是學習目的，與題句的反覆瀏覽不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"using media for homework","explanation":"作業用途未見於題句，不能代替沉迷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"watching media occasionally","explanation":"偶爾觀看與題句的持續行為不符。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The discussion asks whether teenagers who repeatedly return to live streams and miss family conversations might be addicted to technology.","zh":"討論問一些青少年反覆返回網上直播，以致錯過與家人交談，會否可能沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The discussion asks whether teenagers who repeatedly return to live streams and miss family conversations might be hooked on digital media.","answer":"hooked on digital media","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"strongly interested in live streams","explanation":"強烈興趣仍未涵蓋反覆返回而錯過家庭交談的不良影響。"},{"letter":"B","text":"hooked on digital media","explanation":"直播屬數碼內容，反覆返回並影響家庭互動支持口語「難以抽身」。"},{"letter":"C","text":"regular viewers of online events","explanation":"定期觀看可自行安排時間，未必錯過與家人的談話。"},{"letter":"D","text":"occasional live-stream viewers","explanation":"偶爾觀看與題句的反覆返回不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"people who follow creators","explanation":"追蹤創作者不必然在家庭談話時一直看直播。"},{"letter":"F","text":"viewers of educational broadcasts","explanation":"節目用途和內容未交代，不能解釋題句的家庭影響。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"struggling to control technology use","meaning":"難以控制科技使用；審慎改寫","note":"直接描述控制使用時間或頻率的困難，避免未經評估便下病名。","collocations":"struggle to control technology use; difficulty controlling screen time","example":"She is struggling to control technology use because she keeps checking her phone during meals.","exampleZh":"她吃飯時不停查看手機，難以控制科技使用。","contrast":"必須有可見的失控線索；每天為上課用平板並不足以支持這說法。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Rather than diagnosing anyone, the teacher says some pupils described as addicted to technology keep checking phones during lessons despite trying to stop.","zh":"老師沒有診斷任何人，只說一些被形容為沉迷科技的學生在課堂上想停卻仍查看手機。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Rather than diagnosing anyone, the teacher says some pupils are struggling to control technology use because they keep checking phones during lessons despite trying to stop.","answer":"struggling to control technology use","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"struggling to control technology use","explanation":"想停卻在課堂上繼續查看，審慎描述可見困難。"},{"letter":"B","text":"spending time online","explanation":"只說在線時間，未保留題句想停仍繼續。"},{"letter":"C","text":"relying on a school platform","explanation":"實用依賴與控制使用時間的困難不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"enjoying new apps","explanation":"喜愛應用程式不等於無法按時收起裝置。"},{"letter":"E","text":"receiving notifications","explanation":"收到提醒是外部事件，不等於失去控制。"},{"letter":"F","text":"studying online","explanation":"網上學習不必然造成失控。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The counsellor asks whether young people called addicted to technology keep losing track of time online despite setting their own screen-time timers.","zh":"輔導員問被稱為沉迷科技的年輕人，即使自己設定屏幕使用計時器，是否仍常常上網到忘記時間。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The counsellor asks whether young people are struggling to control technology use because they keep losing track of time online despite setting their own screen-time timers.","answer":"struggling to control technology use","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"choosing to stay connected","explanation":"主動決定延長上網，未反映自設計時器仍失去時間感。"},{"letter":"B","text":"struggling to control technology use","explanation":"自設計時器仍反覆上網超時，貼合控制使用時間的困難。"},{"letter":"C","text":"preferring a later screen curfew","explanation":"題句沒有說他們想把限制時間改遲。"},{"letter":"D","text":"forgetting to charge devices","explanation":"忘記充電與上網時間超出自己設定的限制無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"relying on online homework","explanation":"課業需要未解釋為何設定計時器後仍常忘記時間。"},{"letter":"F","text":"using phones occasionally","explanation":"偶爾使用不能概括反覆超過自己計劃的上網時間。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"hooked on technology","meaning":"沉迷科技；非正式說法","note":"口語描述某人難以停止使用科技產品或活動；比 hooked on digital media 範圍廣，但仍需有控制困難或不良影響線索。這不是正式診斷。","collocations":"be hooked on technology; become hooked on technology; seem hooked on a device.","example":"His friends worried that he was hooked on technology when he kept reopening apps after deciding to sleep.","exampleZh":"他決定睡覺後仍不斷重開應用程式，朋友因而擔心他沉迷科技。","contrast":"Keen on technology 只可表示有興趣；hooked on technology 暗示難以抽身。不能僅因學生須在網上交功課便套用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After promising to put his phone away for the night, Ian kept reopening its apps; his friends worried he might be addicted to technology.","zh":"阿恩答應晚上收起手機後仍不斷重開應用程式；朋友擔心他可能沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"After promising to put his phone away for the night, Ian kept reopening its apps; his friends worried he might be hooked on technology.","answer":"hooked on technology","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"keen on technology","explanation":"一般興趣不能說明答應收起手機後仍反覆使用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"reliant on technology for school","explanation":"功課需要可造成實際依賴；題句說的是晚上想停卻重開應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"preoccupied with technology","explanation":"可指心裏常想着科技，但未如題句直接指出使用時難以抽身。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accustomed to technology","explanation":"熟習使用與違背自己的停止決定不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"hooked on technology","explanation":"保留朋友的擔憂與非正式語氣，反覆重開為「難以停下」提供線索。"},{"letter":"F","text":"enthusiastic about new apps","explanation":"熱衷新程式仍可自行按時收起手機；題句顯示他想停卻重開。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The speaker asks whether teenagers who repeatedly put on their virtual-reality headsets and miss planned club meetings could be addicted to technology.","zh":"說話者問一些青少年反覆使用虛擬實境頭戴裝置，因而錯過已安排的學會活動，會否可能沉迷科技。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The speaker asks whether teenagers who repeatedly put on their virtual-reality headsets and miss planned club meetings could be hooked on technology.","answer":"hooked on technology","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"merely interested in devices","explanation":"普通興趣不足以說明反覆返回頭戴裝置並錯過學會活動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"familiar with virtual reality","explanation":"熟悉技術不等於使用到影響已安排的活動。"},{"letter":"C","text":"keen on immersive games","explanation":"熱衷遊戲未必使人錯過多次既定的社交活動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"absorbed in one virtual-reality session","explanation":"只說一次投入，沒有概括反覆使用及持續影響。"},{"letter":"E","text":"regular headset users","explanation":"規律使用未必有題句所見的活動受影響情況。"},{"letter":"F","text":"hooked on technology","explanation":"反覆返回虛擬實境裝置而錯過既定活動，支持可能難以抽身的口語描述。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Dependence · 實用依賴不等於失控","zh":"中文辨析： 用電子平台交功課會依賴設備，但不證明學生難以控制使用；要看具體不良行為。","point":"Practical reliance on school devices does not establish uncontrolled use."},{"word":"Digital media · 範圍較窄","zh":"中文辨析： 影片及社交動態是數碼內容；technology 也包含其他工具，不能一概改成 digital media。","point":"Digital media names content, not every kind of technology."},{"word":"Heavy use · 時間長不足夠","zh":"中文辨析： 每天長時間為學習使用電腦未必有問題；須分清用途、影響及控制能力。","point":"Time spent alone does not show loss of control."},{"word":"Diagnosis · 討論題非診斷","zh":"中文辨析： 原文是討論題，並未提供專業評估；練習避免將任何個別青少年確診。","point":"A discussion prompt does not diagnose an individual."},{"word":"Hooked / keen · 口語強度","zh":"中文辨析： 反覆想停仍使用時可說 hooked on technology；keen on technology 只表示喜愛，不能概括自控困難。","point":"Hooked on suggests hard-to-resist use; keen on can mean ordinary enthusiasm."}],"moduleNumber":87},{"id":"lesson-088","sourceId":29,"headword":"adding subtitles","title":"Adding subtitles","titleZh":"為節目加字幕","subtitle":"為節目加字幕","description":"原文： 2025 年 DSE 7.2〈Young people love subtitles; older people, not so much〉討論題包括 “benefits of adding subtitles to the programmes” 及學生是否歡迎為節目加字幕。","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 年 DSE 7.2〈Young people love subtitles; older people, not so much〉討論題包括 “benefits of adding subtitles to the programmes” 及學生是否歡迎為節目加字幕。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["providing captions","near / conditional","captions 與 subtitles 均可顯示口語；前者在無障礙語境也可能包含音效及說話者資訊，不可反推原文必有那些資料。"],["putting text on screen","false unless specified","畫面文字也可能是標題、廣告或比分；須限定為 spoken dialogue。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["providing captions","提供輔助字幕；可含音效：一般 subtitles 可只轉寫或翻譯對白；captions 可能涵蓋更多聲音資訊，不能反推原文必然如此。"],["subtitling the programmes","為節目製作字幕；動名詞改寫：不是 adding titles；titles 可能只是節目名稱。必須用及物動詞 subtitle 接節目。"],["displaying spoken dialogue on screen","在畫面顯示口語對白；描述性改寫：只表示對白內容，未必含非語音音效；若是字幕翻譯，可補明目標語言。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 畫面文字呈現說話可說 providing captions；若另標音效，也可以這樣稱呼，但不能反推原題必有音效。一般替換動名詞片語可用 subtitling the programmes；要用白話明確表達功能，可說 displaying spoken dialogue on screen。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"providing captions","meaning":"提供輔助字幕；可含音效","note":"在節目播放時以畫面文字顯示說話，可用 captions；在無障礙語境中也可能標明說話者和音效，但原題沒有保證這些額外資料。","collocations":"provide captions for programmes; captions for speech and sounds","example":"Providing captions for the programme helped viewers follow dialogue and sound cues.","exampleZh":"為節目提供輔助字幕，有助觀眾掌握對白及聲音提示。","contrast":"一般 subtitles 可只轉寫或翻譯對白；captions 可能涵蓋更多聲音資訊，不能反推原文必然如此。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The channel is adding subtitles that show dialogue and label doorbell sounds for viewers who cannot hear them.","zh":"頻道加上顯示對白並標明門鈴聲的字幕，方便聽不到聲音的觀眾。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The channel is providing captions that show dialogue and label doorbell sounds for viewers who cannot hear them.","answer":"providing captions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"providing captions","explanation":"字幕同時顯示說話和門鈴聲，符合輔助字幕。"},{"letter":"B","text":"providing dialogue subtitles only","explanation":"只呈現對白，漏掉題句的門鈴或音效標示。"},{"letter":"C","text":"translating the dialogue","explanation":"翻譯說話未必顯示聲音提示或說話者。"},{"letter":"D","text":"publishing a transcript","explanation":"逐字稿可另頁展示，未必同步在畫面。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adding programme titles","explanation":"節目名稱並非同步對白及音效。"},{"letter":"F","text":"dubbing the voices","explanation":"配音增加或替換聲音，沒有文字聲音提示。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The school is adding subtitles to its live debate stream; the text appears as each pupil speaks and identifies the speaker.","zh":"學校正為辯論直播加上字幕；每名學生發言時，文字同步出現並標明說話者。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The school is providing captions for its live debate stream; the text appears as each pupil speaks and identifies the speaker.","answer":"providing captions","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"publishing a transcript after the debate","explanation":"事後逐字稿不能讓直播觀眾在發言當下讀到內容。"},{"letter":"B","text":"providing captions","explanation":"直播中同步呈現說話文字及說話者，符合這裏的字幕用途。"},{"letter":"C","text":"translating the debate in a later newsletter","explanation":"之後刊登譯文，不是直播畫面同步文字。"},{"letter":"D","text":"identifying speakers without showing their words","explanation":"只有姓名仍無法讀到辯論內容。"},{"letter":"E","text":"adding a title card before the debate","explanation":"片頭標題不會跟隨每名學生發言出現。"},{"letter":"F","text":"dubbing the pupils’ voices","explanation":"改換聲音不是提供可閱讀的同步字幕。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"subtitling the programmes","meaning":"為節目製作字幕；動名詞改寫","note":"用動詞 subtitle 的 -ing 形式，指為節目製作及加上對白文字，語法上可取代 adding subtitles to。","collocations":"subtitle a programme; subtitling the programmes","example":"Subtitling the programmes made their interviews easier to follow in a noisy room.","exampleZh":"為那些節目製作字幕，令觀眾在嘈雜房間也較易跟上當中的訪問。","contrast":"不是 adding titles；titles 可能只是節目名稱。必須用及物動詞 subtitle 接節目。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The school is adding subtitles to the programmes so pupils can read the dialogue.","zh":"學校正為節目加上字幕，好讓學生閱讀對白。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The school is subtitling the programmes so pupils can read the dialogue.","answer":"subtitling the programmes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adding opening titles","explanation":"只加片頭名稱，不能讓觀眾逐句讀對白。"},{"letter":"B","text":"publishing a transcript","explanation":"可能是另頁文字，非播放時同步字幕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"subtitling the programmes","explanation":"以動名詞表示為節目加上對白字幕，保留目的。"},{"letter":"D","text":"dubbing the programmes","explanation":"更換聲軌，不是製作畫面文字。"},{"letter":"E","text":"summarising the programmes","explanation":"摘要不會呈現每句台詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"translating speech off-screen","explanation":"畫面外翻譯不保證觀眾看見同步文字。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before distributing its wildlife series abroad, the broadcaster is adding subtitles in Spanish to the programmes for local viewers.","zh":"廣播機構在海外發行野生動物系列節目前，正為節目加上西班牙文字幕，供當地觀眾觀看。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Before distributing its wildlife series abroad, the broadcaster is subtitling the programmes in Spanish for local viewers.","answer":"subtitling the programmes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"publishing a Spanish synopsis with the series","explanation":"西班牙文簡介可介紹節目，卻不會在播放時逐句顯示文字。"},{"letter":"B","text":"translating the scripts for the distributor","explanation":"譯好的劇本只供發行商閱讀；題句要求觀眾在節目畫面看到字幕。"},{"letter":"C","text":"dubbing the programmes in Spanish","explanation":"配音製作西班牙文聲軌，與原句加上可讀文字不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"subtitling the programmes","explanation":"為海外發行的節目製作西班牙文畫面字幕，保留翻譯及播放用途。"},{"letter":"E","text":"recording Spanish narration","explanation":"錄製旁白仍是聲音，並非畫面上的西班牙文字幕。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adding Spanish opening titles only","explanation":"只翻譯片頭名稱，無法讓當地觀眾閱讀節目內容。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"displaying spoken dialogue on screen","meaning":"在畫面顯示口語對白；描述性改寫","note":"把字幕的核心功能說清楚：節目播放時在畫面上呈現其說話文字；比「放文字」精準。","collocations":"display spoken dialogue on screen; display speech as on-screen text","example":"Displaying spoken dialogue on screen helped viewers understand the interview.","exampleZh":"在畫面顯示口語對白，有助觀眾理解訪問內容。","contrast":"只表示對白內容，未必含非語音音效；若是字幕翻譯，可補明目標語言。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The broadcaster is adding subtitles to an archived interview; they reproduce the speakers’ words for viewers replaying it.","zh":"廣播機構正為一段存檔訪問加上字幕，方便重看錄影的觀眾閱讀說話者的原話。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The broadcaster is displaying spoken dialogue on screen during the archived interview for viewers replaying it.","answer":"displaying spoken dialogue on screen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"displaying spoken dialogue on screen","explanation":"題句明說把說話文字同步呈現於訪問畫面。"},{"letter":"B","text":"putting any text on screen","explanation":"太籠統，比分或廣告也符合，未明確指對白。"},{"letter":"C","text":"displaying programme titles","explanation":"節目名稱不是正在說的話。"},{"letter":"D","text":"publishing a separate script","explanation":"另頁劇本不是同步畫面文字。"},{"letter":"E","text":"translating speech orally","explanation":"口譯是聲音，不是觀眾可讀的畫面文字。"},{"letter":"F","text":"showing a summary","explanation":"摘要無法逐句對應說話。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The theatre is adding subtitles to its live-streamed play; each line appears at the moment an actor speaks.","zh":"劇院正為戲劇直播加上字幕；演員說出每句台詞時，相應文字便同步出現。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The theatre is displaying spoken dialogue on screen during its live-streamed play, timing each line to the actor’s speech.","answer":"displaying spoken dialogue on screen","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"publishing a transcript before the performance","explanation":"預先公開逐字稿，不能在演員發言當刻逐句同步顯示。"},{"letter":"B","text":"displaying spoken dialogue on screen","explanation":"戲劇直播中的台詞與畫面文字即時對應，正是題句的做法。"},{"letter":"C","text":"projecting scene summaries between acts","explanation":"幕間摘要沒有同步呈現每句正在說的話。"},{"letter":"D","text":"translating the actors’ speech orally","explanation":"口譯提供聲音，而非直播畫面上的可讀文字。"},{"letter":"E","text":"showing only actor names on screen","explanation":"只見姓名，觀眾仍讀不到演員的台詞。"},{"letter":"F","text":"publishing subtitles after the performance","explanation":"事後字幕錯過了題句強調的直播同步時點。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Captions / subtitles · 重疊但有邊界","zh":"中文辨析： 兩者都可呈現說話；captions 常可另標說話者及音效。原題未明示音效，不能當成原文事實。","point":"Captions may carry sound and speaker information beyond dialogue subtitles."},{"word":"Titles · 標題不是字幕","zh":"中文辨析： Programme title、opening title 是名稱或片頭，沒有把正在說的話同步變成文字。","point":"A title names a programme; subtitles track speech."},{"word":"Transcript · 文字稿未必在畫面","zh":"中文辨析： 逐字稿可另頁閱讀；adding subtitles 指節目播放時畫面上呈現文字。","point":"A transcript can be separate from the video image."},{"word":"Dubbing · 換聲音不等於加文字","zh":"中文辨析： 配音以另一聲軌呈現說話；字幕保留可閱讀的畫面文字。","point":"Dubbing changes or adds voices, while subtitling adds text."}],"moduleNumber":88},{"id":"lesson-089","sourceId":32,"headword":"adulthood","title":"Adulthood","titleZh":"成年階段","subtitle":"成年階段","description":"2025 年 DSE Speaking 2.2〈American teenagers today are driving less than their parents did〉說，從前駕駛執照被看作 “a sign of adulthood”：年輕人不再是孩子，能自行出行而不倚賴別人。這裏的 adulthood 是不可數名詞，指由童年走向成年的人生階段；駕照是象徵，不能單憑持照斷定持有人已具成熟判斷。以下例句與練習均為原創。","sourceSense":"2025 年 DSE Speaking 2.2〈American teenagers today are driving less than their parents did〉說，從前駕駛執照被看作 “a sign of adulthood”：年輕人不再是孩子，能自行出行而不倚賴別人。這裏的 adulthood 是不可數名詞，指由童年走向成年的人生階段；駕照是象徵，不能單憑持照斷定持有人已具成熟判斷。以下例句與練習均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["adult life","可教的階段近義","指成年後的生活；a sign of adult life 可理解，但談成人身分的里程碑時 adulthood 較自然。"],["maturity","不可無條件替換","可指心智成熟或生理成熟；駕照及出行自主不證明審慎或穩重。"],["grown-up years","不優先教","可理解為成年歲月，但書面英語通常說 adult years；不能直接改寫 a sign of adulthood。"],["adult years","補充主要近義","自然指成年後的一段歲月；須改寫 sign of adulthood 之類身分象徵句。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","焦點","選用條件"],"rows":[["adulthood","成年階段或成人身分","可談里程碑：a sign of adulthood。"],["adult life","成年後的日常生活","可談準備、工作與自理。"],["adult years","成年後的一段時期","可談回憶或一般人生歷程；不宜硬接 a sign of。"],["maturity","心智或生理成熟","須有此特質的證據，不能由駕照直接推定。"]],"note":"選詞規則： 說「進入成人階段」用 adulthood；說「成年後怎樣生活」可用 adult life；說一段成年歲月可用 adult years。駕照象徵自主，不是成熟度測試。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Adult Life","meaning":"成年生活","note":"指成年階段的日常生活與責任；當語境討論成年後的生活方式或自主能力時，可改述 adulthood。","collocations":"prepare for adult life; adjust to adult life; independence in adult life; the start of adult life.","example":"Learning to plan a journey alone can help teenagers prepare for adult life.","exampleZh":"學習獨自規劃行程，有助青少年為成年生活作準備。","contrast":"Adult life 偏向生活經驗；adulthood 也可抽象地指法律或社會上的成年階段。Maturity 評價發展或判斷，不等同生活時段。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Before leaving school, Hana learnt to budget and cook so that she would be ready for adulthood.","zh":"離校前，花奈學習理財和煮食，好讓自己為成年生活作好準備。","upgrade":"Before leaving school, Hana learnt to budget and cook so that she would be ready for adult life.","answer":"adult life","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"maturity","explanation":"理財和煮食有助自理，但句子談的是將要進入的生活階段，並非證明她判斷成熟。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adolescence","explanation":"離校前的花奈已在青春期；她正在準備的是其後的生活。"},{"letter":"C","text":"legal adulthood","explanation":"句中沒有指某地法定成年年齡或法律權利。"},{"letter":"D","text":"adult life","explanation":"理財與煮食直接關乎成年後的日常生活，保留 ready for 的自然搭配。"},{"letter":"E","text":"childhood","explanation":"她快要離校，並非為童年生活作準備。"},{"letter":"F","text":"parenthood","explanation":"學習理財和煮食可為成年人自理作準備，但句子沒有說花奈將成為父母。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The workshop discusses how paying rent and arranging travel become part of adulthood.","zh":"工作坊探討支付租金和安排出行如何成為成年生活的一部分。","upgrade":"The workshop discusses how paying rent and arranging travel become part of adult life.","answer":"adult life","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a driving licence","explanation":"交租與安排出行不屬於一張駕照的組成部分。"},{"letter":"B","text":"adult life","explanation":"工作坊談多項成年人日常事務，part of adult life 自然概括。"},{"letter":"C","text":"mature behaviour","explanation":"交租可反映負責任，然而安排生活事項並不直接等於心智成熟。"},{"letter":"D","text":"legal age","explanation":"年齡是一個數字或資格門檻，交租與出行不是「年齡的一部分」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"teenage freedom","explanation":"工作坊提及交租等成年責任，並非只談青少年自由。"},{"letter":"F","text":"childhood","explanation":"支付自己的租金與原句所談的成年生活相反。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Adult Years","meaning":"成年歲月","note":"指成年後的一段歲月，可用於回憶或一般人生歷程；比抽象的 adulthood 更突出時間跨度。","collocations":"during her adult years; throughout his adult years; in their adult years.","example":"She spent her adult years in a city where she rarely needed a car.","exampleZh":"她的成年歲月是在一座很少需要開車的城市度過的。","contrast":"Adult years 很適合說一段生活時期；a sign of adult years 不如 a sign of adulthood 自然，因後者強調步入成年身分。Grown-up years 可理解，但通常不如 adult years 地道。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Looking back, my aunt said she spent most of her adulthood travelling by train.","zh":"回顧過去，姨姨說她成年後的大部分歲月都靠火車出行。","upgrade":"Looking back, my aunt said she spent most of her adult years travelling by train.","answer":"adult years","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"growing years","explanation":"Growing years 容易令人想到成長中的童年或青少年期，與姨姨回顧成年時期不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"mature decisions","explanation":"句子記述多年乘火車的生活，不是在點評某些決定是否成熟。"},{"letter":"C","text":"age of majority","explanation":"Age of majority 是達到法定成年的年齡門檻，不能說姨姨把大部分門檻歲數花在乘火車上。"},{"letter":"D","text":"school years","explanation":"姨姨談的是成年後大部分時間，不能限定為在校歲月。"},{"letter":"E","text":"independent travel","explanation":"出行方式是成年歲月裏的一件事，並非時間段本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"adult years","explanation":"自然表示她成年後的多年時期，與回顧語境及 spent most of her 相配。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In adulthood, people may change careers more than once as their interests and circumstances change.","zh":"成年後，人們可能隨着興趣和環境改變，不止一次轉換職業。","upgrade":"In their adult years, people may change careers more than once as their interests and circumstances change.","answer":"adult years","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"adult years","explanation":"In their adult years 指成年後漫長的一段時期，適合談可能不止一次的職業轉換。"},{"letter":"B","text":"schooldays","explanation":"轉換職業談的是成年工作歷程，不能限於在校歲月。"},{"letter":"C","text":"legal age","explanation":"Legal age 是法律年齡門檻，不是一段可多次轉職的時間。"},{"letter":"D","text":"independence","explanation":"獨立可能伴隨轉職，但本句要標示人生階段，不是抽象自主狀態。"},{"letter":"E","text":"old age","explanation":"成年時期不等於老年；人們可能在成年早期或中期改行。"},{"letter":"F","text":"maturity","explanation":"心智成熟不等於成年多年時間；轉職次數也不能證明判斷成熟。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"人生階段與心智判斷 · Maturity","zh":"學生得到駕照，可能更獨立，卻未必已具審慎判斷。Maturity 在談理智或責任感時才貼切；adulthood 在本文是「不再是孩子」的階段。English contrast: A sign of adult status is not proof of mature judgment.","point":""},{"word":"法律門檻與象徵 · Legal adulthood / driving eligibility","zh":"不同地方申領駕照的年齡與成年法定年齡未必相同。原句說 considered a sign，是在報告人們對自由出行的看法，不是制定法律定義。若題目專論某地法定成年門檻，才可用 legal adulthood。English contrast: A cultural marker and a legal threshold are different claims.","point":""},{"word":"童年、青春期與成年 · Childhood / adolescence","zh":"Childhood 是童年，adolescence 是過渡中的青春期；兩者均不是原句所指的成年階段。若討論青少年尚未取得駕照的生活，adolescence 才可能是主題。English contrast: These terms name other life stages.","point":""},{"word":"成人身分與成人責任 · Responsibility / independence","zh":"獨立出行是原文提到的成年象徵之一，independence 是能力或狀態，responsibility 是責任；兩者都不等於整個成年期。若句子只談「能自行乘車」，可用 independence，不能無條件替換 adulthood。English contrast: A feature of a stage is not the stage itself.","point":""},{"word":"Adult years / grown-up years：常用搭配與語體","zh":"Adult years 是描述成年歲月的自然寫法；grown-up years 雖能理解，卻較不常用，不能把它當成更地道的教材首選。English contrast: Adult years is the idiomatic time-period phrase; grown-up years is an informal, less natural alternative.","point":""}],"moduleNumber":89},{"id":"lesson-090","sourceId":44,"headword":"after-school hangouts","title":"After-school hangouts","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2016 set 4.2 magazine extract is titled “After-School Hangouts” and lists a café, the Space Museum, Hong Kong Park, and a cooking shop. The group prompt asks the Peer Counselling team to present places where students can socialise after school. Hangouts therefore names possible places, not the act of hanging out. The item does not say every listed place is free, open every evening, or a regular meeting point for every student.","sourceSense":"The 2016 set 4.2 magazine extract is titled “After-School Hangouts” and lists a café, the Space Museum, Hong Kong Park, and a cooking shop. The group prompt asks the Peer Counselling team to present places where students can socialise after school. Hangouts therefore names possible places, not the act of hanging out. The item does not say every listed place is free, open every evening, or a regular meeting point for every student.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["places to gather after class","Venue meaning fits, but after class can mean between lessons; repair to after school to preserve the source timing."],["after-class meeting spots","Meeting-place meaning fits only when students actually meet there; after-class may mean a break within the school day. Teach after-school meeting spots with a regular meeting condition."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： After-school social venues adds the organised place viewpoint and is taught. Hangout spots merely repeats the headword's root and adds little. After-school destinations could include a solitary errand and therefore does not itself preserve the source's socialising purpose. Places to spend time after school also permits being alone; it is a broader paraphrase, usable only when the sentence retains friends or socialising. The location/activity distinction is developed below rather than padded with duplicate place phrases."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["places to gather after school","直接列舉朋友在整個上課日結束後可聚集的地方。","After class 可能只是上午一節課後；地點不是活動或朋友本人。"],["after-school meeting spots","某隊員定期或約定在一處碰頭，可隨時間更換固定地點。","一次性的參觀景點未必是慣常 meeting spot。"],["after-school social venues","從開放時間、座位及交談合適度評估可接待學生的場所。","Venue 不等於社交活動、學校批准或免費入場。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 只需說公園、咖啡店等「放學後可聚集的地方」，用 places to gather after school；若是朋友約定或每週重複碰頭處，用 after-school meeting spots；比較座位、時間等場所條件，用 after-school social venues。來源標題指地點，且時間是整個上課日結束後。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"places to gather after school","meaning":"放學後聚集的地方","note":"直接描述學生在整個上課日結束後可與其他人聚集的地方，適合列舉不同類型地點。","collocations":"places to gather after school; a place where friends gather after school; gather at a park or café.","example":"The peer counsellors suggested several places to gather after school, including a park and a library room.","exampleZh":"同伴輔導員提議了幾個放學後可聚集的地方，包括公園及圖書館活動室。","contrast":"After class 可能指上午一節課結束後的休息時間；來源談放學後。此片語不保證地點免費或安全合適。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The peer counsellors recommended the park, café and library room as after-school hangouts for classmates.","zh":"同伴輔導員推薦公園、咖啡店和圖書館活動室，作為同學放學後聚集的地方。","upgrade":"The peer counsellors recommended the park, café and library room as places to gather after school.","answer":"places to gather after school","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"after-school activities","explanation":"公園、咖啡店和活動室是地方；活動是學生在那裏做的事。"},{"letter":"B","text":"friends to meet after school","explanation":"句中列出三個地點，不是要見面的同學。"},{"letter":"C","text":"places to gather after school","explanation":"保留三個供同學聚集的地點，以及標題所說的放學後時段。"},{"letter":"D","text":"places to gather between classes","explanation":"Between classes 是兩節課之間；原句說的是 after-school 地點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"free school facilities","explanation":"咖啡店未必由學校營運，也沒有三處都免費的資料。"},{"letter":"F","text":"quiet places to study alone","explanation":"來源例句安排同學見面，不是獨自溫習；咖啡店也未必安靜。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The guide labels the square and community hall as after-school hangouts for friends to meet at 4 p.m., but excludes a corridor used only during the 11 a.m. break.","zh":"指南把廣場和社區會堂列作朋友下午四時聚會的放學後去處，卻沒有把只在上午十一時小息使用的走廊列入。","upgrade":"The guide labels the square and community hall as places to gather after school at 4 p.m., but excludes a corridor used only during the 11 a.m. break.","answer":"places to gather after school","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"meeting places during lessons","explanation":"下午四時見面是在放學後，不是上課時。"},{"letter":"B","text":"after-class waiting corridors","explanation":"走廊正被排除；after class 也可能指上午十一時一節課後的小息。"},{"letter":"C","text":"free public attractions","explanation":"指南沒有說廣場和會堂都免費，也不是在評旅遊景點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"places to gather after school","explanation":"下午四時朋友聚集與上午十一時課間走廊形成清楚時間對比。"},{"letter":"E","text":"organised school activities","explanation":"廣場和會堂是可聚會的地點，未說學校已籌辦活動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"places to spend time alone","explanation":"句子特意說朋友聚會，而非獨處。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"after-school meeting spots","meaning":"放學後會面地點","note":"朋友約定在放學後碰頭的特定地方，常帶經常使用或容易認出的意味。","collocations":"a usual after-school meeting spot; change an after-school meeting spot; meet friends at the spot.","example":"The café beside the station became the team's usual after-school meeting spot.","exampleZh":"車站旁的咖啡店成了隊員慣常放學後會面的地方。","contrast":"一次性的博物館參觀可屬放學後去處，卻未必是固定 meeting spot；應有約定或重複會面的線索。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The debate team called the same café one of its after-school hangouts because members met there to chat every Thursday before going home.","zh":"辯論隊把同一間咖啡店稱作放學後聚會地點之一，因為隊員每逢星期四回家前都在那裏聊天。","upgrade":"The debate team called the same café one of its after-school meeting spots because members met there to chat every Thursday before going home.","answer":"after-school meeting spots","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one-off field-trip destinations","explanation":"每逢星期四在同一咖啡店見面，不是一次性的參觀行程。"},{"letter":"B","text":"after-school meeting spots","explanation":"Meeting spot 對應隊員約定每週在同一咖啡店碰頭，亦保留放學後時段。"},{"letter":"C","text":"club meeting times","explanation":"星期四是時間，咖啡店是地點，不能把地點改作時間。"},{"letter":"D","text":"quiet study rooms","explanation":"句子說隊員聊天，且地點是咖啡店，未說安靜溫習。"},{"letter":"E","text":"café menus","explanation":"菜單列飲食項目，不是隊員碰頭的地點。"},{"letter":"F","text":"school-approved venues","explanation":"隊員常去不代表學校正式批准該店。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"When the station entrance became too crowded, the club moved its weekly gathering to the square; both places served as after-school hangouts in different terms.","zh":"車站入口變得太擠迫後，社團把每週聚會移到廣場；這兩個地方在不同學期都曾是放學後會面地點。","upgrade":"When the station entrance became too crowded, the club moved its weekly gathering to the square; both places served as after-school meeting spots in different terms.","answer":"after-school meeting spots","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"one-day excursion sites","explanation":"社團每週聚會，並非只到兩處各參觀一天。"},{"letter":"B","text":"school classrooms","explanation":"車站入口和廣場均不是課室。"},{"letter":"C","text":"meeting schedules","explanation":"句子說從一個地方移往另一個地方，沒有改變每週聚會日程的資料。"},{"letter":"D","text":"pedestrian routes","explanation":"車站入口和廣場可在步行路線上，但此處功能是固定約見隊員。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tourist attractions","explanation":"人群擠迫不表示車站入口是景點；句子談社團常用會面處。"},{"letter":"F","text":"after-school meeting spots","explanation":"兩處在不同學期先後充當每週放學後聚會的約定地點，保留變更過程。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"after-school social venues","meaning":"放學後社交場所","note":"從設施或營運場所的角度稱呼適合學生放學後一起交談、參與活動的地點；比泛稱 place 稍正式。","collocations":"after-school social venues; choose a social venue; venues for pupils to meet friends.","example":"The youth centre and café were proposed as after-school social venues for small groups of friends.","exampleZh":"青年中心和咖啡店被提議作為小群朋友放學後的社交場所。","contrast":"Venue 強調可接待人的場所；不是社交活動本身，也不表示所有地點都由學校批准。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The youth centre and café, each with seating for groups to talk, were suggested as after-school hangouts for pupils to meet friends.","zh":"青年中心和咖啡店都有可供群體聊天的座位，因此被建議作為學生放學後與朋友見面的社交場所。","upgrade":"The youth centre and café, each with seating for groups to talk, were suggested as after-school social venues for pupils to meet friends.","answer":"after-school social venues","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"after-school social events","explanation":"青年中心和咖啡店是場所；學生在那裏進行的活動才是 event。"},{"letter":"B","text":"school-approved centres","explanation":"兩處只是被提議，沒有學校正式批准的資料；咖啡店也不是 centre。"},{"letter":"C","text":"private study rooms","explanation":"有座位讓群體聊天，不是私人獨處的溫習室。"},{"letter":"D","text":"admission-free buildings","explanation":"句子沒有說兩處都免收費。"},{"letter":"E","text":"after-school social venues","explanation":"Social venues 抓住兩個可接待朋友聚談的場所與放學後用途。"},{"letter":"F","text":"club timetables","explanation":"時間表列活動安排，不能代替青年中心和咖啡店這兩處地方。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The newsletter compared possible after-school hangouts by their opening hours, group seating and whether teenagers could talk there without disturbing others.","zh":"通訊按開放時間、團體座位，以及青少年能否在不打擾別人的情況下交談，比較不同的放學後社交場所。","upgrade":"The newsletter compared possible after-school social venues by their opening hours, group seating and whether teenagers could talk there without disturbing others.","answer":"after-school social venues","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"after-school social venues","explanation":"開放時間、群體座位與能否交談都是挑選社交場所的條件；通訊正比較可用的地點。"},{"letter":"B","text":"after-school activity schedules","explanation":"時間表不會有團體座位，也不是青少年可以在其中交談的地方。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unsupervised private homes","explanation":"原句沒有說是私人住家或無人看管，不能由「可交談」推斷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"single-use excursion tickets","explanation":"門票不是有開放時間與座位配置的場所。"},{"letter":"E","text":"quiet individual study tasks","explanation":"通訊在比較供青少年聚談的地點，不是個人功課。"},{"letter":"F","text":"free school facilities","explanation":"沒有說候選地點由學校營運或免費。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"hangout / hanging out","zh":"中文辨析： Hangout 在來源是可去的地方；hanging out 是朋友相處的活動，不能拿活動代替公園或咖啡店。","point":"The park is a hangout; spending time in the park is hanging out."},{"word":"after class / after school","zh":"中文辨析： 上午一節課下課後仍在上課日內；來源明說 after school，指放學後。","point":"A break between lessons is not the end of the school day."},{"word":"meeting spot / one-off destination","zh":"中文辨析： 一次性的博物館參觀可以是放學後去處，但未必是朋友慣常約定碰頭的地點。","point":"A destination for one visit need not be a regular meeting spot."},{"word":"free place / social venue","zh":"中文辨析： 來源咖啡店部分設施收費；把社交場所一概改寫成「免費地點」會增添錯誤資訊。","point":"A place to socialise may charge admission or for services."},{"word":"school-approved / suggested","zh":"中文辨析： 來源供學生討論和建議地點，不等於學校已批准每個地點或所有活動。","point":"A suggested venue is not automatically an officially approved one."}],"moduleNumber":90},{"id":"lesson-091","sourceId":45,"headword":"afternoon naps","title":"Afternoon naps","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"The 2024 Health Club prompt asks about the benefits of taking afternoon naps and whether they should be included in the school timetable. The accompanying material discusses a short daytime nap and sleeping pods. A nap involves actual sleep; merely resting with eyes closed is broader. Afternoon specifies the part of the day. The prompt invites discussion, not an assertion that every pupil should nap or that every length of nap has the same effect.","sourceSense":"The 2024 Health Club prompt asks about the benefits of taking afternoon naps and whether they should be included in the school timetable. The accompanying material discusses a short daytime nap and sleeping pods. A nap involves actual sleep; merely resting with eyes closed is broader. Afternoon specifies the part of the day. The prompt invites discussion, not an assertion that every pupil should nap or that every length of nap has the same effect.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["daytime rests","Too broad as a direct synonym: pupils may rest without sleeping. It works only if the sentence explicitly says they fell asleep; then daytime naps is clearer."],["short afternoon sleeps","Close descriptive paraphrase when the naps are brief and pupils actually sleep."]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Daytime naps is a common wider term if the sentence keeps an afternoon time clue. Siestas suggests an early-afternoon rest/sleep custom and needs a setting that licenses actual sleeping. Power naps name deliberately brief sleep intended to refresh; the 2024 material's short-pod context makes this useful, but the term must not be applied to every nap. Catnaps are especially brief, often light or unplanned; they are taught only with that condition. Doze is usually a verb and may describe the act, but it does not by itself say afternoon; post-lunch nap adds a meal timing not required by the source."},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["short afternoon sleeps","明說下午短暫而真正睡着的普通描述。","醒着休息或整晚睡眠都不符合。"],["daytime naps","用較寬的日間詞，但句中仍有下午時刻，例如一時半或二時。","單說 daytime 也包括上午；不能刪掉下午線索。"],["siestas","午飯後慣常安排的午間休息，且有實際入睡線索。","不泛指四時偶然打盹或整個下午長睡。"],["power naps","特意安排短睡，目的是醒後更精神。","不把普通小睡的提神效果當成已證實或必然。"],["catnaps","幾分鐘、較淺、常無意發生的打盹。","不能用來指計劃中的長睡或夜間睡眠。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 只需平實重述午後短睡，用 short afternoon sleeps；用 daytime naps 時留住下午時間；午飯後的固定小睡可用 siestas；刻意安排來提神的短睡可用 power naps；極短、輕淺、偶然的睡眠可用 catnaps。原題討論 afternoon naps，不是單純醒着休息，也沒有斷言所有小睡都有相同效果。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"short afternoon sleeps","meaning":"短暫的午後睡眠","note":"用普通詞語重述學生在下午短時間真正睡着，並非只閉目休息。","collocations":"take short afternoon sleeps; allow short afternoon sleeps; short sleeps after lunch.","example":"The pupils took short afternoon sleeps in the quiet room before the final class.","exampleZh":"學生在最後一節課前，於安靜房間短暫睡了一會兒。","contrast":"Sleep 須真的入睡；rest 可以一直醒着。此片語保留下午時段和短暫性。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The proposed afternoon naps would last fifteen minutes, and pupils would actually sleep in the quiet room before the final lesson.","zh":"建議安排的午後小睡會持續十五分鐘，學生在最後一節課前會於安靜房間真正睡着。","upgrade":"The proposed short afternoon sleeps would last fifteen minutes, and pupils would actually sleep in the quiet room before the final lesson.","answer":"short afternoon sleeps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"short afternoon rests","explanation":"Rests 可指醒着休息；原句明說學生會在安靜房間真正睡着。"},{"letter":"B","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"十五分鐘遠短於 long afternoon sleeps 所指的長睡。"},{"letter":"C","text":"short afternoon sleeps","explanation":"Short afternoon sleeps 同時保留午後、十五分鐘及實際入睡，沒有另加目的或文化慣例。"},{"letter":"D","text":"unplanned afternoon dozes","explanation":"這是學校預先提出的房間安排，不能改成不知不覺發生的 unplanned dozes。"},{"letter":"E","text":"midday siestas","explanation":"句子沒有說午飯後固定休息或午睡文化；siestas 在此增添了線索以外的慣例。"},{"letter":"F","text":"very light catnaps","explanation":"十五分鐘小睡未被描述為極淺、輕易醒來的 catnaps。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The leaflet lists afternoon naps among the school's rest options, noting that pupils actually sleep for a short time between 1 and 4 p.m. without necessarily trying to feel more alert.","zh":"單張把午後小睡列作學校的休息選項，指出學生在下午一時至四時之間短暫地真正入睡，但不一定是為了提神。","upgrade":"The leaflet lists short afternoon sleeps among the school's rest options, noting that pupils actually sleep for a short time between 1 and 4 p.m. without necessarily trying to feel more alert.","answer":"short afternoon sleeps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"brief daytime rests","explanation":"單張特別說學生會真正入睡；brief rests 可一直醒着，範圍太廣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"planned power naps","explanation":"單張說不一定為提神而安排，不能把所有列出的短睡限定為 power naps。"},{"letter":"C","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"明說只短暫睡一會兒，不能換成長時間午後睡眠。"},{"letter":"D","text":"short afternoon sleeps","explanation":"Short afternoon sleeps 直接保留一時至四時、短暫及實際入睡；改寫只替換名詞片語。"},{"letter":"E","text":"post-lunch siestas","explanation":"一時至四時的範圍不保證每次都在午飯後，也沒有固定午間慣例，故 siestas 過窄。"},{"letter":"F","text":"light catnaps","explanation":"單張沒有說睡得特別淺或只幾分鐘，不能把所有例子收窄成 catnaps。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"daytime naps","meaning":"日間小睡","note":"白天的短睡，範圍可包括上午或下午；要與來源相符，句子須另寫明下午時間。","collocations":"take daytime naps; daytime naps at 2 p.m.; distinguish daytime naps from night sleep.","example":"The diary recorded daytime naps at 2 p.m. on three school days.","exampleZh":"日誌記錄了三個上課日下午二時的日間小睡。","contrast":"單說 daytime 比 afternoon 寬；沒有下午線索時不可默認所有日間睡眠都是午後睡眠。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The sleep diary listed the children's afternoon naps at 2 p.m. separately from their overnight sleep.","zh":"睡眠日誌把孩子們下午二時的小睡與整晚睡眠分開記錄。","upgrade":"The sleep diary listed the children's daytime naps at 2 p.m. separately from their overnight sleep.","answer":"daytime naps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"overnight sleep","explanation":"日誌已把二時的小睡與 overnight sleep 分開記錄。"},{"letter":"B","text":"daytime naps","explanation":"Daytime naps 可指白天小睡，at 2 p.m. 又保留其下午時段。"},{"letter":"C","text":"daytime rests","explanation":"Daytime rests 可是不睡的休息；日誌記錄的是孩子真正的小睡。"},{"letter":"D","text":"power naps","explanation":"沒有刻意提神的目的或分鐘數，不宜把日誌中的每次小睡都稱 power naps。"},{"letter":"E","text":"siestas","explanation":"日誌沒有記午間固定休息習慣，二時入睡未必是 siestas。"},{"letter":"F","text":"catnaps","explanation":"沒有說小睡極短而淺，不能限定為 catnaps。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Could the nursery offer afternoon naps at 1:30 p.m. and separate morning naps at 10 a.m. under one daytime-sleep policy?","zh":"託兒所可否在同一日間睡眠政策下，安排下午一時半小睡，以及上午十時的另一節小睡？","upgrade":"Could the nursery offer daytime naps at 1:30 p.m. and separate morning naps at 10 a.m. under one daytime-sleep policy?","answer":"daytime naps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"power naps","explanation":"託兒所的白天政策未說一時半小睡特為提神，不能稱所有安排為 power naps。"},{"letter":"B","text":"waking daytime breaks","explanation":"原句兩節都叫 naps，即有睡眠，而非一直清醒的小息。"},{"letter":"C","text":"siestas","explanation":"政策同時包含十時上午小睡，並未把一時半項目描述為午間文化慣例 siestas。"},{"letter":"D","text":"catnaps","explanation":"沒有說一時半小睡只幾分鐘或輕淺，不能收窄成 catnaps。"},{"letter":"E","text":"nighttime sleep","explanation":"一時半與十時都在白天，不是夜間睡眠。"},{"letter":"F","text":"daytime naps","explanation":"Daytime naps 這較寬的名稱可容納上午與下午小睡；at 1:30 p.m. 保留目標項目的下午時間。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"siestas","meaning":"午睡／午後小憩","note":"慣常在午間或初段下午進行的休息，常含睡眠，並帶特定生活安排或文化語感；練習須明說真的睡着。","collocations":"take a siesta; afternoon siestas; a daily siesta after lunch.","example":"During the summer programme, the children took short siestas after lunch and slept until 1:30 p.m.","exampleZh":"暑期活動中，孩子們午飯後短暫午睡，睡到下午一時半。","contrast":"Siesta 可能指一段休息習慣而未必人人入睡；用作 nap 時要有實際睡眠線索，也不適合任意指下午四時的短睡。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"At the summer camp, afternoon naps were the daily 1 p.m. sleep break; unlike children in a separate quiet-time group, these children actually slept for half an hour.","zh":"在暑期營，午後小睡是每天一時的睡眠時段；與另一組只安靜休息的孩子不同，這組孩子真的睡了半小時。","upgrade":"At the summer camp, siestas were the daily 1 p.m. sleep break; unlike children in a separate quiet-time group, these children actually slept for half an hour.","answer":"siestas","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"waking quiet time","explanation":"這組孩子確實睡了半小時；醒着的 quiet time 是另一組的安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"unplanned catnaps","explanation":"每天一時的定期半小時睡眠不是偶然發生的極短 catnaps。"},{"letter":"C","text":"power naps","explanation":"句子未說這段固定午間睡眠是為立刻提神，power naps 增添了目的。"},{"letter":"D","text":"siestas","explanation":"Siestas 可指每天午間慣常安排的小睡；原句又明說這組孩子真的睡着。"},{"letter":"E","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"半小時固定午睡不等於整段下午長睡。"},{"letter":"F","text":"one-off afternoon dozes","explanation":"One-off 與每天的一時睡眠時段不符；這不是偶發一次的打盹。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"While visiting Spain, the family took afternoon naps during the local midday break, sleeping after lunch before resuming sightseeing.","zh":"到西班牙旅遊時，這家人在當地午間休息時段午飯後小睡，醒來才繼續觀光。","upgrade":"While visiting Spain, the family took siestas during the local midday break, sleeping after lunch before resuming sightseeing.","answer":"siestas","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"siestas","explanation":"這家人在西班牙的當地午間休息時段飯後真正睡着，再繼續觀光，siestas 精確保留該慣例。"},{"letter":"B","text":"unplanned catnaps","explanation":"隨當地午間安排午睡不是無意間發生的幾分鐘 catnaps。"},{"letter":"C","text":"power naps","explanation":"句子沒有說為恢復警覺而限時安排，故 power naps 增添了目的。"},{"letter":"D","text":"waking midday rests","explanation":"一家人明說 sleeping after lunch，不能改成全程醒着的午間休息。"},{"letter":"E","text":"late-afternoon dozes","explanation":"這是在午間而非下午很晚的打盹。"},{"letter":"F","text":"random daytime naps","explanation":"Random 忽略家人參與當地固定午間休息的安排。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"power naps","meaning":"短暫提神小睡","note":"有意安排的短睡，目的是醒後恢復精神；通常比一般午後睡眠更講究短時和提神目的。","collocations":"take a power nap; a short power nap; schedule power naps before a later task.","example":"The volunteers scheduled brief power naps before their evening shift and woke after fifteen minutes.","exampleZh":"義工在晚班前安排短暫提神小睡，十五分鐘後便醒來。","contrast":"普通午後睡眠未必是刻意安排來提神；不可由 afternoon nap 自動推論特定效果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The Health Club proposed afternoon naps of fifteen minutes in sleeping pods, intending pupils to wake before the last lesson feeling more alert.","zh":"健康學會建議學生下午在睡眠艙小睡十五分鐘，目的是讓他們在最後一節課前醒來時精神較佳。","upgrade":"The Health Club proposed power naps of fifteen minutes in sleeping pods, intending pupils to wake before the last lesson feeling more alert.","answer":"power naps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"power naps","explanation":"十五分鐘艙內睡眠是特意建議來讓學生醒後較清醒，符合 power naps；效果仍是學會的期望。"},{"letter":"B","text":"siestas","explanation":"句子未說午飯後的固定午間慣例，不能只因在下午便稱 siestas。"},{"letter":"C","text":"unplanned catnaps","explanation":"睡眠艙內預先安排十五分鐘；unplanned catnaps 加上了與此相反的『未安排』條件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"waking relaxation breaks","explanation":"安排的是實際小睡，非一直醒着的放鬆時段。"},{"letter":"E","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"十五分鐘不屬長時間午後睡眠。"},{"letter":"F","text":"unplanned dozes","explanation":"Health Club 先提出使用睡眠艙的計劃，故不是未安排的 dozes。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The app counted afternoon naps as part of its planned alertness programme only when users deliberately slept for ten to twenty minutes; accidental dozes were logged separately.","zh":"應用程式只把使用者刻意安排的十至二十分鐘午後小睡算進提神計劃；無意間打盹則另外記錄。","upgrade":"The app counted power naps as part of its planned alertness programme only when users deliberately slept for ten to twenty minutes; accidental dozes were logged separately.","answer":"power naps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"accidental catnaps","explanation":"應用程式把偶發極短打盹另外記錄；accidental catnaps 與刻意安排的這一欄不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"siestas","explanation":"提神計劃沒有提到午飯後的文化休息慣例，不應把所有記錄稱為 siestas。"},{"letter":"C","text":"power naps","explanation":"Power naps 同時保留有意安排、十至二十分鐘及提神計劃，與另列的意外打盹分開。"},{"letter":"D","text":"waking rest breaks","explanation":"使用者真的睡十至二十分鐘，非一直醒着的休息。"},{"letter":"E","text":"accidental dozes","explanation":"Accidental dozes 已在應用程式另列，正是此分類要排除的狀況。"},{"letter":"F","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"十至二十分鐘不能稱為長時間午後睡眠。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"catnaps","meaning":"打盹／極短小睡","note":"很短、往往較淺的睡眠，可在座位上短暫打盹；需另有下午線索。","collocations":"take a catnap; brief catnaps on the bus; a five-minute catnap.","example":"On the afternoon bus, the tired passenger took a five-minute catnap and nearly missed her stop.","exampleZh":"疲倦的乘客在下午的巴士上打了五分鐘盹，差點坐過站。","contrast":"Catnap 比一般計劃中的二十分鐘小睡更短、更可能無意間發生；不能代替整晚睡眠。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her afternoon naps in the armchair were so brief and light that a doorbell could wake her after only a few minutes.","zh":"她下午在扶手椅的小睡極短而淺，門鈴過幾分鐘便可能把她吵醒。","upgrade":"Her catnaps in the armchair each afternoon were so brief and light that a doorbell could wake her after only a few minutes.","answer":"catnaps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"deep afternoon sleeps","explanation":"幾分鐘後可被門鈴喚醒，與 deep 的深睡不符。"},{"letter":"B","text":"planned power naps","explanation":"沒有設鬧鐘或提神安排，不可把扶手椅上的輕淺短睡說成 planned power naps。"},{"letter":"C","text":"daytime rests","explanation":"門鈴會把她叫醒，表示真的睡着；rests 可指醒着。"},{"letter":"D","text":"catnaps","explanation":"Catnaps 準確表示幾分鐘、輕淺、容易被吵醒的小睡；改寫保留 each afternoon。"},{"letter":"E","text":"siestas","explanation":"沒有午飯後固定休息的線索，故 siestas 過於特定。"},{"letter":"F","text":"extended afternoon sleeps","explanation":"幾分鐘的小睡不是延長的午後睡眠。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"On the 4 p.m. bus, the traveller slipped into several afternoon naps, each lasting only a few minutes, and nearly missed her stop.","zh":"下午四時的巴士上，旅客不知不覺打了幾次盹，每次只有幾分鐘，差點坐過站。","upgrade":"On the 4 p.m. bus, the traveller slipped into several catnaps, each lasting only a few minutes, and nearly missed her stop.","answer":"catnaps","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"planned power naps","explanation":"Slipped into 表不自覺入睡，沒有刻意安排提神的 power naps。"},{"letter":"B","text":"siestas","explanation":"下午四時的車上偶發短睡，不是規律的午間 siestas。"},{"letter":"C","text":"daytime rests","explanation":"她差點因睡着而坐過站；rests 可只是醒着放鬆。"},{"letter":"D","text":"long afternoon sleeps","explanation":"每次只有幾分鐘，不能說長時間午後睡眠。"},{"letter":"E","text":"catnaps","explanation":"多次無意間、各幾分鐘的打盹符合 catnaps，四時又保留下午時段。"},{"letter":"F","text":"scheduled quiet periods","explanation":"車上不知不覺睡着，不是預定的安靜休息時段。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"rest / nap","zh":"中文辨析： 休息可以只是安靜躺着；nap 表實際睡了一會兒。來源問的是小睡。","point":"A pupil may rest for twenty minutes without falling asleep."},{"word":"daytime / afternoon","zh":"中文辨析： 日間也包括上午；把 afternoon naps 改成 daytime naps 時，句中須保留下午時間。","point":"A 10 a.m. nap is daytime sleep but not an afternoon nap."},{"word":"siesta / all afternoon asleep","zh":"中文辨析： Siesta 通常是午間休息慣例，不能用來暗示學生從午飯一直睡到放學。","point":"A midday break is not an entire afternoon's sleep."},{"word":"power nap / ordinary nap","zh":"中文辨析： Power nap 加入短時、為恢復精神而安排的目的；普通小睡不一定有此目的或證實有效。","point":"A nap need not be a planned refreshment strategy."},{"word":"catnap / full sleep","zh":"中文辨析： Catnap 是極短的打盹；不能指午睡兩小時或一整晚睡眠。","point":"A brief doze is not a long sleep period."}],"moduleNumber":91},{"id":"lesson-092","sourceId":53,"headword":"air-conditioned gondolas","title":"Air-conditioned gondolas","titleZh":"設有空調的摩天輪車廂","subtitle":"設有空調的摩天輪車廂","description":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 3.3〈Central Waterfront Ferris Wheel〉： “The wheel will reach 60 meters into the sky, carrying passengers in air-conditioned gondolas.”","sourceSense":"原文： 2014 年 DSE 3.3〈Central Waterfront Ferris Wheel〉： “The wheel will reach 60 meters into the sky, carrying passengers in air-conditioned gondolas.”","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["cooled passenger cabins","contextual, less exact","可表供乘客乘坐而較涼快的車廂，但 cooled 不保證有空調；若要完整保留原文設備，應明說 air-conditioned。"],["climate-controlled pods","conditional, less idiomatic here","Climate-controlled 可指溫度受控制；pods 可能暗示特定小型艙體設計，原文沒有交代，摩天輪語境以 gondolas/cabins/passenger cars 較自然。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["說法","選用條件"],"rows":[["air-conditioned cabins","有摩天輪語境時，cabins 是常用、較白話的車廂名稱；完整保留空調。"],["air-conditioned passenger cars","遊樂設施或操作說明中可用 cars 指輪上載客車廂；勿誤作道路汽車。"],["climate-controlled gondolas","題句指溫度受空調控制時可用；不能因此額外聲稱設有暖氣。"]],"note":"Quick rule: 想用最通俗車廂名稱選 air-conditioned cabins；描述設施的每個載客單元可選 air-conditioned passenger cars；重點是車廂溫度受控制時選 climate-controlled gondolas。只有較涼、通風或遮陽，都不必然表示設有空調。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"air-conditioned cabins","meaning":"設有空調的車廂；常用改寫","note":"Cabin 是摩天輪供乘客乘坐的空間；有明確輪子語境時可取代 gondola，保留空調設施。","collocations":"air-conditioned cabins on the wheel; ride in an air-conditioned cabin","example":"Families waited to board the air-conditioned cabins on the observation wheel.","exampleZh":"家庭乘客等候登上觀景摩天輪設有空調的車廂。","contrast":"Cabin 也可指飛機或船艙，須靠 on the wheel 等語境限定；只說 cool cabins 不一定表明有空調。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The proposed observation wheel will carry riders in air-conditioned gondolas rather than on exposed seats.","zh":"擬建的觀景摩天輪將讓乘客坐在設有空調的車廂，而非露天座位。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The proposed observation wheel will carry riders in air-conditioned cabins rather than on exposed seats.","answer":"air-conditioned cabins","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"ventilated cabins","explanation":"通風未必有空調，少了設計圖明說的設備。"},{"letter":"B","text":"shaded seats","explanation":"有遮陽棚的座位仍可能露天，不能保留車廂及空調兩項資訊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"cooled passenger cabins","explanation":"可說較涼的車廂，卻未指明冷卻來自空調設備。"},{"letter":"D","text":"air-conditioned cabins","explanation":"保留輪上乘客車廂與空調，並與露天座位作對照。"},{"letter":"E","text":"air-conditioned boats","explanation":"也可有空調，但這是摩天輪，並非載客船。"},{"letter":"F","text":"heated waiting rooms","explanation":"候車室不在輪上；原文也沒有說有暖氣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"On a hot afternoon, families choose the wheel's air-conditioned gondolas instead of its open cars.","zh":"炎熱的下午，家庭乘客選擇摩天輪設有空調的車廂，而非開放式車廂。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"On a hot afternoon, families choose the wheel's air-conditioned cabins instead of its open cars.","answer":"air-conditioned cabins","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"open cabins","explanation":"開放式車廂正是家人沒有選擇的另一類座位。"},{"letter":"B","text":"air-conditioned cabins","explanation":"保留在炎熱天氣中提供空調的輪上乘客車廂。"},{"letter":"C","text":"screened cabins","explanation":"有紗網可防蟲，卻不表示車廂有空調。"},{"letter":"D","text":"shaded cabins","explanation":"遮陽只能減少日曬，未必能提供原句指明的空調。"},{"letter":"E","text":"air-conditioned cable cars","explanation":"纜車沿纜索路線行駛；句子明說是摩天輪。"},{"letter":"F","text":"ventilated cabins","explanation":"通風可能帶來涼意，但不能確認有冷氣設備。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"air-conditioned passenger cars","meaning":"設有空調的乘客車廂；遊樂設施用語","note":"摩天輪上的 passenger car 指每個供乘客乘坐的車廂，不是道路上的私家車；語境應明示是 wheel/ride。","collocations":"air-conditioned passenger cars on a Ferris wheel; each passenger car holds riders","example":"The ride operator inspected the air-conditioned passenger cars before opening the wheel.","exampleZh":"遊樂設施操作員在摩天輪開放前檢查了設有空調的乘客車廂。","contrast":"Car 在此是遊樂設施車廂，並非的士或私家車；保留 air-conditioned 才不會丟失原句的舒適設備資訊。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Each of the air-conditioned gondolas on the Ferris wheel can carry six riders.","zh":"摩天輪上每個設有空調的車廂可載六名乘客。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Each of the air-conditioned passenger cars on the Ferris wheel can carry six riders.","answer":"air-conditioned passenger cars","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"private road cars","explanation":"這裏的 car 是摩天輪車廂，不是路面私家車。"},{"letter":"B","text":"passenger cars without cooling","explanation":"明說沒有冷卻，與原句有空調相反。"},{"letter":"C","text":"air-conditioned passenger cars","explanation":"在 on the Ferris wheel 限定下，car 自然指載人的輪上車廂，並保留空調。"},{"letter":"D","text":"air-conditioned cable cars","explanation":"纜車也可載六人，卻不是題句的摩天輪載具。"},{"letter":"E","text":"enclosed seats","explanation":"只說座位有遮蔽，沒有交代車廂或空調。"},{"letter":"F","text":"station waiting areas","explanation":"候車區不隨摩天輪轉動，不能說每個載六人繞圈。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Before boarding begins, the operator checks all the air-conditioned gondolas attached to the wheel.","zh":"開始登車前，操作員檢查所有連在摩天輪上、設有空調的車廂。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Before boarding begins, the operator checks all the air-conditioned passenger cars attached to the wheel.","answer":"air-conditioned passenger cars","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"air-conditioned railcars","explanation":"鐵路車廂在軌道上，並非連在摩天輪邊緣。"},{"letter":"B","text":"cooled waiting rooms","explanation":"候車室在地面，不是操作員檢查的輪上載客單元。"},{"letter":"C","text":"gondola boats with air conditioning","explanation":"水上船隻不會「連在摩天輪上」。"},{"letter":"D","text":"passenger cars without air conditioning","explanation":"保留車廂，卻否定原句明說的空調設備。"},{"letter":"E","text":"climate-controlled station offices","explanation":"空調辦公室不載乘客繞輪轉動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"air-conditioned passenger cars","explanation":"attached to the wheel 清楚限定為摩天輪乘客車廂，並保留空調。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"climate-controlled gondolas","meaning":"溫度受控制的吊艙；着重車廂環境","note":"當上下文指車廂有可調的溫度控制或空調設備時，可用 climate-controlled 強調乘坐環境。它可比單純 air-conditioned 更寬，不能無端推斷另設暖氣。","collocations":"climate-controlled gondolas; temperature settings in climate-controlled gondolas","example":"Staff checked the temperature in the climate-controlled gondolas before boarding began.","exampleZh":"職員在乘客登車前檢查了溫度受控制的摩天輪吊艙內的溫度。","contrast":"Climate-controlled 不能簡化成 well-ventilated；通風不等於能控制溫度。若只知有空調，不應另外聲稱具加熱功能。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The wheel's air-conditioned gondolas are designed to keep the cabin temperature steady on hot afternoons.","zh":"摩天輪設有空調的車廂經設計可在炎熱下午維持穩定的車廂溫度。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"The wheel's climate-controlled gondolas are designed to keep the cabin temperature steady on hot afternoons.","answer":"climate-controlled gondolas","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"climate-controlled gondolas","explanation":"題句明說車廂有空調並維持溫度，符合溫度受控制的描述。"},{"letter":"B","text":"well-ventilated gondolas","explanation":"空氣流通未必可在炎熱下午維持穩定室溫。"},{"letter":"C","text":"shaded gondolas","explanation":"遮陽可減少日曬，但不表示車廂溫度可保持穩定。"},{"letter":"D","text":"heated gondolas","explanation":"加熱不是炎熱下午所需，原句也沒有暖氣資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"open-air gondolas","explanation":"露天車廂難以像題句那樣控制內部溫度。"},{"letter":"F","text":"weatherproof gondolas","explanation":"防雨防風與維持穩定溫度是不同功能。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Attendants can set the temperature inside the air-conditioned gondolas before each group boards.","zh":"職員可在每組乘客登車前設定設有空調的摩天輪車廂內的溫度。\n\n**Question:** Which option gives the best rewrite for the stated meaning?","upgrade":"Attendants can set the temperature inside the climate-controlled gondolas before each group boards.","answer":"climate-controlled gondolas","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"shaded gondolas","explanation":"遮陽棚的效果不能由職員逐組設定車廂溫度。"},{"letter":"B","text":"climate-controlled gondolas","explanation":"原句明說可預設溫度，突出車廂環境受控制。"},{"letter":"C","text":"naturally cooled gondolas","explanation":"自然通風不能保證職員可設定確切溫度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"soundproof gondolas","explanation":"隔音處理與溫度設定無關。"},{"letter":"E","text":"heated-only gondolas","explanation":"只靠加熱不等於原句的空調，也不能解釋炎熱天氣的需求。"},{"letter":"F","text":"open passenger cars","explanation":"開放式車廂沒有同樣可設定的內部溫度。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Cooled / ventilated · 較涼與有空調不同","zh":"中文辨析： 開窗通風或遮陽也可能令車廂較涼；air-conditioned 明確說有空調設備。只有原句不要求指出設備時，cooled passenger cabins 才可能作較寬的描述。","point":"Cooling or ventilation does not necessarily mean air conditioning."},{"word":"Boat gondolas / cable-car gondolas · 相同名詞、不同載具","zh":"中文辨析： Gondola 可指威尼斯船或纜車車廂；本段有 the wheel 和 carrying passengers，所以是摩天輪車廂。改寫時不可加入船或纜索路線。","point":"The Ferris-wheel context fixes gondola as a wheel cabin."},{"word":"Pod / capsule · 形狀和設計未獲證實","zh":"中文辨析： 某些觀景輪可稱車廂為 pods 或 capsules，但原句沒有描述其特定形狀；climate-controlled pods 會加上不必要的設計暗示。若另一篇文章明稱其為 pod，才可如此寫。","point":"Pod or capsule may name a particular design; this sentence only establishes wheel gondolas."},{"word":"Open cars / enclosed cabins · 不能漏掉設備","zh":"中文辨析： 開放式車廂可有遮陽棚卻未必有空調；只寫 passenger cabins 也會丟失「設有空調」的特點。替換時應保留原文的乘客空間與空調資訊。","point":"Keep both the passenger compartment and its air-conditioning feature."},{"word":"Climate control · 不可推斷額外設施","zh":"中文辨析： 空調支持「溫度受控制」的描述，但並不自動證明車廂也有暖氣或每座可獨立調溫。練習若要講可調控制，必須在原句交代。","point":"Air conditioning supports temperature control, not an unmentioned heater or separate settings."}],"moduleNumber":92},{"id":"lesson-093","sourceId":64,"headword":"amazing and enjoyable experience","title":"Amazing and enjoyable experience","titleZh":"精彩又愉快的體驗","subtitle":"精彩又愉快的體驗","description":"原文： 2017 DSE Paper 4，8.3 的大東山遠足及露營活動宣傳語是「An amazing and enjoyable experience!」這是對參加者預期感受的宣傳評價，兼有「令人驚喜／特別」與「愉快」兩面；不是中性地指一場活動，也不是保證每位參加者已實際感到快樂。原文只是一句簡短口號，以下場景均是原創練習，不冒充考卷行程細節。[2017 Paper 4 set 8.3 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2017-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2017 DSE Paper 4，8.3 的大東山遠足及露營活動宣傳語是「An amazing and enjoyable experience!」這是對參加者預期感受的宣傳評價，兼有「令人驚喜／特別」與「愉快」兩面；不是中性地指一場活動，也不是保證每位參加者已實際感到快樂。原文只是一句簡短口號，以下場景均是原創練習，不冒充考卷行程細節。[2017 Paper 4 set 8.3 再現試卷](https://dsepp.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/2017-DSE-ENG-LANG-4.pdf)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文界線"],"rows":[["remarkable and pleasant experience","有條件的近義","Remarkable 保留值得注意的特別性，pleasant 表舒適愉快但弱於 enjoyable；須有不尋常景觀與舒適體驗的雙重線索。"],["memorable and fun event","不宜直接替換","Event 指舉辦的活動，原句 experience 指參與者的經歷；fun 又偏玩樂，未必包括靜觀風景。可重寫成 a memorable and fun trip，但要有實際趣味線索。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： A wonderful experience 是較概括的雙重正評；a memorable and enjoyable experience 重視回憶與樂趣；an exciting and enjoyable adventure 需要身體活動或刺激；a fantastic time 是口語的參與者角度重寫。An unforgettable experience 強於 memorable，但若沒有長久記憶的明示線索，容易過度承諾；它的主要機制已由 memorable 教授。A delightful trip 偏舒心愉悅但少了驚嘆；a breathtaking hike 只說景色震撼，未保證愉快；a rewarding challenge 只說有收穫，可能過程辛苦。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- 原短語同時評價特別／精彩與愉快，選答案須保留兩面。\n- Wonderful 概括雙重正評；memorable and enjoyable 加上日後仍樂於回憶；remarkable and pleasant 需不尋常而溫和舒適。\n- Exciting and enjoyable adventure 需探索興奮線索；have a fantastic time 從參加者角度用較口語動詞片語重寫。\n- Event 指活動本身，experience 指經歷；breathtaking 只說壯觀，rewarding 只說有收穫，皆不自行證明愉快。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"a wonderful experience","meaning":"美好而精彩的體驗","note":"整體既特別又令人愉快，但句子不需把快樂、震撼各自拆成兩個形容詞時用。較廣泛，須靠上下文證明正面。","collocations":"a wonderful experience for visitors; have a wonderful experience; a truly wonderful experience","example":"The guided mountain walk was a wonderful experience for our class.","exampleZh":"對我們班來說，這次有人帶領的山徑步行是一次美好的體驗。","contrast":"Wonderful 合併正評，卻比 amazing and enjoyable 少了兩個特質的明確分列。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The pupils called the hill walk an amazing and enjoyable experience as they admired the broad valley view and shared stories on the way down.","zh":"學生一邊欣賞開闊山谷景色，一邊在下山途中分享故事，稱這次遠足為精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"The pupils called the hill walk a wonderful experience as they admired the broad valley view and shared stories on the way down.","answer":"a wonderful experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a wonderful experience","explanation":"美景與同行分享兼有精彩和愉快，wonderful 作整體正評，沒有多加未見的細節。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a memorable but tiring experience","explanation":"memorable 可指日後仍記得，但原句只描寫當時；tiring 也無依據。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","explanation":"remarkable 需有罕見或特別值得記錄的景象，開闊山谷本身未有這條件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"adventure 強調探索或挑戰，句中是一般欣賞風景與聊天。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a delightful but ordinary outing","explanation":"delightful 保留愉快，但 ordinary 削弱了精彩美景。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a fun event","explanation":"fun event 把參加者經歷改成舉辦的活動，且沒有涵蓋觀景讚歎。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The trip brochure promises an amazing and enjoyable experience: families can watch the valley brighten at dawn and share a leisurely breakfast outdoors.","zh":"旅程手冊承諾一家人可在戶外看着晨光照亮山谷，然後悠閒共進早餐，享受精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"The trip brochure promises a wonderful experience: families can watch the valley brighten at dawn and share a leisurely breakfast outdoors.","answer":"a wonderful experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"手冊描述未來活動，未有日後長久記憶的證據；memorable 多加承諾。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a remarkable but demanding experience","explanation":"demanding 與悠閒早餐不合，remarkable 亦需罕有線索。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a wonderful experience","explanation":"晨光景色與家人早餐的樂趣兼具，wonderful 是最自然的概括。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an exciting adventure","explanation":"沒有冒險或刺激，只有欣賞景色與悠閒相聚。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a pleasant breakfast event","explanation":"breakfast event 只保留早餐，漏掉晨光與整趟參與經歷。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a rewarding challenge","explanation":"沒有須克服的難題，rewarding challenge 轉移焦點。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","meaning":"難忘而愉快的體驗","note":"活動日後仍清晰記得，而且當時樂在其中；memorable 不必一定令人震驚，故須有值得回想的細節。","collocations":"a memorable and enjoyable experience; make the trip memorable; an enjoyable memory","example":"Watching the sunrise with friends was a memorable and enjoyable experience.","exampleZh":"與朋友一起看日出是一次難忘而愉快的體驗。","contrast":"Memorable 說會記住，amazing 說當下驚嘆；難忘經驗也可能不愉快，所以第二個形容詞不可省。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Ten years after the camp, Mei still keeps its photograph beside her desk and smiles at the games they played; she calls it an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"露營十年後，阿美仍把照片放在書桌旁，每想起當年的遊戲便會微笑；她稱那是精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"Ten years after the camp, Mei still keeps its photograph beside her desk and smiles at the games they played; she calls it a memorable and enjoyable experience.","answer":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a wonderful experience","explanation":"wonderful 可概括好感，卻未點出十年仍保存照片這個記憶線索。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a pleasant but forgettable outing","explanation":"forgettable 與十年保留照片矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"十年後仍看照片微笑，memorable 與 enjoyable 各有證據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a remarkable but difficult challenge","explanation":"沒有困難挑戰，remarkable 也非重點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an exciting outdoor event","explanation":"event 指舉辦的露營活動，句中說的是阿美個人回憶。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a fantastic afternoon","explanation":"fantastic afternoon 把整次露營縮成一個下午，亦漏掉長久記憶。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At graduation, the friends chose one camping memory to write in their class book: the night they finally learned to identify the stars together and laughed at their mistakes. They called it an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"畢業時，朋友們選了一段露營回憶寫進班刊：那夜大家終於一起學會辨認星星，並為自己的錯誤笑個不停。他們稱這是精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"At graduation, the friends chose one camping memory to write in their class book: the night they finally learned to identify the stars together and laughed at their mistakes. They called it a memorable and enjoyable experience.","answer":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"adventure 暗示探索挑戰；題句主要有班刊保存的回憶與共同歡笑。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"把這夜寫進班刊，且回想時歡笑，兼具記憶價值與樂趣。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a remarkable but solitary experience","explanation":"大家一起學，solitary 與情境相反。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a pleasant yet forgettable evening","explanation":"寫進班刊顯示並未忘記，forgettable 不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a fun astronomy event","explanation":"event 會把個人經歷轉成舉辦的天文活動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a difficult but worthwhile lesson","explanation":"學會辨星雖有收穫，但句中同時強調回憶及開心，不只是辛苦課堂。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","meaning":"非同尋常而愉悅的體驗","note":"看見罕見或值得留意的事物，同時過程舒適愉快時可用；pleasant 的喜悅程度比 enjoyable 溫和。","collocations":"a remarkable and pleasant experience; a pleasant walk; a remarkable view","example":"Seeing the rare cloud formation during the calm walk was a remarkable and pleasant experience.","exampleZh":"在平靜的步行途中看到罕見雲層，是一次非同尋常又愉悅的體驗。","contrast":"Remarkable 比 wonderful 更聚焦值得注意的異常；pleasant 不能暗示刺激或狂喜。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"On an easy afternoon walk, we saw a rare halo around the sun and enjoyed the cool breeze; our guide called it an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"一次輕鬆的午後步行中，我們看見太陽周圍罕見的光暈，又享受清涼微風；導遊稱這是精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"On an easy afternoon walk, we saw a rare halo around the sun and enjoyed the cool breeze; our guide called it a remarkable and pleasant experience.","answer":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a wonderful experience","explanation":"wonderful 也能概括正評，但 remarkable and pleasant 逐一對應罕見光暈與舒心微風。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"memorable 要有日後仍記得的線索，題句只說當日所見。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"easy walk 未見探索或刺激，adventure 加入多餘特質。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","explanation":"罕見光暈值得注意，清涼微風使過程愉悅，兩面都有具體根據。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a breathtaking but uncomfortable hike","explanation":"uncomfortable 與享受涼風矛盾。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a delightful yet routine stroll","explanation":"routine 漏掉罕見光暈，delightful 又未明說非同尋常。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At a rest stop, hikers unexpectedly met a retired ranger who told them little-known stories about the trail over tea; they called the conversation an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"遠足者在休息站意外遇到一名退休護林員，邊喝茶邊聽他講山徑鮮為人知的故事；大家稱這次交談為精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"At a rest stop, hikers unexpectedly met a retired ranger who told them little-known stories about the trail over tea; they called the conversation a remarkable and pleasant experience.","answer":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"喝茶交談沒有探險的身體刺激。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a wonderful but ordinary chat","explanation":"ordinary 漏掉意外遇到護林員和鮮為人知的故事。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a memorable and enjoyable event","explanation":"event 把親身交談說成安排好的活動；題句也沒說日後回憶。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","explanation":"意外相遇和罕知故事具特別性，熱茶交談令人舒心，兩面兼備。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a rewarding but exhausting lesson","explanation":"沒有疲累，且重點不是完成課業。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a breathtaking scenery tour","explanation":"談話不是觀景導覽，scenery tour 轉換所述經歷。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","meaning":"刺激而有趣的歷險","note":"遠足有挑戰、探索或興奮感，且參與者享受過程時才可把 experience 具體化為 adventure。純粹平靜的觀景活動不宜。","collocations":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure; embark on an adventure; a safe but exciting adventure","example":"Crossing the easy stream and discovering a hidden viewpoint made the hike an exciting and enjoyable adventure.","exampleZh":"跨過淺溪並發現隱蔽觀景點，令這次遠足成為刺激又有趣的歷險。","contrast":"Adventure 加入探索意味；amazing experience 可只是觀景，不一定有冒險。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The teenagers navigated a marked trail, crossed a shallow stream and cheered when they found a hidden viewpoint; they called the hike an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"青少年沿有標記的山徑前進、跨過淺溪，找到隱蔽觀景點時歡呼，稱這次遠足為精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"The teenagers navigated a marked trail, crossed a shallow stream and cheered when they found a hidden viewpoint; they called the hike an exciting and enjoyable adventure.","answer":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"沿徑探索、跨溪尋景並歡呼，adventure 的探索及 enjoyable 的快樂都獲支持。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a wonderful but passive experience","explanation":"passive 與跨溪、尋找觀景點等主動行動不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"memorable 需日後仍記得，句子描寫的是當下探索。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a remarkable and pleasant rest","explanation":"rest 與行進跨溪相反，pleasant 亦弱化興奮。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a thrilling but joyless challenge","explanation":"joyless 與歡呼矛盾；thrilling 也較像高風險刺激。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a fun organised event","explanation":"event 指主辦活動，題句聚焦親身遠足與探索。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"During the camp, pairs followed map clues to find a new trail marker, then celebrated each discovery with a laugh; they described the challenge as an amazing and enjoyable experience.","zh":"露營期間，兩人一組依地圖線索尋找新的山徑標記，每找到一個便笑着慶祝；他們形容這項挑戰為精彩又愉快的體驗。","upgrade":"During the camp, pairs followed map clues to find a new trail marker, then celebrated each discovery with a laugh; they described the challenge as an exciting and enjoyable adventure.","answer":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a relaxing and predictable pastime","explanation":"尋找新標記有探索性，並非可預測的休閒活動。"},{"letter":"B","text":"an educational but joyless exercise","explanation":"笑着慶祝顯示樂趣，joyless 不符。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"memorable 需之後仍記得，題句只述尋找當時。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"地圖線索與逐一發現有冒險感，歡笑慶祝顯示享受。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a remarkable and pleasant conversation","explanation":"沒有主要交談場景，重點是探索標記。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a rewarding but exhausting task","explanation":"未說疲累；rewarding 又未完整表達發現時的興奮。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"a fantastic time","meaning":"玩得非常開心；較口語","note":"從參加者角度回顧自己很享受、覺得活動精彩時用 have a fantastic time；需把名詞 experience 改成動詞片語。","collocations":"have a fantastic time on the hike; a fantastic time with friends; we had a fantastic time","example":"We had a fantastic time hiking together and watching the valley turn gold at sunset.","exampleZh":"我們一起遠足，看着山谷在夕陽下變成金黃色，玩得非常開心。","contrast":"A fantastic time 口語而注重享受；若要正式描述活動性質，可用 a wonderful experience。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"“We had an amazing and enjoyable experience watching the sunset from camp,” I said in a voice message to my friends that evening.","zh":"「我們在營地看日落，玩得真開心！」我當晚在語音訊息中對朋友說。","upgrade":"“We had a fantastic time watching the sunset from camp,” I said in a voice message to my friends that evening.","answer":"had a fantastic time","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"had a remarkable and pleasant experience","explanation":"remarkable and pleasant 偏正式，且沒有罕見景象；不合對朋友的熱情語音。"},{"letter":"B","text":"had a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"memorable 加上未來會長久記住，當晚尚未證實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"had an exciting and enjoyable adventure","explanation":"只看日落，沒有探索冒險。"},{"letter":"D","text":"had a delightful but ordinary evening","explanation":"delightful 可表愉快，但 ordinary 低估原話的強烈正評。"},{"letter":"E","text":"had a fantastic time","explanation":"對朋友即時口語分享日落樂趣，had a fantastic time 自然又熱烈。"},{"letter":"F","text":"held a wonderful event","explanation":"held an event 說主辦活動，不是我們看日落的親身感受。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At breakfast, my little brother grinned and said, “I had an amazing and enjoyable experience roasting marshmallows and swapping stories last night.”","zh":"早餐時，弟弟笑着說：「昨晚烤棉花糖、交換故事，玩得真開心。」","upgrade":"At breakfast, my little brother grinned and said, “I had a fantastic time roasting marshmallows and swapping stories last night.”","answer":"a fantastic time","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a remarkable and pleasant experience","explanation":"remarkable 太正式，也沒有罕見事物；弟弟是在開心閒聊。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a memorable and enjoyable experience","explanation":"memorable 有日後長久記住的意味，翌晨只見開心回顧。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an exciting adventure","explanation":"烤棉花糖和交換故事不以探索冒險為主。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a wonderful organised event","explanation":"organised event 轉成活動主辦角度，且語氣比弟弟說話正式。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a delightful but quiet evening","explanation":"quiet 未必錯，但原句的強烈快樂更適合 fantastic time。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a fantastic time","explanation":"弟弟笑着向家人敘述昨晚樂趣，I had a fantastic time 是地道口語。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"event / experience · 活動本身與個人經歷","zh":"中文辨析： 一次遠足是 event/trip；參加者對它的感受才是 experience。原映射 a memorable and fun event 轉了焦點；若要寫活動可說 a memorable and fun trip，但需重構句子。","point":"An event is organised; an experience is lived through."},{"word":"amazing / amazed · 令別人驚嘆與自己感到驚嘆","zh":"中文辨析： An amazing experience 令人驚嘆；I was amazed by the view 說我的感受。An amazed experience 不合這個意思。","point":"The experience is amazing; a participant is amazed."},{"word":"breathtaking / enjoyable · 壯觀不保證愉快","zh":"中文辨析： 景色可以 breathtaking，但人可能因惡劣天氣不享受旅程。若要保留原短語兩面，不能只用 a breathtaking hike。","point":"A striking view and an enjoyable trip are distinct claims."},{"word":"rewarding / relaxing / thrilling · 有收穫、放鬆、刺激各不相同","zh":"中文辨析： 艱難遠足或許 rewarding 卻不快樂；安靜觀景可 relaxing 而不刺激；攀爬可 thrilling 但不一定舒服。選詞要看練習場景支持哪種感受。","point":"Benefit, calm and excitement are not interchangeable with enjoyment."},{"word":"memorable / unforgettable · 難忘可正可負且強度不同","zh":"中文辨析： 雷暴中的迷路也會 memorable/unforgettable，卻未必愉快。Unforgettable 比 memorable 更強，宣傳時別暗示所有參加者必定一生不忘。","point":"Remembering an event says nothing by itself about pleasure."}],"moduleNumber":93},{"id":"lesson-094","sourceId":71,"headword":"animal welfare","title":"Animal welfare","titleZh":"動物福利","subtitle":"動物福利","description":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 3.1 的報道標題提及一間香港旅遊公司雖然作出 animal welfare pledge，卻仍提供野生動物體驗；文章又說該公司在訂立 animal welfare policy 後仍推廣有野生動物表演的景點。此處是動物健康、壓力與生活狀況，以及人類對待牠們的標準。報道文字本身沒有證明每場表演都造成傷害，也沒有證明承諾已達成。以下例句與練習為原創。","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 3.1 的報道標題提及一間香港旅遊公司雖然作出 animal welfare pledge，卻仍提供野生動物體驗；文章又說該公司在訂立 animal welfare policy 後仍推廣有野生動物表演的景點。此處是動物健康、壓力與生活狀況，以及人類對待牠們的標準。報道文字本身沒有證明每場表演都造成傷害，也沒有證明承諾已達成。以下例句與練習為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原文語境中的理由"],"rows":[["well-being of animals","近義；偏重結果","指動物實際身心狀況，適合評估承諾成效；改寫政策名稱時要重組句子。"],["humane treatment","相關但較窄","指人是否以減少不必要痛苦的方式對待動物；單有某一種人道做法，不保證整體福利良好。宜補上 of animals。"]],"note":"覆核後的範圍： animal protection 可指保護野生物種或免受傷害，但不必然說明圈養動物每天的健康與壓力；animal rights 是權利主張，立場不同；animal care 可指照料工作，但單憑有照料不等於福利達標。這些重要近詞在第 4 節辨明。上述兩項為此政策／實際狀況語境中最有教學價值的改寫；同一概念的 animals' well-being 是詞序變體，不另佔一項。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子要問甚麼","可用說法","邊界"],"rows":[["動物實際健康、壓力及生活狀態","well-being of animals","政策存在仍須實證"],["人如何餵飼、運送及接觸動物","humane treatment of animals","良好做法仍須看長期結果"]],"note":"Animal welfare 可概括兩方面。談公司的 pledge/policy 時要保留「承諾或政策」這一層，不可把它直接寫成動物已經生活良好。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"well-being of animals","meaning":"動物的身心福祉","note":"聚焦動物實際是否健康、舒適、壓力是否過大。Well-being 通常不可數；可說 the well-being of animals 或 animals' well-being。若原句談政策，改寫成「保障動物福祉的政策」較自然。","collocations":"assess the well-being of animals; protect animals' well-being; evidence of animals' well-being","example":"The sanctuary checked the well-being of animals after moving them to new enclosures.","exampleZh":"保護區把動物移往新圍欄後，檢查牠們的身心狀況。","contrast":"公司發表 animal welfare policy 是宣示或規則；well-being of animals 指牠們的實際狀態，須以觀察及健康資料判斷。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The reviewers assessed animal welfare by checking the elephants' health and stress levels after the journey.","zh":"評審在旅程後檢查大象的健康和壓力水平，以評估動物福利。","upgrade":"The reviewers assessed the well-being of animals by checking the elephants' health and stress levels after the journey.","answer":"the well-being of animals","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"the handlers' humane treatment of the elephants","explanation":"這是人怎樣對待大象；本句量度的是牠們旅程後的健康和壓力結果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the well-being of animals","explanation":"這個說法指動物實際身心狀況，正好由健康和壓力指標評估。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the conservation status of elephant populations","explanation":"物種數量是否穩定，無法單獨表示這些大象旅程後是否受壓。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the company's animal welfare pledge","explanation":"承諾是公司宣示，不是檢查大象所得的實際狀態。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the elephants' legal rights","explanation":"權利條文與這次量度的身體健康及壓力不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"the veterinary treatment planned for injured elephants","explanation":"這說的是受傷時會提供的醫療，非當下所有大象的健康與壓力結果。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Although the zoo published an animal welfare pledge, the researchers still measured animal welfare in its enclosures.","zh":"雖然動物園發表了動物福利承諾，研究員仍量度其圍欄內動物的實際福利狀況。","upgrade":"Although the zoo published an animal welfare pledge, the researchers still measured the well-being of animals in its enclosures.","answer":"the well-being of animals","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"the wording of the animal welfare pledge","explanation":"研究員量度的是圍欄內動物的情況，而非再次分析承諾措辭。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the keepers' humane handling procedures","explanation":"程序說明飼養員應如何操作，不能替代動物身心狀態的測量。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the veterinary care listed in the policy","explanation":"政策所列醫療安排是承諾的內容，未反映每隻動物在圍欄內是否健康。"},{"letter":"D","text":"the well-being of animals","explanation":"指研究員仍要測量的真實健康與壓力結果，與承諾作出區別。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the animals' legal rights under the pledge","explanation":"法律或承諾上的權利，不是研究員要量度的動物目前狀態。"},{"letter":"F","text":"the conservation status of the zoo's species","explanation":"某物種在野外的保育狀況，不能直接描述這些圍欄內個體的福利。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"humane treatment of animals","meaning":"人道對待動物","note":"聚焦人對動物的做法，例如避免造成不必要的痛楚，提供合適休息。它是促進福利的方式或標準，不是動物狀態的完整描述。","collocations":"standards for humane treatment of animals; ensure humane treatment during transport; train staff in humane treatment","example":"The tour operator trained its drivers in the humane treatment of animals during transport.","exampleZh":"旅遊營辦商訓練司機在運送動物期間人道地對待牠們。","contrast":"這個說法問「人怎樣做」；well-being 問「動物情況如何」。一次溫和運送不能單獨證明動物長期生活環境良好。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The new animal welfare rules require handlers to avoid painful restraints and give animals rest during transport.","zh":"新的動物福利規則要求管理員在運送期間避免使用會造成痛楚的束縛方式，並讓動物休息。","upgrade":"The new rules require humane treatment of animals during transport: handlers must avoid painful restraints and give them rest.","answer":"humane treatment of animals","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"conservation of the species during transport","explanation":"物種保育着重群體存續；本句規定管理員運送時如何避免個體疼痛。"},{"letter":"B","text":"veterinary treatment after transport injuries","explanation":"傷後治療有其價值，但原句重點是途中避免痛楚及讓動物休息。"},{"letter":"C","text":"humane treatment of animals","explanation":"避免痛苦束縛和安排休息，直接規定人應怎樣對待動物。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a published animal welfare pledge without handling rules","explanation":"原句是可執行的運送待遇規則，不只是沒有細則的宣言。"},{"letter":"E","text":"measurement of the animals' stress after transport","explanation":"事後量度狀況有助評估福利，但不是要求管理員當時採取的做法。"},{"letter":"F","text":"recognition of legal rights for all transported animals","explanation":"權利主張與避免疼痛束縛的具體操作要求不同。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The inspector checked the shelter's animal welfare practices by watching how staff fed and handled the rescued dogs.","zh":"督察觀察職員如何餵飼及接觸獲救的狗，以查核收容所的動物福利做法。","upgrade":"The inspector checked the humane treatment of animals at the shelter by watching how staff fed and handled the rescued dogs.","answer":"the humane treatment of animals at the shelter","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"the shelter's stated animal welfare policy","explanation":"政策是收容所聲稱會做的事；督察實際觀察職員如何對待狗。"},{"letter":"B","text":"the rescued dogs' long-term well-being measured by veterinary tests","explanation":"長期身心狀態很重要，但本句方法是觀察職員當下餵飼和接觸的方式。"},{"letter":"C","text":"the shelter's contribution to conservation of wild species","explanation":"野外物種保育與這間收容所職員如何對待獲救的狗不同。"},{"letter":"D","text":"veterinary treatment for every injured dog","explanation":"獸醫診治只涵蓋受傷後醫療；原句檢視日常餵飼和接觸方法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"the humane treatment of animals at the shelter","explanation":"聚焦職員餵飼、接觸動物是否人道，吻合督察觀察的對象。"},{"letter":"F","text":"the legal rights claimed for the rescued dogs","explanation":"權利主張與督察觀察到的實際人道待遇並非同一事項。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Animal rights · 權利主張與福利標準","zh":"中文辨析： Animal rights 關乎動物是否擁有某些不可侵犯的權利；animal welfare 可討論既有動物活動下怎樣減少傷害和改善生活狀態。兩者可同時被關注，不能當作同一個政策立場。若文章討論禁止所有動物表演的權利論證，前者才特別適用。","point":"Rights claims and welfare standards can overlap, but they are different claims."},{"word":"Animal protection / conservation · 保護個體與保育物種","zh":"中文辨析： Conservation 可着重防止物種滅絕；一個物種數量回升，不代表每隻圈養動物都活得健康。Animal protection 範圍較廣，可談防虐待；若要說具體的身心狀態，仍須寫清楚。保育數量的句子才適合 conservation。","point":"Conserving a species does not by itself establish the welfare of each animal."},{"word":"Policy / pledge versus outcome · 承諾不等於成果","zh":"中文辨析： 原文出現政策及承諾，但文件存在不能證明動物沒有壓力；同樣，景點有動物表演也不能在缺乏資料時自動推斷每隻動物受虐。評估福利要看待遇和動物的實際情況。","point":"A welfare pledge is a commitment; good welfare is a condition requiring evidence."},{"word":"Animal care / veterinary care · 照料只是部分條件","zh":"中文辨析： 餵食與獸醫診治有助動物福利，但如活動造成持續壓力，單有醫療仍不足夠。若句子只說「治療受傷動物」，veterinary care 較精確；不能用它概括整體福利。","point":"Care practices contribute to welfare but do not automatically describe the whole condition."}],"moduleNumber":94},{"id":"lesson-095","sourceId":72,"headword":"animal-assisted therapy","title":"Animal-assisted therapy","titleZh":"動物輔助治療","subtitle":"動物輔助治療","description":"原文： 2018 DSE Speaking 8.1〈Animal-assisted Therapy〉說：“Animal-assisted therapy was once rare and met with the objection that it would only make hospitals dirty.” 此處是把與動物互動納入治療安排；昔日反對者擔心醫院衛生。Therapy 要有治療目的，並非單純把寵物帶入病房。原文轉述的是一種反對意見，並非證實這種治療必然令醫院骯髒。以下練習皆為原創。","sourceSense":"原文： 2018 DSE Speaking 8.1〈Animal-assisted Therapy〉說：“Animal-assisted therapy was once rare and met with the objection that it would only make hospitals dirty.” 此處是把與動物互動納入治療安排；昔日反對者擔心醫院衛生。Therapy 要有治療目的，並非單純把寵物帶入病房。原文轉述的是一種反對意見，並非證實這種治療必然令醫院骯髒。以下練習皆為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["therapy involving animals","直接的描述性改寫","說明治療安排中有動物參與；須保留「治療」而非泛指任何接觸。"],["animal-supported treatment","可理解但不夠自然；不列為核心教學答案","Supported 可能讓人誤以為動物獨自提供醫療支援。清楚的 therapy with the help of animals 更適合日常釋義。"]],"note":"覆核後的範圍： Pet therapy 口語常見，但 pet 把可參與的動物類別縮窄，且不同場景可能把探訪活動也稱為 pet therapy；本課把它列為有條件的近詞。Animal-assisted intervention 是較廣的總稱，可能包括非治療活動；animal therapy 容易指治療動物本身。這個專門詞組沒有必要硬湊十四項。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["重點","適用表達","留意"],"rows":[["用一般語言說有動物參與的治療","therapy involving animals","仍須有治療目標"],["強調動物促進病人練習與互動","animal-facilitated therapy","治療師不被動物取代"],["對一般讀者說明輔助關係","therapy with the help of animals","不表示保證治癒"]],"note":"原文提及曾有人擔心醫院衛生；那是一種反對意見。判斷這種治療的效果或衛生風險，應另看具體計劃及證據。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"therapy involving animals","meaning":"涉及動物的治療","note":"以一般語言說明治療過程有動物參與；仍須有清楚的治療目標。Involving animals 修飾 therapy，不表示動物是接受治療的病人。","collocations":"offer therapy involving animals; a programme of therapy involving animals; evaluate therapy involving animals","example":"The hospital piloted therapy involving animals for patients who wanted extra support during rehabilitation.","exampleZh":"醫院試辦涉及動物的治療計劃，供希望在復康期間得到額外支援的病人參加。","contrast":"這是清楚而較寬的描述；若只是義工帶狗來探訪，未有治療目標，不宜只因有動物在場便稱為 therapy。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The hospital's animal-assisted therapy programme has written treatment goals and scheduled sessions with trained staff.","zh":"醫院的動物輔助治療計劃有書面治療目標，並安排由受訓職員參與的定期課節。","upgrade":"The hospital's programme of therapy involving animals has written treatment goals and scheduled sessions with trained staff.","answer":"a programme of therapy involving animals","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a programme of therapy involving animals","explanation":"保留動物參與、治療目標和受訓職員安排，適合描述這個計劃。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a programme of animal visits for companionship without treatment goals","explanation":"陪伴探訪沒有保留原句明說的書面治療目標。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a broad animal-assisted activity programme that need not be therapy","explanation":"「動物參與活動」範圍太廣；這裏的定期課節有治療目標。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a programme of animal-assisted education rather than patient therapy","explanation":"動物輔助教學也可有目標，但原句明指病人治療目標。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a rehabilitation plan with a support animal present but no planned interaction","explanation":"只有動物在場，沒有原句所指安排好的動物參與課節。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a supervised social-visit programme with no assessed treatment goals","explanation":"即使有監督，純社交探訪仍缺原句的書面治療目標。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Researchers compared animal-assisted therapy with ordinary rehabilitation and separately checked the hospital's hygiene rules.","zh":"研究員比較動物輔助治療與一般復康治療，另行查核醫院的衛生規則。","upgrade":"Researchers compared therapy involving animals with ordinary rehabilitation and separately checked the hospital's hygiene rules.","answer":"a study comparing therapy involving animals with ordinary rehabilitation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a study comparing supervised animal visits with ordinary rehabilitation, without therapy goals","explanation":"原句的一方是有治療目標的動物輔助治療，不只是受監督探訪。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a study comparing therapy involving animals with ordinary rehabilitation","explanation":"保留兩種病人復康方式的比較，並容許衛生規則另作檢查。"},{"letter":"C","text":"a study of hygiene rules only, without comparing patient treatment","explanation":"原句另行查核衛生，重點比較仍是兩種病人復康方式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a study of animal-assisted activities without defined rehabilitation goals","explanation":"把有治療目標的 therapy 降成未定目標的一般動物活動。"},{"letter":"E","text":"a comparison of patients' enjoyment of pet visits rather than their rehabilitation","explanation":"病人是否喜歡探訪不等同復康效果比較。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a study assuming animal-assisted treatment must be superior to ordinary rehabilitation","explanation":"研究「比較」兩者，未預設動物參與的一方必定更好。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"animal-facilitated therapy","meaning":"由動物協助進行的治療","note":"可見於較舊材料的近義說法；現時正式分類仍宜優先用原文 animal-assisted therapy。它強調動物有助治療師與病人互動或達成治療目標；facilitated 不表示動物取代臨床人員。","collocations":"animal-facilitated therapy sessions; a supervised animal-facilitated therapy programme; use animal-facilitated therapy","example":"The therapist used animal-facilitated therapy to encourage the child to practise speaking.","exampleZh":"治療師使用動物輔助的治療方法，鼓勵孩子練習說話。","contrast":"比一般 therapy involving animals 更突出動物促進治療互動；若動物只在大樓內而沒參與活動，這個說法過強。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"During animal-assisted therapy, a therapist asked the child to give the dog spoken instructions as part of a language goal.","zh":"在動物輔助治療期間，治療師請孩子向狗說出口頭指令，作為語言訓練目標的一部分。","upgrade":"During animal-facilitated therapy, a therapist asked the child to give the dog spoken instructions as part of a language goal.","answer":"animal-facilitated therapy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a supervised animal visit with no language goal","explanation":"有監督仍不足夠；原句還有清楚的孩子語言訓練目標。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a speech session in which the dog was present but took no part","explanation":"狗是孩子口頭指令的對象，並非只在旁邊。"},{"letter":"C","text":"animal-facilitated therapy","explanation":"狗協助治療師引出孩子的說話練習，切合 facilitated 的意思。"},{"letter":"D","text":"an animal-assisted activity judged only by whether the child enjoyed it","explanation":"原句用口頭指令服務語言目標，不只量度孩子是否玩得開心。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an emotional-support dog present for comfort but not used for speaking practice","explanation":"原句讓孩子向狗發出口頭指令，狗不只是安靜陪伴。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a structured speech lesson without the dog taking part","explanation":"保留治療目標，卻漏掉狗作為孩子說話對象的輔助作用。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The physiotherapist used animal-assisted therapy to motivate a recovering patient to practise walking beside a trained dog under supervision.","zh":"物理治療師運用動物輔助治療，鼓勵復康中的病人在監督下練習與受訓犬並肩步行。","upgrade":"The physiotherapist used animal-facilitated therapy to motivate a recovering patient to practise walking beside a trained dog under supervision.","answer":"animal-facilitated therapy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"an ordinary dog visit without a walking goal","explanation":"原句明說病人藉與狗並肩步行練習走路，而非只接受探訪。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a supervised walk in which the dog was present but did not support the exercise","explanation":"狗用來鼓勵病人走路，並非偶然在場。"},{"letter":"C","text":"animal-assisted education about how to walk dogs safely","explanation":"教人遛狗的知識課，並非病人為復康而實際練習步行。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animal-facilitated therapy","explanation":"受訓犬促進病人完成物理治療師安排的步行練習，符合輔助角色。"},{"letter":"E","text":"an animal-assisted activity measured only by the patient's enjoyment","explanation":"目標是步行復康，不能縮成病人是否喜歡狗。"},{"letter":"F","text":"a normal physiotherapy walk with the dog kept outside the exercise area","explanation":"保留物理治療，卻刪去了受訓犬對病人走路的鼓勵作用。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"therapy with the help of animals","meaning":"借助動物的治療","note":"面向一般讀者的解釋性改寫，指治療仍由專業人員規劃，動物作為輔助。句中須說清楚治療的是人，而不是動物。","collocations":"provide therapy with the help of animals; receive therapy with the help of animals; support rehabilitation with the help of animals","example":"Some patients received therapy with the help of animals as part of a supervised rehabilitation plan.","exampleZh":"部分病人接受借助動物的治療，作為受監督復康計劃的一部分。","contrast":"這是說明方式而非專業分類名稱；不等於醫院只讓病人自由抱寵物，也不能保證對每名病人有效。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The leaflet explains animal-assisted therapy to families as a planned treatment in which patients interact with animals under staff supervision.","zh":"單張向家屬解釋動物輔助治療是一種預先安排的治療：病人在職員監督下與動物互動。","upgrade":"The leaflet explains therapy with the help of animals to families as a planned treatment in which patients interact with animals under staff supervision.","answer":"therapy with the help of animals","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a planned animal visit meant only to provide companionship","explanation":"陪伴探訪可有益，但沒有保留單張所寫的病人治療安排。"},{"letter":"B","text":"therapy with the help of animals","explanation":"以淺白語言保留動物輔助、病人治療及職員監督。"},{"letter":"C","text":"an animal-assisted activity with no stated treatment goal","explanation":"單張明確稱為有計劃的治療，不能退成任何動物參與活動。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a therapy session in which an animal is merely in the building","explanation":"病人須在職員監督下與動物互動；動物只在大樓內不足夠。"},{"letter":"E","text":"comfort from an emotional-support animal outside planned treatment sessions","explanation":"舒適陪伴有價值，但沒有保留單張的治療計劃及職員監督互動。"},{"letter":"F","text":"animal-assisted education for families about hospital pet care","explanation":"給家屬的教育可涉及動物，單張描述的卻是病人接受治療。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"After discussing the treatment plan, the patient chose animal-assisted therapy as one part of her supervised recovery programme.","zh":"病人討論治療計劃後，選擇動物輔助治療作為受監督復康計劃的一部分。","upgrade":"After discussing the treatment plan, the patient chose therapy with the help of animals as one part of her supervised recovery programme.","answer":"therapy with the help of animals as one part of recovery","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"a supervised animal-assisted activity outside her treatment plan","explanation":"即使有人監督，若不屬治療計劃就丟失原句的復康目標。"},{"letter":"B","text":"a supervised recreational animal visit kept outside her rehabilitation plan","explanation":"即使有人監督，純消閒探訪若不在復康計劃內，就不是她選擇的治療環節。"},{"letter":"C","text":"therapy with the help of animals as one part of recovery","explanation":"保留動物輔助、病人自選及復康計劃其中一環的範圍。"},{"letter":"D","text":"a relaxation session with an animal but no defined recovery goal","explanation":"放鬆活動或有幫助，但沒有原句受監督復康計劃中的治療目標。"},{"letter":"E","text":"comfort from an emotional-support animal in the ward without a therapy session","explanation":"動物在病房提供陪伴，不等於病人所選的受監督復康治療環節。"},{"letter":"F","text":"animal-assisted intervention that need not involve therapy","explanation":"這個上位詞可包括非治療活動，沒有交代病人選擇的是復康治療的一部分。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Animal-assisted activity / pet visit · 探訪未必是治療","zh":"中文辨析： 動物探訪可以令人愉快，但如沒有明確治療目標及安排，就不能自動改稱 therapy。若句子只說義工帶寵物探望病人，pet visit 才貼切。","point":"A friendly animal visit is not necessarily a planned therapeutic intervention."},{"word":"Animal-assisted intervention · 較廣的總稱","zh":"中文辨析： Intervention 可包括治療、教育或其他有目的的動物參與活動。原文特指 therapy，不能把所有介入方式當作同一種醫療治療；若文章概述各類計劃，可使用較廣名稱。","point":"Therapy can be one kind of animal-assisted intervention; the umbrella term is wider."},{"word":"Veterinary treatment / animal therapy · 誰接受治療","zh":"中文辨析： 獸醫診治病犬是 treatment for an animal；原文卻說動物幫助病人接受治療。Animal therapy 若不交代方向，可能被理解成替動物治病。若真的是受傷動物接受治療，獸醫說法才適合。","point":"In the source, the animal assists a patient's therapy; it is not the patient."},{"word":"Animal-supported treatment / cure · 支援不等於包治","zh":"中文辨析： 原圖譜的 animal-supported treatment 可猜到意思，但不是本課最清楚的常用表達；cure 更誤導，因為輔助治療不保證治癒。若個別研究真的量度某種治療效果，必須按其證據說明，不能一概稱「治癒」。","point":"Animal involvement may support treatment without replacing clinicians or guaranteeing a cure."}],"moduleNumber":95},{"id":"lesson-096","sourceId":75,"headword":"anime movies","title":"Anime movies","titleZh":"日本動畫電影","subtitle":"日本動畫電影","description":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 4.1〈Why Spirited Away Changed Animation Forever〉說：“In 2001, one of the most celebrated anime movies hit theatres in Japan.” 此處指日本動畫電影，例子是《千與千尋》。Movies 是可數的電影；anime 指日本動畫類別。若改成 anime series，就把戲院上映的電影錯換成電視系列。以下例句及問題均為原創。","sourceSense":"原文： 2025 DSE Speaking 4.1〈Why Spirited Away Changed Animation Forever〉說：“In 2001, one of the most celebrated anime movies hit theatres in Japan.” 此處指日本動畫電影，例子是《千與千尋》。Movies 是可數的電影；anime 指日本動畫類別。若改成 anime series，就把戲院上映的電影錯換成電視系列。以下例句及問題均為原創。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["Japanese animated films","直接","同時保留日本來源、動畫媒介、電影格式；最適合向不熟悉 anime 的讀者解說。"],["anime films","直接，正式度略高","Films 與 movies 可在此互換，仍需保留 anime；沒有自動表示所有動畫電影都來自日本。"]],"note":"補充候選覆核： Japanese animated feature films 只在片長／長篇電影語境適用；《千與千尋》是長篇電影，但不能用它概括所有短片。Japanese cartoons 容易縮窄成年齡語感或短篇作品；manga adaptations 需有漫畫改編證據；animated films in Japanese 說語言，不保證日本製作。這三組在第 4 節辨明。Japanese animation films 語序較不自然，應用 Japanese animated films。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["句子需要保留的資訊","選用","留意"],"rows":[["向一般讀者解釋日本來源的動畫電影","Japanese animated films","Animated 不能省掉"],["在影評或片單中把 movies 換成較正式的名詞","anime films","仍指電影而非電視系列"],["已知是長篇電影並要與短片區分","Japanese animated feature films","Feature 增加片長限制"]],"note":"原文的《千與千尋》是電影例子；它能支持 feature film 的說法，但不足以把所有 anime 一律縮成長篇電影。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Japanese animated films","meaning":"日本動畫電影","note":"直接把 anime movies 解釋成日本製作的動畫電影。Films 可數；一部為 a Japanese animated film，多部為 Japanese animated films。","collocations":"watch Japanese animated films; a festival of Japanese animated films; a Japanese animated film released in cinemas","example":"The cinema screened three Japanese animated films over the weekend.","exampleZh":"戲院在週末放映了三部日本動畫電影。","contrast":"保留作品來源與電影格式；animated films in Japanese 只說配音／語言，不足以確立日本製作。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The festival will screen anime movies produced by Japanese studios, not the studios' television series.","zh":"影展將放映日本工作室製作的動畫電影，而不是那些工作室的電視系列。","upgrade":"The festival will screen Japanese animated films instead of television series by the same studios.","answer":"Japanese animated films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese live-action films","explanation":"保留日本來源及電影格式，卻把動畫換成真人作品。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese animated television series","explanation":"保留動畫及來源，但與句末明確排除的電視系列相撞。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese animated films","explanation":"同時保留日本工作室、動畫與供影展放映的電影格式。"},{"letter":"D","text":"animated films dubbed into Japanese but made abroad","explanation":"日語配音不等於由日本工作室製作，還改了原句來源。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Japanese manga volumes adapted for reading rooms","explanation":"漫畫卷冊不是影展要放映的電影。"},{"letter":"F","text":"short Japanese animation clips made only for television","explanation":"電視短片不符合此處與電視系列對比的電影節目。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The catalogue lists anime movies made in Japan, although some are available with English rather than Japanese soundtracks.","zh":"目錄列出在日本製作的動畫電影，儘管其中一些提供英語而非日語聲帶。","upgrade":"The catalogue lists Japanese animated films, although some are available with English rather than Japanese soundtracks.","answer":"Japanese animated films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese animated films","explanation":"製作來源與動畫電影身分不受英語聲帶影響。"},{"letter":"B","text":"animated films spoken only in Japanese","explanation":"原句明說部分作品有英語聲帶，不應限定只能是日語。"},{"letter":"C","text":"animated films made abroad and later dubbed in Japanese","explanation":"把在日本製作改成海外製作，也錯把語言當來源。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Japanese live-action films with English soundtracks","explanation":"即使聲帶條件相似，真人電影仍缺少動畫特徵。"},{"letter":"E","text":"television anime episodes with English subtitles","explanation":"電視集數不是目錄列出的電影，字幕也與聲帶不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"manga volumes translated into English","explanation":"翻譯漫畫是另一種媒介，不能與電影聲帶混同。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"anime films","meaning":"日本動畫電影；較偏電影評論用語","note":"Film 比 movie 在影評、影展介紹中略正式，但此處的格式仍是電影。Anime 本身修飾可數 films；一部為 an anime film。","collocations":"critically acclaimed anime films; an anime film festival; release an anime film","example":"The critic reviewed two anime films released by Japanese studios that summer.","exampleZh":"影評人評論了兩部那年夏天由日本工作室推出的動畫電影。","contrast":"與 anime movies 最接近，只換較正式的電影名詞；不能將 film 解讀成拍攝用膠卷，也不能把它改成電視 series。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The reviewer compared three anime movies that opened in Japanese cinemas, discussing their stories and visual style.","zh":"影評人比較了三部在日本戲院上映的動畫電影，討論它們的故事和視覺風格。","upgrade":"The reviewer compared three anime films that opened in Japanese cinemas, discussing their stories and visual style.","answer":"anime films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"anime television series","explanation":"電視系列通常按集播放，原句明說三部在戲院上映的電影。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese manga stories","explanation":"漫畫有故事，但不是供影評人評論視覺電影的戲院作品。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese-style animated shorts made abroad","explanation":"把日本動畫電影改成海外製作的短片，來源和格式都變了。"},{"letter":"D","text":"anime films","explanation":"在影評語域自然，保留三部日本動畫電影在戲院上映的事實。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Japanese live-action films","explanation":"失去動畫媒介。"},{"letter":"F","text":"anime soundtracks without the films","explanation":"聲帶只是影片一部分，無法承載整部電影的故事與視覺風格。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The library bought licences for five anime movies so members could stream the complete films, not just view trailers.","zh":"圖書館購買了五部日本動畫電影的授權，讓會員可以串流觀看完整電影，而不只是看預告片。","upgrade":"The library bought licences for five anime films so members could stream the complete films, not just view trailers.","answer":"five anime films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"five anime trailers","explanation":"原句明確對比完整電影與預告片，不能只買預告片授權。"},{"letter":"B","text":"five anime television episodes","explanation":"集數與五部完整電影的授權格式不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"five volumes of manga","explanation":"漫畫卷冊不會作為完整電影串流播放。"},{"letter":"D","text":"five Japanese animated advertisements","explanation":"廣告可能有動畫，但不是完整敘事電影。"},{"letter":"E","text":"five anime films","explanation":"保留五部可數的日本動畫電影及完整串流內容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"five Japanese films regardless of whether they are animated","explanation":"把作品範圍擴至真人電影，失去 anime 限定。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Japanese animated feature films","meaning":"日本長篇動畫電影","note":"Feature film 指長篇電影；只在明確是長片時才可收窄 anime movies。原文例子《千與千尋》符合，但一組包含動畫短片的電影不可整組這樣稱呼。","collocations":"award-winning Japanese animated feature films; a Japanese animated feature film; feature films shown at the festival","example":"The retrospective included Japanese animated feature films with full cinema releases.","exampleZh":"回顧影展收錄了曾正式在戲院上映的日本長篇動畫電影。","contrast":"比 Japanese animated films 窄，增加片長／長篇格式條件；若原句只說短片，不應補入 feature。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The archive specialises in anime movies that run for more than an hour and had full theatrical releases in Japan.","zh":"該檔案館專門收藏片長超過一小時、曾在日本正式於戲院上映的日本動畫電影。","upgrade":"The archive specialises in Japanese animated feature films that run for more than an hour and had full theatrical releases in Japan.","answer":"Japanese animated feature films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese animated television episodes","explanation":"電視集數不符合超過一小時並正式在戲院上映的描述。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese animated shorts lasting ten minutes","explanation":"十分鐘短片與原句的長篇片長不符。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese animated feature films","explanation":"Feature 精確指出長篇、戲院放映的日本動畫電影。"},{"letter":"D","text":"live-action feature films from Japan","explanation":"片長和來源雖可能相同，但真人拍攝不符合動畫條件。"},{"letter":"E","text":"manga adaptations of any length, whether animated or not","explanation":"漫畫改編不是已證實來源，且可包括非動畫及短作品。"},{"letter":"F","text":"Japanese-style animated films made abroad","explanation":"改了檔案館收藏的日本來源。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The curator placed anime movies of feature length on one shelf and five-minute animated shorts on another.","zh":"策展人把長篇日本動畫電影放在一個架上，五分鐘動畫短片則放在另一個架上。","upgrade":"The curator placed Japanese animated feature films on one shelf and five-minute animated shorts on another.","answer":"Japanese animated feature films","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Japanese animated shorts","explanation":"這些五分鐘短片已另放一架，不能拿來稱前面的長片。"},{"letter":"B","text":"Japanese animated feature films","explanation":"保留日本動畫電影及明示的長篇條件，與另一架短片分開。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Japanese animated television series","explanation":"電視系列既非這裏的電影，也沒有對應長片分類。"},{"letter":"D","text":"any Japanese film including live-action works","explanation":"擴大到真人電影，失去策展人的動畫分類。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Japanese-style films with no known origin","explanation":"只說風格，不能保留日本動畫電影來源。"},{"letter":"F","text":"manga volumes that inspired films","explanation":"原句分類的是可放映的動畫長片，不是原著漫畫卷冊。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Anime series / animated shorts · 電影格式不能消失","zh":"中文辨析： Anime series 是分集系列；animated shorts 是短片。原文說 movies 在戲院上映。若題目明說每週一集或只有五分鐘，才選相應格式；不可單憑同屬動畫就取代電影。","point":"A series and a short may be anime, but they are not feature-length cinema films."},{"word":"Manga / manga adaptation · 漫畫與改編來源","zh":"中文辨析： Manga 是漫畫，不是可在戲院放映的動畫電影。Manga adaptation 還額外主張電影取材自漫畫；原文沒有提供這種來源證據。若某作品明確改編自漫畫，才可另說是 manga adaptation。","point":"Anime film names the screen medium; a manga adaptation makes an extra source claim."},{"word":"Animated films in Japanese / Japanese-style films · 語言、風格、產地","zh":"中文辨析： 以日語配音的動畫可由別國製作；有日式風格也不保證出自日本工作室。若原句要說日本動畫作品來源，應使用 Japanese animated films；若只知放映語言或風格，不能硬推來源。","point":"Language and style are different from Japanese production origin."},{"word":"Japanese movies / cartoons · 媒介範圍","zh":"中文辨析： Japanese movies 可包括真人電影，失去動畫條件；cartoons 範圍及語感可能偏電視或兒童向，亦未必來自日本。若確實談所有日本電影，前者才合適；若談兒童卡通節目，後者可用。","point":"Japanese movies may be live-action; cartoons need not be Japanese cinema films."}],"moduleNumber":96},{"id":"lesson-097","sourceId":78,"headword":"annual passes","title":"Annual passes","titleZh":"年票","subtitle":"年票","description":"原文： 2019 DSE Speaking 7.1〈A Hong Kong Drink〉說：“The winners will receive two free annual passes for Ocean Park.” 此處是海洋公園的年度入場證，每名得獎者所得票數須依比賽規則理解；原句只說有兩張免費年票，沒有列明啟用日、有效期計法、適用日期或其他會員權益。以下練習會把額外條款寫進原創句子，不能倒推為試卷或海洋公園實際條款。","sourceSense":"原文： 2019 DSE Speaking 7.1〈A Hong Kong Drink〉說：“The winners will receive two free annual passes for Ocean Park.” 此處是海洋公園的年度入場證，每名得獎者所得票數須依比賽規則理解；原句只說有兩張免費年票，沒有列明啟用日、有效期計法、適用日期或其他會員權益。以下練習會把額外條款寫進原創句子，不能倒推為試卷或海洋公園實際條款。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","理由"],"rows":[["year-long admission passes","近義；有效期說明","可說明按年有效的入場證，但不可憑此推斷完全無限制進場或由領獎日起算。"],["annual tickets","含糊，不作核心答案","Ticket 可能只准單次入場；只有產品明確把年票稱為 annual/season ticket 時才可用。此處 pass 更清楚。"]],"note":"補充候選覆核： Passes valid for twelve months 在原創句明確規定連續十二個月時很準確；若票只在某個曆年有效，仍須按條款說。Annual entry passes 保留「可入場的年票」功能，但不保證免預約或包括所有特別活動。Memberships 可能另有折扣和會員服務，不能單獨視為同一產品；day tickets 明顯有效期較短。這些在第 4 節說明。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["題目明說的重點","選用","避免推斷"],"rows":[["一年期、用於入場","year-long admission passes","不是一日票"],["有清楚的連續十二個月起算條款","passes valid for twelve months","不等於可進場十二次"],["與會員折扣等其他權益分開，強調入場","annual entry passes","不保證所有特別活動免費"]],"note":"試卷只說得獎者會獲兩張海洋公園免費年票。任何精確的啟用日、預約規則及附帶權益都要以票面條款為準。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"year-long admission passes","meaning":"一年期入場證","note":"強調證件可在一段約一年的有效期內用作入場；admission 指入場。具體開始和終止日期由條款決定，不能從 year-long 自行算出。","collocations":"win year-long admission passes; activate year-long admission passes; terms for year-long admission passes","example":"The museum awarded year-long admission passes that could be activated before December.","exampleZh":"博物館送出一年期入場證，可於十二月之前啟用。","contrast":"比 annual passes 明說入場與時間長度；它並未說持證人每天都可進場，實際限制須查看票款條件。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The prize notice offers two annual passes for the museum rather than two tickets for a single visit.","zh":"獎品通告提供兩張博物館年票，而不是兩張只限單次參觀的門票。","upgrade":"The prize notice offers two year-long admission passes for the museum rather than two tickets for a single visit.","answer":"two year-long admission passes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"two single-visit admission tickets","explanation":"通告特別把年票與只限單次的票區分，不能換成後者。"},{"letter":"B","text":"two museum memberships with unspecified entry rights","explanation":"會員資格未必包括題目明說的入場證權利。"},{"letter":"C","text":"two year-long admission passes","explanation":"保留兩張入場證的年度期限，也與單次門票形成正確對比。"},{"letter":"D","text":"two vouchers valid only on the award day","explanation":"只在得獎當日有效，與年度有效期不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"two passes for one exhibition only","explanation":"把博物館入場權縮成一次特定展覽，原句沒有此限制。"},{"letter":"F","text":"two subscriptions to the museum newsletter","explanation":"訂閱通訊不構成入場憑證。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The zoo's annual passes last for a year, although holders must still book a time slot before visiting.","zh":"動物園年票有效一年，但持票人到訪前仍須預約時段。","upgrade":"The zoo's year-long admission passes still require holders to book a time slot before visiting.","answer":"year-long admission passes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"passes allowing entry on one named day only","explanation":"單日有效與原句一年期限不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"memberships guaranteeing every special event for free","explanation":"無據地增加特別活動權益，原句只談入場及預約。"},{"letter":"C","text":"passes allowing unlimited entry without booking","explanation":"直接違反仍須預約的條款。"},{"letter":"D","text":"year-long admission passes","explanation":"保留一年有效的入場權，沒有取消預約要求。"},{"letter":"E","text":"passes that expire after one visit","explanation":"一次後失效與年票性質不同。"},{"letter":"F","text":"subscriptions to the zoo's booking website","explanation":"網站訂閱不等於可入場的年票。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"passes valid for twelve months","meaning":"有效期為十二個月的入場證","note":"在條款明確說從某日起連續有效十二個月時，作完整的關係子句改寫。Twelve months 說有效期，不是十二次入場。","collocations":"passes valid for twelve months from activation; issue passes valid for twelve months; two passes valid for twelve months","example":"The aquarium issued passes valid for twelve months from the first visit.","exampleZh":"水族館發出由首次到訪日起計、有效期十二個月的入場證。","contrast":"比泛稱 annual passes 更精確地規定期限；原試卷沒有起算條款，所以本說法只在原創情境明示時可用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The aquarium's annual passes remain valid for twelve months starting on the date of the holder's first visit.","zh":"水族館年票由持票人首次到訪日起計，有效期為十二個月。","upgrade":"The aquarium issues passes valid for twelve months from the holder's first visit.","answer":"passes valid for twelve months","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"passes valid for twelve visits","explanation":"把十二個月期限誤當成最多十二次入場。"},{"letter":"B","text":"passes valid only until the end of this calendar year","explanation":"曆年年底截止未必等於首次到訪後十二個月。"},{"letter":"C","text":"passes valid for twelve months","explanation":"明確說明從首次到訪日起的連續十二個月期限。"},{"letter":"D","text":"passes valid for twelve days","explanation":"把月錯成日，期限短得多。"},{"letter":"E","text":"tickets for a single visit made within twelve months","explanation":"一年內只准一次入場，不等於全年有效的年票。"},{"letter":"F","text":"memberships whose entry benefits have not been stated","explanation":"未說明入場權的會員資格不能代替明確期限的入場證。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The theme park's annual passes expire exactly twelve months after activation, even if the holder first uses them later.","zh":"主題公園年票啟用後剛好十二個月到期，即使持票人較遲才首次使用也一樣。","upgrade":"The theme park's passes are valid for twelve months from activation, even if the holder first uses them later.","answer":"passes valid for twelve months from activation","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"passes valid for twelve months from activation","explanation":"保留啟用日起算及後來才首次使用亦不順延的規則。"},{"letter":"B","text":"passes valid for twelve months from first use","explanation":"把起算日推遲至首次使用，與題目明訂啟用日起算不符。"},{"letter":"C","text":"passes valid for the current calendar year only","explanation":"曆年年底到期未必是啟用後十二個月。"},{"letter":"D","text":"passes admitting the holder twelve times","explanation":"把有效期誤解成入場次數。"},{"letter":"E","text":"passes extended by twelve months after every visit","explanation":"無據加入每次入場都順延的權益。"},{"letter":"F","text":"tickets usable only on the activation date","explanation":"只可在啟用日用，失去其後十二個月期限。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"annual entry passes","meaning":"每年有效的入場證","note":"簡潔說明該證件的核心用途是入場，適合與餐飲折扣、單次門票等其他獎品區分。Entry pass 可數；兩張為 two annual entry passes。","collocations":"annual entry passes to the park; offer annual entry passes as prizes; holders of annual entry passes","example":"The raffle's first prize included two annual entry passes to the wildlife park.","exampleZh":"抽獎頭獎包括兩張野生動物公園的年度入場證。","contrast":"重點是「入場」，不是會員全部服務；annual tickets 容易被誤當作普通一日門票，需看產品名稱。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The contest awards annual passes to the park; the notice mentions admission but no extra membership discounts.","zh":"比賽送出公園年票；通告提到入場權，卻沒有提及額外會員折扣。","upgrade":"The contest awards annual entry passes to the park; the notice mentions admission but no extra membership discounts.","answer":"annual entry passes","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"annual discount-only memberships","explanation":"只提供折扣而未含入場，與通告明說的入場權不同。"},{"letter":"B","text":"one-day admission tickets","explanation":"一日票不足以表達年票期限。"},{"letter":"C","text":"annual entry passes","explanation":"同時表達年度入場憑證，並未額外添加未載明的會員折扣。"},{"letter":"D","text":"entry vouchers valid for one named event","explanation":"單次特定活動票比公園年票範圍窄。"},{"letter":"E","text":"year-long newsletters about the park","explanation":"一年通訊不是入場證。"},{"letter":"F","text":"passes that include every special event for free","explanation":"通告未承諾所有特別活動都免費。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The draw gives the winning family two annual passes for the science centre, one for each parent; the children's tickets are separate.","zh":"抽獎向中獎家庭送出兩張科學中心年票，父母各得一張；孩子們的門票另行處理。","upgrade":"The draw gives the winning family two annual entry passes for the parents to use at the science centre; the children's tickets are separate.","answer":"two annual entry passes for the parents","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"two family memberships covering every child","explanation":"把父母各一張的年票擴成全家會員，與孩子票另計相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"two single-entry tickets for the parents","explanation":"保留兩人數量，但把年度憑證縮成一次入場票。"},{"letter":"C","text":"two passes for a single science show","explanation":"只限一場表演，不能概括中心年票。"},{"letter":"D","text":"two annual entry passes for the parents","explanation":"保留兩張、父母各一、年度入場證三項關鍵資料。"},{"letter":"E","text":"two yearly newsletters addressed to the parents","explanation":"按年寄通訊不提供入場權。"},{"letter":"F","text":"two passes guaranteeing all extra workshops","explanation":"無據加入所有工作坊權益，原句只說中心入場。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Day ticket / single-entry ticket · 一次門票","zh":"中文辨析： 一日票或單次入場票不等於年度通行證。即使免費送兩張，一次票仍只按其單次／當日條款使用。若比賽實際送的是兩張一日票，才可這樣寫。","point":"Two single-entry tickets are not two annual passes."},{"word":"Annual ticket / season ticket · 產品命名須核實","zh":"中文辨析： 某些場館的 season ticket 確實類似年票，但單獨 annual ticket 可能含糊；ticket 不必然可多次入場。若官方條款明確把產品命名為 annual ticket，可採用，但本課優先用 pass。","point":"Ticket terminology depends on the product; pass signals continuing admission more clearly."},{"word":"Membership / subscription · 權益可能不同","zh":"中文辨析： 會員資格可能含折扣、活動預訂等額外福利，也可能不含免費入場；訂閱通常指持續付款服務。原句只保證贈送年票，不能把它說成所有會員權益已包括。","point":"Membership benefits need not match the admission rights of an annual pass."},{"word":"Unlimited entry / free access everywhere · 年票不代表無條件","zh":"中文辨析： 年票可有預約、指定日子或特別活動限制；試卷沒有提供這些條款。若題目只說 annual passes，不能添加「每天無限次進場」或「所有場館都免費」。只有票面明確規定時才可說。","point":"Annual validity does not by itself prove unrestricted access."}],"moduleNumber":97},{"id":"lesson-098","sourceId":94,"headword":"architectural heritage","title":"Architectural heritage","titleZh":"珍貴的歷史建築環境","subtitle":"珍貴的歷史建築環境","description":"The 2012 DSE set 5.1 passage says Hong Kong’s tycoons and prominent citizens have been accused of destroying the city’s environment and “architectural heritage” for profit. The accusation is attributed, not proved by this wording. Here architectural heritage is the valued, inherited physical fabric of the city: buildings and, where context supports it, related streetscapes and structures. It is neither the academic field of architecture nor only inherited building skills. All exercises are original.","sourceSense":"The 2012 DSE set 5.1 passage says Hong Kong’s tycoons and prominent citizens have been accused of destroying the city’s environment and “architectural heritage” for profit. The accusation is attributed, not proved by this wording. Here architectural heritage is the valued, inherited physical fabric of the city: buildings and, where context supports it, related streetscapes and structures. It is neither the academic field of architecture nor only inherited building skills. All exercises are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["historic built environment","有條件近義","包含歷史建築及街道等人造環境，可能比單棟建築範圍廣。"],["inherited building traditions","假近義","指代代相傳的建造知識與習俗，非原文可能被拆毀的有形場所。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： 補入保育用語 built heritage、明確指單棟／多棟的 historic buildings、強調前人留下物質成果的 architectural legacy。Cultural heritage 可含語言和習俗，太廣；old buildings 僅表示年久，未必有保育價值。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["指稱範圍","合適表達"],"rows":[["具價值的人造建築資產總稱","built heritage"],["明確是多棟有歷史價值樓宇","historic buildings"],["樓宇連同街道、廣場等整體","historic built environment"],["前代留下的實體建築成果","architectural legacy"]],"note":"Inherited building traditions 指技藝，不等於可遭拆毀的建築遺產；architecture 是建築學／設計領域（參見 0095）。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"built heritage","meaning":"建成環境遺產","note":"保育領域概括具歷史或文化價值的人造建築及場所；與來源片語最接近。","collocations":"protect built heritage; conserve a city’s built heritage","example":"Residents campaigned to protect the district’s built heritage.","exampleZh":"居民發起運動，保護該區的建築遺產。","contrast":"Built 指有形建造資產；不等同無形的建築技藝。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The town adopted a conservation plan for its architectural heritage, from the old market hall to the stone bridge.","zh":"市鎮為其建築遺產制訂保育計劃，涵蓋舊街市大樓以至石橋。","upgrade":"The town adopted a conservation plan for its built heritage, from the old market hall to the stone bridge.","answer":"built heritage","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"建造傳統是無形技術，並非待保育的舊街市與石橋。"},{"letter":"B","text":"built heritage","explanation":"舊街市及石橋均屬有形建造資產，built heritage 完整概括。"},{"letter":"C","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"建築學研究不是此計劃直接保護的場所。"},{"letter":"D","text":"natural heritage","explanation":"石橋和街市是人造，並非天然遺產。"},{"letter":"E","text":"old buildings only","explanation":"only 把石橋排除，且 old 本身未指保育價值。"},{"letter":"F","text":"cultural heritage broadly","explanation":"文化遺產還可包括語言和節慶，比本句指定的有形資產廣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"A new survey maps the district’s architectural heritage, including former schools, public baths and covered walkways.","zh":"新調查繪製該區建築遺產分布，包括舊校舍、公共浴場和有蓋行人道。","upgrade":"A new survey maps the district’s built heritage, including former schools, public baths and covered walkways.","answer":"built heritage","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"舊建造技藝不是可繪圖定位的校舍、浴場和行人道。"},{"letter":"B","text":"historic buildings only","explanation":"only 把有蓋行人道排除，範圍太窄。"},{"letter":"C","text":"built heritage","explanation":"各類人造歷史場所合稱 built heritage。"},{"letter":"D","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"學科不是所繪製的三類場所。"},{"letter":"E","text":"old urban scenery","explanation":"scenery 偏外觀畫面，未交代保育價值和各類設施。"},{"letter":"F","text":"cultural heritage generally","explanation":"文化遺產可含無形習俗，範圍太廣。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"historic buildings","meaning":"歷史建築物","note":"句子明確指一棟或多棟有歷史價值的建築物時用；比整體 architectural heritage 窄。","collocations":"preserve historic buildings; several historic buildings; a protected historic building","example":"The council listed three historic buildings beside the old market.","exampleZh":"議會把舊街市旁三棟歷史建築列入保護名單。","contrast":"街道格局與公共空間也可能屬 built heritage，卻不都是 buildings。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The council repaired three parts of its architectural heritage: the old courthouse, library and town hall.","zh":"議會修復了三處建築遺產：舊法院、圖書館及市政廳。","upgrade":"The council repaired three historic buildings: the old courthouse, library and town hall.","answer":"historic buildings","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"historic buildings","explanation":"列出的法院、圖書館、市政廳都是具歷史意義的樓宇，historic buildings 最具體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"建築學研究不能像三棟樓般被維修。"},{"letter":"C","text":"built-environment layout","explanation":"layout 指空間格局，不是這三座被修復的樓宇本身。"},{"letter":"D","text":"old buildings regardless of value","explanation":"old 不保證歷史價值，句中把三棟列作 heritage。"},{"letter":"E","text":"traditional building practices","explanation":"技法不等於實際維修對象。"},{"letter":"F","text":"natural heritage","explanation":"這些是人造樓宇，非自然遺產。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Only two items of the village’s architectural heritage are on the protected list: the former post office and the schoolhouse.","zh":"村內只有兩項建築遺產列入保護清單：舊郵局與舊校舍。","upgrade":"Only two historic buildings in the village are on the protected list: the former post office and the schoolhouse.","answer":"historic buildings","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"historic buildings","explanation":"舊郵局和校舍是清單上兩棟具價值樓宇，historic buildings 精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"historic streetscapes","explanation":"streetscapes 指街道整體外觀，句中只列兩座樓。"},{"letter":"C","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"清單保護的是樓宇，不是建造習俗。"},{"letter":"D","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"學術領域不會以舊郵局、校舍兩項列作保護樓宇。"},{"letter":"E","text":"old buildings without heritage status","explanation":"without heritage status 與列入保護清單相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"built environment as a whole","explanation":"整體環境比清單上的兩座樓廣。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"historic built environment","meaning":"歷史建成環境","note":"保育討論連建築、街道和公共空間的整體面貌一併指稱時用；範圍較廣。","collocations":"conserve the historic built environment; study a historic streetscape","example":"The survey recorded the town’s historic built environment, including its lanes and old shops.","exampleZh":"調查記錄了市鎮的歷史建成環境，包括小巷和舊商店。","contrast":"Environment 在此是人造場所，不是自然環境或抽象文化。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The planners documented the neighbourhood’s architectural heritage by recording its old lanes, shopfronts and small squares together.","zh":"規劃人員一併記錄舊巷、店面及小廣場，為該社區的建築遺產存檔。","upgrade":"The planners documented the neighbourhood’s historic built environment by recording its old lanes, shopfronts and small squares together.","answer":"historic built environment","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"historic buildings alone","explanation":"alone 漏掉舊巷和小廣場。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"不是研究學科。"},{"letter":"C","text":"historic built environment","explanation":"樓宇店面、巷道及廣場共同形成歷史建成環境。"},{"letter":"D","text":"natural environment","explanation":"這些場所是人造，非自然環境。"},{"letter":"E","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"建造知識不是被記錄的街景實物。"},{"letter":"F","text":"historic monuments only","explanation":"only 把日常舊巷與廣場縮成紀念碑。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The proposal would protect the district’s architectural heritage as a whole, including the street pattern as well as the buildings.","zh":"建議會整體保護該區建築遺產，包括街道布局及樓宇。","upgrade":"The proposal would protect the district’s historic built environment as a whole, including the street pattern as well as the buildings.","answer":"historic built environment","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"historic built environment","explanation":"街道布局連同樓宇一併保護，historic built environment 捕捉整體。"},{"letter":"B","text":"historic buildings alone","explanation":"alone 排除街道格局。"},{"letter":"C","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"並非只保護工藝傳承。"},{"letter":"D","text":"natural heritage","explanation":"來源是人造街道與樓宇，非自然資產。"},{"letter":"E","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"學科不是被保護的地區。"},{"letter":"F","text":"old buildings without value","explanation":"old without value 與 heritage 所需歷史文化價值不合。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"architectural legacy","meaning":"前人留下的建築成果","note":"強調上一代留下值得重視的建築成果；若只談規劃理念或建築師名聲，須另說明。","collocations":"preserve an architectural legacy; the city’s architectural legacy","example":"The restored theatre remains part of the city’s architectural legacy.","exampleZh":"修復後的劇院仍是這座城市建築遺產的一部分。","contrast":"Legacy 可含影響力；本課必須有建築物或實體場所線索，才能保留來源的有形意思。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The century-old theatre is part of the city’s architectural heritage, a physical gift left by earlier generations.","zh":"百年劇院是這座城市建築遺產的一部分，是前人留下的有形禮物。","upgrade":"The century-old theatre is part of the city’s architectural legacy, a physical gift left by earlier generations.","answer":"architectural legacy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"inherited building traditions","explanation":"題句指百年劇院實物，不只是無形技藝。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural legacy","explanation":"前代留下的有形劇院可稱 architectural legacy。"},{"letter":"C","text":"natural heritage","explanation":"劇院是人造建築。"},{"letter":"D","text":"current design code","explanation":"現行規範不是前代留下的劇院。"},{"letter":"E","text":"architectural reputation","explanation":"名聲可能是無形 legacy，但句中明說 physical gift。"},{"letter":"F","text":"old building regardless of value","explanation":"只說舊樓未交代城市珍視的遺產價值。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"By restoring the old station, residents hoped to pass their architectural heritage on to the next generation.","zh":"居民希望透過修復舊車站，把建築遺產傳給下一代。","upgrade":"By restoring the old station, residents hoped to pass their architectural legacy on to the next generation.","answer":"architectural legacy","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"修復的是舊車站，不是學術研究。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural legacy","explanation":"舊車站作為建築成果傳給後代，architectural legacy 合語境。"},{"letter":"C","text":"inherited construction skills","explanation":"修復實體車站並非單傳授工藝。"},{"letter":"D","text":"modern urban expansion","explanation":"修舊站不是擴建新城。"},{"letter":"E","text":"natural heritage","explanation":"車站非自然資產。"},{"letter":"F","text":"architectural reputation alone","explanation":"alone 只留名聲，漏掉被修復的實體車站。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"inherited building traditions · 建造傳統不是建築物","zh":"中文辨析： 傳統指木工、棚架或設計知識的傳承；原文是可遭破壞的城市建築資產。若文章討論師徒傳技，traditions 才對。","point":"Practices may survive after a building is lost; they are not the building."},{"word":"architecture / architectural studies · 學科與遺產不同","zh":"中文辨析： Architecture 可指設計和建築學科；architectural heritage 指從過去保留下來、有價值的實體。大學建築學系不是一座歷史建築。","point":"The discipline studies built heritage but is not itself the physical heritage."},{"word":"old buildings / ruins · 舊或破不等於有遺產價值","zh":"中文辨析： Old 只說年齡；ruins 只說殘破。歷史建築可仍在使用，也需要文化或歷史價值才能稱 heritage。","point":"Age and damage alone do not establish heritage value."},{"word":"cultural heritage · 文化遺產範圍太廣","zh":"中文辨析： 文化遺產亦可包括節慶、語言、音樂。來源特指建築方面；如改寫成 cultural heritage 應再限定 built/architectural。","point":"Built heritage is one part of cultural heritage."},{"word":"natural environment / scenery · 自然風景不是建築遺產","zh":"中文辨析： 原文另提 city’s environment，與 architectural heritage 並列；若只寫樹木、海岸或風景會漏掉建築。","point":"The source coordinates environment and architectural heritage as related but distinct objects."}],"moduleNumber":98},{"id":"lesson-099","sourceId":95,"headword":"architecture","title":"Architecture","titleZh":"建築學這門領域","subtitle":"建築學這門領域","description":"In 2025 DSE set 5.1, a professor commenting on bamboo scaffolders is identified as being from the University of Hong Kong’s Architecture Department. Architecture here names an academic/professional discipline. It does not specify that the professor only studies building exteriors or that an official department may be renamed by a paraphrase. The available transcription contains an OCR stray letter near “as well as”; that noise does not affect the department phrase. All examples and questions below are original.","sourceSense":"In 2025 DSE set 5.1, a professor commenting on bamboo scaffolders is identified as being from the University of Hong Kong’s Architecture Department. Architecture here names an academic/professional discipline. It does not specify that the professor only studies building exteriors or that an official department may be renamed by a paraphrase. The available transcription contains an OCR stray letter near “as well as”; that noise does not affect the department phrase. All examples and questions below are original.","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選","判斷","界線"],"rows":[["building design","有條件近義","建築學的重要實務部分；不能完整代表歷史、材料、都市空間等整個學科，也不能擅自改動正式學系名稱。"],["structural style","假近義","指單棟建築的結構外觀／風格，不是大學學科；structural engineering 亦是相鄰而不同領域。"]],"note":"遺漏檢查： Architectural studies 可概括學科研究；built-environment studies 可在課程兼研街道與城市環境時使用，範圍稍廣。Architectural design 與 building design 高度重疊，故不重複計數；construction 指施工，architectural heritage 指遺產（參 0094），都不能無條件替換。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"來源的 Architecture Department 是學科名稱，不應把改寫當成正式部門名稱。描述學術研究可用 architectural studies；描述設計樓宇這一部分可用 building design；明確兼論街道與人造公共空間才可用較廣的 built-environment studies。Structural style 是某樓特徵，architectural heritage 是歷史建築資產。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"architectural studies","meaning":"建築學研究","note":"指大學對建築設計、歷史、材料和環境的學術研究；可描述學科領域，不能假作某大學正式學系名稱。","collocations":"research in architectural studies; an architectural studies programme; scholars of architectural studies","example":"Her architectural studies include housing design and the history of public markets.","exampleZh":"她的建築學研究包括房屋設計和公共街市的歷史。","contrast":"Studies 著眼學術範圍；building design 只是一部分實務。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The lecturer’s work in architecture covers both housing design and the history of old public markets.","zh":"講師的建築學工作涵蓋房屋設計，以及舊公共街市的歷史。","upgrade":"The lecturer’s work in architectural studies covers both housing design and the history of old public markets.","answer":"architectural studies","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"building design alone","explanation":"alone 排除題句明列的舊街市歷史研究。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"房屋設計與建築史同屬 architectural studies，範圍合適。"},{"letter":"C","text":"structural engineering","explanation":"結構工程主要處理承重安全，未概括市場歷史。"},{"letter":"D","text":"construction management","explanation":"施工管理與講師研究設計及歷史不同。"},{"letter":"E","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"歷史建築可成研究對象，卻非研究活動本身。"},{"letter":"F","text":"building style","explanation":"style 是建築外觀特徵，不能涵蓋兩項研究。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The university’s new course in architecture combines design, materials, urban history and environmental performance.","zh":"大學新的建築學課程結合設計、材料、城市歷史及環境表現。","upgrade":"The university’s new course in architectural studies combines design, materials, urban history and environmental performance.","answer":"architectural studies","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"structural style","explanation":"外觀風格只是可能研究的一面，漏掉材料和城市歷史。"},{"letter":"B","text":"construction management","explanation":"施工管理未概括設計和環境表現研究。"},{"letter":"C","text":"architectural studies","explanation":"四項內容共同構成建築學研究。"},{"letter":"D","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"歷史建築只是可能的課題，不是這門大學課程本身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"interior design alone","explanation":"室內設計不足以涵蓋城市歷史和建築材料。"},{"letter":"F","text":"building codes alone","explanation":"建築法規可能涉及部分內容，alone 排除其餘學科。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"building design","meaning":"建築物設計","note":"句子明確談繪圖、空間配置、外觀或設計建築時用；是 architecture 的核心活動但不是整個學科。","collocations":"study building design; building design studio; methods of building design","example":"The studio teaches building design through models and site visits.","exampleZh":"這個工作室透過模型和實地考察教授建築物設計。","contrast":"不包括所有建築史與城市研究；University of Hong Kong 的正式部門名稱亦不能任意改寫。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The workshop on architecture asked students to draw floor plans and build models for a small library.","zh":"建築學工作坊要求學生為小型圖書館繪製平面圖及製作模型。","upgrade":"The workshop on building design asked students to draw floor plans and build models for a small library.","answer":"building design","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"這是為新圖書館設計圖與模型，不是保存舊建築。"},{"letter":"B","text":"building design","explanation":"平面圖和模型直接屬 building design。"},{"letter":"C","text":"structural engineering","explanation":"承重計算或許相關，但題句沒有做結構計算。"},{"letter":"D","text":"construction management","explanation":"未談施工排期或工地管理。"},{"letter":"E","text":"architectural history","explanation":"不是回顧舊建築發展。"},{"letter":"F","text":"urban planning","explanation":"只設計一幢圖書館，不是在規劃整個城區。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In the architecture unit, students revised a school building’s layout after wheelchair users tested the first plan.","zh":"在建築學單元中，學生在輪椅使用者測試首份方案後修改校舍布局。","upgrade":"In the building design unit, students revised a school building’s layout after wheelchair users tested the first plan.","answer":"building design","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"building design","explanation":"按使用者測試修改校舍布局，是具體的 building design 任務。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"改設計並非保存歷史校舍。"},{"letter":"C","text":"structural engineering only","explanation":"only 把空間可達性問題錯縮為承重計算。"},{"letter":"D","text":"construction management","explanation":"題句沒有施工監督。"},{"letter":"E","text":"architectural history","explanation":"不是研究過去建築。"},{"letter":"F","text":"urban planning","explanation":"只處理校舍布局，非城市土地規劃。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"built-environment studies","meaning":"建成環境研究","note":"課程或研究明確把建築連同街道、公共空間和人造環境一起討論時用；比純建築設計廣。","collocations":"built-environment studies programme; research in built-environment studies","example":"His built-environment studies examine housing, footpaths and public squares.","exampleZh":"他的建成環境研究考察房屋、行人路和公共廣場。","contrast":"範圍可超出 architecture；只討論單棟樓外觀時不宜用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Her research in architecture examines how housing blocks, bus stops and public squares shape daily life together.","zh":"她的建築學研究考察住宅大樓、巴士站和公共廣場如何共同影響日常生活。","upgrade":"Her research in built-environment studies examines how housing blocks, bus stops and public squares shape daily life together.","answer":"built-environment studies","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"building design alone","explanation":"alone 不能涵蓋巴士站和公共廣場如何共同作用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"structural engineering","explanation":"題句不是研究承重結構。"},{"letter":"C","text":"built-environment studies","explanation":"建築與公共空間的關係符合 built-environment studies。"},{"letter":"D","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"未限定保育歷史建築。"},{"letter":"E","text":"construction management","explanation":"不是管理施工。"},{"letter":"F","text":"interior design","explanation":"研究範圍遠超室內。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The architecture programme in this example includes buildings, streets, drainage and access to public space.","zh":"這個例子中的建築學課程涵蓋樓宇、街道、排水及公共空間的可達性。","upgrade":"The built-environment studies programme in this example includes buildings, streets, drainage and access to public space.","answer":"built-environment studies","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"historic building style","explanation":"只談外觀風格不能涵蓋排水與通達性。"},{"letter":"B","text":"architectural heritage","explanation":"沒有說課程專研歷史遺產。"},{"letter":"C","text":"built-environment studies","explanation":"建築、街道、排水和公共空間共同屬建成環境研究。"},{"letter":"D","text":"building design only","explanation":"only 排除街道和公共空間層面。"},{"letter":"E","text":"construction management","explanation":"不是監督工地施工。"},{"letter":"F","text":"structural engineering alone","explanation":"alone 只看承重結構，未涵蓋完整人造環境。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"structural style / appearance · 單棟樓的外觀不是學科","zh":"中文辨析： Structural style 可描述樓宇呈現的風格，卻不能稱大學 Architecture Department 的整個教研領域。若談某座建築的外觀才可能用。","point":"A building has a style; a department teaches and researches a discipline."},{"word":"structural engineering · 結構工程屬相鄰專業","zh":"中文辨析： 結構工程重點在承重與安全計算；建築學也關心設計、使用者、歷史與城市。兩個學系可能合作，但不能只因有棚架就互換名稱。","point":"Related professional fields have different cores."},{"word":"construction / scaffolding · 施工技術不是整個建築學","zh":"中文辨析： 建造和棚架施工是實務工序。原文教授來自建築學系，並不表示他只研究搭建棚架或親自施工。","point":"Architecture may study construction without being identical to it."},{"word":"architectural heritage · 歷史建築資產不是學科","zh":"中文辨析： 0094 architectural heritage 是前人留下值得保存的有形建築；0095 Architecture Department 是教授所屬學科。前者可成後者研究對象。","point":"Heritage is an object of study; architecture is the discipline."},{"word":"official department name · 釋義不能冒充正式名稱","zh":"中文辨析： 可說某教授研究 architectural studies 或 building design，但引用大學隸屬時應保留正式的 Architecture Department，除非有證據證明另一正式名稱。","point":"A paraphrase of a subject is not automatically an institution’s proper name."}],"moduleNumber":99},{"id":"lesson-100","sourceId":62,"headword":"amaze","title":"Amaze","titleZh":"令人驚嘆","subtitle":"令人驚嘆","description":"原文： 2024 DSE Paper 4，7.1 的香港科學館廣告邀請學生：「Come be amazed by the 22-metre-high Energy Machine and the real aircraft hanging from the ceiling.」這是被動分詞 amazed，把參觀者的驚嘆歸因於大型展品，兼含出乎意料與欣賞；不是逗人發笑、嚇人或令人大惑不解。動詞原形 amaze 可說 The exhibits amaze visitors；改寫原句則通常沿用 be astonished/impressed/awed/dazzled by 等被動式。下列例句與練習均為原創。[2024 Paper 4 set 7.1 再現文本](https://www.scribd.com/document/951718395/DSE-2024-Paper-4)。","sourceSense":"原文： 2024 DSE Paper 4，7.1 的香港科學館廣告邀請學生：「Come be amazed by the 22-metre-high Energy Machine and the real aircraft hanging from the ceiling.」這是被動分詞 amazed，把參觀者的驚嘆歸因於大型展品，兼含出乎意料與欣賞；不是逗人發笑、嚇人或令人大惑不解。動詞原形 amaze 可說 The exhibits amaze visitors；改寫原句則通常沿用 be astonished/impressed/awed/dazzled by 等被動式。下列例句與練習均為原創。[2024 Paper 4 set 7.1 再現文本](https://www.scribd.com/document/951718395/DSE-2024-Paper-4)。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","此處的界線"],"rows":[["astonish","直接，較強","強調大出意料的驚奇；適用於龐大展品令人目瞪口呆時。"],["impress","語境近義","強調對設計、技術或成就的讚賞；不一定有突發驚奇。"],["surprise","有條件","聚焦未預料到；驚訝可正可負，須有驚喜而非驚嚇的線索。"]],"note":"擴展與遺漏挑戰： Awe 指宏偉展品令人敬畏；dazzle 指醒目、炫目的視覺效果令人驚嘆。Astound 常可替換 astonish，但在本課沒有新的可區分用法，故記作未另設練習的近同義詞。Wow 是口語感嘆動詞，可說 The exhibit wowed the visitors，但原廣告的被動邀請與正式教學語域較宜用本課五項。Captivate/fascinate 側重持續吸引注意，可在觀眾久久觀看的句子用，卻不必包含初見展品的驚嘆。Marvel at 以參觀者作主語，需主動重寫；它也是有用的較遠語態轉換，但本課保留被動展品致驚嘆的焦點。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":[],"rows":[],"note":"- Astonish 強調強烈意外；impress 重視技術或品質的讚賞；surprise 指未預料到，語氣本身可正可負。\n- Awe 用於龐大、莊嚴的敬畏；dazzle 用於光影色彩的炫目震撼。\n- 原文是 be amazed by：展品使人驚嘆、參觀者感到驚嘆。Amuse, frighten, confuse 各改變情緒類別。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"astonish","meaning":"使大為驚奇","note":"強調展品的尺度或特徵遠超預期，使人強烈驚訝；可用主動 astonish visitors 或被動 be astonished by。","collocations":"astonish visitors; be astonished by the size; an astonishing display","example":"The enormous moving model astonished the students when its doors opened.","exampleZh":"巨型活動模型的門一打開，就令學生們大為驚奇。","contrast":"Astonish 比一般 surprise 強；單純欣賞製作品質而沒有明顯意外，可用 impress。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The tiny entrance gave no hint of what was inside: visitors were amazed by a towering machine that filled the entire hall.","zh":"細小的入口完全沒有透露館內景象：一座填滿整個大廳的高聳機器令參觀者大為驚奇。","upgrade":"The tiny entrance gave no hint of what was inside: visitors were astonished by a towering machine that filled the entire hall.","answer":"were astonished by a towering machine","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were astonished by a towering machine","explanation":"入口細小而機器竟填滿整館，強烈超預期的規模使 astonished 最精確。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were impressed by a towering machine","explanation":"impressed 可表示欣賞機器，但沒有直接說出入口與規模造成的大出意料。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were dazzled by a towering machine","explanation":"dazzled 多指光影炫目，句中只交代體積，沒有視覺光彩。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were fascinated by a towering machine","explanation":"fascinated 側重持續興趣，題句聚焦初見整館機器的一刻震驚。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were startled by a towering machine","explanation":"startled 偏突然一驚或被嚇，題句的意外來自規模而非突發聲響。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were mildly surprised by a towering machine","explanation":"mildly surprised 程度太輕，填滿整館與入口細小的反差十分強。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The class expected a small photograph, but they were amazed by a real aircraft suspended over their heads.","zh":"全班原以為只會看到一張小照片，卻因頭頂懸掛著一架真飛機而大為驚奇。","upgrade":"The class expected a small photograph, but they were astonished by a real aircraft suspended over their heads.","answer":"were astonished by a real aircraft","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were surprised by a real aircraft","explanation":"surprised 可表意外，但由小照片變成頭頂真飛機，astonished 更能表達強烈反差。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were awed by a real aircraft","explanation":"awed 可形容仰望真飛機的敬畏，但句中主要線索是預期照片與實物的巨大落差。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were astonished by a real aircraft","explanation":"小照片的預期突然變成真飛機，強烈意外適合 astonished。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were impressed by a real aircraft","explanation":"impressed 著重評價工藝；題句沒有說飛機的技術或修復品質。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were startled by a real aircraft","explanation":"startled 偏被突然事物嚇一跳，題句說的是發現實物的驚嘆。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were dazzled by a real aircraft","explanation":"dazzled 需要明亮或炫目的視覺細節，句中沒有。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"impress","meaning":"使留下深刻印象","note":"參觀者因技術、工藝或設計而欣賞展品；be impressed by/with 表示認可，不必真的嚇一跳。","collocations":"impress visitors; be impressed by the engineering; an impressive exhibit","example":"The students were impressed by the careful engineering behind the aircraft display.","exampleZh":"學生對飛機展品背後精細的工程設計印象深刻。","contrast":"Impress 以品質評價為重；amaze/astonish 更含驚奇，dazzle 更含炫目視覺效果。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"After reading how the turbine worked, the engineering students were amazed by the precision of its moving parts.","zh":"工程系學生讀過渦輪運作原理後，對其活動部件的精密程度印象深刻。","upgrade":"After reading how the turbine worked, the engineering students were impressed by the precision of its moving parts.","answer":"were impressed by the precision","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were astonished by the precision","explanation":"astonished 強調意外；學生已讀過原理，重點是欣賞製作精準。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were impressed by the precision","explanation":"學生了解運作原理後認可部件的技術品質，impressed 最貼近。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were surprised by the precision","explanation":"surprised 可指出乎意料，但句中沒有原先低估精度的預期。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were awed by the precision","explanation":"awed 帶宏大敬畏，精細機械的評價未顯示這種情緒。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were dazzled by the precision","explanation":"dazzled 偏炫目光影；句中所述是精準而非亮麗外觀。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were puzzled by the precision","explanation":"puzzled 表不明白，與已讀懂渦輪原理後的欣賞不符。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The students expected the aircraft display to be good; they were amazed by the care taken to restore every original detail.","zh":"學生原本已預期飛機展品不錯；每項原有細節都經細心修復，令他們留下深刻印象。","upgrade":"The students expected the aircraft display to be good; they were impressed by the care taken to restore every original detail.","answer":"were impressed by the care","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were fascinated by the care","explanation":"fascinated 重在持續被吸引；句中重點是評價修復細節的品質。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were surprised by the care","explanation":"surprised 偏意外，但學生本已預期展品不錯。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were awed by the care","explanation":"awed 指敬畏巨大或莊嚴之物，這裏強調修復工藝。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were impressed by the care","explanation":"已預期展品不錯，仍欣賞細心修復的每一處，impressed 最精確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were astonished by the care","explanation":"astonished 太強調與預期相反的大吃一驚。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were dazzled by the care","explanation":"dazzled 側重奪目視覺，細心修復未必炫目。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"surprise","meaning":"使感到意外","note":"在新發現出乎意料時可用；它自身不保證令人讚賞，故練習須交代驚喜的積極語境。","collocations":"surprise the visitors; be surprised by the hidden feature; a pleasant surprise","example":"The hidden aircraft above the doorway surprised the class as they entered.","exampleZh":"學生們走進來時，門口上方隱藏的飛機令全班感到意外。","contrast":"Surprise 可是好或壞的意外；amaze 在原廣告是正面的驚嘆。Startle 偏突然嚇一跳。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Visitors who thought the ceiling was empty were amazed when a hidden aircraft emerged from the shadows.","zh":"參觀者以為天花板空無一物，隱藏的飛機從陰影中現身時，令他們感到意外。","upgrade":"Visitors who thought the ceiling was empty were surprised when a hidden aircraft emerged from the shadows.","answer":"were surprised when a hidden aircraft emerged","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were surprised when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"以為天花板空無一物，卻看見隱藏飛機，surprised 最直接說預期落差。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were astonished when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"astonished 亦可表強烈意外，但句中未描述程度到目瞪口呆。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were impressed when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"impressed 需有設計或技術品質的評價，句中只有發現。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were awed when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"awed 需有敬畏或宏大感，題句只說意料之外的出現。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were startled when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"startled 偏驟然嚇一跳，飛機從陰影出現未明示驚嚇。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were dazzled when a hidden aircraft emerged","explanation":"dazzled 需有炫目光影，陰影中的飛機不支持這義。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The group was amazed when the flight simulator responded to voice commands; the guide had said it accepted only button commands.","zh":"導賞員說飛行模擬器只接受按鈕指令，但小組發現它會回應語音指令，感到驚喜。","upgrade":"The group was surprised when the flight simulator responded to voice commands; the guide had said it accepted only button commands.","answer":"was surprised when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was awed when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"awed 偏莊嚴敬畏；意外發現語音功能未必有這種感受。"},{"letter":"B","text":"was impressed when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"impressed 可讚賞技術，但句中最明確的是導賞員所說與實際功能不同。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was surprised when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"原以為只能按鍵，卻能用語音控制，surprised 準確說預期落差。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was dazzled when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"dazzled 需視覺華彩；語音回應不是炫目畫面。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was astonished when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"astonished 強度可用於更極端的意外；這裏只說額外功能令人驚喜。"},{"letter":"F","text":"was startled when the flight simulator responded to voice commands","explanation":"startled 偏突如其來而嚇一跳；語音控制帶來的是愉快意外。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"awe","meaning":"使敬畏；使驚歎","note":"龐大、壯觀或令人感到渺小的展品引起深刻敬畏時可用 be awed by；比單一意外更有崇敬感。","collocations":"awe the visitors; be awed by the scale; stand in awe of the display","example":"The full-sized aircraft awed the children as they looked up from below.","exampleZh":"孩子們從下方抬頭望向原尺寸飛機，深感震撼與敬畏。","contrast":"Awe 帶宏大或莊嚴感；impress 可以只指欣賞精細工藝，未必有敬畏。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Standing beneath the enormous suspended aircraft, the children were amazed by its size and fell silent for a moment.","zh":"孩子們站在懸掛的巨型飛機下，因其體積深感震撼，一時靜默。","upgrade":"Standing beneath the enormous suspended aircraft, the children were awed by its size and fell silent for a moment.","answer":"were awed by its size","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were astonished by its size","explanation":"astonished 可表規模令人驚奇，但一時靜默及仰望更突出敬畏。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were awed by its size","explanation":"身處巨型真飛機下方而靜默，awed 把震撼與敬畏合起來。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were impressed by its size","explanation":"impressed 表讚賞，沒有充分表達仰望時的莊重感。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were surprised by its size","explanation":"surprised 表出乎意料，題句未說先前以為飛機較小。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were dazzled by its size","explanation":"dazzled 多指炫目光影，這裏只說巨型飛機。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were fascinated by its size","explanation":"fascinated 側重興趣和注意力，未必說出靜默敬畏。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"On seeing a centuries-old tree, the pupils were amazed by its long survival and stepped back respectfully to avoid touching its fragile bark.","zh":"學生看見一棵有數百年歷史的樹，為它歷經歲月仍存活而深感敬畏，並恭敬地退後，以免碰到脆弱的樹皮。","upgrade":"On seeing a centuries-old tree, the pupils were awed by its long survival and stepped back respectfully to avoid touching its fragile bark.","answer":"were awed by its long survival","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were impressed by its long survival","explanation":"impressed 可說讚賞古樹，但學生恭敬退後，還有敬畏與珍惜的意味。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were fascinated by its long survival","explanation":"fascinated 指興趣，未必解釋他們恭敬地避免碰樹。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were surprised by its long survival","explanation":"surprised 需要較明確原先不相信樹會存活的預期。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were awed by its long survival","explanation":"古樹歷數百年仍存活，學生恭敬退後，awed 表敬畏最準確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were astonished by its long survival","explanation":"astonished 著重吃驚，未充分涵蓋對脆弱古樹的尊敬。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were dazzled by its long survival","explanation":"dazzled 需炫目外觀，古樹的年歲和保護行為沒有這種線索。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"dazzle","meaning":"以炫目效果令人驚嘆","note":"展品的鮮明光影、色彩、華麗工藝或戲劇性視覺轉變使觀眾目不暇給時可用 dazzle；不能只因物件體積大便用它。","collocations":"dazzle visitors with coloured light; be dazzled by intricate design; a dazzling transformation","example":"The moving lights on the energy exhibit dazzled the visiting students.","exampleZh":"能源展品上流動的燈光令來訪學生看得目不暇給。","contrast":"Dazzle 重視視覺華彩；awe 重視敬畏，surprise 重視意外。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Visitors were amazed by the shifting bands of brilliant colour on the energy machine, which made the whole hall shimmer.","zh":"能源裝置上鮮亮色彩不斷流轉，令整個大廳閃閃生輝，參觀者看得目不暇給。","upgrade":"Visitors were dazzled by the shifting bands of brilliant colour on the energy machine, which made the whole hall shimmer.","answer":"were dazzled by the shifting colours","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"were awed by the shifting colours","explanation":"awed 側重宏大敬畏，題句特寫鮮亮流動色彩。"},{"letter":"B","text":"were impressed by the shifting colours","explanation":"impressed 可表欣賞，但未具體說色彩令整館閃耀的炫目效果。"},{"letter":"C","text":"were dazzled by the shifting colours","explanation":"鮮亮流動色彩使整館閃耀，dazzled 最精確描述視覺震撼。"},{"letter":"D","text":"were surprised by the shifting colours","explanation":"surprised 需顯示出乎預期，題句沒有先前預期。"},{"letter":"E","text":"were fascinated by the shifting colours","explanation":"fascinated 側重長時間吸引注意；句子主要描述炫目光彩。"},{"letter":"F","text":"were startled by the shifting colours","explanation":"startled 偏突發驚嚇，流動色彩不等於受到驚嚇。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The class was amazed when a plain white model became a richly detailed miniature city through projection mapping.","zh":"一個純白模型經投影映射變成細節豐富的迷你城市，令全班看得目眩神迷。","upgrade":"The class was dazzled when a plain white model became a richly detailed miniature city through projection mapping.","answer":"was dazzled when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"was awed when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"awed 重在敬畏；這裏的關鍵是白模型變成繽紛細緻城景的視覺效果。"},{"letter":"B","text":"was astonished when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"astonished 可表轉變意外，但未點出投影映射的華麗視覺。"},{"letter":"C","text":"was impressed when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"impressed 可讚賞技術品質，卻較少表達眼前豐富影像帶來的目眩神迷。"},{"letter":"D","text":"was surprised when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"surprised 指沒料到變化，未具體傳達絢麗城景的視覺震撼。"},{"letter":"E","text":"was dazzled when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"投影把素白模型化成細節繁多的城景，dazzled 準確說視覺華彩。"},{"letter":"F","text":"was fascinated when a plain white model became a richly detailed city","explanation":"fascinated 指持續吸引注意，沒有直接點出戲劇性視覺轉變的耀眼效果。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"amuse / entertain · 逗樂不等於驚嘆","zh":"中文辨析： 展品可能也有趣，但原文的大型能源裝置與真飛機主要讓人驚奇及欣賞。Amuse 指逗笑或使人消遣；若有滑稽表演才可能合用。","point":"Wonder at a striking exhibit is different from being entertained or made to laugh."},{"word":"startle / frighten · 意外不必是驚嚇","zh":"中文辨析： 飛機若突然發出巨響，觀眾可能 be startled/frightened；原廣告沒有危險或恐怖線索，只邀請學生欣賞展品。","point":"A pleasant surprise is not necessarily a scare."},{"word":"confuse / puzzle · 看不懂不等於驚嘆","zh":"中文辨析： 複雜機械可能令人不明所以，但 be confused by 是困惑；原文說觀看醒目展品的正面感受。要教「看不懂原理」才用 puzzled。","point":"Not understanding a mechanism is different from admiring it."},{"word":"amazing / amazed · 致感者與感受者","zh":"中文辨析： 展品是 amazing，參觀者 are amazed by 展品。說 visitors are amazing by the aircraft 會把人寫成令人驚嘆者，且被動結構不合。","point":"The exhibit amazes; the visitor is amazed."},{"word":"impressed / surprised / awed / dazzled · 正面感受的分界","zh":"中文辨析： Impressed 評價工藝，surprised 說出乎意料，awed 帶敬畏，dazzled 指炫目效果。它們可同時發生，練習用具體線索選最佳一項；不能說其他詞在所有情境均錯。","point":"Choose the emotion supported most specifically by the sentence."}],"moduleNumber":100},{"id":"lesson-101","sourceId":10,"headword":"accessible","title":"Accessible","titleZh":"人人都可取得的知識","subtitle":"人人都可取得的知識","description":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 6.2〈How Humans Will Get to Mars in 2023〉說任務將產生珍貴的科學及社會知識，而那些知識 will be accessible to everyone。此處 accessible 主要指資料將可供所有人取得，to everyone 的普及範圍不可省略；原句並沒有保證所有人都能理解科學細節，也沒有明說是否免費。這是對當年文章表述的語言分析，練習不把該任務預期當成後來已實現的事實。","sourceSense":"2013 年 DSE Speaking 6.2〈How Humans Will Get to Mars in 2023〉說任務將產生珍貴的科學及社會知識，而那些知識 will be accessible to everyone。此處 accessible 主要指資料將可供所有人取得，to everyone 的普及範圍不可省略；原句並沒有保證所有人都能理解科學細節，也沒有明說是否免費。這是對當年文章表述的語言分析，練習不把該任務預期當成後來已實現的事實。","sourceMap":{"headers":["原始候選詞","判斷","原因"],"rows":[["easy to reach","有條件改寫","可形容網站或資料入口容易到達；直接說 knowledge is easy to reach 較生硬，且可能偏向物理距離。"],["available","近義但須補範圍","Available to everyone 保留普及範圍；單獨 available 可能只對少數人開放。"],["open","不宜單獨用","Knowledge is open 太含糊；可改寫為 findings are open to all 或 openly available。"],["open to","有條件","Open to all/everyone 自然修飾資料庫、檔案或研究結果；要保留公開可取的對象與渠道。"]],"note":""},"quickChoice":{"headers":["重點","可用說法"],"rows":[["人人可取得","available to everyone"],["檔案或結果無身分門檻","open to all"],["報告或數據對公眾公開","publicly available"],["登入與索取安排令取得方便","easy for anyone to obtain"],["明示無收費","freely available"]],"note":"快選規則： 原文的 accessible to everyone 先要保留「人人可取得」，再看是否另有 公開平台、容易索取、免費 的證據。可得不等於容易理解，公開也不自動代表免費。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"Available To Everyone","meaning":"人人都可取得","note":"直接保留資料可供所有人取得的核心意思；不保證人人已閱讀或完全明白。","collocations":"available to everyone / the public; make findings available to all.","example":"The researchers made the mission summary available to everyone online.","exampleZh":"研究人員把任務摘要放到網上，讓所有人都可取得。","contrast":"不可省掉 to everyone；只說 available 可能是僅供內部使用。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The mission report will be accessible to everyone through a public website, although reading it is optional.","zh":"任務報告將透過公開網站供所有人取得，但讀不讀由個人選擇。","upgrade":"The mission report will be available to everyone through a public website, although reading it is optional.","answer":"available to everyone","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"easy to download","explanation":"網站公開不必然代表下載過程簡單；原句只說人人可取閱。"},{"letter":"B","text":"hidden from everyone","explanation":"Hidden 與公開網站相反。"},{"letter":"C","text":"understandable to experts","explanation":"Understandable to experts 說能否明白，且只限專家。"},{"letter":"D","text":"available to everyone","explanation":"公開網站讓所有人可取得，不等於都讀過。"},{"letter":"E","text":"available to staff only","explanation":"Staff only 縮窄讀者，違反 everyone。"},{"letter":"F","text":"free of charge","explanation":"人人可在公眾網站閱讀，句子沒有另外確認有沒有下載費。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"At the museum desk, the printed scientific summary is accessible to everyone who asks, though each copy costs HK$10.","zh":"印刷版科學摘要在博物館櫃位供所有索取者取得，但每份售價十港元。","upgrade":"At the museum desk, the printed scientific summary is available to everyone who asks, though each copy costs HK$10.","answer":"available to everyone","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"available to everyone","explanation":"博物館櫃位不限制索取者身分；收費並不改變人人可購得的範圍。"},{"letter":"B","text":"limited to specialists","explanation":"題句明說所有索取者都可買到，不能限於專家。"},{"letter":"C","text":"already mastered by everyone","explanation":"購得摘要不等於每人已理解內容。"},{"letter":"D","text":"available to members","explanation":"櫃位對所有詢問者供應，不能收窄為博物館會員。"},{"letter":"E","text":"easy for everyone to understand","explanation":"題句只交代可取得與價格，沒有證據說科學內容人人易懂。"},{"letter":"F","text":"free of charge","explanation":"每份明收十港元，不能說免費。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Open To All","meaning":"向所有人開放","note":"用於資料庫、研究結果或公開平台沒有特定身分門檻；比裸 open 更完整。","collocations":"open to all; open to everyone; an archive open to the public.","example":"The mission’s data archive will be open to all, not only to universities.","exampleZh":"任務數據檔案將向所有人開放，而不只限大學。","contrast":"Open to all 需搭配可開放的資料或平台；open to suggestions 是願意聽建議，屬別義。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The data archive will be accessible to everyone, including people outside universities; no research affiliation is required.","zh":"數據檔案將向所有人開放，包括大學以外的人士；無須研究機構身分。","upgrade":"The data archive will be open to all, including people outside universities; no research affiliation is required.","answer":"open to all","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"open only to researchers","explanation":"只限研究員與句中大學外人士相反。"},{"letter":"B","text":"open to registered researchers","explanation":"題句明說不需研究機構身分，不能限於已登記研究者。"},{"letter":"C","text":"openly debated","explanation":"Openly debated 說公開討論，不等於資料庫開放。"},{"letter":"D","text":"free to download","explanation":"不要求大學身分只證明讀取範圍，沒有明言是否收費或可下載。"},{"letter":"E","text":"open to all","explanation":"不用研究機構身分，open to all 精確保留開放範圍。"},{"letter":"F","text":"open to suggestions","explanation":"Open to suggestions 指願意接納建議，非資料可取。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Once posted, each interview recording will be accessible to everyone; the project will not reserve any of them for staff.","zh":"每段訪談錄音發佈後都會向所有人開放；研究計劃不會把任何一段留作員工專用。","upgrade":"Once posted, each interview recording will be open to all; the project will not reserve any of them for staff.","answer":"open to all","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"open to staff only","explanation":"研究計劃明說不會把任何錄音留作員工專用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"open to all","explanation":"每段錄音發佈後均不設員工專享限制，公眾都可取得。"},{"letter":"C","text":"open for staff editing","explanation":"這說員工可修改錄音，不是公眾能否取得錄音。"},{"letter":"D","text":"open to selected interviewees","explanation":"只准部分受訪者使用會收窄原句的「所有人」。"},{"letter":"E","text":"released only as a staff summary","explanation":"原句承諾公開每段錄音，而不只是內部摘要。"},{"letter":"F","text":"free of charge","explanation":"向所有人開放不等於明說取得錄音一定免費。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Publicly Available","meaning":"公開可取得","note":"強調公眾可取得資料，常用於報告、數據或研究結果；仍須確認公開是否真的沒有身分限制。","collocations":"publicly available report / data / findings; make results publicly available.","example":"The team said its findings would be publicly available after publication.","exampleZh":"研究團隊表示，成果發表後公眾便可取得。","contrast":"Publicly 指對公眾公開，不必然表示免費或容易理解；當源句特別說人人可得時，必要時補 to everyone。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The report will be accessible to everyone on the agency’s public website after its release.","zh":"報告發表後將放在機構的公開網站，讓所有人都可取得。","upgrade":"The report will be publicly available on the agency’s public website after its release.","answer":"publicly available","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"easy to understand","explanation":"Easy to understand 說明白程度，網站公開不保證。"},{"letter":"B","text":"available to staff only","explanation":"Staff only 違反公眾可取。"},{"letter":"C","text":"available before release","explanation":"句子明說after its release，不能把公開日期提前。"},{"letter":"D","text":"physically nearby","explanation":"Physically nearby 說地理距離，不是網上公開。"},{"letter":"E","text":"available on request","explanation":"報告將直接放上公眾網站，不是只能個別申請索取。"},{"letter":"F","text":"publicly available","explanation":"公開網站讓公眾取得報告，publicly available 簡潔自然。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The survey findings will be accessible to everyone next month when public libraries display printed copies at their information desks.","zh":"下個月公立圖書館在資訊櫃位展示印刷版調查結果後，人人都可以取得。","upgrade":"The survey findings will be publicly available next month when public libraries display printed copies at their information desks.","answer":"publicly available","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"already distributed","explanation":"圖書館要到下個月才展示印刷副本，不能說現在已派發。"},{"letter":"B","text":"restricted to analysts","explanation":"公立圖書館資訊櫃位供公眾索閱，不能限於分析員。"},{"letter":"C","text":"publicly available","explanation":"公立圖書館展示紙本副本，讓公眾取得，不必依靠網上檔案。"},{"letter":"D","text":"easy to master","explanation":"能在圖書館取到調查結果，不代表內容容易理解或掌握。"},{"letter":"E","text":"available to library staff only","explanation":"資訊櫃位供公眾索閱，不能收窄為圖書館職員。"},{"letter":"F","text":"already used by all","explanation":"下個月才公開，不表示目前已人人使用。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Easy For Anyone To Obtain","meaning":"任何人都容易取得","note":"平實完整地把「取得容易」和「對象不設限」說出；需要簡易下載、公開索取等安排作支持。","collocations":"easy for anyone to obtain / download; make a summary easy for anyone to obtain.","example":"The free download made the plain-language summary easy for anyone to obtain.","exampleZh":"免費下載安排令任何人都容易取得淺白版摘要。","contrast":"Obtain 是取得，不保證看得懂；若原文只說可取得但沒有便利安排，勿無故加 easy。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The summary will be accessible to everyone: no login is needed, and one click downloads the file.","zh":"摘要將供人人取得：毋須登入，按一下便可下載檔案。","upgrade":"The summary will be easy for anyone to obtain: no login is needed, and one click downloads the file.","answer":"easy for anyone to obtain","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"easy for anyone to obtain","explanation":"不用登入、一按即得，足以支持「任何人容易取得」。"},{"letter":"B","text":"available to registered users","explanation":"句子明說無須登入，不能加上使用者必須先登記的門檻。"},{"letter":"C","text":"difficult for the public to find","explanation":"與一按即可下載矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","text":"limited to officials","explanation":"與毋須登入的人人取得相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"easy for everyone to understand","explanation":"一按即可取得檔案，不代表摘要的內容人人都能看懂。"},{"letter":"F","text":"impossible to download","explanation":"與明說可以下載相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The public summary is accessible to everyone at the information desk, where visitors can request a copy without an appointment.","zh":"公眾可在資訊櫃位取得摘要，訪客毋須預約即可索取副本。","upgrade":"The public summary is easy for anyone to obtain at the information desk, where visitors can request a copy without an appointment.","answer":"easy for anyone to obtain","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"available by appointment","explanation":"題句明說訪客無須預約便可到櫃位索取。"},{"letter":"B","text":"hard to reach physically","explanation":"Hard to reach physically 沒有路程資料支持。"},{"letter":"C","text":"available only internally","explanation":"Internally 把公開摘要錯說成內部文件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"easy for everyone to understand","explanation":"毋須預約只說索取方便，沒有證據說摘要內容人人易懂。"},{"letter":"E","text":"easy for anyone to obtain","explanation":"資訊櫃位可直接索取而無身分門檻，說容易取得合理。"},{"letter":"F","text":"only for researchers to read","explanation":"Only for researchers 違反公眾及訪客可取。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Freely Available","meaning":"免費可取得（須有證據）","note":"在句子明示無收費時才適用；比源句單純人人可得多一層「免費」資訊。","collocations":"freely available online; freely available to everyone; make findings freely available.","example":"The team placed the full report online without a fee, making it freely available.","exampleZh":"研究團隊把完整報告免費放到網上，讓公眾可取得。","contrast":"Freely 在公開資料語境常暗示毋須付費；源文沒有明說費用，所以本項只能用於另有免費證據的練習。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"The findings will be accessible to everyone through a website that charges no fee and needs no membership.","zh":"研究結果將經由一個不收費、無須會員身分的網站供所有人取得。","upgrade":"The findings will be freely available to everyone through a website that charges no fee and needs no membership.","answer":"freely available","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"available with a paid subscription","explanation":"網站明說不收費、也不需會員身分；付費訂閱與兩項條件都衝突。"},{"letter":"B","text":"available for a fee","explanation":"For a fee 與不收費矛盾。"},{"letter":"C","text":"freely available","explanation":"明說不收費也無會員門檻，freely available 的較強含義有根據。"},{"letter":"D","text":"available only to subscribers","explanation":"只限訂閱者與無會員要求相反。"},{"letter":"E","text":"easy for all to understand","explanation":"不收費不表示所有人都能理解內容。"},{"letter":"F","text":"available only to staff","explanation":"網站毋須會員身分並供所有人取得，不能改成只讓職員使用。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The printed scientific report is accessible to everyone at local libraries, which distribute copies at no charge.","zh":"印刷版科學報告可在本地圖書館供所有人取得；圖書館免費派發副本。","upgrade":"The printed scientific report is freely available to everyone at local libraries, which distribute copies at no charge.","answer":"freely available","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"easy to understand","explanation":"免費派發紙本報告，不代表每個人都看得懂科學內容。"},{"letter":"B","text":"already read by the public","explanation":"圖書館有免費副本，不等於公眾已經閱讀。"},{"letter":"C","text":"available for a charge","explanation":"圖書館 at no charge 派發，直接否定收費。"},{"letter":"D","text":"available only at one research library","explanation":"題句說本地多間圖書館都免費派發，不能收窄成只在一家研究圖書館提供。"},{"letter":"E","text":"only available on request to staff","explanation":"圖書館免費派給所有人，沒有說只供職員索取。"},{"letter":"F","text":"freely available","explanation":"圖書館明確免費派發紙本副本，freely available to everyone 保留費用與範圍。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"accessible / understandable：可得與易懂","zh":"研究報告可在網上人人取得，仍可能只有專家看得懂。原文的 accessible to everyone 主要是取得權；不可自動改成 easy for everyone to understand。","point":"Open access to information does not guarantee comprehension."},{"word":"available / available to everyone：範圍","zh":"Available 只說有供應；available to everyone 才保留原文「所有人」的範圍。若只供研究員閱覽，就不是原句承諾。","point":"The audience qualifier everyone is essential to the original claim."},{"word":"open / open to：介詞與主語","zh":"The archive is open to all 可指公開資料庫；裸句 the knowledge is open 不清楚是公開還是尚可討論。改寫時應明示資料或平台及 to all。","point":"Open to all works for archives, data and findings; bare open is ambiguous."},{"word":"free / public：費用不能推斷","zh":"Publicly available 說公眾可取；freely available 常暗示不用付款。原文 accessible 本身未明說免費；只有練習明示無收費才可用較強說法。","point":"Public availability does not by itself establish that no fee is charged."},{"word":"reach / access：實體與資訊","zh":"Easy to reach 常指地方或網站入口；科學知識本身說 obtain/access the findings 較自然。若要用 reach，通常須改寫成網站或平台容易進入。","point":"Reach is more natural for a place or site than for knowledge itself."},{"word":"accessible to / accessible by：搭配","zh":"原文說知識 accessible to everyone；說資料可由某群體取得也可見 accessible by，但本課在一般使用者語境以 to 最自然。Access 名詞則常接 to。","point":"Keep the natural preposition and preserve the universal audience."}],"moduleNumber":101},{"id":"lesson-102","sourceId":16,"headword":"accuse","title":"Accuse","titleZh":"同義詞教學","subtitle":"同義詞教學","description":"In the 2012 heritage passage, tycoons and prominent citizens have been accused of deliberately destroying heritage for profit. The passive reports an allegation, not a finding of guilt or a criminal charge.","sourceSense":"In the 2012 heritage passage, tycoons and prominent citizens have been accused of deliberately destroying heritage for profit. The passive reports an allegation, not a finding of guilt or a criminal charge.","sourceMap":{"headers":["Incoming candidate","Judgment for source sense"],"rows":[["charge","contextual: strong public charge; legal sense needs evidence"],["allege wrongdoing","recast: must supply alleged act and agent"],["blame","contextual: responsibility judgment"],["allege wrongdoing by","recast: agent named but act still needed"]],"note":"Omission challenge · 遺漏檢查： Claim that 因可保留失當行為的未證實陳述而加入；make allegations against 是 allege 的名詞式改寫，須另外補回「毀壞古蹟」的具體內容，故在搭配對比中說明而不重複作一個教學義項。Point the finger at 較口語，可能只指懷疑，與原文嚴肅的保育指控語域不合；denounce 偏譴責，可不提出具體罪行。原始候選 allege wrongdoing by 太籠統，會遺失具體毀壞行為；indict/convict 暗示司法程序，來源沒有支持。"},"quickChoice":{"headers":["Expression","Use it when","Boundary"],"rows":[["allege","對未經證實的失當行為提出主張；可用被動 it is alleged that 或主動 critics allege that。","不要把 allegation 寫成已證實的事實；改寫時須保留 alleged act。"],["charge with","可指正式起訴，亦可指言辭強烈的公開指控；須標明非法律語境。","原文不證明有人被刑事檢控，故練習只能用明示的評論語境。"],["blame for","把不良結果的責任放在某人身上；比僅說有人指控更接近責任判斷。","須有明確的負面結果；不能把尚未證實的來源指控寫成作者自己認定的事實。"],["claim that","說某件事是真的，但未保證有證據或已證實；若內容是失當行為，可從陳述角度改寫 accuse。","Claim that 本身不一定有責難意味；練習必須保留具體失當指稱，且不可寫成已證實。"]],"note":"Quick rule · 快速判斷： 強調尚未證實的指稱，用 allege that 或明說不當行為的 claim that；強烈的公開指責可用 charge someone with，但勿憑此說成刑事起訴；句子明確歸責某項損失時用 blame someone for。Convict 必須有法庭定罪，不能替代公開指控。"},"words":[{"order":1,"word":"allege","meaning":"聲稱／指稱","note":"對未經證實的失當行為提出主張；可用被動 it is alleged that 或主動 critics allege that。","collocations":"allege that; it is alleged that.","example":"Critics alleged that the developer ignored the site’s heritage value.","exampleZh":"批評者指稱發展商漠視該地點的歷史價值。","contrast":"不要把 allegation 寫成已證實的事實；改寫時須保留 alleged act。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Campaigners accuse the firm of ignoring the old building’s cultural value, but no finding has been made.","zh":"保育人士指稱公司漠視舊建築的文化價值，但尚無裁定。","upgrade":"Campaigners allege that the firm ignored the old building’s cultural value, but no finding has been made.","answer":"allege","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"prove","explanation":"尚無裁定，不能把公開指稱寫成已證明。"},{"letter":"B","text":"convict","explanation":"定罪必須有司法程序，不是保育人士發言。"},{"letter":"C","text":"allege","explanation":"Allege that 保留主張未獲證實的狀態。"},{"letter":"D","text":"suspect","explanation":"Suspect 偏懷疑，比明確對外提出的指控弱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"blame","explanation":"會把責任歸於公司，比保留未證實主張更強。"},{"letter":"F","text":"insinuate","explanation":"暗示不等於明確指稱漠視文化價值。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Parents accuse the tutoring centre of charging hidden fees; the centre denies this.","zh":"家長指稱補習中心收取隱藏費用；中心否認此事。","upgrade":"Parents allege that the tutoring centre charged hidden fees; the centre denies this.","answer":"allege","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"confirm","explanation":"補習中心仍否認，不能把家長的指稱當成已核實收費。"},{"letter":"B","text":"convict","explanation":"家長可提出收費指控，卻無權對中心作刑事定罪。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suspect","explanation":"家長已明確提出收隱藏費的指稱，不只是心中懷疑。"},{"letter":"D","text":"allege","explanation":"Allege that 保留補習中心被指控收費、但事實仍有爭議的狀態。"},{"letter":"E","text":"blame","explanation":"Blame 着重歸責；本句重點是家長提出未證實的具體收費主張。"},{"letter":"F","text":"predict","explanation":"指控涉及已被收取的費用，不是預測將來可能收費。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"charge with","meaning":"嚴正指控","note":"可指正式起訴，亦可指言辭強烈的公開指控；須標明非法律語境。","collocations":"charge someone with neglect; be charged with an offence.","example":"The columnist charged the council with neglecting the old market.","exampleZh":"專欄作者嚴正指責議會忽視舊街市。","contrast":"原文不證明有人被刑事檢控，故練習只能用明示的評論語境。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"In a newspaper column, critics strongly accuse the council of neglecting the historic market.","zh":"評論者在報章專欄強烈指責議會忽視歷史街市。","upgrade":"In a newspaper column, critics charge the council with neglecting the historic market.","answer":"charge with","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"convict","explanation":"報章評論不能裁定議會有罪。"},{"letter":"B","text":"charge with","explanation":"Charge ... with 可作強烈指責；此處不是法律控罪。"},{"letter":"C","text":"prosecute","explanation":"評論者不能代表公權力提出刑事檢控。"},{"letter":"D","text":"suspect","explanation":"欄目已公開嚴厲指責，不是停留在懷疑。"},{"letter":"E","text":"charge for","explanation":"Charge someone for 常指收費，不能代替 charge someone with neglecting 這個指責搭配。"},{"letter":"F","text":"acquit","explanation":"免責與公開指控相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"In a public letter, heritage groups accuse officials of serious negligence over the preservation requests; no court case has been brought.","zh":"保育團體在公開信中指責官員處理保育要求時嚴重疏忽；事件並無進入司法程序。","upgrade":"In a public letter, heritage groups charge officials with serious negligence over the preservation requests; no court case has been brought.","answer":"charge with","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"prosecute for","explanation":"公開信可提出指責，prosecute for 卻表示正式檢控，而句子明說沒有法庭案件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"charge of","explanation":"嚴正指控某人疏忽要說 charge someone with negligence，不能用 charge of 接人。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suspect of","explanation":"Suspect of 只表示懷疑，沒有公開信明確指出嚴重疏忽的強度。"},{"letter":"D","text":"accuse with","explanation":"Accuse someone with negligence 混用了搭配；應說 accuse of 或 charge with。"},{"letter":"E","text":"charge with","explanation":"Charge officials with serious negligence 可作公開信中的嚴正指責；沒有法庭案件便不當作刑事起訴。"},{"letter":"F","text":"convict of","explanation":"Convict of 要有法庭裁定；公開信不能判定官員有罪。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"blame for","meaning":"歸咎於","note":"把不良結果的責任放在某人身上；比僅說有人指控更接近責任判斷。","collocations":"blame someone for damage; be blamed for a loss.","example":"Some residents blamed the developer for the loss of the old theatre.","exampleZh":"一些居民把舊戲院消失歸咎於發展商。","contrast":"須有明確的負面結果；不能把尚未證實的來源指控寫成作者自己認定的事實。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Residents accuse the contractor of causing the damage and hold it responsible in their protest letter.","zh":"居民在抗議信中指責承建商造成損害，認為它須負責。","upgrade":"Residents blame the contractor for the damage in their protest letter.","answer":"blame for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"convict","explanation":"居民抗議信不能判定刑事有罪。"},{"letter":"B","text":"suspect","explanation":"只表示懷疑，未保留信中明確歸責。"},{"letter":"C","text":"blame for","explanation":"Blame ... for 保留居民將損害責任歸於承建商的觀點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"allege","explanation":"可保留指稱，但未表達居民認為承建商須負責的結果焦點。"},{"letter":"E","text":"formally charge","explanation":"居民可在信中歸責，卻不能對承建商提出正式刑事控罪。"},{"letter":"F","text":"acquit","explanation":"免責與追究損害責任相反。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Parents accuse the bus operator of cancelling the school route without warning and demand a refund for the missed journeys.","zh":"家長指責校車營辦商沒有預告便取消路線，並要求退還未乘搭車程的費用。","upgrade":"The bus operator is blamed by parents for cancelling the school route without warning; they demand a refund for the missed journeys.","answer":"blame for","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"acquit","explanation":"家長正在要求退款，並非正式宣告營辦商無責。"},{"letter":"B","text":"suspect","explanation":"家長已公開指責取消路線並追討費用，超過私下懷疑。"},{"letter":"C","text":"allege","explanation":"可以保留取消路線的指稱，卻沒有 blame 對退款責任的焦點。"},{"letter":"D","text":"criticise","explanation":"泛泛批評服務欠佳，未必把未乘搭車程的責任歸給營辦商。"},{"letter":"E","text":"exonerate","explanation":"宣告營辦商無責與家長追討退款的立場相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"blame for","explanation":"Be blamed for cancelling 保留家長把無預告取消及退款責任歸於營辦商的觀點。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","note":"說某件事是真的，但未保證有證據或已證實；若內容是失當行為，可從陳述角度改寫 accuse。","collocations":"claim that someone did something; claim wrongdoing.","example":"Campaigners claim that the company hid its demolition plans.","exampleZh":"保育人士聲稱公司隱瞞了拆卸計劃。","contrast":"Claim that 本身不一定有責難意味；練習必須保留具體失當指稱，且不可寫成已證實。","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Residents accuse the developer of hiding its demolition plans; the developer denies this.","zh":"居民指稱發展商隱瞞拆卸計劃；發展商否認。","upgrade":"Residents claim that the developer hid its demolition plans; the developer denies this.","answer":"claim that","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"claim that","explanation":"Claim that 保留居民提出的、尚有爭議的具體主張。"},{"letter":"B","text":"prove that","explanation":"仍有否認，沒有證明指稱屬實。"},{"letter":"C","text":"confirm that","explanation":"確認比原有指稱更強，原句沒有核實。"},{"letter":"D","text":"suspect that","explanation":"懷疑較弱，居民已公開提出主張。"},{"letter":"E","text":"deny that","explanation":"與居民的指控方向相反。"},{"letter":"F","text":"convict of","explanation":"定罪是法律結論，不是居民說法。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Did the parents publicly accuse the board of using trip funds without approval, or was the concern only raised privately?","zh":"家長有否公開指稱校董會未經批准便使用旅行經費，還是只曾私下提出疑慮？","upgrade":"Did the parents publicly claim that the board used trip funds without approval, or was the concern only raised privately?","answer":"claim that","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"establish that","explanation":"問題只查有沒有公開提出指稱，並未說旅行經費的用途已獲證實。"},{"letter":"B","text":"prove that","explanation":"家長公開發言與證明校董會違規是兩回事。"},{"letter":"C","text":"suspect that","explanation":"私下懷疑不能保留題目特意問的「有否公開提出主張」。"},{"letter":"D","text":"claim that","explanation":"Publicly claim that 可問家長是否對外提出具體的經費使用指稱。"},{"letter":"E","text":"deny that","explanation":"Deny 是否認違規；題目問家長是否提出違規指稱。"},{"letter":"F","text":"convict of","explanation":"家長不能對校董會作司法定罪，題目也沒有法庭程序。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"convict / accuse","zh":"中文辨析： Convict 是法庭裁定有罪；原文只說有人提出指控。","point":"An accusation is not a conviction."},{"word":"charge / accuse","zh":"中文辨析： Charge with 在司法語境暗示正式控罪；原文沒有說當局檢控。","point":"A public criticism is not automatically a legal charge."},{"word":"blame / accuse","zh":"中文辨析： Blame 偏向歸咎責任，可讓人覺得責任已確立；accuse 保留指稱性質。","point":"Responsibility and an allegation should not be conflated."},{"word":"suspect / accuse","zh":"中文辨析： Suspect 是懷疑；accuse 通常已有向外提出的指責。","point":"A private suspicion is not the same speech act."}],"moduleNumber":102}];
